\c 1
\s1 The Creation
\p \v 1 \rb In the beginning|בְּרֵאשִׁ֖ית\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֑ים\rb*\rb |אֵ֥ת\rb* \rb created|בָּרָ֣א\rb* \rb the heavens|הַשָּׁמַ֖יִם\rb* \rb and|וְאֵ֥ת\rb* \rb the earth|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb*.
\p \v 2 \rb Now the earth|וְהָאָ֗רֶץ\rb* \rb was|הָיְתָ֥ה\rb* \rb formless|תֹ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb and void|וָבֹ֔הוּ\rb*, \rb and darkness|וְחֹ֖שֶׁךְ\rb* \rb was over|עַל־\rb* \rb the surface|פְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the deep|תְה֑וֹם\rb*. \rb And the Spirit|וְר֣וּחַ\rb* \rb of God|אֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb* \rb was hovering|מְרַחֶ֖פֶת\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb the surface|פְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the waters|הַמָּֽיִם׃\rb*.
\s2 The First Day
\p \v 3 \rb And God|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Let there be|יְהִ֣י\rb* \rb light|א֑וֹר\rb*,”\f + \fr 1:3 \ft Cited in 2 Corinthians 4:6\f* \rb and there was|וַֽיְהִי־\rb* \rb light|אֽוֹר׃\rb*. \v 4 \rb And God|אֱלֹהִ֛ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb saw|וַיַּ֧רְא\rb* \rb that|כִּי־\rb* \rb the light|הָא֖וֹר\rb* \rb was good|ט֑וֹב\rb*, \rb and He|אֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb* \rb separated|וַיַּבְדֵּ֣ל\rb* \rb the light|הָא֖וֹר\rb* \rb from|וּבֵ֥ין\rb*\rb |בֵּ֥ין\rb* \rb the darkness|הַחֹֽשֶׁךְ׃\rb*. \v 5 \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֤ים׀\rb* \rb called|וַיִּקְרָ֨א\rb* \rb the light|לָאוֹר֙\rb* “\rb day|י֔וֹם\rb*,” \rb and the darkness|וְלַחֹ֖שֶׁךְ\rb* \rb He called|קָ֣רָא\rb* “\rb night|לָ֑יְלָה\rb*.”
\p \rb And there was|וַֽיְהִי־\rb* \rb evening|עֶ֥רֶב\rb*, \rb and there was|וַֽיְהִי־\rb* \rb morning|בֹ֖קֶר\rb* — \rb the first|אֶחָֽד׃פ\rb* \rb day|י֥וֹם\rb*.\f + \fr 1:5 \ft Literally \ft day one\f*
\s2 The Second Day
\p \v 6 \rb And God|אֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Let there be|יְהִ֥י\rb* \rb an expanse|רָקִ֖יעַ\rb*\f + \fr 1:6 \ft Or \fqa a canopy \ft or \fqa a firmament \ft or \fqa a vault\ft ; also in verses 7, 8, 14, 15, 17, and 20\f* \rb between|בְּת֣וֹךְ\rb* \rb the waters|הַמָּ֑יִם\rb*, \rb to|וִיהִ֣י\rb* \rb separate|מַבְדִּ֔יל\rb*\rb |בֵּ֥ין\rb* \rb the waters|מַ֖יִם\rb* \rb from the waters|לָמָֽיִם׃\rb*.” \v 7 \rb So God|אֱלֹהִים֮\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb made|וַיַּ֣עַשׂ\rb* \rb the expanse|הָרָקִיעַ֒\rb* \rb and separated|וַיַּבְדֵּ֗ל\rb*\rb |בֵּ֤ין\rb* \rb the waters|הַמַּ֙יִם֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb beneath|מִתַּ֣חַת\rb* \rb it|לָרָקִ֔יעַ\rb* \rb from|וּבֵ֣ין\rb* \rb the waters|הַמַּ֔יִם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb above|מֵעַ֣ל\rb*\rb |לָרָקִ֑יעַ\rb*. \rb And it was|וַֽיְהִי־\rb* \rb so|כֵֽן׃\rb*. \v 8 \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֛ים\rb* \rb called|וַיִּקְרָ֧א\rb* \rb the expanse|לָֽרָקִ֖יעַ\rb* “\rb sky|שָׁמָ֑יִם\rb*.”
\p \rb And there was|וַֽיְהִי־\rb* \rb evening|עֶ֥רֶב\rb*, \rb and there was|וַֽיְהִי־\rb* \rb morning|בֹ֖קֶר\rb* — \rb the second|שֵׁנִֽי׃פ\rb* \rb day|י֥וֹם\rb*.
\s2 The Third Day
\p \v 9 \rb And God|אֱלֹהִ֗ים\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Let the waters|הַמַּ֜יִם\rb* \rb under|מִתַּ֤חַת\rb* \rb the sky|הַשָּׁמַ֙יִם֙\rb* \rb be gathered|יִקָּו֨וּ\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb one|אֶחָ֔ד\rb* \rb place|מָק֣וֹם\rb*, \rb so that the dry land|הַיַּבָּשָׁ֑ה\rb* \rb may appear|וְתֵרָאֶ֖ה\rb*.” \rb And it was|וַֽיְהִי־\rb* \rb so|כֵֽן׃\rb*. \v 10 \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֤ים׀\rb* \rb called|וַיִּקְרָ֨א\rb* \rb the dry land|לַיַּבָּשָׁה֙\rb* “\rb earth|אֶ֔רֶץ\rb*,” \rb and the gathering|וּלְמִקְוֵ֥ה\rb* \rb of waters|הַמַּ֖יִם\rb* \rb He called|קָרָ֣א\rb* “\rb seas|יַמִּ֑ים\rb*.” \rb And God|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb saw|וַיַּ֥רְא\rb* \rb that|כִּי־\rb* \rb it was good|טֽוֹב׃\rb*.
\p \v 11 \rb Then God|אֱלֹהִ֗ים\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Let the earth|הָאָ֙רֶץ֙\rb* \rb bring forth|תַּֽדְשֵׁ֤א\rb* \rb vegetation|דֶּ֔שֶׁא\rb*: \rb seed-bearing|מַזְרִ֣יעַ\rb*\rb |זֶ֔רַע\rb* \rb plants|עֵ֚שֶׂב\rb* \rb and fruit|פְּרִ֞י\rb* \rb trees|עֵ֣ץ\rb*, \rb each bearing|עֹ֤שֶׂה\rb* \rb fruit|פְּרִי֙\rb* \rb with seed|זַרְעוֹ־\rb* \rb according to its kind|לְמִינ֔וֹ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb*\rb |ב֖וֹ\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb*\rb |הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb*.” \rb And it was|וַֽיְהִי־\rb* \rb so|כֵֽן׃\rb*. \v 12 \rb The earth|הָאָ֜רֶץ\rb* \rb produced|וַתּוֹצֵ֨א\rb* \rb vegetation|דֶּ֠שֶׁא\rb*: \rb seed-bearing|מַזְרִ֤יעַ\rb*\rb |זֶ֙רַע֙\rb* \rb plants|עֵ֣שֶׂב\rb* \rb according to their kinds|לְמִינֵ֔הוּ\rb* \rb and trees|וְעֵ֧ץ\rb* \rb bearing|עֹֽשֶׂה־\rb* \rb fruit|פְּרִ֛י\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb with seed|זַרְעוֹ־\rb*\rb |ב֖וֹ\rb* \rb according to their kinds|לְמִינֵ֑הוּ\rb*. \rb And God|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb saw|וַיַּ֥רְא\rb* \rb that|כִּי־\rb* \rb it was good|טֽוֹב׃\rb*.
\p \v 13 \rb And there was|וַֽיְהִי־\rb* \rb evening|עֶ֥רֶב\rb*, \rb and there was|וַֽיְהִי־\rb* \rb morning|בֹ֖קֶר\rb* — \rb the third|שְׁלִישִֽׁי׃פ\rb* \rb day|י֥וֹם\rb*.
\s2 The Fourth Day
\p \v 14 \rb And God|אֱלֹהִ֗ים\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Let there be|יְהִ֤י\rb* \rb lights|מְאֹרֹת֙\rb* \rb in the expanse|בִּרְקִ֣יעַ\rb* \rb of the sky|הַשָּׁמַ֔יִם\rb* \rb to distinguish|לְהַבְדִּ֕יל\rb* \rb between|בֵּ֥ין\rb* \rb the day|הַיּ֖וֹם\rb* \rb and|וּבֵ֣ין\rb* \rb the night|הַלָּ֑יְלָה\rb*, \rb and let them be|וְהָי֤וּ\rb* \rb signs to mark|לְאֹתֹת֙\rb* \rb the seasons|וּלְמ֣וֹעֲדִ֔ים\rb* \rb and days|וּלְיָמִ֖ים\rb* \rb and years|וְשָׁנִֽים׃\rb*. \v 15 \rb And let them serve|וְהָי֤וּ\rb* \rb as lights|לִמְאוֹרֹת֙\rb* \rb in the expanse|בִּרְקִ֣יעַ\rb* \rb of the sky|הַשָּׁמַ֔יִם\rb* \rb to shine|לְהָאִ֖יר\rb* \rb upon|עַל־\rb* \rb the earth|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb*.” \rb And it was|וַֽיְהִי־\rb* \rb so|כֵֽן׃\rb*.
\p \v 16 \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb made|וַיַּ֣עַשׂ\rb* \rb two|שְׁנֵ֥י\rb* \rb great|הַגְּדֹלִ֑ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb lights|הַמְּאֹרֹ֖ת\rb*: \rb the greater|הַגָּדֹל֙\rb* \rb light|הַמָּא֤וֹר\rb* \rb to rule|לְמֶמְשֶׁ֣לֶת\rb* \rb the day|הַיּ֔וֹם\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the lesser|הַקָּטֹן֙\rb* \rb light|הַמָּא֤וֹר\rb* \rb to rule|לְמֶמְשֶׁ֣לֶת\rb* \rb the night|הַלַּ֔יְלָה\rb*. \rb And He made|וְאֵ֖ת\rb* \rb the stars as well|הַכּוֹכָבִֽים׃\rb*.
\p \v 17 \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb set|וַיִּתֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb these lights|אֹתָ֛ם\rb* \rb in the expanse|בִּרְקִ֣יעַ\rb* \rb of the sky|הַשָּׁמָ֑יִם\rb* \rb to shine|לְהָאִ֖יר\rb* \rb upon|עַל־\rb* \rb the earth|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb*, \v 18 \rb to preside over|וְלִמְשֹׁל֙\rb* \rb the day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb and the night|וּבַלַּ֔יְלָה\rb*, \rb and to separate|וּֽלֲהַבְדִּ֔יל\rb* \rb the light|הָא֖וֹר\rb* \rb from|וּבֵ֣ין\rb*\rb |בֵּ֥ין\rb* \rb the darkness|הַחֹ֑שֶׁךְ\rb*. \rb And God|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb saw|וַיַּ֥רְא\rb* \rb that|כִּי־\rb* \rb it was good|טֽוֹב׃\rb*.
\p \v 19 \rb And there was|וַֽיְהִי־\rb* \rb evening|עֶ֥רֶב\rb*, \rb and there was|וַֽיְהִי־\rb* \rb morning|בֹ֖קֶר\rb* — \rb the fourth|רְבִיעִֽי׃פ\rb* \rb day|י֥וֹם\rb*.
\s2 The Fifth Day
\p \v 20 \rb And God|אֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Let the waters|הַמַּ֔יִם\rb* \rb teem|יִשְׁרְצ֣וּ\rb* \rb with living|נֶ֣פֶשׁ\rb*\rb |חַיָּ֑ה\rb* \rb creatures|שֶׁ֖רֶץ\rb*, \rb and let birds|וְעוֹף֙\rb* \rb fly|יְעוֹפֵ֣ף\rb* \rb above|עַל־\rb* \rb the earth|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb the open|פְּנֵ֖י\rb* \rb expanse|רְקִ֥יעַ\rb* \rb of the sky|הַשָּׁמָֽיִם׃\rb*.” \v 21 \rb So|אֶת־\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb* \rb created|וַיִּבְרָ֣א\rb* \rb the great|הַגְּדֹלִ֑ים\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֣ת\rb* \rb sea creatures|הַתַּנִּינִ֖ם\rb* \rb and every|כָּל־\rb* \rb living|הַֽחַיָּ֣ה׀\rb* \rb thing|נֶ֣פֶשׁ\rb* \rb that moves|הָֽרֹמֶ֡שֶׂת\rb*, \rb with which|אֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb the waters|הַמַּ֜יִם\rb* \rb teemed|שָׁרְצ֨וּ\rb* \rb according to their kinds|לְמִֽינֵהֶ֗ם\rb*, \rb and|וְאֵ֨ת\rb* \rb every|כָּל־\rb* \rb winged|כָּנָף֙\rb* \rb bird|ע֤וֹף\rb* \rb after its kind|לְמִינֵ֔הוּ\rb*. \rb And God|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb saw|וַיַּ֥רְא\rb* \rb that|כִּי־\rb* \rb it was good|טֽוֹב׃\rb*.
\p \v 22 \rb Then God|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb blessed|וַיְבָ֧רֶךְ\rb* \rb them|אֹתָ֛ם\rb* \rb and said|לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*, “\rb Be fruitful|פְּר֣וּ\rb* \rb and multiply|וּרְב֗וּ\rb* \rb and fill|וּמִלְא֤וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the waters|הַמַּ֙יִם֙\rb* \rb of the seas|בַּיַּמִּ֔ים\rb*, \rb and let birds|וְהָע֖וֹף\rb* \rb multiply|יִ֥רֶב\rb* \rb on the earth|בָּאָֽרֶץ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 23 \rb And there was|וַֽיְהִי־\rb* \rb evening|עֶ֥רֶב\rb*, \rb and there was|וַֽיְהִי־\rb* \rb morning|בֹ֖קֶר\rb* — \rb the fifth|חֲמִישִֽׁי׃פ\rb* \rb day|י֥וֹם\rb*.
\s2 The Sixth Day
\p \v 24 \rb And God|אֱלֹהִ֗ים\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Let the earth|הָאָ֜רֶץ\rb* \rb bring forth|תּוֹצֵ֨א\rb* \rb living|חַיָּה֙\rb* \rb creatures|נֶ֤פֶשׁ\rb* \rb according to their kinds|לְמִינָ֔הּ\rb*: \rb livestock|בְּהֵמָ֥ה\rb*, \rb land crawlers|וָרֶ֛מֶשׂ\rb*, \rb and beasts|וְחַֽיְתוֹ־\rb* \rb of the earth|אֶ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb according to their kinds|לְמִינָ֑הּ\rb*.” \rb And it was|וַֽיְהִי־\rb* \rb so|כֵֽן׃\rb*. \v 25 \rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִים֩\rb* \rb made|וַיַּ֣עַשׂ\rb* \rb the beasts|חַיַּ֨ת\rb* \rb of the earth|הָאָ֜רֶץ\rb* \rb according to their kinds|לְמִינָ֗הּ\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the livestock|הַבְּהֵמָה֙\rb* \rb according to their kinds|לְמִינָ֔הּ\rb*, \rb and|וְאֵ֛ת\rb* \rb everything|כָּל־\rb* \rb that crawls|רֶ֥מֶשׂ\rb* \rb upon the earth|הָֽאֲדָמָ֖ה\rb* \rb according to its kind|לְמִינֵ֑הוּ\rb*. \rb And God|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb saw|וַיַּ֥רְא\rb* \rb that|כִּי־\rb* \rb it was good|טֽוֹב׃\rb*.
\p \v 26 \rb Then God|אֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Let Us make|נַֽעֲשֶׂ֥ה\rb* \rb man|אָדָ֛ם\rb* \rb in Our image|בְּצַלְמֵ֖נוּ\rb*, \rb after Our likeness|כִּדְמוּתֵ֑נוּ\rb*, \rb to rule|וְיִרְדּוּ֩\rb* \rb over the fish|בִדְגַ֨ת\rb* \rb of the sea|הַיָּ֜ם\rb* \rb and the birds|וּבְע֣וֹף\rb* \rb of the air|הַשָּׁמַ֗יִם\rb*, \rb over the livestock|וּבַבְּהֵמָה֙\rb*, \rb and over all|וּבְכָל־\rb* \rb the earth itself|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb*\f + \fr 1:26 \ft MT; Syriac \fqa and over all the beasts of the earth\f* \rb and every|וּבְכָל־\rb* \rb creature|הָרֶ֖מֶשׂ\rb* \rb that crawls|הָֽרֹמֵ֥שׂ\rb* \rb upon|עַל־\rb* \rb it|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb*.”
\b 
\q1 \v 27 \rb So God|אֱלֹהִ֤ים׀\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb created|וַיִּבְרָ֨א\rb* \rb man|הָֽאָדָם֙\rb* \rb in His own image|בְּצַלְמ֔וֹ\rb*;
\q2 \rb in the image|בְּצֶ֥לֶם\rb* \rb of God|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb He created|בָּרָ֣א\rb* \rb him|אֹת֑וֹ\rb*;
\q2 \rb male|זָכָ֥ר\rb* \rb and female|וּנְקֵבָ֖ה\rb* \rb He created|בָּרָ֥א\rb* \rb them|אֹתָֽם׃\rb*.\f + \fr 1:27 \ft Cited in Matthew 19:4 and Mark 10:6\f*
\p \v 28 \rb God|אֱלֹהִים֒\rb* \rb blessed|וַיְבָ֣רֶךְ\rb* \rb them|אֹתָם֮\rb* \rb and|אֱלֹהִ֗ים\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to them|לָהֶ֜ם\rb*, “\rb Be fruitful|פְּר֥וּ\rb* \rb and multiply|וּרְב֛וּ\rb*, \rb and fill|וּמִלְא֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the earth|הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb and subdue it|וְכִבְשֻׁ֑הָ\rb*; \rb rule|וּרְד֞וּ\rb* \rb over the fish|בִּדְגַ֤ת\rb* \rb of the sea|הַיָּם֙\rb* \rb and the birds|וּבְע֣וֹף\rb* \rb of the air|הַשָּׁמַ֔יִם\rb* \rb and every|וּבְכָל־\rb* \rb creature|חַיָּ֖ה\rb* \rb that crawls|הָֽרֹמֶ֥שֶׂת\rb* \rb upon|עַל־\rb* \rb the earth|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 29 \rb Then God|אֱלֹהִ֗ים\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Behold|הִנֵּה֩\rb*, \rb I have given|נָתַ֨תִּי\rb* \rb you|לָכֶ֜ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb every|כָּל־\rb*\rb |זֹרֵ֣עַ\rb* \rb seed-bearing|זֶ֗רַע\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb plant|עֵ֣שֶׂב׀\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the face|פְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of all|כָל־\rb* \rb the earth|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb*, \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb every|כָּל־\rb* \rb tree|הָעֵ֛ץ\rb* \rb whose|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb fruit|פְרִי־\rb* \rb contains|זֹרֵ֣עַ\rb*\rb |בּ֥וֹ\rb*\rb |עֵ֖ץ\rb* \rb seed|זָ֑רַע\rb*. \rb They will be|יִֽהְיֶ֖ה\rb* \rb yours|לָכֶ֥ם\rb* \rb for food|לְאָכְלָֽה׃\rb*. \v 30 \rb And to every|וּֽלְכָל־\rb* \rb beast|חַיַּ֣ת\rb* \rb of the earth|הָ֠אָרֶץ\rb* \rb and every|וּלְכָל־\rb* \rb bird|ע֨וֹף\rb* \rb of the air|הַשָּׁמַ֜יִם\rb* \rb and every|וּלְכֹ֣ל׀\rb* \rb creature that crawls|רוֹמֵ֣שׂ\rb* \rb upon|עַל־\rb* \rb the earth|הָאָ֗רֶץ\rb* — \rb everything that has|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the breath|נֶ֣פֶשׁ\rb* \rb of life|חַיָּ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb in it|בּוֹ֙\rb* — \rb I have given every|כָּל־\rb* \rb green|יֶ֥רֶק\rb* \rb plant|עֵ֖שֶׂב\rb* \rb for food|לְאָכְלָ֑ה\rb*.” \rb And it was|וַֽיְהִי־\rb* \rb so|כֵֽן׃\rb*.
\p \v 31 \rb And God|אֱלֹהִים֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb looked upon|וַיַּ֤רְא\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb He had made|עָשָׂ֔ה\rb*, \rb and indeed|וְהִנֵּה־\rb*, \rb it was very|מְאֹ֑ד\rb* \rb good|ט֖וֹב\rb*.
\p \rb And there was|וַֽיְהִי־\rb* \rb evening|עֶ֥רֶב\rb*, \rb and there was|וַֽיְהִי־\rb* \rb morning|בֹ֖קֶר\rb* — \rb the sixth|הַשִּׁשִּֽׁי׃פ\rb* \rb day|י֥וֹם\rb*.
\c 2
\s1 The Seventh Day
\p \v 1 \rb Thus the heavens|הַשָּׁמַ֥יִם\rb* \rb and the earth|וְהָאָ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb were completed|וַיְכֻלּ֛וּ\rb* \rb in all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb their vast array|צְבָאָֽם׃\rb*. \v 2 \rb And by the seventh|הַשְּׁבִיעִ֔י\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִים֙\rb* \rb had finished|וַיְכַ֤ל\rb* \rb the work|מְלַאכְתּ֖וֹ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb He had been doing|עָשָׂ֑ה\rb*; \rb so on that|הַשְּׁבִיעִ֔י\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb He rested|וַיִּשְׁבֹּת֙\rb* \rb from all|מִכָּל־\rb* \rb His work|מְלַאכְתּ֖וֹ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb*\rb |עָשָֽׂה׃\rb*.\f + \fr 2:2 \ft Cited in Hebrews 4:4\f*
\p \v 3 \rb Then God|אֱלֹהִים֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb blessed|וַיְבָ֤רֶךְ\rb* \rb the seventh|הַשְּׁבִיעִ֔י\rb* \rb day|י֣וֹם\rb* \rb and sanctified|וַיְקַדֵּ֖שׁ\rb* \rb it|אֹת֑וֹ\rb*, \rb because|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb on that day|ב֤וֹ\rb* \rb He rested|שָׁבַת֙\rb* \rb from all|מִכָּל־\rb* \rb the work|מְלַאכְתּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb of creation|בָּרָ֥א\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb He|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb had accomplished|לַעֲשֽׂוֹת׃פ\rb*.
\s1 Man and Woman in the Garden
\p \v 4 \rb This|אֵ֣לֶּה\rb* \rb is the account|תוֹלְד֧וֹת\rb* \rb of the heavens|הַשָּׁמַ֛יִם\rb* \rb and the earth|וְהָאָ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb when they were created|בְּהִבָּֽרְאָ֑ם\rb*, \rb in the day|בְּי֗וֹם\rb* \rb that the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb*\f + \fr 2:4 \fqa LORD \ft or \fqa GOD\ft , with capital letters, represents the proper name of the God of Israel and the one true God, transliterated from the Hebrew as \fqa YHWH\ft ; here and throughout the Scriptures.\f* \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb made|עֲשׂ֛וֹת\rb* \rb them|אֶ֥רֶץ\rb*\rb |וְשָׁמָֽיִם׃\rb*.
\p \v 5 \rb Now|וְכֹ֣ל׀\rb* \rb no shrub|שִׂ֣יחַ\rb* \rb of the field|הַשָּׂדֶ֗ה\rb* \rb had yet|טֶ֚רֶם\rb* \rb appeared|יִֽהְיֶ֣ה\rb* \rb on the earth|בָאָ֔רֶץ\rb*, \rb nor had any|וְכָל־\rb* \rb plant|עֵ֥שֶׂב\rb* \rb of the field|הַשָּׂדֶ֖ה\rb*\rb |טֶ֣רֶם\rb* \rb sprouted|יִצְמָ֑ח\rb*, \rb for|כִּי֩\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִים֙\rb* \rb had not yet|לֹ֨א\rb* \rb sent rain|הִמְטִ֜יר\rb* \rb upon|עַל־\rb* \rb the earth|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb*, \rb and there was no|אַ֔יִן\rb* \rb man|וְאָדָ֣ם\rb* \rb to cultivate|לַֽעֲבֹ֖ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the ground|הָֽאֲדָמָֽה׃\rb*. \v 6 \rb But springs|וְאֵ֖ד\rb*\f + \fr 2:6 \ft Or \fqa mist\f* \rb welled up|יַֽעֲלֶ֣ה\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the earth|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb* \rb and watered|וְהִשְׁקָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb surface|פְּנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of the ground|הָֽאֲדָמָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 7 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֨ה\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֜ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb formed|וַיִּיצֶר֩\rb* \rb man|הָֽאָדָ֗ם\rb* \rb from the dust|עָפָר֙\rb* \rb of|מִן־\rb* \rb the ground|הָ֣אֲדָמָ֔ה\rb* \rb and breathed|וַיִּפַּ֥ח\rb* \rb the breath|נִשְׁמַ֣ת\rb* \rb of life|חַיִּ֑ים\rb* \rb into his nostrils|בְּאַפָּ֖יו\rb*, \rb and the man|הָֽאָדָ֖ם\rb* \rb became|וַֽיְהִ֥י\rb* \rb a living|חַיָּֽה׃\rb* \rb being|לְנֶ֥פֶשׁ\rb*.\f + \fr 2:7 \ft Or \fqa a living soul\ft ; cited in 1 Corinthians 15:45\f*
\p \v 8 \rb And the LORD|יְהוָ֧ה\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֛ים\rb* \rb planted|וַיִּטַּ֞ע\rb* \rb a garden|גַּן־\rb* \rb in Eden|בְעֵ֖דֶן\rb*, \rb in the east|מִקֶּ֑דֶם\rb*, \rb where|שָׁ֔ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb He placed|וַיָּ֣שֶׂם\rb* \rb the man|הָֽאָדָ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb He had formed|יָצָֽר׃\rb*. \v 9 \rb Out|מִן־\rb* \rb of the ground|הָ֣אֲדָמָ֔ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִים֙\rb* \rb gave growth|וַיַּצְמַ֞ח\rb* \rb to every|כָּל־\rb* \rb tree|עֵ֛ץ\rb* \rb that is pleasing|נֶחְמָ֥ד\rb* \rb to the eye|לְמַרְאֶ֖ה\rb* \rb and good|וְט֣וֹב\rb* \rb for food|לְמַאֲכָ֑ל\rb*. \rb And in the middle|בְּת֣וֹךְ\rb* \rb of the garden|הַגָּ֔ן\rb* \rb were the tree|וְעֵ֤ץ\rb* \rb of life|הַֽחַיִּים֙\rb* \rb and the tree|וְעֵ֕ץ\rb* \rb of the knowledge|הַדַּ֖עַת\rb* \rb of good|ט֥וֹב\rb* \rb and evil|וָרָֽע׃\rb*.
\p \v 10 \rb Now a river|וְנָהָר֙\rb* \rb flowed out|יֹצֵ֣א\rb* \rb of Eden|מֵעֵ֔דֶן\rb* \rb to water|לְהַשְׁק֖וֹת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the garden|הַגָּ֑ן\rb*, \rb and from there|וּמִשָּׁם֙\rb* \rb it branched into|יִפָּרֵ֔ד\rb*\rb |וְהָיָ֖ה\rb* \rb four|לְאַרְבָּעָ֥ה\rb* \rb headwaters|רָאשִֽׁים׃\rb*:
\b 
\li1 \v 11 \rb The name|שֵׁ֥ם\rb* \rb of the first river|הָֽאֶחָ֖ד\rb* \rb is the Pishon|פִּישׁ֑וֹן\rb*; \rb it|ה֣וּא\rb* \rb winds through|הַסֹּבֵ֗ב\rb*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb* \rb the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb land|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Havilah|הַֽחֲוִילָ֔ה\rb*, \rb where|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb there is|שָׁ֖ם\rb* \rb gold|הַזָּהָֽב׃\rb*. \v 12 \rb And the gold|וּֽזֲהַ֛ב\rb* \rb of that|הַהִ֖וא\rb* \rb land|הָאָ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb is pure|ט֑וֹב\rb*, \rb and bdellium|הַבְּדֹ֖לַח\rb*\rb |וְאֶ֥בֶן\rb* \rb and onyx|הַשֹּֽׁהַם׃\rb* \rb are found there|שָׁ֥ם\rb*.
\li1 \v 13 \rb The name|וְשֵֽׁם־\rb* \rb of the second|הַשֵּׁנִ֖י\rb* \rb river|הַנָּהָ֥ר\rb* \rb is the Gihon|גִּיח֑וֹן\rb*; \rb it|ה֣וּא\rb* \rb winds through|הַסּוֹבֵ֔ב\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb land|אֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Cush|כּֽוּשׁ׃\rb*.
\li1 \v 14 \rb The name|וְשֵׁ֨ם\rb* \rb of the third|הַשְּׁלִישִׁי֙\rb* \rb river|הַנָּהָ֤ר\rb* \rb is the Tigris|חִדֶּ֔קֶל\rb*; \rb it|ה֥וּא\rb* \rb runs along|הַֽהֹלֵ֖ךְ\rb* \rb the east side|קִדְמַ֣ת\rb* \rb of Assyria|אַשּׁ֑וּר\rb*.
\li1 \rb And the fourth|הָֽרְבִיעִ֖י\rb* \rb river|וְהַנָּהָ֥ר\rb* \rb is the|ה֥וּא\rb* \rb Euphrates|פְרָֽת׃\rb*.
\p \v 15 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb took|וַיִּקַּ֛ח\rb* \rb the man|הָֽאָדָ֑ם\rb* \rb and placed him|וַיַּנִּחֵ֣הוּ\rb* \rb in the Garden|בְגַן־\rb* \rb of Eden|עֵ֔דֶן\rb* \rb to cultivate|לְעָבְדָ֖הּ\rb* \rb and keep it|וּלְשָׁמְרָֽהּ׃\rb*.
\p \v 16 \rb And the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb commanded|וַיְצַו֙\rb* \rb him|הָֽאָדָ֖ם\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*, “\rb You may eat freely|אָכֹ֥ל\rb*\rb |תֹּאכֵֽל׃\rb* \rb from every|מִכֹּ֥ל\rb* \rb tree|עֵֽץ־\rb* \rb of the garden|הַגָּ֖ן\rb*, \v 17 \rb but you must not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb eat|תֹאכַ֖ל\rb* \rb from|מִמֶּ֑נּוּ\rb* \rb the tree|וּמֵעֵ֗ץ\rb* \rb of the knowledge|הַדַּ֙עַת֙\rb* \rb of good|ט֣וֹב\rb* \rb and evil|וָרָ֔ע\rb*; \rb for|כִּ֗י\rb* \rb in the day|בְּי֛וֹם\rb* \rb that you eat|אֲכָלְךָ֥\rb* \rb of it|מִמֶּ֖נּוּ\rb*, \rb you will surely die|מ֥וֹת\rb*\rb |תָּמֽוּת׃\rb*.”
\p \v 18 \rb The LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb* \rb also said|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb*, “\rb It is not|לֹא־\rb* \rb good|ט֛וֹב\rb* \rb for the man|הָֽאָדָ֖ם\rb* \rb to be|הֱי֥וֹת\rb* \rb alone|לְבַדּ֑וֹ\rb*. \rb I will make|אֶֽעֱשֶׂהּ־\rb* \rb for him|לּ֥וֹ\rb* \rb a suitable|כְּנֶגְדּֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb helper|עֵ֖זֶר\rb*.”
\p \v 19 \rb And out of|מִן־\rb* \rb the ground|הָֽאֲדָמָ֗ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֨ה\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֜ים\rb* \rb formed|וַיִּצֶר֩\rb* \rb every|כָּל־\rb* \rb beast|חַיַּ֤ת\rb* \rb of the field|הַשָּׂדֶה֙\rb*\rb |וְאֵת֙\rb* \rb and every|כָּל־\rb* \rb bird|ע֣וֹף\rb* \rb of the air|הַשָּׁמַ֔יִם\rb*, \rb and He brought them|וַיָּבֵא֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the man|הָ֣אָדָ֔ם\rb* \rb to see|לִרְא֖וֹת\rb* \rb what|מַה־\rb* \rb he would name|יִּקְרָא־\rb*\rb |ל֑וֹ\rb* \rb each one|וְכֹל֩\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb*. \rb And whatever the man|הָֽאָדָ֛ם\rb* \rb called|יִקְרָא־\rb*\rb |ל֧וֹ\rb* \rb each living|חַיָּ֖ה\rb* \rb creature|נֶ֥פֶשׁ\rb*, \rb that|ה֥וּא\rb* \rb was its name|שְׁמֽוֹ׃\rb*. \v 20 \rb The man|הָֽאָדָ֜ם\rb* \rb gave|וַיִּקְרָ֨א\rb* \rb names|שֵׁמ֗וֹת\rb* \rb to all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb the livestock|הַבְּהֵמָה֙\rb*, \rb to the birds|וּלְע֣וֹף\rb* \rb of the air|הַשָּׁמַ֔יִם\rb*, \rb and to every|וּלְכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb beast|חַיַּ֣ת\rb* \rb of the field|הַשָּׂדֶ֑ה\rb*. \rb But for Adam|וּלְאָדָ֕ם\rb*\f + \fr 2:20 \ft Or \fqa the man\ft , as in verses 19 and 21\f* \rb no|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb suitable|כְּנֶגְדּֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb helper|עֵ֖זֶר\rb* \rb was found|מָצָ֥א\rb*.
\p \v 21 \rb So the LORD|יְהוָ֨ה\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֧ים׀\rb* \rb caused|וַיַּפֵּל֩\rb* \rb the man|הָאָדָ֖ם\rb* \rb to fall into|עַל־\rb* \rb a deep sleep|תַּרְדֵּמָ֛ה\rb*, \rb and while he slept|וַיִּישָׁ֑ן\rb*, \rb He took|וַיִּקַּ֗ח\rb* \rb one|אַחַת֙\rb* \rb of the man’s ribs|מִצַּלְעֹתָ֔יו\rb*\f + \fr 2:21 \ft Or \fqa took part of the man’s side\ft ; similarly in verse 22\f* \rb and closed up|וַיִּסְגֹּ֥ר\rb* \rb the area|תַּחְתֶּֽנָּה׃\rb* \rb with flesh|בָּשָׂ֖ר\rb*. \v 22 \rb And from the rib|הַצֵּלָ֛ע\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֨ה\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֧ים׀\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb had taken|לָקַ֥ח\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the man|הָֽאָדָ֖ם\rb*, \rb He made|וַיִּבֶן֩\rb* \rb a woman|לְאִשָּׁ֑ה\rb* \rb and brought her|וַיְבִאֶ֖הָ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb him|הָֽאָדָֽם׃\rb*. \v 23 \rb And the man|הָֽאָדָם֒\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּאמֶר֮\rb*:
\b 
\q1 “\rb This|זֹ֣את\rb* \rb is now|הַפַּ֗עַם\rb* \rb bone|עֶ֚צֶם\rb* \rb of my bones|מֵֽעֲצָמַ֔י\rb*
\q2 \rb and flesh|וּבָשָׂ֖ר\rb* \rb of my flesh|מִבְּשָׂרִ֑י\rb*;
\q1 \rb she|לְזֹאת֙\rb* \rb shall be called|יִקָּרֵ֣א\rb* ‘\rb woman|אִשָּׁ֔ה\rb*,’
\q2 \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb out of man|מֵאִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb she|זֹּֽאת׃\rb* \rb was taken|לֻֽקֳחָה־\rb*.”
\p \v 24 \rb For|עַל־\rb* \rb this reason|כֵּן֙\rb* \rb a man|אִ֔ישׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb will leave|יַֽעֲזָב־\rb* \rb his father|אָבִ֖יו\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb mother|אִמּ֑וֹ\rb* \rb and be united|וְדָבַ֣ק\rb* \rb to his wife|בְּאִשְׁתּ֔וֹ\rb*, \rb and they will become|וְהָי֖וּ\rb* \rb one|אֶחָֽד׃\rb* \rb flesh|לְבָשָׂ֥ר\rb*.\f + \fr 2:24 \ft LXX \fqa and the two will become one flesh\ft ; cited in Matthew 19:5, Mark 10:7–8, 1 Corinthians 6:16, and Ephesians 5:31\f*
\p \v 25 \rb And the man|הָֽאָדָ֖ם\rb* \rb and his wife|וְאִשְׁתּ֑וֹ\rb* \rb were|וַיִּֽהְי֤וּ\rb* \rb both|שְׁנֵיהֶם֙\rb* \rb naked|עֲרוּמִּ֔ים\rb*, \rb and they were not|וְלֹ֖א\rb* \rb ashamed|יִתְבֹּשָֽׁשׁוּ׃\rb*.
\c 3
\s1 The Serpent’s Deception
\p \v 1 \rb Now the serpent|וְהַנָּחָשׁ֙\rb*\f + \fr 3:1 \ft Hebrew \fqa nachash\ft , translated in this chapter as \fqa serpent\ft , is translated in most cases as \fqa snake\ft .\f* \rb was|הָיָ֣ה\rb* \rb more crafty|עָר֔וּם\rb* \rb than any|מִכֹּל֙\rb* \rb beast|חַיַּ֣ת\rb* \rb of the field|הַשָּׂדֶ֔ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֑ים\rb* \rb had made|עָשָׂ֖ה\rb*. \rb And he said|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the woman|הָ֣אִשָּׁ֔ה\rb*, “\rb Did God|אֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb* \rb really|כִּֽי־\rb*\rb |אַ֚ף\rb* \rb say|אָמַ֣ר\rb*, ‘\rb You must not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb eat|תֹֽאכְל֔וּ\rb* \rb from any|מִכֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb tree|עֵ֥ץ\rb* \rb in the garden|הַגָּֽן׃\rb*?’”
\p \v 2 \rb The woman|הָֽאִשָּׁ֖ה\rb* \rb answered|וַתֹּ֥אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the serpent|הַנָּחָ֑שׁ\rb*, “\rb We may eat|נֹאכֵֽל׃\rb* \rb the fruit|מִפְּרִ֥י\rb* \rb of the trees|עֵֽץ־\rb* \rb of the garden|הַגָּ֖ן\rb*, \v 3 \rb but about the fruit|וּמִפְּרִ֣י\rb* \rb of the tree|הָעֵץ֮\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb in the middle|בְּתוֹךְ־\rb* \rb of the garden|הַגָּן֒\rb*, \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֗ים\rb* \rb has said|אָמַ֣ר\rb*, ‘\rb You must not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb eat|תֹֽאכְלוּ֙\rb* \rb of it|מִמֶּ֔נּוּ\rb* \rb or|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb touch|תִגְּע֖וּ\rb* \rb it|בּ֑וֹ\rb*, \rb or|פֶּן־\rb* \rb you will die|תְּמֻתֽוּן׃\rb*.’”
\p \v 4 “\rb You will not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb surely die|מ֖וֹת\rb*\rb |תְּמֻתֽוּן׃\rb*,” \rb the serpent|הַנָּחָ֖שׁ\rb* \rb told|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the woman|הָֽאִשָּׁ֑ה\rb*. \v 5 “\rb For|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb* \rb knows|יֹדֵ֣עַ\rb* \rb that|כִּ֗י\rb* \rb in the day|בְּיוֹם֙\rb* \rb you eat|אֲכָלְכֶ֣ם\rb* \rb of it|מִמֶּ֔נּוּ\rb*, \rb your eyes|עֵֽינֵיכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb will be|וִהְיִיתֶם֙\rb* \rb opened|וְנִפְקְח֖וּ\rb* \rb and you will be like God|כֵּֽאלֹהִ֔ים\rb*, \rb knowing|יֹדְעֵ֖י\rb* \rb good|ט֥וֹב\rb* \rb and evil|וָרָֽע׃\rb*.”
\p \v 6 \rb When the woman|הָֽאִשָּׁ֡ה\rb* \rb saw|וַתֵּ֣רֶא\rb* \rb that|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb the tree|הָעֵ֨ץ\rb* \rb was good|טוֹב֩\rb* \rb for food|לְמַאֲכָ֜ל\rb* \rb and|וְכִ֧י\rb*\rb |ה֣וּא\rb* \rb pleasing|תַֽאֲוָה־\rb* \rb to the eyes|לָעֵינַ֗יִם\rb*, \rb and that it was|הָעֵץ֙\rb* \rb desirable|וְנֶחְמָ֤ד\rb* \rb for obtaining wisdom|לְהַשְׂכִּ֔יל\rb*, \rb she took|וַתִּקַּ֥ח\rb* \rb the fruit|מִפִּרְי֖וֹ\rb* \rb and ate it|וַתֹּאכַ֑ל\rb*. \rb She also gave some|וַתִּתֵּ֧ן\rb*\rb |גַּם־\rb* \rb to her husband|לְאִישָׁ֛הּ\rb* \rb who was with her|עִמָּ֖הּ\rb*, \rb and he ate it|וַיֹּאכַֽל׃\rb*.
\p \v 7 \rb And the eyes|עֵינֵ֣י\rb* \rb of both of them|שְׁנֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb were opened|וַתִּפָּקַ֙חְנָה֙\rb*, \rb and they|הֵ֑ם\rb* \rb knew|וַיֵּ֣דְע֔וּ\rb* \rb that|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb they were naked|עֵֽירֻמִּ֖ם\rb*; \rb so they sewed together|וַֽיִּתְפְּרוּ֙\rb* \rb fig|תְאֵנָ֔ה\rb* \rb leaves|עֲלֵ֣ה\rb* \rb and made|וַיַּעֲשׂ֥וּ\rb* \rb coverings|חֲגֹרֹֽת׃\rb* \rb for themselves|לָהֶ֖ם\rb*.
\s1 God Arraigns Adam and Eve
\p \v 8 \rb Then the man|הָֽאָדָ֜ם\rb* \rb and his wife|וְאִשְׁתּ֗וֹ\rb* \rb heard|וַֽיִּשְׁמְע֞וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the voice|ק֨וֹל\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֧ה\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֛ים\rb* \rb walking|מִתְהַלֵּ֥ךְ\rb* \rb in the garden|בַּגָּ֖ן\rb* \rb in the breeze|לְר֣וּחַ\rb*\f + \fr 3:8 \ft Or \fqa at the breezy (time)\ft ; Hebrew \fqa unto the Ruach\f* \rb of the day|הַיּ֑וֹם\rb*, \rb and they hid themselves|וַיִּתְחַבֵּ֨א\rb* \rb from the presence|מִפְּנֵי֙\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb* \rb among|בְּת֖וֹךְ\rb* \rb the trees|עֵ֥ץ\rb* \rb of the garden|הַגָּֽן׃\rb*.
\p \v 9 \rb But the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb called out|וַיִּקְרָ֛א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the man|הָֽאָדָ֑ם\rb*\rb |וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb*\rb |ל֖וֹ\rb*, “\rb Where are you|אַיֶּֽכָּה׃\rb*?”
\p \v 10 “\rb I heard|שָׁמַ֖עְתִּי\rb* \rb Your voice|קֹלְךָ֥\rb* \rb in the garden|בַּגָּ֑ן\rb*,” \rb he replied|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*, “\rb and I was afraid|וָאִירָ֛א\rb* \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I|אָנֹ֖כִי\rb* \rb was naked|עֵירֹ֥ם\rb*; \rb so I hid myself|וָאֵחָבֵֽא׃\rb*.”
\p \v 11 “\rb Who|מִ֚י\rb* \rb told|הִגִּ֣יד\rb*\rb |לְךָ֔\rb* \rb you|אָ֑תָּה\rb* \rb that|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb you were naked|עֵירֹ֖ם\rb*?” \rb asked the LORD God|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*. “\rb Have you eaten|אֲכָל־\rb* \rb from|הֲמִן־\rb* \rb the tree|הָעֵ֗ץ\rb* \rb of which|אֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb* \rb I commanded you|צִוִּיתִ֛יךָ\rb* \rb not to|לְבִלְתִּ֥י\rb* \rb eat|אָכָֽלְתָּ׃\rb*\rb |מִמֶּ֖נּוּ\rb*?”
\p \v 12 \rb And the man|הָֽאָדָ֑ם\rb* \rb answered|וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb*, “\rb The woman|הָֽאִשָּׁה֙\rb* \rb whom|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb You gave|נָתַ֣תָּה\rb* \rb me|עִמָּדִ֔י\rb*, \rb she|הִ֛וא\rb* \rb gave|נָֽתְנָה־\rb* \rb me|לִּ֥י\rb* \rb fruit from|מִן־\rb* \rb the tree|הָעֵ֖ץ\rb*, \rb and I ate it|וָאֹכֵֽל׃\rb*.”
\p \v 13 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֧ה\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֛ים\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to the woman|לָאִשָּׁ֖ה\rb*, “\rb What|מַה־\rb* \rb is this|זֹּ֣את\rb* \rb you have done|עָשִׂ֑ית\rb*?”
\p “\rb The serpent|הַנָּחָ֥שׁ\rb* \rb deceived me|הִשִּׁיאַ֖נִי\rb*,” \rb she|הָֽאִשָּׁ֔ה\rb* \rb replied|וַתֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb*, “\rb and I ate|וָאֹכֵֽל׃\rb*.”
\s1 The Fate of the Serpent
\p \v 14 \rb So the LORD|יְהֹוָ֨ה\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֥ים׀\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּאמֶר֩\rb* \rb to|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb the serpent|הַנָּחָשׁ֮\rb*:
\b 
\q1 “\rb Because|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb you have done|עָשִׂ֣יתָ\rb* \rb this|זֹּאת֒\rb*,
\q2 \rb cursed|אָר֤וּר\rb* \rb are you|אַתָּה֙\rb* \rb above all|מִכָּל־\rb* \rb livestock|הַבְּהֵמָ֔ה\rb*
\q2 \rb and every|וּמִכֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb beast|חַיַּ֣ת\rb* \rb of the field|הַשָּׂדֶ֑ה\rb*!
\q1 \rb On|עַל־\rb* \rb your belly|גְּחֹנְךָ֣\rb* \rb will you go|תֵלֵ֔ךְ\rb*,
\q2 \rb and dust|וְעָפָ֥ר\rb* \rb you will eat|תֹּאכַ֖ל\rb*,
\q2 \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the days|יְמֵ֥י\rb* \rb of your life|חַיֶּֽיךָ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 15 \rb And|בֵּֽינְךָ֙\rb* \rb I will put|אָשִׁ֗ית\rb* \rb enmity|וְאֵיבָ֣ה׀\rb* \rb between you|וּבֵ֣ין\rb* \rb and the woman|הָֽאִשָּׁ֔ה\rb*,
\q2 \rb and between|וּבֵ֥ין\rb* \rb your seed|זַרְעֲךָ֖\rb*\rb |וּבֵ֣ין\rb* \rb and her seed|זַרְעָ֑הּ\rb*.
\q1 \rb He|ה֚וּא\rb* \rb will crush|יְשׁוּפְךָ֣\rb* \rb your head|רֹ֔אשׁ\rb*,
\q2 \rb and you|וְאַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb will strike|תְּשׁוּפֶ֥נּוּ\rb* \rb his heel|עָקֵֽב׃ס\rb*.\f + \fr 3:15 \ft Or \fqa He will bruise your head, and you will bruise his heel\ft . The same Hebrew root for \fqa crush\ft , \fqa bruise\ft , or \fqa strike \ft appears twice in this verse.\f*”
\s1 The Punishment of Mankind
\p \v 16 \rb To|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb the woman|הָאִשָּׁ֣ה\rb* \rb He said|אָמַ֗ר\rb*:
\b 
\q1 “\rb I will sharply increase|הַרְבָּ֤ה\rb*\rb |אַרְבֶּה֙\rb* \rb your pain|עִצְּבוֹנֵ֣ךְ\rb* \rb in childbirth|וְהֵֽרֹנֵ֔ךְ\rb*;
\q2 \rb in pain|בְּעֶ֖צֶב\rb* \rb you will bring forth|תֵּֽלְדִ֣י\rb* \rb children|בָנִ֑ים\rb*.
\q1 \rb Your desire|תְּשׁ֣וּקָתֵ֔ךְ\rb* \rb will be for|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb your husband|אִישֵׁךְ֙\rb*,\f + \fr 3:16 \ft Or \fqa You will desire to control your husband\f*
\q2 \rb and he|וְה֖וּא\rb* \rb will rule|יִמְשָׁל־\rb* \rb over you|בָּֽךְ׃ס\rb*.”
\p \v 17 \rb And to Adam|וּלְאָדָ֣ם\rb* \rb He said|אָמַ֗ר\rb*:
\b 
\q1 “\rb Because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb you have listened|שָׁמַעְתָּ֮\rb* \rb to the voice|לְק֣וֹל\rb* \rb of|מִן־\rb* \rb your wife|אִשְׁתֶּךָ֒\rb*
\q2 \rb and have eaten|וַתֹּ֙אכַל֙\rb* \rb from the tree|הָעֵ֔ץ\rb*
\q2 \rb of which|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb I commanded|צִוִּיתִ֙יךָ֙\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb you not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb to eat|תֹאכַ֖ל\rb*\rb |מִמֶּ֑נּוּ\rb*,
\q1 \rb cursed|אֲרוּרָ֤ה\rb* \rb is the ground|הָֽאֲדָמָה֙\rb* \rb because of you|בַּֽעֲבוּרֶ֔ךָ\rb*;
\q2 \rb through toil|בְּעִצָּבוֹן֙\rb* \rb you will eat of it|תֹּֽאכֲלֶ֔נָּה\rb*
\q2 \rb all|כֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb the days|יְמֵ֥י\rb* \rb of your life|חַיֶּֽיךָ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 18 \rb Both thorns|וְק֥וֹץ\rb* \rb and thistles|וְדַרְדַּ֖ר\rb* \rb it will yield|תַּצְמִ֣יחַֽ\rb* \rb for you|לָ֑ךְ\rb*,
\q2 \rb and you will eat|וְאָכַלְתָּ֖\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the plants|עֵ֥שֶׂב\rb* \rb of the field|הַשָּׂדֶֽה׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 19 \rb By the sweat|בְּזֵעַ֤ת\rb* \rb of your brow|אַפֶּ֙יךָ֙\rb*
\q2 \rb you will eat|תֹּ֣אכַל\rb* \rb your bread|לֶ֔חֶם\rb*,
\q1 \rb until|עַ֤ד\rb* \rb you return|שֽׁוּבְךָ֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the ground|הָ֣אֲדָמָ֔ה\rb* —
\q2 \rb because|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb out of it|מִמֶּ֖נָּה\rb* \rb were you taken|לֻקָּ֑חְתָּ\rb*.
\q1 \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb dust|עָפָ֣ר\rb* \rb you are|אַ֔תָּה\rb*,
\q2 \rb and to|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb dust|עָפָ֖ר\rb* \rb you shall return|תָּשֽׁוּב׃\rb*.”
\p \v 20 \rb And Adam|הָֽאָדָ֛ם\rb*\rb |וַיִּקְרָ֧א\rb* \rb named|שֵׁ֥ם\rb* \rb his wife|אִשְׁתּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb Eve|חַוָּ֑ה\rb*,\f + \fr 3:20 \fqa Eve \ft sounds like the Hebrew for \fqa giving life \ft or \fqa living\ft .\f* \rb because|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb she|הִ֥וא\rb* \rb would be|הָֽיְתָ֖ה\rb* \rb the mother|אֵ֥ם\rb* \rb of all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the living|חָֽי׃\rb*.
\s1 The Expulsion from Paradise
\p \v 21 \rb And the LORD|יְהוָ֨ה\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֜ים\rb* \rb made|וַיַּעַשׂ֩\rb* \rb garments|כָּתְנ֥וֹת\rb* \rb of skin|ע֖וֹר\rb* \rb for Adam|לְאָדָ֧ם\rb* \rb and his wife|וּלְאִשְׁתּ֛וֹ\rb*, \rb and He clothed them|וַיַּלְבִּשֵֽׁם׃פ\rb*.
\p \v 22 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֗ים\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר׀\rb*, “\rb Behold|הֵ֤ן\rb*, \rb the man|הָֽאָדָם֙\rb* \rb has become|הָיָה֙\rb* \rb like one|כְּאַחַ֣ד\rb* \rb of Us|מִמֶּ֔נּוּ\rb*, \rb knowing|לָדַ֖עַת\rb* \rb good|ט֣וֹב\rb* \rb and evil|וָרָ֑ע\rb*. \rb And now|וְעַתָּ֣ה׀\rb*, \rb lest|פֶּן־\rb* \rb he reach out|יִשְׁלַ֣ח\rb* \rb his hand|יָד֗וֹ\rb* \rb and take|וְלָקַח֙\rb* \rb also|גַּ֚ם\rb* \rb from the tree|מֵעֵ֣ץ\rb* \rb of life|הַֽחַיִּ֔ים\rb*, \rb and eat|וְאָכַ֖ל\rb*, \rb and live|וָחַ֥י\rb* \rb forever|לְעֹלָֽם׃\rb*...”
\p \v 23 \rb Therefore the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb banished him|וַֽיְשַׁלְּחֵ֛הוּ\rb* \rb from the Garden|מִגַּן־\rb* \rb of Eden|עֵ֑דֶן\rb* \rb to work|לַֽעֲבֹד֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the ground|הָ֣אֲדָמָ֔ה\rb* \rb from which|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb he had been taken|לֻקַּ֖ח\rb*\rb |מִשָּֽׁם׃\rb*. \v 24 \rb So He drove out|וַיְגָ֖רֶשׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the man|הָֽאָדָ֑ם\rb* \rb and|אֶת־\rb* \rb stationed|וַיַּשְׁכֵּן֩\rb* \rb cherubim|הַכְּרֻבִ֗ים\rb* \rb on the east side|מִקֶּ֨דֶם\rb* \rb of the Garden|לְגַן־\rb* \rb of Eden|עֵ֜דֶן\rb*, \rb along with|וְאֵ֨ת\rb* \rb a whirling|הַמִּתְהַפֶּ֔כֶת\rb* \rb sword|הַחֶ֙רֶב֙\rb* \rb of flame|לַ֤הַט\rb* \rb to guard|לִשְׁמֹ֕ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the way|דֶּ֖רֶךְ\rb* \rb to the tree|עֵ֥ץ\rb* \rb of life|הַֽחַיִּֽים׃ס\rb*.
\c 4
\s1 Cain and Abel
\p \v 1 \rb And Adam|וְהָ֣אָדָ֔ם\rb* \rb had relations with|יָדַ֖ע\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his wife|אִשְׁתּ֑וֹ\rb* \rb Eve|חַוָּ֣ה\rb*, \rb and she conceived|וַתַּ֙הַר֙\rb* \rb and gave birth to|וַתֵּ֣לֶד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Cain|קַ֔יִן\rb*.\f + \fr 4:1 \fqa Cain \ft sounds like the Hebrew for \fqa acquired \ft or \fqa brought forth\ft .\f*
\p “\rb With the help of|אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb I have brought forth|קָנִ֥יתִי\rb* \rb a man|אִ֖ישׁ\rb*,” \rb she said|וַתֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*.
\p \v 2 \rb Later|וַתֹּ֣סֶף\rb* \rb she gave birth|לָלֶ֔דֶת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb to Cain’s brother|אָחִ֖יו\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Abel|הָ֑בֶל\rb*.
\p \rb Now|וַֽיְהִי־\rb* \rb Abel|הֶ֙בֶל֙\rb* \rb was|הָיָ֖ה\rb* \rb a keeper|רֹ֣עֵה\rb* \rb of sheep|צֹ֔אן\rb*, \rb while Cain|וְקַ֕יִן\rb* \rb was a tiller|עֹבֵ֥ד\rb* \rb of the soil|אֲדָמָֽה׃\rb*. \v 3 \rb So in the course|מִקֵּ֣ץ\rb* \rb of time|יָמִ֑ים\rb*\rb |וַֽיְהִ֖י\rb*, \rb Cain|קַ֜יִן\rb* \rb brought|וַיָּבֵ֨א\rb* \rb some of the fruit|מִפְּרִ֧י\rb* \rb of the soil|הָֽאֲדָמָ֛ה\rb* \rb as an offering|מִנְחָ֖ה\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָֽה׃\rb*, \v 4 \rb while Abel|וְהֶ֨בֶל\rb*\rb |ה֛וּא\rb*\rb |גַם־\rb* \rb brought|הֵבִ֥יא\rb* \rb the best portions|וּמֵֽחֶלְבֵהֶ֑ן\rb* \rb of the firstborn|מִבְּכֹר֥וֹת\rb* \rb of his flock|צֹאנ֖וֹ\rb*.
\p \rb And the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb looked with favor|וַיִּ֣שַׁע\rb* \rb on|אֶל־\rb* \rb Abel|הֶ֖בֶל\rb* \rb and|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb his offering|מִנְחָתֽוֹ׃\rb*, \v 5 \rb but|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb He had no|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb regard|שָׁעָ֑ה\rb* \rb for|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb Cain|קַ֥יִן\rb* \rb and his offering|מִנְחָת֖וֹ\rb*. \rb So Cain|לְקַ֙יִן֙\rb* \rb became very|מְאֹ֔ד\rb* \rb angry|וַיִּ֤חַר\rb*, \rb and his countenance|פָּנָֽיו׃\rb* \rb fell|וַֽיִּפְּל֖וּ\rb*.
\p \v 6 “\rb Why|לָ֚מָּה\rb* \rb are you angry|חָ֣רָה\rb*,” \rb said|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Cain|קָ֑יִן\rb*, “\rb |לָ֔ךְ\rb* \rb and why|וְלָ֖מָּה\rb* \rb has your countenance|פָנֶֽיךָ׃\rb* \rb fallen|נָפְל֥וּ\rb*? \v 7 \rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb you do what is right|תֵּיטִיב֙\rb*, \rb will|הֲל֤וֹא\rb* \rb you not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb be accepted|שְׂאֵ֔ת\rb*? \rb But if|וְאִם֙\rb* \rb you refuse to do what is right|תֵיטִ֔יב\rb*, \rb sin|חַטָּ֣את\rb* \rb is crouching|רֹבֵ֑ץ\rb* \rb at your door|לַפֶּ֖תַח\rb*; \rb it desires|תְּשׁ֣וּקָת֔וֹ\rb* \rb you|וְאֵלֶ֙יךָ֙\rb*,\f + \fr 4:7 \ft Or \fqa it desires to control you\f* \rb but you|וְאַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb must master|תִּמְשָׁל־\rb* \rb it|בּֽוֹ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 8 \rb Then Cain|קַ֖יִן\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his brother|אָחִ֑יו\rb* \rb Abel, “Let us go out to the field.”|הֶ֣בֶל\rb*\f + \fr 4:8 \ft SP, LXX, Syriac, and Vulgate; Hebrew \fqa Then Cain spoke to his brother Abel.\f* \rb And|וַֽיְהִי֙\rb* \rb while they were|בִּהְיוֹתָ֣ם\rb* \rb in the field|בַּשָּׂדֶ֔ה\rb*, \rb Cain|קַ֛יִן\rb* \rb rose up|וַיָּ֥קָם\rb* \rb against|אֶל־\rb* \rb his brother|אָחִ֖יו\rb* \rb Abel|הֶ֥בֶל\rb* \rb and killed him|וַיַּהַרְגֵֽהוּ׃\rb*.
\p \v 9 \rb And the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Cain|קַ֔יִן\rb*, “\rb Where|אֵ֖י\rb* \rb is your brother|אָחִ֑יךָ\rb* \rb Abel|הֶ֣בֶל\rb*?”
\p “\rb I do not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb know|יָדַ֔עְתִּי\rb*!” \rb he answered|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb*. “\rb Am I|אָנֹֽכִי׃\rb* \rb my brother’s|אָחִ֖י\rb* \rb keeper|הֲשֹׁמֵ֥ר\rb*?”
\p \v 10 “\rb What|מֶ֣ה\rb* \rb have you done|עָשִׂ֑יתָ\rb*?” \rb replied the LORD|וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb*. “\rb The voice|ק֚וֹל\rb* \rb of your brother’s|אָחִ֔יךָ\rb* \rb blood|דְּמֵ֣י\rb* \rb cries out|צֹעֲקִ֥ים\rb* \rb to Me|אֵלַ֖י\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the ground|הָֽאֲדָמָֽה׃\rb*. \v 11 \rb Now|וְעַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb you|אָ֑תָּה\rb* \rb are cursed and banished|אָר֣וּר\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the ground|הָֽאֲדָמָה֙\rb*, \rb which|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb has opened|פָּצְתָ֣ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb its mouth|פִּ֔יהָ\rb* \rb to receive|לָקַ֛חַת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your brother’s|אָחִ֖יךָ\rb* \rb blood|דְּמֵ֥י\rb* \rb from your hand|מִיָּדֶֽךָ׃\rb*. \v 12 \rb When|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb you till|תַֽעֲבֹד֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the ground|הָ֣אֲדָמָ֔ה\rb*, \rb it will no|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb longer|תֹסֵ֥ף\rb* \rb yield|תֵּת־\rb* \rb its produce|כֹּחָ֖הּ\rb* \rb to you|לָ֑ךְ\rb*. \rb You will be|תִּֽהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb a fugitive|נָ֥ע\rb* \rb and a wanderer|וָנָ֖ד\rb* \rb on the earth|בָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 13 \rb But Cain|קַ֖יִן\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*, “\rb My punishment|עֲוֺנִ֖י\rb*\f + \fr 4:13 \ft Or \fqa guilt \ft or \fqa sin\f* \rb is greater|גָּד֥וֹל\rb* \rb than I can bear|מִנְּשֹֽׂא׃\rb*. \v 14 \rb Behold|הֵן֩\rb*, \rb this|אֹתִ֜י\rb* \rb day|הַיּ֗וֹם\rb* \rb You have driven me|גֵּרַ֨שְׁתָּ\rb* \rb from the face|פְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the earth|הָֽאֲדָמָ֔ה\rb*, \rb and from|מֵעַל֙\rb* \rb Your face|וּמִפָּנֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb I will be hidden|אֶסָּתֵ֑ר\rb*; \rb I will be|וְהָיִ֜יתִי\rb* \rb a fugitive|נָ֤ע\rb* \rb and a wanderer|וָנָד֙\rb* \rb on the earth|בָּאָ֔רֶץ\rb*, \rb and|וְהָיָ֥ה\rb* \rb whoever|כָל־\rb* \rb finds me|מֹצְאִ֖י\rb* \rb will kill me|יַֽהַרְגֵֽנִי׃\rb*.”
\p \v 15 “\rb Not so|לָכֵן֙\rb*!”\f + \fr 4:15 \ft LXX, Vulgate, and Syriac; Hebrew \fqa “Very well!” \ft or \fqa “Therefore:”\f* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֧אמֶר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb*\rb |ל֣וֹ\rb*. “\rb If anyone|כָּל־\rb* \rb slays|הֹרֵ֣ג\rb* \rb Cain|קַ֔יִן\rb*, \rb then Cain will be avenged|יֻקָּ֑ם\rb* \rb sevenfold|שִׁבְעָתַ֖יִם\rb*.” \rb And the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb placed|וַיָּ֨שֶׂם\rb* \rb a mark|א֔וֹת\rb* \rb on Cain|לְקַ֙יִן֙\rb*, \rb so that no one|לְבִלְתִּ֥י\rb*\rb |כָּל־\rb* \rb who found him|מֹצְאֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb would kill|הַכּוֹת־\rb* \rb him|אֹת֖וֹ\rb*.
\p \v 16 \rb So Cain|קַ֖יִן\rb* \rb went out|וַיֵּ֥צֵא\rb* \rb from the presence|מִלִּפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb and settled|וַיֵּ֥שֶׁב\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶֽרֶץ־\rb* \rb of Nod|נ֖וֹד\rb*,\f + \fr 4:16 \fqa Nod \ft means \fqa wandering\ft .\f* \rb east|קִדְמַת־\rb* \rb of Eden|עֵֽדֶן׃\rb*.
\s1 The Descendants of Cain
\p \v 17 \rb And Cain|קַ֙יִן֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb had relations with|וַיֵּ֤דַע\rb* \rb his wife|אִשְׁתּ֔וֹ\rb*, \rb and she conceived|וַתַּ֖הַר\rb* \rb and gave birth to|וַתֵּ֣לֶד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Enoch|חֲנ֑וֹךְ\rb*. \rb Then|וַֽיְהִי֙\rb* \rb Cain built|בֹּ֣נֶה\rb* \rb a city|עִ֔יר\rb* \rb and named|וַיִּקְרָא֙\rb*\rb |שֵׁ֣ם\rb* \rb it|הָעִ֔יר\rb* \rb after|כְּשֵׁ֖ם\rb* \rb his son|בְּנ֥וֹ\rb* \rb Enoch|חֲנֽוֹךְ׃\rb*.
\p \v 18 \rb Now to Enoch|לַֽחֲנוֹךְ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb was born|וַיִּוָּלֵ֤ד\rb* \rb Irad|עִירָ֔ד\rb*, \rb and Irad|וְעִירָ֕ד\rb* \rb was the father of|יָלַ֖ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Mehujael|מְחֽוּיָאֵ֑ל\rb*, \rb and Mehujael|וּמְחִיּיָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb was the father of|יָלַד֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Methusael|מְת֣וּשָׁאֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb and Methusael|וּמְתוּשָׁאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb was the father of|יָלַ֥ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Lamech|לָֽמֶךְ׃\rb*. \v 19 \rb And Lamech|לֶ֖מֶךְ\rb* \rb married|וַיִּֽקַּֽח־\rb*\rb |ל֥וֹ\rb* \rb two|שְׁתֵּ֣י\rb* \rb women|נָשִׁ֑ים\rb*, \rb one|הָֽאַחַת֙\rb* \rb named|שֵׁ֤ם\rb* \rb Adah|עָדָ֔ה\rb* \rb and|וְשֵׁ֥ם\rb* \rb the other|הַשֵּׁנִ֖ית\rb* \rb Zillah|צִלָּֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 20 \rb Adah|עָדָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb gave birth to|וַתֵּ֥לֶד\rb* \rb Jabal|יָבָ֑ל\rb*; \rb he|ה֣וּא\rb* \rb was|הָיָ֔ה\rb* \rb the father|אֲבִ֕י\rb* \rb of those who dwell|יֹשֵׁ֥ב\rb* \rb in tents|אֹ֖הֶל\rb* \rb and raise livestock|וּמִקְנֶֽה׃\rb*. \v 21 \rb And his brother’s|אָחִ֖יו\rb* \rb name|וְשֵׁ֥ם\rb* \rb was Jubal|יוּבָ֑ל\rb*; \rb he|ה֣וּא\rb* \rb was|הָיָ֔ה\rb* \rb the father|אֲבִ֕י\rb* \rb of all|כָּל־\rb* \rb who play|תֹּפֵ֥שׂ\rb* \rb the harp|כִּנּ֖וֹר\rb* \rb and flute|וְעוּגָֽב׃\rb*.
\p \v 22 \rb And Zillah|וְצִלָּ֣ה\rb*\rb |הִ֗וא\rb*\rb |גַם־\rb* \rb gave birth to|יָֽלְדָה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |תּ֣וּבַל\rb* \rb Tubal-cain|קַ֔יִן\rb*, \rb a forger|לֹטֵ֕שׁ\rb* \rb of every|כָּל־\rb* \rb implement|חֹרֵ֥שׁ\rb* \rb of bronze|נְחֹ֖שֶׁת\rb* \rb and iron|וּבַרְזֶ֑ל\rb*. \rb And the sister|וַֽאֲח֥וֹת\rb*\rb |תּֽוּבַל־\rb* \rb of Tubal-cain|קַ֖יִן\rb* \rb was Naamah|נַֽעֲמָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 23 \rb Then Lamech|לֶ֜מֶךְ\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to his wives|לְנָשָׁ֗יו\rb*:
\b 
\q1 “\rb Adah|עָדָ֤ה\rb* \rb and Zillah|וְצִלָּה֙\rb*, \rb hear|שְׁמַ֣עַן\rb* \rb my voice|קוֹלִ֔י\rb*;
\q2 \rb wives|נְשֵׁ֣י\rb* \rb of Lamech|לֶ֔מֶךְ\rb*, \rb listen|הַאְזֵ֖נָּה\rb* \rb to my speech|אִמְרָתִ֑י\rb*.
\q1 \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb I|אִ֤ישׁ\rb* \rb have slain a man|הָרַ֙גְתִּי֙\rb* \rb for wounding me|לְפִצְעִ֔י\rb*,
\q2 \rb a young man|וְיֶ֖לֶד\rb* \rb for striking me|לְחַבֻּרָתִֽי׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 24 \rb If|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb Cain|קָ֑יִן\rb* \rb is avenged|יֻקַּם־\rb* \rb sevenfold|שִׁבְעָתַ֖יִם\rb*,
\q2 \rb then Lamech|וְלֶ֖מֶךְ\rb*\rb |שִׁבְעִ֥ים\rb* \rb seventy-sevenfold|וְשִׁבְעָֽה׃\rb*.”\f + \fr 4:24 \ft Hebrew; LXX can be translated as either \fqa seventy times seven \ft or \fqa seventy-sevenfold\ft ; see also Matthew 18:22.\f*
\s1 Seth and Enosh
\p \v 25 \rb And Adam|אָדָ֥ם\rb* \rb again|עוֹד֙\rb* \rb had relations with|וַיֵּ֨דַע\rb* \rb his wife|אִשְׁתּ֔וֹ\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb and she gave birth to|וַתֵּ֣לֶד\rb* \rb a son|בֵּ֔ן\rb* \rb and named|וַתִּקְרָ֥א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb him|שְׁמ֖וֹ\rb* \rb Seth|שֵׁ֑ת\rb*,\f + \fr 4:25 \fqa Seth \ft probably means \fqa granted \ft or \fqa appointed\ft .\f* \rb saying|כִּ֣י\rb*, “\rb God|אֱלֹהִים֙\rb* \rb has granted|שָֽׁת־\rb* \rb me|לִ֤י\rb* \rb another|אַחֵ֔ר\rb* \rb seed|זֶ֣רַע\rb* \rb in place|תַּ֣חַת\rb* \rb of Abel|הֶ֔בֶל\rb*, \rb since|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb Cain|קָֽיִן׃\rb* \rb killed him|הֲרָג֖וֹ\rb*.”
\p \v 26 \rb And to Seth|וּלְשֵׁ֤ת\rb*\rb |הוּא֙\rb* \rb also|גַּם־\rb* \rb a son|בֵּ֔ן\rb* \rb was born|יֻלַּד־\rb*, \rb and he called|וַיִּקְרָ֥א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb him|שְׁמ֖וֹ\rb* \rb Enosh|אֱנ֑וֹשׁ\rb*.
\p \rb At that time|אָ֣ז\rb* \rb men began|הוּחַ֔ל\rb* \rb to call upon|לִקְרֹ֖א\rb*\f + \fr 4:26 \ft Or \fqa to proclaim\ft ; some translators \fqa to invoke \ft or \fqa to call themselves by \ft or \fqa to profane \f* \rb the name|בְּשֵׁ֥ם\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃פ\rb*.
\c 5
\s1 The Descendants of Adam
\p \v 1 \rb This|זֶ֣ה\rb* \rb is the book|סֵ֔פֶר\rb* \rb of the generations|תּוֹלְדֹ֖ת\rb* \rb of Adam|אָדָ֑ם\rb*. \rb In the day|בְּי֗וֹם\rb* \rb that God|אֱלֹהִים֙\rb* \rb created|בְּרֹ֤א\rb* \rb man|אָדָ֔ם\rb*, \rb He made|עָשָׂ֥ה\rb* \rb him|אֹתֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb in His own likeness|בִּדְמ֥וּת\rb*\rb |אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb*. \v 2 \rb Male|זָכָ֥ר\rb* \rb and female|וּנְקֵבָ֖ה\rb* \rb He created them|בְּרָאָ֑ם\rb*,\f + \fr 5:2 \ft Cited in Matthew 19:4 and Mark 10:6\f* \rb and He blessed|וַיְבָ֣רֶךְ\rb* \rb them|אֹתָ֗ם\rb*. \rb And in the day|בְּי֖וֹם\rb* \rb they were created|הִבָּֽרְאָֽם׃ס\rb*, \rb He called|וַיִּקְרָ֤א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb them|שְׁמָם֙\rb* “\rb man|אָדָ֔ם\rb*.”\f + \fr 5:2 \ft Hebrew \fqa Adam\f*
\p \v 3 \rb When Adam|אָדָ֗ם\rb* \rb was|וַֽיְחִ֣י\rb* \rb 130|שְׁלֹשִׁ֤ים\rb*\rb |וּמְאַת֙\rb* \rb years old|שָׁנָ֔ה\rb*, \rb he had a son|וַיּ֥וֹלֶד\rb* \rb in his own likeness|בִּדְמוּת֖וֹ\rb*, \rb after his own image|כְּצַלְמ֑וֹ\rb*; \rb and he named him|וַיִּקְרָ֥א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |שְׁמ֖וֹ\rb* \rb Seth|שֵֽׁת׃\rb*. \v 4 \rb And after|אַֽחֲרֵי֙\rb* \rb he had become the father of|הוֹלִיד֣וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Seth|שֵׁ֔ת\rb*,\rb |יְמֵי־\rb* \rb Adam|אָדָ֗ם\rb* \rb lived|וַיִּֽהְי֣וּ\rb* \rb 800|שְׁמֹנֶ֥ה\rb*\rb |מֵאֹ֖ת\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָ֑ה\rb* \rb and had other|וַיּ֥וֹלֶד\rb* \rb sons|בָּנִ֖ים\rb* \rb and daughters|וּבָנֽוֹת׃\rb*. \v 5 \rb So Adam|אָדָם֙\rb* \rb lived|וַיִּֽהְי֞וּ\rb* \rb a total of|כָּל־\rb*\rb |יְמֵ֤י\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb*\rb |חַ֔י\rb* \rb 930|תְּשַׁ֤ע\rb*\rb |מֵאוֹת֙\rb*\rb |וּשְׁלֹשִׁ֖ים\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָ֔ה\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֑ה\rb*, \rb and then he died|וַיָּמֹֽת׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 6 \rb When Seth|שֵׁ֕ת\rb* \rb was|וַֽיְחִי־\rb* \rb 105|וּמְאַ֣ת\rb*\rb |שָׁנִ֖ים\rb*\rb |חָמֵ֥שׁ\rb* \rb years old|שָׁנָ֑ה\rb*, \rb he became the father of|וַיּ֖וֹלֶד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Enosh|אֱנֽוֹשׁ׃\rb*. \v 7 \rb And after|אַֽחֲרֵי֙\rb* \rb he had become the father of|הוֹלִיד֣וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Enosh|אֱנ֔וֹשׁ\rb*, \rb Seth|שֵׁ֗ת\rb* \rb lived|וַֽיְחִי־\rb* \rb 807|וּשְׁמֹנֶ֥ה\rb*\rb |מֵא֖וֹת\rb*\rb |שָׁנִ֔ים\rb*\rb |שֶׁ֣בַע\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָ֑ה\rb* \rb and had other|וַיּ֥וֹלֶד\rb* \rb sons|בָּנִ֖ים\rb* \rb and daughters|וּבָנֽוֹת׃\rb*. \v 8 \rb So Seth|שֵׁ֔ת\rb*\rb |שְׁתֵּ֤ים\rb* \rb lived|וַיִּֽהְיוּ֙\rb* \rb a total of|כָּל־\rb*\rb |יְמֵי־\rb* \rb 912|וּתְשַׁ֥ע\rb*\rb |מֵא֖וֹת\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֔ה\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵה֙\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָ֑ה\rb*, \rb and then he died|וַיָּמֹֽת׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 9 \rb When Enosh|אֱנ֖וֹשׁ\rb* \rb was|וַֽיְחִ֥י\rb* \rb 90|תִּשְׁעִ֣ים\rb* \rb years old|שָׁנָ֑ה\rb*, \rb he became the father of|וַיּ֖וֹלֶד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Kenan|קֵינָֽן׃\rb*. \v 10 \rb And after|אַֽחֲרֵי֙\rb* \rb he had become the father of|הוֹלִיד֣וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Kenan|קֵינָ֔ן\rb*, \rb Enosh|אֱנ֗וֹשׁ\rb* \rb lived|וַֽיְחִ֣י\rb* \rb 815|חֲמֵ֤שׁ\rb*\rb |וּשְׁמֹנֶ֥ה\rb*\rb |מֵא֖וֹת\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֔ה\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵה֙\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָ֑ה\rb* \rb and had other|וַיּ֥וֹלֶד\rb* \rb sons|בָּנִ֖ים\rb* \rb and daughters|וּבָנֽוֹת׃\rb*. \v 11 \rb So Enosh|אֱנ֔וֹשׁ\rb* \rb lived|וַיִּֽהְיוּ֙\rb* \rb a total of|כָּל־\rb*\rb |יְמֵ֣י\rb* \rb 905|וּתְשַׁ֥ע\rb*\rb |מֵא֖וֹת\rb*\rb |שָׁנִ֔ים\rb*\rb |חָמֵ֣שׁ\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָ֑ה\rb*, \rb and then he died|וַיָּמֹֽת׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 12 \rb When Kenan|קֵינָ֖ן\rb* \rb was|וַֽיְחִ֥י\rb* \rb 70|שִׁבְעִ֣ים\rb* \rb years old|שָׁנָ֑ה\rb*, \rb he became the father of|וַיּ֖וֹלֶד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Mahalalel|מַֽהֲלַלְאֵֽל׃\rb*. \v 13 \rb And after|אַחֲרֵי֙\rb* \rb he had become the father of|הוֹלִיד֣וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Mahalalel|מַֽהֲלַלְאֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb Kenan|קֵינָ֗ן\rb* \rb lived|וַיְחִ֣י\rb* \rb 840|וּשְׁמֹנֶ֥ה\rb*\rb |מֵא֖וֹת\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֔ה\rb*\rb |אַרְבָּעִ֣ים\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָ֑ה\rb* \rb and had other|וַיּ֥וֹלֶד\rb* \rb sons|בָּנִ֖ים\rb* \rb and daughters|וּבָנֽוֹת׃\rb*. \v 14 \rb So Kenan|קֵינָ֔ן\rb* \rb lived|וַיִּֽהְיוּ֙\rb* \rb a total of|כָּל־\rb*\rb |יְמֵ֣י\rb* \rb 910|וּתְשַׁ֥ע\rb*\rb |מֵא֖וֹת\rb*\rb |שָׁנִ֔ים\rb*\rb |עֶ֣שֶׂר\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָ֑ה\rb*, \rb and then he died|וַיָּמֹֽת׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 15 \rb When Mahalalel|מַֽהֲלַלְאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb was|וַֽיְחִ֣י\rb* \rb 65|וְשִׁשִּׁ֣ים\rb*\rb |שָׁנִ֖ים\rb*\rb |חָמֵ֥שׁ\rb* \rb years old|שָׁנָ֑ה\rb*, \rb he became the father of|וַיּ֖וֹלֶד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Jared|יָֽרֶד׃\rb*. \v 16 \rb And after|אַֽחֲרֵי֙\rb* \rb he had become the father of|הוֹלִיד֣וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Jared|יֶ֔רֶד\rb*, \rb Mahalalel|מַֽהֲלַלְאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb lived|וַֽיְחִ֣י\rb* \rb 830|וּשְׁמֹנֶ֥ה\rb*\rb |מֵא֖וֹת\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֔ה\rb*\rb |שְׁלֹשִׁ֣ים\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָ֑ה\rb* \rb and had other|וַיּ֥וֹלֶד\rb* \rb sons|בָּנִ֖ים\rb* \rb and daughters|וּבָנֽוֹת׃\rb*. \v 17 \rb So Mahalalel|מַהֲלַלְאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb lived|וַיִּהְיוּ֙\rb* \rb a total of|כָּל־\rb*\rb |יְמֵ֣י\rb* \rb 895|וּשְׁמֹנֶ֥ה\rb*\rb |מֵא֖וֹת\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֔ה\rb*\rb |וְתִשְׁעִים֙\rb*\rb |חָמֵ֤שׁ\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָ֑ה\rb*, \rb and then he died|וַיָּמֹֽת׃ס\rb*.
\s1 God Takes Up Enoch
\p \v 18 \rb When Jared|יֶ֕רֶד\rb* \rb was|וַֽיְחִי־\rb* \rb 162|וּמְאַ֣ת\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֖ה\rb*\rb |וְשִׁשִּׁ֛ים\rb*\rb |שְׁתַּ֧יִם\rb* \rb years old|שָׁנָ֑ה\rb*, \rb he became the father of|וַיּ֖וֹלֶד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Enoch|חֲנֽוֹךְ׃\rb*. \v 19 \rb And after|אַֽחֲרֵי֙\rb* \rb he had become the father of|הוֹלִיד֣וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Enoch|חֲנ֔וֹךְ\rb*, \rb Jared|יֶ֗רֶד\rb* \rb lived|וַֽיְחִי־\rb* \rb 800|שְׁמֹנֶ֥ה\rb*\rb |מֵא֖וֹת\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָ֑ה\rb* \rb and had other|וַיּ֥וֹלֶד\rb* \rb sons|בָּנִ֖ים\rb* \rb and daughters|וּבָנֽוֹת׃\rb*. \v 20 \rb So Jared|יֶ֔רֶד\rb* \rb lived|וַיִּֽהְיוּ֙\rb* \rb a total of|כָּל־\rb*\rb |יְמֵי־\rb* \rb 962|וּתְשַׁ֥ע\rb*\rb |מֵא֖וֹת\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֔ה\rb*\rb |וְשִׁשִּׁים֙\rb*\rb |שְׁתַּ֤יִם\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָ֑ה\rb*, \rb and then he died|וַיָּמֹֽת׃פ\rb*.
\p \v 21 \rb When Enoch|חֲנ֔וֹךְ\rb* \rb was|וַֽיְחִ֣י\rb* \rb 65|וְשִׁשִּׁ֖ים\rb*\rb |חָמֵ֥שׁ\rb* \rb years old|שָׁנָ֑ה\rb*, \rb he became the father of|וַיּ֖וֹלֶד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Methuselah|מְתוּשָֽׁלַח׃\rb*. \v 22 \rb And after|אַֽחֲרֵי֙\rb* \rb he had become the father of|הוֹלִיד֣וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Methuselah|מְתוּשֶׁ֔לַח\rb*, \rb Enoch|חֲנ֜וֹךְ\rb* \rb walked|וַיִּתְהַלֵּ֨ךְ\rb* \rb with|אֶת־\rb* \rb God|הָֽאֱלֹהִ֗ים\rb*\f + \fr 5:22 \ft LXX \fqa pleased God\ft ; also in verse 24\f* \rb 300|שְׁלֹ֥שׁ\rb*\rb |מֵא֖וֹת\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָ֑ה\rb* \rb and had other|וַיּ֥וֹלֶד\rb* \rb sons|בָּנִ֖ים\rb* \rb and daughters|וּבָנֽוֹת׃\rb*. \v 23 \rb So Enoch|חֲנ֑וֹךְ\rb* \rb lived|וַיְהִ֖י\rb* \rb a total of|כָּל־\rb*\rb |יְמֵ֣י\rb* \rb 365|וּשְׁלֹ֥שׁ\rb*\rb |מֵא֖וֹת\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֔ה\rb*\rb |וְשִׁשִּׁים֙\rb*\rb |חָמֵ֤שׁ\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 24 \rb Enoch|חֲנ֖וֹךְ\rb* \rb walked|וַיִּתְהַלֵּ֥ךְ\rb* \rb with|אֶת־\rb* \rb God|הָֽאֱלֹהִ֑ים\rb*, \rb and then he was no more|וְאֵינֶ֕נּוּ\rb*, \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִֽים׃פ\rb* \rb had taken him away|לָקַ֥ח\rb*\rb |אֹת֖וֹ\rb*.\f + \fr 5:24 \ft LXX \fqa and he was not found, because God had taken him away\ft ; cited in Hebrews 11:5\f*
\s1 From Methuselah to Noah
\p \v 25 \rb When Methuselah|מְתוּשֶׁ֔לַח\rb* \rb was|וַיְחִ֣י\rb* \rb 187|וּמְאַ֣ת\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֖ה\rb*\rb |וּשְׁמֹנִ֛ים\rb*\rb |שֶׁ֧בַע\rb* \rb years old|שָׁנָ֑ה\rb*, \rb he became the father of|וַיּ֖וֹלֶד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Lamech|לָֽמֶךְ׃\rb*. \v 26 \rb And after|אַֽחֲרֵי֙\rb* \rb he had become the father of|הוֹלִיד֣וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Lamech|לֶ֔מֶךְ\rb*, \rb Methuselah|מְתוּשֶׁ֗לַח\rb* \rb lived|וַֽיְחִ֣י\rb* \rb 782|וּשְׁבַ֥ע\rb*\rb |מֵא֖וֹת\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֔ה\rb*\rb |וּשְׁמוֹנִים֙\rb*\rb |שְׁתַּ֤יִם\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָ֑ה\rb* \rb and had other|וַיּ֥וֹלֶד\rb* \rb sons|בָּנִ֖ים\rb* \rb and daughters|וּבָנֽוֹת׃\rb*. \v 27 \rb So Methuselah|מְתוּשֶׁ֔לַח\rb* \rb lived|וַיִּהְיוּ֙\rb* \rb a total of|כָּל־\rb*\rb |יְמֵ֣י\rb* \rb 969|תֵּ֤שַׁע\rb*\rb |מֵא֖וֹת\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֔ה\rb*\rb |וְשִׁשִּׁים֙\rb*\rb |וּתְשַׁ֥ע\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָ֑ה\rb*, \rb and then he died|וַיָּמֹֽת׃פ\rb*.
\p \v 28 \rb When Lamech|לֶ֕מֶךְ\rb* \rb was|וַֽיְחִי־\rb* \rb 182|וּמְאַ֣ת\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֖ה\rb*\rb |וּשְׁמֹנִ֛ים\rb*\rb |שְׁתַּ֧יִם\rb* \rb years old|שָׁנָ֑ה\rb*, \rb he had|וַיּ֖וֹלֶד\rb* \rb a son|בֵּֽן׃\rb*. \v 29 \rb And he named him|וַיִּקְרָ֧א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |שְׁמ֛וֹ\rb* \rb Noah|נֹ֖חַ\rb*,\f + \fr 5:29 \fqa Noah \ft sounds like the Hebrew for \fqa rest \ft or \fqa comfort\ft .\f* \rb saying|לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*, “\rb May this one|זֶ֠ה\rb* \rb comfort us|יְנַחֲמֵ֤נוּ\rb* \rb in the labor|מִֽמַּעֲשֵׂ֙נוּ֙\rb* \rb and toil|וּמֵעִצְּב֣וֹן\rb* \rb of our hands|יָדֵ֔ינוּ\rb* \rb caused by|מִן־\rb* \rb the ground|הָ֣אֲדָמָ֔ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb has cursed|אֵֽרְרָ֖הּ\rb*.” \v 30 \rb And after|אַֽחֲרֵי֙\rb* \rb he had become the father of|הוֹלִיד֣וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Noah|נֹ֔חַ\rb*, \rb Lamech|לֶ֗מֶךְ\rb* \rb lived|וַֽיְחִי־\rb* \rb 595|חָמֵ֤שׁ\rb*\rb |מֵאֹ֖ת\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֔ה\rb*\rb |וְתִשְׁעִים֙\rb*\rb |וַחֲמֵ֥שׁ\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָ֑ה\rb* \rb and had other|וַיּ֥וֹלֶד\rb* \rb sons|בָּנִ֖ים\rb* \rb and daughters|וּבָנֽוֹת׃\rb*. \v 31 \rb So Lamech|לֶ֔מֶךְ\rb* \rb lived|וַֽיְהִי֙\rb* \rb a total of|כָּל־\rb*\rb |יְמֵי־\rb* \rb 777|שֶׁ֤בַע\rb*\rb |מֵא֖וֹת\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֔ה\rb*\rb |וְשִׁבְעִים֙\rb*\rb |וּשְׁבַ֥ע\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָ֑ה\rb*, \rb and then he died|וַיָּמֹֽת׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 32 \rb After|אֶת־\rb* \rb Noah|נֹ֕חַ\rb* \rb was|וַֽיְהִי־\rb* \rb 500|חֲמֵ֥שׁ\rb*\rb |מֵא֖וֹת\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָ֑ה\rb* \rb old|בֶּן־\rb*, \rb he|נֹ֔חַ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb became the father of|וַיּ֣וֹלֶד\rb* \rb Shem|שֵׁ֖ם\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Ham|חָ֥ם\rb*, \rb and Japheth|יָֽפֶת׃\rb*.
\c 6
\s1 Corruption on the Earth
\p \v 1 \rb Now|וַֽיְהִי֙\rb* \rb when|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb men|הָֽאָדָ֔ם\rb* \rb began|הֵחֵ֣ל\rb* \rb to multiply|לָרֹ֖ב\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the face|פְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the earth|הָֽאֲדָמָ֑ה\rb* \rb and daughters|וּבָנ֖וֹת\rb* \rb were born|יֻלְּד֥וּ\rb* \rb to them|לָהֶֽם׃\rb*, \v 2 \rb the sons|בְנֵי־\rb* \rb of God|הָֽאֱלֹהִים֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb saw|וַיִּרְא֤וּ\rb* \rb that|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb the daughters|בְּנ֣וֹת\rb* \rb of men|הָֽאָדָ֔ם\rb*\rb |הֵ֑נָּה\rb* \rb were beautiful|טֹבֹ֖ת\rb*, \rb and they took|וַיִּקְח֤וּ\rb*\rb |לָהֶם֙\rb* \rb as wives|נָשִׁ֔ים\rb*\rb |מִכֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb whomever|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb they chose|בָּחָֽרוּ׃\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb So the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb My Spirit|רוּחִ֤י\rb* \rb will not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb contend|יָד֨וֹן\rb* \rb with man|בָֽאָדָם֙\rb* \rb forever|לְעֹלָ֔ם\rb*,\f + \fr 6:3 \ft LXX and Syriac \fqa My Spirit will not remain in man forever\f* \rb for|בְּשַׁגַּ֖ם\rb* \rb he is|ה֣וּא\rb* \rb mortal|בָשָׂ֑ר\rb*; \rb his days|יָמָ֔יו\rb* \rb shall be|וְהָי֣וּ\rb* \rb 120|מֵאָ֥ה\rb*\rb |וְעֶשְׂרִ֖ים\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָֽה׃\rb*.”
\p \v 4 \rb The Nephilim|הַנְּפִלִ֞ים\rb* \rb were|הָי֣וּ\rb* \rb on the earth|בָאָרֶץ֮\rb* \rb in those days|בַּיָּמִ֣ים\rb*—\rb |הָהֵם֒\rb* \rb and|וְגַ֣ם\rb* \rb afterward as well|אַֽחֲרֵי־\rb*\rb |כֵ֗ן\rb*— \rb when|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the sons|בְּנֵ֤י\rb* \rb of God|הָֽאֱלֹהִים֙\rb* \rb had relations with|יָבֹ֜אוּ\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the daughters|בְּנ֣וֹת\rb* \rb of men|הָֽאָדָ֔ם\rb*. \rb And they bore|וְיָלְד֖וּ\rb* \rb them|לָהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb children who|הֵ֧מָּה\rb* \rb became the mighty men|הַגִּבֹּרִ֛ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb of old|מֵעוֹלָ֖ם\rb*, \rb men|אַנְשֵׁ֥י\rb* \rb of renown|הַשֵּֽׁם׃פ\rb*.
\p \v 5 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb saw|וַיַּ֣רְא\rb* \rb that|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb the wickedness|רָעַ֥ת\rb* \rb of man|הָאָדָ֖ם\rb* \rb was great|רַבָּ֛ה\rb* \rb upon the earth|בָּאָ֑רֶץ\rb*, \rb and that every|וְכָל־\rb* \rb inclination|יֵ֙צֶר֙\rb* \rb of the thoughts|מַחְשְׁבֹ֣ת\rb* \rb of his heart|לִבּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb was altogether|רַ֥ק\rb* \rb evil|רַ֖ע\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the time|הַיּֽוֹם׃\rb*. \v 6 \rb And the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb regretted|וַיִּנָּ֣חֶם\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb He had made|עָשָׂ֥ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb man|הָֽאָדָ֖ם\rb* \rb on the earth|בָּאָ֑רֶץ\rb*, \rb and He was grieved|וַיִּתְעַצֵּ֖ב\rb* \rb in|אֶל־\rb* \rb His heart|לִבּֽוֹ׃\rb*. \v 7 \rb So the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb I will blot out|אֶמְחֶ֨ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb man|הָאָדָ֤ם\rb*, \rb whom|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I have created|בָּרָ֙אתִי֙\rb*, \rb from|מֵעַל֙\rb* \rb the face|פְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the earth|הָֽאֲדָמָ֔ה\rb* — \rb every man|מֵֽאָדָם֙\rb*\rb |עַד־\rb* \rb and|עַד־\rb* \rb beast|בְּהֵמָ֔ה\rb* \rb and|וְעַד־\rb* \rb crawling creature|רֶ֖מֶשׂ\rb* \rb and bird|ע֣וֹף\rb* \rb of the air|הַשָּׁמָ֑יִם\rb* — \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb I am grieved|נִחַ֖מְתִּי\rb* \rb that|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb I have made them|עֲשִׂיתִֽם׃\rb*.”
\s1 Noah’s Favor with God
\p \v 8 \rb Noah, however,|וְנֹ֕חַ\rb* \rb found|מָ֥צָא\rb* \rb favor|חֵ֖ן\rb* \rb in the eyes|בְּעֵינֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃פ\rb*.
\p \v 9 \rb This is|אֵ֚לֶּה\rb* \rb the account|תּוֹלְדֹ֣ת\rb* \rb of Noah|נֹ֔חַ\rb*. \rb Noah|נֹ֗חַ\rb*\rb |אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb was|הָיָ֖ה\rb* \rb a righteous man|צַדִּ֛יק\rb*, \rb blameless|תָּמִ֥ים\rb* \rb in his generation|בְּדֹֽרֹתָ֑יו\rb*; \rb Noah|נֹֽחַ׃\rb* \rb walked|הִֽתְהַלֶּךְ־\rb* \rb with|אֶת־\rb* \rb God|הָֽאֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb*. \v 10 \rb And|אֶת־\rb* \rb Noah|נֹ֖חַ\rb* \rb had|וַיּ֥וֹלֶד\rb* \rb three|שְׁלֹשָׁ֣ה\rb* \rb sons|בָנִ֑ים\rb*:\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Shem|שֵׁ֖ם\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Ham|חָ֥ם\rb*, \rb and Japheth|יָֽפֶת׃\rb*.
\p \v 11 \rb Now the earth|הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb was corrupt|וַתִּשָּׁחֵ֥ת\rb* \rb in the sight|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of God|הָֽאֱלֹהִ֑ים\rb*, \rb and|הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb full|וַתִּמָּלֵ֥א\rb* \rb of violence|חָמָֽס׃\rb*. \v 12 \rb And God|אֱלֹהִ֛ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb looked|וַיַּ֧רְא\rb* \rb upon the earth|הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb and saw that|וְהִנֵּ֣ה\rb* \rb it was corrupt|נִשְׁחָ֑תָה\rb*; \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb living creatures|בָּשָׂ֛ר\rb*\f + \fr 6:12 \ft Literally \fqa all flesh\ft ; similarly in verses 13, 17, and 19\f*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the earth|הָאָֽרֶץ׃ס\rb* \rb had corrupted|הִשְׁחִ֧ית\rb* \rb their ways|דַּרְכּ֖וֹ\rb*.
\s1 Preparing the Ark
\p \v 13 \rb Then God|אֱלֹהִ֜ים\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to Noah|לְנֹ֗חַ\rb*, “\rb The end|קֵ֤ץ\rb* \rb of all|כָּל־\rb* \rb living creatures|בָּשָׂר֙\rb* \rb has come|בָּ֣א\rb* \rb before Me|לְפָנַ֔י\rb*, \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb through them|מִפְּנֵיהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb the earth|הָאָ֛רֶץ\rb* \rb is full of|מָלְאָ֥ה\rb* \rb violence|חָמָ֖ס\rb*. \rb Now behold|וְהִנְנִ֥י\rb*, \rb I will destroy both them|מַשְׁחִיתָ֖ם\rb* \rb and|אֶת־\rb* \rb the earth|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb*.
\p \v 14 \rb Make|עֲשֵׂ֤ה\rb* \rb for yourself|לְךָ֙\rb* \rb an ark|תֵּבַ֣ת\rb* \rb of gopher|גֹ֔פֶר\rb* \rb wood|עֲצֵי־\rb*;\f + \fr 6:14 \fqa Gopher \ft is an unknown kind of tree; possibly \fqa cypress \ft or \fqa cedar\ft .\f* \rb make|תַּֽעֲשֶׂ֣ה\rb* \rb rooms|קִנִּ֖ים\rb* \rb in|אֶת־\rb* \rb the ark|הַתֵּבָ֑ה\rb* \rb and coat|וְכָֽפַרְתָּ֥\rb* \rb it|אֹתָ֛הּ\rb* \rb with pitch|בַּכֹּֽפֶר׃\rb* \rb inside|מִבַּ֥יִת\rb* \rb and out|וּמִח֖וּץ\rb*. \v 15 \rb And this|וְזֶ֕ה\rb* \rb is how|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you are to build|תַּֽעֲשֶׂ֖ה\rb* \rb it|אֹתָ֑הּ\rb*: \rb The ark|הַתֵּבָ֔ה\rb* \rb is to be 300|שְׁלֹ֧שׁ\rb*\rb |מֵא֣וֹת\rb* \rb cubits|אַמָּ֗ה\rb* \rb long|אֹ֚רֶךְ\rb*, \rb 50|חֲמִשִּׁ֤ים\rb* \rb cubits|אַמָּה֙\rb* \rb wide|רָחְבָּ֔הּ\rb*, \rb and 30|וּשְׁלֹשִׁ֥ים\rb* \rb cubits|אַמָּ֖ה\rb* \rb high|קוֹמָתָֽהּ׃\rb*.\f + \fr 6:15 \ft The ark was approximately 450 feet long, 75 feet wide, and 45 feet high (137.2 meters long, 22.9 meters wide, and 13.7 meters high).\f* \v 16 \rb You are to make|תַּֽעֲשֶׂ֣ה\rb* \rb a roof|צֹ֣הַר׀\rb*\f + \fr 6:16 \ft Or \fqa skylight \ft or \fqa window\f* \rb for the ark|לַתֵּבָ֗ה\rb*,\rb |וְאֶל־\rb* \rb finish its walls|תְּכַלֶ֣נָּה\rb* \rb a cubit|אַמָּה֙\rb* \rb from the top|מִלְמַ֔עְלָה\rb*,\f + \fr 6:16 \fqa A cubit \ft is approximately 18 inches or 45.7 centimeters.\f* \rb place|תָּשִׂ֑ים\rb* \rb a door|וּפֶ֥תַח\rb* \rb in the side|בְּצִדָּ֣הּ\rb* \rb of the ark|הַתֵּבָ֖ה\rb*, \rb and build|תַּֽעֲשֶֽׂהָ׃\rb* \rb lower|תַּחְתִּיִּ֛ם\rb*, \rb middle|שְׁנִיִּ֥ם\rb*, \rb and upper decks|וּשְׁלִשִׁ֖ים\rb*.
\p \v 17 \rb And|וַאֲנִ֗י\rb* \rb behold|הִנְנִי֩\rb*, \rb I will bring|מֵבִ֨יא\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb floodwaters|הַמַּבּ֥וּל\rb*\rb |מַ֙יִם֙\rb* \rb upon|עַל־\rb* \rb the earth|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb to destroy|לְשַׁחֵ֣ת\rb* \rb every|כָּל־\rb* \rb creature|בָּשָׂ֗ר\rb* \rb under|מִתַּ֖חַת\rb* \rb the heavens|הַשָּׁמָ֑יִם\rb* \rb that has|אֲשֶׁר־\rb*\rb |בּוֹ֙\rb* \rb the breath|ר֣וּחַ\rb* \rb of life|חַיִּ֔ים\rb*. \rb Everything|כֹּ֥ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb on the earth|בָּאָ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb will perish|יִגְוָֽע׃\rb*. \v 18 \rb But I will establish|וַהֲקִמֹתִ֥י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My covenant|בְּרִיתִ֖י\rb* \rb with you|אִתָּ֑ךְ\rb*, \rb and you will enter|וּבָאתָ֙\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the ark|הַתֵּבָ֔ה\rb* — \rb you|אַתָּ֕ה\rb* \rb and your sons|וּבָנֶ֛יךָ\rb* \rb and your wife|וְאִשְׁתְּךָ֥\rb* \rb and your sons’|בָנֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb wives|וּנְשֵֽׁי־\rb* \rb with you|אִתָּֽךְ׃\rb*.
\p \v 19 \rb And|וּמִכָּל־\rb* \rb you are to bring|תָּבִ֥יא\rb* \rb two|שְׁנַ֧יִם\rb* \rb of every|מִכֹּ֛ל\rb* \rb living|הָ֠חַי\rb*\rb |מִֽכָּל־\rb* \rb creature|בָּשָׂ֞ר\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb the ark|הַתֵּבָ֖ה\rb* — \rb male|זָכָ֥ר\rb* \rb and female|וּנְקֵבָ֖ה\rb*\rb |יִֽהְיֽוּ׃\rb* — \rb to keep them alive|לְהַחֲיֹ֣ת\rb* \rb with you|אִתָּ֑ךְ\rb*. \v 20 \rb Two|שְׁנַ֧יִם\rb* \rb of every kind|מִכֹּ֛ל\rb* \rb of|וּמִן־\rb* \rb bird|מֵהָע֣וֹף\rb*\rb |לְמִינֵ֗הוּ\rb* \rb and animal|הַבְּהֵמָה֙\rb*\rb |לְמִינָ֔הּ\rb* \rb and|מִכֹּ֛ל\rb* \rb crawling creature|רֶ֥מֶשׂ\rb*\rb |הָֽאֲדָמָ֖ה\rb*\rb |לְמִינֵ֑הוּ\rb* \rb will come|יָבֹ֥אוּ\rb* \rb to you|אֵלֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb to be kept alive|לְהַֽחֲיֽוֹת׃\rb*. \v 21 \rb You are also|וְאַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb to take|קַח־\rb* \rb for yourself|לְךָ֗\rb* \rb every kind|מִכָּל־\rb* \rb of food|מַֽאֲכָל֙\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb is eaten|יֵֽאָכֵ֔ל\rb* \rb and gather it|וְאָסַפְתָּ֖\rb*\rb |וְהָיָ֥ה\rb* \rb as food|לְאָכְלָֽה׃\rb* \rb for yourselves|אֵלֶ֑יךָ\rb* \rb and for|לְךָ֛\rb* \rb the animals|וְלָהֶ֖ם\rb*.”
\p \v 22 \rb So Noah|נֹ֑חַ\rb* \rb did|וַיַּ֖עַשׂ\rb* \rb everything|כְּ֠כֹל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb precisely as|כֵּ֥ן\rb*\rb |עָשָֽׂה׃ס\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb had commanded|צִוָּ֥ה\rb* \rb him|אֹת֛וֹ\rb*.
\c 7
\s1 The Great Flood
\p \v 1 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to Noah|לְנֹ֔חַ\rb*, “\rb Go|בֹּֽא־\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb the ark|הַתֵּבָ֑ה\rb*, \rb you|אַתָּ֥ה\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb your family|בֵּיתְךָ֖\rb*, \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I have found|רָאִ֛יתִי\rb* \rb you|אֹתְךָ֥\rb* \rb righteous|צַדִּ֥יק\rb*\rb |לְפָנַ֖י\rb* \rb in this|הַזֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb generation|בַּדּ֥וֹר\rb*. \v 2 \rb You|לְךָ֛\rb* \rb are to take with you|תִּֽקַּח־\rb* \rb seven pairs of|שִׁבְעָ֥ה\rb*\rb |שִׁבְעָ֖ה\rb*\f + \fr 7:2 \ft Or \fqa by sevens\ft ; also in verse 3\f* \rb every kind of|מִכֹּ֣ל׀\rb* \rb clean|הַטְּהוֹרָ֗ה\rb* \rb animal|הַבְּהֵמָ֣ה\rb*, \rb a male|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb and its mate|וְאִשְׁתּ֑וֹ\rb*;\rb |הִ֛וא\rb* \rb a pair|שְׁנַ֖יִם\rb* \rb of|וּמִן־\rb* \rb every kind of|אֲ֠שֶׁר\rb*\rb |לֹ֣א\rb* \rb unclean|טְהֹרָ֥ה\rb* \rb animal|הַבְּהֵמָ֡ה\rb*, \rb a male|אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb and its mate|וְאִשְׁתּֽוֹ׃\rb*; \v 3 \rb and|גַּ֣ם\rb* \rb seven pairs|שִׁבְעָ֖ה\rb* \rb of every kind of bird|מֵע֧וֹף\rb* \rb of the air|הַשָּׁמַ֛יִם\rb*,\rb |שִׁבְעָ֥ה\rb* \rb male|זָכָ֣ר\rb* \rb and female|וּנְקֵבָ֑ה\rb*, \rb to preserve|לְחַיּ֥וֹת\rb* \rb their offspring|זֶ֖רַע\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the face|פְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of all|כָל־\rb* \rb the earth|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb*. \v 4 \rb For|כִּי֩\rb* \rb seven|שִׁבְעָ֗ה\rb* \rb days|לְיָמִ֨ים\rb* \rb from now|ע֜וֹד\rb* \rb I|אָֽנֹכִי֙\rb* \rb will send rain|מַמְטִ֣יר\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the earth|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb for forty|אַרְבָּעִ֣ים\rb* \rb days|י֔וֹם\rb* \rb and forty|וְאַרְבָּעִ֖ים\rb* \rb nights|לָ֑יְלָה\rb*, \rb and I will wipe|וּמָחִ֗יתִי\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb from|מֵעַ֖ל\rb* \rb the face|פְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the earth|הָֽאֲדָמָֽה׃\rb* \rb every|כָּל־\rb* \rb living thing|הַיְקוּם֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb I have made|עָשִׂ֔יתִי\rb*.”
\p \v 5 \rb And Noah|נֹ֑חַ\rb* \rb did|וַיַּ֖עַשׂ\rb* \rb all|כְּכֹ֥ל\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb had commanded him|צִוָּ֖הוּ\rb*.
\p \v 6 \rb Now Noah|וְנֹ֕חַ\rb* \rb was 600|שֵׁ֥שׁ\rb*\rb |מֵא֖וֹת\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָ֑ה\rb* \rb old|בֶּן־\rb* \rb when the floodwaters|וְהַמַּבּ֣וּל\rb*\rb |מַ֖יִם\rb* \rb came|הָיָ֔ה\rb* \rb upon|עַל־\rb* \rb the earth|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb*. \v 7 \rb And Noah|נֹ֗חַ\rb* \rb and his wife|וְאִשְׁתּ֧וֹ\rb*, \rb with|אִתּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb his sons|וּ֠בָנָיו\rb* \rb and their|בָנָ֛יו\rb* \rb wives|וּנְשֵֽׁי־\rb*, \rb entered|וַיָּ֣בֹא\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the ark|הַתֵּבָ֑ה\rb* \rb to escape|מִפְּנֵ֖י\rb* \rb the waters|מֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the flood|הַמַּבּֽוּל׃\rb*. \v 8 \rb The|מִן־\rb* \rb clean|הַטְּהוֹרָ֔ה\rb*\rb |הַבְּהֵמָה֙\rb* \rb and|וּמִן־\rb*\rb |וּמִ֨ן־\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb*\rb |אֵינֶ֖נָּה\rb* \rb unclean|טְהֹרָ֑ה\rb* \rb animals|הַ֨בְּהֵמָ֔ה\rb*, \rb the birds|הָע֔וֹף\rb*, \rb and everything|וְכֹ֥ל\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb crawls|רֹמֵ֖שׂ\rb* \rb along|עַל־\rb* \rb the ground|הָֽאֲדָמָֽה׃\rb* \v 9 \rb came|בָּ֧אוּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Noah|נֹ֛חַ\rb* \rb to enter|אֶל־\rb* \rb the ark|הַתֵּבָ֖ה\rb*, \rb two|שְׁנַ֨יִם\rb* \rb by two|שְׁנַ֜יִם\rb*, \rb male|זָכָ֣ר\rb* \rb and female|וּנְקֵבָ֑ה\rb*, \rb as|כַּֽאֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb had commanded|צִוָּ֥ה\rb* \rb Noah|נֹֽחַ׃\rb*.
\p \v 10 \rb And after|וַֽיְהִ֖י\rb* \rb seven|לְשִׁבְעַ֣ת\rb* \rb days|הַיָּמִ֑ים\rb* \rb the floodwaters|וּמֵ֣י\rb*\rb |הַמַּבּ֔וּל\rb* \rb came|הָי֖וּ\rb* \rb upon|עַל־\rb* \rb the earth|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb*. \v 11 \rb In|בִּשְׁנַ֨ת\rb* \rb the six|שֵׁשׁ־\rb* \rb hundredth|מֵא֤וֹת\rb* \rb year|שָׁנָה֙\rb* \rb of Noah’s|נֹ֔חַ\rb* \rb life|לְחַיֵּי־\rb*, \rb on the seventeenth|בְּשִׁבְעָֽה־\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֥ר\rb* \rb day|י֖וֹם\rb*\rb |לַחֹ֑דֶשׁ\rb* \rb of the second|הַשֵּׁנִ֔י\rb* \rb month|בַּחֹ֙דֶשׁ֙\rb*,\rb |הַזֶּ֗ה\rb*\rb |בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb all|כָּֽל־\rb* \rb the fountains|מַעְיְנֹת֙\rb* \rb of the great|רַבָּ֔ה\rb* \rb deep|תְּה֣וֹם\rb* \rb burst forth|נִבְקְעוּ֙\rb*, \rb and the floodgates|וַאֲרֻבֹּ֥ת\rb* \rb of the heavens|הַשָּׁמַ֖יִם\rb* \rb were opened|נִפְתָּֽחוּ׃\rb*. \v 12 \rb And the rain|הַגֶּ֖שֶׁם\rb* \rb fell|וַֽיְהִ֥י\rb* \rb upon|עַל־\rb* \rb the earth|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb* \rb for forty|אַרְבָּעִ֣ים\rb* \rb days|י֔וֹם\rb* \rb and forty|וְאַרְבָּעִ֖ים\rb* \rb nights|לָֽיְלָה׃\rb*.
\p \v 13 \rb On that very|בְּעֶ֨צֶם\rb* \rb day|הַיּ֤וֹם\rb*\rb |הַזֶּה֙\rb* \rb Noah|נֹ֔חַ\rb* \rb entered|בָּ֣א\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the ark|הַתֵּבָֽה׃\rb*, \rb along with his sons|בְּנֵי־\rb*\rb |נֹ֑חַ\rb* \rb Shem|וְשֵׁם־\rb*, \rb Ham|וְחָ֥ם\rb*, \rb and Japheth|וָיֶ֖פֶת\rb*, \rb and his|נֹ֗חַ\rb* \rb wife|וְאֵ֣שֶׁת\rb*, \rb and the three|וּשְׁלֹ֧שֶׁת\rb* \rb wives|נְשֵֽׁי־\rb* \rb of his sons|בָנָ֛יו\rb*\rb |אִתָּ֖ם\rb* — \v 14 \rb they|הֵ֜מָּה\rb*\rb |וְכָל־\rb* \rb and|וְכָל־\rb* \rb every|וְכָל־\rb* \rb kind of|לְמִינָ֗הּ\rb* \rb wild animal|הַֽחַיָּ֣ה\rb*, \rb livestock|הַבְּהֵמָה֙\rb*\rb |לְמִינָ֔הּ\rb*, \rb crawling creature|הָרֶ֛מֶשׂ\rb*\rb |הָרֹמֵ֥שׂ\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb*\rb |הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb*\rb |לְמִינֵ֑הוּ\rb*,\rb |וְכָל־\rb*\rb |כָּל־\rb*\rb |לְמִינֵ֔הוּ\rb* \rb bird|הָע֣וֹף\rb*, \rb and|כֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb winged creature|צִפּ֥וֹר\rb*\rb |כָּנָֽף׃\rb*. \v 15 \rb They came|וַיָּבֹ֥אוּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Noah|נֹ֖חַ\rb* \rb to enter|אֶל־\rb* \rb the ark|הַתֵּבָ֑ה\rb*, \rb two|שְׁנַ֤יִם\rb* \rb by two|שְׁנַ֙יִם֙\rb* \rb of every|מִכָּל־\rb* \rb creature|הַבָּשָׂ֔ר\rb*\f + \fr 7:15 \ft Literally \fqa of all flesh\ft ; similarly in verses 16 and 21\f* \rb with|אֲשֶׁר־\rb*\rb |בּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb the breath|ר֥וּחַ\rb* \rb of life|חַיִּֽים׃\rb*. \v 16 \rb And they entered|וְהַבָּאִ֗ים\rb*\rb |בָּ֔אוּ\rb*, \rb the male|זָכָ֨ר\rb* \rb and female|וּנְקֵבָ֤ה\rb* \rb of every|מִכָּל־\rb* \rb living thing|בָּשָׂר֙\rb*, \rb as|כַּֽאֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֑ים\rb* \rb had commanded|צִוָּ֥ה\rb* \rb Noah|אֹת֖וֹ\rb*. \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*\rb |בַּֽעֲדֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb shut him in|וַיִּסְגֹּ֥ר\rb*.
\p \v 17 \rb For forty|אַרְבָּעִ֥ים\rb* \rb days|י֖וֹם\rb* \rb the flood|הַמַּבּ֛וּל\rb* \rb kept coming|וַֽיְהִ֧י\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the earth|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb*, \rb and the waters|הַמַּ֗יִם\rb* \rb rose|וַיִּרְבּ֣וּ\rb* \rb and lifted|וַיִּשְׂאוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the ark|הַתֵּבָ֔ה\rb*\rb |וַתָּ֖רָם\rb* \rb high above|מֵעַ֥ל\rb* \rb the earth|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb*. \v 18 \rb So the waters|הַמַּ֛יִם\rb* \rb continued to surge|וַיִּגְבְּר֥וּ\rb* \rb and rise|וַיִּרְבּ֥וּ\rb* \rb greatly|מְאֹ֖ד\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the earth|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb*, \rb and|וַתֵּ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb the ark|הַתֵּבָ֖ה\rb* \rb floated on|עַל־\rb* \rb the surface|פְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the waters|הַמָּֽיִם׃\rb*. \v 19 \rb Finally, the waters|וְהַמַּ֗יִם\rb* \rb completely|מְאֹ֥ד\rb*\rb |מְאֹ֖ד\rb* \rb prevailed|גָּֽבְר֛וּ\rb* \rb upon|עַל־\rb* \rb the earth|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb*, \rb so that all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the high|הַגְּבֹהִ֔ים\rb* \rb mountains|הֶֽהָרִים֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb under|תַּ֖חַת\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the heavens|הַשָּׁמָֽיִם׃\rb* \rb were covered|וַיְכֻסּ֗וּ\rb*.
\p \v 20 \rb The waters|הַמָּ֑יִם\rb* \rb rose|גָּבְר֖וּ\rb* \rb and covered|וַיְכֻסּ֖וּ\rb* \rb the mountaintops|הֶהָרִֽים׃\rb* \rb to a depth|מִלְמַ֔עְלָה\rb* \rb of fifteen|חֲמֵ֨שׁ\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵ֤ה\rb* \rb cubits|אַמָּה֙\rb*.\f + \fr 7:20 \fqa 15 cubits \ft is approximately 22.5 feet or 6.9 meters.\f* \v 21 \rb And every|כָּל־\rb* \rb living thing|בָּשָׂ֣ר׀\rb* \rb that moved|הָרֹמֵ֣שׂ\rb* \rb upon|עַל־\rb* \rb the earth|הָאָ֗רֶץ\rb* \rb perished|וַיִּגְוַ֞ע\rb* — \rb birds|בָּע֤וֹף\rb*, \rb livestock|וּבַבְּהֵמָה֙\rb*, \rb animals|וּבַ֣חַיָּ֔ה\rb*, \rb every|וּבְכָל־\rb* \rb creature that swarms|הַשֶּׁ֖רֶץ\rb*\rb |הַשֹּׁרֵ֣ץ\rb* \rb upon|עַל־\rb* \rb the earth|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb*, \rb and all|וְכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb mankind|הָאָדָֽם׃\rb*. \v 22 \rb Of all|מִכֹּ֛ל\rb* \rb that was|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb on dry land|בֶּחָֽרָבָ֖ה\rb*, \rb everything|כֹּ֡ל\rb* \rb that had|אֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb the breath|נִשְׁמַת־\rb* \rb of|ר֨וּחַ\rb* \rb life|חַיִּ֜ים\rb* \rb in its nostrils|בְּאַפָּ֗יו\rb* \rb died|מֵֽתוּ׃\rb*. \v 23 \rb And every|כָּל־\rb* \rb living thing|הַיְק֣וּם׀\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר׀\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the face|פְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the earth|הָֽאֲדָמָ֗ה\rb* \rb was destroyed|וַיִּ֜מַח\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* — \rb man|מֵאָדָ֤ם\rb* \rb and|עַד־\rb*\rb |עַד־\rb* \rb livestock|בְּהֵמָה֙\rb*\rb |וְעַד־\rb*, \rb crawling creatures|רֶ֙מֶשׂ֙\rb* \rb and birds|ע֣וֹף\rb* \rb of the air|הַשָּׁמַ֔יִם\rb*; \rb they were blotted out|וַיִּמָּח֖וּ\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the earth|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb*, \rb and only|אַךְ־\rb* \rb Noah|נֹ֛חַ\rb* \rb and those|וַֽאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb with him|אִתּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb in the ark|בַּתֵּבָֽה׃\rb* \rb remained|וַיִשָּׁ֧אֶר\rb*.
