\s1 The Ark Rests on Ararat
\p \v 1 \rb But|אֶת־\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִים֙\rb* \rb remembered|וַיִּזְכֹּ֤ר\rb* \rb Noah|נֹ֔חַ\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֤ת\rb* \rb and all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the animals|הַֽחַיָּה֙\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb*\rb |כָּל־\rb* \rb livestock|הַבְּהֵמָ֔ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb were with him|אִתּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb in the ark|בַּתֵּבָ֑ה\rb*. \rb And God|אֱלֹהִ֥ים\rb* \rb sent a wind|ר֙וּחַ֙\rb*\rb |וַיַּעֲבֵ֨ר\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb the earth|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb*, \rb and the waters|הַמָּֽיִם׃\rb* \rb began to subside|וַיָּשֹׁ֖כּוּ\rb*. \v 2 \rb The springs|מַעְיְנֹ֣ת\rb* \rb of the deep|תְּה֔וֹם\rb* \rb and the floodgates|וַֽאֲרֻבֹּ֖ת\rb* \rb of the heavens|הַשָּׁמָ֑יִם\rb* \rb were closed|וַיִּסָּֽכְרוּ֙\rb*, \rb and the rain|הַגֶּ֖שֶׁם\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the sky|הַשָּׁמָֽיִם׃\rb* \rb was restrained|וַיִּכָּלֵ֥א\rb*. \v 3 \rb The waters|הַמַּ֛יִם\rb* \rb receded|וַיָּשֻׁ֧בוּ\rb* \rb steadily|הָל֣וֹךְ\rb*\rb |וָשׁ֑וֹב\rb* \rb from|מֵעַ֥ל\rb* \rb the earth|הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb*, \rb and after|מִקְצֵ֕ה\rb* \rb 150|וּמְאַ֖ת\rb*\rb |חֲמִשִּׁ֥ים\rb* \rb days|יֽוֹם׃\rb* \rb the waters|הַמַּ֔יִם\rb* \rb had gone down|וַיַּחְסְר֣וּ\rb*.
\p \v 4 \rb On the seventeenth|בְּשִׁבְעָה־\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֥ר\rb* \rb day|י֖וֹם\rb*\rb |לַחֹ֑דֶשׁ\rb* \rb of the seventh|הַשְּׁבִיעִ֔י\rb* \rb month|בַּחֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb*, \rb the ark|הַתֵּבָה֙\rb* \rb came to rest|וַתָּ֤נַח\rb* \rb on|עַ֖ל\rb* \rb the mountains|הָרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Ararat|אֲרָרָֽט׃\rb*. \v 5 \rb And the waters|וְהַמַּ֗יִם\rb*\rb |הָיוּ֙\rb* \rb continued|הָל֣וֹךְ\rb* \rb to recede|וְחָס֔וֹר\rb* \rb until|עַ֖ד\rb* \rb the tenth|הָֽעֲשִׂירִ֑י\rb* \rb month|הַחֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb*, \rb and on the first|בְּאֶחָ֣ד\rb* \rb day|לַחֹ֔דֶשׁ\rb* \rb of the tenth month|בָּֽעֲשִׂירִי֙\rb* \rb the tops|רָאשֵׁ֥י\rb* \rb of the mountains|הֶֽהָרִֽים׃\rb* \rb became visible|נִרְא֖וּ\rb*.
\s1 Noah Sends a Raven and a Dove
\p \v 6 \rb |וַֽיְהִ֕י\rb* \rb After|מִקֵּ֖ץ\rb* \rb forty|אַרְבָּעִ֣ים\rb* \rb days|י֑וֹם\rb* \rb Noah|נֹ֔חַ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb opened|וַיִּפְתַּ֣ח\rb* \rb the window|חַלּ֥וֹן\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb he had made|עָשָֽׂה׃\rb* \rb in the ark|הַתֵּבָ֖ה\rb* \v 7 \rb and sent out|וַיְשַׁלַּ֖ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb a raven|הָֽעֹרֵ֑ב\rb*. \rb It kept flying back and forth|וַיֵּצֵ֤א\rb*\rb |יָצוֹא֙\rb*\rb |וָשׁ֔וֹב\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb the waters|הַמַּ֖יִם\rb* \rb had dried up|יְבֹ֥שֶׁת\rb* \rb from|מֵעַ֥ל\rb* \rb the earth|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb*.
\p \v 8 \rb Then Noah sent out|וַיְשַׁלַּ֥ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |מֵאִתּ֑וֹ\rb*\f + \fr 8:8 \ft Literally \fqa sent out from him \ft or \fqa sent out from it\f* \rb a dove|הַיּוֹנָ֖ה\rb* \rb to see|לִרְאוֹת֙\rb* \rb if the waters|הַמַּ֔יִם\rb* \rb had receded|הֲקַ֣לּוּ\rb* \rb from|מֵעַ֖ל\rb* \rb the surface|פְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the ground|הָֽאֲדָמָֽה׃\rb*. \v 9 \rb But the dove|הַיּוֹנָ֨ה\rb* \rb found|מָצְאָה֩\rb* \rb no|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb place to rest|מָנ֜וֹחַ\rb* \rb her foot|לְכַף־\rb*\rb |רַגְלָ֗הּ\rb*, \rb and she returned|וַתָּ֤שָׁב\rb* \rb to him|אֵלָיו֙\rb* \rb in|אֶל־\rb* \rb the ark|הַתֵּבָ֔ה\rb*, \rb because|כִּי־\rb* \rb the waters|מַ֖יִם\rb* \rb were still covering|עַל־\rb* \rb the surface|פְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of all|כָל־\rb* \rb the earth|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb*. \rb So he reached out|וַיִּשְׁלַ֤ח\rb* \rb his hand|יָדוֹ֙\rb*\rb |וַיִּקָּחֶ֔הָ\rb* \rb and brought|וַיָּבֵ֥א\rb* \rb her|אֹתָ֛הּ\rb* \rb back|אֵלָ֖יו\rb* \rb inside|אֶל־\rb* \rb the ark|הַתֵּבָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 10 \rb Noah waited|וַיָּ֣חֶל\rb*\rb |ע֔וֹד\rb* \rb seven|שִׁבְעַ֥ת\rb* \rb more|אֲחֵרִ֑ים\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֖ים\rb* \rb and again|וַיֹּ֛סֶף\rb* \rb sent out|שַׁלַּ֥ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the dove|הַיּוֹנָ֖ה\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the ark|הַתֵּבָֽה׃\rb*. \v 11 \rb And behold|וְהִנֵּ֥ה\rb*, \rb the dove|הַיּוֹנָה֙\rb* \rb returned|וַתָּבֹ֨א\rb* \rb to him|אֵלָ֤יו\rb* \rb in the evening|לְעֵ֣ת\rb*\rb |עֶ֔רֶב\rb* \rb with a freshly plucked|טָרָ֣ף\rb* \rb olive|זַ֖יִת\rb* \rb leaf|עֲלֵה־\rb* \rb in her beak|בְּפִ֑יהָ\rb*. \rb So Noah|נֹ֔חַ\rb* \rb knew|וַיֵּ֣דַע\rb* \rb that|כִּי־\rb* \rb the waters|הַמַּ֖יִם\rb* \rb had receded|קַ֥לּוּ\rb* \rb from|מֵעַ֥ל\rb* \rb the earth|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb*.
\p \v 12 \rb And Noah waited|וַיִּיָּ֣חֶל\rb*\rb |ע֔וֹד\rb* \rb seven|שִׁבְעַ֥ת\rb* \rb more|אֲחֵרִ֑ים\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֖ים\rb* \rb and sent out|וַיְשַׁלַּח֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the dove again|הַיּוֹנָ֔ה\rb*, \rb but this time|יָסְפָ֥ה\rb*\rb |עֽוֹד׃\rb*\rb |וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb she did not return|שׁוּב־\rb* \rb to him|אֵלָ֖יו\rb*.
\s1 Exiting the Ark
\p \v 13 \rb |וַֽ֠יְהִי\rb* \rb In Noah’s six|וְשֵׁשׁ־\rb* \rb hundred|מֵא֜וֹת\rb* \rb and first|בְּאַחַ֨ת\rb* \rb year|שָׁנָ֗ה\rb*, \rb on the first|בְּאֶחָ֣ד\rb* \rb day|לַחֹ֔דֶשׁ\rb* \rb of the first month|בָּֽרִאשׁוֹן֙\rb*, \rb the waters|הַמַּ֖יִם\rb* \rb had dried up|חָֽרְב֥וּ\rb* \rb from|מֵעַ֣ל\rb* \rb the earth|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb*. \rb So Noah|נֹ֙חַ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb removed|וַיָּ֤סַר\rb* \rb the covering|מִכְסֵ֣ה\rb* \rb from the ark|הַתֵּבָ֔ה\rb* \rb and saw|וַיַּ֕רְא\rb*\rb |וְהִנֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb that the surface|פְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the ground|הָֽאֲדָמָֽה׃\rb* \rb was dry|חָֽרְב֖וּ\rb*. \v 14 \rb By the twenty-seventh|בְּשִׁבְעָ֧ה\rb*\rb |וְעֶשְׂרִ֛ים\rb* \rb day|י֖וֹם\rb*\rb |לַחֹ֑דֶשׁ\rb* \rb of the second|הַשֵּׁנִ֔י\rb* \rb month|וּבַחֹ֙דֶשׁ֙\rb*, \rb the earth|הָאָֽרֶץ׃ס\rb* \rb was fully dry|יָבְשָׁ֖ה\rb*.
\p \v 15 \rb Then God|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb said|וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Noah|נֹ֥חַ\rb*,\rb |לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 16 “\rb Come out|צֵ֖א\rb* \rb of|מִן־\rb* \rb the ark|הַתֵּבָ֑ה\rb*, \rb you|אַתָּ֕ה\rb* \rb and your wife|וְאִשְׁתְּךָ֛\rb*, \rb along with|אִתָּֽךְ׃\rb* \rb your sons|וּבָנֶ֥יךָ\rb* \rb and their|בָנֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb wives|וּנְשֵֽׁי־\rb*. \v 17 \rb Bring out|הוֹצֵא\rb*\rb |אִתָּ֑ךְ\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the living creatures|הַחַיָּ֨ה\rb*\rb |מִכָּל־\rb*\rb |בָּשָׂ֗ר\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶֽׁר־\rb* \rb are with you|אִתְּךָ֜\rb*— \rb birds|בָּע֧וֹף\rb*, \rb livestock|וּבַבְּהֵמָ֛ה\rb*, \rb and everything|וּבְכָל־\rb*\rb |הָרֶ֛מֶשׂ\rb* \rb that crawls|הָרֹמֵ֥שׂ\rb* \rb upon|עַל־\rb* \rb the ground|הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb*— \rb so that they can spread out|וְשָֽׁרְצ֣וּ\rb* \rb over the earth|בָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb and be fruitful|וּפָר֥וּ\rb* \rb and multiply|וְרָב֖וּ\rb* \rb upon|עַל־\rb* \rb it|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 18 \rb So Noah|נֹ֑חַ\rb* \rb came out|וַיֵּ֖צֵא־\rb*, \rb along with|אִתּֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb his sons|וּבָנָ֛יו\rb* \rb and his wife|וְאִשְׁתּ֥וֹ\rb* \rb and his sons’|בָנָ֖יו\rb* \rb wives|וּנְשֵֽׁי־\rb*. \v 19 \rb Every|כָּל־\rb* \rb living creature|הַֽחַיָּ֗ה\rb*, \rb every|כָּל־\rb* \rb creeping thing|הָרֶ֙מֶשׂ֙\rb*, \rb and every|וְכָל־\rb* \rb bird|הָע֔וֹף\rb* — \rb everything|כֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb that moves|רוֹמֵ֣שׂ\rb* \rb upon|עַל־\rb* \rb the earth|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb* — \rb came out|יָצְא֖וּ\rb* \rb of|מִן־\rb* \rb the ark|הַתֵּבָֽה׃\rb*, \rb kind by kind|לְמִשְׁפְּחֹ֣תֵיהֶ֔ם\rb*.
\s1 Noah Builds an Altar
\p \v 20 \rb Then Noah|נֹ֛חַ\rb* \rb built|וַיִּ֥בֶן\rb* \rb an altar|מִזְבֵּ֖חַ\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָ֑ה\rb*. \rb And taking|וַיִּקַּ֞ח\rb* \rb from every kind|מִכֹּ֣ל׀\rb* \rb of clean|הַטְּהוֹרָ֗ה\rb* \rb animal|הַבְּהֵמָ֣ה\rb* \rb and|וּמִכֹּל֙\rb* \rb clean|הַטָּהֹ֔ר\rb* \rb bird|הָע֣וֹף\rb*, \rb he offered|וַיַּ֥עַל\rb* \rb burnt offerings|עֹלֹ֖ת\rb* \rb on the altar|בַּמִּזְבֵּֽחַ׃\rb*. \v 21 \rb When the LORD|יְהוָה֮\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb smelled|וַיָּ֣רַח\rb* \rb the pleasing|הַנִּיחֹחַ֒\rb* \rb aroma|רֵ֣יחַ\rb*, \rb He|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb in|אֶל־\rb* \rb His heart|לִבּ֗וֹ\rb*, “\rb Never again|לֹֽא־\rb*\rb |אֹ֠סִף\rb*\rb |ע֤וֹד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb will I curse|לְקַלֵּ֨ל\rb* \rb the ground|הָֽאֲדָמָה֙\rb* \rb because of|בַּעֲב֣וּר\rb* \rb man|הָֽאָדָ֔ם\rb*, \rb even though|כִּ֠י\rb* \rb every inclination|יֵ֣צֶר\rb* \rb of his|הָאָדָ֛ם\rb* \rb heart|לֵ֧ב\rb* \rb is evil|רַ֖ע\rb* \rb from his youth|מִנְּעֻרָ֑יו\rb*. \rb And never|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb again|אֹסִ֥ף\rb*\rb |ע֛וֹד\rb* \rb will I destroy|לְהַכּ֥וֹת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb living creatures|חַ֖י\rb* \rb as|כַּֽאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I have done|עָשִֽׂיתִי׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 22 \rb As long as|עֹ֖ד\rb*\rb |כָּל־\rb* \rb the earth|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb* \rb endures|יְמֵ֣י\rb*,
\q2 \rb seedtime|זֶ֡רַע\rb* \rb and harvest|וְ֠קָצִיר\rb*,
\q1 \rb cold|וְקֹ֨ר\rb* \rb and heat|וָחֹ֜ם\rb*,
\q2 \rb summer|וְקַ֧יִץ\rb* \rb and winter|וָחֹ֛רֶף\rb*,
\q1 \rb day|וְי֥וֹם\rb* \rb and night|וָלַ֖יְלָה\rb*
\q2 \rb shall never|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb cease|יִשְׁבֹּֽתוּ׃\rb*.”
\c 9
\s1 The Covenant of the Rainbow
\p \v 1 \rb And God|אֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb blessed|וַיְבָ֣רֶךְ\rb* \rb Noah|נֹ֖חַ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and his sons|בָּנָ֑יו\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֧אמֶר\rb* \rb to them|לָהֶ֛ם\rb*, “\rb Be fruitful|פְּר֥וּ\rb* \rb and multiply|וּרְב֖וּ\rb* \rb and fill|וּמִלְא֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the earth|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb*. \v 2 \rb The fear|וּמוֹרַאֲכֶ֤ם\rb* \rb and dread of you|וְחִתְּכֶם֙\rb* \rb will fall|יִֽהְיֶ֔ה\rb* \rb on|עַ֚ל\rb* \rb every|כָּל־\rb* \rb living creature|חַיַּ֣ת\rb* \rb on the earth|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb*,\rb |וְעַ֖ל\rb* \rb every|כָּל־\rb* \rb bird|ע֣וֹף\rb* \rb of the air|הַשָּׁמָ֑יִם\rb*, \rb every|בְּכֹל֩\rb* \rb creature that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb crawls|תִּרְמֹ֧שׂ\rb* \rb on the ground|הָֽאֲדָמָ֛ה\rb*, \rb and all|וּֽבְכָל־\rb* \rb the fish|דְּגֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the sea|הַיָּ֖ם\rb*. \rb They are delivered|נִתָּֽנוּ׃\rb* \rb into your hand|בְּיֶדְכֶ֥ם\rb*. \v 3 \rb Everything|כָּל־\rb* \rb that lives|חַ֔י\rb* \rb and moves|רֶ֙מֶשׂ֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb*\rb |הוּא־\rb* \rb will be|יִהְיֶ֖ה\rb* \rb food|לְאָכְלָ֑ה\rb* \rb for you|לָכֶ֥ם\rb*; \rb just as I gave you the green|כְּיֶ֣רֶק\rb* \rb plants|עֵ֔שֶׂב\rb*, \rb I now give|נָתַ֥תִּי\rb* \rb you|לָכֶ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all things|כֹּֽל׃\rb*. \v 4 \rb But|אַךְ־\rb* \rb you must not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb eat|תֹאכֵֽלוּ׃\rb* \rb meat|בָּשָׂ֕ר\rb* \rb with its lifeblood|בְּנַפְשׁ֥וֹ\rb* \rb still in it|דָמ֖וֹ\rb*. \v 5 \rb And surely|וְאַ֨ךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb I will require|אֶדְרֹ֔שׁ\rb*\rb |מִיַּ֥ד\rb* \rb the life of any|כָּל־\rb* \rb man|הָֽאָדָ֗ם\rb* \rb or beast|חַיָּ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶדְרְשֶׁ֑נּוּ\rb*\rb |וּמִיַּ֣ד\rb* \rb by whose hand|מִיַּד֙\rb* \rb your lifeblood is shed|לְנַפְשֹֽׁתֵיכֶם֙\rb*\rb |דִּמְכֶ֤ם\rb*. \rb I will demand an accounting|אֶדְרֹ֖שׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb from anyone|הָֽאָדָֽם׃\rb* \rb who takes the life|נֶ֥פֶשׁ\rb* \rb of his fellow man|אִ֣ישׁ\rb*\rb |אָחִ֔יו\rb*:
\b 
\q1 \v 6 \rb Whoever sheds|שֹׁפֵךְ֙\rb* \rb the blood|דַּ֣ם\rb* \rb of man|הָֽאָדָ֔ם\rb*,
\q2 \rb by man|בָּֽאָדָ֖ם\rb* \rb his blood|דָּמ֣וֹ\rb* \rb will be shed|יִשָּׁפֵ֑ךְ\rb*;
\q1 \rb for|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb in His own|אֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb* \rb image|בְּצֶ֣לֶם\rb*
\q2 \rb God has made|עָשָׂ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb mankind|הָאָדָֽם׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 7 \rb But as for you|וְאַתֶּ֖ם\rb*,
\q2 \rb be fruitful|פְּר֣וּ\rb* \rb and multiply|וּרְב֑וּ\rb*;
\q1 \rb spread out|שִׁרְצ֥וּ\rb* \rb across the earth|בָאָ֖רֶץ\rb*
\q2 \rb and multiply|וּרְבוּ־\rb* \rb upon it|בָֽהּ׃ס\rb*.”
\p \v 8 \rb Then God|אֱלֹהִים֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Noah|נֹ֔חַ\rb*\rb |וְאֶל־\rb* \rb and his sons|בָּנָ֥יו\rb* \rb with him|אִתּ֖וֹ\rb*,\rb |לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 9 “\rb Behold|הִנְנִ֥י\rb*, \rb I now|וַאֲנִ֕י\rb* \rb establish|מֵקִ֛ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My covenant|בְּרִיתִ֖י\rb* \rb with you|אִתְּכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb and your|וְאֶֽת־\rb* \rb descendants|זַרְעֲכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb after you|אַֽחֲרֵיכֶֽם׃\rb*, \v 10 \rb and with|וְאֵ֨ת\rb* \rb every|כָּל־\rb* \rb living|הַֽחַיָּה֙\rb* \rb creature|נֶ֤פֶשׁ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb was with you|אִתְּכֶ֔ם\rb* — \rb the birds|בָּע֧וֹף\rb*, \rb the livestock|בַּבְּהֵמָ֛ה\rb*, \rb and every|וּֽבְכָל־\rb* \rb beast|חַיַּ֥ת\rb* \rb of the earth|הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb*\rb |אִתְּכֶ֑ם\rb*— \rb every|מִכֹּל֙\rb* \rb living thing|חַיַּ֥ת\rb*\rb |הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb* \rb that came out|יֹצְאֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the ark|הַתֵּבָ֔ה\rb*\rb |לְכֹ֖ל\rb*. \v 11 \rb And I establish|וַהֲקִמֹתִ֤י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My covenant|בְּרִיתִי֙\rb* \rb with you|אִתְּכֶ֔ם\rb*: \rb Never|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb again|ע֖וֹד\rb* \rb will all|כָּל־\rb* \rb life|בָּשָׂ֛ר\rb* \rb be cut off|יִכָּרֵ֧ת\rb* \rb by the waters|מִמֵּ֣י\rb* \rb of a flood|הַמַּבּ֑וּל\rb*; \rb never|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb again|ע֛וֹד\rb* \rb will there be|יִהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb a flood|מַבּ֖וּל\rb* \rb to destroy|לְשַׁחֵ֥ת\rb* \rb the earth|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 12 \rb And God|אֱלֹהִ֗ים\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb This|זֹ֤את\rb* \rb is the sign|אֽוֹת־\rb* \rb of the covenant|הַבְּרִית֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb am making|נֹתֵ֗ן\rb* \rb between Me|בֵּינִי֙\rb* \rb and you|וּבֵ֣ינֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb and|וּבֵ֛ין\rb* \rb every|כָּל־\rb* \rb living|חַיָּ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb creature|נֶ֥פֶשׁ\rb* \rb with you|אִתְּכֶ֑ם\rb*, \rb a covenant for all generations|לְדֹרֹ֖ת\rb* \rb to come|עוֹלָֽם׃\rb*: \v 13 \rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb I have set|נָתַ֖תִּי\rb* \rb My rainbow|קַשְׁתִּ֕י\rb* \rb in the clouds|בֶּֽעָנָ֑ן\rb*, \rb and it will be|וְהָֽיְתָה֙\rb* \rb a sign|לְא֣וֹת\rb* \rb of the covenant|בְּרִ֔ית\rb* \rb between|בֵּינִ֖י\rb* \rb Me|וּבֵ֥ין\rb* \rb and the earth|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb*.
\p \v 14 \rb |וְהָיָ֕ה\rb* \rb Whenever I form|בְּעַֽנְנִ֥י\rb* \rb clouds|עָנָ֖ן\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb the earth|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb* \rb and the rainbow|הַקֶּ֖שֶׁת\rb* \rb appears|וְנִרְאֲתָ֥ה\rb* \rb in the clouds|בֶּעָנָֽן׃\rb*, \v 15 \rb I will remember|וְזָכַרְתִּ֣י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My covenant|בְּרִיתִ֗י\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb between Me|בֵּינִי֙\rb* \rb and you|וּבֵ֣ינֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb and|וּבֵ֛ין\rb* \rb every|כָּל־\rb* \rb living|חַיָּ֖ה\rb* \rb creature|נֶ֥פֶשׁ\rb* \rb of every|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb kind|בָּשָׂ֑ר\rb*. \rb Never|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb again|ע֤וֹד\rb* \rb will the waters|הַמַּ֙יִם֙\rb* \rb become|יִֽהְיֶ֨ה\rb* \rb a flood|לְמַבּ֔וּל\rb* \rb to destroy|לְשַׁחֵ֖ת\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb life|בָּשָֽׂר׃\rb*. \v 16 \rb And whenever the rainbow|הַקֶּ֖שֶׁת\rb* \rb appears|וְהָיְתָ֥ה\rb* \rb in the clouds|בֶּֽעָנָ֑ן\rb*, \rb I will see it|וּרְאִיתִ֗יהָ\rb* \rb and remember|לִזְכֹּר֙\rb* \rb the everlasting|עוֹלָ֔ם\rb* \rb covenant|בְּרִ֣ית\rb* \rb between|בֵּ֣ין\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb* \rb and|וּבֵין֙\rb* \rb every|כָּל־\rb* \rb living|חַיָּ֔ה\rb* \rb creature|נֶ֣פֶשׁ\rb* \rb of every|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb kind|בָּשָׂ֖ר\rb* \rb that is|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the earth|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 17 \rb So God|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Noah|נֹ֑חַ\rb*, “\rb This|זֹ֤את\rb* \rb is the sign|אֽוֹת־\rb* \rb of the covenant|הַבְּרִית֙\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb I have established|הֲקִמֹ֔תִי\rb* \rb between|בֵּינִ֕י\rb* \rb Me|וּבֵ֥ין\rb* \rb and every|כָּל־\rb* \rb creature|בָּשָׂ֖ר\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the earth|הָאָֽרֶץ׃פ\rb*.”
\s1 Noah’s Shame and Canaan’s Curse
\p \v 18 \rb The sons|בְנֵי־\rb* \rb of Noah|נֹ֗חַ\rb* \rb who came out|הַיֹּֽצְאִים֙\rb* \rb of|מִן־\rb* \rb the ark|הַתֵּבָ֔ה\rb* \rb were|וַיִּֽהְי֣וּ\rb* \rb Shem|שֵׁ֖ם\rb*, \rb Ham|וְחָ֣ם\rb*, \rb and Japheth|וָיָ֑פֶת\rb*. \rb And Ham|וְחָ֕ם\rb*\rb |ה֖וּא\rb* \rb was the father|אֲבִ֥י\rb* \rb of Canaan|כְנָֽעַן׃\rb*. \v 19 \rb These|אֵ֖לֶּה\rb* \rb three|שְׁלֹשָׁ֥ה\rb* \rb were the sons|בְּנֵי־\rb* \rb of Noah|נֹ֑חַ\rb*, \rb and from them|וּמֵאֵ֖לֶּה\rb* \rb the whole|כָל־\rb* \rb earth|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb* \rb was populated|נָֽפְצָ֥ה\rb*.
\p \v 20 \rb Now Noah|נֹ֖חַ\rb*, \rb a man|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb of the soil|הָֽאֲדָמָ֑ה\rb*, \rb proceeded|וַיָּ֥חֶל\rb*\f + \fr 9:20 \ft Or \fqa was the first\f* \rb to plant|וַיִּטַּ֖ע\rb* \rb a vineyard|כָּֽרֶם׃\rb*. \v 21 \rb But when he drank|וַיֵּ֥שְׁתְּ\rb* \rb some of|מִן־\rb* \rb its wine|הַיַּ֖יִן\rb*, \rb he became drunk|וַיִּשְׁכָּ֑ר\rb* \rb and uncovered himself|וַיִּתְגַּ֖ל\rb* \rb inside|בְּת֥וֹךְ\rb* \rb his tent|אָהֳלֹֽה׃\rb*. \v 22 \rb And Ham|חָ֚ם\rb*, \rb the father|אֲבִ֣י\rb* \rb of Canaan|כְנַ֔עַן\rb*,\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb saw|וַיַּ֗רְא\rb* \rb his father’s|אָבִ֑יו\rb* \rb nakedness|עֶרְוַ֣ת\rb* \rb and told|וַיַּגֵּ֥ד\rb* \rb his two|לִשְׁנֵֽי־\rb* \rb brothers|אֶחָ֖יו\rb* \rb outside|בַּחֽוּץ׃\rb*.
\p \v 23 \rb Then Shem|שֵׁ֨ם\rb* \rb and Japheth|וָיֶ֜פֶת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb took|וַיִּקַּח֩\rb* \rb a garment|הַשִּׂמְלָ֗ה\rb* \rb and placed|וַיָּשִׂ֙ימוּ֙\rb* \rb it across|עַל־\rb*\rb |שְׁנֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb their shoulders|שְׁכֶ֣ם\rb*, \rb and walking|וַיֵּֽלְכוּ֙\rb* \rb backward|אֲחֹ֣רַנִּ֔ית\rb*, \rb they covered|וַיְכַסּ֕וּ\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb their father’s|אֲבִיהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb nakedness|עֶרְוַ֣ת\rb*. \rb Their faces|וּפְנֵיהֶם֙\rb* \rb were turned away|אֲחֹ֣רַנִּ֔ית\rb* \rb so that they did not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb see|רָאֽוּ׃\rb* \rb their father’s|אֲבִיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb nakedness|וְעֶרְוַ֥ת\rb*.
\p \v 24 \rb When Noah|נֹ֖חַ\rb* \rb awoke|וַיִּ֥יקֶץ\rb* \rb from his drunkenness|מִיֵּינ֑וֹ\rb* \rb and learned|וַיֵּ֕דַע\rb*\rb |אֵ֛ת\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb his youngest|הַקָּטָֽן׃\rb* \rb son|בְּנ֥וֹ\rb* \rb had done|עָ֥שָׂה־\rb* \rb to him|ל֖וֹ\rb*, \v 25 \rb he said|וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb*,
\b 
\q1 “\rb Cursed be|אָר֣וּר\rb* \rb Canaan|כְּנָ֑עַן\rb*!
\q2 \rb A servant|עֶ֥בֶד\rb* \rb of servants|עֲבָדִ֖ים\rb*
\q2 \rb shall he be|יִֽהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb to his brothers|לְאֶחָֽיו׃\rb*.”
\s1 Shem’s Blessing and Noah’s Death
\p \v 26 \rb He also declared|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*:
\b 
\q1 “\rb Blessed|בָּר֥וּךְ\rb* \rb be the LORD|יְהֹוָ֖ה\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹ֣הֵי\rb* \rb of Shem|שֵׁ֑ם\rb*!
\q2 \rb May Canaan|כְנַ֖עַן\rb* \rb be|וִיהִ֥י\rb* \rb the servant|עֶ֥בֶד\rb* \rb of Shem|לָֽמוֹ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 27 \rb May God|אֱלֹהִים֙\rb* \rb expand the territory|יַ֤פְתְּ\rb* \rb of Japheth|לְיֶ֔פֶת\rb*;\f + \fr 9:27 \fqa Japheth \ft sounds like the Hebrew for \fqa expand\ft .\f*
\q2 \rb may he dwell|וְיִשְׁכֹּ֖ן\rb* \rb in the tents|בְּאָֽהֳלֵי־\rb* \rb of Shem|שֵׁ֑ם\rb*,
\q2 \rb and may Canaan|כְנַ֖עַן\rb* \rb be|וִיהִ֥י\rb* \rb his servant|עֶ֥בֶד\rb*\rb |לָֽמוֹ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 28 \rb After|אַחַ֣ר\rb* \rb the flood|הַמַּבּ֑וּל\rb*, \rb Noah|נֹ֖חַ\rb* \rb lived|וַֽיְחִי־\rb* \rb 350|שְׁלֹ֤שׁ\rb*\rb |מֵאוֹת֙\rb*\rb |וַֽחֲמִשִּׁ֖ים\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָֽה׃\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֔ה\rb*. \v 29 \rb So Noah|נֹ֔חַ\rb* \rb lived|יְמֵי־\rb* \rb a total of|וַיִּֽהְיוּ֙\rb*\rb |כָּל־\rb* \rb 950|תְּשַׁ֤ע\rb*\rb |מֵאוֹת֙\rb*\rb |וַחֲמִשִּׁ֖ים\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֑ה\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָ֔ה\rb*, \rb and then he died|וַיָּמֹֽת׃פ\rb*.
\c 10
\s1 The Table of Nations
\p \v 1 \rb This|וְאֵ֙לֶּה֙\rb* \rb is the account|תּוֹלְדֹ֣ת\rb* \rb of Noah’s|נֹ֔חַ\rb* \rb sons|בְּנֵי־\rb* \rb Shem|שֵׁ֖ם\rb*, \rb Ham|חָ֣ם\rb*, \rb and Japheth|וָיָ֑פֶת\rb*,\rb |וַיִּוָּלְד֥וּ\rb* \rb who also|לָהֶ֛ם\rb* \rb had sons|בָּנִ֖ים\rb* \rb after|אַחַ֥ר\rb* \rb the flood|הַמַּבּֽוּל׃\rb*.
\s2 The Japhethites
\p \v 2 \rb The sons|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Japheth|יֶ֔פֶת\rb*:
\p \rb Gomer|גֹּ֣מֶר\rb*, \rb Magog|וּמָג֔וֹג\rb*, \rb Madai|וּמָדַ֖י\rb*, \rb Javan|וְיָוָ֣ן\rb*, \rb Tubal|וְתֻבָ֑ל\rb*, \rb Meshech|וּמֶ֖שֶׁךְ\rb*, \rb and Tiras|וְתִירָֽס׃\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb The sons|וּבְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb of Gomer|גֹּ֑מֶר\rb*:
\p \rb Ashkenaz|אַשְׁכֲּנַ֥ז\rb*, \rb Riphath|וְרִיפַ֖ת\rb*, \rb and Togarmah|וְתֹגַרְמָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 4 \rb And the sons|וּבְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Javan|יָוָ֖ן\rb*:
\p \rb Elishah|אֱלִישָׁ֣ה\rb*, \rb Tarshish|וְתַרְשִׁ֑ישׁ\rb*, \rb the Kittites|כִּתִּ֖ים\rb*, \rb and the Rodanites|וְדֹדָנִֽים׃\rb*.\f + \fr 10:4 \ft SP and some MT manuscripts (see also LXX and 1 Chronicles 1:7); most MT manuscripts \fqa Dodanites\f* \v 5 \rb From these|מֵ֠אֵלֶּה\rb*, \rb the maritime|אִיֵּ֤י\rb* \rb peoples|הַגּוֹיִם֙\rb* \rb separated|נִפְרְד֞וּ\rb* \rb into their territories|בְּאַרְצֹתָ֔ם\rb*,\rb |אִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb according to their languages|לִלְשֹׁנ֑וֹ\rb*, \rb by clans|לְמִשְׁפְּחֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb within their nations|בְּגוֹיֵהֶֽם׃\rb*.
\s2 The Hamites
\p \v 6 \rb The sons|וּבְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb of Ham|חָ֑ם\rb*:
\p \rb Cush|כּ֥וּשׁ\rb*, \rb Mizraim|וּמִצְרַ֖יִם\rb*, \rb Put|וּפ֥וּט\rb*, \rb and Canaan|וּכְנָֽעַן׃\rb*.
\p \v 7 \rb The sons|וּבְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Cush|כ֔וּשׁ\rb*:
\p \rb Seba|סְבָא֙\rb*, \rb Havilah|וַֽחֲוִילָ֔ה\rb*, \rb Sabtah|וְסַבְתָּ֥ה\rb*,\f + \fr 10:7 \fqa Sabtah \ft is a variant of \fqa Sabta\ft ; see 1 Chronicles 1:9.\f* \rb Raamah|וְרַעְמָ֖ה\rb*, \rb and Sabteca|וְסַבְתְּכָ֑א\rb*.
\p \rb And the sons|וּבְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Raamah|רַעְמָ֖ה\rb*:
\p \rb Sheba|שְׁבָ֥א\rb* \rb and Dedan|וּדְדָֽן׃\rb*.
\p \v 8 \rb Cush|וְכ֖וּשׁ\rb* \rb was the father of|יָלַ֣ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Nimrod|נִמְרֹ֑ד\rb*, \rb who|ה֣וּא\rb* \rb began|הֵחֵ֔ל\rb* \rb to be|לִֽהְי֥וֹת\rb* \rb a mighty one|גִּבֹּ֖ר\rb*\f + \fr 10:8 \ft Or \fqa who established himself as a mighty warrior \ft or \fqa who became the first fearless leader\f* \rb on the earth|בָּאָֽרֶץ׃\rb*. \v 9 \rb He|הֽוּא־\rb* \rb was|הָיָ֥ה\rb* \rb a mighty|גִבֹּֽר־\rb* \rb hunter|צַ֖יִד\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb*\f + \fr 10:9 \ft Or \fqa in defiance of\ft ; twice in this verse\f* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*; \rb so|עַל־\rb*\rb |כֵּן֙\rb* \rb it is said|יֵֽאָמַ֔ר\rb*, “\rb Like Nimrod|כְּנִמְרֹ֛ד\rb*, \rb a mighty|גִּבּ֥וֹר\rb* \rb hunter|צַ֖יִד\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*.” \v 10 \rb |וַתְּהִ֨י\rb* \rb His kingdom|מַמְלַכְתּוֹ֙\rb* \rb began|רֵאשִׁ֤ית\rb* \rb in Babylon|בָּבֶ֔ל\rb*, \rb Erech|וְאֶ֖רֶךְ\rb*, \rb Accad|וְאַכַּ֣ד\rb*, \rb and Calneh|וְכַלְנֵ֑ה\rb*, \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb of Shinar|שִׁנְעָֽר׃\rb*.\f + \fr 10:10 \ft That is, Babylonia\f* \v 11 \rb From|מִן־\rb* \rb that|הַהִ֖וא\rb* \rb land|הָאָ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb he went forth|יָצָ֣א\rb* \rb into Assyria|אַשּׁ֑וּר\rb*, \rb where he built|וַיִּ֙בֶן֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Nineveh|נִ֣ינְוֵ֔ה\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Rehoboth-Ir|רְחֹבֹ֥ת\rb*,\rb |עִ֖יר\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Calah|כָּֽלַח׃\rb*, \v 12 \rb |וְֽאֶת־\rb* \rb and Resen|רֶ֔סֶן\rb*, \rb which is between|בֵּ֥ין\rb* \rb Nineveh|נִֽינְוֵ֖ה\rb*\rb |וּבֵ֣ין\rb* \rb and the great|הַגְּדֹלָֽה׃\rb* \rb city|הָעִ֥יר\rb* \rb of Calah|כָּ֑לַח\rb*\rb |הִ֖וא\rb*.
\p \v 13 \rb Mizraim|וּמִצְרַ֡יִם\rb* \rb was the father of|יָלַ֞ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Ludites|לוּדִ֧ים\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the Anamites|עֲנָמִ֛ים\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the Lehabites|לְהָבִ֖ים\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the Naphtuhites|נַפְתֻּחִֽים׃\rb*, \v 14 \rb |וְֽאֶת־\rb* \rb the Pathrusites|פַּתְרֻסִ֞ים\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the Casluhites|כַּסְלֻחִ֗ים\rb* (\rb from|מִשָּׁ֛ם\rb* \rb whom|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the Philistines|פְּלִשְׁתִּ֖ים\rb* \rb came|יָצְא֥וּ\rb*), \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the Caphtorites|כַּפְתֹּרִֽים׃ס\rb*.\f + \fr 10:14 \ft Some translators adjust the Hebrew word order to \fqa the Casluhites, and the Caphtorites (from whom the Philistines came)\ft ; see also Jeremiah 47:4 and Amos 9:7.\f*
\p \v 15 \rb And Canaan|וּכְנַ֗עַן\rb* \rb was the father of|יָלַ֛ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Sidon|צִידֹ֥ן\rb* \rb his firstborn|בְּכֹר֖וֹ\rb*,\f + \fr 10:15 \ft Or \fqa of the Sidonians, the foremost\f* \rb and of|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the Hittites|חֵֽת׃\rb*, \v 16 \rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the Jebusites|הַיְבוּסִי֙\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the Amorites|הָ֣אֱמֹרִ֔י\rb*,\rb |וְאֵ֖ת\rb* \rb the Girgashites|הַגִּרְגָּשִֽׁי׃\rb*, \v 17 \rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the Hivites|הַֽחִוִּ֥י\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the Arkites|הַֽעַרְקִ֖י\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the Sinites|הַסִּינִֽי׃\rb*, \v 18 \rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the Arvadites|הָֽאַרְוָדִ֥י\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the Zemarites|הַצְּמָרִ֖י\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and the Hamathites|הַֽחֲמָתִ֑י\rb*.
\p \rb Later|וְאַחַ֣ר\rb* \rb the Canaanite|הַֽכְּנַעֲנִֽי׃\rb* \rb clans|מִשְׁפְּח֖וֹת\rb* \rb were scattered|נָפֹ֔צוּ\rb*, \v 19 \rb and the borders|גְּב֤וּל\rb* \rb of Canaan|הַֽכְּנַעֲנִי֙\rb* \rb extended from|וַֽיְהִ֞י\rb* \rb Sidon|מִצִּידֹ֔ן\rb*\rb |בֹּאֲכָ֥ה\rb* \rb toward Gerar|גְרָ֖רָה\rb* \rb as|עַד־\rb* \rb far as Gaza|עַזָּ֑ה\rb*, \rb and then|בֹּאֲכָ֞ה\rb* \rb toward Sodom|סְדֹ֧מָה\rb*, \rb Gomorrah|וַעֲמֹרָ֛ה\rb*, \rb Admah|וְאַדְמָ֥ה\rb*, \rb and Zeboiim|וּצְבֹיִ֖ם\rb*, \rb as|עַד־\rb* \rb far as Lasha|לָֽשַׁע׃\rb*.
\p \v 20 \rb These are|אֵ֣לֶּה\rb* \rb the sons|בְנֵי־\rb* \rb of Ham|חָ֔ם\rb* \rb according to their clans|לְמִשְׁפְּחֹתָ֖ם\rb*, \rb languages|לִלְשֹֽׁנֹתָ֑ם\rb*, \rb lands|בְּאַרְצֹתָ֖ם\rb*, \rb and nations|בְּגוֹיֵהֶֽם׃ס\rb*.
\s2 The Semites
\p \v 21 \rb And sons were also born|יֻלַּ֖ד\rb*\rb |גַּם־\rb* \rb to Shem|וּלְשֵׁ֥ם\rb*, \rb the older|הַגָּדֽוֹל׃\rb* \rb brother|אֲחִ֖י\rb* \rb of Japheth|יֶ֥פֶת\rb*;\f + \fr 10:21 \ft Or \fqa Shem, whose older brother was Japheth\f* \rb Shem|ה֑וּא\rb* \rb was the forefather|אֲבִי֙\rb* \rb of all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the sons|בְּנֵי־\rb* \rb of Eber|עֵ֔בֶר\rb*.
\p \v 22 \rb The sons|בְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Shem|שֵׁ֖ם\rb*:
\p \rb Elam|עֵילָ֣ם\rb*, \rb Asshur|וְאַשּׁ֑וּר\rb*, \rb Arphaxad|וְאַרְפַּכְשַׁ֖ד\rb*, \rb Lud|וְל֥וּד\rb*, \rb and Aram|וַֽאֲרָֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 23 \rb The sons|וּבְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb of Aram|אֲרָ֑ם\rb*:
\p \rb Uz|ע֥וּץ\rb*, \rb Hul|וְח֖וּל\rb*, \rb Gether|וְגֶ֥תֶר\rb*, \rb and Mash|וָמַֽשׁ׃\rb*.\f + \fr 10:23 \ft Hebrew; LXX and 1 Chronicles 1:17 \fqa Meshech\f*
\p \v 24 \rb Arphaxad|וְאַרְפַּכְשַׁ֖ד\rb* \rb was the father of|יָלַ֣ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Shelah|שָׁ֑לַח\rb*,\f + \fr 10:24 \ft Hebrew; LXX (see also Luke 3:35–36) \fqa And Arphaxad was the father of Cainan, and Cainan was the father of Shelah,\f* \rb and Shelah|וְשֶׁ֖לַח\rb* \rb was the father of|יָלַ֥ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Eber|עֵֽבֶר׃\rb*.
\p \v 25 \rb Two|שְׁנֵ֣י\rb* \rb sons|בָנִ֑ים\rb* \rb were born|יֻלַּ֖ד\rb* \rb to Eber|וּלְעֵ֥בֶר\rb*: \rb One|הָֽאֶחָ֞ד\rb* \rb was named|שֵׁ֣ם\rb* \rb Peleg|פֶּ֗לֶג\rb*,\f + \fr 10:25 \fqa Peleg \ft means \fqa division\ft .\f* \rb because|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb in his days|בְיָמָיו֙\rb* \rb the earth|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb was divided|נִפְלְגָ֣ה\rb*, \rb and his brother|אָחִ֖יו\rb* \rb was named|וְשֵׁ֥ם\rb* \rb Joktan|יָקְטָֽן׃\rb*.
\p \v 26 \rb And Joktan|וְיָקְטָ֣ן\rb* \rb was the father of|יָלַ֔ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Almodad|אַלְמוֹדָ֖ד\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Sheleph|שָׁ֑לֶף\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Hazarmaveth|חֲצַרְמָ֖וֶת\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Jerah|יָֽרַח׃\rb*, \v 27 \rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Hadoram|הֲדוֹרָ֥ם\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Uzal|אוּזָ֖ל\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Diklah|דִּקְלָֽה׃\rb*, \v 28 \rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Obal|עוֹבָ֥ל\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Abimael|אֲבִֽימָאֵ֖ל\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Sheba|שְׁבָֽא׃\rb*, \v 29 \rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Ophir|אוֹפִ֥ר\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Havilah|חֲוִילָ֖ה\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and Jobab|יוֹבָ֑ב\rb*. \rb All|כָּל־\rb* \rb these|אֵ֖לֶּה\rb* \rb were sons|בְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Joktan|יָקְטָֽן׃\rb*. \v 30 \rb |וַֽיְהִ֥י\rb* \rb Their territory|מוֹשָׁבָ֖ם\rb* \rb extended from|בֹּאֲכָ֥ה\rb* \rb Mesha|מִמֵּשָׁ֑א\rb* \rb to Sephar|סְפָ֖רָה\rb*, \rb in the eastern|הַקֶּֽדֶם׃\rb* \rb hill country|הַ֥ר\rb*.
\p \v 31 \rb These|אֵ֣לֶּה\rb* \rb are the sons|בְנֵי־\rb* \rb of Shem|שֵׁ֔ם\rb*, \rb according to their clans|לְמִשְׁפְּחֹתָ֖ם\rb*, \rb languages|לִלְשֹׁנֹתָ֑ם\rb*, \rb lands|בְּאַרְצֹתָ֖ם\rb*, \rb and nations|לְגוֹיֵהֶֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 32 \rb All these|אֵ֣לֶּה\rb* \rb are the clans|מִשְׁפְּחֹ֧ת\rb* \rb of Noah’s|נֹ֛חַ\rb* \rb sons|בְּנֵי־\rb*, \rb according to their generations|לְתוֹלְדֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb and nations|בְּגוֹיֵהֶ֑ם\rb*. \rb From these|וּמֵאֵ֜לֶּה\rb* \rb the nations|הַגּוֹיִ֛ם\rb* \rb of the earth|בָּאָ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb spread out|נִפְרְד֧וּ\rb* \rb after|אַחַ֥ר\rb* \rb the flood|הַמַּבּֽוּל׃פ\rb*.
\c 11
\s1 The Tower of Babel
\p \v 1 \rb Now the whole|כָל־\rb* \rb world|הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb had|וַֽיְהִ֥י\rb* \rb one|אֶחָ֑ת\rb* \rb language|שָׂפָ֣ה\rb* \rb and a common|אֲחָדִֽים׃\rb* \rb form of speech|וּדְבָרִ֖ים\rb*. \v 2 \rb And|וַֽיְהִ֖י\rb* \rb as people journeyed|בְּנָסְעָ֣ם\rb* \rb eastward|מִקֶּ֑דֶם\rb*,\f + \fr 11:2 \ft Or \fqa from the east \ft or \fqa in the east\f* \rb they found|וַֽיִּמְצְא֥וּ\rb* \rb a plain|בִקְעָ֛ה\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Shinar|שִׁנְעָ֖ר\rb*\f + \fr 11:2 \ft That is, Babylonia\f* \rb and settled|וַיֵּ֥שְׁבוּ\rb* \rb there|שָֽׁם׃\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb And they said|וַיֹּאמְר֞וּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb one|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb another|רֵעֵ֗הוּ\rb*, “\rb Come|הָ֚בָה\rb*, \rb let us make|נִלְבְּנָ֣ה\rb* \rb bricks|לְבֵנִ֔ים\rb* \rb and bake them|וְנִשְׂרְפָ֖ה\rb* \rb thoroughly|לִשְׂרֵפָ֑ה\rb*.” \rb So they used|וַתְּהִ֨י\rb*\rb |לָהֶ֤ם\rb* \rb brick|הַלְּבֵנָה֙\rb* \rb instead of stone|לְאָ֔בֶן\rb*, \rb and tar|וְהַ֣חֵמָ֔ר\rb*\rb |הָיָ֥ה\rb*\rb |לָהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb instead of mortar|לַחֹֽמֶר׃\rb*.
\p \v 4 “\rb Come|הָ֣בָה׀\rb*,” \rb they said|וַיֹּאמְר֞וּ\rb*, “\rb let us build|נִבְנֶה־\rb* \rb for ourselves|לָּ֣נוּ\rb* \rb a city|עִ֗יר\rb* \rb with a tower|וּמִגְדָּל֙\rb* \rb that reaches|וְרֹאשׁ֣וֹ\rb* \rb to the heavens|בַשָּׁמַ֔יִם\rb*, \rb that we may make|וְנַֽעֲשֶׂה־\rb* \rb a name|שֵׁ֑ם\rb* \rb for ourselves|לָּ֖נוּ\rb* \rb and not|פֶּן־\rb* \rb be scattered|נָפ֖וּץ\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb the face|פְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of all|כָל־\rb* \rb the earth|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 5 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb came down|וַיֵּ֣רֶד\rb* \rb to see|לִרְאֹ֥ת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the city|הָעִ֖יר\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and the tower|הַמִּגְדָּ֑ל\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb the sons|בְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of men|הָאָדָֽם׃\rb* \rb were building|בָּנ֖וּ\rb*. \v 6 \rb And the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb If|הֵ֣ן\rb* \rb they have begun|הַחִלָּ֣ם\rb* \rb to do|לַעֲשׂ֑וֹת\rb* \rb this|וְזֶ֖ה\rb* \rb as one|אֶחָד֙\rb* \rb people|עַ֤ם\rb* \rb speaking the same|לְכֻלָּ֔ם\rb*\rb |אַחַת֙\rb* \rb language|וְשָׂפָ֤ה\rb*, \rb then|וְעַתָּה֙\rb* \rb nothing|לֹֽא־\rb*\rb |כֹּ֛ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb they devise|יָזְמ֖וּ\rb*\rb |לַֽעֲשֽׂוֹת׃\rb* \rb will be beyond|יִבָּצֵ֣ר\rb* \rb them|מֵהֶ֔ם\rb*. \v 7 \rb Come|הָ֚בָה\rb*, \rb let Us go down|נֵֽרְדָ֔ה\rb*\rb |שָׁ֖ם\rb* \rb and confuse|וְנָבְלָ֥ה\rb* \rb their language|שְׂפָתָ֑ם\rb*, \rb so that|אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb they will not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb understand|יִשְׁמְע֔וּ\rb* \rb one|אִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb another’s|רֵעֵֽהוּ׃\rb* \rb speech|שְׂפַ֥ת\rb*.”
\p \v 8 \rb So the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֛ם\rb* \rb scattered them|וַיָּ֨פֶץ\rb* \rb from there|מִשָּׁ֖ם\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb the face|פְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of all|כָל־\rb* \rb the earth|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb*, \rb and they stopped|וַֽיַּחְדְּל֖וּ\rb* \rb building|לִבְנֹ֥ת\rb* \rb the city|הָעִֽיר׃\rb*. \v 9 \rb That is why|עַל־\rb*\rb |כֵּ֞ן\rb* \rb it|שְׁמָהּ֙\rb* \rb is called|קָרָ֤א\rb* \rb Babel|בָּבֶ֔ל\rb*,\f + \fr 11:9 \ft Or \fqa Babylon\ft ; the Hebrew word for \fqa Babel \ft sounds like the Hebrew for \fqa confused\ft .\f* \rb for|כִּי־\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֛ם\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb confused|בָּלַ֥ל\rb* \rb the language|שְׂפַ֣ת\rb* \rb of the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb world|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb*, \rb and from that place|וּמִשָּׁם֙\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb scattered them|הֱפִיצָ֣ם\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb the face|פְּנֵ֖י\rb* \rb of all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the earth|הָאָֽרֶץ׃פ\rb*.
\s1 Genealogy from Shem to Abram
\p \v 10 \rb This|אֵ֚לֶּה\rb* \rb is the account|תּוֹלְדֹ֣ת\rb* \rb of Shem|שֵׁ֔ם\rb*. \rb Two years|שְׁנָתַ֖יִם\rb* \rb after|אַחַ֥ר\rb* \rb the flood|הַמַּבּֽוּל׃\rb*, \rb when Shem|שֵׁ֚ם\rb* \rb was 100|מְאַ֣ת\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָ֔ה\rb* \rb old|בֶּן־\rb*, \rb he became the father of|וַיּ֖וֹלֶד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Arphaxad|אַרְפַּכְשָׁ֑ד\rb*. \v 11 \rb And after|אַֽחֲרֵי֙\rb* \rb he had become the father of|הוֹלִיד֣וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Arphaxad|אַרְפַּכְשָׁ֔ד\rb*, \rb Shem|שֵׁ֗ם\rb* \rb lived|וַֽיְחִי־\rb* \rb 500|חֲמֵ֥שׁ\rb*\rb |מֵא֖וֹת\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָ֑ה\rb* \rb and had|וַיּ֥וֹלֶד\rb* \rb other sons|בָּנִ֖ים\rb* \rb and daughters|וּבָנֽוֹת׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 12 \rb When Arphaxad|וְאַרְפַּכְשַׁ֣ד\rb* \rb was|חַ֔י\rb* \rb 35|חָמֵ֥שׁ\rb*\rb |וּשְׁלֹשִׁ֖ים\rb* \rb years old|שָׁנָ֑ה\rb*, \rb he became the father of|וַיּ֖וֹלֶד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Shelah|שָֽׁלַח׃\rb*. \v 13 \rb And after|אַֽחֲרֵי֙\rb* \rb he had become the father of|הוֹלִיד֣וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Shelah|שֶׁ֔לַח\rb*, \rb Arphaxad|אַרְפַּכְשַׁ֗ד\rb* \rb lived|וַֽיְחִ֣י\rb* \rb 403|שָׁלֹ֣שׁ\rb*\rb |וְאַרְבַּ֥ע\rb*\rb |מֵא֖וֹת\rb* \rb years|שָׁנִ֔ים\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֑ה\rb* \rb and had|וַיּ֥וֹלֶד\rb* \rb other sons|בָּנִ֖ים\rb* \rb and daughters|וּבָנֽוֹת׃ס\rb*.\f + \fr 11:13 \ft Hebrew; LXX (see also Luke 3:35–36) \fv 12\fv*When Arphaxad was 135 years old, he became the father of Cainan. \fv 13\fv*And after he had become the father of Cainan, Arphaxad lived 430 years and had other sons and daughters, and then he died. When Cainan had lived 130 years, he became the father of Shelah. And after he had become the father of Shelah, Cainan lived 330 years and had other sons and daughters.\ft Note that LXX also adds 100 years to the ages of Shelah, Eber, Peleg, Reu, Serug, and Nahor in this genealogy.\f*
\p \v 14 \rb When Shelah|וְשֶׁ֥לַח\rb* \rb was|חַ֖י\rb* \rb 30|שְׁלֹשִׁ֣ים\rb* \rb years old|שָׁנָ֑ה\rb*, \rb he became the father of|וַיּ֖וֹלֶד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Eber|עֵֽבֶר׃\rb*. \v 15 \rb And after|אַחֲרֵי֙\rb* \rb he had become the father of|הוֹלִיד֣וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Eber|עֵ֔בֶר\rb*, \rb Shelah|שֶׁ֗לַח\rb* \rb lived|וַֽיְחִי־\rb* \rb 403|וְאַרְבַּ֥ע\rb*\rb |מֵא֖וֹת\rb*\rb |שָׁלֹ֣שׁ\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֑ה\rb* \rb years|שָׁנִ֔ים\rb* \rb and had|וַיּ֥וֹלֶד\rb* \rb other sons|בָּנִ֖ים\rb* \rb and daughters|וּבָנֽוֹת׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 16 \rb When Eber|עֵ֕בֶר\rb* \rb was|וַֽיְחִי־\rb* \rb 34|אַרְבַּ֥ע\rb*\rb |וּשְׁלֹשִׁ֖ים\rb* \rb years old|שָׁנָ֑ה\rb*, \rb he became the father of|וַיּ֖וֹלֶד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Peleg|פָּֽלֶג׃\rb*. \v 17 \rb And after|אַחֲרֵי֙\rb* \rb he had become the father of|הוֹלִיד֣וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Peleg|פֶּ֔לֶג\rb*, \rb Eber|עֵ֗בֶר\rb* \rb lived|וַֽיְחִי־\rb* \rb 430|שְׁלֹשִׁ֣ים\rb*\rb |וְאַרְבַּ֥ע\rb*\rb |מֵא֖וֹת\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֑ה\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָ֔ה\rb* \rb and had|וַיּ֥וֹלֶד\rb* \rb other sons|בָּנִ֖ים\rb* \rb and daughters|וּבָנֽוֹת׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 18 \rb When Peleg|פֶ֖לֶג\rb* \rb was|וַֽיְחִי־\rb* \rb 30|שְׁלֹשִׁ֣ים\rb* \rb years old|שָׁנָ֑ה\rb*, \rb he became the father of|וַיּ֖וֹלֶד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Reu|רְעֽוּ׃\rb*. \v 19 \rb And after|אַחֲרֵי֙\rb* \rb he had become the father of|הוֹלִיד֣וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Reu|רְע֔וּ\rb*, \rb Peleg|פֶ֗לֶג\rb* \rb lived|וַֽיְחִי־\rb* \rb 209|תֵּ֥שַׁע\rb*\rb |וּמָאתַ֣יִם\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֑ה\rb* \rb years|שָׁנִ֖ים\rb* \rb and had|וַיּ֥וֹלֶד\rb* \rb other sons|בָּנִ֖ים\rb* \rb and daughters|וּבָנֽוֹת׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 20 \rb When Reu|רְע֔וּ\rb* \rb was|וַיְחִ֣י\rb* \rb 32|שְׁתַּ֥יִם\rb*\rb |וּשְׁלֹשִׁ֖ים\rb* \rb years old|שָׁנָ֑ה\rb*, \rb he became the father of|וַיּ֖וֹלֶד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Serug|שְׂרֽוּג׃\rb*. \v 21 \rb And after|אַחֲרֵי֙\rb* \rb he had become the father of|הוֹלִיד֣וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Serug|שְׂר֔וּג\rb*, \rb Reu|רְע֗וּ\rb* \rb lived|וַיְחִ֣י\rb* \rb 207|שֶׁ֥בַע\rb*\rb |וּמָאתַ֣יִם\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֑ה\rb* \rb years|שָׁנִ֖ים\rb* \rb and had|וַיּ֥וֹלֶד\rb* \rb other sons|בָּנִ֖ים\rb* \rb and daughters|וּבָנֽוֹת׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 22 \rb When Serug|שְׂר֖וּג\rb* \rb was|וַיְחִ֥י\rb* \rb 30|שְׁלֹשִׁ֣ים\rb* \rb years old|שָׁנָ֑ה\rb*, \rb he became the father of|וַיּ֖וֹלֶד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Nahor|נָחֽוֹר׃\rb*. \v 23 \rb And after|אַחֲרֵ֛י\rb* \rb he had become the father of|הוֹלִיד֥וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Nahor|נָח֖וֹר\rb*, \rb Serug|שְׂר֗וּג\rb* \rb lived|וַיְחִ֣י\rb* \rb 200|מָאתַ֣יִם\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָ֑ה\rb* \rb and had|וַיּ֥וֹלֶד\rb* \rb other sons|בָּנִ֖ים\rb* \rb and daughters|וּבָנֽוֹת׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 24 \rb When Nahor|נָח֔וֹר\rb* \rb was|וַיְחִ֣י\rb* \rb 29|תֵּ֥שַׁע\rb*\rb |וְעֶשְׂרִ֖ים\rb* \rb years old|שָׁנָ֑ה\rb*, \rb he became the father of|וַיּ֖וֹלֶד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Terah|תָּֽרַח׃\rb*. \v 25 \rb And after|אַחֲרֵי֙\rb* \rb he had become the father of|הוֹלִיד֣וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Terah|תֶּ֔רַח\rb*, \rb Nahor|נָח֗וֹר\rb* \rb lived|וַיְחִ֣י\rb* \rb 119|תְּשַֽׁע־\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵ֥ה\rb*\rb |וּמְאַ֣ת\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֑ה\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָ֖ה\rb* \rb and had|וַיּ֥וֹלֶד\rb* \rb other sons|בָּנִ֖ים\rb* \rb and daughters|וּבָנֽוֹת׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 26 \rb When Terah|תֶ֖רַח\rb* \rb was|וַֽיְחִי־\rb* \rb 70|שִׁבְעִ֣ים\rb* \rb years old|שָׁנָ֑ה\rb*, \rb he became the father of|וַיּ֙וֹלֶד֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Abram|אַבְרָ֔ם\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Nahor|נָח֖וֹר\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and Haran|הָרָֽן׃\rb*.
\s1 Terah’s Descendants
\p \v 27 \rb This|וְאֵ֙לֶּה֙\rb* \rb is the account|תּוֹלְדֹ֣ת\rb* \rb of Terah|תֶּ֔רַח\rb*. \rb Terah|תֶּ֚רַח\rb* \rb became the father of|הוֹלִ֣יד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Abram|אַבְרָ֔ם\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Nahor|נָח֖וֹר\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and Haran|הָרָ֑ן\rb*. \rb And Haran|וְהָרָ֖ן\rb* \rb became the father of|הוֹלִ֥יד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Lot|לֽוֹט׃\rb*. \v 28 \rb During|עַל־\rb*\rb |פְּנֵ֖י\rb* \rb his father|אָבִ֑יו\rb* \rb Terah’s lifetime|תֶּ֣רַח\rb*, \rb Haran|הָרָ֔ן\rb* \rb died|וַיָּ֣מָת\rb* \rb in his native|מוֹלַדְתּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb land|בְּאֶ֥רֶץ\rb*, \rb in Ur|בְּא֥וּר\rb* \rb of the Chaldeans|כַּשְׂדִּֽים׃\rb*.
\p \v 29 \rb And Abram|אַבְרָ֧ם\rb* \rb and Nahor|וְנָח֛וֹר\rb* \rb took|וַיִּקַּ֨ח\rb* \rb wives|נָשִׁ֑ים\rb* \rb for themselves|לָהֶ֖ם\rb*. \rb Abram’s|אַבְרָם֙\rb* \rb wife|אֵֽשֶׁת־\rb* \rb was named|שֵׁ֤ם\rb* \rb Sarai|שָׂרָ֔י\rb*, \rb and Nahor’s|נָחוֹר֙\rb* \rb wife|אֵֽשֶׁת־\rb* \rb was named|וְשֵׁ֤ם\rb* \rb Milcah|מִלְכָּ֔ה\rb*; \rb she was the daughter|בַּת־\rb* \rb of Haran|הָרָ֥ן\rb*, \rb who was the father|אֲבִֽי־\rb* \rb of both Milcah|מִלְכָּ֖ה\rb*\rb |וַֽאֲבִ֥י\rb* \rb and Iscah|יִסְכָּֽה׃\rb*. \v 30 \rb But Sarai|שָׂרַ֖י\rb* \rb was|וַתְּהִ֥י\rb* \rb barren|עֲקָרָ֑ה\rb*; \rb she had|לָ֖הּ\rb* \rb no|אֵ֥ין\rb* \rb children|וָלָֽד׃\rb*.
\p \v 31 \rb And Terah|תֶּ֜רַח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb took|וַיִּקַּ֨ח\rb* \rb his son|בְּנ֗וֹ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Abram|אַבְרָ֣ם\rb*, \rb his grandson|בֶּן־\rb*\rb |בֶּן־\rb* \rb Lot|ל֤וֹט\rb* \rb son|בְּנ֔וֹ\rb* \rb of Haran|הָרָן֙\rb*, \rb and|וְאֵת֙\rb* \rb his daughter-in-law|כַּלָּת֔וֹ\rb* \rb Sarai|שָׂרַ֣י\rb* \rb the wife|אֵ֖שֶׁת\rb*\rb |בְּנ֑וֹ\rb* \rb of Abram|אַבְרָ֣ם\rb*, \rb and they set out|וַיֵּצְא֨וּ\rb*\rb |אִתָּ֜ם\rb* \rb from Ur|מֵא֣וּר\rb* \rb of the Chaldeans|כַּשְׂדִּ֗ים\rb* \rb for|לָלֶ֙כֶת֙\rb* \rb the land|אַ֣רְצָה\rb* \rb of Canaan|כְּנַ֔עַן\rb*. \rb But when they arrived|וַיָּבֹ֥אוּ\rb* \rb in|עַד־\rb* \rb Haran|חָרָ֖ן\rb*, \rb they settled|וַיֵּ֥שְׁבוּ\rb* \rb there|שָֽׁם׃\rb*. \v 32 \rb Terah|תֶ֔רַח\rb* \rb lived|וַיִּהְי֣וּ\rb*\rb |יְמֵי־\rb* \rb 205|חָמֵ֥שׁ\rb*\rb |וּמָאתַ֣יִם\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֑ה\rb* \rb years|שָׁנִ֖ים\rb*, \rb and he died|וַיָּ֥מָת\rb*\rb |תֶּ֖רַח\rb* \rb in Haran|בְּחָרָֽן׃ס\rb*.
\c 12
\s1 The Call of Abram
\p \v 1 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Abram|אַבְרָ֔ם\rb*, “\rb Leave|לֶךְ־\rb* \rb your|לְךָ֛\rb* \rb country|מֵאַרְצְךָ֥\rb*, \rb your kindred|וּמִמּֽוֹלַדְתְּךָ֖\rb*, \rb and your father’s|אָבִ֑יךָ\rb* \rb household|וּמִבֵּ֣ית\rb*, \rb and go to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I will show you|אַרְאֶֽךָּ׃\rb*.\f + \fr 12:1 \ft Cited in Acts 7:3\f*
\b 
\q1 \v 2 \rb I will make|וְאֶֽעֶשְׂךָ֙\rb* \rb you into a great|גָּד֔וֹל\rb* \rb nation|לְג֣וֹי\rb*,
\q2 \rb and I will bless you|וַאֲבָ֣רֶכְךָ֔\rb*;
\q1 \rb I will make your name|שְׁמֶ֑ךָ\rb* \rb great|וַאֲגַדְּלָ֖ה\rb*,
\q2 \rb so that you will be|וֶהְיֵ֖ה\rb* \rb a blessing|בְּרָכָֽה׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 3 \rb I will bless|וַאֲבָֽרֲכָה֙\rb* \rb those who bless you|מְבָ֣רְכֶ֔יךָ\rb*
\q2 \rb and curse|אָאֹ֑ר\rb* \rb those who curse you|וּמְקַלֶּלְךָ֖\rb*;
\q1 \rb and all|כֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb the families|מִשְׁפְּחֹ֥ת\rb* \rb of the earth|הָאֲדָמָֽה׃\rb*
\q2 \rb will be blessed|וְנִבְרְכ֣וּ\rb* \rb through you|בְךָ֔\rb*.\f + \fr 12:3 \ft See Galatians 3:8\f*”
\p \v 4 \rb So Abram|אַבְרָ֗ם\rb* \rb departed|וַיֵּ֣לֶךְ\rb*, \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb had directed him|דִּבֶּ֤ר\rb*,\rb |אֵלָיו֙\rb* \rb and Lot|ל֑וֹט\rb* \rb went|וַיֵּ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb with him|אִתּ֖וֹ\rb*. \rb Abram|וְאַבְרָ֗ם\rb* \rb was seventy-five|חָמֵ֤שׁ\rb*\rb |וְשִׁבְעִ֣ים\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָ֔ה\rb* \rb old|בֶּן־\rb*\rb |שָׁנִים֙\rb* \rb when he left|בְּצֵאת֖וֹ\rb* \rb Haran|מֵחָרָֽן׃\rb*. \v 5 \rb And Abram|אַבְרָם֩\rb* \rb took|וַיִּקַּ֣ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his wife|אִשְׁתּ֜וֹ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Sarai|שָׂרַ֨י\rb*, \rb his nephew|בֶּן־\rb*\rb |אָחִ֗יו\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Lot|ל֣וֹט\rb*, \rb and all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the possessions|רְכוּשָׁם֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb*\rb |רָכָ֔שׁוּ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and people|הַנֶּ֖פֶשׁ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb they had acquired|עָשׂ֣וּ\rb* \rb in Haran|בְחָרָ֑ן\rb*, \rb and set out|וַיֵּצְא֗וּ\rb*\rb |לָלֶ֙כֶת֙\rb* \rb for the land|אַ֣רְצָה\rb* \rb of Canaan|כְּנַ֔עַן\rb*.
\p \rb When they came|וַיָּבֹ֖אוּ\rb* \rb to the land|אַ֥רְצָה\rb* \rb of Canaan|כְּנָֽעַן׃\rb*, \v 6 \rb Abram|אַבְרָם֙\rb* \rb traveled|וַיַּעֲבֹ֤ר\rb* \rb through the land|בָּאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb as far as|עַ֚ד\rb* \rb the site|מְק֣וֹם\rb*\rb |עַ֖ד\rb* \rb of the Oak|אֵל֣וֹן\rb*\f + \fr 12:6 \ft Or \fqa Terebinth \ft or \fqa Great Tree\f* \rb of Moreh|מוֹרֶ֑ה\rb* \rb at Shechem|שְׁכֶ֔ם\rb*. \rb And at that time|אָ֥ז\rb* \rb the Canaanites|וְהַֽכְּנַעֲנִ֖י\rb* \rb were in the land|בָּאָֽרֶץ׃\rb*.
\p \v 7 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb appeared|וַיֵּרָ֤א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Abram|אַבְרָ֔ם\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*, “\rb I will give|אֶתֵּ֖ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּ֑את\rb* \rb land|הָאָ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb to your offspring|לְזַ֨רְעֲךָ֔\rb*.\f + \fr 12:7 \ft Cited in Galatians 3:16\f*” \rb So Abram built|וַיִּ֤בֶן\rb* \rb an altar|מִזְבֵּ֔חַ\rb* \rb there|שָׁם֙\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֖ה\rb*, \rb who had appeared|הַנִּרְאֶ֥ה\rb* \rb to him|אֵלָֽיו׃\rb*.
\p \v 8 \rb From there|מִשָּׁ֜ם\rb* \rb Abram moved on|וַיַּעְתֵּ֨ק\rb* \rb to the hill country|הָהָ֗רָה\rb* \rb east|מִקֶּ֛דֶם\rb* \rb of|לְבֵֽית־\rb* \rb Bethel|אֵ֖ל\rb* \rb and pitched|וַיֵּ֣ט\rb* \rb his tent|אָהֳלֹ֑ה\rb*, \rb with Bethel|בֵּֽית־\rb*\rb |אֵ֤ל\rb* \rb to the west|מִיָּם֙\rb* \rb and Ai|וְהָעַ֣י\rb* \rb to the east|מִקֶּ֔דֶם\rb*. \rb There|שָׁ֤ם\rb* \rb he built|וַיִּֽבֶן־\rb* \rb an altar|מִזְבֵּ֙חַ֙\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָ֔ה\rb*, \rb and he called|וַיִּקְרָ֖א\rb* \rb on the name|בְּשֵׁ֥ם\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 9 \rb And Abram|אַבְרָ֔ם\rb* \rb journeyed on|וַיִּסַּ֣ע\rb*\rb |הָל֥וֹךְ\rb* \rb toward|וְנָס֖וֹעַ\rb* \rb the Negev|הַנֶּֽגְבָּה׃פ\rb*.
\s1 Abram and Sarai in Egypt
\p \v 10 \rb Now there was|וַיְהִ֥י\rb* \rb a famine|רָעָ֖ב\rb* \rb in the land|בָּאָ֑רֶץ\rb*. \rb So Abram|אַבְרָ֤ם\rb* \rb went down|וַיֵּ֨רֶד\rb* \rb to Egypt|מִצְרַ֙יְמָה֙\rb* \rb to live there|שָׁ֔ם\rb* \rb for a while|לָג֣וּר\rb* \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the famine|הָרָעָ֖ב\rb*\rb |בָּאָֽרֶץ׃\rb* \rb was severe|כָבֵ֥ד\rb*. \v 11 \rb |וַיְהִ֕י\rb* \rb As|כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb he was about|הִקְרִ֖יב\rb* \rb to enter|לָב֣וֹא\rb* \rb Egypt|מִצְרָ֑יְמָה\rb*, \rb he said|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his wife|אִשְׁתּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb Sarai|שָׂרַ֣י\rb*, “\rb Look|הִנֵּה־\rb*,\rb |נָ֣א\rb* \rb I know|יָדַ֔עְתִּי\rb* \rb that|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb you|אָֽתְּ׃\rb* \rb are a beautiful|יְפַת־\rb*\rb |מַרְאֶ֖ה\rb* \rb woman|אִשָּׁ֥ה\rb*, \v 12 \rb and|וְהָיָ֗ה\rb* \rb when|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the Egyptians|הַמִּצְרִ֔ים\rb* \rb see you|יִרְא֤וּ\rb*,\rb |אֹתָךְ֙\rb* \rb they will say|וְאָמְר֖וּ\rb*, ‘\rb This|זֹ֑את\rb* \rb is his wife|אִשְׁתּ֣וֹ\rb*.’ \rb Then they will kill|וְהָרְג֥וּ\rb* \rb me|אֹתִ֖י\rb* \rb but|וְאֹתָ֥ךְ\rb* \rb will let you live|יְחַיּֽוּ׃\rb*. \v 13 \rb Please|נָ֖א\rb* \rb say|אִמְרִי־\rb* \rb you are|אָ֑תְּ\rb* \rb my sister|אֲחֹ֣תִי\rb*, \rb so that|לְמַ֙עַן֙\rb* \rb I will be treated well|יִֽיטַב־\rb*\rb |לִ֣י\rb* \rb for your sake|בַעֲבוּרֵ֔ךְ\rb*, \rb and on account of you|בִּגְלָלֵֽךְ׃\rb* \rb my life|נַפְשִׁ֖י\rb* \rb will be spared|וְחָיְתָ֥ה\rb*.”
\p \v 14 \rb So|וַיְהִ֕י\rb* \rb when Abram|אַבְרָ֖ם\rb* \rb entered|כְּב֥וֹא\rb* \rb Egypt|מִצְרָ֑יְמָה\rb*, \rb the Egyptians|הַמִּצְרִים֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb saw|וַיִּרְא֤וּ\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the woman|הָ֣אִשָּׁ֔ה\rb* \rb was very|מְאֹֽד׃\rb* \rb beautiful|יָפָ֥ה\rb*.\rb |הִ֖וא\rb* \v 15 \rb When Pharaoh’s|פַרְעֹ֔ה\rb* \rb officials|שָׂרֵ֣י\rb* \rb saw|וַיִּרְא֤וּ\rb* \rb Sarai|אֹתָהּ֙\rb*, \rb they commended|וַיְהַֽלְל֥וּ\rb* \rb her|אֹתָ֖הּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb him|פַּרְעֹ֑ה\rb*, \rb and she|הָאִשָּׁ֖ה\rb* \rb was taken|וַתֻּקַּ֥ח\rb* \rb into the palace|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹֽה׃\rb*. \v 16 \rb He treated Abram|וּלְאַבְרָ֥ם\rb* \rb well|הֵיטִ֖יב\rb* \rb on her account|בַּעֲבוּרָ֑הּ\rb*, \rb and Abram acquired|וַֽיְהִי־\rb*\rb |ל֤וֹ\rb* \rb sheep|צֹאן־\rb* \rb and cattle|וּבָקָר֙\rb*, \rb male and female donkeys|וַחֲמֹרִ֔ים\rb*\rb |וַאֲתֹנֹ֖ת\rb*, \rb menservants|וַעֲבָדִים֙\rb* \rb and maidservants|וּשְׁפָחֹ֔ת\rb*, \rb and camels|וּגְמַלִּֽים׃\rb*.
\p \v 17 \rb The LORD, however|יְהוָ֧ה׀\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb afflicted|וַיְנַגַּ֨ע\rb* \rb Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹ֛ה\rb* \rb and his household|בֵּית֑וֹ\rb* \rb with severe|גְּדֹלִ֖ים\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb plagues|נְגָעִ֥ים\rb* \rb because of|עַל־\rb*\rb |דְּבַ֥ר\rb* \rb Abram’s|אַבְרָֽם׃\rb* \rb wife|אֵ֥שֶׁת\rb* \rb Sarai|שָׂרַ֖י\rb*. \v 18 \rb So Pharaoh|פַרְעֹה֙\rb* \rb summoned|וַיִּקְרָ֤א\rb* \rb Abram|לְאַבְרָ֔ם\rb* \rb and asked|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*, “\rb What|מַה־\rb*\rb |זֹּ֖את\rb* \rb have you done|עָשִׂ֣יתָ\rb* \rb to me|לִּ֑י\rb*? \rb Why|לָ֚מָּה\rb* \rb didn’t|לֹא־\rb* \rb you tell|הִגַּ֣דְתָּ\rb* \rb me|לִּ֔י\rb*\rb |כִּ֥י\rb* \rb she|הִֽוא׃\rb* \rb was your wife|אִשְׁתְּךָ֖\rb*? \v 19 \rb Why|לָמָ֤ה\rb* \rb did you say|אָמַ֙רְתָּ֙\rb*, ‘\rb She is|הִ֔וא\rb* \rb my sister|אֲחֹ֣תִי\rb*,’ \rb so that I took|וָאֶקַּ֥ח\rb* \rb her|אֹתָ֛הּ\rb* \rb as my|לִ֖י\rb* \rb wife|לְאִשָּׁ֑ה\rb*? \rb Now then|וְעַתָּ֕ה\rb*, \rb here|הִנֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb is your wife|אִשְׁתְּךָ֖\rb*. \rb Take her|קַ֥ח\rb* \rb and go|וָלֵֽךְ׃\rb*!”
\p \v 20 \rb Then Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹ֖ה\rb* \rb gave his men|אֲנָשִׁ֑ים\rb* \rb orders|וַיְצַ֥ו\rb* \rb concerning Abram|עָלָ֛יו\rb*, \rb and they sent him away|וַֽיְשַׁלְּח֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֹת֛וֹ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb with his wife|אִשְׁתּ֖וֹ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and all his possessions|כָּל־\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb*.
\c 13
\s1 Abram and Lot Part Ways
\p \v 1 \rb So Abram|אַבְרָ֨ם\rb* \rb went up|וַיַּעַל֩\rb* \rb out of Egypt|מִמִּצְרַ֜יִם\rb* \rb into the Negev|הַנֶּֽגְבָּה׃\rb*— \rb he|ה֠וּא\rb* \rb and his wife|וְאִשְׁתּ֧וֹ\rb* \rb and all his possessions|וְכָל־\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb*\rb |ל֛וֹ\rb*— \rb and Lot was|וְל֥וֹט\rb* \rb with him|עִמּ֖וֹ\rb*. \v 2 \rb And Abram|וְאַבְרָ֖ם\rb* \rb had become extremely|מְאֹ֑ד\rb* \rb wealthy|כָּבֵ֣ד\rb* \rb in livestock|בַּמִּקְנֶ֕ה\rb* \rb and silver|בַּכֶּ֖סֶף\rb* \rb and gold|וּבַזָּהָֽב׃\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb From the Negev|מִנֶּ֖גֶב\rb* \rb he journeyed|וַיֵּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb from place to place|לְמַסָּעָ֔יו\rb* \rb toward|בֵּֽית־\rb* \rb Bethel|אֵ֑ל\rb*, \rb until he came|וְעַד־\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb* \rb the place|הַמָּק֗וֹם\rb* \rb between|בֵּ֥ין\rb*\rb |בֵּֽית־\rb* \rb Bethel|אֵ֖ל\rb* \rb and|וּבֵ֥ין\rb* \rb Ai|הָעָֽי׃\rb* \rb where|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb his tent|אָהֳלֹה\rb* \rb had formerly|בַּתְּחִלָּ֔ה\rb* \rb been pitched|הָ֨יָה\rb*\rb |שָׁ֤ם\rb*, \v 4 \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the site|מְקוֹם֙\rb* \rb where|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb he had built|עָ֥שָׂה\rb*\rb |בָּרִאשֹׁנָ֑ה\rb* \rb the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֔חַ\rb*. \rb And there|שָׁ֖ם\rb* \rb Abram|אַבְרָ֖ם\rb* \rb called|וַיִּקְרָ֥א\rb*\rb |שָׁ֛ם\rb* \rb on the name|בְּשֵׁ֥ם\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 5 \rb Now Lot|לְל֔וֹט\rb*, \rb who was traveling|הַהֹלֵ֖ךְ\rb* \rb with|אֶת־\rb* \rb Abram|אַבְרָ֑ם\rb*, \rb also|וְגַם־\rb* \rb had|הָיָ֥ה\rb* \rb flocks|צֹאן־\rb* \rb and herds|וּבָקָ֖ר\rb* \rb and tents|וְאֹהָלִֽים׃\rb*. \v 6 \rb But the land|הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb was unable|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb to support|נָשָׂ֥א\rb* \rb both of them|אֹתָ֛ם\rb* \rb while they stayed|לָשֶׁ֣בֶת\rb* \rb together|יַחְדָּ֑ו\rb*, \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb they had|הָיָ֤ה\rb* \rb so many|רָ֔ב\rb* \rb possessions|רְכוּשָׁם֙\rb* \rb that they were unable|יָֽכְל֖וּ\rb*\rb |וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb to coexist|לָשֶׁ֥בֶת\rb*\rb |יַחְדָּֽו׃\rb*. \v 7 \rb And there was|וַֽיְהִי־\rb* \rb discord|רִ֗יב\rb* \rb between|בֵּ֚ין\rb* \rb the herdsmen|רֹעֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Abram|אַבְרָ֔ם\rb*\rb |וּבֵ֖ין\rb*\rb |מִקְנֵֽה־\rb* \rb and the herdsmen|רֹעֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Lot|ל֑וֹט\rb*\rb |מִקְנֵה־\rb*. \rb At that time|אָ֖ז\rb* \rb the Canaanites|וְהַֽכְּנַעֲנִי֙\rb* \rb and the Perizzites|וְהַפְּרִזִּ֔י\rb* \rb were also living|יֹשֵׁ֥ב\rb* \rb in the land|בָּאָֽרֶץ׃\rb*.
\p \v 8 \rb So Abram|אַבְרָ֜ם\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Lot|ל֗וֹט\rb*, “\rb Please|נָ֨א\rb* \rb let there be|תְהִ֤י\rb* \rb no|אַל־\rb* \rb contention|מְרִיבָה֙\rb* \rb between you and me|בֵּינִ֣י\rb*, \rb or between|וּבֵינֶ֔יךָ\rb*\rb |וּבֵ֥ין\rb* \rb your herdsmen|רֹעַ֖י\rb*\rb |וּבֵ֣ין\rb* \rb and my herdsmen|רֹעֶ֑יךָ\rb*. \rb After all|כִּֽי־\rb*,\rb |אֲנָשִׁ֥ים\rb* \rb we|אֲנָֽחְנוּ׃\rb* \rb are kinsmen|אַחִ֖ים\rb*. \v 9 \rb Is not|הֲלֹ֤א\rb* \rb the whole|כָל־\rb* \rb land|הָאָ֙רֶץ֙\rb* \rb before you|לְפָנֶ֔יךָ\rb*? \rb Now|נָ֖א\rb* \rb separate yourself|הִפָּ֥רֶד\rb* \rb from me|מֵעָלָ֑י\rb*. \rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb you go to the left|הַשְּׂמֹ֣אל\rb*, \rb I will go to the right|וְאֵימִ֔נָה\rb*; \rb if|וְאִם־\rb* \rb you go to the right|הַיָּמִ֖ין\rb*, \rb I will go to the left|וְאַשְׂמְאִֽילָה׃\rb*.”
\s1 Lot Proceeds toward Sodom
\p \v 10 \rb And Lot|ל֣וֹט\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb looked out|וַיִּשָּׂא־\rb*\rb |עֵינָ֗יו\rb* \rb and saw|וַיַּרְא֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb that the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb plain|כִּכַּ֣ר\rb* \rb of the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּ֔ן\rb*,\rb |כִּ֥י\rb* \rb all the way|בֹּאֲכָ֖ה\rb* \rb to Zoar|צֹֽעַר׃\rb*, \rb was well watered|מַשְׁקֶ֑ה\rb*\rb |כֻלָּ֖הּ\rb* \rb like the garden|כְּגַן־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*, \rb like the land|כְּאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֔יִם\rb*. \rb (This was before|לִפְנֵ֣י׀\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb destroyed|שַׁחֵ֣ת\rb* \rb Sodom|סְדֹם֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and Gomorrah|עֲמֹרָ֔ה\rb*.) \v 11 \rb So Lot|ל֗וֹט\rb*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb* \rb chose|וַיִּבְחַר־\rb* \rb the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb plain|כִּכַּ֣ר\rb* \rb of the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּ֔ן\rb* \rb for himself|ל֣וֹ\rb* \rb and|ל֖וֹט\rb* \rb set out|וַיִּסַּ֥ע\rb* \rb toward the east|מִקֶּ֑דֶם\rb*. \rb And Abram and Lot parted|וַיִּפָּ֣רְד֔וּ\rb* \rb company|מֵעַ֥ל\rb*\rb |אִ֖ישׁ\rb*\rb |אָחִֽיו׃\rb*.
\p \v 12 \rb Abram|אַבְרָ֖ם\rb* \rb lived|יָשַׁ֣ב\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶֽרֶץ־\rb* \rb of Canaan|כְּנָ֑עַן\rb*, \rb but Lot|וְל֗וֹט\rb* \rb settled|יָשַׁב֙\rb* \rb in the cities|בְּעָרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the plain|הַכִּכָּ֔ר\rb* \rb and pitched his tent|וַיֶּאֱהַ֖ל\rb* \rb toward|עַד־\rb* \rb Sodom|סְדֹֽם׃\rb*. \v 13 \rb But the men|וְאַנְשֵׁ֣י\rb* \rb of Sodom|סְדֹ֔ם\rb* \rb were wicked|רָעִ֖ים\rb*, \rb sinning|וְחַטָּאִ֑ים\rb* \rb greatly|מְאֹֽד׃\rb* \rb against the LORD|לַיהוָ֖ה\rb*.
\s1 God Renews the Promise to Abram
\p \v 14 \rb After|אַחֲרֵי֙\rb* \rb Lot|ל֣וֹט\rb* \rb had departed|הִפָּֽרֶד־\rb*\rb |מֵֽעִמּ֔וֹ\rb*, \rb the LORD|וַֽיהוָ֞ה\rb* \rb said|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Abram|אַבְרָ֗ם\rb*, “\rb Now|נָ֤א\rb* \rb lift up|שָׂ֣א\rb* \rb your eyes|עֵינֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the place|הַמָּק֖וֹם\rb* \rb where|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb you|אַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb are|שָׁ֑ם\rb*, \rb and look|וּרְאֵ֔ה\rb* \rb to the north|צָפֹ֥נָה\rb* \rb and south|וָנֶ֖גְבָּה\rb* \rb and east|וָקֵ֥דְמָה\rb* \rb and west|וָיָֽמָּה׃\rb*, \v 15 \rb for|כִּ֧י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֛רֶץ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb you|אַתָּ֥ה\rb* \rb see|רֹאֶ֖ה\rb*, \rb I will give|אֶתְּנֶ֑נָּה\rb* \rb to you|לְךָ֣\rb* \rb and your offspring|וּֽלְזַרְעֲךָ֖\rb* \rb forever|עַד־\rb*\rb |עוֹלָֽם׃\rb*.\f + \fr 13:15 \ft Cited in Galatians 3:16\f*
\p \v 16 \rb I will make|וְשַׂמְתִּ֥י\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb your offspring|זַרְעֲךָ֖\rb* \rb like the dust|כַּעֲפַ֣ר\rb* \rb of the earth|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb*, \rb so that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר׀\rb* \rb if|אִם־\rb* \rb one|אִ֗ישׁ\rb* \rb could|יוּכַ֣ל\rb* \rb count|לִמְנוֹת֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the dust|עֲפַ֣ר\rb* \rb of the earth|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb*, \rb then|גַּֽם־\rb* \rb your offspring|זַרְעֲךָ֖\rb* \rb could be counted|יִמָּנֶֽה׃\rb*. \v 17 \rb Get up|ק֚וּם\rb* \rb and walk|הִתְהַלֵּ֣ךְ\rb* \rb around the land|בָּאָ֔רֶץ\rb*, \rb through its length|לְאָרְכָּ֖הּ\rb* \rb and breadth|וּלְרָחְבָּ֑הּ\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb I will give it|אֶתְּנֶֽנָּה׃\rb* \rb to you|לְךָ֖\rb*.”
\p \v 18 \rb So Abram|אַבְרָ֗ם\rb* \rb moved his tent|וַיֶּאֱהַ֣ל\rb* \rb and went|וַיָּבֹ֛א\rb* \rb to live|וַיֵּ֛שֶׁב\rb* \rb near the Oaks|בְּאֵלֹנֵ֥י\rb*\f + \fr 13:18 \ft Or \fqa Terebinths \ft or \fqa Great Trees\f* \rb of Mamre|מַמְרֵ֖א\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb at Hebron|בְּחֶבְר֑וֹן\rb*, \rb where|שָׁ֥ם\rb* \rb he built|וַיִּֽבֶן־\rb* \rb an altar|מִזְבֵּ֖חַ\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָֽה׃פ\rb*.
\c 14
\s1 The War of the Kings
\p \v 1 \rb |וַיְהִ֗י\rb* \rb In those days|בִּימֵי֙\rb* \rb Amraphel|אַמְרָפֶ֣ל\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Shinar|שִׁנְעָ֔ר\rb*,\f + \fr 14:1 \ft That is, Babylonia; also in verse 9\f* \rb Arioch|אַרְי֖וֹךְ\rb* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Ellasar|אֶלָּסָ֑ר\rb*, \rb Chedorlaomer|כְּדָרְלָעֹ֙מֶר֙\rb* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Elam|עֵילָ֔ם\rb*, \rb and Tidal|וְתִדְעָ֖ל\rb* \rb king|מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Goiim|גּוֹיִֽם׃\rb* \v 2 \rb went to|עָשׂ֣וּ\rb* \rb war|מִלְחָמָ֗ה\rb* \rb against|אֶת־\rb* \rb Bera|בֶּ֙רַע֙\rb* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Sodom|סְדֹ֔ם\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Birsha|בִּרְשַׁ֖ע\rb* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Gomorrah|עֲמֹרָ֑ה\rb*, \rb Shinab|שִׁנְאָ֣ב׀\rb* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Admah|אַדְמָ֗ה\rb*, \rb Shemeber|וְשֶׁמְאֵ֙בֶר֙\rb* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Zeboiim|צְבֹיִים\rb*, \rb and the king|וּמֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Bela|בֶּ֖לַע\rb* \rb (that is|הִיא־\rb*, \rb Zoar)|צֹֽעַר׃\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb The latter|אֵ֙לֶּה֙\rb* \rb five|כָּל־\rb* \rb came as allies|חָֽבְר֔וּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the Valley|עֵ֖מֶק\rb* \rb of Siddim|הַשִּׂדִּ֑ים\rb* \rb (that is|ה֖וּא\rb*, \rb the Salt|הַמֶּֽלַח׃\rb* \rb Sea|יָ֥ם\rb*\f + \fr 14:3 \ft That is, the Dead Sea\f*). \v 4 \rb For twelve|שְׁתֵּ֤ים\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵה֙\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָ֔ה\rb* \rb they had been subject|עָבְד֖וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb to Chedorlaomer|כְּדָרְלָעֹ֑מֶר\rb*, \rb but in the thirteenth|וּשְׁלֹשׁ־\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵ֥ה\rb* \rb year|שָׁנָ֖ה\rb* \rb they rebelled|מָרָֽדוּ׃\rb*.
\p \v 5 \rb In the fourteenth|וּבְאַרְבַּע֩\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵ֨ה\rb* \rb year|שָׁנָ֜ה\rb*, \rb Chedorlaomer|כְדָרְלָעֹ֗מֶר\rb* \rb and the kings|וְהַמְּלָכִים֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb allied with him|אִתּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb went out|בָּ֣א\rb* \rb and defeated|וַיַּכּ֤וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Rephaites|רְפָאִים֙\rb* \rb in|בְּעַשְׁתְּרֹ֣ת\rb* \rb Ashteroth-karnaim|קַרְנַ֔יִם\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the Zuzites|הַזּוּזִ֖ים\rb* \rb in Ham|בְּהָ֑ם\rb*,\rb |וְאֵת֙\rb* \rb the Emites|הָֽאֵימִ֔ים\rb* \rb in Shaveh-kiriathaim|בְּשָׁוֵ֖ה\rb*\rb |קִרְיָתָֽיִם׃\rb*, \v 6 \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the Horites|הַחֹרִ֖י\rb* \rb in the area of Mount|בְּהַרְרָ֣ם\rb* \rb Seir|שֵׂעִ֑יר\rb*, \rb as far as|עַ֚ד\rb*\rb |אֵ֣יל\rb* \rb El-paran|פָּארָ֔ן\rb*, \rb which is|אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb near|עַל־\rb* \rb the desert|הַמִּדְבָּֽר׃\rb*. \v 7 \rb Then they turned back|וַ֠יָּשֻׁבוּ\rb* \rb to invade|וַיָּבֹ֜אוּ\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |עֵ֤ין\rb* \rb En-mishpat|מִשְׁפָּט֙\rb* \rb (that is|הִ֣וא\rb*, \rb Kadesh)|קָדֵ֔שׁ\rb*, \rb and they conquered|וַיַּכּ֕וּ\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb territory|שְׂדֵ֖ה\rb* \rb of the Amalekites|הָעֲמָלֵקִ֑י\rb*, \rb as|וְגַם֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb well as the Amorites|הָ֣אֱמֹרִ֔י\rb* \rb who lived|הַיֹּשֵׁ֖ב\rb*\rb |בְּחַֽצְצֹ֥ן\rb* \rb in Hazazon-tamar|תָּמָֽר׃\rb*.
\p \v 8 \rb Then the king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Sodom|סְדֹ֜ם\rb*, \rb the king|וּמֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Gomorrah|עֲמֹרָ֗ה\rb*, \rb the king|וּמֶ֤לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Admah|אַדְמָה֙\rb*, \rb the king|וּמֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Zeboiim|צְבֹיִים\rb*, \rb and the king|וּמֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Bela|בֶּ֖לַע\rb* \rb (that is|הִוא־\rb*, \rb Zoar|צֹ֑עַר\rb*) \rb marched out|וַיֵּצֵ֨א\rb* \rb and arrayed|וַיַּֽעַרְכ֤וּ\rb* \rb themselves|אִתָּם֙\rb* \rb for battle|מִלְחָמָ֔ה\rb* \rb in the Valley|בְּעֵ֖מֶק\rb* \rb of Siddim|הַשִּׂדִּֽים׃\rb*\f + \fr 14:8 \ft That is, the Valley of the Dead Sea\f* \v 9 \rb against|אֵ֣ת\rb* \rb Chedorlaomer|כְּדָרְלָעֹ֜מֶר\rb* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Elam|עֵילָ֗ם\rb*, \rb Tidal|וְתִדְעָל֙\rb* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Goiim|גּוֹיִ֔ם\rb*, \rb Amraphel|וְאַמְרָפֶל֙\rb* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Shinar|שִׁנְעָ֔ר\rb*, \rb and Arioch|וְאַרְי֖וֹךְ\rb* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Ellasar|אֶלָּסָ֑ר\rb*— \rb four|אַרְבָּעָ֥ה\rb* \rb kings|מְלָכִ֖ים\rb* \rb against|אֶת־\rb* \rb five|הַחֲמִשָּֽׁה׃\rb*.
\s1 Abram Rescues Lot
\p \v 10 \rb Now the Valley|וְעֵ֣מֶק\rb* \rb of Siddim|הַשִׂדִּ֗ים\rb* \rb was full of tar|חֵמָ֔ר\rb* \rb pits|בֶּֽאֱרֹ֤ת\rb*\rb |בֶּאֱרֹת֙\rb*, \rb and as the kings|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Sodom|סְדֹ֥ם\rb* \rb and Gomorrah|וַעֲמֹרָ֖ה\rb* \rb fled|וַיָּנֻ֛סוּ\rb*, \rb some men fell|וַיִּפְּלוּ־\rb* \rb into the pits|שָׁ֑מָּה\rb*, \rb but the survivors|וְהַנִּשְׁאָרִ֖ים\rb* \rb fled|נָּֽסוּ׃\rb* \rb to the hill country|הֶ֥רָה\rb*.
\p \v 11 \rb The four kings seized|וַ֠יִּקְחוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the goods|רְכֻ֨שׁ\rb* \rb of Sodom|סְדֹ֧ם\rb* \rb and Gomorrah|וַעֲמֹרָ֛ה\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and all|כָּל־\rb* \rb their food|אָכְלָ֖ם\rb*, \rb and they went on their way|וַיֵּלֵֽכוּ׃\rb*. \v 12 \rb They also carried off|וַיִּקְח֨וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |וַיֵּלֵ֑כוּ\rb* \rb Abram’s|אַבְרָ֖ם\rb* \rb nephew|בֶּן־\rb*\rb |אֲחִ֥י\rb* \rb Lot|ל֧וֹט\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and his possessions|רְכֻשׁ֛וֹ\rb*, \rb since Lot|וְה֥וּא\rb* \rb was living|יֹשֵׁ֖ב\rb* \rb in Sodom|בִּסְדֹֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 13 \rb Then an escapee|הַפָּלִ֔יט\rb* \rb came|וַיָּבֹא֙\rb* \rb and reported this|וַיַּגֵּ֖ד\rb* \rb to Abram|לְאַבְרָ֣ם\rb* \rb the Hebrew|הָעִבְרִ֑י\rb*. \rb Now Abram|וְהוּא֩\rb* \rb was living|שֹׁכֵ֨ן\rb* \rb near the Oaks|בְּאֵֽלֹנֵ֜י\rb*\f + \fr 14:13 \ft Or \fqa Terebinths \ft or \fqa Great Trees\f* \rb of Mamre|מַמְרֵ֣א\rb* \rb the Amorite|הָאֱמֹרִ֗י\rb*, \rb a brother|אֲחִ֤י\rb* \rb of Eshcol|אֶשְׁכֹּל֙\rb* \rb and|וַאֲחִ֣י\rb* \rb Aner|עָנֵ֔ר\rb*, \rb all of whom|וְהֵ֖ם\rb* \rb were bound|בַּעֲלֵ֥י\rb* \rb by treaty|בְרִית־\rb*\f + \fr 14:13 \ft Forms of the Hebrew \fqa berit \ft are translated in most passages as \fqa covenant\ft .\f* \rb to Abram|אַבְרָֽם׃\rb*. \v 14 \rb And when Abram|אַבְרָ֔ם\rb* \rb heard|וַיִּשְׁמַ֣ע\rb* \rb that|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb his relative|אָחִ֑יו\rb* \rb had been captured|נִשְׁבָּ֖ה\rb*, \rb he mobilized|וַיָּ֨רֶק\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the 318|שְׁמֹנָ֤ה\rb*\rb |עָשָׂר֙\rb*\rb |וּשְׁלֹ֣שׁ\rb*\rb |מֵא֔וֹת\rb* \rb trained men|חֲנִיכָ֜יו\rb* \rb born|יְלִידֵ֣י\rb* \rb in his household|בֵית֗וֹ\rb*, \rb and they set out in pursuit|וַיִּרְדֹּ֖ף\rb* \rb as|עַד־\rb* \rb far as Dan|דָּֽן׃\rb*.
\p \v 15 \rb During the night|לַ֛יְלָה\rb*, \rb Abram|ה֥וּא\rb* \rb divided|וַיֵּחָלֵ֨ק\rb*\rb |עֲלֵיהֶ֧ם׀\rb* \rb his forces|וַעֲבָדָ֖יו\rb* \rb and routed Chedorlaomer’s army|וַיַּכֵּ֑ם\rb*, \rb pursuing them|וַֽיִּרְדְּפֵם֙\rb* \rb as far as|עַד־\rb* \rb Hobah|חוֹבָ֔ה\rb*,\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb north|מִשְּׂמֹ֖אל\rb* \rb of Damascus|לְדַמָּֽשֶׂק׃\rb*. \v 16 \rb He retrieved|וַיָּ֕שֶׁב\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the goods|הָרְכֻ֑שׁ\rb*, \rb as well as|וְגַם֩\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his relative|אָחִ֤יו\rb* \rb Lot|ל֨וֹט\rb* \rb and his possessions|וּרְכֻשׁוֹ֙\rb*,\rb |הֵשִׁ֔יב\rb* \rb together with|וְגַ֥ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the women|הַנָּשִׁ֖ים\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and the rest of the people|הָעָֽם׃\rb*.
\s1 Melchizedek Blesses Abram
\p \v 17 \rb After|אַחֲרֵ֣י\rb* \rb Abram returned|שׁוּב֗וֹ\rb* \rb from defeating|מֵֽהַכּוֹת֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |כְּדָר־\rb* \rb Chedorlaomer|לָעֹ֔מֶר\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and the kings|הַמְּלָכִ֖ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb allied with him|אִתּ֑וֹ\rb*, \rb the king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Sodom|סְדֹם֮\rb* \rb went out|וַיֵּצֵ֣א\rb* \rb to meet him|לִקְרָאתוֹ֒\rb* \rb in|אֶל־\rb* \rb the Valley|עֵ֣מֶק\rb* \rb of Shaveh|שָׁוֵ֔ה\rb* \rb (that is|ה֖וּא\rb*, \rb the King’s|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb* \rb Valley)|עֵ֥מֶק\rb*.
\p \v 18 \rb |וּמַלְכִּי־\rb* \rb Then Melchizedek|צֶ֙דֶק֙\rb* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Salem|שָׁלֵ֔ם\rb* \rb brought out|הוֹצִ֖יא\rb* \rb bread|לֶ֣חֶם\rb* \rb and wine|וָיָ֑יִן\rb* — \rb since he|וְה֥וּא\rb* \rb was priest|כֹהֵ֖ן\rb* \rb of God|לְאֵ֥ל\rb* \rb Most High|עֶלְיֽוֹן׃\rb*\f + \fr 14:18 \ft Hebrew \fqa El-Elyon\ft ; also in verses 19, 20, and 22; cited in Hebrews 7:1\f* — \v 19 \rb and he blessed Abram|וַֽיְבָרְכֵ֖הוּ\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּאמַ֑ר\rb*:
\b 
\q1 “\rb Blessed be|בָּר֤וּךְ\rb* \rb Abram|אַבְרָם֙\rb* \rb by God|לְאֵ֣ל\rb* \rb Most High|עֶלְי֔וֹן\rb*,
\q2 \rb Creator|קֹנֵ֖ה\rb* \rb of heaven|שָׁמַ֥יִם\rb* \rb and earth|וָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb*,
\q1 \v 20 \rb and blessed be|וּבָרוּךְ֙\rb* \rb God|אֵ֣ל\rb* \rb Most High|עֶלְי֔וֹן\rb*,
\q2 \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb has delivered|מִגֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb your enemies|צָרֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb into your hand|בְּיָדֶ֑ךָ\rb*.”
\p \rb Then Abram gave|וַיִּתֶּן־\rb* \rb Melchizedek|ל֥וֹ\rb* \rb a tenth|מַעֲשֵׂ֖ר\rb* \rb of everything|מִכֹּֽל׃\rb*.
\p \v 21 \rb The king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Sodom|סְדֹ֖ם\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Abram|אַבְרָ֑ם\rb*, “\rb Give|תֶּן־\rb* \rb me|לִ֣י\rb* \rb the people|הַנֶּ֔פֶשׁ\rb*, \rb but take|קַֽח־\rb* \rb the goods|וְהָרְכֻ֖שׁ\rb* \rb for yourself|לָֽךְ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 22 \rb But Abram|אַבְרָ֖ם\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Sodom|סְדֹ֑ם\rb*, “\rb I have raised|הֲרִימֹ֨תִי\rb* \rb my hand|יָדִ֤י\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb God|אֵ֣ל\rb* \rb Most High|עֶלְי֔וֹן\rb*, \rb Creator|קֹנֵ֖ה\rb* \rb of heaven|שָׁמַ֥יִם\rb* \rb and earth|וָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb*, \v 23 \rb that|אִם־\rb* \rb I will not|וְאִם־\rb* \rb accept|אֶקַּ֖ח\rb* \rb even|וְעַ֣ד\rb* \rb a thread|מִחוּט֙\rb*, \rb or a strap|שְׂרֽוֹךְ־\rb* \rb of a sandal|נַ֔עַל\rb*, \rb or anything|מִכָּל־\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb belongs to you|לָ֑ךְ\rb*, \rb lest|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb you should say|תֹאמַ֔ר\rb*, ‘\rb I have made|אֲנִ֖י\rb* \rb Abram|אַבְרָֽם׃\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb rich|הֶעֱשַׁ֥רְתִּי\rb*.’ \v 24 \rb I will accept nothing|בִּלְעָדַ֗י\rb* \rb but|רַ֚ק\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb my men|הַנְּעָרִ֔ים\rb* \rb have eaten|אָֽכְל֣וּ\rb* \rb and the share|וְחֵ֙לֶק֙\rb* \rb for the men|הָֽאֲנָשִׁ֔ים\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb went|הָלְכ֖וּ\rb* \rb with me|אִתִּ֑י\rb*— \rb Aner|עָנֵר֙\rb*, \rb Eshcol|אֶשְׁכֹּ֣ל\rb*, \rb and Mamre|וּמַמְרֵ֔א\rb*. \rb They|הֵ֖ם\rb* \rb may take|יִקְח֥וּ\rb* \rb their portion|חֶלְקָֽם׃ס\rb*.”
\c 15
\s1 God’s Covenant with Abram
\p \v 1 \rb After|אַחַ֣ר׀\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֗לֶּה\rb* \rb events|הַדְּבָרִ֣ים\rb*, \rb the word|דְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb came|הָיָ֤ה\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Abram|אַבְרָ֔ם\rb* \rb in a vision|בַּֽמַּחֲזֶ֖ה\rb*:\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*
\b 
\q1 “\rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb be afraid|תִּירָ֣א\rb*, \rb Abram|אַבְרָ֗ם\rb*.
\q2 \rb I am|אָנֹכִי֙\rb* \rb your|לָ֔ךְ\rb* \rb shield|מָגֵ֣ן\rb*,
\q2 \rb your very|מְאֹֽד׃\rb* \rb great|הַרְבֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb reward|שְׂכָרְךָ֖\rb*.”
\p \v 2 \rb But Abram|אַבְרָ֗ם\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb O Lord|אֲדֹנָ֤י\rb* \rb GOD|יֱהוִה֙\rb*, \rb what|מַה־\rb* \rb can You give|תִּתֶּן־\rb* \rb me|לִ֔י\rb*, \rb since I|וְאָנֹכִ֖י\rb* \rb remain|הוֹלֵ֣ךְ\rb* \rb childless|עֲרִירִ֑י\rb*, \rb and the heir|וּבֶן־\rb*\rb |מֶ֣שֶׁק\rb* \rb of my house|בֵּיתִ֔י\rb*\rb |ה֖וּא\rb* \rb is Eliezer|אֱלִיעֶֽזֶר׃\rb* \rb of Damascus|דַּמֶּ֥שֶׂק\rb*?” \v 3 \rb Abram|אַבְרָ֔ם\rb* \rb continued|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Behold|הֵ֣ן\rb*, \rb You have given|נָתַ֖תָּה\rb* \rb me|לִ֔י\rb* \rb no|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb offspring|זָ֑רַע\rb*, \rb so|וְהִנֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb a servant|בֶן־\rb* \rb in my household|בֵּיתִ֖י\rb* \rb will be my heir|יוֹרֵ֥שׁ\rb*\rb |אֹתִֽי׃\rb*.”
\p \v 4 \rb Then|וְהִנֵּ֨ה\rb* \rb the word|דְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb came to Abram|אֵלָיו֙\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb*, “\rb This|זֶ֑ה\rb* \rb one will not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb be your heir|יִֽירָשְׁךָ֖\rb*, \rb but|כִּי־\rb*\rb |אִם֙\rb* \rb one|ה֖וּא\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb comes from|יֵצֵ֣א\rb* \rb your own body|מִמֵּעֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb will be your heir|יִֽירָשֶֽׁךָ׃\rb*.” \v 5 \rb And the LORD took|וַיּוֹצֵ֨א\rb* \rb him|אֹת֜וֹ\rb* \rb outside|הַח֗וּצָה\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb*, “\rb Now|נָ֣א\rb* \rb look|הַבֶּט־\rb* \rb to the heavens|הַשָּׁמַ֗יְמָה\rb* \rb and count|וּסְפֹר֙\rb* \rb the stars|הַכּ֣וֹכָבִ֔ים\rb*, \rb if you|אִם־\rb* \rb are able|תּוּכַ֖ל\rb*\rb |לִסְפֹּ֣ר\rb*.”\rb |אֹתָ֑ם\rb* \rb Then He told|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb him|ל֔וֹ\rb*, “\rb So shall|כֹּ֥ה\rb* \rb your offspring|זַרְעֶֽךָ׃\rb* \rb be|יִהְיֶ֖ה\rb*.”\f + \fr 15:5 \ft Cited in Romans 4:18\f*
\p \v 6 \rb Abram believed|וְהֶאֱמִ֖ן\rb* \rb the LORD|בַּֽיהוָ֑ה\rb*, \rb and it was credited|וַיַּחְשְׁבֶ֥הָ\rb* \rb to him|לּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb as righteousness|צְדָקָֽה׃\rb*.\f + \fr 15:6 \ft Cited in Romans 4:3, Romans 4:22, Galatians 3:6, and James 2:23\f*
\p \v 7 \rb The LORD also told|וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb* \rb him|אֵלָ֑יו\rb*, “\rb I|אֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb*, \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb brought you|הוֹצֵאתִ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb out of Ur|מֵא֣וּר\rb* \rb of the Chaldeans|כַּשְׂדִּ֔ים\rb* \rb to give|לָ֧תֶת\rb* \rb you|לְךָ֛\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּ֖את\rb* \rb land|הָאָ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb to possess|לְרִשְׁתָּֽהּ׃\rb*.”
\s1 God Confirms His Promise
\p \v 8 \rb But Abram replied|וַיֹּאמַ֑ר\rb*, “\rb Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יֱהוִ֔ה\rb*, \rb how|בַּמָּ֥ה\rb* \rb can I know|אֵדַ֖ע\rb* \rb that|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb I will possess it|אִֽירָשֶֽׁנָּה׃\rb*?”
\p \v 9 \rb And the LORD said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to him|אֵלָ֗יו\rb*, “\rb Bring|קְחָ֥ה\rb* \rb Me|לִי֙\rb*\rb |מְשֻׁלֶּ֔שֶׁת\rb* \rb a heifer|עֶגְלָ֣ה\rb*,\rb |מְשֻׁלֶּ֖שֶׁת\rb* \rb a goat|וְעֵ֥ז\rb*, \rb and a ram|וְאַ֣יִל\rb*, \rb each three years old|מְשֻׁלָּ֑שׁ\rb*, \rb along with a turtledove|וְתֹ֖ר\rb* \rb and a young pigeon|וְגוֹזָֽל׃\rb*.”
\p \v 10 \rb So Abram brought|וַיִּֽקַּֽח־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb these|אֵ֗לֶּה\rb* \rb to Him|ל֣וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*, \rb split|וַיְבַתֵּ֤ר\rb* \rb each of them|אֹתָם֙\rb* \rb down the middle|בַּתָּ֔וֶךְ\rb*, \rb and laid|וַיִּתֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb the halves|בִּתְר֖וֹ\rb* \rb opposite|לִקְרַ֣את\rb* \rb each|אִישׁ־\rb* \rb other|רֵעֵ֑הוּ\rb*. \rb The birds|הַצִפֹּ֖ר\rb*, \rb however|וְאֶת־\rb*, \rb he did not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb cut in half|בָתָֽר׃\rb*. \v 11 \rb And the birds of prey|הָעַ֖יִט\rb* \rb descended|וַיֵּ֥רֶד\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the carcasses|הַפְּגָרִ֑ים\rb*, \rb but Abram|אַבְרָֽם׃\rb* \rb drove them away|וַיַּשֵּׁ֥ב\rb*.\rb |אֹתָ֖ם\rb* \v 12 \rb As the sun|הַשֶּׁ֙מֶשׁ֙\rb* \rb was|וַיְהִ֤י\rb* \rb setting|לָב֔וֹא\rb*, \rb Abram|אַבְרָ֑ם\rb* \rb fell|נָפְלָ֣ה\rb* \rb into|עַל־\rb* \rb a deep sleep|וְתַרְדֵּמָ֖ה\rb*, \rb and suddenly|וְהִנֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb great|גְדֹלָ֖ה\rb* \rb terror|אֵימָ֛ה\rb* \rb and darkness|חֲשֵׁכָ֥ה\rb* \rb overwhelmed|נֹפֶ֥לֶת\rb* \rb him|עָלָֽיו׃\rb*.
\p \v 13 \rb Then the LORD said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to Abram|לְאַבְרָ֗ם\rb*, “\rb Know for certain|יָדֹ֨עַ\rb*\rb |תֵּדַ֜ע\rb* \rb that|כִּי־\rb* \rb your descendants|זַרְעֲךָ֗\rb* \rb will be|יִהְיֶ֣ה\rb* \rb strangers|גֵ֣ר׀\rb* \rb in a land|בְּאֶ֙רֶץ֙\rb* \rb that is not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb their own|לָהֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb and they will be enslaved|וַעֲבָד֖וּם\rb* \rb and mistreated|וְעִנּ֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֑ם\rb* \rb four|אַרְבַּ֥ע\rb* \rb hundred|מֵא֖וֹת\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָֽה׃\rb*. \v 14 \rb But|וְגַ֧ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb I|אָנֹ֑כִי\rb* \rb will judge|דָּ֣ן\rb* \rb the nation|הַגּ֛וֹי\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb they serve as slaves|יַעֲבֹ֖דוּ\rb*, \rb and afterward|וְאַחֲרֵי־\rb*\rb |כֵ֥ן\rb* \rb they will depart|יֵצְא֖וּ\rb* \rb with many|גָּדֽוֹל׃\rb* \rb possessions|בִּרְכֻ֥שׁ\rb*.\f + \fr 15:14 \ft Cited in Acts 7:6–7\f* \v 15 \rb You, however|וְאַתָּ֛ה\rb*, \rb will go|תָּב֥וֹא\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb your fathers|אֲבֹתֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb in peace|בְּשָׁל֑וֹם\rb* \rb and be buried|תִּקָּבֵ֖ר\rb* \rb at a ripe old age|בְּשֵׂיבָ֥ה\rb*\rb |טוֹבָֽה׃\rb*. \v 16 \rb In the fourth|רְבִיעִ֖י\rb* \rb generation|וְד֥וֹר\rb* \rb your descendants will return|יָשׁ֣וּבוּ\rb* \rb here|הֵ֑נָּה\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֧י\rb* \rb the iniquity|עֲוֺ֥ן\rb* \rb of the Amorites|הָאֱמֹרִ֖י\rb* \rb is not|לֹא־\rb* \rb yet|עַד־\rb*\rb |הֵֽנָּה׃\rb* \rb complete|שָׁלֵ֛ם\rb*.”
\p \v 17 \rb When the sun|הַשֶּׁ֙מֶשׁ֙\rb* \rb had set|בָּ֔אָה\rb* \rb and darkness|וַעֲלָטָ֖ה\rb* \rb had fallen|וַיְהִ֤י\rb*,\rb |הָיָ֑ה\rb* \rb behold|וְהִנֵּ֨ה\rb*, \rb a smoking|עָשָׁן֙\rb* \rb firepot|תַנּ֤וּר\rb* \rb and a flaming|אֵ֔שׁ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb torch|וְלַפִּ֣יד\rb* \rb appeared and passed|עָבַ֔ר\rb* \rb between|בֵּ֖ין\rb* \rb the halves|הַגְּזָרִ֥ים\rb* \rb of the carcasses|הָאֵֽלֶּה׃\rb*. \v 18 \rb On that|הַה֗וּא\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb made|כָּרַ֧ת\rb* \rb a covenant|בְּרִ֣ית\rb* \rb with|אֶת־\rb* \rb Abram|אַבְרָ֖ם\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*, “\rb To your descendants|לְזַרְעֲךָ֗\rb* \rb I have given|נָתַ֙תִּי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּ֔את\rb* \rb land|הָאָ֣רֶץ\rb* — \rb from the river|מִנְּהַ֣ר\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb* \rb the great|הַגָּדֹ֖ל\rb* \rb River|הַנָּהָ֥ר\rb* \rb Euphrates|פְּרָֽת׃\rb*\rb |נְהַר־\rb* — \v 19 \rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the land of the Kenites|הַקֵּינִי֙\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Kenizzites|הַקְּנִזִּ֔י\rb*,\rb |וְאֵ֖ת\rb* \rb Kadmonites|הַקַּדְמֹנִֽי׃\rb*, \v 20 \rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Hittites|הַחִתִּ֥י\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Perizzites|הַפְּרִזִּ֖י\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Rephaites|הָרְפָאִֽים׃\rb*, \v 21 \rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Amorites|הָֽאֱמֹרִי֙\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Canaanites|הַֽכְּנַעֲנִ֔י\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Girgashites|הַגִּרְגָּשִׁ֖י\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and Jebusites|הַיְבוּסִֽי׃ס\rb*.”
\c 16
\s1 Hagar and Ishmael
\p \v 1 \rb Now Abram’s|אַבְרָ֔ם\rb* \rb wife|אֵ֣שֶׁת\rb* \rb Sarai|וְשָׂרַי֙\rb* \rb had borne|יָלְדָ֖ה\rb* \rb him|ל֑וֹ\rb* \rb no children|לֹ֥א\rb*, \rb but|וְלָ֛הּ\rb* \rb she had an Egyptian|מִצְרִ֖ית\rb* \rb maidservant|שִׁפְחָ֥ה\rb* \rb named|וּשְׁמָ֥הּ\rb* \rb Hagar|הָגָֽר׃\rb*. \v 2 \rb So Sarai|שָׂרַ֜י\rb* \rb said|וַתֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Abram|אַבְרָ֗ם\rb*, “\rb Look|הִנֵּה־\rb* \rb now|נָ֞א\rb*, \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb has prevented me|עֲצָרַ֤נִי\rb* \rb from bearing children|מִלֶּ֔דֶת\rb*. \rb Please|נָא֙\rb* \rb go|בֹּא־\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb my maidservant|שִׁפְחָתִ֔י\rb*; \rb perhaps|אוּלַ֥י\rb* \rb I can build a family|אִבָּנֶ֖ה\rb* \rb by her|מִמֶּ֑נָּה\rb*.”
\p \rb And Abram|אַבְרָ֖ם\rb* \rb listened|וַיִּשְׁמַ֥ע\rb* \rb to the voice|לְק֥וֹל\rb* \rb of Sarai|שָׂרָֽי׃\rb*. \v 3 \rb So after|מִקֵּץ֙\rb* \rb he|אַבְרָ֖ם\rb* \rb had lived|לְשֶׁ֥בֶת\rb*\rb |בְּאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb in Canaan|כְּנָ֑עַן\rb* \rb for ten|עֶ֣שֶׂר\rb* \rb years|שָׁנִ֔ים\rb*, \rb his|אַבְרָ֗ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb wife|אֵֽשֶׁת־\rb* \rb Sarai|שָׂרַ֣י\rb* \rb took|וַתִּקַּ֞ח\rb* \rb her Egyptian|הַמִּצְרִית֙\rb* \rb maidservant|שִׁפְחָתָ֔הּ\rb* \rb Hagar|הָגָ֤ר\rb* \rb and gave|וַתִּתֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb her|אֹתָ֛הּ\rb* \rb to Abram|לְאַבְרָ֥ם\rb*\rb |אִישָׁ֖הּ\rb* \rb to be|ל֥וֹ\rb* \rb his wife|לְאִשָּֽׁה׃\rb*. \v 4 \rb And he slept with|וַיָּבֹ֥א\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb Hagar|הָגָ֖ר\rb*, \rb and she conceived|וַתַּ֑הַר\rb*. \rb But when Hagar realized|וַתֵּ֙רֶא֙\rb* \rb that|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb she was pregnant|הָרָ֔תָה\rb*, \rb she began to despise|וַתֵּקַ֥ל\rb*\rb |בְּעֵינֶֽיהָ׃\rb* \rb her mistress|גְּבִרְתָּ֖הּ\rb*.\f + \fr 16:4 \ft Or \fqa her mistress became despised in her sight\f*
\p \v 5 \rb Then Sarai|שָׂרַ֣י\rb* \rb said|וַתֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Abram|אַבְרָם֮\rb*, “\rb May the wrong done to me|חֲמָסִ֣י\rb* \rb be upon you|עָלֶיךָ֒\rb*! \rb I|אָנֹכִ֗י\rb* \rb delivered|נָתַ֤תִּי\rb* \rb my servant|שִׁפְחָתִי֙\rb* \rb into your arms|בְּחֵיקֶ֔ךָ\rb*, \rb and ever since she saw|וַתֵּ֙רֶא֙\rb* \rb that|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb she was pregnant|הָרָ֔תָה\rb*, \rb she has treated me with contempt|וָאֵקַ֖ל\rb*\rb |בְּעֵינֶ֑יהָ\rb*. \rb May the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb judge|יִשְׁפֹּ֥ט\rb* \rb between you and me|בֵּינִ֥י\rb*\rb |וּבֵינֶֽיׄךָ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 6 “\rb Here|הִנֵּ֤ה\rb*,” \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb Abram|אַבְרָ֜ם\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |שָׂרַ֗י\rb*, “\rb your servant|שִׁפְחָתֵךְ֙\rb* \rb is in your hands|בְּיָדֵ֔ךְ\rb*. \rb Do|עֲשִׂי־\rb* \rb whatever you want|הַטּ֣וֹב\rb* \rb with her|לָ֖הּ\rb*.” \rb Then Sarai|שָׂרַ֔י\rb* \rb treated|וַתְּעַנֶּ֣הָ\rb* \rb Hagar so harshly that she fled|וַתִּבְרַ֖ח\rb* \rb from her|מִפָּנֶֽיהָ׃\rb*.
\p \v 7 \rb Now the angel|מַלְאַ֧ךְ\rb*\f + \fr 16:7 \ft Or \fqa Angel\ft ; also in verses 9, 10, and 11; corresponding pronouns may also be capitalized.\f* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb found|וַֽיִּמְצָאָ֞הּ\rb* \rb Hagar by|עַל־\rb* \rb a spring|עֵ֥ין\rb* \rb of water|הַמַּ֖יִם\rb* \rb in the desert|בַּמִּדְבָּ֑ר\rb* —\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb the spring|הָעַ֖יִן\rb* \rb along the road|בְּדֶ֥רֶךְ\rb* \rb to Shur|שֽׁוּר׃\rb*. \v 8 “\rb Hagar|הָגָ֞ר\rb*, \rb servant|שִׁפְחַ֥ת\rb* \rb of Sarai|שָׂרַ֛י\rb*,” \rb he said|וַיֹּאמַ֗ר\rb*, “\rb where|אֵֽי־\rb*\rb |מִזֶּ֥ה\rb* \rb have you come from|בָ֖את\rb*, \rb and where|וְאָ֣נָה\rb* \rb are you going|תֵלֵ֑כִי\rb*?”
\p “\rb I am|אָנֹכִ֖י\rb* \rb running away|בֹּרַֽחַת׃\rb* \rb from|מִפְּנֵי֙\rb* \rb my mistress|גְּבִרְתִּ֔י\rb* \rb Sarai|שָׂרַ֣י\rb*,” \rb she replied|וַתֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*.
\p \v 9 \rb So the angel|מַלְאַ֣ךְ\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb told|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb her|לָהּ֙\rb*, “\rb Return|שׁ֖וּבִי\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb your mistress|גְּבִרְתֵּ֑ךְ\rb* \rb and submit|וְהִתְעַנִּ֖י\rb* \rb to her authority|תַּ֥חַת\rb*\rb |יָדֶֽיהָ׃\rb*.” \v 10 \rb Then the angel|מַלְאַ֣ךְ\rb*\rb |יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb added|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb*, “\rb I will greatly multiply|הַרְבָּ֥ה\rb*\rb |אַרְבֶּ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your offspring|זַרְעֵ֑ךְ\rb* \rb so that|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb they will be too numerous|מֵרֹֽב׃\rb* \rb to count|יִסָּפֵ֖ר\rb*.”
\p \v 11 \rb The angel|מַלְאַ֣ךְ\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb proceeded|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb*\rb |לָהּ֙\rb*:
\b 
\q1 “\rb Behold|הִנָּ֥ךְ\rb*, \rb you have conceived|הָרָ֖ה\rb* \rb and will bear|וְיֹלַ֣דְתְּ\rb* \rb a son|בֵּ֑ן\rb*.
\q2 \rb And you shall name him|וְקָרָ֤את\rb*\rb |שְׁמוֹ֙\rb* \rb Ishmael|יִשְׁמָעֵ֔אל\rb*,\f + \fr 16:11 \fqa Ishmael \ft means \fqa God hears\ft .\f*
\q2 \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb has heard|שָׁמַ֥ע\rb* \rb your cry of affliction|עָנְיֵֽךְ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 12 \rb He|וְה֤וּא\rb* \rb will be|יִהְיֶה֙\rb* \rb a wild donkey|פֶּ֣רֶא\rb* \rb of a man|אָדָ֔ם\rb*,
\q2 \rb and his hand|יָד֣וֹ\rb* \rb will be against everyone|בַכֹּ֔ל\rb*,
\q2 \rb and everyone’s|כֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb hand|וְיַ֥ד\rb* \rb against him|בּ֑וֹ\rb*;
\q1 \rb he will live|יִשְׁכֹּֽן׃\rb* \rb in hostility|וְעַל־\rb*
\q2 \rb toward|פְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb all|כָל־\rb* \rb his brothers|אֶחָ֖יו\rb*.”
\p \v 13 \rb So Hagar gave|וַתִּקְרָ֤א\rb* \rb this name|שֵׁם־\rb* \rb to the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb who had spoken|הַדֹּבֵ֣ר\rb* \rb to her|אֵלֶ֔יהָ\rb*: “\rb You are|אַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb the God|אֵ֣ל\rb* \rb who sees me|רֳאִ֑י\rb*,\f + \fr 16:13 \ft Hebrew \fqa El-Roi\f*” \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb she said|אָֽמְרָ֗ה\rb*, “\rb Here|הֲלֹ֛ם\rb* \rb I have|הֲגַ֥ם\rb* \rb seen|רָאִ֖יתִי\rb*\rb |אַחֲרֵ֥י\rb* \rb the One who sees me|רֹאִֽי׃\rb*!” \v 14 \rb Therefore|עַל־\rb*\rb |כֵּן֙\rb* \rb the well|לַבְּאֵ֔ר\rb* \rb was called|קָרָ֣א\rb*\rb |בְּאֵ֥ר\rb*\rb |לַחַ֖י\rb* \rb Beer-lahai-roi|רֹאִ֑י\rb*.\f + \fr 16:14 \fqa Beer-lahai-roi \ft means \fqa well of the Living One who sees me\ft .\f* \rb It is located|הִנֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb between|בֵין־\rb* \rb Kadesh|קָדֵ֖שׁ\rb*\rb |וּבֵ֥ין\rb* \rb and Bered|בָּֽרֶד׃\rb*.
\p \v 15 \rb And Hagar|הָגָ֛ר\rb* \rb bore|וַתֵּ֧לֶד\rb* \rb Abram|לְאַבְרָ֖ם\rb* \rb a son|בֵּ֑ן\rb*, \rb and Abram|אַבְרָ֧ם\rb* \rb gave|וַיִּקְרָ֨א\rb* \rb the name|שֶׁם־\rb* \rb Ishmael|יִשְׁמָעֵֽאל׃\rb* \rb to the son|בְּנ֛וֹ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb she|הָגָ֖ר\rb* \rb had borne|יָלְדָ֥ה\rb*. \v 16 \rb Abram|וְאַבְרָ֕ם\rb* \rb was eighty-six|שְׁמֹנִ֥ים\rb*\rb |וְשֵׁ֣שׁ\rb* \rb years|שָׁנִ֑ים\rb* \rb old|בֶּן־\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֖ה\rb* \rb when Hagar|הָגָ֥ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb bore|בְּלֶֽדֶת־\rb* \rb Ishmael|יִשְׁמָעֵ֖אל\rb* \rb to him|לְאַבְרָֽם׃ס\rb*.
\c 17
\s1 Abraham to Father Many Nations
\p \v 1 \rb When Abram|אַבְרָ֔ם\rb* \rb was|וַיְהִ֣י\rb* \rb ninety-nine|תִּשְׁעִ֥ים\rb*\rb |וְתֵ֣שַׁע\rb* \rb years|שָׁנִ֑ים\rb* \rb old|בֶּן־\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֖ה\rb*, \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb appeared|וַיֵּרָ֨א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb him|אַבְרָ֗ם\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb*,\rb |אֵלָיו֙\rb* “\rb I|אֲנִי־\rb* \rb am God|אֵ֣ל\rb* \rb Almighty|שַׁדַּ֔י\rb*.\f + \fr 17:1 \ft Hebrew \fqa El-Shaddai\f* \rb Walk|הִתְהַלֵּ֥ךְ\rb* \rb before Me|לְפָנַ֖י\rb* \rb and be|וֶהְיֵ֥ה\rb* \rb blameless|תָמִֽים׃\rb*. \v 2 \rb I will establish|וְאֶתְּנָ֥ה\rb* \rb My covenant|בְרִיתִ֖י\rb* \rb between Me and you|בֵּינִ֣י\rb*,\rb |וּבֵינֶ֑ךָ\rb* \rb and I will multiply|וְאַרְבֶּ֥ה\rb* \rb you|אוֹתְךָ֖\rb* \rb exceedingly|בִּמְאֹ֥ד\rb*\rb |מְאֹֽד׃\rb*.”
\p \v 3 \rb Then Abram|אַבְרָ֖ם\rb* \rb fell facedown|וַיִּפֹּ֥ל\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb*\rb |פָּנָ֑יו\rb*, \rb and God|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb* \rb said|וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb to him|אִתּ֛וֹ\rb*, \v 4 “\rb As for Me|אֲנִ֕י\rb*, \rb this is|הִנֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb My covenant|בְרִיתִ֖י\rb* \rb with you|אִתָּ֑ךְ\rb*: \rb You will be|וְהָיִ֕יתָ\rb* \rb the father|לְאַ֖ב\rb* \rb of many|הֲמ֥וֹן\rb* \rb nations|גּוֹיִֽם׃\rb*. \v 5 \rb No|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb longer will|ע֛וֹד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb you be called|יִקָּרֵ֥א\rb*\rb |שִׁמְךָ֖\rb* \rb Abram|אַבְרָ֑ם\rb*,\f + \fr 17:5 \fqa Abram \ft means \fqa exalted father\ft .\f* \rb but your name|שִׁמְךָ֙\rb* \rb will be|וְהָיָ֤ה\rb* \rb Abraham|אַבְרָהָ֔ם\rb*,\f + \fr 17:5 \fqa Abraham \ft means \fqa father of many\ft .\f* \rb for|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb I have made you|נְתַתִּֽיךָ׃\rb* \rb a father|אַב־\rb* \rb of many|הֲמ֥וֹן\rb* \rb nations|גּוֹיִ֖ם\rb*.\f + \fr 17:5 \ft Cited in Romans 4:17\f*
\p \v 6 \rb I will make you exceedingly|בִּמְאֹ֣ד\rb*\rb |מְאֹ֔ד\rb*\rb |אֹֽתְךָ֙\rb* \rb fruitful|וְהִפְרֵתִ֤י\rb*; \rb I will make|וּנְתַתִּ֖יךָ\rb* \rb nations of you|לְגוֹיִ֑ם\rb*, \rb and kings|וּמְלָכִ֖ים\rb* \rb will descend|יֵצֵֽאוּ׃\rb* \rb from you|מִמְּךָ֥\rb*.
\p \v 7 \rb I will establish|וַהֲקִמֹתִ֨י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My covenant|בְּרִיתִ֜י\rb* \rb as an everlasting|עוֹלָ֑ם\rb* \rb covenant|לִבְרִ֣ית\rb* \rb between Me and you|בֵּינִ֣י\rb*\rb |וּבֵינֶ֗ךָ\rb*\rb |וּבֵ֨ין\rb* \rb and your descendants|אַחֲרֶ֛יךָ\rb*\rb |לְדֹרֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb after you|זַרְעֲךָ֧\rb*, \rb to be|לִהְי֤וֹת\rb* \rb your|לְךָ֙\rb* \rb God|לֵֽאלֹהִ֔ים\rb* \rb and the God of your descendants|וּֽלְזַרְעֲךָ֖\rb* \rb after you|אַחֲרֶֽיךָ׃\rb*.
\p \v 8 \rb And to you|לְ֠ךָ\rb* \rb and your descendants|וּלְזַרְעֲךָ֨\rb*\rb |אֵ֣ת׀\rb* \rb I will give|וְנָתַתִּ֣י\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb where you are residing|מְגֻרֶ֗יךָ\rb*—\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Canaan|כְּנַ֔עַן\rb*— \rb as an eternal|עוֹלָ֑ם\rb* \rb possession|לַאֲחֻזַּ֖ת\rb*; \rb and I will be|וְהָיִ֥יתִי\rb* \rb their|לָהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb God|לֵאלֹהִֽים׃\rb*.”
\s1 The Covenant of Circumcision
\p \v 9 \rb God|אֱלֹהִים֙\rb* \rb also said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Abraham|אַבְרָהָ֔ם\rb*, “\rb You|וְאַתָּ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb must keep|תִשְׁמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb My covenant|בְּרִיתִ֣י\rb*— \rb you|אַתָּ֛ה\rb* \rb and your descendants|וְזַרְעֲךָ֥\rb* \rb in the generations|לְדֹרֹתָֽם׃\rb* \rb after you|אַֽחֲרֶ֖יךָ\rb*. \v 10 \rb This|זֹ֣את\rb* \rb is My covenant|בְּרִיתִ֞י\rb* \rb with|בֵּינִי֙\rb*\rb |וּבֵ֣ינֵיכֶ֔ם\rb*\rb |וּבֵ֥ין\rb* \rb you and your descendants|זַרְעֲךָ֖\rb* \rb after you|אַחֲרֶ֑יךָ\rb*, \rb which|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb you are to keep|תִּשְׁמְר֗וּ\rb*: \rb Every|כָּל־\rb* \rb male among you|זָכָֽר׃\rb* \rb must be circumcised|הִמּ֥וֹל\rb*. \v 11 \rb You are to circumcise|וּנְמַלְתֶּ֕ם\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb the flesh|בְּשַׂ֣ר\rb* \rb of your foreskin|עָרְלַתְכֶ֑ם\rb*, \rb and this will be|וְהָיָה֙\rb* \rb a sign|לְא֣וֹת\rb* \rb of the covenant|בְּרִ֔ית\rb* \rb between Me and you|בֵּינִ֖י\rb*.\rb |וּבֵינֵיכֶֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 12 \rb Generation after generation|לְדֹרֹתֵיכֶ֑ם\rb*, \rb every|כָּל־\rb* \rb male|זָכָ֖ר\rb*\rb |לָכֶ֛ם\rb* \rb must be circumcised|יִמּ֥וֹל\rb*\rb |וּבֶן־\rb* \rb when he is eight|שְׁמֹנַ֣ת\rb* \rb days old|יָמִ֗ים\rb*, \rb including those born|יְלִ֣יד\rb* \rb in your household|בָּ֔יִת\rb* \rb and those purchased|וּמִקְנַת־\rb*\rb |כֶּ֙סֶף֙\rb* \rb from a|מִכֹּ֣ל\rb*\rb |בֶּן־\rb* \rb foreigner|נֵכָ֔ר\rb* — \rb even those|הֽוּא׃\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb are not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb your offspring|מִֽזַּרְעֲךָ֖\rb*. \v 13 \rb Whether they are born|יְלִ֥יד\rb* \rb in your household|בֵּֽיתְךָ֖\rb* \rb or purchased|וּמִקְנַ֣ת\rb*\rb |כַּסְפֶּ֑ךָ\rb*, \rb they must be circumcised|הִמּ֧וֹל׀\rb*\rb |יִמּ֛וֹל\rb*. \rb My covenant|בְרִיתִ֛י\rb* \rb in your flesh|בִּבְשַׂרְכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb will be|וְהָיְתָ֧ה\rb* \rb an everlasting|עוֹלָֽם׃\rb* \rb covenant|לִבְרִ֥ית\rb*.
\p \v 14 \rb |וְעָרֵ֣ל׀\rb* \rb But if any male|זָכָ֗ר\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb is not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb circumcised|יִמּוֹל֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |בְּשַׂ֣ר\rb*\rb |עָרְלָת֔וֹ\rb*, \rb he|הַהִ֖וא\rb*\rb |הַנֶּ֥פֶשׁ\rb* \rb will be cut off|וְנִכְרְתָ֛ה\rb* \rb from his people|מֵעַמֶּ֑יהָ\rb*;\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb he has broken|הֵפַֽר׃ס\rb* \rb My covenant|בְּרִיתִ֖י\rb*.”
\p \v 15 \rb Then God|אֱלֹהִים֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Abraham|אַבְרָהָ֔ם\rb*, “\rb As for Sarai|שָׂרַ֣י\rb* \rb your wife|אִשְׁתְּךָ֔\rb*, \rb do not|לֹא־\rb* \rb call|תִקְרָ֥א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb her|שְׁמָ֖הּ\rb* \rb Sarai|שָׂרָ֑י\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb her name is to be|שְׁמָֽהּ׃\rb* \rb Sarah|שָׂרָ֖ה\rb*.\f + \fr 17:15 \ft Both \fqa Sarai \ft and \fqa Sarah \ft mean \fqa princess\ft ; the change in spelling may reflect the difference in dialect between Ur and Canaan.\f* \v 16 \rb And I will bless her|וּבֵרַכְתִּ֣י\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֔הּ\rb* \rb and will surely|וְגַ֨ם\rb* \rb give|נָתַ֧תִּי\rb* \rb you|לְךָ֖\rb* \rb a son|בֵּ֑ן\rb* \rb by her|מִמֶּ֛נָּה\rb*. \rb I will bless her|וּבֵֽרַכְתִּ֙יהָ֙\rb*, \rb and she will be|וְהָֽיְתָ֣ה\rb* \rb the mother of nations|לְגוֹיִ֔ם\rb*; \rb kings|מַלְכֵ֥י\rb* \rb of peoples|עַמִּ֖ים\rb* \rb will descend|יִהְיֽוּ׃\rb* \rb from her|מִמֶּ֥נָּה\rb*.”
\p \v 17 \rb Abraham|אַבְרָהָ֛ם\rb* \rb fell facedown|וַיִּפֹּ֧ל\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb*.\rb |פָּנָ֖יו\rb* \rb Then he laughed|וַיִּצְחָ֑ק\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to himself|בְּלִבּ֗וֹ\rb*, “\rb Can a child be born|יִוָּלֵ֔ד\rb*\rb |וְאִ֨ם־\rb* \rb to a man who is|הַלְּבֶ֤ן\rb* \rb a hundred|מֵאָֽה־\rb* \rb years old|שָׁנָה֙\rb*? \rb Can Sarah|שָׂרָ֔ה\rb*\rb |הֲבַת־\rb* \rb give birth|תֵּלֵֽד׃\rb* \rb at the age of ninety|תִּשְׁעִ֥ים\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֖ה\rb*?” \v 18 \rb And Abraham|אַבְרָהָ֖ם\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb God|הָֽאֱלֹהִ֑ים\rb*, “\rb O that|ל֥וּ\rb* \rb Ishmael|יִשְׁמָעֵ֖אל\rb* \rb might live|יִחְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb under Your blessing|לְפָנֶֽיךָ׃\rb*!”
\p \v 19 \rb But God|אֱלֹהִ֗ים\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Your wife|אִשְׁתְּךָ֗\rb* \rb Sarah|שָׂרָ֣ה\rb* \rb will indeed|אֲבָל֙\rb* \rb bear|יֹלֶ֤דֶת\rb* \rb you|לְךָ֙\rb* \rb a son|בֵּ֔ן\rb*, \rb and you are to name|וְקָרָ֥אתָ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb him|שְׁמ֖וֹ\rb* \rb Isaac|יִצְחָ֑ק\rb*.\f + \fr 17:19 \fqa Isaac \ft means \fqa he laughs\ft .\f* \rb I will establish|וַהֲקִמֹתִ֨י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My covenant|בְּרִיתִ֥י\rb* \rb with him|אִתּ֛וֹ\rb* \rb as an everlasting|עוֹלָ֖ם\rb* \rb covenant|לִבְרִ֥ית\rb* \rb for his descendants|לְזַרְע֥וֹ\rb* \rb after him|אַחֲרָֽיו׃\rb*. \v 20 \rb As for Ishmael|וּֽלְיִשְׁמָעֵ֘אל\rb*, \rb I have heard you|שְׁמַעְתִּיךָ֒\rb*, \rb and I will surely|הִנֵּ֣ה׀\rb* \rb bless|בֵּרַ֣כְתִּי\rb* \rb him|אֹת֗וֹ\rb*; \rb I will make him fruitful|וְהִפְרֵיתִ֥י\rb*\rb |אֹת֛וֹ\rb* \rb and multiply|וְהִרְבֵּיתִ֥י\rb* \rb him|אֹת֖וֹ\rb* \rb greatly|בִּמְאֹ֣ד\rb*\rb |מְאֹ֑ד\rb*. \rb He will become the father|יוֹלִ֔יד\rb* \rb of twelve|שְׁנֵים־\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֤ר\rb* \rb rulers|נְשִׂיאִם֙\rb*, \rb and I will make him|וּנְתַתִּ֖יו\rb* \rb into a great|גָּדֽוֹל׃\rb* \rb nation|לְג֥וֹי\rb*. \v 21 \rb But|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb I will establish|אָקִ֣ים\rb* \rb My covenant|בְּרִיתִ֖י\rb* \rb with|אֶת־\rb* \rb Isaac|יִצְחָ֑ק\rb*, \rb whom|אֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb Sarah|שָׂרָה֙\rb* \rb will bear|תֵּלֵ֨ד\rb* \rb to you|לְךָ֤\rb* \rb at this|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb time|לַמּוֹעֵ֣ד\rb* \rb next|הָאַחֶֽרֶת׃\rb* \rb year|בַּשָּׁנָ֖ה\rb*.”
\p \v 22 \rb When He had finished|וַיְכַ֖ל\rb* \rb speaking|לְדַבֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb with Abraham|אִתּ֑וֹ\rb*, \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb* \rb went up|וַיַּ֣עַל\rb* \rb from|מֵעַ֖ל\rb* \rb him|אַבְרָהָֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 23 \rb On that|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb very|בְּעֶ֙צֶם֙\rb* \rb day|הַיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb Abraham|אַבְרָהָ֜ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb took|וַיִּקַּ֨ח\rb* \rb his son|בְּנ֗וֹ\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֨ת\rb* \rb Ishmael|יִשְׁמָעֵ֣אל\rb* \rb and all|כָּל־\rb* \rb those born|יְלִידֵ֤י\rb* \rb in his household|בֵיתוֹ֙\rb*\rb |וְאֵת֙\rb* \rb or purchased|מִקְנַ֣ת\rb* \rb with his money|כַּסְפּ֔וֹ\rb*—\rb |כָּל־\rb* \rb every|כָּל־\rb* \rb male|זָכָ֕ר\rb* \rb among the members|בְּאַנְשֵׁ֖י\rb* \rb of Abraham’s|אַבְרָהָ֑ם\rb* \rb household|בֵּ֣ית\rb*— \rb and he circumcised them|וַיָּ֜מָל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |בְּשַׂ֣ר\rb*\rb |עָרְלָתָ֗ם\rb*, \rb just as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִֽים׃\rb* \rb had told|דִּבֶּ֥ר\rb* \rb him|אִתּ֖וֹ\rb*.
\p \v 24 \rb So Abraham|וְאַ֨בְרָהָ֔ם\rb* \rb was ninety-nine|תִּשְׁעִ֥ים\rb*\rb |וָתֵ֖שַׁע\rb* \rb years old|בֶּן־\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֑ה\rb*\rb |בְּשַׂ֥ר\rb*\rb |עָרְלָתֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb when he was circumcised|בְּהִמֹּל֖וֹ\rb*, \v 25 \rb and his son|בְּנ֔וֹ\rb* \rb Ishmael|וְיִשְׁמָעֵ֣אל\rb* \rb was thirteen|שְׁלֹ֥שׁ\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵ֖ה\rb*\rb |בֶּן־\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֑ה\rb*\rb |בְּשַׂ֥ר\rb*\rb |עָרְלָתֽוֹ׃\rb*\rb |בְּהִ֨מֹּל֔וֹ\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb*; \v 26 \rb Abraham|אַבְרָהָ֑ם\rb* \rb and his son|בְּנֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb Ishmael|וְיִשְׁמָעֵ֖אל\rb* \rb were circumcised|נִמּ֖וֹל\rb* \rb on the|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb same|בְּעֶ֙צֶם֙\rb* \rb day|הַיּ֣וֹם\rb*. \v 27 \rb And all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the men|אַנְשֵׁ֤י\rb* \rb of Abraham’s household|בֵיתוֹ֙\rb*— \rb both servants born|יְלִ֣יד\rb* \rb in his household|בָּ֔יִת\rb* \rb and those purchased|וּמִקְנַת־\rb*\rb |כֶּ֖סֶף\rb*\rb |מֵאֵ֣ת\rb*\rb |אִתּֽוֹ׃פ\rb* \rb from foreigners|בֶּן־\rb*\rb |נֵכָ֑ר\rb*— \rb were circumcised with him|נִמֹּ֖לוּ\rb*.
\c 18
\s1 The Three Visitors
\p \v 1 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb appeared|וַיֵּרָ֤א\rb* \rb to Abraham|אֵלָיו֙\rb* \rb by the Oaks|בְּאֵלֹנֵ֖י\rb*\f + \fr 18:1 \ft Or \fqa Terebinths \ft or \fqa Great Trees\f* \rb of Mamre|מַמְרֵ֑א\rb* \rb in the heat|כְּחֹ֥ם\rb* \rb of the day|הַיּֽוֹם׃\rb*, \rb while he|וְה֛וּא\rb* \rb was sitting|יֹשֵׁ֥ב\rb* \rb at the entrance|פֶּֽתַח־\rb* \rb of his tent|הָאֹ֖הֶל\rb*. \v 2 \rb And Abraham looked up|וַיִּשָּׂ֤א\rb*\rb |עֵינָיו֙\rb* \rb and saw|וַיַּ֔רְא\rb*\rb |וְהִנֵּה֙\rb* \rb three|שְׁלֹשָׁ֣ה\rb* \rb men|אֲנָשִׁ֔ים\rb* \rb standing|נִצָּבִ֖ים\rb* \rb nearby|עָלָ֑יו\rb*. \rb When he saw them|וַיַּ֗רְא\rb*, \rb he ran from|וַיָּ֤רָץ\rb* \rb the entrance|מִפֶּ֣תַח\rb* \rb of his tent|הָאֹ֔הֶל\rb* \rb to meet them|לִקְרָאתָם֙\rb* \rb and bowed low|וַיִּשְׁתַּ֖חוּ\rb* \rb to the ground|אָֽרְצָה׃\rb*.
\p \v 3 “\rb My lord|אֲדֹנָ֗י\rb*,” \rb said Abraham|וַיֹּאמַ֑ר\rb*, “\rb if|אִם־\rb* \rb I have found|מָצָ֤אתִי\rb* \rb favor|חֵן֙\rb* \rb in your sight|בְּעֵינֶ֔יךָ\rb*, \rb please|נָ֨א\rb* \rb do not|אַל־\rb*\rb |נָ֥א\rb* \rb pass|תַעֲבֹ֖ר\rb*\rb |מֵעַ֥ל\rb* \rb your servant by|עַבְדֶּֽךָ׃\rb*. \v 4 \rb Let a little|מְעַט־\rb* \rb water|מַ֔יִם\rb* \rb be brought|יֻקַּֽח־\rb*,\rb |נָ֣א\rb* \rb that you may wash|וְרַחֲצ֖וּ\rb* \rb your feet|רַגְלֵיכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb and rest|וְהִֽשָּׁעֲנ֖וּ\rb* \rb yourselves under|תַּ֥חַת\rb* \rb the tree|הָעֵֽץ׃\rb*. \v 5 \rb And I will bring|וְאֶקְחָ֨ה\rb* \rb a bit|פַת־\rb* \rb of bread|לֶ֜חֶם\rb* \rb so that you may refresh|וְסַעֲד֤וּ\rb* \rb yourselves|לִבְּכֶם֙\rb*. \rb This is why|כִּֽי־\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb*\rb |כֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb you have passed|תַּעֲבֹ֔רוּ\rb* \rb your servant’s way|עַבְדְּכֶ֑ם\rb*. \rb After that|אַחַ֣ר\rb*, \rb you may continue on your way|עֲבַרְתֶּ֖ם\rb*\rb |עַֽל־\rb*.”
\p “\rb Yes|כֵּ֥ן\rb*,” \rb they replied|וַיֹּ֣אמְר֔וּ\rb*, “\rb you may do|תַּעֲשֶׂ֖ה\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you have said|דִּבַּֽרְתָּ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 6 \rb So Abraham|אַבְרָהָ֛ם\rb* \rb hurried|וַיְמַהֵ֧ר\rb* \rb into the tent|הָאֹ֖הֱלָה\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Sarah|שָׂרָ֑ה\rb*, “\rb Quick! Prepare|מַהֲרִ֞י\rb* \rb three|שְׁלֹ֤שׁ\rb* \rb seahs|סְאִים֙\rb* \rb of fine|סֹ֔לֶת\rb* \rb flour|קֶ֣מַח\rb*,\f + \fr 18:6 \fqa 3 seahs \ft is approximately 19.8 dry quarts or 21.9 liters (probably about 24.5 pounds or 11.1 kilograms of flour).\f* \rb knead it|ל֖וּשִׁי\rb*, \rb and bake|וַעֲשִׂ֥י\rb* \rb some bread|עֻגֽוֹת׃\rb*.”
\p \v 7 \rb Meanwhile, Abraham|אַבְרָהָ֑ם\rb* \rb ran|רָ֣ץ\rb* \rb to|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb the herd|הַבָּקָ֖ר\rb*, \rb selected|וַיִּקַּ֨ח\rb* \rb a tender|רַ֤ךְ\rb* \rb and choice|וָטוֹב֙\rb* \rb calf|בֶּן־\rb*\rb |בָּקָ֜ר\rb*, \rb and gave|וַיִּתֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb it to|אֶל־\rb* \rb a servant|הַנַּ֔עַר\rb*, \rb who hurried|וַיְמַהֵ֖ר\rb* \rb to prepare|לַעֲשׂ֥וֹת\rb* \rb it|אֹתֽוֹ׃\rb*. \v 8 \rb Then Abraham brought|וַיִּקַּ֨ח\rb* \rb curds|חֶמְאָ֜ה\rb* \rb and milk|וְחָלָ֗ב\rb* \rb and the calf|וּבֶן־\rb*\rb |הַבָּקָר֙\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb had been prepared|עָשָׂ֔ה\rb*, \rb and he set them|וַיִּתֵּ֖ן\rb* \rb before the men|לִפְנֵיהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb and|וְהֽוּא־\rb* \rb stood|עֹמֵ֧ד\rb* \rb by them|עֲלֵיהֶ֛ם\rb* \rb under|תַּ֥חַת\rb* \rb the tree|הָעֵ֖ץ\rb* \rb as they ate|וַיֹּאכֵֽלוּ׃\rb*.
\s1 Sarah Laughs at the Promise
\p \v 9 “\rb Where|אַיֵּ֖ה\rb* \rb is your wife|אִשְׁתֶּ֑ךָ\rb* \rb Sarah|שָׂרָ֣ה\rb*?” \rb they asked|וַיֹּאמְר֣וּ\rb*.\rb |אֵׄלָׄ֔יׄוׄ\rb*
\p “\rb There|הִנֵּ֥ה\rb*, \rb in the tent|בָאֹֽהֶל׃\rb*,” \rb he replied|וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb*.
\p \v 10 \rb Then the LORD said|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*, “\rb I will surely return|שׁ֣וֹב\rb*\rb |אָשׁ֤וּב\rb* \rb to you|אֵלֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb at this time next year|כָּעֵ֣ת\rb*\rb |חַיָּ֔ה\rb*,\rb |וְהִנֵּה־\rb* \rb and your wife|אִשְׁתֶּ֑ךָ\rb* \rb Sarah|לְשָׂרָ֣ה\rb* \rb will have a son|בֵ֖ן\rb*!”
\p \rb Now Sarah|וְשָׂרָ֥ה\rb*\rb |וְה֥וּא\rb* \rb was behind him|אַחֲרָֽיו׃\rb*, \rb listening|שֹׁמַ֛עַת\rb* \rb at the entrance|פֶּ֥תַח\rb* \rb to the tent|הָאֹ֖הֶל\rb*. \v 11 \rb And Abraham|וְאַבְרָהָ֤ם\rb* \rb and Sarah|וְשָׂרָה֙\rb* \rb were already old|זְקֵנִ֔ים\rb* \rb and well along|בָּאִ֖ים\rb* \rb in years|בַּיָּמִ֑ים\rb*; \rb Sarah|לְשָׂרָ֔ה\rb* \rb had passed|חָדַל֙\rb*\rb |לִהְי֣וֹת\rb* \rb the age of childbearing|אֹ֖רַח\rb*\rb |כַּנָּשִֽׁים׃\rb*. \v 12 \rb So she|שָׂרָ֖ה\rb* \rb laughed|וַתִּצְחַ֥ק\rb* \rb to herself|בְּקִרְבָּ֣הּ\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*, “\rb After|אַחֲרֵ֤י\rb* \rb I am worn out|בְלֹתִי֙\rb* \rb and my master|וַֽאדֹנִ֖י\rb* \rb is old|זָקֵֽן׃\rb*, \rb will I now have|הָֽיְתָה־\rb*\rb |לִּ֣י\rb* \rb this pleasure|עֶדְנָ֔ה\rb*?”
\p \v 13 \rb And the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb asked|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb* \rb Abraham|אַבְרָהָ֑ם\rb*, “\rb Why|לָ֣מָּה\rb*\rb |זֶּה֩\rb* \rb did Sarah|שָׂרָ֜ה\rb* \rb laugh|צָחֲקָ֨ה\rb* \rb and say|לֵאמֹ֗ר\rb*, ‘\rb Can I really|הַאַ֥ף\rb*\rb |אֻמְנָ֛ם\rb* \rb bear a child|אֵלֵ֖ד\rb* \rb when I am|וַאֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb old|זָקַֽנְתִּי׃\rb*?’ \v 14 \rb Is anything|דָּבָ֑ר\rb* \rb too difficult|הֲיִפָּלֵ֥א\rb* \rb for the LORD|מֵיְהוָ֖ה\rb*? \rb At the appointed time|לַמּוֹעֵ֞ד\rb* \rb I will return|אָשׁ֥וּב\rb* \rb to you|אֵלֶ֛יךָ\rb* — \rb in about a year|כָּעֵ֥ת\rb*\rb |חַיָּ֖ה\rb* — \rb and Sarah|וּלְשָׂרָ֥ה\rb* \rb will have a son|בֵֽן׃\rb*.”\f + \fr 18:14 \ft Cited in Romans 9:9\f*
\p \v 15 \rb But Sarah|שָׂרָ֧ה׀\rb* \rb was afraid|יָרֵ֑אָה\rb*, \rb so|כִּ֣י׀\rb* \rb she denied it|וַתְּכַחֵ֨שׁ\rb* \rb and said|לֵאמֹ֛ר\rb*, \rb “I did not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb laugh|צָחַ֖קְתִּי\rb*.”
\p “\rb No|לֹ֖א\rb*,” \rb replied the LORD|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר׀\rb*, “\rb but|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb you did laugh|צָחָֽקְתְּ׃\rb*.”
\s1 Abraham Intercedes for Sodom
\p \v 16 \rb When the men got up|וַיָּקֻ֤מוּ\rb* \rb to leave|מִשָּׁם֙\rb*, \rb they|הָֽאֲנָשִׁ֔ים\rb* \rb looked out|וַיַּשְׁקִ֖פוּ\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb*\rb |פְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb Sodom|סְדֹ֑ם\rb*, \rb and Abraham|וְאַ֨בְרָהָ֔ם\rb* \rb walked along|הֹלֵ֥ךְ\rb* \rb with them|עִמָּ֖ם\rb* \rb to see them off|לְשַׁלְּחָֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 17 \rb And the LORD|וַֽיהֹוָ֖ה\rb* \rb said|אָמָ֑ר\rb*, “\rb Shall I|אֲנִי֙\rb* \rb hide|הַֽמְכַסֶּ֤ה\rb* \rb from Abraham|מֵֽאַבְרָהָ֔ם\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb am about to do|עֹשֶֽׂה׃\rb*? \v 18 \rb Abraham|וְאַ֨בְרָהָ֔ם\rb* \rb will surely become|הָי֧וֹ\rb*\rb |יִֽהְיֶ֛ה\rb* \rb a great|גָּד֖וֹל\rb* \rb and powerful|וְעָצ֑וּם\rb* \rb nation|לְג֥וֹי\rb*, \rb and through him|ב֔וֹ\rb* \rb all|כֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb the nations|גּוֹיֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the earth|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb* \rb will be blessed|וְנִ֨בְרְכוּ\rb*. \v 19 \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb I have chosen|יְדַעְתִּ֗יו\rb* \rb him|לְמַעַן֩\rb*, \rb so that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb he will command|יְצַוֶּ֜ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his children|בָּנָ֤יו\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb his household|בֵּיתוֹ֙\rb* \rb after him|אַחֲרָ֔יו\rb* \rb to keep|וְשָֽׁמְרוּ֙\rb* \rb the way|דֶּ֣רֶךְ\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb by doing|לַעֲשׂ֥וֹת\rb* \rb what is right|צְדָקָ֖ה\rb* \rb and just|וּמִשְׁפָּ֑ט\rb*, \rb in order that|לְמַ֗עַן\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb may bring|הָבִ֤יא\rb* \rb upon|עַל־\rb* \rb Abraham|אַבְרָהָ֔ם\rb*\rb |אֵ֥ת\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb He has promised|דִּבֶּ֖ר\rb*\rb |עָלָֽיו׃\rb*.”
\p \v 20 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb The outcry|זַעֲקַ֛ת\rb* \rb against Sodom|סְדֹ֥ם\rb* \rb and Gomorrah|וַעֲמֹרָ֖ה\rb* \rb is great|רָ֑בָּה\rb*. \rb Because|כִּי־\rb* \rb their sin|וְחַ֨טָּאתָ֔ם\rb*\rb |כִּ֥י\rb* \rb is so|מְאֹֽד׃\rb* \rb grievous|כָבְדָ֖ה\rb*, \v 21 \rb I will go down|אֵֽרֲדָה־\rb*\rb |נָּ֣א\rb* \rb to see|וְאֶרְאֶ֔ה\rb* \rb if their actions|עָשׂ֣וּ׀\rb* \rb fully|כָּלָ֑ה\rb* \rb justify the outcry|הַכְּצַעֲקָתָ֛הּ\rb* \rb that has reached|הַבָּ֥אָה\rb* \rb Me|אֵלַ֖י\rb*. \rb If|וְאִם־\rb* \rb not|לֹ֖א\rb*, \rb I will find out|אֵדָֽעָה׃\rb*.”
\p \v 22 \rb And the two men|הָֽאֲנָשִׁ֔ים\rb* \rb turned|וַיִּפְנ֤וּ\rb* \rb away|מִשָּׁם֙\rb* \rb and went|וַיֵּלְכ֖וּ\rb* \rb toward Sodom|סְדֹ֑מָה\rb*, \rb but Abraham|וְאַ֨בְרָהָ֔ם\rb* \rb remained|עוֹדֶ֥נּוּ\rb* \rb standing|עֹמֵ֖ד\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 23 \rb Abraham|אַבְרָהָ֖ם\rb* \rb stepped forward|וַיִּגַּ֥שׁ\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּאמַ֑ר\rb*, “\rb Will You really|הַאַ֣ף\rb* \rb sweep away|תִּסְפֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb the righteous|צַדִּ֖יק\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb the wicked|רָשָֽׁע׃\rb*? \v 24 \rb What if|אוּלַ֥י\rb* \rb there are|יֵ֛שׁ\rb* \rb fifty|חֲמִשִּׁ֥ים\rb* \rb righteous ones|צַדִּיקִ֖ם\rb* \rb in|בְּת֣וֹךְ\rb* \rb the city|הָעִ֑יר\rb*? \rb Will You really|הַאַ֤ף\rb* \rb sweep it away|תִּסְפֶּה֙\rb* \rb and not|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb spare|תִשָּׂ֣א\rb* \rb the place|לַמָּק֔וֹם\rb* \rb for the sake of|לְמַ֛עַן\rb* \rb the fifty|חֲמִשִּׁ֥ים\rb* \rb righteous ones|הַצַּדִּיקִ֖ם\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb are there|בְּקִרְבָּֽהּ׃\rb*? \v 25 \rb Far be it|חָלִ֨לָה\rb* \rb from You|לְּךָ֜\rb* \rb to do|מֵעֲשֹׂ֣ת׀\rb* \rb such|הַזֶּ֗ה\rb* \rb a thing|כַּדָּבָ֣ר\rb* — \rb to kill|לְהָמִ֤ית\rb* \rb the righteous|צַדִּיק֙\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb the wicked|רָשָׁ֔ע\rb*, \rb so that the righteous|כַצַּדִּ֖יק\rb* \rb and the wicked|כָּרָשָׁ֑ע\rb* \rb are treated alike|וְהָיָ֥ה\rb*. \rb Far be it|חָלִ֣לָה\rb* \rb from You|לָּ֔ךְ\rb*! \rb Will not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb the Judge|הֲשֹׁפֵט֙\rb* \rb of all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the earth|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb do|יַעֲשֶׂ֖ה\rb* \rb what is right|מִשְׁפָּֽט׃\rb*?”
\p \v 26 \rb So the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb I find|אֶמְצָ֥א\rb* \rb fifty|חֲמִשִּׁ֥ים\rb* \rb righteous ones|צַדִּיקִ֖ם\rb* \rb within|בְּת֣וֹךְ\rb* \rb the city|הָעִ֑יר\rb* \rb of Sodom|בִסְדֹ֛ם\rb*, \rb on their account|בַּעֲבוּרָֽם׃\rb* \rb I will spare|וְנָשָׂ֥אתִי\rb* \rb the whole|לְכָל־\rb* \rb place|הַמָּק֖וֹם\rb*.”
\p \v 27 \rb Then Abraham|אַבְרָהָ֖ם\rb*\rb |וַיֹּאמַ֑ר\rb* \rb answered|וַיַּ֥עַן\rb*, “\rb Now that|הִנֵּה־\rb*\rb |נָ֤א\rb* \rb I have ventured|הוֹאַ֙לְתִּי֙\rb* \rb to speak|לְדַבֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֔י\rb*— \rb though I|וְאָנֹכִ֖י\rb* \rb am but dust|עָפָ֥ר\rb* \rb and ashes|וָאֵֽפֶר׃\rb*— \v 28 \rb suppose|א֠וּלַי\rb* \rb the fifty|חֲמִשִּׁ֤ים\rb* \rb righteous ones|הַצַּדִּיקִם֙\rb* \rb lack|יַחְסְר֞וּן\rb* \rb five|חֲמִשָּׁ֔ה\rb*. \rb Will You destroy|הֲתַשְׁחִ֥ית\rb* \rb the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb city|הָעִ֑יר\rb* \rb for the lack of five|בַּחֲמִשָּׁ֖ה\rb*?”\rb |אֶת־\rb*
\p \rb He replied|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb*, “\rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb I find|אֶמְצָ֣א\rb* \rb forty-five|אַרְבָּעִ֖ים\rb*\rb |וַחֲמִשָּֽׁה׃\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֔ם\rb*, \rb I will not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb destroy it|אַשְׁחִ֔ית\rb*.”
\p \v 29 \rb Once again|וַיֹּ֨סֶף\rb*\rb |ע֜וֹד\rb* \rb Abraham spoke|לְדַבֵּ֤ר\rb* \rb to the LORD|אֵלָיו֙\rb*, “\rb Suppose|אוּלַ֛י\rb* \rb forty|אַרְבָּעִ֑ים\rb*\rb |וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb* \rb are found|יִמָּצְא֥וּן\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֖ם\rb*?”
\p \rb He answered|וַיֹּאמַ֔ר\rb*, “\rb On account|בַּעֲב֖וּר\rb* \rb of the forty|הָאַרְבָּעִֽים׃\rb*, \rb I will not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb do it|אֶֽעֱשֶׂ֔ה\rb*.”
\p \v 30 \rb Then Abraham said|וַ֠יֹּאמֶר\rb*, “\rb May the Lord|לַֽאדֹנָי֙\rb* \rb not|אַל־\rb*\rb |נָ֞א\rb* \rb be angry|יִ֤חַר\rb*, \rb but let me speak further|וַאֲדַבֵּ֔רָה\rb*. \rb Suppose|אוּלַ֛י\rb* \rb thirty|שְׁלֹשִׁ֑ים\rb* \rb are found|יִמָּצְא֥וּן\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֖ם\rb*?”
\p \rb He replied|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb*, “\rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb I find|אֶמְצָ֥א\rb* \rb thirty|שְׁלֹשִֽׁים׃\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֖ם\rb*, \rb I will not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb do it|אֶֽעֱשֶׂ֔ה\rb*.”
\p \v 31 \rb And Abraham said|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Now that|הִנֵּֽה־\rb*\rb |נָ֤א\rb* \rb I have ventured|הוֹאַ֙לְתִּי֙\rb* \rb to speak|לְדַבֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֔י\rb*, \rb suppose|אוּלַ֛י\rb* \rb twenty|עֶשְׂרִ֑ים\rb* \rb are found|יִמָּצְא֥וּן\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֖ם\rb*?”
\p \rb He answered|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb*, “\rb On account|בַּעֲב֖וּר\rb* \rb of the twenty|הָֽעֶשְׂרִֽים׃\rb*, \rb I will not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb destroy it|אַשְׁחִ֔ית\rb*.”
\p \v 32 \rb Finally, Abraham said|וַ֠יֹּאמֶר\rb*, “\rb May the Lord|לַֽאדֹנָי֙\rb* \rb not|אַל־\rb*\rb |נָ֞א\rb* \rb be angry|יִ֤חַר\rb*, \rb but let me speak|וַאֲדַבְּרָ֣ה\rb*\rb |אַךְ־\rb* \rb once more|הַפַּ֔עַם\rb*. \rb Suppose|אוּלַ֛י\rb* \rb ten|עֲשָׂרָ֑ה\rb* \rb are found|יִמָּצְא֥וּן\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֖ם\rb*?”
\p \rb And He answered|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb*, “\rb On account|בַּעֲב֖וּר\rb* \rb of the ten|הָעֲשָׂרָֽה׃\rb*, \rb I will not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb destroy it|אַשְׁחִ֔ית\rb*.”
\p \v 33 \rb When|כַּאֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb had finished|כִּלָּ֔ה\rb* \rb speaking|לְדַבֵּ֖ר\rb* \rb with|אֶל־\rb* \rb Abraham|אַבְרָהָ֑ם\rb*, \rb He departed|וַיֵּ֣לֶךְ\rb*, \rb and Abraham|וְאַבְרָהָ֖ם\rb* \rb returned|שָׁ֥ב\rb* \rb home|לִמְקֹמֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\c 19
\s1 Lot Welcomes the Angels
\p \v 1 \rb Now the two|שְׁנֵ֨י\rb* \rb angels|הַמַּלְאָכִ֤ים\rb* \rb arrived|וַ֠יָּבֹאוּ\rb* \rb at Sodom|סְדֹ֙מָה֙\rb* \rb in the evening|בָּעֶ֔רֶב\rb*, \rb and Lot|וְל֖וֹט\rb* \rb was sitting|יֹשֵׁ֣ב\rb* \rb in the gateway|בְּשַֽׁעַר־\rb* \rb of the city|סְדֹ֑ם\rb*. \rb When Lot|לוֹט֙\rb* \rb saw them|וַיַּרְא־\rb*, \rb he got up|וַיָּ֣קָם\rb* \rb to meet them|לִקְרָאתָ֔ם\rb*, \rb bowed|וַיִּשְׁתַּ֥חוּ\rb* \rb facedown|אַפַּ֖יִם\rb*\rb |אָֽרְצָה׃\rb*, \v 2 \rb and said|וַיֹּ֜אמֶר\rb*, “\rb |הִנֶּ֣ה\rb*\rb |נָּא־\rb* \rb My lords|אֲדֹנַ֗י\rb*, \rb please|נָ֠א\rb* \rb turn aside|ס֣וּרוּ\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֨ית\rb* \rb of your servant|עַבְדְּכֶ֤ם\rb*; \rb wash|וְרַחֲצ֣וּ\rb* \rb your feet|רַגְלֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb and spend the night|וְלִ֙ינוּ֙\rb*. \rb Then you can rise early|וְהִשְׁכַּמְתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb and go|וַהֲלַכְתֶּ֣ם\rb* \rb on your way|לְדַרְכְּכֶ֑ם\rb*.”
\p “\rb No|לֹּ֔א\rb*,”\rb |כִּ֥י\rb* \rb they answered|וַיֹּאמְר֣וּ\rb*, “\rb we will spend the night|נָלִֽין׃\rb* \rb in the square|בָרְח֖וֹב\rb*.”
\p \v 3 \rb But Lot insisted|וַיִּפְצַר־\rb*\rb |בָּ֣ם\rb* \rb so strongly|מְאֹ֔ד\rb* \rb that they followed|וַיָּסֻ֣רוּ\rb* \rb him|אֵלָ֔יו\rb*\rb |וַיָּבֹ֖אוּ\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb his house|בֵּית֑וֹ\rb*. \rb He prepared|וַיַּ֤עַשׂ\rb* \rb a feast|מִשְׁתֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb for them|לָהֶם֙\rb* \rb and baked|אָפָ֖ה\rb* \rb unleavened bread|וּמַצּ֥וֹת\rb*, \rb and they ate|וַיֹּאכֵֽלוּ׃\rb*.
\p \v 4 \rb Before|טֶרֶם֮\rb* \rb they had gone to bed|יִשְׁכָּבוּ֒\rb*, \rb all|כָּל־\rb*\rb |הָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb the men|וְאַנְשֵׁ֨י\rb* \rb of the city|הָעִ֜יר\rb*\rb |אַנְשֵׁ֤י\rb* \rb of Sodom|סְדֹם֙\rb*, \rb both young|מִנַּ֖עַר\rb* \rb and|וְעַד־\rb* \rb old|זָקֵ֑ן\rb*,\rb |מִקָּצֶֽה׃\rb* \rb surrounded|נָסַ֣בּוּ\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb the house|הַבַּ֔יִת\rb*. \v 5 \rb They called out|וַיִּקְרְא֤וּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Lot|לוֹט֙\rb*, \rb saying|וַיֹּ֣אמְרוּ\rb*, “\rb Where|אַיֵּ֧ה\rb* \rb are the men|הָאֲנָשִׁ֛ים\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb came|בָּ֥אוּ\rb* \rb to you tonight|אֵלֶ֖יךָ\rb*\rb |הַלָּ֑יְלָה\rb*? \rb Send them out|הוֹצִיאֵ֣ם\rb* \rb to us|אֵלֵ֔ינוּ\rb* \rb so we can have relations|וְנֵדְעָ֖ה\rb* \rb with them|אֹתָֽם׃\rb*!”
\p \v 6 \rb Lot|ל֖וֹט\rb* \rb went|וַיֵּצֵ֧א\rb* \rb outside|הַפֶּ֑תְחָה\rb* \rb to meet them|אֲלֵהֶ֛ם\rb*, \rb shutting|סָגַ֥ר\rb* \rb the door|וְהַדֶּ֖לֶת\rb* \rb behind him|אַחֲרָֽיו׃\rb*. \v 7 “\rb Please|נָ֥א\rb*, \rb my brothers|אַחַ֖י\rb*,” \rb he pleaded|וַיֹּאמַ֑ר\rb*, “\rb don’t|אַל־\rb* \rb do such a wicked thing|תָּרֵֽעוּ׃\rb*! \v 8 \rb Look|הִנֵּה־\rb*,\rb |נָ֨א\rb* \rb I have|לִ֜י\rb* \rb two|שְׁתֵּ֣י\rb* \rb daughters|בָנ֗וֹת\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb have never|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb slept with|יָדְעוּ֙\rb* \rb a man|אִ֔ישׁ\rb*. \rb Let me bring|אוֹצִֽיאָה־\rb*\rb |נָּ֤א\rb* \rb them|אֶתְהֶן֙\rb* \rb to you|אֲלֵיכֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb and you can do|וַעֲשׂ֣וּ\rb* \rb to them|לָהֶ֔ן\rb* \rb as you please|כַּטּ֖וֹב\rb*\rb |בְּעֵינֵיכֶ֑ם\rb*. \rb But|רַ֠ק\rb* \rb do not|אַל־\rb* \rb do|תַּעֲשׂ֣וּ\rb* \rb anything|דָבָ֔ר\rb* \rb to these|הָאֵל֙\rb* \rb men|לָֽאֲנָשִׁ֤ים\rb*, \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb*\rb |כֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb they have come|בָּ֖אוּ\rb* \rb under the protection|בְּצֵ֥ל\rb* \rb of my roof|קֹרָתִֽי׃\rb*.”
\p \v 9 “\rb Get out of the way|גֶּשׁ־\rb*\rb |הָ֗לְאָה\rb*!” \rb they replied|וַיֹּאמְר֣וּ׀\rb*. \rb And they declared|וַיֹּֽאמְרוּ֙\rb*, “\rb This one|הָאֶחָ֤ד\rb* \rb came here|בָּֽא־\rb* \rb as a foreigner|לָגוּר֙\rb*, \rb and he is already acting like a judge|וַיִּשְׁפֹּ֣ט\rb*\rb |שָׁפ֔וֹט\rb*! \rb Now|עַתָּ֕ה\rb* \rb we will treat you worse|נָרַ֥ע\rb* \rb than them|מֵהֶ֑ם\rb*.” \rb And they pressed|וַיִּפְצְר֨וּ\rb*\rb |בָאִ֤ישׁ\rb* \rb in on Lot|בְּלוֹט֙\rb*\rb |מְאֹ֔ד\rb* \rb and moved in|וַֽיִּגְּשׁ֖וּ\rb* \rb to break down|לִשְׁבֹּ֥ר\rb* \rb the door|הַדָּֽלֶת׃\rb*.
\p \v 10 \rb But the men inside|הָֽאֲנָשִׁים֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb reached out|וַיִּשְׁלְח֤וּ\rb*\rb |יָדָ֔ם\rb*, \rb pulled|וַיָּבִ֧יאוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Lot|ל֛וֹט\rb* \rb into the house|הַבָּ֑יְתָה\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb with them|אֲלֵיהֶ֖ם\rb*, \rb and shut|סָגָֽרוּ׃\rb* \rb the door|הַדֶּ֖לֶת\rb*. \v 11 \rb And|וְֽאֶת־\rb* \rb they struck|הִכּוּ֙\rb* \rb the men|הָאֲנָשִׁ֞ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb at the entrance|פֶּ֣תַח\rb*\rb |הַבַּ֗יִת\rb*, \rb young|מִקָּטֹ֖ן\rb* \rb and|וְעַד־\rb* \rb old|גָּד֑וֹל\rb*, \rb with blindness|בַּסַּנְוֵרִ֔ים\rb*, \rb so that they wearied themselves|וַיִּלְא֖וּ\rb* \rb trying to find|לִמְצֹ֥א\rb* \rb the door|הַפָּֽתַח׃\rb*.
\s1 Lot Flees to Zoar
\p \v 12 \rb Then the two men|הָאֲנָשִׁ֜ים\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּאמְר֨וּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Lot|ל֗וֹט\rb*, “\rb Do|מִֽי־\rb* \rb you have anyone|לְךָ֣\rb* \rb else|עֹ֚ד\rb* \rb here|פֹ֔ה\rb* — \rb a son-in-law|חָתָן֙\rb*, \rb your sons|וּבָנֶ֣יךָ\rb* \rb or daughters|וּבְנֹתֶ֔יךָ\rb*, \rb or anyone|וְכֹ֥ל\rb* \rb else in the city|בָּעִ֑יר\rb* \rb who belongs|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb to you|לְךָ֖\rb*? \rb Get them out|הוֹצֵ֖א\rb* \rb of|מִן־\rb* \rb here|הַמָּקֽוֹם׃\rb*, \v 13 \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb we|אֲנַ֔חְנוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb are about to destroy|מַשְׁחִתִ֣ים\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb place|הַמָּק֖וֹם\rb*. \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the outcry|צַעֲקָתָם֙\rb* \rb to|אֶת־\rb*\rb |פְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb against its people is so great|גָֽדְלָ֤ה\rb* \rb that He|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb has sent us|וַיְשַׁלְּחֵ֥נוּ\rb* \rb to destroy it|לְשַׁחֲתָֽהּ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 14 \rb So Lot|ל֜וֹט\rb* \rb went out|וַיֵּצֵ֨א\rb* \rb and spoke|וַיְדַבֵּ֣ר׀\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the sons-in-law|חֲתָנָ֣יו׀\rb* \rb who were pledged in marriage to|לֹקְחֵ֣י\rb* \rb his daughters|בְנֹתָ֗יו\rb*. “\rb Get up|ק֤וּמוּ\rb*,” \rb he said|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb*. “\rb Get out|צְּאוּ֙\rb* \rb of|מִן־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb place|הַמָּק֣וֹם\rb*, \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb is about to destroy|מַשְׁחִ֥ית\rb* \rb the city|הָעִ֑יר\rb*!” \rb But his sons-in-law|חֲתָנָֽיו׃\rb* \rb thought|בְּעֵינֵ֥י\rb* \rb he was|וַיְהִ֥י\rb* \rb joking|כִמְצַחֵ֖ק\rb*.
\p \v 15 \rb At|וּכְמוֹ֙\rb* \rb daybreak|הַשַּׁ֣חַר\rb*\rb |עָלָ֔ה\rb* \rb the angels|הַמַּלְאָכִ֖ים\rb* \rb hurried|וַיָּאִ֥יצוּ\rb* \rb Lot along|בְּל֣וֹט\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*, “\rb Get up|קוּם֩\rb*! \rb Take|קַ֨ח\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb your wife|אִשְׁתְּךָ֜\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and your two|שְׁתֵּ֤י\rb* \rb daughters|בְנֹתֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb who are here|הַנִּמְצָאֹ֔ת\rb*, \rb or|פֶּן־\rb* \rb you will be swept away|תִּסָּפֶ֖ה\rb* \rb in the punishment|בַּעֲוֺ֥ן\rb* \rb of the city|הָעִֽיר׃\rb*.” \v 16 \rb But when Lot hesitated|וַֽיִּתְמַהְמָ֓הּ׀\rb*, \rb the men|הָאֲנָשִׁ֜ים\rb* \rb grabbed|וַיַּחֲזִ֨קוּ\rb* \rb his hand|בְּיָד֣וֹ\rb* \rb and the hands|וּבְיַד־\rb* \rb of his wife|אִשְׁתּ֗וֹ\rb* \rb and|וּבְיַד֙\rb* \rb his two|שְׁתֵּ֣י\rb* \rb daughters|בְנֹתָ֔יו\rb*. \rb And they led them|וַיֹּצִאֻ֥הוּ\rb* \rb safely|וַיַּנִּחֻ֖הוּ\rb* \rb out of|מִח֥וּץ\rb* \rb the city|לָעִֽיר׃\rb*, \rb because of the LORD’s|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb compassion|בְּחֶמְלַ֥ת\rb* \rb for them|עָלָ֑יו\rb*.
\p \v 17 \rb |וַיְהִי֩\rb* \rb As soon as the men had brought|כְהוֹצִיאָ֨ם\rb* \rb them|אֹתָ֜ם\rb* \rb out|הַח֗וּצָה\rb*, \rb one of them said|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb*, “\rb Run|הִמָּלֵ֣ט\rb* \rb for|עַל־\rb* \rb your lives|נַפְשֶׁ֔ךָ\rb*! \rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb look|תַּבִּ֣יט\rb* \rb back|אַחֲרֶ֔יךָ\rb*, \rb and do not|וְאַֽל־\rb* \rb stop|תַּעֲמֹ֖ד\rb* \rb anywhere|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb on the plain|הַכִּכָּ֑ר\rb*! \rb Flee|הִמָּלֵ֖ט\rb* \rb to the mountains|הָהָ֥רָה\rb*, \rb or|פֶּן־\rb* \rb you will be swept away|תִּסָּפֶֽה׃\rb*!”
\p \v 18 \rb But Lot|ל֖וֹט\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֲלֵהֶ֑ם\rb*, “\rb No|אַל־\rb*, \rb my lords|אֲדֹנָֽי׃\rb*, \rb please|נָ֖א\rb*! \v 19 \rb Your servant|עַבְדְּךָ֣\rb* \rb has indeed|הִנֵּה־\rb*\rb |נָ֠א\rb* \rb found|מָצָ֨א\rb* \rb favor|חֵן֮\rb* \rb in your sight|בְּעֵינֶיךָ֒\rb*, \rb and you have shown me|עָשִׂ֙יתָ֙\rb*\rb |עִמָּדִ֔י\rb* \rb great|וַתַּגְדֵּ֣ל\rb* \rb kindness|חַסְדְּךָ֗\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb by sparing|לְהַחֲי֖וֹת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb my life|נַפְשִׁ֑י\rb*. \rb But I|וְאָנֹכִ֗י\rb* \rb cannot|לֹ֤א\rb*\rb |אוּכַל֙\rb* \rb run|לְהִמָּלֵ֣ט\rb* \rb to the mountains|הָהָ֔רָה\rb*;\rb |פֶּן־\rb* \rb the disaster|הָרָעָ֖ה\rb* \rb will overtake me|תִּדְבָּקַ֥נִי\rb*, \rb and I will die|וָמַֽתִּי׃\rb*. \v 20 \rb Look|הִנֵּה־\rb*, \rb there is|הַזֹּ֧את\rb* \rb a town|הָעִ֨יר\rb* \rb nearby|קְרֹבָ֛ה\rb* \rb where|שָׁ֖מָּה\rb* \rb I can flee|לָנ֥וּס\rb*, \rb and it|וְהִ֣יא\rb* \rb is a small place|מִצְעָ֑ר\rb*. \rb Please|נָ֠א\rb* \rb let me flee|אִמָּלְטָ֨ה\rb*\rb |נָּ֜א\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֗מָּה\rb* — \rb is it|הִ֖וא\rb* \rb not|הֲלֹ֥א\rb* \rb a small place|מִצְעָ֛ר\rb*? \rb Then my life|נַפְשִֽׁי׃\rb* \rb will be saved|וּתְחִ֥י\rb*.”
\p \v 21 “\rb Very well|הִנֵּה֙\rb*,” \rb he answered|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֵלָ֔יו\rb*, “\rb I will grant this request|נָשָׂ֣אתִי\rb*\rb |פָנֶ֔יךָ\rb*\rb |הַזֶּ֑ה\rb*\rb |לַדָּבָ֣ר\rb* \rb as well|גַּ֖ם\rb*, \rb and will not|לְבִלְתִּ֛י\rb* \rb demolish|הָפְכִּ֥י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the town|הָעִ֖יר\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you indicate|דִּבַּֽרְתָּ׃\rb*. \v 22 \rb Hurry|מַהֵר֙\rb*! \rb Run|הִמָּלֵ֣ט\rb* \rb there quickly|שָׁ֔מָּה\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb I cannot|לֹ֤א\rb*\rb |אוּכַל֙\rb* \rb do|לַעֲשׂ֣וֹת\rb* \rb anything|דָּבָ֔ר\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb you reach|בֹּאֲךָ֖\rb* \rb it|שָׁ֑מָּה\rb*.” \rb That is why|עַל־\rb*\rb |כֵּ֛ן\rb* \rb the town|הָעִ֖יר\rb* \rb was called|קָרָ֥א\rb*\rb |שֵׁם־\rb* \rb Zoar|צֽוֹעַר׃\rb*.\f + \fr 19:22 \fqa Zoar \ft means \fqa small\ft .\f*
\p \v 23 \rb And by the time the sun|הַשֶּׁ֖מֶשׁ\rb* \rb had risen|יָצָ֣א\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb*, \rb Lot|וְל֖וֹט\rb* \rb had reached|בָּ֥א\rb* \rb Zoar|צֹֽעֲרָה׃\rb*.
\s1 The Destruction of Sodom and Gomorrah
\p \v 24 \rb Then the LORD|וַֽיהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb rained down|הִמְטִ֧יר\rb* \rb sulfur|גָּפְרִ֣ית\rb* \rb and fire|וָאֵ֑שׁ\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb Sodom|סְדֹ֛ם\rb*\rb |וְעַל־\rb* \rb and Gomorrah|עֲמֹרָ֖ה\rb* — \rb from|מֵאֵ֥ת\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb out of|מִן־\rb* \rb the heavens|הַשָּׁמָֽיִם׃\rb*. \v 25 \rb Thus He destroyed|וַֽיַּהֲפֹךְ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֔ל\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֖ת\rb* \rb cities|הֶעָרִ֣ים\rb* \rb and the entire|כָּל־\rb* \rb plain|הַכִּכָּ֑ר\rb*, \rb including|וְאֵת֙\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the inhabitants|יֹשְׁבֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the cities|הֶעָרִ֔ים\rb* \rb and everything that grew|וְצֶ֖מַח\rb* \rb on the ground|הָאֲדָמָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 26 \rb But Lot’s wife|אִשְׁתּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb looked|וַתַּבֵּ֥ט\rb* \rb back|מֵאַחֲרָ֑יו\rb*, \rb and she became|וַתְּהִ֖י\rb* \rb a pillar|נְצִ֥יב\rb* \rb of salt|מֶֽלַח׃\rb*.
\p \v 27 \rb Early the next morning|בַּבֹּ֑קֶר\rb*, \rb Abraham|אַבְרָהָ֖ם\rb* \rb got up|וַיַּשְׁכֵּ֥ם\rb* \rb and returned to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the place|הַ֨מָּק֔וֹם\rb* \rb where|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb he had stood|עָ֥מַד\rb*\rb |שָׁ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb before|פְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*. \v 28 \rb He looked|וַיַּשְׁקֵ֗ף\rb* \rb down|עַל־\rb* \rb toward|פְּנֵ֤י\rb* \rb Sodom|סְדֹם֙\rb* \rb and Gomorrah|וַעֲמֹרָ֔ה\rb*\rb |וְעַֽל־\rb* \rb and all|כָּל־\rb*\rb |פְּנֵ֖י\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of the plain|הַכִּכָּ֑ר\rb*, \rb and he saw|וַיַּ֗רְא\rb*\rb |וְהִנֵּ֤ה\rb* \rb the smoke|קִיטֹ֣ר\rb* \rb rising|עָלָה֙\rb* \rb from the land|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb like smoke|כְּקִיטֹ֖ר\rb* \rb from a furnace|הַכִּבְשָֽׁן׃\rb*.
\p \v 29 \rb So|וַיְהִ֗י\rb* \rb when God|אֱלֹהִים֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb destroyed|בְּשַׁחֵ֤ת\rb* \rb the cities|עָרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the plain|הַכִּכָּ֔ר\rb*, \rb He|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb remembered|וַיִּזְכֹּ֥ר\rb* \rb Abraham|אַבְרָהָ֑ם\rb*, \rb and He brought|וַיְשַׁלַּ֤ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Lot|לוֹט֙\rb* \rb out of the|מִתּ֣וֹךְ\rb* \rb catastrophe|הַהֲפֵכָ֔ה\rb* \rb that destroyed|בַּהֲפֹךְ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the cities|הֶ֣עָרִ֔ים\rb* \rb where|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb he|לֽוֹט׃\rb* \rb had lived|יָשַׁ֥ב\rb*\rb |בָּהֵ֖ן\rb*.
\s1 Lot and His Daughters
\p \v 30 \rb Lot|ל֨וֹט\rb* \rb and|עִמּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb his two|וּשְׁתֵּ֤י\rb* \rb daughters|בְנֹתָיו֙\rb* \rb left|וַיַּעַל֩\rb* \rb Zoar|מִצּ֜וֹעַר\rb* \rb and settled|וַיֵּ֣שֶׁב\rb* \rb in the mountains|בָּהָ֗ר\rb* — \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb he was afraid|יָרֵ֖א\rb* \rb to stay|לָשֶׁ֣בֶת\rb* \rb in Zoar|בְּצ֑וֹעַר\rb* — \rb where they|ה֖וּא\rb*\rb |וּשְׁתֵּ֥י\rb*\rb |בְנֹתָֽיו׃\rb* \rb lived|וַיֵּ֙שֶׁב֙\rb* \rb in a cave|בַּמְּעָרָ֔ה\rb*.
\p \v 31 \rb One day the older daughter|הַבְּכִירָ֛ה\rb* \rb said|וַתֹּ֧אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the younger|הַצְּעִירָ֖ה\rb*, “\rb Our father|אָבִ֣ינוּ\rb* \rb is old|זָקֵ֑ן\rb*, \rb and there is no|אֵ֤ין\rb* \rb man|וְאִ֨ישׁ\rb* \rb in the land|בָּאָ֙רֶץ֙\rb* \rb to sleep with|לָב֣וֹא\rb* \rb us|עָלֵ֔ינוּ\rb*, \rb as is the custom|כְּדֶ֖רֶךְ\rb* \rb over all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the earth|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb*. \v 32 \rb Come|לְכָ֨ה\rb*, \rb let us get our father|אָבִ֛ינוּ\rb* \rb drunk|נַשְׁקֶ֧ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb with wine|יַ֖יִן\rb* \rb so we can sleep|וְנִשְׁכְּבָ֣ה\rb* \rb with him|עִמּ֑וֹ\rb* \rb and preserve|וּנְחַיֶּ֥ה\rb* \rb his|מֵאָבִ֖ינוּ\rb* \rb line|זָֽרַע׃\rb*.”
\p \v 33 \rb So that|ה֑וּא\rb* \rb night|בַּלַּ֣יְלָה\rb* \rb they got their father|אֲבִיהֶ֛ן\rb* \rb drunk|וַתַּשְׁקֶ֧יןָ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb with wine|יַ֖יִן\rb*, \rb and the firstborn|הַבְּכִירָה֙\rb* \rb went in|וַתָּבֹ֤א\rb* \rb and slept with|וַתִּשְׁכַּ֣ב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb her father|אָבִ֔יהָ\rb*; \rb he was not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb aware|יָדַ֥ע\rb* \rb when she lay down|בְּשִׁכְבָ֖הּ\rb* \rb or when she got up|וּבְקׄוּמָֽהּ׃\rb*.
\p \v 34 \rb |וַֽיְהִי֙\rb* \rb The next day|מִֽמָּחֳרָ֔ת\rb* \rb the older daughter|הַבְּכִירָה֙\rb* \rb said|וַתֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the younger|הַצְּעִירָ֔ה\rb*, “\rb Look|הֵן־\rb*, \rb I slept with|שָׁכַ֥בְתִּי\rb* \rb my father|אָבִ֑י\rb* \rb last night|אֶ֖מֶשׁ\rb*.\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Let us get him drunk|נַשְׁקֶ֨נּוּ\rb* \rb with wine|יַ֜יִן\rb* \rb again|גַּם־\rb* \rb tonight|הַלַּ֗יְלָה\rb* \rb so you can go in|וּבֹ֙אִי֙\rb* \rb and sleep|שִׁכְבִ֣י\rb* \rb with him|עִמּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb and we can preserve|וּנְחַיֶּ֥ה\rb* \rb our father’s|מֵאָבִ֖ינוּ\rb* \rb line|זָֽרַע׃\rb*.”
\p \v 35 \rb So again|גַּ֣ם\rb* \rb that|הַה֛וּא\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb night|בַּלַּ֧יְלָה\rb* \rb they got their father|אֲבִיהֶ֖ן\rb* \rb drunk|וַתַּשְׁקֶ֜יןָ\rb* \rb with wine|יָ֑יִן\rb*, \rb and the younger daughter|הַצְּעִירָה֙\rb* \rb went in|וַתָּ֤קָם\rb* \rb and slept|וַתִּשְׁכַּ֣ב\rb* \rb with him|עִמּ֔וֹ\rb*; \rb he was not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb aware|יָדַ֥ע\rb* \rb when she lay down|בְּשִׁכְבָ֖הּ\rb* \rb or when she got up|וּבְקֻמָֽהּ׃\rb*.
\p \v 36 \rb Thus both|שְׁתֵּ֥י\rb* \rb of Lot’s|ל֖וֹט\rb* \rb daughters|בְנֽוֹת־\rb* \rb became pregnant|וַֽתַּהֲרֶ֛יןָ\rb* \rb by their father|מֵאֲבִיהֶֽן׃\rb*. \v 37 \rb The older daughter|הַבְּכִירָה֙\rb* \rb gave birth to|וַתֵּ֤לֶד\rb* \rb a son|בֵּ֔ן\rb* \rb and named him|וַתִּקְרָ֥א\rb*\rb |שְׁמ֖וֹ\rb* \rb Moab|מוֹאָ֑ב\rb*.\f + \fr 19:37 \fqa Moab \ft sounds like the Hebrew for \fqa from my father\ft .\f* \rb He|ה֥וּא\rb* \rb is the father|אֲבִֽי־\rb* \rb of the Moabites|מוֹאָ֖ב\rb* \rb of|עַד־\rb* \rb today|הַיּֽוֹם׃\rb*. \v 38 \rb The younger daughter|וְהַצְּעִירָ֤ה\rb* \rb also|גַם־\rb* \rb gave birth to|יָ֣לְדָה\rb* \rb a son|בֵּ֔ן\rb*, \rb and she named|וַתִּקְרָ֥א\rb* \rb him|שְׁמ֖וֹ\rb*\rb |בֶּן־\rb* \rb Ben-ammi|עַמִּ֑י\rb*.\f + \fr 19:38 \fqa Ben-ammi \ft means \fqa son of my people\ft .\f*\rb |ה֛וּא\rb* \rb He is the father|אֲבִ֥י\rb* \rb of the Ammonites|בְנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |עַמּ֖וֹן\rb* \rb of|עַד־\rb* \rb today|הַיּֽוֹם׃ס\rb*.
\c 20
\s1 Abraham, Sarah, and Abimelech
\p \v 1 \rb Now Abraham|אַבְרָהָם֙\rb* \rb journeyed|וַיִּסַּ֨ע\rb* \rb from there|מִשָּׁ֤ם\rb* \rb to the region|אַ֣רְצָה\rb* \rb of the Negev|הַנֶּ֔גֶב\rb* \rb and settled|וַיֵּ֥שֶׁב\rb* \rb between|בֵּין־\rb* \rb Kadesh|קָדֵ֖שׁ\rb*\rb |וּבֵ֣ין\rb* \rb and Shur|שׁ֑וּר\rb*. \rb While he was staying|וַיָּ֖גָר\rb* \rb in Gerar|בִּגְרָֽר׃\rb*, \v 2 \rb Abraham|אַבְרָהָ֛ם\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֧אמֶר\rb* \rb of|אֶל־\rb* \rb his wife|אִשְׁתּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb Sarah|שָׂרָ֥ה\rb*, “\rb She|הִ֑וא\rb* \rb is my sister|אֲחֹ֣תִי\rb*.” \rb So Abimelech|אֲבִימֶ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Gerar|גְּרָ֔ר\rb* \rb had Sarah|שָׂרָֽה׃\rb* \rb brought|וַיִּשְׁלַ֗ח\rb* \rb to him|וַיִּקַּ֖ח\rb*.\rb |אֶת־\rb*
\p \v 3 \rb One night, however|הַלָּ֑יְלָה\rb*, \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֛ים\rb* \rb came|וַיָּבֹ֧א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Abimelech|אֲבִימֶ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb in a dream|בַּחֲל֣וֹם\rb* \rb and told|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb him|ל֗וֹ\rb*,\rb |הִנְּךָ֥\rb* “\rb You are as good as dead|מֵת֙\rb* \rb because of|עַל־\rb* \rb the woman|הָאִשָּׁ֣ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb you have taken|לָקַ֔חְתָּ\rb*, \rb for she|וְהִ֖וא\rb* \rb is a married|בְּעֻ֥לַת\rb* \rb woman.|בָּֽעַל׃\rb*”
\p \v 4 \rb Now Abimelech|וַאֲבִימֶ֕לֶךְ\rb* \rb had not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb gone|קָרַ֖ב\rb* \rb near her|אֵלֶ֑יהָ\rb*, \rb so he replied|וַיֹּאמַ֕ר\rb*, “\rb Lord|אֲדֹנָ֕י\rb*, \rb would You destroy|תַּהֲרֹֽג׃\rb* \rb a nation|הֲג֥וֹי\rb* \rb even though|גַּם־\rb* \rb it is innocent|צַדִּ֖יק\rb*? \v 5 \rb Didn’t|הֲלֹ֨א\rb* \rb Abraham|ה֤וּא\rb* \rb tell|אָֽמַר־\rb* \rb me|לִי֙\rb*, ‘\rb She|הִ֔וא\rb* \rb is my sister|אֲחֹ֣תִי\rb*’? \rb And she|וְהִֽיא־\rb*\rb |גַם־\rb* \rb herself|הִ֥וא\rb* \rb said|אָֽמְרָ֖ה\rb*, ‘\rb He|ה֑וּא\rb* \rb is my brother|אָחִ֣י\rb*.’ \rb I have done|עָשִׂ֥יתִי\rb* \rb this|זֹֽאת׃\rb* \rb in the integrity|בְּתָם־\rb* \rb of my heart|לְבָבִ֛י\rb* \rb and the innocence|וּבְנִקְיֹ֥ן\rb* \rb of my hands|כַּפַּ֖י\rb*.”
\p \v 6 \rb Then God|הָֽאֱלֹהִ֜ים\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּאמֶר֩\rb* \rb to Abimelech|אֵלָ֨יו\rb* \rb in the dream|בַּחֲלֹ֗ם\rb*, “\rb Yes|גַּ֣ם\rb*, \rb I|אָנֹכִ֤י\rb* \rb know|יָדַ֙עְתִּי֙\rb* \rb that|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb you did|עָשִׂ֣יתָ\rb* \rb this|זֹּ֔את\rb* \rb with a clear|בְתָם־\rb* \rb conscience|לְבָבְךָ֙\rb*, \rb and so I|אָנֹכִ֛י\rb*\rb |גַּם־\rb* \rb have kept|וָאֶחְשֹׂ֧ךְ\rb* \rb you|אֽוֹתְךָ֖\rb* \rb from sinning|מֵחֲטוֹ־\rb* \rb against Me|לִ֑י\rb*. \rb That is why|עַל־\rb*\rb |כֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb I did not|לֹא־\rb* \rb let|נְתַתִּ֖יךָ\rb* \rb you touch|לִנְגֹּ֥עַ\rb* \rb her|אֵלֶֽיהָ׃\rb*. \v 7 \rb Now|וְעַתָּ֗ה\rb* \rb return|הָשֵׁ֤ב\rb* \rb the man’s|הָאִישׁ֙\rb* \rb wife|אֵֽשֶׁת־\rb*, \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb he|ה֔וּא\rb* \rb is a prophet|נָבִ֣יא\rb*; \rb he will pray|וְיִתְפַּלֵּ֥ל\rb* \rb for you|בַּֽעַדְךָ֖\rb* \rb and you will live|וֶֽחְיֵ֑ה\rb*. \rb But if|וְאִם־\rb* \rb you do not|אֵֽינְךָ֣\rb* \rb restore her|מֵשִׁ֗יב\rb*, \rb be aware|דַּ֚ע\rb* \rb that|כִּי־\rb* \rb you will surely die|מ֣וֹת\rb*\rb |תָּמ֔וּת\rb* — \rb you|אַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb who belong|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb to you|לָֽךְ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 8 \rb Early the next morning|בַּבֹּ֗קֶר\rb* \rb Abimelech|אֲבִימֶ֜לֶךְ\rb* \rb got up|וַיַּשְׁכֵּ֨ם\rb* \rb and summoned|וַיִּקְרָא֙\rb* \rb all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb his servants|עֲבָדָ֔יו\rb*; \rb and when he described to them|וַיְדַבֵּ֛ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |בְּאָזְנֵיהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb that|הָאֵ֖לֶּה\rb* \rb had happened|הַדְּבָרִ֥ים\rb*, \rb the men|הָאֲנָשִׁ֖ים\rb* \rb were terrified|וַיִּֽירְא֥וּ\rb*\rb |מְאֹֽד׃\rb*.
\p \v 9 \rb Then Abimelech|אֲבִימֶ֜לֶךְ\rb* \rb called|וַיִּקְרָ֨א\rb* \rb Abraham|לְאַבְרָהָ֗ם\rb* \rb and asked|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb*, “\rb What|מֶֽה־\rb* \rb have you done|עָשִׂ֤יתָ\rb* \rb to us|לָּ֙נוּ֙\rb*? \rb How|וּמֶֽה־\rb* \rb have I sinned|חָטָ֣אתִי\rb* \rb against you|לָ֔ךְ\rb*, \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb you have brought|הֵבֵ֧אתָ\rb* \rb such tremendous|גְדֹלָ֑ה\rb* \rb guilt|חֲטָאָ֣ה\rb* \rb upon me|עָלַ֛י\rb* \rb and|וְעַל־\rb* \rb my kingdom|מַמְלַכְתִּ֖י\rb*? \rb You have done|עָשִׂ֖יתָ\rb* \rb things|מַעֲשִׂים֙\rb* \rb to me|עִמָּדִֽי׃\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb should not|לֹא־\rb* \rb be done|יֵֽעָשׂ֔וּ\rb*.” \v 10 \rb Abimelech|אֲבִימֶ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb also asked|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb Abraham|אַבְרָהָ֑ם\rb*, “\rb What|מָ֣ה\rb* \rb prompted|רָאִ֔יתָ\rb*\rb |כִּ֥י\rb* \rb you to do|עָשִׂ֖יתָ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb such|הַזֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb a thing|הַדָּבָ֥ר\rb*?”
\p \v 11 \rb Abraham|אַבְרָהָ֔ם\rb*\rb |כִּ֣י\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb*, “\rb I thought to myself|אָמַ֗רְתִּי\rb*, ‘\rb Surely|רַ֚ק\rb* \rb there is no|אֵין־\rb* \rb fear|יִרְאַ֣ת\rb* \rb of God|אֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb* \rb in this|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb place|בַּמָּק֖וֹם\rb*. \rb They will kill me|וַהֲרָג֖וּנִי\rb* \rb on account of|עַל־\rb*\rb |דְּבַ֥ר\rb* \rb my wife|אִשְׁתִּֽי׃\rb*.’ \v 12 \rb Besides|וְגַם־\rb*, \rb she|הִ֔וא\rb* \rb really|אָמְנָ֗ה\rb* \rb is my sister|אֲחֹתִ֤י\rb*, \rb the daughter|בַת־\rb* \rb of my father|אָבִי֙\rb* — \rb though|אַ֖ךְ\rb* \rb not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb the daughter|בַת־\rb* \rb of my mother|אִמִּ֑י\rb* — \rb and she became|וַתְּהִי־\rb* \rb my|לִ֖י\rb* \rb wife|לְאִשָּֽׁה׃\rb*. \v 13 \rb |וַיְהִ֞י\rb* \rb So when|כַּאֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִים֮\rb* \rb had me journey|הִתְע֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֹתִ֗י\rb* \rb from my father’s|אָבִי֒\rb* \rb house|מִבֵּ֣ית\rb*, \rb I said|וָאֹמַ֣ר\rb* \rb to Sarah|לָ֔הּ\rb*, ‘\rb This is how|זֶ֣ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you can show|תַּעֲשִׂ֖י\rb* \rb your loyalty|חַסְדֵּ֔ךְ\rb* \rb to me|עִמָּדִ֑י\rb*:\rb |אֶ֤ל\rb* \rb Wherever|כָּל־\rb*\rb |הַמָּקוֹם֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb we go|נָב֣וֹא\rb*,\rb |שָׁ֔מָּה\rb* \rb say|אִמְרִי־\rb* \rb of me|לִ֖י\rb*, “\rb He is|הֽוּא׃\rb* \rb my brother|אָחִ֥י\rb*.”’”
\p \v 14 \rb So Abimelech|אֲבִימֶ֜לֶךְ\rb* \rb brought|וַיִּקַּ֨ח\rb* \rb sheep|צֹ֣אן\rb* \rb and cattle|וּבָקָ֗ר\rb*, \rb menservants|וַעֲבָדִים֙\rb* \rb and maidservants|וּשְׁפָחֹ֔ת\rb*, \rb and he gave them|וַיִּתֵּ֖ן\rb* \rb to Abraham|לְאַבְרָהָ֑ם\rb* \rb and restored|וַיָּ֣שֶׁב\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb his wife|אִשְׁתּֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb Sarah|שָׂרָ֥ה\rb* \rb to him|ל֔וֹ\rb*. \v 15 \rb And Abimelech|אֲבִימֶ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Look|הִנֵּ֥ה\rb*, \rb my land|אַרְצִ֖י\rb* \rb is before you|לְפָנֶ֑יךָ\rb*. \rb Settle wherever you please|שֵֽׁב׃\rb*\rb |בַּטּ֥וֹב\rb*\rb |בְּעֵינֶ֖יךָ\rb*.” \v 16 \rb And he said|אָמַ֗ר\rb* \rb to Sarah|וּלְשָׂרָ֣ה\rb*, “\rb See|הִנֵּ֨ה\rb*, \rb I am giving|נָתַ֜תִּי\rb* \rb your brother|לְאָחִ֔יךְ\rb*\rb |הִנֵּ֤ה\rb* \rb a thousand pieces|אֶ֤לֶף\rb* \rb of silver|כֶּ֙סֶף֙\rb*.\f + \fr 20:16 \ft Or \fqa a thousand shekels of silver\ft ; that is, approximately 25.1 pounds or 11.4 kilograms of silver\f* \rb It is|הוּא־\rb* \rb your|לָךְ֙\rb* \rb vindication|כְּס֣וּת\rb*\rb |עֵינַ֔יִם\rb* \rb before all|לְכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb are with you|אִתָּ֑ךְ\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֥ת\rb*; \rb you are completely|כֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb cleared|וְנֹכָֽחַת׃\rb*.”
\p \v 17 \rb Then Abraham|אַבְרָהָ֖ם\rb* \rb prayed|וַיִּתְפַּלֵּ֥ל\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb God|הָאֱלֹהִ֑ים\rb*, \rb and God|אֱלֹהִ֜ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb healed|וַיִּרְפָּ֨א\rb* \rb Abimelech|אֲבִימֶ֧לֶךְ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and his wife|אִשְׁתּ֛וֹ\rb* \rb and his maidservants|וְאַמְהֹתָ֖יו\rb*, \rb so that they could again bear children|וַיֵּלֵֽדוּ׃\rb* — \v 18 \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb account|דְּבַ֥ר\rb* \rb of Abraham’s|אַבְרָהָֽם׃ס\rb* \rb wife|אֵ֥שֶׁת\rb* \rb Sarah|שָׂרָ֖ה\rb*, \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*\rb |בְּעַ֥ד\rb* \rb had completely closed|עָצֹ֤ר\rb*\rb |עָצַר֙\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the wombs|רֶ֖חֶם\rb* \rb in Abimelech’s|אֲבִימֶ֑לֶךְ\rb* \rb household|לְבֵ֣ית\rb*.
\c 21
\s1 The Birth of Isaac
\p \v 1 \rb Now the LORD|וַֽיהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb attended|פָּקַ֥ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb to Sarah|שָׂרָ֖ה\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb He had said|אָמָ֑ר\rb*, \rb and the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb did|וַיַּ֧עַשׂ\rb* \rb for Sarah|לְשָׂרָ֖ה\rb* \rb what|כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb He had promised|דִּבֵּֽר׃\rb*. \v 2 \rb So Sarah|שָׂרָ֧ה\rb* \rb conceived|וַתַּהַר֩\rb* \rb and bore|וַתֵּ֨לֶד\rb* \rb a son|בֵּ֖ן\rb* \rb to Abraham|לְאַבְרָהָ֛ם\rb* \rb in his old age|לִזְקֻנָ֑יו\rb*, \rb at the very time|לַמּוֹעֵ֕ד\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִֽים׃\rb* \rb had promised|דִּבֶּ֥ר\rb*\rb |אֹת֖וֹ\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb And Abraham|אַבְרָהָ֜ם\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb gave|וַיִּקְרָ֨א\rb* \rb the name|שֶׁם־\rb* \rb Isaac|יִצְחָֽק׃\rb*\f + \fr 21:3 \fqa Isaac \ft means \fqa he laughs\ft .\f* \rb to the son|בְּנ֧וֹ\rb*\rb |הַנּֽוֹלַד־\rb*\rb |ל֛וֹ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb Sarah|שָׂרָ֖ה\rb* \rb bore|יָלְדָה־\rb* \rb to him|לּ֥וֹ\rb*. \v 4 \rb When his son|בְּנ֔וֹ\rb*\rb |בֶּן־\rb* \rb Isaac|יִצְחָ֣ק\rb* \rb was eight|שְׁמֹנַ֖ת\rb* \rb days old|יָמִ֑ים\rb*, \rb Abraham|אַבְרָהָם֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb circumcised him|וַיָּ֤מָל\rb*, \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִֽים׃\rb* \rb had commanded him|צִוָּ֥ה\rb*.\rb |אֹת֖וֹ\rb* \v 5 \rb Abraham|וְאַבְרָהָ֖ם\rb* \rb was a hundred|מְאַ֣ת\rb* \rb years old|בֶּן־\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֑ה\rb* \rb when his son|בְּנֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb Isaac|יִצְחָ֥ק\rb* \rb was born|בְּהִוָּ֣לֶד\rb* \rb to him|ל֔וֹ\rb*.\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb*
\p \v 6 \rb Then Sarah|שָׂרָ֔ה\rb* \rb said|וַתֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb God|אֱלֹהִ֑ים\rb* \rb has made|עָ֥שָׂה\rb* \rb me|לִ֖י\rb* \rb laugh|צְחֹ֕ק\rb*, \rb and everyone|כָּל־\rb* \rb who hears of this|הַשֹּׁמֵ֖עַ\rb* \rb will laugh|יִֽצְחַק־\rb* \rb with me|לִֽי׃\rb*.” \v 7 \rb She added|וַתֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Who|מִ֤י\rb* \rb would have told|מִלֵּל֙\rb* \rb Abraham|לְאַבְרָהָ֔ם\rb* \rb that Sarah|שָׂרָ֑ה\rb* \rb would nurse|הֵינִ֥יקָה\rb* \rb children|בָנִ֖ים\rb*? \rb Yet|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I have borne him|יָלַ֥דְתִּי\rb* \rb a son|בֵ֖ן\rb* \rb in his old age|לִזְקֻנָֽיו׃\rb*.”
\p \v 8 \rb So the child|הַיֶּ֖לֶד\rb* \rb grew|וַיִּגְדַּ֥ל\rb* \rb and was weaned|וַיִּגָּמַ֑ל\rb*, \rb and Abraham|אַבְרָהָם֙\rb* \rb held|וַיַּ֤עַשׂ\rb* \rb a great|גָד֔וֹל\rb* \rb feast|מִשְׁתֶּ֣ה\rb* \rb on the day|בְּי֖וֹם\rb* \rb Isaac|יִצְחָֽק׃\rb* \rb was weaned|הִגָּמֵ֥ל\rb*.\rb |אֶת־\rb*
\s1 Sarah Turns against Hagar
\p \v 9 \rb But Sarah|שָׂרָ֜ה\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb saw that|וַתֵּ֨רֶא\rb* \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb whom|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb Hagar|הָגָ֧ר\rb* \rb the Egyptian|הַמִּצְרִ֛ית\rb* \rb had borne|יָלְדָ֥ה\rb* \rb to Abraham|לְאַבְרָהָ֖ם\rb* \rb was mocking her son|מְצַחֵֽק׃\rb*,\f + \fr 21:9 \ft LXX and Vulgate; Hebrew lacks \fqa her son\f* \v 10 \rb and she said|וַתֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb* \rb to Abraham|לְאַבְרָהָ֔ם\rb*, “\rb Expel|גָּרֵ֛שׁ\rb* \rb the|הַזֹּ֖את\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb slave woman|הָאָמָ֥ה\rb* \rb and her son|בְּנָ֑הּ\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb the slave woman’s|הָאָמָ֣ה\rb*\rb |הַזֹּ֔את\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb will never|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb share in the inheritance|יִירַשׁ֙\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb my son|בְּנִ֖י\rb*\rb |עִם־\rb* \rb Isaac|יִצְחָֽק׃\rb*!”\f + \fr 21:10 \ft Cited in Galatians 4:30\f*
\p \v 11 \rb Now this matter|הַדָּבָ֛ר\rb* \rb distressed|וַיֵּ֧רַע\rb*\rb |בְּעֵינֵ֣י\rb* \rb Abraham|אַבְרָהָ֑ם\rb* \rb greatly|מְאֹ֖ד\rb*\rb |עַ֖ל\rb* \rb because it concerned|אוֹדֹ֥ת\rb* \rb his son Ishmael|בְּנֽוֹ׃\rb*. \v 12 \rb But God|אֱלֹהִ֜ים\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Abraham|אַבְרָהָ֗ם\rb*, “\rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb be distressed|יֵרַ֤ע\rb*\rb |בְּעֵינֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb about|עַל־\rb* \rb the boy|הַנַּ֣עַר\rb*\rb |וְעַל־\rb* \rb and your maidservant|אֲמָתֶ֔ךָ\rb*. \rb Listen to|שְׁמַ֣ע\rb*\rb |בְּקֹלָ֑הּ\rb* \rb everything|כֹּל֩\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb Sarah|שָׂרָ֖ה\rb* \rb tells|תֹּאמַ֥ר\rb* \rb you|אֵלֶ֛יךָ\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb through Isaac|בְיִצְחָ֔ק\rb* \rb your|לְךָ֖\rb* \rb offspring|זָֽרַע׃\rb* \rb will be reckoned|יִקָּרֵ֥א\rb*.\f + \fr 21:12 \ft Cited in Romans 9:7 and Hebrews 11:18\f* \v 13 \rb But I will also|וְגַ֥ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb make|אֲשִׂימֶ֑נּוּ\rb* \rb a nation|לְג֣וֹי\rb* \rb of the slave woman’s|הָאָמָ֖ה\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb*, \rb because|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb he|הֽוּא׃\rb* \rb is your offspring|זַרְעֲךָ֖\rb*.”
\p \v 14 \rb Early in the morning|בַּבֹּ֡קֶר\rb*, \rb Abraham|אַבְרָהָ֣ם׀\rb* \rb got up|וַיַּשְׁכֵּ֣ם\rb*, \rb took|וַיִּֽקַּֽח־\rb* \rb bread|לֶחֶם֩\rb* \rb and a skin of water|וְחֵ֨מַת\rb*\rb |מַ֜יִם\rb*,\rb |וַיִּתֵּ֣ן\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb put them|שָׂ֧ם\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb Hagar’s|הָ֠גָר\rb* \rb shoulders|שִׁכְמָ֛הּ\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and sent her away with the boy|הַיֶּ֖לֶד\rb*\rb |וַֽיְשַׁלְּחֶ֑הָ\rb*. \rb She left|וַתֵּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb and wandered|וַתֵּ֔תַע\rb* \rb in the Wilderness|בְּמִדְבַּ֖ר\rb* \rb of|בְּאֵ֥ר\rb* \rb Beersheba|שָֽׁבַע׃\rb*. \v 15 \rb When the water|הַמַּ֖יִם\rb* \rb in|מִן־\rb* \rb the skin|הַחֵ֑מֶת\rb* \rb was gone|וַיִּכְל֥וּ\rb*, \rb she left|וַתַּשְׁלֵ֣ךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the boy|הַיֶּ֔לֶד\rb* \rb under|תַּ֖חַת\rb* \rb one|אַחַ֥ד\rb* \rb of the bushes|הַשִּׂיחִֽם׃\rb*. \v 16 \rb Then she went off|וַתֵּלֶךְ֩\rb* \rb and sat down|וַתֵּ֨שֶׁב\rb* \rb nearby|מִנֶּ֗גֶד\rb*, \rb about a bowshot|כִּמְטַחֲוֵ֣י\rb*\rb |קֶ֔שֶׁת\rb* \rb away|הַרְחֵק֙\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb she said|אָֽמְרָ֔ה\rb*, “\rb I cannot|אַל־\rb* \rb bear to watch|אֶרְאֶ֖ה\rb* \rb the boy|הַיָּ֑לֶד\rb* \rb die|בְּמ֣וֹת\rb*!” \rb And as she sat|וַתֵּ֣שֶׁב\rb* \rb nearby|מִנֶּ֔גֶד\rb*, \rb she lifted up|וַתִּשָּׂ֥א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb her voice|קֹלָ֖הּ\rb* \rb and wept|וַתֵּֽבְךְּ׃\rb*.\f + \fr 21:16 \ft Hebrew; LXX \fqa the child lifted up his voice and wept\f*
\p \v 17 \rb Then God|אֱלֹהִים֮\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb heard|וַיִּשְׁמַ֣ע\rb* \rb the voice|ק֣וֹל\rb* \rb of the boy|הַנַּעַר֒\rb*, \rb and the angel|מַלְאַ֨ךְ\rb* \rb of God|אֱלֹהִ֤ים׀\rb* \rb called|וַיִּקְרָא֩\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Hagar|הָגָר֙\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb heaven|הַשָּׁמַ֔יִם\rb*\rb |וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb*, “\rb What is wrong|מַה־\rb*, \rb Hagar|הָגָ֑ר\rb*? \rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb be afraid|תִּ֣ירְאִ֔י\rb*, \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֛ים\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb has heard|שָׁמַ֧ע\rb* \rb the voice|ק֥וֹל\rb* \rb of the boy|הַנַּ֖עַר\rb* \rb where|בַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb he|הוּא־\rb* \rb lies|שָֽׁם׃\rb*. \v 18 \rb Get up|ק֚וּמִי\rb*, \rb lift up|שְׂאִ֣י\rb* \rb the boy|הַנַּ֔עַר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*, \rb and take|וְהַחֲזִ֥יקִי\rb* \rb him|בּ֑וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb by the hand|יָדֵ֖ךְ\rb*, \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I will make him|אֲשִׂימֶֽנּוּ׃\rb* \rb into a great|גָּד֖וֹל\rb* \rb nation|לְג֥וֹי\rb*.” \v 19 \rb Then God|אֱלֹהִים֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb opened|וַיִּפְקַ֤ח\rb* \rb her eyes|עֵינֶ֔יהָ\rb*, \rb and she saw|וַתֵּ֖רֶא\rb* \rb a well|בְּאֵ֣ר\rb* \rb of water|מָ֑יִם\rb*. \rb So she went|וַתֵּ֜לֶךְ\rb* \rb and filled|וַתְּמַלֵּ֤א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the skin with water|הַחֵ֙מֶת֙\rb*\rb |מַ֔יִם\rb* \rb and gave the boy|הַנָּֽעַר׃\rb* \rb a drink|וַתַּ֖שְׁקְ\rb*.\rb |אֶת־\rb*
\p \v 20 \rb And God|אֱלֹהִ֛ים\rb* \rb was|וַיְהִ֧י\rb* \rb with|אֶת־\rb* \rb the boy|הַנַּ֖עַר\rb*, \rb and he grew up|וַיִּגְדָּ֑ל\rb* \rb and settled|וַיֵּ֙שֶׁב֙\rb* \rb in the wilderness|בַּמִּדְבָּ֔ר\rb* \rb and became|וַיְהִ֖י\rb* \rb a great|רֹבֶ֥ה\rb* \rb archer|קַשָּֽׁת׃\rb*. \v 21 \rb And while he was dwelling|וַיֵּ֖שֶׁב\rb* \rb in the Wilderness|בְּמִדְבַּ֣ר\rb* \rb of Paran|פָּארָ֑ן\rb*, \rb his mother|אִמּ֛וֹ\rb* \rb got|וַתִּֽקַּֽח־\rb* \rb a wife|אִשָּׁ֖ה\rb* \rb for him|ל֥וֹ\rb* \rb from the land|מֵאֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרָֽיִם׃פ\rb*.
\s1 The Covenant at Beersheba
\p \v 22 \rb |וַֽיְהִי֙\rb* \rb At that|הַהִ֔וא\rb* \rb time|בָּעֵ֣ת\rb* \rb Abimelech|אֲבִימֶ֗לֶךְ\rb* \rb and Phicol|וּפִיכֹל֙\rb* \rb the commander|שַׂר־\rb* \rb of his army|צְבָא֔וֹ\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Abraham|אַבְרָהָ֖ם\rb*,\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* “\rb God|אֱלֹהִ֣ים\rb* \rb is with you|עִמְּךָ֔\rb* \rb in all|בְּכֹ֥ל\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb you|אַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb do|עֹשֶֽׂה׃\rb*. \v 23 \rb Now, therefore|וְעַתָּ֗ה\rb*, \rb swear|הִשָּׁ֨בְעָה\rb* \rb to me|לִּ֤י\rb* \rb here|הֵ֔נָּה\rb* \rb before God|בֵֽאלֹהִים֙\rb* \rb that you will not|אִם־\rb* \rb deal falsely|תִּשְׁקֹ֣ר\rb* \rb with me|לִ֔י\rb* \rb or my children|וּלְנִינִ֖י\rb* \rb or descendants|וּלְנֶכְדִּ֑י\rb*. \rb Show|תַּעֲשֶׂ֣ה\rb* \rb to me|עִמָּדִ֔י\rb* \rb and|וְעִם־\rb* \rb to the country|הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb in which|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb you reside|גַּ֥רְתָּה\rb*\rb |בָּֽהּ׃\rb* \rb the same kindness|כַּחֶ֜סֶד\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I have shown|עָשִׂ֤יתִי\rb* \rb to you|עִמְּךָ֙\rb*.”
\p \v 24 \rb And Abraham|אַבְרָהָ֔ם\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb*, “\rb I|אָנֹכִ֖י\rb* \rb swear it.|אִשָּׁבֵֽעַ׃\rb*”
\p \v 25 \rb But when Abraham|אַבְרָהָ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb complained|וְהוֹכִ֥חַ\rb* \rb to Abimelech|אֲבִימֶ֑לֶךְ\rb* \rb about|עַל־\rb*\rb |אֹדוֹת֙\rb* \rb a well|בְּאֵ֣ר\rb*\rb |הַמַּ֔יִם\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb Abimelech’s|אֲבִימֶֽלֶךְ׃\rb* \rb servants|עַבְדֵ֥י\rb* \rb had seized|גָּזְל֖וּ\rb*, \v 26 \rb Abimelech|אֲבִימֶ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb I do not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb know|יָדַ֔עְתִּי\rb* \rb who|מִ֥י\rb* \rb has done|עָשָׂ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb*\rb |וְגַם־\rb*\rb |הַדָּבָ֣ר\rb*. \rb You|אַתָּ֞ה\rb* \rb did not|לֹא־\rb* \rb tell|הִגַּ֣דְתָּ\rb* \rb me|לִּ֗י\rb*,\rb |וְגַ֧ם\rb* \rb so I|אָנֹכִ֛י\rb* \rb have not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb heard|שָׁמַ֖עְתִּי\rb* \rb about it until today|בִּלְתִּ֥י\rb*\rb |הַיּֽוֹם׃\rb*.”
\p \v 27 \rb So Abraham|אַבְרָהָם֙\rb* \rb brought|וַיִּקַּ֤ח\rb* \rb sheep|צֹ֣אן\rb* \rb and cattle|וּבָקָ֔ר\rb* \rb and gave them|וַיִּתֵּ֖ן\rb* \rb to Abimelech|לַאֲבִימֶ֑לֶךְ\rb*, \rb and the two men|שְׁנֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb made|וַיִּכְרְת֥וּ\rb* \rb a covenant|בְּרִֽית׃\rb*. \v 28 \rb Abraham|אַבְרָהָ֗ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb separated|וַיַּצֵּ֣ב\rb*\rb |לְבַדְּהֶֽן׃\rb* \rb seven|שֶׁ֛בַע\rb* \rb ewe lambs|כִּבְשֹׂ֥ת\rb* \rb from the flock|הַצֹּ֖אן\rb*, \v 29 \rb and Abimelech|אֲבִימֶ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb asked|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb him|אַבְרָהָ֑ם\rb*, “\rb Why|מָ֣ה\rb*\rb |הֵ֗נָּה\rb* \rb have you set apart|הִצַּ֖בְתָּ\rb*\rb |לְבַדָּֽנָה׃\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֔לֶּה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb seven|שֶׁ֤בַע\rb* \rb ewe lambs|כְּבָשֹׂת֙\rb*?”
\p \v 30 \rb He replied|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*, “\rb You are to accept|תִּקַּ֖ח\rb* \rb the seven|שֶׁ֣בַע\rb* \rb ewe lambs|כְּבָשֹׂ֔ת\rb* \rb from my hand|מִיָּדִ֑י\rb*\rb |בַּעֲבוּר֙\rb*\rb |תִּֽהְיֶה־\rb*\rb |לִּ֣י\rb* \rb as my witness|לְעֵדָ֔ה\rb* \rb that|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb I dug|חָפַ֖רְתִּי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּֽאת׃\rb* \rb well|הַבְּאֵ֥ר\rb*.” \v 31 \rb So|עַל־\rb*\rb |כֵּ֗ן\rb* \rb that|הַה֖וּא\rb* \rb place|לַמָּק֥וֹם\rb* \rb was called|קָרָ֛א\rb* \rb Beersheba|שָׁ֑בַע\rb*,\f + \fr 21:31 \fqa Beersheba \ft means \fqa well of seven \ft or \fqa well of the oath\ft .\f* \rb because|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb it was there|שָׁ֥ם\rb* \rb that the two|שְׁנֵיהֶֽם׃\rb* \rb of them swore an oath|נִשְׁבְּע֖וּ\rb*. \v 32 \rb After they had made|וַיִּכְרְת֥וּ\rb* \rb the covenant|בְרִ֖ית\rb*\rb |בִּבְאֵ֣ר\rb* \rb at Beersheba|שָׁ֑בַע\rb*, \rb Abimelech|אֲבִימֶ֗לֶךְ\rb* \rb and Phicol|וּפִיכֹל֙\rb* \rb the commander|שַׂר־\rb* \rb of his army|צְבָא֔וֹ\rb* \rb got up|וַיָּ֣קָם\rb* \rb and returned|וַיָּשֻׁ֖בוּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of the Philistines|פְּלִשְׁתִּֽים׃\rb*.
\p \v 33 \rb And Abraham planted|וַיִּטַּ֥ע\rb* \rb a tamarisk tree|אֶ֖שֶׁל\rb*\rb |בִּבְאֵ֣ר\rb* \rb in Beersheba|שָׁ֑בַע\rb*, \rb and there|שָׁ֔ם\rb* \rb he called|וַיִּ֨קְרָא־\rb* \rb upon the name|בְּשֵׁ֥ם\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*, \rb the Eternal|עוֹלָֽם׃\rb* \rb God|אֵ֥ל\rb*.\f + \fr 21:33 \ft Hebrew \fqa El-Olam\f* \v 34 \rb And Abraham|אַבְרָהָ֛ם\rb* \rb resided|וַיָּ֧גָר\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of the Philistines|פְּלִשְׁתִּ֖ים\rb* \rb for a long|רַבִּֽים׃פ\rb* \rb time|יָמִ֥ים\rb*.
\c 22
\s1 The Offering of Isaac
\p \v 1 \rb |וַיְהִ֗י\rb* \rb Some time later|אַחַר֙\rb*\rb |הָאֵ֔לֶּה\rb*\rb |הַדְּבָרִ֣ים\rb* \rb God|וְהָ֣אֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb* \rb tested|נִסָּ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Abraham|אַבְרָהָ֑ם\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to him|אֵלָ֔יו\rb*, “\rb Abraham|אַבְרָהָ֖ם\rb*!”
\p “\rb Here I am|הִנֵּֽנִי׃\rb*,” \rb he answered|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb*.
\p \v 2 “\rb Take|קַח־\rb*\rb |נָ֠א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your son|בִּנְךָ֙\rb*,”\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb God said|וַיֹּ֡אמֶר\rb*, “\rb your only|יְחִֽידְךָ֤\rb* \rb son Isaac|יִצְחָ֔ק\rb*, \rb whom|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb you love|אָהַ֙בְתָּ֙\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb and go|וְלֶךְ־\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb of Moriah|הַמֹּרִיָּ֑ה\rb*. \rb Offer him|וְהַעֲלֵ֤הוּ\rb* \rb there|שָׁם֙\rb* \rb as a burnt offering|לְעֹלָ֔ה\rb* \rb on|עַ֚ל\rb* \rb one|אַחַ֣ד\rb* \rb of the mountains|הֶֽהָרִ֔ים\rb*, \rb which|אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb I will show|אֹמַ֥ר\rb* \rb you|אֵלֶֽיךָ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 3 \rb So Abraham|אַבְרָהָ֜ם\rb* \rb got up early|וַיַּשְׁכֵּ֨ם\rb* \rb the next morning|בַּבֹּ֗קֶר\rb*, \rb saddled|וַֽיַּחֲבֹשׁ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his donkey|חֲמֹר֔וֹ\rb*, \rb and took|וַיִּקַּ֞ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb along|אִתּ֔וֹ\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֖ת\rb* \rb two|שְׁנֵ֤י\rb* \rb of his servants|נְעָרָיו֙\rb* \rb and his son|בְּנ֑וֹ\rb* \rb Isaac|יִצְחָ֣ק\rb*. \rb He split|וַיְבַקַּע֙\rb* \rb the wood|עֲצֵ֣י\rb* \rb for a burnt offering|עֹלָ֔ה\rb* \rb and set out for|וַיָּ֣קָם\rb*\rb |וַיֵּ֔לֶךְ\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the place|הַמָּק֖וֹם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb God|הָאֱלֹהִֽים׃\rb* \rb had designated|אָֽמַר־\rb*\rb |ל֥וֹ\rb*.
\p \v 4 \rb On the third|הַשְּׁלִישִׁ֗י\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb Abraham|אַבְרָהָ֧ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb looked up|וַיִּשָּׂ֨א\rb*\rb |עֵינָ֛יו\rb* \rb and saw|וַיַּ֥רְא\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the place|הַמָּק֖וֹם\rb* \rb in the distance|מֵרָחֹֽק׃\rb*. \v 5 “\rb Stay|שְׁבוּ־\rb* \rb here|פֹּה֙\rb* \rb with|עִֽם־\rb* \rb the donkey|הַחֲמ֔וֹר\rb*,” \rb Abraham|אַבְרָהָ֜ם\rb* \rb told|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb his servants|נְעָרָ֗יו\rb*. “\rb The boy|וְהַנַּ֔עַר\rb* \rb and I|וַאֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb will go|נֵלְכָ֖ה\rb* \rb over|עַד־\rb* \rb there|כֹּ֑ה\rb* \rb to worship|וְנִֽשְׁתַּחֲוֶ֖ה\rb*, \rb and then we will return|וְנָשׁ֥וּבָה\rb* \rb to you|אֲלֵיכֶֽם׃\rb*.”
\p \v 6 \rb Abraham|אַבְרָהָ֜ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb took|וַיִּקַּ֨ח\rb* \rb the wood|עֲצֵ֣י\rb* \rb for the burnt offering|הָעֹלָ֗ה\rb* \rb and placed|וַיָּ֙שֶׂם֙\rb* \rb it on|עַל־\rb* \rb his son|בְּנ֔וֹ\rb* \rb Isaac|יִצְחָ֣ק\rb*. \rb He himself carried|וַיִּקַּ֣ח\rb*\rb |בְּיָד֔וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the fire|הָאֵ֖שׁ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and the sacrificial knife|הַֽמַּאֲכֶ֑לֶת\rb*, \rb and the two|שְׁנֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb of them walked on|וַיֵּלְכ֥וּ\rb* \rb together|יַחְדָּֽו׃\rb*.
\p \v 7 \rb Then Isaac|יִצְחָ֜ק\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his father|אָבִיו֙\rb* \rb Abraham|אַבְרָהָ֤ם\rb*\rb |וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb My father|אָבִ֔י\rb*!”
\p “\rb Here I am|הִנֶּ֣נִּֽי\rb*, \rb my son|בְנִ֑י\rb*,” \rb he replied|וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb*.
\p “\rb The fire|הָאֵשׁ֙\rb* \rb and the wood|וְהָ֣עֵצִ֔ים\rb* \rb are here|הִנֵּ֤ה\rb*,” \rb said Isaac|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*, “\rb but where|וְאַיֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb is the lamb|הַשֶּׂ֖ה\rb* \rb for the burnt offering|לְעֹלָֽה׃\rb*?”
\p \v 8 \rb Abraham|אַבְרָהָ֔ם\rb* \rb answered|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb*, “\rb God|אֱלֹהִ֞ים\rb* \rb Himself|לּ֥וֹ\rb* \rb will provide|יִרְאֶה־\rb* \rb the lamb|הַשֶּׂ֛ה\rb* \rb for the burnt offering|לְעֹלָ֖ה\rb*, \rb my son|בְּנִ֑י\rb*.” \rb And the two|שְׁנֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb walked on|וַיֵּלְכ֥וּ\rb* \rb together|יַחְדָּֽו׃\rb*.
\p \v 9 \rb When they arrived|וַיָּבֹ֗אוּ\rb* \rb at|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb the place|הַמָּקוֹם֮\rb* \rb God|הָאֱלֹהִים֒\rb* \rb had designated|אָֽמַר־\rb*\rb |ל֣וֹ\rb*, \rb Abraham|אַבְרָהָם֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb built|וַיִּ֨בֶן\rb* \rb the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֔חַ\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֤ם\rb* \rb and arranged|וַֽיַּעֲרֹ֖ךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the wood|הָעֵצִ֑ים\rb*. \rb He bound|וַֽיַּעֲקֹד֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his son|בְּנ֔וֹ\rb* \rb Isaac|יִצְחָ֣ק\rb* \rb and placed|וַיָּ֤שֶׂם\rb* \rb him|אֹתוֹ֙\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֔חַ\rb*, \rb atop|מִמַּ֖עַל\rb* \rb the wood|לָעֵצִֽים׃\rb*. \v 10 \rb Then Abraham|אַבְרָהָם֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb reached out|וַיִּשְׁלַ֤ח\rb* \rb his hand|יָד֔וֹ\rb* \rb and took|וַיִּקַּ֖ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the knife|הַֽמַּאֲכֶ֑לֶת\rb* \rb to slaughter|לִשְׁחֹ֖ט\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his son|בְּנֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\s1 The LORD Provides the Sacrifice
\p \v 11 \rb Just then the angel|מַלְאַ֤ךְ\rb*\f + \fr 22:11 \ft Or \fqa Angel\ft ; also in verses 12 and 15\f* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb called out|וַיִּקְרָ֨א\rb* \rb to him|אֵלָ֜יו\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb heaven|הַשָּׁמַ֔יִם\rb*\rb |וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Abraham|אַבְרָהָ֣ם׀\rb*, \rb Abraham|אַבְרָהָ֑ם\rb*!”
\p “\rb Here I am|הִנֵּֽנִי׃\rb*,” \rb he replied|וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb*.
\p \v 12 “\rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb lay|תִּשְׁלַ֤ח\rb* \rb a hand|יָֽדְךָ֙\rb* \rb on|אֶל־\rb* \rb the boy|הַנַּ֔עַר\rb*\rb |וְאַל־\rb* \rb or do|תַּ֥עַשׂ\rb* \rb anything|מְא֑וּמָּה\rb* \rb to him|ל֖וֹ\rb*,” \rb said the angel|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*, “\rb for|כִּ֣י׀\rb* \rb now|עַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb I know|יָדַ֗עְתִּי\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb you|אַ֔תָּה\rb* \rb fear|יְרֵ֤א\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִים֙\rb*, \rb since you have not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb withheld|חָשַׂ֛כְתָּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your only|יְחִידְךָ֖\rb* \rb son|בִּנְךָ֥\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb from me|מִמֶּֽנִּי׃\rb*.\f + \fr 22:12 \ft Or \fqa from Me\f*”
\p \v 13 \rb Then Abraham|אַבְרָהָ֜ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb looked up|וַיִּשָּׂ֨א\rb*\rb |עֵינָ֗יו\rb* \rb and saw|וַיַּרְא֙\rb* \rb behind him|אַחַ֕ר\rb* \rb a ram|אַ֔יִל\rb*\f + \fr 22:13 \ft Most MT manuscripts; other Hebrew manuscripts, SP, LXX, and Syriac \fqa saw one ram\f* \rb in a thicket|בַּסְּבַ֖ךְ\rb*, \rb caught|נֶאֱחַ֥ז\rb* \rb by its horns|בְּקַרְנָ֑יו\rb*. \rb So he|אַבְרָהָם֙\rb* \rb went|וַיֵּ֤לֶךְ\rb* \rb and took|וַיִּקַּ֣ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the ram|הָאַ֔יִל\rb* \rb and offered|וַיַּעֲלֵ֥הוּ\rb* \rb it as a burnt offering|לְעֹלָ֖ה\rb* \rb in place of|תַּ֥חַת\rb* \rb his son|בְּנֽוֹ׃\rb*. \v 14 \rb And Abraham|אַבְרָהָ֛ם\rb* \rb called|וַיִּקְרָ֧א\rb*\rb |שֵֽׁם־\rb* \rb that|הַה֖וּא\rb* \rb place|הַמָּק֥וֹם\rb* \rb The LORD|יְהוָ֣ה׀\rb* \rb Will Provide|יִרְאֶ֑ה\rb*.\f + \fr 22:14 \ft Hebrew \fqa YHWH Yireh\f* \rb So|אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb to this day|הַיּ֔וֹם\rb* \rb it is said|יֵאָמֵ֣ר\rb*, “\rb On the mountain|בְּהַ֥ר\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb it will be provided|יֵרָאֶֽה׃\rb*.”
\p \v 15 \rb And the angel|מַלְאַ֥ךְ\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb called|וַיִּקְרָ֛א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Abraham|אַבְרָהָ֑ם\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb heaven|הַשָּׁמָֽיִם׃\rb* \rb a second time|שֵׁנִ֖ית\rb*, \v 16 \rb saying|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*, “\rb By Myself|בִּ֥י\rb* \rb I have sworn|נִשְׁבַּ֖עְתִּי\rb*, \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*, \rb that|כִּ֗י\rb* \rb because|יַ֚עַן\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb you have done|עָשִׂ֙יתָ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb*\rb |הַדָּבָ֣ר\rb* \rb and have not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb withheld|חָשַׂ֖כְתָּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your only|יְחִידֶֽךָ׃\rb* \rb son|בִּנְךָ֥\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \v 17 \rb |כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I will surely bless you|בָרֵ֣ךְ\rb*\rb |אֲבָרֶכְךָ֗\rb*, \rb and I will multiply|וְהַרְבָּ֨ה\rb*\rb |אַרְבֶּ֤ה\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb your descendants|זַרְעֲךָ֙\rb*\f + \fr 22:17 \ft Cited in Hebrews 6:14\f* \rb like the stars|כְּכוֹכְבֵ֣י\rb* \rb in the sky|הַשָּׁמַ֔יִם\rb* \rb and the sand|וְכַח֕וֹל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the seashore|שְׂפַ֣ת\rb*\rb |הַיָּ֑ם\rb*. \rb Your descendants|זַרְעֲךָ֔\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb will possess|וְיִרַ֣שׁ\rb* \rb the gates|שַׁ֥עַר\rb* \rb of their enemies|אֹיְבָֽיו׃\rb*. \v 18 \rb And through your offspring|בְזַרְעֲךָ֔\rb* \rb all|כֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb nations|גּוֹיֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the earth|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb* \rb will be blessed|וְהִתְבָּרֲכ֣וּ\rb*,\f + \fr 22:18 \ft Cited in Acts 3:25\f* \rb because|עֵ֕קֶב\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you have obeyed|שָׁמַ֖עְתָּ\rb* \rb My voice|בְּקֹלִֽי׃\rb*.”
\p \v 19 \rb Abraham|אַבְרָהָם֙\rb* \rb went back|וַיָּ֤שָׁב\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his servants|נְעָרָ֔יו\rb*, \rb and they got up|וַיָּקֻ֛מוּ\rb* \rb and set out|וַיֵּלְכ֥וּ\rb* \rb together|יַחְדָּ֖ו\rb* \rb for|אֶל־\rb*\rb |בְּאֵ֣ר\rb* \rb Beersheba|שָׁ֑בַע\rb*. \rb And Abraham|אַבְרָהָ֖ם\rb* \rb settled|וַיֵּ֥שֶׁב\rb* \rb in|בִּבְאֵ֥ר\rb* \rb Beersheba|שָֽׁבַע׃פ\rb*.
\s1 The Sons of Nahor
\p \v 20 \rb Some time later|וַיְהִ֗י\rb*\rb |אַחֲרֵי֙\rb*\rb |הָאֵ֔לֶּה\rb*\rb |הַדְּבָרִ֣ים\rb*, \rb Abraham|לְאַבְרָהָ֖ם\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*\rb |הִ֠נֵּה\rb* \rb was told|וַיֻּגַּ֥ד\rb*, “\rb Milcah|מִלְכָּ֥ה\rb* \rb has also|גַם־\rb*\rb |הִ֛וא\rb* \rb borne|יָלְדָ֨ה\rb* \rb sons|בָּנִ֖ים\rb* \rb to your brother|אָחִֽיךָ׃\rb* \rb Nahor|לְנָח֥וֹר\rb*: \v 21 \rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Uz|ע֥וּץ\rb* \rb the firstborn|בְּכֹר֖וֹ\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb his brother|אָחִ֑יו\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Buz|בּ֣וּז\rb*, \rb Kemuel|קְמוּאֵ֖ל\rb* (\rb the father|אֲבִ֥י\rb* \rb of Aram|אֲרָֽם׃\rb*), \v 22 \rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Chesed|כֶּ֣שֶׂד\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Hazo|חֲז֔וֹ\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Pildash|פִּלְדָּ֖שׁ\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Jidlaph|יִדְלָ֑ף\rb*,\rb |וְאֵ֖ת\rb* \rb and Bethuel|בְּתוּאֵֽל׃\rb*.”
\p \v 23 \rb And Bethuel|וּבְתוּאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb became the father of|יָלַ֣ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Rebekah|רִבְקָ֑ה\rb*. \rb Milcah|מִלְכָּ֔ה\rb* \rb bore|יָלְדָ֣ה\rb* \rb these|אֵ֙לֶּה֙\rb* \rb eight sons|שְׁמֹנָ֥ה\rb* \rb to Abraham’s|אַבְרָהָֽם׃\rb* \rb brother|אֲחִ֥י\rb* \rb Nahor|לְנָח֖וֹר\rb*. \v 24 \rb Moreover|גַּם־\rb*, \rb Nahor’s concubine|וּפִֽילַגְשׁ֖וֹ\rb*, \rb whose name|וּשְׁמָ֣הּ\rb* \rb was Reumah|רְאוּמָ֑ה\rb*,\rb |הִוא֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb bore|וַתֵּ֤לֶד\rb* \rb Tebah|טֶ֣בַח\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Gaham|גַּ֔חַם\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Tahash|תַּ֖חַשׁ\rb*,\rb |וְאֶֽת־\rb* \rb and Maacah|מַעֲכָֽה׃ס\rb*.
\c 23
\s1 The Death and Burial of Sarah
\p \v 1 \rb Now|וַיִּהְיוּ֙\rb* \rb Sarah|שָׂרָ֔ה\rb* \rb lived to be|חַיֵּ֣י\rb* \rb 127|מֵאָ֥ה\rb*\rb |וְעֶשְׂרִ֥ים\rb*\rb |וְשֶׁ֣בַע\rb*\rb |שָׁנִ֑ים\rb*\rb |שְׁנֵ֖י\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָ֛ה\rb* \rb old|שָׁנָ֖ה\rb*\rb |שָׂרָֽה׃\rb*\rb |חַיֵּ֥י\rb*. \v 2 \rb She|שָׂרָ֗ה\rb* \rb died|וַתָּ֣מָת\rb*\rb |בְּקִרְיַ֥ת\rb* \rb in Kiriath-arba|אַרְבַּ֛ע\rb* \rb (that is|הִ֥וא\rb*, \rb Hebron)|חֶבְר֖וֹן\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Canaan|כְּנָ֑עַן\rb*, \rb and Abraham|אַבְרָהָ֔ם\rb* \rb went out|וַיָּבֹא֙\rb* \rb to mourn|לִסְפֹּ֥ד\rb* \rb and to weep|וְלִבְכֹּתָֽהּ׃\rb* \rb for her|לְשָׂרָ֖ה\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb Then Abraham|אַבְרָהָ֔ם\rb* \rb got up|וַיָּ֙קָם֙\rb* \rb from|מֵעַ֖ל\rb* \rb beside|פְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb his dead wife|מֵת֑וֹ\rb* \rb and said|וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the Hittites|בְּנֵי־\rb*\rb |חֵ֖ת\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*,\f + \fr 23:3 \ft Or \fqa sons of Heth\ft ; also in verses 5, 7, 10, 16, 18, and 20\f* \v 4 “\rb I am|אָנֹכִ֖י\rb* \rb a foreigner|גֵּר־\rb* \rb and an outsider|וְתוֹשָׁ֥ב\rb* \rb among you|עִמָּכֶ֑ם\rb*. \rb Give|תְּנ֨וּ\rb* \rb me|לִ֤י\rb* \rb a burial|קֶ֙בֶר֙\rb* \rb site|אֲחֻזַּת־\rb* \rb among you|עִמָּכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb so that I can bury|וְאֶקְבְּרָ֥ה\rb* \rb my dead|מֵתִ֖י\rb*.”\rb |מִלְּפָנָֽי׃\rb*
\p \v 5 \rb The Hittites|בְנֵי־\rb*\rb |חֵ֛ת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb replied|וַיַּעֲנ֧וּ\rb* \rb to Abraham|אַבְרָהָ֖ם\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֥ר\rb*, \v 6 “\rb Listen to us|שְׁמָעֵ֣נוּ׀\rb*, \rb sir|אֲדֹנִ֗י\rb*. \rb You|אַתָּה֙\rb* \rb are God’s|אֱלֹהִ֤ים\rb* \rb chosen one|נְשִׂ֨יא\rb* \rb among us|בְּתוֹכֵ֔נוּ\rb*. \rb Bury|קְבֹ֖ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your dead|מֵתֶ֑ךָ\rb*\rb |אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb in the finest|בְּמִבְחַ֣ר\rb* \rb of our tombs|קְבָרֵ֔ינוּ\rb*. \rb None|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb of us|מִמֶּ֔נּוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb will withhold|יִכְלֶ֥ה\rb*\rb |מִמְּךָ֖\rb* \rb his tomb|קִבְר֛וֹ\rb* \rb for burying|מִקְּבֹ֥ר\rb* \rb your dead|מֵתֶֽךָ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 7 \rb Then Abraham|אַבְרָהָ֛ם\rb* \rb rose|וַיָּ֧קָם\rb* \rb and bowed down|וַיִּשְׁתַּ֥חוּ\rb* \rb before the people|לְעַם־\rb* \rb of the land|הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb*, \rb the Hittites|לִבְנֵי־\rb*\rb |חֵֽת׃\rb*. \v 8 “\rb If|אִם־\rb*\rb |יֵ֣שׁ\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb you are willing|נַפְשְׁכֶ֗ם\rb* \rb for me to bury|לִקְבֹּ֤ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb my dead|מֵתִי֙\rb*,” \rb he said|וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb to them|אִתָּ֖ם\rb*,\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* “\rb |מִלְּפָנַ֔י\rb* \rb listen to me|שְׁמָע֕וּנִי\rb*, \rb and approach|וּפִגְעוּ־\rb* \rb Ephron|בְּעֶפְר֥וֹן\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Zohar|צֹֽחַר׃\rb* \rb on my behalf|לִ֖י\rb* \v 9 \rb to sell|וְיִתֶּן־\rb* \rb me|לִ֗י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the cave|מְעָרַ֤ת\rb* \rb of Machpelah|הַמַּכְפֵּלָה֙\rb* \rb that belongs|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb to him|ל֔וֹ\rb*; \rb it|אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb is at the end|בִּקְצֵ֣ה\rb* \rb of his field|שָׂדֵ֑הוּ\rb*. \rb Let him sell it|יִתְּנֶ֥נָּה\rb* \rb to me|לִ֛י\rb* \rb in your presence|בְּתוֹכְכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb for full|מָלֵ֜א\rb* \rb price|בְּכֶ֨סֶף\rb*, \rb so that I may have a burial|קָֽבֶר׃\rb* \rb site|לַאֲחֻזַּת־\rb*.”
\p \v 10 \rb Now Ephron|וְעֶפְר֥וֹן\rb* \rb was sitting|יֹשֵׁ֖ב\rb* \rb among|בְּת֣וֹךְ\rb* \rb the sons|בְּנֵי־\rb* \rb of Heth|חֵ֑ת\rb*. \rb So in the presence|בְּאָזְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of all|לְכֹ֛ל\rb* \rb the Hittites|בְנֵי־\rb*\rb |חֵ֔ת\rb* \rb who had come|בָּאֵ֥י\rb* \rb to the gate|שַֽׁעַר־\rb* \rb of his city|עִיר֖וֹ\rb*,\rb |לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb* \rb Ephron|עֶפְר֨וֹן\rb* \rb the Hittite|הַחִתִּ֤י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb answered|וַיַּעַן֩\rb* \rb Abraham|אַבְרָהָם֙\rb*, \v 11 “\rb No|לֹֽא־\rb*, \rb my lord|אֲדֹנִ֣י\rb*. \rb Listen to me|שְׁמָעֵ֔נִי\rb*. \rb I give|נָתַ֣תִּי\rb* \rb you|לָ֔ךְ\rb* \rb the field|הַשָּׂדֶה֙\rb*, \rb and I give|נְתַתִּ֑יהָ\rb* \rb you the cave|וְהַמְּעָרָ֥ה\rb* \rb that is in it|אֲשֶׁר־\rb*.\rb |בּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb I give it|נְתַתִּ֥יהָ\rb* \rb to you|לְךָ֣\rb* \rb in the presence|לְעֵינֵ֧י\rb* \rb of my people|בְנֵי־\rb*\rb |עַמִּ֛י\rb*. \rb Bury|קְבֹ֥ר\rb* \rb your dead|מֵתֶֽךָ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 12 \rb Again Abraham|אַבְרָהָ֔ם\rb* \rb bowed down|וַיִּשְׁתַּ֙חוּ֙\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb the people|עַ֥ם\rb* \rb of the land|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb* \v 13 \rb and said|וַיְדַבֵּ֨ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Ephron|עֶפְר֜וֹן\rb* \rb in their presence|בְּאָזְנֵ֤י\rb*\rb |עַם־\rb*\rb |הָאָ֙רֶץ֙\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb*,\rb |אַ֛ךְ\rb* “\rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb you|אַתָּ֥ה\rb* \rb will please|ל֖וּ\rb* \rb listen to me|שְׁמָעֵ֑נִי\rb*, \rb I will pay you|נָתַ֜תִּי\rb* \rb the price|כֶּ֤סֶף\rb* \rb of the field|הַשָּׂדֶה֙\rb*. \rb Accept|קַ֣ח\rb* \rb it from me|מִמֶּ֔נִּי\rb*, \rb so that I may bury|וְאֶקְבְּרָ֥ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb my dead|מֵתִ֖י\rb* \rb there|שָֽׁמָּה׃\rb*.”
\p \v 14 \rb Ephron|עֶפְר֛וֹן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb answered|וַיַּ֧עַן\rb* \rb Abraham|אַבְרָהָ֖ם\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֥ר\rb*, \v 15 “\rb Listen to me|שְׁמָעֵ֔נִי\rb*, \rb my lord|אֲדֹנִ֣י\rb*. \rb The land|אֶרֶץ֩\rb* \rb is worth four|אַרְבַּ֨ע\rb* \rb hundred|מֵאֹ֧ת\rb* \rb shekels|שֶֽׁקֶל־\rb* \rb of silver|כֶּ֛סֶף\rb*,\f + \fr 23:15 \fqa 400 shekels \ft is approximately 10.1 pounds or 4.6 kilograms of silver; also in verse 16.\f* \rb but what|מַה־\rb* \rb is that|הִ֑וא\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb between you and me|בֵּינִ֥י\rb*\rb |וּבֵֽינְךָ֖\rb*? \rb Bury|קְבֹֽר׃\rb* \rb your dead|מֵתְךָ֖\rb*.”
\p \v 16 \rb Abraham|אַבְרָהָם֮\rb* \rb agreed|וַיִּשְׁמַ֣ע\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Ephron’s terms|עֶפְרוֹן֒\rb* \rb and|אַבְרָהָם֙\rb* \rb weighed out|וַיִּשְׁקֹ֤ל\rb* \rb for him|לְעֶפְרֹ֔ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the price|הַכֶּ֕סֶף\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb he had named|דִּבֶּ֖ר\rb* \rb in the hearing|בְּאָזְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the Hittites|בְנֵי־\rb*\rb |חֵ֑ת\rb*: \rb four|אַרְבַּ֤ע\rb* \rb hundred|מֵאוֹת֙\rb* \rb shekels|שֶׁ֣קֶל\rb* \rb of silver|כֶּ֔סֶף\rb*, \rb according to the standard|עֹבֵ֖ר\rb* \rb of the merchants|לַסֹּחֵֽר׃\rb*.
\p \v 17 \rb So Ephron’s|עֶפְר֗וֹן\rb* \rb field|שְׂדֵ֣ה\rb* \rb at Machpelah|בַּמַּכְפֵּלָ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb near|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb Mamre|מַמְרֵ֑א\rb*\rb |הַשָּׂדֶה֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר֙\rb*, \rb the cave|וְהַמְּעָרָ֣ה\rb* \rb that was|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb in it|בּ֔וֹ\rb*, \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the trees|הָעֵץ֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb within|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb the boundaries|גְּבֻל֖וֹ\rb*\rb |סָבִֽיב׃\rb* \rb of the field|בַּשָּׂדֶ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb were deeded over|וַיָּ֣קָם׀\rb* \v 18 \rb to Abraham’s|לְאַבְרָהָ֥ם\rb* \rb possession|לְמִקְנָ֖ה\rb* \rb in the presence|לְעֵינֵ֣י\rb* \rb of all|בְּכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb the Hittites|בְנֵי־\rb*\rb |חֵ֑ת\rb* \rb who had come|בָּאֵ֥י\rb* \rb to the gate|שַֽׁעַר־\rb* \rb of his city|עִירֽוֹ׃\rb*. \v 19 \rb After|וְאַחֲרֵי־\rb* \rb this|כֵן֩\rb*, \rb Abraham|אַבְרָהָ֜ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb buried|קָבַ֨ר\rb* \rb his wife|אִשְׁתּ֗וֹ\rb* \rb Sarah|שָׂרָ֣ה\rb* \rb in|אֶל־\rb* \rb the cave|מְעָרַ֞ת\rb* \rb of the field|שְׂדֵ֧ה\rb* \rb at Machpelah|הַמַּכְפֵּלָ֛ה\rb* \rb near|עַל־\rb*\rb |פְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb Mamre|מַמְרֵ֖א\rb* \rb (that is|הִ֣וא\rb*, \rb Hebron|חֶבְר֑וֹן\rb*) \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb of Canaan|כְּנָֽעַן׃\rb*. \v 20 \rb So the field|הַשָּׂדֶ֜ה\rb* \rb and its|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb cave|וְהַמְּעָרָ֧ה\rb* \rb were deeded|וַיָּ֨קָם\rb* \rb by the Hittites|בְּנֵי־\rb*\rb |חֵֽת׃ס\rb* \rb to Abraham|לְאַבְרָהָ֖ם\rb* \rb as a burial|קָ֑בֶר\rb*\rb |מֵאֵ֖ת\rb* \rb site|לַאֲחֻזַּת־\rb*.
\c 24
\s1 A Wife for Isaac
\p \v 1 \rb By now Abraham|וְאַבְרָהָ֣ם\rb* \rb was old|זָקֵ֔ן\rb* \rb and well along|בָּ֖א\rb* \rb in years|בַּיָּמִ֑ים\rb*, \rb and the LORD|וַֽיהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb had blessed|בֵּרַ֥ךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb him|אַבְרָהָ֖ם\rb* \rb in every way|בַּכֹּֽל׃\rb*. \v 2 \rb So Abraham|אַבְרָהָ֗ם\rb* \rb instructed|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the chief|זְקַ֣ן\rb* \rb servant|עַבְדּוֹ֙\rb* \rb of his household|בֵּית֔וֹ\rb*, \rb who managed|הַמֹּשֵׁ֖ל\rb* \rb all he owned|בְּכָל־\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb*, “\rb Place|שִֽׂים־\rb*\rb |נָ֥א\rb* \rb your hand|יָדְךָ֖\rb* \rb under|תַּ֥חַת\rb* \rb my thigh|יְרֵכִֽי׃\rb*, \v 3 \rb and I will have you swear|וְאַשְׁבִּ֣יעֲךָ֔\rb* \rb by the LORD|בַּֽיהוָה֙\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of heaven|הַשָּׁמַ֔יִם\rb* \rb and the God|וֵֽאלֹהֵ֖י\rb* \rb of earth|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb*, \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb you will not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb take|תִקַּ֤ח\rb* \rb a wife|אִשָּׁה֙\rb* \rb for my son|לִבְנִ֔י\rb* \rb from the daughters|מִבְּנוֹת֙\rb* \rb of the Canaanites|הַֽכְּנַעֲנִ֔י\rb* \rb among|בְּקִרְבּֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb whom|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I|אָנֹכִ֖י\rb* \rb am dwelling|יוֹשֵׁ֥ב\rb*, \v 4 \rb but|כִּ֧י\rb* \rb will go|תֵּלֵ֑ךְ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb my country|אַרְצִ֛י\rb* \rb and|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb my kindred|מוֹלַדְתִּ֖י\rb* \rb to take|וְלָקַחְתָּ֥\rb* \rb a wife|אִשָּׁ֖ה\rb* \rb for my son|לִבְנִ֥י\rb* \rb Isaac|לְיִצְחָֽק׃\rb*.”
\p \v 5 \rb The servant|הָעֶ֔בֶד\rb* \rb asked|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb him|אֵלָיו֙\rb*, “\rb What if|אוּלַי֙\rb* \rb the woman|הָֽאִשָּׁ֔ה\rb* \rb is unwilling|לֹא־\rb*\rb |תֹאבֶ֣ה\rb* \rb to follow me|לָלֶ֥כֶת\rb*\rb |אַחֲרַ֖י\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּ֑את\rb* \rb land|הָאָ֣רֶץ\rb*? \rb Shall I then take your son back|הֶֽהָשֵׁ֤ב\rb*\rb |בִּנְךָ֔\rb*\rb |אָשִׁיב֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb from|מִשָּֽׁם׃\rb* \rb which|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb you came|יָצָ֥אתָ\rb*?”
\p \v 6 \rb Abraham|אַבְרָהָ֑ם\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb*,\rb |אֵלָ֖יו\rb* “\rb Make sure|הִשָּׁ֣מֶר\rb* \rb that you do not|פֶּן־\rb* \rb take my son|בְּנִ֖י\rb* \rb back|תָּשִׁ֥יב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb there|שָֽׁמָּה׃\rb*. \v 7 \rb The LORD|יְהוָ֣ה׀\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of heaven|הַשָּׁמַ֗יִם\rb*, \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb brought me|לְקָחַ֜נִי\rb* \rb from my father’s|אָבִי֮\rb* \rb house|מִבֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb and my native|מֽוֹלַדְתִּי֒\rb* \rb land|וּמֵאֶ֣רֶץ\rb*, \rb who|וַאֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb spoke|דִּבֶּר־\rb* \rb to me|לִ֜י\rb* \rb and|וַאֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb promised me on oath|נִֽשְׁבַּֽע־\rb*\rb |לִי֙\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb*, ‘\rb To your offspring|לְזַ֨רְעֲךָ֔\rb* \rb I will give|אֶתֵּ֖ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּ֑את\rb* \rb land|הָאָ֣רֶץ\rb*’— \rb He|ה֗וּא\rb* \rb will send|יִשְׁלַ֤ח\rb* \rb His angel|מַלְאָכוֹ֙\rb* \rb before you|לְפָנֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb so that you can take|וְלָקַחְתָּ֥\rb* \rb a wife|אִשָּׁ֛ה\rb* \rb for my son|לִבְנִ֖י\rb* \rb from there|מִשָּֽׁם׃\rb*. \v 8 \rb And if|וְאִם־\rb* \rb the woman|הָֽאִשָּׁה֙\rb* \rb is unwilling|לֹ֨א\rb*\rb |תֹאבֶ֤ה\rb* \rb to follow|לָלֶ֣כֶת\rb* \rb you|אַחֲרֶ֔יךָ\rb*, \rb then you are released|וְנִקִּ֕יתָ\rb* \rb from this|זֹ֑את\rb* \rb oath of mine|מִשְּׁבֻעָתִ֖י\rb*. \rb Only|רַ֣ק\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb do not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb take|תָשֵׁ֖ב\rb* \rb my son|בְּנִ֔י\rb* \rb back there|שָֽׁמָּה׃\rb*.”
\p \v 9 \rb So the servant|הָעֶ֙בֶד֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb placed|וַיָּ֤שֶׂם\rb* \rb his hand|יָד֔וֹ\rb* \rb under|תַּ֛חַת\rb* \rb the thigh|יֶ֥רֶךְ\rb* \rb of his master|אֲדֹנָ֑יו\rb* \rb Abraham|אַבְרָהָ֖ם\rb* \rb and swore an oath|וַיִּשָּׁ֣בַֽע\rb* \rb to him|ל֔וֹ\rb* \rb concerning|עַל־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb matter|הַדָּבָ֖ר\rb*.
\p \v 10 \rb Then the servant|הָ֠עֶבֶד\rb* \rb took|וַיִּקַּ֣ח\rb* \rb ten|עֲשָׂרָ֨ה\rb* \rb of his master’s|אֲדֹנָיו֙\rb* \rb camels|גְמַלִּ֜ים\rb*\rb |מִגְּמַלֵּ֤י\rb* \rb and departed|וַיֵּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb with all manner|וְכָל־\rb* \rb of good things|ט֥וּב\rb* \rb from his master|אֲדֹנָ֖יו\rb* \rb in hand|בְּיָד֑וֹ\rb*. \rb And he set out|וַיָּ֗קָם\rb*\rb |וַיֵּ֛לֶךְ\rb* \rb for|אֶל־\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb Nahor’s|נָחֽוֹר׃\rb* \rb hometown|עִ֥יר\rb*\rb |אֲרַ֥ם\rb* \rb in Aram-naharaim|נַֽהֲרַ֖יִם\rb*.\f + \fr 24:10 \ft That is, Mesopotamia; \fqa Aram-naharaim \ft means \fqa Aram of the two rivers\ft , likely the region between the Euphrates and Balih Rivers in northwestern Mesopotamia.\f* \v 11 \rb As evening approached|עֶ֔רֶב\rb*\rb |לְעֵ֣ת\rb*, \rb he made the camels|הַגְּמַלִּ֛ים\rb* \rb kneel down|וַיַּבְרֵ֧ךְ\rb* \rb near|אֶל־\rb* \rb the well|בְּאֵ֣ר\rb*\rb |הַמָּ֑יִם\rb* \rb outside|מִח֥וּץ\rb* \rb the town|לָעִ֖יר\rb* \rb at the time|לְעֵ֖ת\rb* \rb when the women went out|צֵ֥את\rb* \rb to draw water|הַשֹּׁאֲבֹֽת׃\rb*.
\p \v 12 “\rb O LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb*, \rb God|אֱלֹהֵי֙\rb* \rb of my master|אֲדֹנִ֣י\rb* \rb Abraham|אַבְרָהָ֔ם\rb*,” \rb he prayed|וַיֹּאמַ֓ר׀\rb*, “\rb please|נָ֥א\rb* \rb grant me success today|הַקְרֵה־\rb*\rb |לְפָנַ֖י\rb*\rb |הַיּ֑וֹם\rb*, \rb and show|וַעֲשֵׂה־\rb* \rb kindness|חֶ֕סֶד\rb* \rb to|עִ֖ם\rb* \rb my master|אֲדֹנִ֥י\rb* \rb Abraham|אַבְרָהָֽם׃\rb*. \v 13 \rb Here|הִנֵּ֛ה\rb* \rb I am|אָנֹכִ֥י\rb*, \rb standing|נִצָּ֖ב\rb* \rb beside|עַל־\rb* \rb the spring|עֵ֣ין\rb*\rb |הַמָּ֑יִם\rb*, \rb and the daughters|וּבְנוֹת֙\rb* \rb of the townspeople|אַנְשֵׁ֣י\rb*\rb |הָעִ֔יר\rb* \rb are coming out|יֹצְאֹ֖ת\rb* \rb to draw|לִשְׁאֹ֥ב\rb* \rb water|מָֽיִם׃\rb*. \v 14 \rb Now may it happen|וְהָיָ֣ה\rb* \rb that the girl|הַֽנַּעֲרָ֗\rb* \rb to|אֵלֶ֙יהָ֙\rb* \rb whom|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb I say|אֹמַ֤ר\rb*, ‘\rb Please|נָ֤א\rb* \rb let down|הַטִּי־\rb* \rb your jar|כַדֵּךְ֙\rb* \rb that I may drink|וְאֶשְׁתֶּ֔ה\rb*,’ \rb and who responds|וְאָמְרָ֣ה\rb*, ‘\rb Drink|שְׁתֵ֔ה\rb*, \rb and I will water|אַשְׁקֶ֑ה\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֤הּ\rb* \rb your camels|גְּמַלֶּ֖יךָ\rb* \rb as well|וְגַם־\rb*’— \rb let her be the one You have appointed|הֹכַ֙חְתָּ֙\rb* \rb for Your servant|לְעַבְדְּךָ֣\rb* \rb Isaac|לְיִצְחָ֔ק\rb*. \rb By this|וּבָ֣הּ\rb* \rb I will know|אֵדַ֔ע\rb* \rb that|כִּי־\rb* \rb You have shown|עָשִׂ֥יתָ\rb* \rb kindness|חֶ֖סֶד\rb* \rb to|עִם־\rb* \rb my master|אֲדֹנִֽי׃\rb*.”
\s1 Rebekah Is Chosen
\p \v 15 \rb |וַֽיְהִי־\rb* \rb Before|טֶרֶם֮\rb* \rb the servant|ה֗וּא\rb* \rb had finished|כִּלָּ֣ה\rb* \rb praying|לְדַבֵּר֒\rb*,\rb |וְהִנֵּ֧ה\rb* \rb Rebekah|רִבְקָ֣ה\rb* \rb came out|יֹצֵ֗את\rb* \rb with her jar|וְכַדָּ֖הּ\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb her shoulder|שִׁכְמָֽהּ׃\rb*. \rb She|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb was|יֻלְּדָה֙\rb* \rb the daughter of Bethuel|לִבְתוּאֵ֣ל\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Milcah|מִלְכָּ֔ה\rb*, \rb the wife|אֵ֥שֶׁת\rb* \rb of Abraham’s|אַבְרָהָ֑ם\rb* \rb brother|אֲחִ֣י\rb* \rb Nahor|נָח֖וֹר\rb*. \v 16 \rb Now the girl|וְהַֽנַּעֲרָ֗\rb* \rb was very|מְאֹ֔ד\rb* \rb beautiful|טֹבַ֤ת\rb*\rb |מַרְאֶה֙\rb*, \rb a virgin|בְּתוּלָ֕ה\rb*\rb |לֹ֣א\rb* \rb who had not had relations|יְדָעָ֑הּ\rb* \rb with any man|וְאִ֖ישׁ\rb*. \rb She went down|וַתֵּ֣רֶד\rb* \rb to the spring|הָעַ֔יְנָה\rb*, \rb filled|וַתְּמַלֵּ֥א\rb* \rb her jar|כַדָּ֖הּ\rb*, \rb and came up again|וַתָּֽעַל׃\rb*.
\p \v 17 \rb So the servant|הָעֶ֖בֶד\rb* \rb ran|וַיָּ֥רָץ\rb* \rb to meet her|לִקְרָאתָ֑הּ\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Please|נָ֛א\rb* \rb let me have|הַגְמִיאִ֥ינִי\rb* \rb a little|מְעַט־\rb* \rb water|מַ֖יִם\rb* \rb from your jar|מִכַּדֵּֽךְ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 18 “\rb Drink|שְׁתֵ֣ה\rb*, \rb my lord|אֲדֹנִ֑י\rb*,” \rb she replied|וַתֹּ֖אמֶר\rb*, \rb and she quickly|וַתְּמַהֵ֗ר\rb* \rb lowered|וַתֹּ֧רֶד\rb* \rb her jar|כַּדָּ֛הּ\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb her hands|יָדָ֖הּ\rb* \rb and gave him a drink|וַתַּשְׁקֵֽהוּ׃\rb*.
\p \v 19 \rb After she|וַתְּכַ֖ל\rb* \rb had given him a drink|לְהַשְׁקֹת֑וֹ\rb*, \rb she said|וַתֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*, “\rb I will also|גַּ֤ם\rb* \rb draw water|אֶשְׁאָ֔ב\rb* \rb for your camels|לִגְמַלֶּ֙יךָ֙\rb*, \rb until|עַ֥ד\rb*\rb |אִם־\rb* \rb they have had enough|כִּלּ֖וּ\rb* \rb to drink|לִשְׁתֹּֽת׃\rb*.” \v 20 \rb And she quickly|וַתְּמַהֵ֗ר\rb* \rb emptied|וַתְּעַ֤ר\rb* \rb her jar|כַּדָּהּ֙\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb the trough|הַשֹּׁ֔קֶת\rb* \rb and ran|וַתָּ֥רָץ\rb* \rb back|ע֛וֹד\rb* \rb to|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb the well|הַבְּאֵ֖ר\rb* \rb to draw water|לִשְׁאֹ֑ב\rb*, \rb until she had drawn water|וַתִּשְׁאַ֖ב\rb* \rb for all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb his camels|גְּמַלָּֽיו׃\rb*.
\p \v 21 \rb Meanwhile, the man|וְהָאִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb watched|מִשְׁתָּאֵ֖ה\rb* \rb her|לָ֑הּ\rb* \rb silently|מַחֲרִ֕ישׁ\rb* \rb to see|לָדַ֗עַת\rb* \rb whether|אִם־\rb* \rb or not|לֹֽא׃\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb had made his journey|דַּרְכּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb a success|הַֽהִצְלִ֧יחַ\rb*.
\p \v 22 \rb And|וַיְהִ֗י\rb* \rb after|כַּאֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the camels|הַגְּמַלִּים֙\rb* \rb had finished|כִּלּ֤וּ\rb* \rb drinking|לִשְׁתּ֔וֹת\rb*, \rb he|הָאִישׁ֙\rb* \rb took out|וַיִּקַּ֤ח\rb* \rb a gold|זָהָ֔ב\rb* \rb ring|נֶ֣זֶם\rb* \rb weighing|מִשְׁקָל֑וֹ\rb* \rb a beka|בֶּ֖קַע\rb*,\f + \fr 24:22 \fqa A beka \ft is half a shekel, or approximately 0.2 ounces or 5.7 grams.\f* \rb and two|וּשְׁנֵ֤י\rb* \rb gold|זָהָ֖ב\rb* \rb bracelets|צְמִידִים֙\rb* \rb for|עַל־\rb* \rb her wrists|יָדֶ֔יהָ\rb* \rb weighing|מִשְׁקָלָֽם׃\rb* \rb ten shekels|עֲשָׂרָ֥ה\rb*.\f + \fr 24:22 \fqa 10 shekels \ft is approximately 4 ounces or 114 grams.\f* \v 23 “\rb Whose|מִ֣י\rb* \rb daughter|בַּת־\rb* \rb are you|אַ֔תְּ\rb*?” \rb he asked|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb*. “\rb Please|נָ֖א\rb* \rb tell|הַגִּ֥ידִי\rb* \rb me|לִ֑י\rb*, \rb is there|הֲיֵ֧שׁ\rb* \rb room|מָק֥וֹם\rb* \rb in your father’s|אָבִ֛יךְ\rb* \rb house|בֵּית־\rb* \rb for us|לָ֖נוּ\rb* \rb to spend the night|לָלִֽין׃\rb*?”
\p \v 24 \rb She replied|וַתֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*,\rb |אֵלָ֔יו\rb* “\rb I|אָנֹ֑כִי\rb* \rb am the daughter|בַּת־\rb* \rb of Bethuel|בְּתוּאֵ֖ל\rb*, \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb Milcah|מִלְכָּ֕ה\rb* \rb bore|יָלְדָ֖ה\rb* \rb to Nahor|לְנָחֽוֹר׃\rb*.” \v 25 \rb Then she added|וַתֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֵלָ֔יו\rb*, “\rb We have|עִמָּ֑נוּ\rb*\rb |גַּם־\rb* \rb plenty|רַ֣ב\rb* \rb of straw|תֶּ֥בֶן\rb* \rb and|גַּם־\rb* \rb feed|מִסְפּ֖וֹא\rb*, \rb as well as|גַּם־\rb* \rb a place for you|מָק֖וֹם\rb* \rb to spend the night|לָלֽוּן׃\rb*.”
\p \v 26 \rb Then the man|הָאִ֔ישׁ\rb* \rb bowed down|וַיִּקֹּ֣ד\rb* \rb and worshiped|וַיִּשְׁתַּ֖חוּ\rb* \rb the LORD|לַֽיהוָֽה׃\rb*, \v 27 \rb saying|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Blessed|בָּר֤וּךְ\rb* \rb be the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵי֙\rb* \rb of my master|אֲדֹנִ֣י\rb* \rb Abraham|אַבְרָהָ֔ם\rb*, \rb who|אֲ֠שֶׁר\rb* \rb has not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb withheld|עָזַ֥ב\rb* \rb His kindness|חַסְדּ֛וֹ\rb* \rb and faithfulness|וַאֲמִתּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb from|מֵעִ֣ם\rb* \rb my master|אֲדֹנִ֑י\rb*. \rb As for me|אָנֹכִ֗י\rb*, \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb has led me|נָחַ֣נִי\rb* \rb on the journey|בַּדֶּ֙רֶךְ֙\rb* \rb to the house|בֵּ֖ית\rb* \rb of my master’s|אֲדֹנִֽי׃\rb* \rb relatives|אֲחֵ֥י\rb*.”
\p \v 28 \rb The girl|הַֽנַּעֲרָ֔\rb* \rb ran|וַתָּ֙רָץ֙\rb* \rb and told|וַתַּגֵּ֖ד\rb* \rb her mother’s|אִמָּ֑הּ\rb* \rb household|לְבֵ֣ית\rb* \rb about these|הָאֵֽלֶּה׃\rb* \rb things|כַּדְּבָרִ֖ים\rb*. \v 29 \rb Now Rebekah|וּלְרִבְקָ֥ה\rb* \rb had a brother|אָ֖ח\rb* \rb named|וּשְׁמ֣וֹ\rb* \rb Laban|לָבָ֑ן\rb*, \rb and he|לָבָ֧ן\rb* \rb rushed|וַיָּ֨רָץ\rb* \rb out|הַח֖וּצָה\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the man|הָאִ֛ישׁ\rb* \rb at|אֶל־\rb* \rb the spring|הָעָֽיִן׃\rb*. \v 30 \rb |וַיְהִ֣י׀\rb* \rb As soon as he saw|כִּרְאֹ֣ת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the ring|הַנֶּ֗זֶם\rb*, \rb and|וְֽאֶת־\rb* \rb the bracelets|הַצְּמִדִים֮\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb his sister’s|אֲחֹתוֹ֒\rb* \rb wrists|יְדֵ֣י\rb*, \rb and heard|וּכְשָׁמְע֗וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |אֲחֹתוֹ֙\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb Rebekah’s|רִבְקָ֤ה\rb* \rb words|דִּבְרֵ֞י\rb*, “\rb The man|הָאִ֑ישׁ\rb* \rb said|דִבֶּ֥ר\rb* \rb this|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֖י\rb*,” \rb he went and found|וַיָּבֹא֙\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the man|הָאִ֔ישׁ\rb* \rb standing|עֹמֵ֥ד\rb*\rb |וְהִנֵּ֛ה\rb* \rb by|עַל־\rb* \rb the camels|הַגְּמַלִּ֖ים\rb* \rb near|עַל־\rb* \rb the spring|הָעָֽיִן׃\rb*.
\p \v 31 “\rb Come|בּ֖וֹא\rb*, \rb you who are blessed|בְּר֣וּךְ\rb* \rb by the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*,” \rb said Laban|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*. “\rb Why|לָ֤מָּה\rb* \rb are you standing|תַעֲמֹד֙\rb* \rb out here|בַּח֔וּץ\rb*? \rb I|וְאָנֹכִי֙\rb* \rb have prepared|פִּנִּ֣יתִי\rb* \rb the house|הַבַּ֔יִת\rb* \rb and a place|וּמָק֖וֹם\rb* \rb for the camels|לַגְּמַלִּֽים׃\rb*.” \v 32 \rb So the man|הָאִישׁ֙\rb* \rb came|וַיָּבֹ֤א\rb* \rb to the house|הַבַּ֔יְתָה\rb*, \rb and the camels|הַגְּמַלִּ֑ים\rb* \rb were unloaded|וַיְפַתַּ֖ח\rb*. \rb Straw|תֶּ֤בֶן\rb* \rb and feed|וּמִסְפּוֹא֙\rb* \rb were brought|וַיִּתֵּ֨ן\rb* \rb to the camels|לַגְּמַלִּ֔ים\rb*, \rb and water|וּמַ֙יִם֙\rb* \rb to wash|לִרְחֹ֣ץ\rb* \rb his feet|רַגְלָ֔יו\rb* \rb and the feet|וְרַגְלֵ֥י\rb* \rb of his companions|הָאֲנָשִׁ֖ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb*\rb |אִתּֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\p \v 33 \rb Then a meal was set|וַיִּישֶׂם\rb* \rb before the man|לְפָנָיו֙\rb*, \rb but he said|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb*, “\rb I will not|לֹ֣א\rb*\rb |אֹכַ֔ל\rb* \rb eat|לֶאֱכֹ֔ל\rb* \rb until|עַ֥ד\rb*\rb |אִם־\rb* \rb I have told you|דִּבַּ֖רְתִּי\rb* \rb what I came to say|דְּבָרָ֑י\rb*.”
\p \rb So Laban said|וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Please speak|דַּבֵּֽר׃\rb*.”
\p \v 34 “\rb I|אָנֹֽכִי׃\rb* \rb am Abraham’s|אַבְרָהָ֖ם\rb* \rb servant|עֶ֥בֶד\rb*,” \rb he replied|וַיֹּאמַ֑ר\rb*. \v 35 “\rb The LORD|וַיהוָ֞ה\rb* \rb has greatly|מְאֹ֖ד\rb* \rb blessed|בֵּרַ֧ךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb my master|אֲדֹנִ֛י\rb*, \rb and he has become rich|וַיִּגְדָּ֑ל\rb*. \rb He has given|וַיִּתֶּן־\rb* \rb him|ל֞וֹ\rb* \rb sheep|צֹ֤אן\rb* \rb and cattle|וּבָקָר֙\rb*, \rb silver|וְכֶ֣סֶף\rb* \rb and gold|וְזָהָ֔ב\rb*, \rb menservants|וַעֲבָדִם֙\rb* \rb and maidservants|וּשְׁפָחֹ֔ת\rb*, \rb camels|וּגְמַלִּ֖ים\rb* \rb and donkeys|וַחֲמֹרִֽים׃\rb*. \v 36 \rb My master’s|אֲדֹנִ֥י\rb* \rb wife|אֵ֨שֶׁת\rb* \rb Sarah|שָׂרָה֩\rb* \rb has borne|וַתֵּ֡לֶד\rb* \rb him|לַֽאדֹנִ֔י\rb* \rb a son|בֵן֙\rb* \rb in|אַחֲרֵ֖י\rb* \rb her old age|זִקְנָתָ֑הּ\rb*, \rb and my master has given|וַיִּתֶּן־\rb* \rb him|לּ֖וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb everything he owns|כָּל־\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb*.
\p \v 37 \rb My master|אֲדֹנִ֖י\rb* \rb made me swear an oath|וַיַּשְׁבִּעֵ֥נִי\rb* \rb and said|לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*, ‘\rb You shall not|לֹא־\rb* \rb take|תִקַּ֤ח\rb* \rb a wife|אִשָּׁה֙\rb* \rb for my son|לִבְנִ֔י\rb* \rb from the daughters|מִבְּנוֹת֙\rb* \rb of the Canaanites|הַֽכְּנַעֲנִ֔י\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb in whose land|בְּאַרְצֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb I|אָנֹכִ֖י\rb* \rb dwell|יֹשֵׁ֥ב\rb*, \v 38 \rb but|אִם־\rb*\rb |לֹ֧א\rb* \rb you shall go|תֵּלֵ֖ךְ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb my father’s|אָבִ֛י\rb* \rb house|בֵּית־\rb* \rb and to|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb my kindred|מִשְׁפַּחְתִּ֑י\rb* \rb to take|וְלָקַחְתָּ֥\rb* \rb a wife|אִשָּׁ֖ה\rb* \rb for my son|לִבְנִֽי׃\rb*.’
\p \v 39 \rb Then I asked|וָאֹמַ֖ר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb my master|אֲדֹנִ֑י\rb*, ‘\rb What if|אֻלַ֛י\rb* \rb the woman|הָאִשָּׁ֖ה\rb* \rb will not|לֹא־\rb* \rb come|תֵלֵ֥ךְ\rb* \rb back with me|אַחֲרָֽי׃\rb*?’
\p \v 40 \rb And he told|וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb* \rb me|אֵלָ֑י\rb*, ‘\rb The LORD|יְהוָ֞ה\rb*, \rb before|לְפָנָ֗יו\rb* \rb whom|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I have walked|הִתְהַלַּ֣כְתִּי\rb*, \rb will send|יִשְׁלַ֨ח\rb* \rb His angel|מַלְאָכ֤וֹ\rb* \rb with you|אִתָּךְ֙\rb* \rb and make your journey|דַּרְכֶּ֔ךָ\rb* \rb a success|וְהִצְלִ֣יחַ\rb*, \rb so that you may take|וְלָקַחְתָּ֤\rb* \rb a wife|אִשָּׁה֙\rb* \rb for my son|לִבְנִ֔י\rb* \rb from my kindred|מִמִּשְׁפַּחְתִּ֖י\rb* \rb and from my father’s|אָבִֽי׃\rb* \rb house|וּמִבֵּ֥ית\rb*. \v 41 \rb And when|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb you go|תָב֖וֹא\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb my kindred|מִשְׁפַּחְתִּ֑י\rb*,\rb |תִּנָּקֶה֙\rb*\rb |מֵאָ֣לָתִ֔י\rb* \rb if|וְאִם־\rb* \rb they refuse to|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb give her|יִתְּנוּ֙\rb* \rb to you|לָ֔ךְ\rb*, \rb then|אָ֤ז\rb* \rb you will be|וְהָיִ֥יתָ\rb* \rb released|נָקִ֖י\rb* \rb from my oath|מֵאָלָתִֽי׃\rb*.’
\p \v 42 \rb So when I came|וָאָבֹ֥א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the spring|הָעָ֑יִן\rb* \rb today|הַיּ֖וֹם\rb*, \rb I prayed|וָאֹמַ֗ר\rb*: \rb O LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*, \rb God|אֱלֹהֵי֙\rb* \rb of my master|אֲדֹנִ֣י\rb* \rb Abraham|אַבְרָהָ֔ם\rb*, \rb if only|אִם־\rb* \rb You would|יֶשְׁךָ־\rb*\rb |נָּא֙\rb* \rb make my journey|דַּרְכִּ֔י\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb*\rb |אָנֹכִ֖י\rb*\rb |הֹלֵ֥ךְ\rb*\rb |עָלֶֽיהָ׃\rb* \rb a success|מַצְלִ֣יחַ\rb*! \v 43 \rb Here|הִנֵּ֛ה\rb* \rb I am|אָנֹכִ֥י\rb*, \rb standing|נִצָּ֖ב\rb* \rb beside|עַל־\rb* \rb this spring|עֵ֣ין\rb*\rb |הַמָּ֑יִם\rb*. \rb Now if|וְהָיָ֤ה\rb* \rb a maiden|הָֽעַלְמָה֙\rb* \rb comes out|הַיֹּצֵ֣את\rb* \rb to draw water|לִשְׁאֹ֔ב\rb* \rb and I say|וְאָמַרְתִּ֣י\rb* \rb to her|אֵלֶ֔יהָ\rb*, ‘\rb Please|נָ֥א\rb* \rb let me drink|הַשְׁקִֽינִי־\rb* \rb a little|מְעַט־\rb* \rb water|מַ֖יִם\rb* \rb from your jar|מִכַּדֵּֽךְ׃\rb*,’ \v 44 \rb and she replies|וְאָמְרָ֤ה\rb*\rb |אֵלַי֙\rb*, ‘\rb Drink|שְׁתֵ֔ה\rb*,\rb |וְגַ֥ם\rb* \rb and I will draw water|אֶשְׁאָ֑ב\rb* \rb for your camels|לִגְמַלֶּ֖יךָ\rb* \rb as well|גַּם־\rb*,’\rb |אַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb may she|הִ֣וא\rb* \rb be the woman|הָֽאִשָּׁ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb has appointed|הֹכִ֥יחַ\rb* \rb for my master’s|אֲדֹנִֽי׃\rb* \rb son|לְבֶן־\rb*.
\p \v 45 \rb And before|טֶ֨רֶם\rb* \rb I|אֲנִי֩\rb* \rb had finished|אֲכַלֶּ֜ה\rb* \rb praying|לְדַבֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb in|אֶל־\rb* \rb my heart|לִבִּ֗י\rb*, \rb there|וְהִנֵּ֨ה\rb* \rb was Rebekah|רִבְקָ֤ה\rb* \rb coming out|יֹצֵאת֙\rb* \rb with her jar|וְכַדָּ֣הּ\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb her shoulder|שִׁכְמָ֔הּ\rb*, \rb and she went down|וַתֵּ֥רֶד\rb* \rb to the spring|הָעַ֖יְנָה\rb* \rb and drew water|וַתִּשְׁאָ֑ב\rb*. \rb So I said|וָאֹמַ֥ר\rb* \rb to her|אֵלֶ֖יהָ\rb*, ‘\rb Please|נָֽא׃\rb* \rb give me a drink|הַשְׁקִ֥ינִי\rb*.’
\p \v 46 \rb She quickly|וַתְּמַהֵ֗ר\rb* \rb lowered|וַתּ֤וֹרֶד\rb* \rb her jar|כַּדָּהּ֙\rb* \rb from her shoulder|מֵֽעָלֶ֔יהָ\rb* \rb and said|וַתֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, ‘\rb Drink|שְׁתֵ֔ה\rb*, \rb and I will water|אַשְׁקֶ֑ה\rb* \rb your camels|גְּמַלֶּ֖יךָ\rb* \rb as well|וְגַם־\rb*.’ \rb So I drank|וָאֵ֕שְׁתְּ\rb*, \rb and she also|וְגַ֥ם\rb* \rb watered|הִשְׁקָֽתָה׃\rb* \rb the camels|הַגְּמַלִּ֖ים\rb*.
\p \v 47 \rb Then I asked her|וָאֶשְׁאַ֣ל\rb*,\rb |אֹתָ֗הּ\rb* ‘\rb Whose|מִ֣י\rb* \rb daughter|בַּת־\rb* \rb are you|אַתְּ֒\rb*?’
\p \rb |וַתֹּ֗אמֶר\rb* \rb She replied|וָאֹמַר֮\rb*, ‘\rb The daughter|בַּת־\rb* \rb of Bethuel|בְּתוּאֵל֙\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Nahor|נָח֔וֹר\rb*, \rb whom|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb Milcah|מִלְכָּ֑ה\rb* \rb bore|יָֽלְדָה־\rb* \rb to him|לּ֖וֹ\rb*.’ \rb So I put|וָאָשִׂ֤ם\rb* \rb the ring|הַנֶּ֙זֶם֙\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb her nose|אַפָּ֔הּ\rb* \rb and the bracelets|וְהַצְּמִידִ֖ים\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb her wrists|יָדֶֽיהָ׃\rb*. \v 48 \rb Then I bowed down|וָאֶקֹּ֥ד\rb* \rb and worshiped|וָֽאֶשְׁתַּחֲוֶ֖ה\rb* \rb the LORD|לַיהוָ֑ה\rb*; \rb and I blessed|וָאֲבָרֵ֗ךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵי֙\rb* \rb of my master|אֲדֹנִ֣י\rb* \rb Abraham|אַבְרָהָ֔ם\rb*, \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb led me|הִנְחַ֙נִי֙\rb* \rb on the right|אֱמֶ֔ת\rb* \rb road|בְּדֶ֣רֶךְ\rb* \rb to take|לָקַ֛חַת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the granddaughter|בַּת־\rb* \rb of my master’s|אֲדֹנִ֖י\rb* \rb brother|אֲחִ֥י\rb* \rb for his son|לִבְנֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\p \v 49 \rb Now|וְ֠עַתָּה\rb* \rb if|אִם־\rb* \rb you will|יֶשְׁכֶ֨ם\rb* \rb show|עֹשִׂ֜ים\rb* \rb kindness|חֶ֧סֶד\rb* \rb and faithfulness|וֶֽאֱמֶ֛ת\rb* \rb to|אֶת־\rb* \rb my master|אֲדֹנִ֖י\rb*, \rb tell|הַגִּ֣ידוּ\rb* \rb me|לִ֑י\rb*; \rb but if|וְאִם־\rb* \rb not|לֹ֕א\rb*, \rb let me know|הַגִּ֣ידוּ\rb*\rb |לִ֔י\rb*, \rb so that I may go|וְאֶפְנֶ֥ה\rb* \rb elsewhere|עַל־\rb*\rb |יָמִ֖ין\rb*\rb |א֥וֹ\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb*\rb |שְׂמֹֽאל׃\rb*.”
\p \v 50 \rb Laban|לָבָ֤ן\rb* \rb and Bethuel|וּבְתוּאֵל֙\rb*\rb |וַיֹּ֣אמְר֔וּ\rb* \rb answered|וַיַּ֨עַן\rb*, “\rb This is from|יָצָ֣א\rb* \rb the LORD|מֵיְהוָ֖ה\rb*; \rb we have no choice|לֹ֥א\rb*\rb |נוּכַ֛ל\rb*\rb |דַּבֵּ֥ר\rb*\rb |אֵלֶ֖יךָ\rb*\rb |רַ֥ע\rb*\rb |אוֹ־\rb*\rb |טֽוֹב׃\rb* \rb in the matter|הַדָּבָ֑ר\rb*. \v 51 \rb Rebekah|רִבְקָ֥ה\rb* \rb is here|הִנֵּֽה־\rb* \rb before you|לְפָנֶ֖יךָ\rb*. \rb Take her|קַ֣ח\rb* \rb and go|וָלֵ֑ךְ\rb*, \rb and let her become|וּתְהִ֤י\rb* \rb the wife|אִשָּׁה֙\rb* \rb of your master’s|אֲדֹנֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb son|לְבֶן־\rb*, \rb just as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb has decreed|דִּבֶּ֥ר\rb*.”
\p \v 52 \rb |וַיְהִ֕י\rb* \rb When|כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb Abraham’s|אַבְרָהָ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb servant|עֶ֥בֶד\rb* \rb heard|שָׁמַ֛ע\rb* \rb their words|דִּבְרֵיהֶ֑ם\rb*, \rb he bowed down|וַיִּשְׁתַּ֥חוּ\rb* \rb to the ground|אַ֖רְצָה\rb* \rb before the LORD|לַֽיהוָֽה׃\rb*. \v 53 \rb Then he|הָעֶ֜בֶד\rb* \rb brought out|וַיּוֹצֵ֨א\rb* \rb jewels|כְּלֵי־\rb* \rb of silver|כֶ֨סֶף\rb*\rb |וּכְלֵ֤י\rb* \rb and gold|זָהָב֙\rb*, \rb and articles of clothing|וּבְגָדִ֔ים\rb*, \rb and he gave them|וַיִּתֵּ֖ן\rb* \rb to Rebekah|לְרִבְקָ֑ה\rb*. \rb He also gave|נָתַ֥ן\rb* \rb precious gifts|וּמִ֨גְדָּנֹ֔ת\rb* \rb to her brother|לְאָחִ֖יהָ\rb* \rb and her mother|וּלְאִמָּֽהּ׃\rb*. \v 54 \rb Then he|ה֛וּא\rb* \rb and the men|וְהָאֲנָשִׁ֥ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb with him|עִמּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb ate|וַיֹּאכְל֣וּ\rb* \rb and drank|וַיִּשְׁתּ֗וּ\rb* \rb and spent the night there|וַיָּלִ֑ינוּ\rb*.
\p \rb When they got up|וַיָּק֣וּמוּ\rb* \rb the next morning|בַבֹּ֔קֶר\rb*, \rb he said|וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Send me on my way|שַׁלְּחֻ֥נִי\rb* \rb to my master|לַֽאדֹנִֽי׃\rb*.”
\p \v 55 \rb But her brother|אָחִ֙יהָ֙\rb* \rb and mother|וְאִמָּ֔הּ\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Let the girl|הַנַּעֲרָ֥\rb* \rb remain|תֵּשֵׁ֨ב\rb* \rb with us|אִתָּ֛נוּ\rb* \rb ten|עָשׂ֑וֹר\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֖ים\rb* \rb or so|א֣וֹ\rb*. \rb After that|אַחַ֖ר\rb*, \rb she may go|תֵּלֵֽךְ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 56 \rb But he replied|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֲלֵהֶם֙\rb*, “\rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb delay me|תְּאַחֲר֣וּ\rb*,\rb |אֹתִ֔י\rb* \rb since the LORD|וַֽיהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb has made my journey|דַּרְכִּ֑י\rb* \rb a success|הִצְלִ֣יחַ\rb*. \rb Send me on my way|שַׁלְּח֕וּנִי\rb* \rb so that I may go|וְאֵלְכָ֖ה\rb* \rb to my master|לַֽאדֹנִֽי׃\rb*.”
\p \v 57 \rb So they said|וַיֹּאמְר֖וּ\rb*, “\rb We will call|נִקְרָ֣א\rb* \rb the girl|לַֽנַּעֲרָ֑\rb* \rb and ask|וְנִשְׁאֲלָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb her opinion|פִּֽיהָ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 58 \rb They called|וַיִּקְרְא֤וּ\rb* \rb Rebekah|לְרִבְקָה֙\rb* \rb and asked|וַיֹּאמְר֣וּ\rb* \rb her|אֵלֶ֔יהָ\rb*, “\rb Will you go|הֲתֵלְכִ֖י\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb man|הָאִ֣ישׁ\rb*?”
\p “\rb I will go|אֵלֵֽךְ׃\rb*,” \rb she replied|וַתֹּ֖אמֶר\rb*.
\p \v 59 \rb So they sent|וַֽיְשַׁלְּח֛וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their sister|אֲחֹתָ֖ם\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Rebekah on her way|רִבְקָ֥ה\rb*, \rb along with her nurse|מֵנִקְתָּ֑הּ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and Abraham’s|אַבְרָהָ֖ם\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb servant|עֶ֥בֶד\rb* \rb and his men|אֲנָשָֽׁיו׃\rb*. \v 60 \rb And they blessed|וַיְבָרֲכ֤וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Rebekah|רִבְקָה֙\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֣אמְרוּ\rb* \rb to her|לָ֔הּ\rb*,
\b 
\q1 “\rb Our sister|אֲחֹתֵ֕נוּ\rb*, \rb may you|אַ֥תְּ\rb* \rb become the mother|הֲיִ֖י\rb*
\q2 \rb of thousands|לְאַלְפֵ֣י\rb* \rb upon thousands|רְבָבָ֑ה\rb*.
\q1 \rb May your offspring|זַרְעֵ֔ךְ\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb possess|וְיִירַ֣שׁ\rb*
\q2 \rb the gates|שַׁ֥עַר\rb* \rb of their enemies|שֹׂנְאָֽיו׃\rb*.”
\p \v 61 \rb Then Rebekah|רִבְקָ֜ה\rb* \rb and her servant girls|וְנַעֲרֹתֶ֗יהָ\rb* \rb got ready|וַתָּ֨קָם\rb*, \rb mounted|וַתִּרְכַּ֙בְנָה֙\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb the camels|הַגְּמַלִּ֔ים\rb*, \rb and followed|וַתֵּלַ֖כְנָה\rb*\rb |אַחֲרֵ֣י\rb* \rb the man|הָאִ֑ישׁ\rb*. \rb So the servant|הָעֶ֛בֶד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb took|וַיִּקַּ֥ח\rb* \rb Rebekah|רִבְקָ֖ה\rb* \rb and left|וַיֵּלַֽךְ׃\rb*.
\s1 Isaac Marries Rebekah
\p \v 62 \rb Now Isaac|וְיִצְחָק֙\rb* \rb had just returned|בָּ֣א\rb* \rb from|מִבּ֔וֹא\rb*\rb |בְּאֵ֥ר\rb*\rb |לַחַ֖י\rb* \rb Beer-lahai-roi|רֹאִ֑י\rb*, \rb for he|וְה֥וּא\rb* \rb was living|יוֹשֵׁ֖ב\rb* \rb in the Negev|הַנֶּֽגֶב׃\rb*\rb |בְּאֶ֥רֶץ\rb*. \v 63 \rb Early in the evening|עָ֑רֶב\rb*, \rb Isaac|יִצְחָ֛ק\rb* \rb went out|וַיֵּצֵ֥א\rb* \rb to the field|בַּשָּׂדֶ֖ה\rb* \rb to meditate|לָשׂ֥וּחַ\rb*,\rb |לִפְנ֣וֹת\rb* \rb and looking up|וַיִּשָּׂ֤א\rb*,\rb |עֵינָיו֙\rb* \rb he saw|וַיַּ֔רְא\rb*\rb |וְהִנֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb the camels|גְמַלִּ֖ים\rb* \rb approaching|בָּאִֽים׃\rb*.
\p \v 64 \rb And when Rebekah|רִבְקָה֙\rb* \rb looked up|וַתִּשָּׂ֤א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |עֵינֶ֔יהָ\rb* \rb and saw|וַתֵּ֖רֶא\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Isaac|יִצְחָ֑ק\rb*, \rb she got down|וַתִּפֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb from|מֵעַ֥ל\rb* \rb her camel|הַגָּמָֽל׃\rb* \v 65 \rb and asked|וַתֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the servant|הָעֶ֗בֶד\rb*, “\rb Who|מִֽי־\rb* \rb is that|הַלָּזֶה֙\rb* \rb man|הָאִ֤ישׁ\rb* \rb in the field|בַּשָּׂדֶה֙\rb* \rb coming|הַהֹלֵ֤ךְ\rb* \rb to meet us|לִקְרָאתֵ֔נוּ\rb*?”
\p “\rb It|ה֣וּא\rb* \rb is my master|אֲדֹנִ֑י\rb*,” \rb the servant|הָעֶ֖בֶד\rb* \rb answered|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb*. \rb So she took|וַתִּקַּ֥ח\rb* \rb her veil|הַצָּעִ֖יף\rb* \rb and covered herself|וַתִּתְכָּֽס׃\rb*. \v 66 \rb Then the servant|הָעֶ֖בֶד\rb* \rb told|וַיְסַפֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb Isaac|לְיִצְחָ֑ק\rb*\rb |אֵ֥ת\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb*\rb |הַדְּבָרִ֖ים\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb he had done|עָשָֽׂה׃\rb*.
\p \v 67 \rb And Isaac|יִצְחָ֗ק\rb* \rb brought|וַיְבִאֶ֣הָ\rb* \rb her into the tent|הָאֹ֙הֱלָה֙\rb* \rb of his mother|אִמּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb Sarah|שָׂרָ֣ה\rb* \rb and took|וַיִּקַּ֧ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Rebekah|רִבְקָ֛ה\rb* \rb as|וַתְּהִי־\rb* \rb his|ל֥וֹ\rb* \rb wife|לְאִשָּׁ֖ה\rb*. \rb And Isaac|יִצְחָ֖ק\rb* \rb loved her|וַיֶּאֱהָבֶ֑הָ\rb* \rb and was comforted|וַיִּנָּחֵ֥ם\rb* \rb after|אַחֲרֵ֥י\rb* \rb his mother’s death|אִמּֽוֹ׃פ\rb*.
\c 25
\s1 Abraham and Keturah
\p \v 1 \rb Now Abraham|אַבְרָהָ֛ם\rb* \rb had taken|וַיִּקַּ֥ח\rb* \rb another|וַיֹּ֧סֶף\rb* \rb wife|אִשָּׁ֖ה\rb*, \rb named|וּשְׁמָ֥הּ\rb* \rb Keturah|קְטוּרָֽה׃\rb*, \v 2 \rb and she bore|וַתֵּ֣לֶד\rb* \rb him|אֶת־\rb* \rb Zimran|זִמְרָן֙\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Jokshan|יָקְשָׁ֔ן\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Medan|מְדָ֖ן\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Midian|מִדְיָ֑ן\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Ishbak|יִשְׁבָּ֖ק\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and Shuah|שֽׁוּחַ׃\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb Jokshan|וְיָקְשָׁ֣ן\rb* \rb was the father of|יָלַ֔ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Sheba|שְׁבָ֖א\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and Dedan|דְּדָ֑ן\rb*. \rb And the sons|וּבְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Dedan|דְדָ֔ן\rb* \rb were|הָי֛וּ\rb* \rb the Asshurites|אַשּׁוּרִ֥ם\rb*, \rb the Letushites|וּלְטוּשִׁ֖ים\rb*, \rb and the Leummites|וּלְאֻמִּֽים׃\rb*.
\p \v 4 \rb The sons|וּבְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Midian|מִדְיָ֗ן\rb* \rb were Ephah|עֵיפָ֤ה\rb*, \rb Epher|וָעֵ֙פֶר֙\rb*, \rb Hanoch|וַחֲנֹ֔ךְ\rb*, \rb Abida|וַאֲבִידָ֖ע\rb*, \rb and Eldaah|וְאֶלְדָּעָ֑ה\rb*.
\p \rb All|כָּל־\rb* \rb these|אֵ֖לֶּה\rb* \rb were descendants|בְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Keturah|קְטוּרָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 5 \rb Abraham|אַבְרָהָ֛ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb left|וַיִּתֵּ֧ן\rb* \rb everything|כָּל־\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb he owned|ל֖וֹ\rb* \rb to Isaac|לְיִצְחָֽק׃\rb*. \v 6 \rb But while he was still|בְּעוֹדֶ֣נּוּ\rb* \rb alive|חַ֔י\rb*, \rb Abraham|לְאַבְרָהָ֔ם\rb* \rb gave|נָתַ֥ן\rb* \rb gifts|מַתָּנֹ֑ת\rb* \rb to the sons|וְלִבְנֵ֤י\rb* \rb of his|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb*\rb |אַבְרָהָ֖ם\rb* \rb concubines|הַפִּֽילַגְשִׁים֙\rb* \rb and sent them away|וַֽיְשַׁלְּחֵ֞ם\rb* \rb from|מֵעַ֨ל\rb* \rb his son|בְּנוֹ֙\rb* \rb Isaac|יִצְחָ֤ק\rb*\rb |קֵ֖דְמָה\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of the east|קֶֽדֶם׃\rb*.
\s1 The Death of Abraham
\p \v 7 \rb Abraham|אַבְרָהָ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb*\rb |חָ֑י\rb* \rb lived|חַיֵּ֥י\rb* \rb a total of|וְאֵ֗לֶּה\rb*\rb |יְמֵ֛י\rb*\rb |שְׁנֵֽי־\rb* \rb 175|מְאַ֥ת\rb*\rb |וְשִׁבְעִ֥ים\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֖ה\rb*\rb |וְחָמֵ֥שׁ\rb*\rb |שָׁנִֽים׃\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָ֛ה\rb*. \v 8 \rb And at a ripe|טוֹבָ֖ה\rb* \rb old age|בְּשֵׂיבָ֥ה\rb* \rb he breathed his last|וַיִּגְוַ֨ע\rb* \rb and died|וַיָּ֧מָת\rb*\rb |אַבְרָהָ֛ם\rb*, \rb old|זָקֵ֣ן\rb* \rb and contented|וְשָׂבֵ֑עַ\rb*, \rb and was gathered|וַיֵּאָ֖סֶף\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his people|עַמָּֽיו׃\rb*.
\p \v 9 \rb His sons|בָּנָ֔יו\rb* \rb Isaac|יִצְחָ֤ק\rb* \rb and Ishmael|וְיִשְׁמָעֵאל֙\rb* \rb buried|וַיִּקְבְּר֨וּ\rb* \rb him|אֹת֜וֹ\rb* \rb in|אֶל־\rb* \rb the cave|מְעָרַ֖ת\rb* \rb of Machpelah|הַמַּכְפֵּלָ֑ה\rb* \rb near|עַל־\rb*\rb |פְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb Mamre|מַמְרֵֽא׃\rb*, \rb in|אֶל־\rb* \rb the field|שְׂדֵ֞ה\rb* \rb of Ephron|עֶפְרֹ֤ן\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Zohar|צֹ֙חַר֙\rb* \rb the Hittite|הַֽחִתִּ֔י\rb*.\rb |אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \v 10 \rb This was the field|הַשָּׂדֶ֛ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb Abraham|אַבְרָהָ֖ם\rb*\rb |מֵאֵ֣ת\rb* \rb had bought|קָנָ֥ה\rb* \rb from the Hittites|בְּנֵי־\rb*\rb |חֵ֑ת\rb*. \rb Abraham|אַבְרָהָ֖ם\rb* \rb was buried|קֻבַּ֥ר\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֛מָּה\rb* \rb with his wife|אִשְׁתּֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb Sarah|וְשָׂרָ֥ה\rb*.
\p \v 11 \rb |וַיְהִ֗י\rb* \rb After|אַחֲרֵי֙\rb* \rb Abraham’s|אַבְרָהָ֔ם\rb* \rb death|מ֣וֹת\rb*, \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb blessed|וַיְבָ֥רֶךְ\rb* \rb his son|בְּנ֑וֹ\rb* \rb Isaac|יִצְחָ֣ק\rb*, \rb who|יִצְחָ֔ק\rb* \rb lived|וַיֵּ֣שֶׁב\rb* \rb near|עִם־\rb*\rb |בְּאֵ֥ר\rb*\rb |לַחַ֖י\rb* \rb Beer-lahai-roi|רֹאִֽי׃ס\rb*.
\s1 The Descendants of Ishmael
\p \v 12 \rb This|וְאֵ֛לֶּה\rb* \rb is the account|תֹּלְדֹ֥ת\rb* \rb of Abraham’s|אַבְרָהָ֑ם\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb Ishmael|יִשְׁמָעֵ֖אל\rb*, \rb whom|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb Hagar|הָגָ֧ר\rb* \rb the Egyptian|הַמִּצְרִ֛ית\rb*, \rb Sarah’s|שָׂרָ֖ה\rb* \rb maidservant|שִׁפְחַ֥ת\rb*, \rb bore|יָלְדָ֜ה\rb* \rb to Abraham|לְאַבְרָהָֽם׃\rb*. \v 13 \rb These|וְאֵ֗לֶּה\rb* \rb are the names|שְׁמוֹת֙\rb* \rb of the sons|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Ishmael|יִשְׁמָעֵ֔אל\rb*\rb |בִּשְׁמֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb in the order of their birth|לְתוֹלְדֹתָ֑ם\rb*: \rb Nebaioth|נְבָיֹ֔ת\rb* \rb the firstborn|בְּכֹ֤ר\rb* \rb of Ishmael|יִשְׁמָעֵאל֙\rb*, \rb then Kedar|וְקֵדָ֥ר\rb*, \rb Adbeel|וְאַדְבְּאֵ֖ל\rb*, \rb Mibsam|וּמִבְשָֽׂם׃\rb*, \v 14 \rb Mishma|וּמִשְׁמָ֥ע\rb*, \rb Dumah|וְדוּמָ֖ה\rb*, \rb Massa|וּמַשָּֽׂא׃\rb*, \v 15 \rb Hadad|חֲדַ֣ד\rb*, \rb Tema|וְתֵימָ֔א\rb*, \rb Jetur|יְט֥וּר\rb*, \rb Naphish|נָפִ֖ישׁ\rb*, \rb and Kedemah|וָקֵֽדְמָה׃\rb*.
\p \v 16 \rb These|אֵ֣לֶּה\rb* \rb were|הֵ֞ם\rb* \rb the sons|בְּנֵ֤י\rb* \rb of Ishmael|יִשְׁמָעֵאל֙\rb*, \rb and these|וְאֵ֣לֶּה\rb* \rb were their names|שְׁמֹתָ֔ם\rb* \rb by their villages|בְּחַצְרֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb and encampments|וּבְטִֽירֹתָ֑ם\rb* — \rb twelve|שְׁנֵים־\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֥ר\rb* \rb princes|נְשִׂיאִ֖ם\rb* \rb of their tribes|לְאֻמֹּתָֽם׃\rb*. \v 17 \rb Ishmael|יִשְׁמָעֵ֔אל\rb* \rb lived|חַיֵּ֣י\rb* \rb a total of|וְאֵ֗לֶּה\rb*\rb |שְׁנֵי֙\rb* \rb 137|מְאַ֥ת\rb*\rb |וּשְׁלֹשִׁ֥ים\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֖ה\rb*\rb |וְשֶׁ֣בַע\rb*\rb |שָׁנִ֑ים\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָ֛ה\rb*. \rb Then he breathed his last|וַיִּגְוַ֣ע\rb* \rb and died|וַיָּ֔מָת\rb*, \rb and was gathered|וַיֵּאָ֖סֶף\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his people|עַמָּֽיו׃\rb*.
\p \v 18 \rb Ishmael’s descendants settled|וַיִּשְׁכְּנ֨וּ\rb* \rb from Havilah|מֵֽחֲוִילָ֜ה\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb* \rb Shur|שׁ֗וּר\rb*, \rb which|אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb is near|עַל־\rb* \rb the border|פְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb as you go|בֹּאֲכָ֖ה\rb* \rb toward Asshur|אַשּׁ֑וּרָה\rb*.\f + \fr 25:18 \ft Or \fqa Assyria\f* \rb And they lived|נָפָֽל׃פ\rb* \rb in hostility|עַל־\rb* \rb toward|פְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb all|כָל־\rb* \rb their brothers|אֶחָ֖יו\rb*.
\s1 Jacob and Esau
\p \v 19 \rb This|וְאֵ֛לֶּה\rb* \rb is the account|תּוֹלְדֹ֥ת\rb* \rb of Abraham’s|אַבְרָהָ֑ם\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb Isaac|יִצְחָ֖ק\rb*. \rb Abraham|אַבְרָהָ֖ם\rb* \rb became the father of|הוֹלִ֥יד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Isaac|יִצְחָֽק׃\rb*, \v 20 \rb and Isaac|יִצְחָק֙\rb* \rb was|וַיְהִ֤י\rb* \rb forty|אַרְבָּעִ֣ים\rb* \rb years old|בֶּן־\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֔ה\rb* \rb when he married|בְּקַחְתּ֣וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Rebekah|רִבְקָ֗ה\rb*, \rb the daughter|בַּת־\rb* \rb of Bethuel|בְּתוּאֵל֙\rb* \rb the Aramean|הָֽאֲרַמִּ֔י\rb*\rb |מִפַּדַּ֖ן\rb* \rb from Paddan-aram|אֲרָ֑ם\rb*\f + \fr 25:20 \ft That is, northwest Mesopotamia\f* \rb and the sister|אֲח֛וֹת\rb* \rb of Laban|לָבָ֥ן\rb* \rb the Aramean|הָאֲרַמִּ֖י\rb*.
\p \v 21 \rb Later, Isaac|יִצְחָ֤ק\rb* \rb prayed|וַיֶּעְתַּ֨ר\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָה֙\rb* \rb on behalf of|לְנֹ֣כַח\rb* \rb his wife|אִשְׁתּ֔וֹ\rb*, \rb because|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb she|הִ֑וא\rb* \rb was barren|עֲקָרָ֖ה\rb*. \rb And the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb heard his prayer|וַיֵּעָ֤תֶר\rb*, \rb and his wife|אִשְׁתּֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb Rebekah|רִבְקָ֥ה\rb* \rb conceived|וַתַּ֖הַר\rb*.
\p \v 22 \rb But the children|הַבָּנִים֙\rb* \rb inside her|בְּקִרְבָּ֔הּ\rb* \rb struggled with each other|וַיִּתְרֹֽצֲצ֤וּ\rb*, \rb and she said|וַתֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*,\rb |אִם־\rb*\rb |כֵּ֔ן\rb* “\rb Why|לָ֥מָּה\rb* \rb is this|זֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb happening to me|אָנֹ֑כִי\rb*?” \rb So Rebekah went|וַתֵּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb to inquire|לִדְרֹ֥שׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*, \v 23 \rb and He|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb declared|לָ֗הּ\rb* \rb to her|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb*:
\b 
\q1 “\rb Two|שְׁנֵ֤י\rb* \rb nations|גֹיִים\rb* \rb are in your womb|בְּבִטְנֵ֔ךְ\rb*,
\q2 \rb and two|וּשְׁנֵ֣י\rb* \rb peoples|לְאֻמִּ֔ים\rb* \rb from within you|מִמֵּעַ֖יִךְ\rb* \rb will be separated|יִפָּרֵ֑דוּ\rb*;
\q1 \rb one people|וּלְאֹם֙\rb* \rb will be stronger|יֶֽאֱמָ֔ץ\rb* \rb than the other|מִלְאֹ֣ם\rb*,
\q2 \rb and the older|וְרַ֖ב\rb* \rb will serve|יַעֲבֹ֥ד\rb* \rb the younger|צָעִֽיר׃\rb*.”\f + \fr 25:23 \ft Cited in Romans 9:12\f*
\p \v 24 \rb When her time|יָמֶ֖יהָ\rb* \rb came|וַיִּמְלְא֥וּ\rb* \rb to give birth|לָלֶ֑דֶת\rb*, \rb there were indeed|וְהִנֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb twins|תוֹמִ֖ם\rb* \rb in her womb|בְּבִטְנָֽהּ׃\rb*. \v 25 \rb The first|הָרִאשׁוֹן֙\rb* \rb one came out|וַיֵּצֵ֤א\rb* \rb red|אַדְמוֹנִ֔י\rb*,\rb |כֻּלּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb covered with hair|שֵׂעָ֑ר\rb* \rb like a fur coat|כְּאַדֶּ֣רֶת\rb*; \rb so they named him|וַיִּקְרְא֥וּ\rb*\rb |שְׁמ֖וֹ\rb* \rb Esau|עֵשָֽׂו׃\rb*.\f + \fr 25:25 \fqa Esau \ft sounds like a Hebrew term that means \fqa hairy\ft .\f* \v 26 \rb After|וְאַֽחֲרֵי־\rb* \rb this|כֵ֞ן\rb*, \rb his brother|אָחִ֗יו\rb* \rb came out|יָצָ֣א\rb* \rb grasping|אֹחֶ֙זֶת֙\rb* \rb Esau’s|עֵשָׂ֔ו\rb* \rb heel|בַּעֲקֵ֣ב\rb*\rb |וְיָד֤וֹ\rb*; \rb so he was named|וַיִּקְרָ֥א\rb*\rb |שְׁמ֖וֹ\rb* \rb Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֑ב\rb*.\f + \fr 25:26 \fqa Jacob \ft means \fqa he grasps the heel \ft or \fqa he deceives\ft .\f* \rb And Isaac|וְיִצְחָ֛ק\rb* \rb was sixty|שִׁשִּׁ֥ים\rb* \rb years old|בֶּן־\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֖ה\rb* \rb when the twins were born|בְּלֶ֥דֶת\rb*\rb |אֹתָֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 27 \rb When the boys|הַנְּעָרִ֔ים\rb* \rb grew up|וַֽיִּגְדְּלוּ֙\rb*, \rb Esau|עֵשָׂ֗ו\rb* \rb became|וַיְהִ֣י\rb* \rb a skillful|יֹדֵ֥עַ\rb* \rb hunter|צַ֖יִד\rb*, \rb a man|אִ֛ישׁ\rb* \rb of the field|שָׂדֶ֑ה\rb*, \rb while Jacob|וְיַעֲקֹב֙\rb*\rb |אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb was a quiet|תָּ֔ם\rb* \rb man|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb who stayed|יֹשֵׁ֖ב\rb* \rb at home|אֹהָלִֽים׃\rb*. \v 28 \rb Because|כִּי־\rb* \rb Isaac|יִצְחָ֛ק\rb* \rb had a taste|בְּפִ֑יו\rb* \rb for wild game|צַ֣יִד\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb he loved|וַיֶּאֱהַ֥ב\rb* \rb Esau|עֵשָׂ֖ו\rb*; \rb but Rebekah|וְרִבְקָ֖ה\rb* \rb loved|אֹהֶ֥בֶת\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb Jacob|יַעֲקֹֽב׃\rb*.
\s1 Esau Sells His Birthright
\p \v 29 \rb One day, while Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֖ב\rb* \rb was cooking|וַיָּ֥זֶד\rb* \rb some stew|נָזִ֑יד\rb*, \rb Esau|עֵשָׂ֛ו\rb* \rb came in|וַיָּבֹ֥א\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the field|הַשָּׂדֶ֖ה\rb* \rb and|וְה֥וּא\rb* \rb was famished|עָיֵֽף׃\rb*. \v 30 \rb He|עֵשָׂ֜ו\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֗ב\rb*, “\rb Let me eat|הַלְעִיטֵ֤נִי\rb*\rb |נָא֙\rb* \rb some of|מִן־\rb* \rb that|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb red|הָאָדֹ֤ם\rb* \rb stew|הָאָדֹם֙\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb I am|אָנֹ֑כִי\rb* \rb famished|עָיֵ֖ף\rb*.” (\rb That is why|עַל־\rb*\rb |כֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb he was also called|קָרָֽא־\rb*\rb |שְׁמ֖וֹ\rb* \rb Edom|אֱדֽוֹם׃\rb*.\f + \fr 25:30 \fqa Edom \ft means \fqa red\ft .\f*)
\p \v 31 “\rb First|כַיּ֛וֹם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb sell|מִכְרָ֥ה\rb* \rb me|לִֽי׃\rb* \rb your birthright|בְּכֹֽרָתְךָ֖\rb*,” \rb Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֑ב\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb*.
\p \v 32 “\rb Look|הִנֵּ֛ה\rb*,” \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb Esau|עֵשָׂ֔ו\rb*, “\rb I am|אָנֹכִ֥י\rb* \rb about to die|הוֹלֵ֖ךְ\rb*\rb |לָמ֑וּת\rb*, \rb so what good|וְלָמָּה־\rb*\rb |זֶּ֥ה\rb* \rb is a birthright|בְּכֹרָֽה׃\rb* \rb to me|לִ֖י\rb*?”
\p \v 33 “\rb Swear to me first|הִשָּׁ֤בְעָה\rb*\rb |כַּיּ֔וֹם\rb*,” \rb Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֗ב\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*.
\p \rb So Esau swore|וַיִּשָּׁבַ֖ע\rb* \rb to Jacob|ל֑וֹ\rb* \rb and sold|וַיִּמְכֹּ֥ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb him|לְיַעֲקֹֽב׃\rb* \rb the birthright|בְּכֹרָת֖וֹ\rb*. \v 34 \rb Then Jacob|וְיַעֲקֹ֞ב\rb* \rb gave|נָתַ֣ן\rb* \rb some bread|לֶ֚חֶם\rb* \rb and lentil|עֲדָשִׁ֔ים\rb* \rb stew|וּנְזִ֣יד\rb* \rb to Esau|לְעֵשָׂ֗ו\rb*, \rb who ate|וַיֹּ֣אכַל\rb* \rb and drank|וַיֵּ֔שְׁתְּ\rb* \rb and then got up|וַיָּ֖קָם\rb* \rb and went away|וַיֵּלַ֑ךְ\rb*. \rb Thus Esau|עֵשָׂ֖ו\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb despised|וַיִּ֥בֶז\rb* \rb his birthright|הַבְּכֹרָֽה׃ס\rb*.
\c 26
\s1 God’s Promise to Isaac
\p \v 1 \rb Now there was|וַיְהִ֤י\rb* \rb another famine|רָעָב֙\rb* \rb in the land|בָּאָ֔רֶץ\rb*, \rb subsequent to|מִלְּבַד֙\rb* \rb the one|הָרָעָ֣ב\rb*\rb |הָרִאשׁ֔וֹן\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb had occurred|הָיָ֖ה\rb* \rb in Abraham’s|אַבְרָהָ֑ם\rb* \rb time|בִּימֵ֣י\rb*. \rb And Isaac|יִצְחָ֛ק\rb* \rb went|וַיֵּ֧לֶךְ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Abimelech|אֲבִימֶּ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of the Philistines|פְּלִשְׁתִּ֖ים\rb* \rb at Gerar|גְּרָֽרָה׃\rb*.
\p \v 2 \rb The LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb appeared|וַיֵּרָ֤א\rb* \rb to|אֵלָיו֙\rb* \rb Isaac and said|וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb go down|תֵּרֵ֣ד\rb* \rb to Egypt|מִצְרָ֑יְמָה\rb*. \rb Settle|שְׁכֹ֣ן\rb* \rb in the land|בָּאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb where|אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb I tell you|אֹמַ֥ר\rb*.\rb |אֵלֶֽיךָ׃\rb* \v 3 \rb Stay|גּ֚וּר\rb* \rb in this|הַזֹּ֔את\rb* \rb land as a foreigner|בָּאָ֣רֶץ\rb*, \rb and I will be|וְאֶֽהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb with|עִמְּךָ֖\rb* \rb you and bless you|וַאֲבָרְכֶ֑ךָּ\rb*. \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I will give|אֶתֵּן֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb lands|הָֽאֲרָצֹ֣ת\rb* \rb to you|לְךָ֣\rb* \rb and your offspring|וּֽלְזַרְעֲךָ֗\rb*, \rb and I will confirm|וַהֲקִֽמֹתִי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the oath|הַשְּׁבֻעָ֔ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I swore|נִשְׁבַּ֖עְתִּי\rb* \rb to your father|אָבִֽיךָ׃\rb* \rb Abraham|לְאַבְרָהָ֥ם\rb*. \v 4 \rb I will make your descendants|זַרְעֲךָ֙\rb* \rb as numerous|וְהִרְבֵּיתִ֤י\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb as the stars|כְּכוֹכְבֵ֣י\rb* \rb in the sky|הַשָּׁמַ֔יִם\rb*, \rb and I will give|וְנָתַתִּ֣י\rb* \rb them|לְזַרְעֲךָ֔\rb*\rb |אֵ֥ת\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb lands|הָאֲרָצֹ֖ת\rb*, \rb and through your offspring|בְזַרְעֲךָ֔\rb* \rb all|כֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb nations|גּוֹיֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the earth|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb* \rb will be blessed|וְהִתְבָּרֲכ֣וּ\rb*, \v 5 \rb because|עֵ֕קֶב\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb Abraham|אַבְרָהָ֖ם\rb* \rb listened|שָׁמַ֥ע\rb* \rb to My voice|בְּקֹלִ֑י\rb* \rb and kept|וַיִּשְׁמֹר֙\rb* \rb My charge|מִשְׁמַרְתִּ֔י\rb*, \rb My commandments|מִצְוֺתַ֖י\rb*, \rb My statutes|חֻקּוֹתַ֥י\rb*, \rb and My laws|וְתוֹרֹתָֽי׃\rb*.”
\s1 Isaac Deceives Abimelech
\p \v 6 \rb So Isaac|יִצְחָ֖ק\rb* \rb settled|וַיֵּ֥שֶׁב\rb* \rb in Gerar|בִּגְרָֽר׃\rb*. \v 7 \rb But when the men|אַנְשֵׁ֤י\rb* \rb of that place|הַמָּקוֹם֙\rb* \rb asked|וַֽיִּשְׁאֲל֞וּ\rb* \rb about his wife|לְאִשְׁתּ֔וֹ\rb*, \rb he said|וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb*, “\rb She|הִ֑וא\rb* \rb is my sister|אֲחֹ֣תִי\rb*.” \rb For|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb he was afraid|יָרֵא֙\rb* \rb to say|לֵאמֹ֣ר\rb*, “\rb She is my wife|אִשְׁתִּ֔י\rb*,” \rb since he thought to himself|פֶּן־\rb*, “\rb The men|אַנְשֵׁ֤י\rb* \rb of this place|הַמָּקוֹם֙\rb* \rb will kill me|יַֽהַרְגֻ֜נִי\rb* \rb on account of|עַל־\rb* \rb Rebekah|רִבְקָ֔ה\rb*, \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb she|הִֽיא׃\rb* \rb is so beautiful|טוֹבַ֥ת\rb*\rb |מַרְאֶ֖ה\rb*.”
\p \v 8 \rb |וַיְהִ֗י\rb* \rb When|כִּ֣י\rb*\rb |אָֽרְכוּ־\rb* \rb Isaac|ל֥וֹ\rb* \rb had been there|שָׁם֙\rb* \rb a long time|הַיָּמִ֔ים\rb*, \rb Abimelech|אֲבִימֶ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of the Philistines|פְּלִשְׁתִּ֔ים\rb* \rb looked down|וַיַּשְׁקֵ֗ף\rb* \rb from|בְּעַ֖ד\rb* \rb the window|הַֽחַלּ֑וֹן\rb* \rb and was surprised to see|וַיַּ֗רְא\rb*\rb |וְהִנֵּ֤ה\rb* \rb Isaac|יִצְחָק֙\rb* \rb caressing|מְצַחֵ֔ק\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb his wife|אִשְׁתּֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb Rebekah|רִבְקָ֥ה\rb*. \v 9 \rb Abimelech|אֲבִימֶ֜לֶךְ\rb* \rb sent for|וַיִּקְרָ֨א\rb* \rb Isaac|לְיִצְחָ֗ק\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb*, “\rb So she|הִ֔וא\rb* \rb is really|אַ֣ךְ\rb*\rb |הִנֵּ֤ה\rb* \rb your wife|אִשְׁתְּךָ֙\rb*! \rb How|וְאֵ֥יךְ\rb* \rb could you say|אָמַ֖רְתָּ\rb*, ‘\rb She|הִ֑וא\rb* \rb is my sister|אֲחֹ֣תִי\rb*’?”
\p \rb Isaac|יִצְחָ֔ק\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb*,\rb |אֵלָיו֙\rb* “\rb Because|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb I thought|אָמַ֔רְתִּי\rb* \rb I might|פֶּן־\rb* \rb die|אָמ֖וּת\rb* \rb on account of her|עָלֶֽיהָ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 10 “\rb What|מַה־\rb* \rb is this|זֹּ֖את\rb* \rb you have done|עָשִׂ֣יתָ\rb* \rb to us|לָּ֑נוּ\rb*?” \rb asked|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb Abimelech|אֲבִימֶ֔לֶךְ\rb*. “\rb One|אַחַ֤ד\rb* \rb of the people|הָעָם֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb could easily|כִּ֠מְעַט\rb* \rb have slept with|שָׁכַ֞ב\rb* \rb your wife|אִשְׁתֶּ֔ךָ\rb*, \rb and you would have brought|וְהֵבֵאתָ֥\rb* \rb guilt|אָשָֽׁם׃\rb* \rb upon us|עָלֵ֖ינוּ\rb*.” \v 11 \rb So Abimelech|אֲבִימֶ֔לֶךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb warned|וַיְצַ֣ו\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֖ם\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*, “\rb Whoever harms|הַנֹּגֵ֜עַ\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֛ה\rb* \rb man|בָּאִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb or his wife|וּבְאִשְׁתּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb will surely be put to death|מ֥וֹת\rb*\rb |יוּמָֽת׃\rb*.”
\s1 Isaac’s Prosperity
\p \v 12 \rb Now Isaac|יִצְחָק֙\rb* \rb sowed seed|וַיִּזְרַ֤ע\rb* \rb in the|הַהִ֔וא\rb* \rb land|בָּאָ֣רֶץ\rb*, \rb and that very|הַהִ֖וא\rb* \rb year|בַּשָּׁנָ֥ה\rb* \rb he reaped|וַיִּמְצָ֛א\rb* \rb a hundredfold|מֵאָ֣ה\rb*\rb |שְׁעָרִ֑ים\rb*. \rb And the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb blessed him|וַֽיְבָרֲכֵ֖הוּ\rb*, \v 13 \rb and he|הָאִ֑ישׁ\rb* \rb became richer and richer|וַיִּגְדַּ֖ל\rb*\rb |וַיֵּ֤לֶךְ\rb*\rb |הָלוֹךְ֙\rb*, \rb until|עַ֥ד\rb*\rb |כִּֽי־\rb*\rb |גָדַ֖ל\rb* \rb he was exceedingly|מְאֹֽד׃\rb* \rb wealthy|וְגָדֵ֔ל\rb*. \v 14 \rb He owned so many|וַֽיְהִי־\rb* \rb flocks|מִקְנֵה־\rb*\rb |צֹאן֙\rb* \rb and herds|וּמִקְנֵ֣ה\rb*\rb |בָקָ֔ר\rb* \rb and|רַבָּ֑ה\rb* \rb servants|וַעֲבֻדָּ֖ה\rb* \rb that the Philistines|פְּלִשְׁתִּֽים׃\rb* \rb envied him|וַיְקַנְא֥וּ\rb*.\rb |אֹת֖וֹ\rb* \v 15 \rb So the Philistines|פְּלִשְׁתִּ֔ים\rb* \rb took|וַיְמַלְא֖וּם\rb* \rb dirt|עָפָֽר׃\rb* \rb and stopped up|סִתְּמ֣וּם\rb* \rb all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the wells|הַבְּאֵרֹ֗ת\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb his father’s|אָבִ֔יו\rb* \rb servants|עַבְדֵ֣י\rb* \rb had dug|חָֽפְרוּ֙\rb* \rb in the days|בִּימֵ֖י\rb* \rb of his father|אָבִ֑יו\rb* \rb Abraham|אַבְרָהָ֣ם\rb*.
\p \v 16 \rb Then Abimelech|אֲבִימֶ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Isaac|יִצְחָ֑ק\rb*, “\rb Depart from|לֵ֚ךְ\rb* \rb us|מֵֽעִמָּ֔נוּ\rb*, \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb you are much|מְאֹֽד׃\rb* \rb too powerful|עָצַֽמְתָּ־\rb* \rb for us|מִמֶּ֖נּוּ\rb*.”
\p \v 17 \rb So Isaac|יִצְחָ֑ק\rb* \rb left|וַיֵּ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb that place|מִשָּׁ֖ם\rb* \rb and encamped|וַיִּ֥חַן\rb* \rb in the Valley|בְּנַֽחַל־\rb* \rb of Gerar|גְּרָ֖ר\rb* \rb and settled|וַיֵּ֥שֶׁב\rb* \rb there|שָֽׁם׃\rb*. \v 18 \rb Isaac|יִצְחָ֜ק\rb* \rb reopened|וַיָּ֨שָׁב\rb*\rb |וַיַּחְפֹּ֣ר׀\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the wells|בְּאֵרֹ֣ת\rb*\rb |הַמַּ֗יִם\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb had been dug|חָֽפְרוּ֙\rb* \rb in the days|בִּימֵי֙\rb* \rb of his father|אָבִ֔יו\rb* \rb Abraham|אַבְרָהָ֣ם\rb*, \rb which the Philistines|פְּלִשְׁתִּ֔ים\rb* \rb had stopped up|וַיְסַתְּמ֣וּם\rb* \rb after|אַחֲרֵ֖י\rb* \rb Abraham|אַבְרָהָ֑ם\rb* \rb died|מ֣וֹת\rb*. \rb And he gave|וַיִּקְרָ֤א\rb* \rb these wells|לָהֶן֙\rb* \rb the same names|שֵׁמ֔וֹת\rb*\rb |כַּשֵּׁמֹ֕ת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb his father|אָבִֽיו׃\rb* \rb had given|קָרָ֥א\rb* \rb them|לָהֶ֖ן\rb*.
\p \v 19 \rb Then Isaac’s|יִצְחָ֖ק\rb* \rb servants|עַבְדֵֽי־\rb* \rb dug|וַיַּחְפְּר֥וּ\rb* \rb in the valley|בַּנָּ֑חַל\rb* \rb and found|וַיִּ֨מְצְאוּ־\rb* \rb a well|בְּאֵ֖ר\rb* \rb of fresh|חַיִּֽים׃\rb* \rb water|מַ֥יִם\rb*\f + \fr 26:19 \ft Or \fqa flowing water \ft or \fqa living water\f* \rb there|שָׁ֔ם\rb*. \v 20 \rb But the herdsmen|רֹעֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Gerar|גְרָ֗ר\rb* \rb quarreled|וַיָּרִ֜יבוּ\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb Isaac’s|יִצְחָ֛ק\rb* \rb herdsmen|רֹעֵ֥י\rb* \rb and said|לֵאמֹ֖ר\rb*, “\rb The water is ours|הַמָּ֑יִם\rb*!” \rb So he named|וַיִּקְרָ֤א\rb*\rb |שֵֽׁם־\rb* \rb the well|הַבְּאֵר֙\rb* \rb Esek|עֵ֔שֶׂק\rb*,\f + \fr 26:20 \fqa Esek \ft means \fqa contention\ft .\f* \rb because|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb they contended|הִֽתְעַשְּׂק֖וּ\rb* \rb with him|עִמּֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\p \v 21 \rb Then they dug|וַֽיַּחְפְּרוּ֙\rb* \rb another|אַחֶ֔רֶת\rb* \rb well|בְּאֵ֣ר\rb* \rb and quarreled|וַיָּרִ֖יבוּ\rb* \rb over|עָלֶ֑יהָ\rb* \rb that one also|גַּם־\rb*; \rb so he named|וַיִּקְרָ֥א\rb* \rb it|שְׁמָ֖הּ\rb* \rb Sitnah|שִׂטְנָֽה׃\rb*.\f + \fr 26:21 \fqa Sitnah \ft means \fqa enmity \ft or \fqa hostility\ft .\f*
\p \v 22 \rb He moved on|וַיַּעְתֵּ֣ק\rb* \rb from there|מִשָּׁ֗ם\rb* \rb and dug|וַיַּחְפֹּר֙\rb*\rb |בְּאֵ֣ר\rb* \rb another well|אַחֶ֔רֶת\rb*, \rb and they did not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb quarrel|רָב֖וּ\rb* \rb over it|עָלֶ֑יהָ\rb*. \rb He named|וַיִּקְרָ֤א\rb* \rb it|שְׁמָהּ֙\rb* \rb Rehoboth|רְחֹב֔וֹת\rb*\f + \fr 26:22 \fqa Rehoboth \ft means \fqa broad places \ft or \fqa open spaces\ft .\f* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*, “\rb At last|כִּֽי־\rb*\rb |עַתָּ֞ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb has made room|הִרְחִ֧יב\rb* \rb for us|לָ֖נוּ\rb*, \rb and we will be fruitful|וּפָרִ֥ינוּ\rb* \rb in the land|בָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 23 \rb From there|מִשָּׁ֖ם\rb* \rb Isaac went up|וַיַּ֥עַל\rb* \rb to Beersheba|שָֽׁבַע׃\rb*, \v 24 \rb and that|הַה֔וּא\rb* \rb night|בַּלַּ֣יְלָה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb appeared|וַיֵּרָ֨א\rb* \rb to him|אֵלָ֤יו\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*, “\rb I|אָנֹכִ֕י\rb* \rb am the God|אֱלֹהֵ֖י\rb* \rb of your father|אָבִ֑יךָ\rb* \rb Abraham|אַבְרָהָ֣ם\rb*. \rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb be afraid|תִּירָא֙\rb*, \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I|אָנֹ֔כִי\rb* \rb am with you|אִתְּךָ֣\rb*. \rb I will bless|וּבֵֽרַכְתִּ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb you and multiply|וְהִרְבֵּיתִ֣י\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb your descendants|זַרְעֲךָ֔\rb* \rb for the sake|בַּעֲב֖וּר\rb* \rb of My servant|עַבְדִּֽי׃\rb* \rb Abraham|אַבְרָהָ֥ם\rb*.”
\p \v 25 \rb So Isaac built|וַיִּ֧בֶן\rb* \rb an altar|מִזְבֵּ֗חַ\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֣ם\rb* \rb and called|וַיִּקְרָא֙\rb* \rb on the name|בְּשֵׁ֣ם\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*, \rb and he pitched|וַיֶּט־\rb* \rb his tent|אָהֳל֑וֹ\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֖ם\rb*. \rb His|יִצְחָ֖ק\rb* \rb servants|עַבְדֵי־\rb* \rb also dug|וַיִּכְרוּ־\rb* \rb a well|בְּאֵֽר׃\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֥ם\rb*.
\s1 Isaac’s Covenant with Abimelech
\p \v 26 \rb Later, Abimelech|וַאֲבִימֶ֕לֶךְ\rb* \rb came|הָלַ֥ךְ\rb* \rb to Isaac|אֵלָ֖יו\rb* \rb from Gerar|מִגְּרָ֑ר\rb*, \rb with Ahuzzath|וַאֲחֻזַּת֙\rb* \rb his adviser|מֵֽרֵעֵ֔הוּ\rb* \rb and Phicol|וּפִיכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb the commander|שַׂר־\rb* \rb of his army|צְבָאֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\p \v 27 “\rb Why|מַדּ֖וּעַ\rb* \rb have you come|בָּאתֶ֣ם\rb* \rb to me|אֵלָ֑י\rb*?” \rb Isaac|יִצְחָ֔ק\rb* \rb asked|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb them|אֲלֵהֶם֙\rb*. “\rb You|וְאַתֶּם֙\rb* \rb hated|שְׂנֵאתֶ֣ם\rb* \rb me|אֹתִ֔י\rb* \rb and sent me away|וַתְּשַׁלְּח֖וּנִי\rb*\rb |מֵאִתְּכֶֽם׃\rb*.”
\p \v 28 “\rb We can plainly see|רָא֣וֹ\rb*\rb |רָאִינוּ֮\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה׀\rb* \rb has been|הָיָ֣ה\rb* \rb with you|עִמָּךְ֒\rb*,” \rb they replied|וַיֹּאמְר֗וּ\rb*. “\rb We recommend that|וַנֹּ֗אמֶר\rb* \rb there should now be|תְּהִ֨י\rb*\rb |נָ֥א\rb* \rb an oath|אָלָ֛ה\rb* \rb between|בֵּינוֹתֵ֖ינוּ\rb* \rb us|בֵּינֵ֣ינוּ\rb* \rb and you|וּבֵינֶ֑ךָ\rb*. \rb Let us make|וְנִכְרְתָ֥ה\rb* \rb a covenant|בְרִ֖ית\rb* \rb with you|עִמָּֽךְ׃\rb* \v 29 \rb that you will not|אִם־\rb* \rb harm|רָעָ֗ה\rb* \rb us|עִמָּ֜נוּ\rb*, \rb just as|כַּאֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb we have not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb harmed you|נְגַֽעֲנ֔וּךָ\rb* \rb but|וְכַאֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb have done|עָשִׂ֤ינוּ\rb* \rb only|רַק־\rb* \rb good|ט֔וֹב\rb* \rb to you|עִמְּךָ֙\rb*, \rb sending you on your way|וַנְּשַׁלֵּֽחֲךָ֖\rb* \rb in peace|בְּשָׁל֑וֹם\rb*. \rb And now|עַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb you|אַתָּ֥ה\rb* \rb are blessed|בְּר֥וּךְ\rb* \rb by the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*.”
\p \v 30 \rb So Isaac prepared|וַיַּ֤עַשׂ\rb* \rb a feast|מִשְׁתֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb for them|לָהֶם֙\rb*, \rb and they ate|וַיֹּאכְל֖וּ\rb* \rb and drank|וַיִּשְׁתּֽוּ׃\rb*. \v 31 \rb And they got up early|וַיַּשְׁכִּ֣ימוּ\rb* \rb the next morning|בַבֹּ֔קֶר\rb* \rb and swore an oath|וַיִּשָּׁבְע֖וּ\rb* \rb to each|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb other|לְאָחִ֑יו\rb*. \rb Then Isaac|יִצְחָ֔ק\rb* \rb sent them on their way|וַיְשַׁלְּחֵ֣ם\rb*, \rb and they left him|וַיֵּלְכ֥וּ\rb*\rb |מֵאִתּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb in peace|בְּשָׁלֽוֹם׃\rb*.
\p \v 32 \rb |וַיְהִ֣י׀\rb* \rb On that same|הַה֗וּא\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb*, \rb Isaac’s|יִצְחָ֔ק\rb* \rb servants|עַבְדֵ֣י\rb* \rb came|וַיָּבֹ֙אוּ֙\rb* \rb and told|וַיַּגִּ֣דוּ\rb* \rb him|ל֔וֹ\rb* \rb about|עַל־\rb*\rb |אֹד֥וֹת\rb* \rb the well|הַבְּאֵ֖ר\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb they had dug|חָפָ֑רוּ\rb*. “\rb We have found|מָצָ֥אנוּ\rb* \rb water|מָֽיִם׃\rb*!” \rb they told|וַיֹּ֥אמְרוּ\rb* \rb him|ל֖וֹ\rb*. \v 33 \rb So he called|וַיִּקְרָ֥א\rb* \rb it|אֹתָ֖הּ\rb* \rb Shibah|שִׁבְעָ֑ה\rb*,\f + \fr 26:33 \fqa Shibah \ft can mean \fqa oath \ft or \fqa seven\ft .\f* \rb and|עַל־\rb*\rb |כֵּ֤ן\rb* \rb to|עַ֖ד\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּֽה׃ס\rb* \rb day|הַיּ֥וֹם\rb* \rb the name|שֵׁם־\rb* \rb of the city|הָעִיר֙\rb*\rb |בְּאֵ֣ר\rb* \rb is Beersheba|שֶׁ֔בַע\rb*.\f + \fr 26:33 \fqa Beersheba \ft means \fqa well of seven \ft or \fqa well of the oath\ft .\f*
\s1 Esau’s Wives
\p \v 34 \rb When Esau|עֵשָׂו֙\rb* \rb was|וַיְהִ֤י\rb* \rb forty|אַרְבָּעִ֣ים\rb* \rb years old|בֶּן־\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֔ה\rb*, \rb he took|וַיִּקַּ֤ח\rb* \rb as his wives|אִשָּׁה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Judith|יְהוּדִ֔ית\rb* \rb daughter|בַּת־\rb* \rb of Beeri|בְּאֵרִ֖י\rb* \rb the Hittite|הַֽחִתִּ֑י\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and Basemath|בָּ֣שְׂמַ֔ת\rb* \rb daughter|בַּת־\rb* \rb of Elon|אֵילֹ֖ן\rb* \rb the Hittite|הַֽחִתִּֽי׃\rb*. \v 35 \rb And|וַתִּהְיֶ֖יןָ\rb* \rb they brought|ר֑וּחַ\rb* \rb grief|מֹ֣רַת\rb* \rb to Isaac|לְיִצְחָ֖ק\rb* \rb and Rebekah|וּלְרִבְקָֽה׃ס\rb*.
\c 27
\s1 Isaac Blesses Jacob
\p \v 1 \rb When|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb Isaac|יִצְחָ֔ק\rb* \rb was|וַיְהִי֙\rb* \rb old|זָקֵ֣ן\rb* \rb and his eyes|עֵינָ֖יו\rb* \rb were so weak|וַתִּכְהֶ֥יןָ\rb* \rb that he could no longer see|מֵרְאֹ֑ת\rb*, \rb he called|וַיִּקְרָ֞א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his older|הַגָּדֹ֗ל\rb* \rb son|בְּנ֣וֹ\rb* \rb Esau|עֵשָׂ֣ו׀\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to him|אֵלָיו֙\rb*, “\rb My son|בְּנִ֔י\rb*.”
\p “\rb Here I am|הִנֵּֽנִי׃\rb*,” \rb Esau replied|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֵלָ֖יו\rb*.
\p \v 2 “\rb Look|הִנֵּה־\rb*,” \rb said Isaac|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*, “\rb I am now|נָ֖א\rb* \rb old|זָקַ֑נְתִּי\rb*, \rb and I do not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb know|יָדַ֖עְתִּי\rb* \rb the day|י֥וֹם\rb* \rb of my death|מוֹתִֽי׃\rb*. \v 3 \rb |וְעַתָּה֙\rb* \rb Take|שָׂא־\rb*\rb |נָ֣א\rb* \rb your weapons|כֵלֶ֔יךָ\rb* — \rb your quiver|תֶּלְיְךָ֖\rb* \rb and bow|וְקַשְׁתֶּ֑ךָ\rb* — \rb and go out|וְצֵא֙\rb* \rb into the field|הַשָּׂדֶ֔ה\rb* \rb to hunt|וְצ֥וּדָה\rb* \rb some game|צֵידָה׃\rb* \rb for me|לִּ֖י\rb*. \v 4 \rb Then prepare|וַעֲשֵׂה־\rb* \rb a tasty dish|מַטְעַמִּ֜ים\rb* \rb that|כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I love|אָהַ֛בְתִּי\rb* \rb and bring|וְהָבִ֥יאָה\rb* \rb it to me|לִּ֖י\rb* \rb to eat|וְאֹכֵ֑לָה\rb*, \rb so that|בַּעֲב֛וּר\rb* \rb I|נַפְשִׁ֖י\rb* \rb may bless|תְּבָרֶכְךָ֥\rb* \rb you before|בְּטֶ֥רֶם\rb* \rb I die|אָמֽוּת׃\rb*.”
\p \v 5 \rb Now Rebekah|וְרִבְקָ֣ה\rb* \rb was listening|שֹׁמַ֔עַת\rb* \rb to what Isaac|יִצְחָ֔ק\rb* \rb told|בְּדַבֵּ֣ר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb his son|בְּנ֑וֹ\rb* \rb Esau|עֵשָׂ֖ו\rb*. \rb So when Esau|עֵשָׂו֙\rb* \rb went|וַיֵּ֤לֶךְ\rb* \rb into the field|הַשָּׂדֶ֔ה\rb* \rb to hunt|לָצ֥וּד\rb* \rb game|צַ֖יִד\rb* \rb and bring it back|לְהָבִֽיא׃\rb*, \v 6 \rb Rebekah|וְרִבְקָה֙\rb* \rb said|אָֽמְרָ֔ה\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb her son|בְּנָ֖הּ\rb* \rb Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֥ב\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*, “\rb Behold|הִנֵּ֤ה\rb*, \rb I overheard|שָׁמַ֙עְתִּי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your father|אָבִ֔יךָ\rb* \rb saying|מְדַבֵּ֛ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb your brother|אָחִ֖יךָ\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb* \rb Esau|עֵשָׂ֥ו\rb*, \v 7 ‘\rb Bring|הָבִ֨יאָה\rb* \rb me|לִּ֥י\rb* \rb some game|צַ֛יִד\rb* \rb and prepare|וַעֲשֵׂה־\rb* \rb me|לִ֥י\rb* \rb a tasty dish|מַטְעַמִּ֖ים\rb* \rb to eat|וְאֹכֵ֑לָה\rb*, \rb so that I may bless you|וַאֲבָרֶכְכָ֛ה\rb* \rb in the presence|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb I die|מוֹתִֽי׃\rb*.’
\p \v 8 \rb Now|וְעַתָּ֥ה\rb*, \rb my son|בְנִ֖י\rb*, \rb listen to|שְׁמַ֣ע\rb* \rb my voice|בְּקֹלִ֑י\rb* \rb and do exactly as|לַאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֖י\rb* \rb tell|מְצַוָּ֥ה\rb* \rb you|אֹתָֽךְ׃\rb*. \v 9 \rb Go out|לֶךְ־\rb*\rb |נָא֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the flock|הַצֹּ֔אן\rb* \rb and bring|וְקַֽח־\rb* \rb me|לִ֣י\rb*\rb |מִשָּׁ֗ם\rb* \rb two|שְׁנֵ֛י\rb* \rb choice|טֹבִ֑ים\rb* \rb young goats|גְּדָיֵ֥י\rb*\rb |עִזִּ֖ים\rb*, \rb so that I can make|וְאֶֽעֱשֶׂ֨ה\rb* \rb them|אֹתָ֧ם\rb* \rb into a tasty dish|מַטְעַמִּ֛ים\rb* \rb for your father|לְאָבִ֖יךָ\rb*— \rb the kind|כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb he loves|אָהֵֽב׃\rb*. \v 10 \rb Then take|וְהֵבֵאתָ֥\rb* \rb it to your father|לְאָבִ֖יךָ\rb* \rb to eat|וְאָכָ֑ל\rb*, \rb so that|בַּעֲבֻ֛ר\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb he may bless|יְבָרֶכְךָ֖\rb* \rb you before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb he dies|מוֹתֽוֹ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 11 \rb Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֔ב\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb answered|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb his mother|אִמּ֑וֹ\rb* \rb Rebekah|רִבְקָ֖ה\rb*, “\rb Look|הֵ֣ן\rb*, \rb my brother|אָחִי֙\rb* \rb Esau|עֵשָׂ֤ו\rb* \rb is a hairy|שָׂעִ֔ר\rb* \rb man|אִ֣ישׁ\rb*, \rb but I am|וְאָנֹכִ֖י\rb*\rb |אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb smooth-skinned|חָלָֽק׃\rb*. \v 12 \rb What if|אוּלַ֤י\rb* \rb my father|אָבִ֔י\rb* \rb touches me|יְמֻשֵּׁ֙נִי֙\rb*? \rb Then I would be revealed|וְהָיִ֥יתִי\rb* \rb to him|בְעֵינָ֖יו\rb* \rb as a deceiver|כִּמְתַעְתֵּ֑עַ\rb*, \rb and I would bring|וְהֵבֵאתִ֥י\rb* \rb upon myself|עָלַ֛י\rb* \rb a curse|קְלָלָ֖ה\rb* \rb rather than|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb a blessing|בְרָכָֽה׃\rb*.”
\p \v 13 \rb His mother|אִמּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb replied|וַתֹּ֤אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Your curse|קִלְלָתְךָ֖\rb* \rb be on me|עָלַ֥י\rb*, \rb my son|בְּנִ֑י\rb*. \rb Just|אַ֛ךְ\rb* \rb obey|שְׁמַ֥ע\rb* \rb my voice|בְּקֹלִ֖י\rb* \rb and go|וְלֵ֥ךְ\rb* \rb get them|קַֽח־\rb* \rb for me|לִֽי׃\rb*.”
\p \v 14 \rb So Jacob went|וַיֵּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb and got two goats|וַיִּקַּ֔ח\rb* \rb and brought them|וַיָּבֵ֖א\rb* \rb to his mother|לְאִמּ֑וֹ\rb*, \rb who|אִמּוֹ֙\rb* \rb made|וַתַּ֤עַשׂ\rb* \rb the tasty food|מַטְעַמִּ֔ים\rb*\rb |כַּאֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb his father|אָבִֽיו׃\rb* \rb loved|אָהֵ֥ב\rb*. \v 15 \rb And Rebekah|רִ֠בְקָה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb took|וַתִּקַּ֣ח\rb* \rb the finest|הַחֲמֻדֹ֔ת\rb* \rb clothes|בִּגְדֵ֨י\rb* \rb in the house|בַּבָּ֑יִת\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb belonged|אִתָּ֖הּ\rb* \rb to her older|הַגָּדֹל֙\rb* \rb son|בְּנָ֤הּ\rb* \rb Esau|עֵשָׂ֜ו\rb*, \rb and she put them on|וַתַּלְבֵּ֥שׁ\rb* \rb her younger|הַקָּטָֽן׃\rb* \rb son|בְּנָ֥הּ\rb* \rb Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֖ב\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb*. \v 16 \rb |וְאֵ֗ת\rb* \rb She also put|הִלְבִּ֖ישָׁה\rb* \rb the skins|עֹרֹת֙\rb* \rb of the young|גְּדָיֵ֣י\rb* \rb goats|הָֽעִזִּ֔ים\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb his hands|יָדָ֑יו\rb* \rb and on|וְעַ֖ל\rb* \rb the smooth part|חֶלְקַ֥ת\rb* \rb of his neck|צַוָּארָֽיו׃\rb*. \v 17 \rb Then|אֶת־\rb* \rb she handed|וַתִּתֵּ֧ן\rb*\rb |בְּיַ֖ד\rb* \rb her son|בְּנָֽהּ׃\rb* \rb Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֥ב\rb* \rb the tasty food|הַמַּטְעַמִּ֛ים\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and bread|הַלֶּ֖חֶם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb she had made|עָשָׂ֑תָה\rb*.
\p \v 18 \rb So Jacob went|וַיָּבֹ֥א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his father|אָבִ֖יו\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb My father|אָבִ֑י\rb*.”
\p “\rb Here I am|הִנֶּ֔נִּי\rb*!” \rb he answered|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*. “\rb Which one|מִ֥י\rb* \rb are you|אַתָּ֖ה\rb*, \rb my son|בְּנִֽי׃\rb*?”
\p \v 19 \rb Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֜ב\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his father|אָבִ֗יו\rb*, “\rb I|אָנֹכִי֙\rb* \rb am Esau|עֵשָׂ֣ו\rb*, \rb your firstborn|בְּכֹרֶ֔ךָ\rb*. \rb I have done|עָשִׂ֕יתִי\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you told me|דִּבַּ֖רְתָּ\rb*.\rb |אֵלָ֑י\rb* \rb Please|נָ֣א\rb*\rb |קֽוּם־\rb* \rb sit up|שְׁבָ֗ה\rb* \rb and eat|וְאָכְלָה֙\rb* \rb some of my game|מִצֵּידִ֔י\rb*, \rb so that|בַּעֲב֖וּר\rb* \rb you|נַפְשֶֽׁךָ׃\rb* \rb may bless me|תְּבָרֲכַ֥נִּי\rb*.”
\p \v 20 \rb But Isaac|יִצְחָק֙\rb* \rb asked|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb his son|בְּנ֔וֹ\rb*, “\rb How|מַה־\rb* \rb did you ever find|לִמְצֹ֖א\rb* \rb it so|זֶּ֛ה\rb* \rb quickly|מִהַ֥רְתָּ\rb*, \rb my son|בְּנִ֑י\rb*?”
\p “\rb Because|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb brought it|הִקְרָ֛ה\rb* \rb to me|לְפָנָֽי׃\rb*,” \rb he replied|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*.
\p \v 21 \rb Then Isaac|יִצְחָק֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֔ב\rb*, “\rb Please|נָּ֥א\rb* \rb come closer|גְּשָׁה־\rb* \rb so I can touch you|וַאֲמֻֽשְׁךָ֖\rb*, \rb my son|בְּנִ֑י\rb*. \rb Are you|הַֽאַתָּ֥ה\rb* \rb really|זֶ֛ה\rb* \rb my son|בְּנִ֥י\rb* \rb Esau|עֵשָׂ֖ו\rb*, \rb or|אִם־\rb* \rb not|לֹֽא׃\rb*?”
\p \v 22 \rb So Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֛ב\rb* \rb came close|וַיִּגַּ֧שׁ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his father|אָבִ֖יו\rb* \rb Isaac|יִצְחָ֥ק\rb*, \rb who touched him|וַיְמֻשֵּׁ֑הוּ\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*, “\rb The voice|הַקֹּל֙\rb* \rb is the voice|ק֣וֹל\rb* \rb of Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֔ב\rb*, \rb but the hands|וְהַיָּדַ֖יִם\rb* \rb are the hands|יְדֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Esau|עֵשָֽׂו׃\rb*.” \v 23 \rb Isaac did not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb recognize him|הִכִּיר֔וֹ\rb*, \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb his hands|יָדָ֗יו\rb* \rb were|הָי֣וּ\rb* \rb hairy|שְׂעִרֹ֑ת\rb* \rb like those|כִּידֵ֛י\rb* \rb of his brother|אָחִ֖יו\rb* \rb Esau|עֵשָׂ֥ו\rb*; \rb so he blessed him|וַֽיְבָרְכֵֽהוּ׃\rb*.
\p \v 24 \rb Again he asked|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Are you|אַתָּ֥ה\rb* \rb really|זֶ֖ה\rb* \rb my son|בְּנִ֣י\rb* \rb Esau|עֵשָׂ֑ו\rb*?”
\p \rb And he replied|וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb*, “\rb I am|אָֽנִי׃\rb*.”
\p \v 25 “\rb Serve|הַגִּ֤שָׁה\rb* \rb me|לִּי֙\rb*,” \rb said Isaac|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*, “\rb and let me eat|וְאֹֽכְלָה֙\rb* \rb some of my son’s|בְּנִ֔י\rb* \rb game|מִצֵּ֣יד\rb*, \rb so that|לְמַ֥עַן\rb* \rb I|נַפְשִׁ֑י\rb* \rb may bless you|תְּבָֽרֶכְךָ֖\rb*.”
\p \rb Jacob brought it|וַיַּגֶּשׁ־\rb* \rb to him|לוֹ֙\rb*, \rb and he ate|וַיֹּאכַ֔ל\rb*; \rb then he brought|וַיָּ֧בֵא\rb* \rb him|ל֦וֹ\rb* \rb wine|יַ֖יִן\rb*, \rb and he drank|וַיֵּֽשְׁתְּ׃\rb*.
\p \v 26 \rb Then his father|אָבִ֑יו\rb* \rb Isaac|יִצְחָ֣ק\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb* \rb to him|אֵלָ֖יו\rb*, “\rb Please|נָּ֥א\rb* \rb come near|גְּשָׁה־\rb* \rb and kiss|וּשְׁקָה־\rb* \rb me|לִּ֖י\rb*, \rb my son|בְּנִֽי׃\rb*.”
\p \v 27 \rb So he came near|וַיִּגַּשׁ֙\rb* \rb and kissed|וַיִּשַּׁק־\rb* \rb him|ל֔וֹ\rb*. \rb When Isaac smelled|וַיָּ֛רַח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his clothing|בְּגָדָ֖יו\rb*, \rb he blessed him|וַֽיְבָרֲכֵ֑הוּ\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*:
\b 
\q1 “\rb Ah|רְאֵה֙\rb*, \rb the smell|כְּרֵ֣יחַ\rb* \rb of my son|בְּנִ֔י\rb*
\q2 \rb is like the smell|רֵ֣יחַ\rb* \rb of a field|שָׂדֶ֔ה\rb*
\q2 \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb has blessed|בֵּרֲכ֖וֹ\rb*.
\q1 \v 28 \rb May God|הָאֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb* \rb give|וְיִֽתֶּן־\rb* \rb to you|לְךָ֙\rb* \rb the dew|מִטַּל֙\rb* \rb of heaven|הַשָּׁמַ֔יִם\rb*
\q2 \rb and the richness|וּמִשְׁמַנֵּ֖י\rb* \rb of the earth|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb* —
\q2 \rb an abundance|וְרֹ֥ב\rb* \rb of grain|דָּגָ֖ן\rb* \rb and new wine|וְתִירֹֽשׁ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 29 \rb May peoples|עַמִּ֗ים\rb* \rb serve you|יַֽעַבְד֣וּךָ\rb*
\q2 \rb and nations|לְאֻמִּ֔ים\rb* \rb bow down|וְיִשְׁתַּחוּ\rb* \rb to you|לְךָ֙\rb*.
\q1 \rb May you be|הֱוֵ֤ה\rb* \rb the master|גְבִיר֙\rb* \rb of your brothers|לְאַחֶ֔יךָ\rb*,
\q2 \rb and may the sons|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of your mother|אִמֶּ֑ךָ\rb* \rb bow down|וְיִשְׁתַּחֲוּ֥וּ\rb* \rb to you|לְךָ֖\rb*.
\q1 \rb May those who curse you|אֹרְרֶ֣יךָ\rb* \rb be cursed|אָר֔וּר\rb*,
\q2 \rb and those who bless you|וּֽמְבָרֲכֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb be blessed|בָּרֽוּךְ׃\rb*.”
\s1 Esau’s Lost Hope
\p \v 30 \rb |וַיְהִ֗י\rb* \rb As soon as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb Isaac|יִצְחָק֮\rb* \rb had finished|כִּלָּ֣ה\rb* \rb blessing|לְבָרֵ֣ךְ\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb him|יַעֲקֹב֒\rb*\rb |וַיְהִ֗י\rb*\rb |אַ֣ךְ\rb* \rb and Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֔ב\rb*\rb |מֵאֵ֥ת\rb* \rb had left|יָצֹ֤א\rb*\rb |יָצָא֙\rb* \rb his father’s|אָבִ֑יו\rb* \rb presence|פְּנֵ֖י\rb*\rb |יִצְחָ֣ק\rb*, \rb his brother|אָחִ֔יו\rb* \rb Esau|וְעֵשָׂ֣ו\rb* \rb returned|בָּ֖א\rb* \rb from the hunt|מִצֵּידֽוֹ׃\rb*. \v 31 \rb He|הוּא֙\rb* \rb too|גַּם־\rb* \rb made|וַיַּ֤עַשׂ\rb* \rb some tasty food|מַטְעַמִּ֔ים\rb*, \rb brought|וַיָּבֵ֖א\rb* \rb it to his father|לְאָבִ֑יו\rb*, \rb and said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to him|לְאָבִ֗יו\rb*, “\rb My father|אָבִי֙\rb*, \rb sit up|יָקֻ֤ם\rb* \rb and eat|וְיֹאכַל֙\rb* \rb of your son’s|בְּנ֔וֹ\rb* \rb game|מִצֵּ֣יד\rb*, \rb so that|בַּעֲב֖וּר\rb* \rb you|נַפְשֶֽׁךָ׃\rb* \rb may bless me|תְּבָרֲכַ֥נִּי\rb*.”
\p \v 32 \rb But his father|אָבִ֖יו\rb* \rb Isaac|יִצְחָ֥ק\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Who|מִי־\rb* \rb are you|אָ֑תָּה\rb*?”
\p “\rb I|אֲנִ֛י\rb* \rb am Esau|עֵשָֽׂו׃\rb*, \rb your firstborn|בְכֹֽרְךָ֖\rb* \rb son|בִּנְךָ֥\rb*,” \rb he answered|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*.
\p \v 33 \rb Isaac|יִצְחָ֣ק\rb* \rb began to tremble violently|וַיֶּחֱרַ֨ד\rb*\rb |חֲרָדָה֮\rb*\rb |גְּדֹלָ֣ה\rb*\rb |עַד־\rb*\rb |מְאֹד֒\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֡אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Who|מִֽי־\rb* \rb was it|ה֣וּא\rb*, \rb then|אֵפ֡וֹא\rb*, \rb who hunted|הַצָּֽד־\rb* \rb the game|צַיִד֩\rb* \rb and brought it|וַיָּ֨בֵא\rb* \rb to me|לִ֜י\rb*? \rb Before|בְּטֶ֥רֶם\rb* \rb you came in|תָּב֖וֹא\rb*, \rb I ate|וָאֹכַ֥ל\rb* \rb it all|מִכֹּ֛ל\rb* \rb and blessed him|וָאֲבָרֲכֵ֑הוּ\rb* — \rb and indeed|גַּם־\rb*, \rb he will be|יִהְיֶֽה׃\rb* \rb blessed|בָּר֖וּךְ\rb*!”
\p \v 34 \rb When Esau|עֵשָׂו֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb heard|כִּשְׁמֹ֤עַ\rb* \rb his father’s|אָבִ֔יו\rb* \rb words|דִּבְרֵ֣י\rb*, \rb he let out|וַיִּצְעַ֣ק\rb* \rb a loud|גְּדֹלָ֥ה\rb* \rb and bitter|וּמָרָ֖ה\rb*\rb |עַד־\rb*\rb |מְאֹ֑ד\rb* \rb cry|צְעָקָ֔ה\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to his father|לְאָבִ֔יו\rb*, “\rb Bless me|בָּרֲכֵ֥נִי\rb* \rb too|גַם־\rb*,\rb |אָ֖נִי\rb* \rb O my father|אָבִֽי׃\rb*!”
\p \v 35 \rb But Isaac replied|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Your brother|אָחִ֖יךָ\rb* \rb came|בָּ֥א\rb* \rb deceitfully|בְּמִרְמָ֑ה\rb* \rb and took|וַיִּקַּ֖ח\rb* \rb your blessing|בִּרְכָתֶֽךָ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 36 \rb So Esau declared|וַיֹּ֡אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Is he not rightly|הֲכִי֩\rb* \rb named|קָרָ֨א\rb*\rb |שְׁמ֜וֹ\rb* \rb Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֗ב\rb*?\f + \fr 27:36 \fqa Jacob \ft means \fqa he grasps the heel \ft or \fqa he deceives\ft .\f* \rb For he has cheated me|וַֽיַּעְקְבֵ֙נִי֙\rb*\rb |זֶ֣ה\rb* \rb twice|פַעֲמַ֔יִם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*. \rb He took|לָקָ֔ח\rb* \rb my birthright|בְּכֹרָתִ֣י\rb*, \rb and|וְהִנֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb now|עַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb he has taken|לָקַ֣ח\rb* \rb my blessing|בִּרְכָתִ֑י\rb*.” \rb Then he asked|וַיֹּאמַ֕ר\rb*, “\rb Haven’t|הֲלֹא־\rb* \rb you saved|אָצַ֥לְתָּ\rb* \rb a blessing|בְּרָכָֽה׃\rb* \rb for me|לִּ֖י\rb*?”
\p \v 37 \rb But Isaac|יִצְחָ֜ק\rb*\rb |וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb answered|וַיַּ֨עַן\rb* \rb Esau|לְעֵשָׂ֗ו\rb*: “\rb Look|הֵ֣ן\rb*, \rb I have made|שַׂמְתִּ֥יו\rb* \rb him|לָךְ֙\rb* \rb your master|גְּבִ֞יר\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb given|נָתַ֤תִּי\rb* \rb him|לוֹ֙\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb his relatives|אֶחָ֗יו\rb* \rb as servants|לַעֲבָדִ֔ים\rb*; \rb I have sustained|סְמַכְתִּ֑יו\rb* \rb him|וּלְכָ֣ה\rb* \rb with grain|וְדָגָ֥ן\rb* \rb and new wine|וְתִירֹ֖שׁ\rb*. \rb What|מָ֥ה\rb* \rb is left|אֵפ֔וֹא\rb* \rb that I can do for you|אֶֽעֱשֶׂ֖ה\rb*, \rb my son|בְּנִֽי׃\rb*?”
\p \v 38 \rb Esau|עֵשָׂ֜ו\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his father|אָבִ֗יו\rb*, “\rb Do you have only one|אַחַ֤ת\rb*\rb |הִֽוא־\rb* \rb blessing|הַֽבְרָכָ֨ה\rb*, \rb my father|אָבִ֔י\rb*? \rb Bless me|בָּרֲכֵ֥נִי\rb* \rb too|גַם־\rb*,\rb |אָ֖נִי\rb* \rb O my father|אָבִ֑י\rb*!” \rb Then Esau|עֵשָׂ֛ו\rb* \rb wept|וַיֵּֽבְךְּ׃\rb* \rb aloud|וַיִּשָּׂ֥א\rb*\rb |קֹל֖וֹ\rb*.
\p \v 39 \rb His father|אָבִ֖יו\rb*\rb |וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֵלָ֑יו\rb* \rb Isaac|יִצְחָ֥ק\rb* \rb answered him|וַיַּ֛עַן\rb*:
\b 
\q1 “\rb Behold|הִנֵּ֞ה\rb*, \rb your dwelling place|מֽוֹשָׁבֶ֔ךָ\rb* \rb shall be|יִהְיֶ֣ה\rb*
\q2 \rb away from the richness|מִשְׁמַנֵּ֤י\rb* \rb of the land|הָאָ֙רֶץ֙\rb*,
\q2 \rb away from the dew|וּמִטַּ֥ל\rb* \rb of heaven|הַשָּׁמַ֖יִם\rb* \rb above|מֵעָֽל׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 40 \rb You shall live|תִֽחְיֶ֔ה\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb by|וְעַל־\rb* \rb the sword|חַרְבְּךָ֣\rb*
\q2 \rb and serve|תַּעֲבֹ֑ד\rb*\rb |וְהָיָה֙\rb* \rb your brother|אָחִ֖יךָ\rb*.
\q1 \rb But when|כַּאֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb you rebel|תָּרִ֔יד\rb*,
\q2 \rb you will tear|וּפָרַקְתָּ֥\rb* \rb his yoke|עֻלּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb from|מֵעַ֥ל\rb* \rb your neck|צַוָּארֶֽךָ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 41 \rb Esau|עֵשָׂו֙\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb held a grudge|וַיִּשְׂטֹ֤ם\rb* \rb against Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֔ב\rb* \rb because of|עַל־\rb* \rb the blessing|הַ֨בְּרָכָ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb his father|אָבִ֑יו\rb* \rb had given him|בֵּרֲכ֖וֹ\rb*. \rb And Esau|עֵשָׂ֜ו\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb in his heart|בְּלִבּ֗וֹ\rb*, “\rb The days|יְמֵי֙\rb* \rb of mourning|אֵ֣בֶל\rb* \rb for my father|אָבִ֔י\rb* \rb are at hand|יִקְרְבוּ֙\rb*; \rb then I will kill|וְאַֽהַרְגָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb my brother|אָחִֽי׃\rb* \rb Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֥ב\rb*.”
\p \v 42 \rb When the words|דִּבְרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of her older|הַגָּדֹ֑ל\rb* \rb son|בְּנָ֣הּ\rb* \rb Esau|עֵשָׂ֖ו\rb* \rb were relayed|וַיֻּגַּ֣ד\rb* \rb to Rebekah|לְרִבְקָ֔ה\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb she sent for|וַתִּשְׁלַ֞ח\rb*\rb |וַתִּקְרָ֤א\rb* \rb her younger|הַקָּטָ֔ן\rb* \rb son|בְּנָ֣הּ\rb* \rb Jacob|לְיַעֲקֹב֙\rb* \rb and told|וַתֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb him|אֵלָ֔יו\rb*, “\rb Look|הִנֵּה֙\rb*, \rb your brother|אָחִ֔יךָ\rb* \rb Esau|עֵשָׂ֣ו\rb* \rb is consoling himself|מִתְנַחֵ֥ם\rb* \rb by|לְךָ֖\rb* \rb plotting to kill you|לְהָרְגֶֽךָ׃\rb*. \v 43 \rb So now|וְעַתָּ֥ה\rb*, \rb my son|בְנִ֖י\rb*, \rb obey|שְׁמַ֣ע\rb* \rb my voice|בְּקֹלִ֑י\rb* \rb and flee|בְּרַח־\rb* \rb at once|וְק֧וּם\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb my brother|אָחִ֖י\rb* \rb Laban|לָבָ֥ן\rb* \rb in Haran|חָרָֽנָה׃\rb*. \v 44 \rb Stay|וְיָשַׁבְתָּ֥\rb* \rb with him|עִמּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb for a while|אֲחָדִ֑ים\rb*\rb |יָמִ֣ים\rb*, \rb until|עַ֥ד\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb your brother’s|אָחִֽיךָ׃\rb* \rb fury|חֲמַ֥ת\rb* \rb subsides|תָּשׁ֖וּב\rb*— \v 45 \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb your brother’s|אָחִ֜יךָ\rb* \rb rage|אַף־\rb* \rb against you|מִמְּךָ֗\rb* \rb wanes|שׁ֨וּב\rb* \rb and he forgets|וְשָׁכַח֙\rb*\rb |אֵ֣ת\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb you have done|עָשִׂ֣יתָ\rb* \rb to him|לּ֔וֹ\rb*. \rb Then I will send for you|וְשָׁלַחְתִּ֖י\rb* \rb and bring you back|וּלְקַחְתִּ֣יךָ\rb* \rb from there|מִשָּׁ֑ם\rb*. \rb Why|לָמָ֥ה\rb* \rb should I lose|אֶשְׁכַּ֛ל\rb* \rb both|גַּם־\rb* \rb of you|שְׁנֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb in one|אֶחָֽד׃\rb* \rb day|י֥וֹם\rb*?”
\p \v 46 \rb Then Rebekah|רִבְקָה֙\rb* \rb said|וַתֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Isaac|יִצְחָ֔ק\rb*, “\rb I am weary|קַ֣צְתִּי\rb* \rb of my life|בְחַיַּ֔י\rb* \rb because of|מִפְּנֵ֖י\rb* \rb these Hittite|חֵ֑ת\rb* \rb women|בְּנ֣וֹת\rb*.\f + \fr 27:46 \ft Or \fqa daughters of Heth\f* \rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb Jacob|יַ֠עֲקֹב\rb* \rb takes|לֹקֵ֣חַ\rb* \rb a Hittite|חֵ֤ת\rb* \rb wife|אִשָּׁ֨ה\rb* \rb from|מִבְּנֽוֹת־\rb* \rb among them|כָּאֵ֙לֶּה֙\rb*,\rb |מִבְּנ֣וֹת\rb*\rb |הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb what good|לָ֥מָּה\rb* \rb is my|לִּ֖י\rb* \rb life|חַיִּֽים׃\rb*?”
\c 28
\s1 Jacob’s Departure
\p \v 1 \rb So Isaac|יִצְחָ֛ק\rb*\rb |אֶֽל־\rb* \rb called for|וַיִּקְרָ֥א\rb* \rb Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֖ב\rb* \rb and blessed|וַיְבָ֣רֶךְ\rb* \rb him|אֹת֑וֹ\rb*. “\rb Do not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb take|תִקַּ֥ח\rb* \rb a wife|אִשָּׁ֖ה\rb* \rb from the Canaanite|כְּנָֽעַן׃\rb* \rb women|מִבְּנ֥וֹת\rb*,” \rb he commanded|וַיְצַוֵּ֙הוּ֙\rb*\rb |וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*. \v 2 “\rb Go|לֵךְ֙\rb* \rb at once|ק֥וּם\rb*\rb |פַּדֶּ֣נָֽה\rb* \rb to Paddan-aram|אֲרָ֔ם\rb*,\f + \fr 28:2 \ft That is, northwest Mesopotamia; also in verses 5, 6, and 7\f* \rb to the house|בֵּ֥יתָה\rb* \rb of your mother’s|אִמֶּ֑ךָ\rb* \rb father|אֲבִ֣י\rb* \rb Bethuel|בְתוּאֵ֖ל\rb*, \rb and take|וְקַח־\rb*\rb |מִשָּׁם֙\rb* \rb a wife|אִשָּׁ֔ה\rb* \rb from among the daughters|מִבְּנ֥וֹת\rb* \rb of Laban|לָבָ֖ן\rb*, \rb your mother’s|אִמֶּֽךָ׃\rb* \rb brother|אֲחִ֥י\rb*. \v 3 \rb May God|וְאֵ֤ל\rb* \rb Almighty|שַׁדַּי֙\rb*\f + \fr 28:3 \ft Hebrew \fqa El-Shaddai\f* \rb bless|יְבָרֵ֣ךְ\rb* \rb you|אֹֽתְךָ֔\rb* \rb and make you fruitful|וְיַפְרְךָ֖\rb* \rb and multiply you|וְיַרְבֶּ֑ךָ\rb*, \rb so that you may become|וְהָיִ֖יתָ\rb* \rb a company|לִקְהַ֥ל\rb* \rb of peoples|עַמִּֽים׃\rb*. \v 4 \rb And may He give|וְיִֽתֶּן־\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the blessing|בִּרְכַּ֣ת\rb* \rb of Abraham|אַבְרָהָ֔ם\rb* \rb to you|לְךָ֖\rb* \rb and your descendants|וּלְזַרְעֲךָ֣\rb*\rb |אִתָּ֑ךְ\rb*, \rb so that you may possess|לְרִשְׁתְּךָ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb where you dwell as a foreigner|מְגֻרֶ֔יךָ\rb*, \rb the land|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb gave|נָתַ֥ן\rb* \rb to Abraham|לְאַבְרָהָֽם׃\rb*.”
\p \v 5 \rb So Isaac|יִצְחָק֙\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb sent|וַיִּשְׁלַ֤ח\rb* \rb Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֔ב\rb*\rb |וַיֵּ֖לֶךְ\rb*\rb |פַּדֶּ֣נָֽה\rb* \rb to Paddan-aram|אֲרָ֑ם\rb*, \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Laban|לָבָ֤ן\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Bethuel|בְּתוּאֵל֙\rb* \rb the Aramean|הָֽאֲרַמִּ֔י\rb*, \rb the brother|אֲחִ֣י\rb* \rb of Rebekah|רִבְקָ֔ה\rb*, \rb who was the mother|אֵ֥ם\rb* \rb of Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֖ב\rb* \rb and Esau|וְעֵשָֽׂו׃\rb*.
\s1 Esau Marries Mahalath
\p \v 6 \rb Now Esau|עֵשָׂ֗ו\rb* \rb learned|וַיַּ֣רְא\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb Isaac|יִצְחָק֮\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb had blessed|בֵרַ֣ךְ\rb* \rb Jacob|יַעֲקֹב֒\rb* \rb and sent|וְשִׁלַּ֤ח\rb* \rb him|אֹתוֹ֙\rb*\rb |פַּדֶּ֣נָֽה\rb* \rb to Paddan-aram|אֲרָ֔ם\rb* \rb to take|לָקַֽחַת־\rb* \rb a wife|אִשָּׁ֑ה\rb* \rb there|מִשָּׁ֖ם\rb*,\rb |בְּבָרֲכ֣וֹ\rb*\rb |אֹת֔וֹ\rb* \rb commanding|וַיְצַ֤ו\rb* \rb him|עָלָיו֙\rb*,\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* “\rb Do not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb marry|תִקַּ֥ח\rb*\rb |אִשָּׁ֖ה\rb* \rb a Canaanite|כְּנָֽעַן׃\rb* \rb woman|מִבְּנ֥וֹת\rb*,” \v 7 \rb and that Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֔ב\rb* \rb had obeyed|וַיִּשְׁמַ֣ע\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb his father|אָבִ֖יו\rb*\rb |וְאֶל־\rb* \rb and mother|אִמּ֑וֹ\rb* \rb and gone|וַיֵּ֖לֶךְ\rb*\rb |פַּדֶּ֥נָֽה\rb* \rb to Paddan-aram|אֲרָֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 8 \rb And|עֵשָׂ֔ו\rb* \rb seeing|וַיַּ֣רְא\rb* \rb that|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb his father|אָבִֽיו׃\rb* \rb Isaac|יִצְחָ֥ק\rb* \rb disapproved of|רָע֖וֹת\rb*\rb |בְּעֵינֵ֖י\rb* \rb the Canaanite|כְּנָ֑עַן\rb* \rb women|בְּנ֣וֹת\rb*, \v 9 \rb Esau|עֵשָׂ֖ו\rb* \rb went|וַיֵּ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Ishmael|יִשְׁמָעֵ֑אל\rb* \rb and married|וַיִּקַּ֡ח\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb Mahalath|מָחֲלַ֣ת׀\rb*, \rb the sister|אֲח֧וֹת\rb* \rb of Nebaioth|נְבָי֛וֹת\rb* \rb and daughter|בַּת־\rb* \rb of Abraham’s|אַבְרָהָ֜ם\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb Ishmael|יִשְׁמָעֵ֨אל\rb*, \rb in addition to|עַל־\rb* \rb the wives|לְאִשָּֽׁה׃ס\rb*\rb |נָשָׁ֖יו\rb* \rb he already had|ל֥וֹ\rb*.
\s1 Jacob’s Ladder
\p \v 10 \rb Meanwhile Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֖ב\rb* \rb left|וַיֵּצֵ֥א\rb* \rb Beersheba|שָׁ֑בַע\rb* \rb and set out for|וַיֵּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb Haran|חָרָֽנָה׃\rb*. \v 11 \rb On reaching|וַיִּפְגַּ֨ע\rb* \rb a certain place|בַּמָּק֜וֹם\rb*, \rb he spent the night|וַיָּ֤לֶן\rb* \rb there|שָׁם֙\rb* \rb because|כִּי־\rb* \rb the sun|הַשֶּׁ֔מֶשׁ\rb* \rb had set|בָ֣א\rb*. \rb And taking|וַיִּקַּח֙\rb* \rb one of the stones|מֵאַבְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb from that place|הַמָּק֔וֹם\rb*, \rb he put|וַיָּ֖שֶׂם\rb* \rb it under his head|מְרַֽאֲשֹׁתָ֑יו\rb* \rb and lay down|וַיִּשְׁכַּ֖ב\rb*\rb |הַהֽוּא׃\rb* \rb to sleep|בַּמָּק֥וֹם\rb*.
\p \v 12 \rb And Jacob had a dream|וַֽיַּחֲלֹ֗ם\rb* \rb about|וְהִנֵּ֤ה\rb* \rb a ladder|סֻלָּם֙\rb* \rb that rested|מֻצָּ֣ב\rb* \rb on the earth|אַ֔רְצָה\rb* \rb with its top|וְרֹאשׁ֖וֹ\rb* \rb reaching|מַגִּ֣יעַ\rb* \rb up to heaven|הַשָּׁמָ֑יְמָה\rb*,\rb |וְהִנֵּה֙\rb* \rb and God’s|אֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb* \rb angels|מַלְאֲכֵ֣י\rb* \rb were going up|עֹלִ֥ים\rb* \rb and down|וְיֹרְדִ֖ים\rb* \rb the ladder|בּֽוֹ׃\rb*. \v 13 \rb And there|וְהִנֵּ֨ה\rb* \rb at the top|עָלָיו֮\rb*\f + \fr 28:13 \ft Or \fqa there beside him\f* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb was standing|נִצָּ֣ב\rb* \rb and saying|וַיֹּאמַר֒\rb*, “\rb I|אֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵי֙\rb* \rb of your father|אָבִ֔יךָ\rb* \rb Abraham|אַבְרָהָ֣ם\rb* \rb and the God|וֵאלֹהֵ֖י\rb* \rb of Isaac|יִצְחָ֑ק\rb*. \rb I will give you|אֶתְּנֶ֖נָּה\rb* \rb and your descendants|וּלְזַרְעֶֽךָ׃\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֗רֶץ\rb* \rb on which|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb you|אַתָּה֙\rb* \rb now lie|שֹׁכֵ֣ב\rb*\rb |עָלֶ֔יהָ\rb*\rb |לְךָ֥\rb*. \v 14 \rb Your descendants|זַרְעֲךָ֙\rb* \rb will be|וְהָיָ֤ה\rb* \rb like the dust|כַּעֲפַ֣ר\rb* \rb of the earth|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb*, \rb and you will spread out|וּפָרַצְתָּ֛\rb* \rb to the west|יָ֥מָּה\rb* \rb and east|וָקֵ֖דְמָה\rb* \rb and north|וְצָפֹ֣נָה\rb* \rb and south|וָנֶ֑גְבָּה\rb*. \rb All|כָּל־\rb* \rb the families|מִשְׁפְּחֹ֥ת\rb* \rb of the earth|הָאֲדָמָ֖ה\rb* \rb will be blessed|וְנִבְרֲכ֥וּ\rb* \rb through you|בְךָ֛\rb* \rb and your offspring|וּבְזַרְעֶֽךָ׃\rb*. \v 15 \rb Look|וְהִנֵּ֨ה\rb*, \rb I|אָנֹכִ֜י\rb* \rb am with you|עִמָּ֗ךְ\rb*, \rb and I will watch over you|וּשְׁמַרְתִּ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb wherever|בְּכֹ֣ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb you go|תֵּלֵ֔ךְ\rb*, \rb and I will bring you back|וַהֲשִׁ֣בֹתִ֔יךָ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּ֑את\rb* \rb land|הָאֲדָמָ֖ה\rb*. \rb For|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb I will not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb leave|אֶֽעֱזָבְךָ֔\rb* \rb you until|עַ֚ד\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb*\rb |אִם־\rb* \rb I have done|עָשִׂ֔יתִי\rb*\rb |אֵ֥ת\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I have promised|דִּבַּ֖רְתִּי\rb* \rb you|לָֽךְ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 16 \rb When Jacob|יַעֲקֹב֮\rb* \rb woke up|וַיִּיקַ֣ץ\rb*\rb |מִשְּׁנָתוֹ֒\rb*, \rb he said|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Surely|אָכֵן֙\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb is|יֵ֣שׁ\rb* \rb in this|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb place|בַּמָּק֖וֹם\rb*, \rb and I|וְאָנֹכִ֖י\rb*\rb |לֹ֥א\rb* \rb was unaware of it|יָדָֽעְתִּי׃\rb*.” \v 17 \rb And he was afraid|וַיִּירָא֙\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּאמַ֔ר\rb*, “\rb How|מַה־\rb* \rb awesome|נּוֹרָ֖א\rb* \rb is this|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb place|הַמָּק֣וֹם\rb*! \rb This|זֶ֗ה\rb* \rb is none|אֵ֣ין\rb* \rb other than|כִּ֚י\rb*\rb |אִם־\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of God|אֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb*; \rb this|וְזֶ֖ה\rb* \rb is the gate|שַׁ֥עַר\rb* \rb of heaven|הַשָּׁמָֽיִם׃\rb*!”
\s1 The Stone of Bethel
\p \v 18 \rb Early|וַיַּשְׁכֵּ֨ם\rb* \rb the next morning|בַּבֹּ֗קֶר\rb*, \rb Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֜ב\rb* \rb took|וַיִּקַּ֤ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the stone|הָאֶ֙בֶן֙\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb he had placed|וַיָּ֥שֶׂם\rb* \rb under his head|מְרַֽאֲשֹׁתָ֔יו\rb*,\rb |אֹתָ֖הּ\rb* \rb and he set it up|שָׂ֣ם\rb* \rb as a pillar|מַצֵּבָ֑ה\rb*. \rb He poured|וַיִּצֹ֥ק\rb* \rb oil|שֶׁ֖מֶן\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb top of it|רֹאשָֽׁהּ׃\rb*, \v 19 \rb and he called|וַיִּקְרָ֛א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |שֵֽׁם־\rb* \rb that|הַה֖וּא\rb* \rb place|הַמָּק֥וֹם\rb*\rb |בֵּֽית־\rb* \rb Bethel|אֵ֑ל\rb*,\f + \fr 28:19 \fqa Bethel \ft means \fqa house of God\ft .\f* \rb though|וְאוּלָ֛ם\rb* \rb previously|לָרִאשֹׁנָֽה׃\rb* \rb the city|הָעִ֖יר\rb* \rb had been named|שֵׁם־\rb* \rb Luz|ל֥וּז\rb*.
\p \v 20 \rb Then Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֖ב\rb* \rb made|וַיִּדַּ֥ר\rb* \rb a vow|נֶ֣דֶר\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*, “\rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֜ים\rb* \rb will be|יִהְיֶ֨ה\rb* \rb with me|עִמָּדִ֗י\rb* \rb and watch over me|וּשְׁמָרַ֙נִי֙\rb* \rb on this|הַזֶּה֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb*\rb |אָנֹכִ֣י\rb*\rb |הוֹלֵ֔ךְ\rb* \rb journey|בַּדֶּ֤רֶךְ\rb*, \rb and if He will provide|וְנָֽתַן־\rb* \rb me|לִ֥י\rb* \rb with food|לֶ֛חֶם\rb* \rb to eat|לֶאֱכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb and clothes|וּבֶ֥גֶד\rb* \rb to wear|לִלְבֹּֽשׁ׃\rb*, \v 21 \rb so that I may return|וְשַׁבְתִּ֥י\rb* \rb safely|בְשָׁל֖וֹם\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb my father’s|אָבִ֑י\rb* \rb house|בֵּ֣ית\rb*, \rb then the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb will be|וְהָיָ֧ה\rb* \rb my|לִ֖י\rb* \rb God|לֵאלֹהִֽים׃\rb*. \v 22 \rb And this|הַזֹּ֗את\rb* \rb stone|וְהָאֶ֣בֶן\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I have set up|שַׂ֙מְתִּי֙\rb* \rb as a pillar|מַצֵּבָ֔ה\rb* \rb will be|יִהְיֶ֖ה\rb* \rb God’s|אֱלֹהִ֑ים\rb* \rb house|בֵּ֣ית\rb*, \rb and of all|וְכֹל֙\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb You give|תִּתֶּן־\rb* \rb me|לִ֔י\rb* \rb I will surely give You a tenth|עַשֵּׂ֖ר\rb*\rb |אֲעַשְּׂרֶ֥נּוּ\rb*\rb |לָֽךְ׃\rb*.”
\c 29
\s1 Jacob Meets Rachel
\p \v 1 \rb Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֖ב\rb* \rb resumed his journey|וַיִּשָּׂ֥א\rb*\rb |רַגְלָ֑יו\rb* \rb and came|וַיֵּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb to the land|אַ֥רְצָה\rb* \rb of the people|בְנֵי־\rb* \rb of the east|קֶֽדֶם׃\rb*. \v 2 \rb He looked|וַיַּ֞רְא\rb* \rb and saw|וְהִנֵּ֧ה\rb* \rb a well|בְאֵ֣ר\rb* \rb in the field|בַּשָּׂדֶ֗ה\rb*, \rb and|וְהִנֵּה־\rb* \rb near it|שָׁ֞ם\rb*\rb |עָלֶ֔יהָ\rb* \rb lay|רֹבְצִ֣ים\rb* \rb three|שְׁלֹשָׁ֤ה\rb* \rb flocks|עֶדְרֵי־\rb* \rb of sheep|צֹאן֙\rb*, \rb because|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb the sheep|הָעֲדָרִ֑ים\rb* \rb were watered|יַשְׁק֖וּ\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb this|הַהִ֔וא\rb* \rb well|הַבְּאֵ֣ר\rb*. \rb And a large|גְּדֹלָ֖ה\rb* \rb stone|וְהָאֶ֥בֶן\rb* \rb covered|עַל־\rb* \rb the mouth|פִּ֥י\rb* \rb of the well|הַבְּאֵֽר׃\rb*. \v 3 \rb When all|כָל־\rb* \rb the flocks|הָעֲדָרִ֗ים\rb* \rb had been gathered|וְנֶאֶסְפוּ־\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֣מָּה\rb*, \rb the shepherds would roll away|וְגָלֲל֤וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the stone|הָאֶ֙בֶן֙\rb* \rb from|מֵעַל֙\rb* \rb the mouth|פִּ֣י\rb* \rb of the well|הַבְּאֵ֔ר\rb* \rb and water|וְהִשְׁק֖וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the sheep|הַצֹּ֑אן\rb*. \rb Then they would return|וְהֵשִׁ֧יבוּ\rb* \rb the stone|הָאֶ֛בֶן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb to its place|לִמְקֹמָֽהּ׃\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb the mouth|פִּ֥י\rb* \rb of the well|הַבְּאֵ֖ר\rb*.
\p \v 4 “\rb My brothers|אַחַ֖י\rb*,” \rb Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֔ב\rb* \rb asked|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb the shepherds|לָהֶם֙\rb*, “\rb where|מֵאַ֣יִן\rb* \rb are you from|אַתֶּ֑ם\rb*?”
\p “\rb We are|אֲנָֽחְנוּ׃\rb* \rb from Haran|מֵחָרָ֖ן\rb*,” \rb they answered|וַיֹּ֣אמְר֔וּ\rb*.
\p \v 5 “\rb Do you know|הַיְדַעְתֶּ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Laban|לָבָ֣ן\rb* \rb the grandson|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Nahor|נָח֑וֹר\rb*?” \rb Jacob asked|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*.
\p “\rb We know him|יָדָֽעְנוּ׃\rb*,” \rb they replied|וַיֹּאמְר֖וּ\rb*.
\p \v 6 “\rb Is he well|הֲשָׁל֣וֹם\rb*?” \rb Jacob inquired|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb*.
\p “\rb Yes|שָׁל֔וֹם\rb*,” \rb they answered|וַיֹּאמְר֣וּ\rb*, “\rb and here|וְהִנֵּה֙\rb* \rb comes|בָּאָ֖ה\rb* \rb his daughter|בִּתּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb Rachel|רָחֵ֣ל\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb his sheep|הַצֹּֽאן׃\rb*.”
\p \v 7 “\rb Look|הֵ֥ן\rb*,” \rb said Jacob|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*, “\rb it is still|עוֹד֙\rb* \rb broad|גָּד֔וֹל\rb* \rb daylight|הַיּ֣וֹם\rb*; \rb it is not yet|לֹא־\rb* \rb time|עֵ֖ת\rb* \rb to gather|הֵאָסֵ֣ף\rb* \rb the livestock|הַמִּקְנֶ֑ה\rb*. \rb Water|הַשְׁק֥וּ\rb* \rb the sheep|הַצֹּ֖אן\rb* \rb and take them back|וּלְכ֥וּ\rb* \rb to pasture|רְעֽוּ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 8 \rb But they replied|וַיֹּאמְרוּ֮\rb*, “\rb We cannot|לֹ֣א\rb*\rb |נוּכַל֒\rb*, \rb until|עַ֣ד\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the flocks|הָ֣עֲדָרִ֔ים\rb* \rb have been gathered|יֵאָֽסְפוּ֙\rb* \rb and the stone|הָאֶ֔בֶן\rb* \rb has been rolled|וְגָֽלֲלוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb away from|מֵעַ֖ל\rb* \rb the mouth|פִּ֣י\rb* \rb of the well|הַבְּאֵ֑ר\rb*. \rb Then we will water|וְהִשְׁקִ֖ינוּ\rb* \rb the sheep|הַצֹּֽאן׃\rb*.”
\p \v 9 \rb While|עוֹדֶ֖נּוּ\rb* \rb he was still speaking|מְדַבֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb with them|עִמָּ֑ם\rb*, \rb Rachel|וְרָחֵ֣ל׀\rb* \rb arrived|בָּ֗אָה\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb her father’s|לְאָבִ֔יהָ\rb* \rb sheep|הַצֹּאן֙\rb*,\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb she|הִֽוא׃\rb* \rb was a shepherdess|רֹעָ֖ה\rb*. \v 10 \rb |וַיְהִ֡י\rb* \rb As soon as|כַּאֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֜ב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb saw|רָאָ֨ה\rb* \rb Rachel|רָחֵ֗ל\rb*, \rb the daughter|בַּת־\rb* \rb of his mother’s|אִמּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb brother|אֲחִ֣י\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Laban|לָבָן֙\rb*, \rb with Laban’s|לָבָ֖ן\rb* \rb sheep|צֹ֥אן\rb*, \rb he|יַעֲקֹ֗ב\rb* \rb went up|וַיִּגַּ֣שׁ\rb* \rb and rolled|וַיָּ֤גֶל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the stone|הָאֶ֙בֶן֙\rb* \rb away from|מֵעַל֙\rb* \rb the mouth|פִּ֣י\rb* \rb of the well|הַבְּאֵ֔ר\rb* \rb and watered|וַיַּ֕שְׁקְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his uncle’s|אֲחִ֣י\rb*\rb |אִמּ֑וֹ\rb*\rb |לָבָ֖ן\rb*\rb |אֲחִ֥י\rb*\rb |אִמּֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb sheep|צֹ֥אן\rb*. \v 11 \rb Then Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֖ב\rb* \rb kissed|וַיִּשַּׁ֥ק\rb* \rb Rachel|לְרָחֵ֑ל\rb* \rb and wept|וַיֵּֽבְךְּ׃\rb* \rb aloud|וַיִּשָּׂ֥א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |קֹל֖וֹ\rb*. \v 12 \rb He|יַעֲקֹ֜ב\rb* \rb told|וַיַּגֵּ֨ד\rb* \rb Rachel|לְרָחֵ֗ל\rb* \rb that|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb he was|ה֔וּא\rb* \rb Rebekah’s|רִבְקָ֖ה\rb*\rb |ה֑וּא\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb*,\rb |וְכִ֥י\rb* \rb a relative|אֲחִ֤י\rb* \rb of her father|אָבִ֙יהָ֙\rb*, \rb and she ran|וַתָּ֖רָץ\rb* \rb and told|וַתַּגֵּ֥ד\rb* \rb her father|לְאָבִֽיהָ׃\rb*.
\p \v 13 \rb |וַיְהִי֩\rb* \rb When Laban|לָבָ֜ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb heard|כִשְׁמֹ֨עַ\rb* \rb the news|שֵׁ֣מַע׀\rb* \rb about his sister’s|אֲחֹת֗וֹ\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֣ב\rb*, \rb he ran out|וַיָּ֤רָץ\rb* \rb to meet him|לִקְרָאתוֹ֙\rb*. \rb He embraced|וַיְחַבֶּק־\rb* \rb him|לוֹ֙\rb* \rb and kissed|וַיְנַשֶּׁק־\rb* \rb him|ל֔וֹ\rb* \rb and brought him|וַיְבִיאֵ֖הוּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his home|בֵּית֑וֹ\rb*, \rb where Jacob told|וַיְסַפֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb him|לְלָבָ֔ן\rb*\rb |אֵ֥ת\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb that had happened|הַדְּבָרִ֖ים\rb*\rb |הָאֵֽלֶּה׃\rb*.
\s1 Jacob Marries Leah and Rachel
\p \v 14 \rb Then Laban|לָבָ֔ן\rb* \rb declared|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb*\rb |לוֹ֙\rb*, “\rb You are|אָ֑תָּה\rb* \rb indeed|אַ֛ךְ\rb* \rb my own flesh|וּבְשָׂרִ֖י\rb* \rb and blood|עַצְמִ֥י\rb*.”
\p \rb After Jacob had stayed|וַיֵּ֥שֶׁב\rb* \rb with him|עִמּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb a month|חֹ֥דֶשׁ\rb*\rb |יָמִֽים׃\rb*, \v 15 \rb Laban|לָבָן֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to him|לְיַעֲקֹ֔ב\rb*, “\rb Just because|הֲכִי־\rb* \rb you are|אַ֔תָּה\rb* \rb my relative|אָחִ֣י\rb*, \rb should you work|וַעֲבַדְתַּ֖נִי\rb* \rb for nothing|חִנָּ֑ם\rb*? \rb Tell|הַגִּ֥ידָה\rb* \rb me|לִּ֖י\rb* \rb what|מַה־\rb* \rb your wages should be|מַּשְׂכֻּרְתֶּֽךָ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 16 \rb Now Laban|וּלְלָבָ֖ן\rb* \rb had two|שְׁתֵּ֣י\rb* \rb daughters|בָנ֑וֹת\rb*; \rb the older|הַגְּדֹלָה֙\rb* \rb was named|שֵׁ֤ם\rb* \rb Leah|לֵאָ֔ה\rb*, \rb and the younger|הַקְּטַנָּ֖ה\rb* \rb was named|וְשֵׁ֥ם\rb* \rb Rachel|רָחֵֽל׃\rb*. \v 17 \rb Leah|לֵאָ֖ה\rb* \rb had weak|רַכּ֑וֹת\rb* \rb eyes|וְעֵינֵ֥י\rb*,\f + \fr 29:17 \ft Or \fqa had delicate eyes\f* \rb but Rachel|וְרָחֵל֙\rb* \rb was|הָֽיְתָ֔ה\rb* \rb shapely|יְפַת־\rb*\rb |תֹּ֖אַר\rb* \rb and beautiful|וִיפַ֥ת\rb*\rb |מַרְאֶֽה׃\rb*. \v 18 \rb Since Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֖ב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb loved|וַיֶּאֱהַ֥ב\rb* \rb Rachel|רָחֵ֑ל\rb*, \rb he answered|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*, “\rb I will serve|אֶֽעֱבָדְךָ֙\rb* \rb you seven|שֶׁ֣בַע\rb* \rb years|שָׁנִ֔ים\rb* \rb for your younger|הַקְּטַנָּֽה׃\rb* \rb daughter|בִּתְּךָ֖\rb* \rb Rachel|בְּרָחֵ֥ל\rb*.”
\p \v 19 \rb Laban|לָבָ֗ן\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Better|ט֚וֹב\rb* \rb that I give|תִּתִּ֣י\rb* \rb her|אֹתָ֣הּ\rb* \rb to you|לָ֔ךְ\rb* \rb than|מִתִּתִּ֥י\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֖הּ\rb*\rb |לְאִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb to another|אַחֵ֑ר\rb*. \rb Stay here|שְׁבָ֖ה\rb* \rb with me|עִמָּדִֽי׃\rb*.” \v 20 \rb So Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֛ב\rb* \rb served|וַיַּעֲבֹ֧ד\rb* \rb seven|שֶׁ֣בַע\rb* \rb years|שָׁנִ֑ים\rb* \rb for Rachel|בְּרָחֵ֖ל\rb*, \rb yet it seemed|וַיִּהְי֤וּ\rb* \rb but a few|אֲחָדִ֔ים\rb* \rb days|כְּיָמִ֣ים\rb* \rb because of his love|בְּאַהֲבָת֖וֹ\rb* \rb for her|אֹתָֽהּ׃\rb*.
\p \v 21 \rb Finally Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֤ב\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Laban|לָבָן֙\rb*, “\rb Grant|הָבָ֣ה\rb* \rb me|אֶת־\rb* \rb my wife|אִשְׁתִּ֔י\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb my time|יָמָ֑י\rb* \rb is complete|מָלְא֖וּ\rb*, \rb and I want to sleep with|וְאָב֖וֹאָה\rb* \rb her|אֵלֶֽיהָ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 22 \rb |וַיֶּאֱסֹ֥ף\rb* \rb So Laban|לָבָ֛ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb invited all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the men|אַנְשֵׁ֥י\rb* \rb of that place|הַמָּק֖וֹם\rb* \rb and prepared|וַיַּ֥עַשׂ\rb* \rb a feast|מִשְׁתֶּֽה׃\rb*. \v 23 \rb But when|וַיְהִ֣י\rb* \rb evening came|בָעֶ֔רֶב\rb*, \rb Laban took|וַיִּקַּח֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his daughter|בִתּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb Leah|לֵאָ֣ה\rb* \rb and gave|וַיָּבֵ֥א\rb* \rb her|אֹתָ֖הּ\rb* \rb to Jacob|אֵלָ֑יו\rb*, \rb and he slept with|וַיָּבֹ֖א\rb* \rb her|אֵלֶֽיהָ׃\rb*. \v 24 \rb And Laban|לָבָן֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb gave|וַיִּתֵּ֤ן\rb* \rb his servant girl|שִׁפְחָת֑וֹ\rb* \rb Zilpah|זִלְפָּ֖ה\rb* \rb to his daughter|בִתּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb Leah|לְלֵאָ֥ה\rb* \rb as her maidservant|שִׁפְחָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 25 \rb When morning|בַבֹּ֔קֶר\rb* \rb came|וַיְהִ֣י\rb*, \rb there|וְהִנֵּה־\rb*\rb |הִ֖וא\rb* \rb was Leah|לֵאָ֑ה\rb*! “\rb What|מַה־\rb*\rb |זֹּאת֙\rb* \rb have you done|עָשִׂ֣יתָ\rb* \rb to me|לִּ֔י\rb*?” \rb Jacob said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Laban|לָבָ֗ן\rb*. “\rb Wasn’t|הֲלֹ֤א\rb* \rb it for Rachel|בְרָחֵל֙\rb* \rb that I served|עָבַ֣דְתִּי\rb* \rb you|עִמָּ֔ךְ\rb*? \rb Why|וְלָ֖מָּה\rb* \rb have you deceived me|רִמִּיתָֽנִי׃\rb*?”
\p \v 26 \rb Laban|לָבָ֔ן\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb It is not|לֹא־\rb* \rb our custom|יֵעָשֶׂ֥ה\rb*\rb |כֵ֖ן\rb* \rb here|בִּמְקוֹמֵ֑נוּ\rb* \rb to give the younger daughter|הַצְּעִירָ֖ה\rb* \rb in marriage|לָתֵ֥ת\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the older|הַבְּכִירָֽה׃\rb*. \v 27 \rb Finish|מַלֵּ֖א\rb* \rb this|זֹ֑את\rb* \rb week’s celebration|שְׁבֻ֣עַ\rb*\rb |גַּם־\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*, \rb and we will give|וְנִתְּנָ֨ה\rb* \rb you|לְךָ֜\rb* \rb the younger one|זֹ֗את\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb in return for|תַּעֲבֹ֣ד\rb*\rb |ע֖וֹד\rb* \rb another|אֲחֵרֽוֹת׃\rb* \rb seven|שֶֽׁבַע־\rb* \rb years|שָׁנִ֥ים\rb*\rb |עִמָּדִ֔י\rb* \rb of work|בַּעֲבֹדָה֙\rb*.”
\p \v 28 \rb And Jacob|יַעֲקֹב֙\rb* \rb did|וַיַּ֤עַשׂ\rb* \rb just that|כֵּ֔ן\rb*. \rb He finished|וַיְמַלֵּ֖א\rb* \rb the week’s celebration|שְׁבֻ֣עַ\rb*,\rb |זֹ֑את\rb* \rb and Laban gave|וַיִּתֶּן־\rb*\rb |ל֛וֹ\rb* \rb him|אֶת־\rb* \rb his daughter|בִּתּ֖וֹ\rb*\rb |ל֥וֹ\rb* \rb Rachel|רָחֵ֥ל\rb* \rb as his wife|לְאִשָּֽׁה׃\rb*. \v 29 \rb Laban also|לָבָן֙\rb* \rb gave|וַיִּתֵּ֤ן\rb* \rb his servant girl|שִׁפְחָת֑וֹ\rb* \rb Bilhah|בִּלְהָ֖ה\rb* \rb to his daughter|בִּתּ֔וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Rachel|לְרָחֵ֣ל\rb* \rb as her|לָ֖הּ\rb* \rb maidservant|לְשִׁפְחָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 30 \rb Jacob slept with|וַיָּבֹא֙\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb Rachel|רָחֵ֔ל\rb* \rb as well|גַּ֣ם\rb*, \rb and indeed|גַּֽם־\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb he loved|וַיֶּאֱהַ֥ב\rb* \rb Rachel|רָחֵ֖ל\rb* \rb more than Leah|מִלֵּאָ֑ה\rb*. \rb So he worked|וַיַּעֲבֹ֣ד\rb* \rb for|עִמּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb Laban|ע֖וֹד\rb* \rb another|אֲחֵרֽוֹת׃\rb* \rb seven|שֶֽׁבַע־\rb* \rb years|שָׁנִ֥ים\rb*.
\s1 Reuben, Simeon, Levi, and Judah
\p \v 31 \rb When the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb saw|וַיַּ֤רְא\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb Leah|לֵאָ֔ה\rb* \rb was unloved|שְׂנוּאָ֣ה\rb*, \rb He opened|וַיִּפְתַּ֖ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb her womb|רַחְמָ֑הּ\rb*; \rb but Rachel|וְרָחֵ֖ל\rb* \rb was barren|עֲקָרָֽה׃\rb*. \v 32 \rb And Leah|לֵאָה֙\rb* \rb conceived|וַתַּ֤הַר\rb* \rb and gave birth to|וַתֵּ֣לֶד\rb* \rb a son|בֵּ֔ן\rb*, \rb and she named him|וַתִּקְרָ֥א\rb*\rb |שְׁמ֖וֹ\rb* \rb Reuben|רְאוּבֵ֑ן\rb*,\f + \fr 29:32 \fqa Reuben \ft means \fqa Look, a son \ft and also sounds like the Hebrew for \fqa He has seen my misery\ft .\f* \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb she said|אָֽמְרָ֗ה\rb*, “\rb The LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb has seen|רָאָ֤ה\rb* \rb my affliction|בְּעָנְיִ֔י\rb*.\rb |כִּ֥י\rb* \rb Surely|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb my husband|אִישִֽׁי׃\rb* \rb will love me|יֶאֱהָבַ֥נִי\rb* \rb now|עַתָּ֖ה\rb*.”
\p \v 33 \rb Again|עוֹד֮\rb* \rb she conceived|וַתַּ֣הַר\rb* \rb and gave birth to|וַתֵּ֣לֶד\rb* \rb a son|בֵּן֒\rb*, \rb and she said|וַתֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Because the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*\rb |כִּֽי־\rb* \rb has heard|שָׁמַ֤ע\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I|אָנֹ֔כִי\rb* \rb am unloved|שְׂנוּאָ֣ה\rb*, \rb He has given|וַיִּתֶּן־\rb* \rb me|לִ֖י\rb* \rb this son|זֶ֑ה\rb* \rb as well|גַּם־\rb*.”\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb So she named him|וַתִּקְרָ֥א\rb*\rb |שְׁמ֖וֹ\rb* \rb Simeon|שִׁמְעֽוֹן׃\rb*.\f + \fr 29:33 \fqa Simeon \ft probably means \fqa one who hears\ft .\f*
\p \v 34 \rb Once again|עוֹד֮\rb* \rb Leah conceived|וַתַּ֣הַר\rb* \rb and gave birth to|וַתֵּ֣לֶד\rb* \rb a son|בֵּן֒\rb*, \rb and she said|וַתֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Now|עַתָּ֤ה\rb* \rb at last|הַפַּ֙עַם֙\rb* \rb my husband|אִישִׁי֙\rb* \rb will become attached|יִלָּוֶ֤ה\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֔י\rb*, \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I have borne|יָלַ֥דְתִּי\rb* \rb him|ל֖וֹ\rb* \rb three|שְׁלֹשָׁ֣ה\rb* \rb sons|בָנִ֑ים\rb*.” \rb So|עַל־\rb*\rb |כֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb he was named|קָרָֽא־\rb*\rb |שְׁמ֖וֹ\rb* \rb Levi|לֵוִֽי׃\rb*.\f + \fr 29:34 \fqa Levi \ft sounds like the Hebrew for \fqa being attached to \ft or \fqa feeling affection for\ft .\f*
\p \v 35 \rb And once more|ע֜וֹד\rb* \rb she conceived|וַתַּ֨הַר\rb* \rb and gave birth to|וַתֵּ֣לֶד\rb* \rb a son|בֵּ֗ן\rb* \rb and said|וַתֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb*, “\rb This time|הַפַּ֙עַם֙\rb* \rb I will praise|אוֹדֶ֣ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*.” \rb So|עַל־\rb*\rb |כֵּ֛ן\rb* \rb she named him|קָרְאָ֥ה\rb*\rb |שְׁמ֖וֹ\rb* \rb Judah|יְהוּדָ֑ה\rb*.\f + \fr 29:35 \fqa Judah \ft sounds like the Hebrew for \fqa praise\ft .\f* \rb Then Leah stopped|וַֽתַּעֲמֹ֖ד\rb* \rb having children|מִלֶּֽדֶת׃\rb*.
\c 30
\s1 Dan and Naphtali
\p \v 1 \rb When Rachel|רָחֵ֗ל\rb* \rb saw|וַתֵּ֣רֶא\rb* \rb that|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb she was not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb bearing|יָֽלְדָה֙\rb* \rb any children|רָחֵ֖ל\rb* \rb for Jacob|לְיַעֲקֹ֔ב\rb*, \rb she envied|וַתְּקַנֵּ֥א\rb* \rb her sister|בַּאֲחֹתָ֑הּ\rb*. “\rb Give|הָֽבָה־\rb* \rb me|לִּ֣י\rb* \rb children|בָנִ֔ים\rb*, \rb or|וְאִם־\rb*\rb |אַ֖יִן\rb* \rb I|אָנֹֽכִי׃\rb* \rb will die|מֵתָ֥ה\rb*!” \rb she said|וַתֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb Jacob|יַעֲקֹב֙\rb*.
\p \v 2 \rb Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֖ב\rb* \rb became angry|וַיִּֽחַר־\rb*\rb |אַ֥ף\rb* \rb with Rachel|בְּרָחֵ֑ל\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Am I|אָנֹ֔כִי\rb* \rb in the place|הֲתַ֤חַת\rb* \rb of God|אֱלֹהִים֙\rb*, \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb has withheld|מָנַ֥ע\rb* \rb children|פְּרִי־\rb*\rb |בָֽטֶן׃\rb* \rb from you|מִמֵּ֖ךְ\rb*?”
\p \v 3 \rb Then she said|וַתֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Here|הִנֵּ֛ה\rb* \rb is my maidservant|אֲמָתִ֥י\rb* \rb Bilhah|בִלְהָ֖ה\rb*. \rb Sleep with|בֹּ֣א\rb* \rb her|אֵלֶ֑יהָ\rb*, \rb that she may bear children|וְתֵלֵד֙\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb for me|בִּרְכַּ֔י\rb*,\f + \fr 30:3 \ft Literally \fqa bear children on my knees\f* \rb so that through her|מִמֶּֽנָּה׃\rb* \rb I|אָנֹכִ֖י\rb* \rb too|גַם־\rb* \rb can build a family|וְאִבָּנֶ֥ה\rb*.”
\p \v 4 \rb So Rachel gave|וַתִּתֶּן־\rb*\rb |ל֛וֹ\rb* \rb Jacob|אֶת־\rb* \rb her servant|שִׁפְחָתָ֖הּ\rb* \rb Bilhah|בִּלְהָ֥ה\rb* \rb as a wife|לְאִשָּׁ֑ה\rb*, \rb and he|יַעֲקֹֽב׃\rb* \rb slept with|וַיָּבֹ֥א\rb* \rb her|אֵלֶ֖יהָ\rb*, \v 5 \rb and Bilhah|בִּלְהָ֔ה\rb* \rb conceived|וַתַּ֣הַר\rb* \rb and bore|וַתֵּ֥לֶד\rb* \rb him|לְיַעֲקֹ֖ב\rb* \rb a son|בֵּֽן׃\rb*. \v 6 \rb Then Rachel|רָחֵל֙\rb* \rb said|וַתֹּ֤אמֶר\rb*, “\rb God|אֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb* \rb has vindicated me|דָּנַ֣נִּי\rb*;\rb |וְגַם֙\rb* \rb He has heard|שָׁמַ֣ע\rb* \rb my plea|בְּקֹלִ֔י\rb* \rb and given|וַיִּתֶּן־\rb* \rb me|לִ֖י\rb* \rb a son|בֵּ֑ן\rb*.”\rb |עַל־\rb*\rb |כֵּ֛ן\rb* \rb So she named him|קָרְאָ֥ה\rb*\rb |שְׁמ֖וֹ\rb* \rb Dan|דָּֽן׃\rb*.\f + \fr 30:6 \fqa Dan \ft means \fqa He has judged \ft or \fqa He has vindicated\ft .\f*
\p \v 7 \rb And Rachel’s|רָחֵ֑ל\rb* \rb servant|שִׁפְחַ֣ת\rb* \rb Bilhah|בִּלְהָ֖ה\rb* \rb conceived|וַתַּ֣הַר\rb* \rb again|ע֔וֹד\rb* \rb and bore|וַתֵּ֕לֶד\rb* \rb Jacob|לְיַעֲקֹֽב׃\rb* \rb a second|שֵׁנִ֖י\rb* \rb son|בֵּ֥ן\rb*. \v 8 \rb Then Rachel|רָחֵ֗ל\rb* \rb said|וַתֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb In my great struggles|נַפְתּוּלֵ֨י\rb*\rb |אֱלֹהִ֧ים׀\rb*, \rb I have wrestled|נִפְתַּ֛לְתִּי\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb my sister|אֲחֹתִ֖י\rb* \rb and|גַּם־\rb* \rb won|יָכֹ֑לְתִּי\rb*.” \rb So she named|וַתִּקְרָ֥א\rb* \rb him|שְׁמ֖וֹ\rb* \rb Naphtali|נַפְתָּלִֽי׃\rb*.\f + \fr 30:8 \fqa Naphtali \ft sounds like the Hebrew for \fqa wrestling\ft .\f*
\s1 Gad and Asher
\p \v 9 \rb When Leah|לֵאָ֔ה\rb* \rb saw|וַתֵּ֣רֶא\rb* \rb that|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb she had stopped|עָמְדָ֖ה\rb* \rb having children|מִלֶּ֑דֶת\rb*,\rb |וַתִּקַּח֙\rb* \rb she gave|וַתִּתֵּ֥ן\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֛הּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb her servant|שִׁפְחָתָ֔הּ\rb* \rb Zilpah|זִלְפָּ֣ה\rb* \rb to Jacob|לְיַעֲקֹ֖ב\rb* \rb as a wife|לְאִשָּֽׁה׃\rb*. \v 10 \rb And Leah’s|לֵאָ֖ה\rb* \rb servant|שִׁפְחַ֥ת\rb* \rb Zilpah|זִלְפָּ֛ה\rb* \rb bore|וַתֵּ֗לֶד\rb* \rb Jacob|לְיַעֲקֹ֥ב\rb* \rb a son|בֵּֽן׃\rb*. \v 11 \rb Then Leah|לֵאָ֖ה\rb* \rb said|וַתֹּ֥אמֶר\rb*, “\rb How fortunate|בְּגָד\rb*!”\f + \fr 30:11 \ft Alternate MT reading (see also LXX); the other alternate reads \fqa “A troop is coming!”\f* \rb So she named|וַתִּקְרָ֥א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb him|שְׁמ֖וֹ\rb* \rb Gad|גָּֽד׃\rb*.\f + \fr 30:11 \fqa Gad \ft sounds like the Hebrew for \fqa good fortune\ft , or alternately for \fqa band of raiders\ft .\f*
\p \v 12 \rb When Leah’s|לֵאָ֔ה\rb* \rb servant|שִׁפְחַ֣ת\rb* \rb Zilpah|זִלְפָּה֙\rb* \rb bore|וַתֵּ֗לֶד\rb* \rb Jacob|לְיַעֲקֹֽב׃\rb* \rb a second|שֵׁנִ֖י\rb* \rb son|בֵּ֥ן\rb*, \v 13 \rb Leah|לֵאָ֔ה\rb* \rb said|וַתֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb How happy I am|בְּאָשְׁרִ֕י\rb*! \rb For|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb the women|בָּנ֑וֹת\rb* \rb call me happy|אִשְּׁר֖וּנִי\rb*.” \rb So she named|וַתִּקְרָ֥א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb him|שְׁמ֖וֹ\rb* \rb Asher|אָשֵֽׁר׃\rb*.\f + \fr 30:13 \fqa Asher \ft means \fqa happy\ft .\f*
\p \v 14 \rb Now during the wheat|חִטִּ֗ים\rb* \rb harvest|קְצִיר־\rb*, \rb Reuben|רְאוּבֵ֜ן\rb*\rb |בִּימֵ֣י\rb* \rb went out|וַיֵּ֨לֶךְ\rb* \rb and found|וַיִּמְצָ֤א\rb* \rb some mandrakes|דֽוּדָאִים֙\rb* \rb in the field|בַּשָּׂדֶ֔ה\rb*. \rb When he brought|וַיָּבֵ֣א\rb* \rb them|אֹתָ֔ם\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his mother|אִמּ֑וֹ\rb*\rb |לֵאָ֖ה\rb*, \rb Rachel|רָחֵל֙\rb* \rb begged|וַתֹּ֤אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb Leah|לֵאָ֔ה\rb*, “\rb Please|נָ֣א\rb* \rb give me|תְּנִי־\rb* \rb some of|לִ֔י\rb* \rb your son’s|בְּנֵֽךְ׃\rb* \rb mandrakes|מִדּוּדָאֵ֖י\rb*.”
\p \v 15 \rb But Leah replied|וַתֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Is it not enough|הַמְעַט֙\rb* \rb that you have taken away|קַחְתֵּ֣ךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb my husband|אִישִׁ֔י\rb*? \rb Now you|גַּ֥ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb want to take|וְלָקַ֕חַת\rb* \rb my son’s|בְּנִ֑י\rb* \rb mandrakes as well|דּוּדָאֵ֖י\rb*?”
\p “\rb Very well|לָכֵן֙\rb*,” \rb said|וַתֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb Rachel|רָחֵ֗ל\rb*, “\rb he may sleep|יִשְׁכַּ֤ב\rb* \rb with you|עִמָּךְ֙\rb* \rb tonight|הַלַּ֔יְלָה\rb* \rb in exchange for|תַּ֖חַת\rb* \rb your son’s|בְנֵֽךְ׃\rb* \rb mandrakes|דּוּדָאֵ֥י\rb*.”
\p \v 16 \rb When Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֣ב\rb* \rb came in|וַיָּבֹ֨א\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the field|הַשָּׂדֶה֮\rb* \rb that evening|בָּעֶרֶב֒\rb*, \rb Leah|לֵאָ֜ה\rb* \rb went out|וַתֵּצֵ֨א\rb* \rb to meet him|לִקְרָאת֗וֹ\rb* \rb and said|וַתֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb*, “\rb You must come|תָּב֔וֹא\rb* \rb with me|אֵלַ֣י\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb I have hired you|שָׂכֹ֣ר\rb*\rb |שְׂכַרְתִּ֔יךָ\rb* \rb with my son’s|בְּנִ֑י\rb* \rb mandrakes|בְּדוּדָאֵ֖י\rb*.” \rb So he slept|וַיִּשְׁכַּ֥ב\rb* \rb with her|עִמָּ֖הּ\rb* \rb that|הֽוּא׃\rb* \rb night|בַּלַּ֥יְלָה\rb*.
\s1 Issachar, Zebulun, and Dinah
\p \v 17 \rb And God|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb listened|וַיִּשְׁמַ֥ע\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Leah|לֵאָ֑ה\rb*, \rb and she conceived|וַתַּ֛הַר\rb* \rb and bore|וַתֵּ֥לֶד\rb* \rb a fifth|חֲמִישִֽׁי׃\rb* \rb son|בֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb to Jacob|לְיַעֲקֹ֖ב\rb*. \v 18 \rb Then Leah|לֵאָ֗ה\rb* \rb said|וַתֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb God|אֱלֹהִים֙\rb* \rb has rewarded me|נָתַ֤ן\rb*\rb |שְׂכָרִ֔י\rb* \rb for|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb giving|נָתַ֥תִּי\rb* \rb my maidservant|שִׁפְחָתִ֖י\rb* \rb to my husband|לְאִישִׁ֑י\rb*.” \rb So she named him|וַתִּקְרָ֥א\rb*\rb |שְׁמ֖וֹ\rb* \rb Issachar|יִשָּׂשכָֽר׃\rb*.\f + \fr 30:18 \fqa Issachar \ft sounds like the Hebrew for \fqa wages \ft or \fqa reward\ft .\f*
\p \v 19 \rb Again|עוֹד֙\rb* \rb Leah|לֵאָ֔ה\rb* \rb conceived|וַתַּ֤הַר\rb* \rb and bore|וַתֵּ֥לֶד\rb* \rb a sixth|שִׁשִּׁ֖י\rb* \rb son|בֵּן־\rb* \rb to Jacob|לְּיַעֲקֹֽב׃\rb*. \v 20 “\rb God|אֱלֹהִ֥ים׀\rb*\rb |אֹתִי֮\rb* \rb has given me|זְבָדַ֨נִי\rb* \rb a good|טוֹב֒\rb* \rb gift|זֵ֣בֶד\rb*,” \rb she|לֵאָ֗ה\rb* \rb said|וַתֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*. “\rb This time|הַפַּ֙עַם֙\rb* \rb my husband|אִישִׁ֔י\rb* \rb will honor me|יִזְבְּלֵ֣נִי\rb*, \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I have borne|יָלַ֥דְתִּי\rb* \rb him|ל֖וֹ\rb* \rb six|שִׁשָּׁ֣ה\rb* \rb sons|בָנִ֑ים\rb*.” \rb And she named|וַתִּקְרָ֥א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb him|שְׁמ֖וֹ\rb* \rb Zebulun|זְבֻלֽוּן׃\rb*.\f + \fr 30:20 \fqa Zebulun \ft sounds like the Hebrew for \fqa honor\ft .\f*
\p \v 21 \rb After that|וְאַחַ֖ר\rb*, \rb Leah gave birth to|יָ֣לְדָה\rb* \rb a daughter|בַּ֑ת\rb* \rb and named|וַתִּקְרָ֥א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb her|שְׁמָ֖הּ\rb* \rb Dinah|דִּינָֽה׃\rb*.
\s1 Joseph
\p \v 22 \rb Then God|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb remembered|וַיִּזְכֹּ֥ר\rb* \rb Rachel|רָחֵ֑ל\rb*. \rb He|אֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb* \rb listened|וַיִּשְׁמַ֤ע\rb* \rb to her|אֵלֶ֙יהָ֙\rb* \rb and opened|וַיִּפְתַּ֖ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb her womb|רַחְמָֽהּ׃\rb*, \v 23 \rb and she conceived|וַתַּ֖הַר\rb* \rb and gave birth to|וַתֵּ֣לֶד\rb* \rb a son|בֵּ֑ן\rb*. “\rb God|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb has taken away|אָסַ֥ף\rb* \rb my shame|חֶרְפָּתִֽי׃\rb*,” \rb she said|וַתֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*. \v 24 \rb She named|וַתִּקְרָ֧א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb him|שְׁמ֛וֹ\rb* \rb Joseph|יוֹסֵ֖ף\rb*,\f + \fr 30:24 \fqa Joseph \ft means \fqa may He add\ft .\f* \rb and said|לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*, “\rb May the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb add|יֹסֵ֧ף\rb* \rb to me|לִ֖י\rb* \rb another|אַחֵֽר׃\rb* \rb son|בֵּ֥ן\rb*.”
\s1 Jacob Prospers
\p \v 25 \rb Now|וַיְהִ֕י\rb* \rb after|כַּאֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb Rachel|רָחֵ֖ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb had given birth to|יָלְדָ֥ה\rb* \rb Joseph|יוֹסֵ֑ף\rb*, \rb Jacob|יַעֲקֹב֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Laban|לָבָ֔ן\rb*, “\rb Send me on my way|שַׁלְּחֵ֙נִי֙\rb* \rb so I can return|וְאֵ֣לְכָ֔ה\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb my homeland|מְקוֹמִ֖י\rb*\rb |וּלְאַרְצִֽי׃\rb*. \v 26 \rb Give|תְּנָ֞ה\rb* \rb me|אֶת־\rb* \rb my wives|נָשַׁ֣י\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb children|יְלָדַ֗י\rb* \rb for whom|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb I have served you|עָבַ֧דְתִּי\rb*,\rb |אֹֽתְךָ֛\rb*\rb |בָּהֵ֖ן\rb* \rb that I may go on my way|וְאֵלֵ֑כָה\rb*.\rb |כִּ֚י\rb* \rb You|אַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb know|יָדַ֔עְתָּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb how|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb hard I have worked|עֲבֹדָתִ֖י\rb* \rb for you|עֲבַדְתִּֽיךָ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 27 \rb But Laban|לָבָ֔ן\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֵלָיו֙\rb*, “\rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb I have found|מָצָ֥אתִי\rb* \rb favor|חֵ֖ן\rb* \rb in your eyes|בְּעֵינֶ֑יךָ\rb*, \rb please stay|נָ֛א\rb*. \rb I have learned by divination|נִחַ֕שְׁתִּי\rb* \rb that the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb has blessed me|וַיְבָרֲכֵ֥נִי\rb* \rb because of you|בִּגְלָלֶֽךָ׃\rb*.” \v 28 \rb And he added|וַיֹּאמַ֑ר\rb*, “\rb Name|נָקְבָ֧ה\rb* \rb your wages|שְׂכָרְךָ֛\rb*,\rb |עָלַ֖י\rb* \rb and I will pay them|וְאֶתֵּֽנָה׃\rb*.”
\p \v 29 \rb Then Jacob answered|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֵלָ֔יו\rb*, “\rb You|אַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb know|יָדַ֔עְתָּ\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb how|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb I have served you|עֲבַדְתִּ֑יךָ\rb* \rb and|וְאֵ֛ת\rb* \rb how|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb your livestock|מִקְנְךָ֖\rb* \rb have thrived|הָיָ֥ה\rb* \rb under my care|אִתִּֽי׃\rb*. \v 30 \rb Indeed|כִּ֡י\rb*, \rb you had|הָיָ֨ה\rb*\rb |לְךָ֤\rb* \rb very little|מְעַט֩\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb before my arrival|לְפָנַי֙\rb*, \rb but now your wealth|לָרֹ֔ב\rb* \rb has increased many times over|וַיִּפְרֹ֣ץ\rb*. \rb The LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb has blessed|וַיְבָ֧רֶךְ\rb* \rb you|אֹתְךָ֖\rb* \rb wherever I set foot|לְרַגְלִ֑י\rb*. \rb But now|וְעַתָּ֗ה\rb*, \rb when|מָתַ֛י\rb* \rb may I|אָנֹכִ֖י\rb* \rb also|גַם־\rb* \rb provide|אֶֽעֱשֶׂ֥ה\rb* \rb for my own household|לְבֵיתִֽי׃\rb*?”
\p \v 31 “\rb What|מָ֣ה\rb* \rb can I give|אֶתֶּן־\rb* \rb you|לָ֑ךְ\rb*?” \rb Laban asked|וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb*.
\p “\rb You do not|לֹא־\rb* \rb need to give|תִתֶּן־\rb* \rb me|לִ֣י\rb* \rb anything|מְא֔וּמָה\rb*,” \rb Jacob replied|יַעֲקֹב֙\rb*\rb |וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb*. “\rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb you do|תַּֽעֲשֶׂה־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb one thing|הַדָּבָ֣ר\rb* \rb for me|לִּי֙\rb*, \rb I will keep on|אָשׁ֛וּבָה\rb* \rb shepherding|אֶרְעֶ֥ה\rb* \rb and keeping|אֶשְׁמֹֽר׃\rb* \rb your flocks|צֹֽאנְךָ֖\rb*. \v 32 \rb Let me go|אֶֽעֱבֹ֨ר\rb* \rb through all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb your flocks|צֹֽאנְךָ֜\rb* \rb today|הַיּ֗וֹם\rb* \rb and remove|הָסֵ֨ר\rb* \rb from them|מִשָּׁ֜ם\rb* \rb every|כָּל־\rb* \rb speckled|נָקֹ֣ד\rb* \rb or spotted|וְטָל֗וּא\rb* \rb sheep|שֶׂ֣ה׀\rb*, \rb every|וְכָל־\rb* \rb dark-colored|חוּם֙\rb*\rb |שֶׂה־\rb* \rb lamb|בַּכְּשָׂבִ֔ים\rb*, \rb and every spotted|וְטָל֥וּא\rb* \rb or speckled|וְנָקֹ֖ד\rb* \rb goat|בָּעִזִּ֑ים\rb*. \rb These will be|וְהָיָ֖ה\rb* \rb my wages|שְׂכָרִֽי׃\rb*. \v 33 \rb So my honesty|צִדְקָתִי֙\rb* \rb will testify|וְעָֽנְתָה־\rb* \rb for me|בִּ֤י\rb* \rb when|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb you come to check|תָב֥וֹא\rb*\rb |לְפָנֶ֑יךָ\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb my wages|שְׂכָרִ֖י\rb* \rb in the future|בְּי֣וֹם\rb*\rb |מָחָ֔ר\rb*. \rb If I have|אִתִּֽי׃\rb* \rb any|כֹּ֣ל\rb* \rb goats|בָּֽעִזִּ֗ים\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb are not|אֵינֶנּוּ֩\rb* \rb speckled|נָקֹ֨ד\rb* \rb or spotted|וְטָל֜וּא\rb*, \rb or any lambs|בַּכְּשָׂבִ֔ים\rb* \rb that are not dark-colored|וְחוּם֙\rb*, \rb they|ה֖וּא\rb* \rb will be considered stolen|גָּנ֥וּב\rb*.”
\p \v 34 “\rb Agreed|הֵ֑ן\rb*,”\rb |ל֖וּ\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb* \rb Laban|לָבָ֖ן\rb*. “\rb Let it be|יְהִ֥י\rb* \rb as you have said|כִדְבָרֶֽךָ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 35 \rb That very|הַה֨וּא\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb day|בַּיּוֹם֩\rb* \rb Laban removed|וַיָּ֣סַר\rb* \rb all the streaked|הָֽעֲקֻדִּ֣ים\rb* \rb or spotted|וְהַטְּלֻאִ֗ים\rb* \rb male goats|הַתְּיָשִׁ֜ים\rb* \rb and|וְאֵ֤ת\rb* \rb every|כָּל־\rb* \rb speckled|הַנְּקֻדּ֣וֹת\rb* \rb or spotted|וְהַטְּלֻאֹ֔ת\rb* \rb female goat|הָֽעִזִּים֙\rb*— \rb every one|כֹּ֤ל\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb had any white|לָבָן֙\rb* \rb on it|בּ֔וֹ\rb*— \rb and every|וְכָל־\rb* \rb dark-colored|ח֖וּם\rb* \rb lamb|בַּכְּשָׂבִ֑ים\rb*, \rb and he placed them|וַיִּתֵּ֖ן\rb* \rb under the care|בְּיַד־\rb* \rb of his sons|בָּנָֽיו׃\rb*. \v 36 \rb Then he put|וַיָּ֗שֶׂם\rb* \rb a three-day|שְׁלֹ֣שֶׁת\rb*\rb |יָמִ֔ים\rb* \rb journey|דֶּ֚רֶךְ\rb* \rb between himself|בֵּינ֖וֹ\rb*\rb |וּבֵ֣ין\rb* \rb and Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֑ב\rb*, \rb while Jacob|וְיַעֲקֹ֗ב\rb* \rb was shepherding|רֹעֶ֛ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the rest|הַנּוֹתָרֹֽת׃\rb* \rb of Laban’s|לָבָ֖ן\rb* \rb flocks|צֹ֥אן\rb*.
\p \v 37 \rb Jacob, however|יַעֲקֹ֗ב\rb*, \rb took|וַיִּֽקַּֽח־\rb*\rb |ל֣וֹ\rb* \rb fresh|לַ֖ח\rb* \rb branches|מַקַּ֥ל\rb* \rb of poplar|לִבְנֶ֛ה\rb*, \rb almond|וְל֣וּז\rb*, \rb and plane trees|וְעֶרְמ֑וֹן\rb*, \rb and peeled|וַיְפַצֵּ֤ל\rb* \rb the bark|בָּהֵן֙\rb*, \rb exposing|מַחְשֹׂף֙\rb*\rb |הַלָּבָ֔ן\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb the white|לְבָנ֔וֹת\rb* \rb inner wood|פְּצָל֣וֹת\rb* \rb of|עַל־\rb* \rb the branches|הַמַּקְלֽוֹת׃\rb*. \v 38 \rb Then he set|וַיַּצֵּ֗ג\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the peeled|פִּצֵּ֔ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb branches|הַמַּקְלוֹת֙\rb*\rb |בָּרֳהָטִ֖ים\rb* \rb in the watering|הַמָּ֑יִם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb troughs|בְּשִֽׁקֲת֣וֹת\rb* \rb in front of|לְנֹ֣כַח\rb* \rb the flocks|הַצֹּ֤אן\rb* \rb coming in|תָּבֹ֨אןָ\rb* \rb to drink|לִשְׁתּוֹת֙\rb*. \rb So when the flocks|הַצֹּ֔אן\rb* \rb were in heat|וַיֵּחַ֖מְנָה\rb* \rb and came|בְּבֹאָ֥ן\rb* \rb to drink|לִשְׁתּֽוֹת׃\rb*, \v 39 \rb they|הַצֹּ֖אן\rb* \rb mated|וַיֶּחֱמ֥וּ\rb* \rb in front of|אֶל־\rb* \rb the branches|הַמַּקְל֑וֹת\rb*. \rb And they bore|וַתֵּלַ֣דְןָ\rb* \rb young that were|הַצֹּ֔אן\rb* \rb streaked|עֲקֻדִּ֥ים\rb* \rb or speckled|נְקֻדִּ֖ים\rb* \rb or spotted|וּטְלֻאִֽים׃\rb*. \v 40 \rb Jacob|יַעֲקֹב֒\rb* \rb set apart|הִפְרִ֣יד\rb* \rb the young|וְהַכְּשָׂבִים֮\rb*, \rb but made|וַ֠יִּתֵּן\rb* \rb the rest|הַצֹּ֧אן\rb* \rb face|פְּנֵ֨י\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the streaked|עָקֹ֛ד\rb*\rb |וְכָל־\rb* \rb dark-colored|ח֖וּם\rb* \rb sheep in Laban’s|לָבָ֑ן\rb* \rb flocks|בְּצֹ֣אן\rb*. \rb Then he set|וַיָּֽשֶׁת־\rb* \rb his own|ל֤וֹ\rb* \rb stock|עֲדָרִים֙\rb* \rb apart|לְבַדּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb and did not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb put them|שָׁתָ֖ם\rb* \rb with|עַל־\rb* \rb Laban’s|לָבָֽן׃\rb* \rb animals|צֹ֥אן\rb*.
\p \v 41 \rb |וְהָיָ֗ה\rb* \rb Whenever|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb the stronger females|הַמְקֻשָּׁרוֹת֒\rb* \rb of the flock|הַצֹּ֣אן\rb* \rb were in heat|יַחֵם֮\rb*, \rb Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֧ב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb would place|וְשָׂ֨ם\rb* \rb the branches|הַמַּקְל֛וֹת\rb* \rb in the troughs|בָּרֳהָטִ֑ים\rb*, \rb in full view|לְעֵינֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the animals|הַצֹּ֖אן\rb*, \rb so that they would breed|לְיַחְמֵ֖נָּה\rb* \rb in front of the branches|בַּמַּקְלֽוֹת׃\rb*. \v 42 \rb But if the animals|הַצֹּ֖אן\rb* \rb were weak|וּבְהַעֲטִ֥יף\rb*, \rb he did not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb set out the branches|יָשִׂ֑ים\rb*. \rb So the weaker animals|הָעֲטֻפִים֙\rb* \rb went to|וְהָיָ֤ה\rb* \rb Laban|לְלָבָ֔ן\rb* \rb and the stronger ones|וְהַקְּשֻׁרִ֖ים\rb* \rb to Jacob|לְיַעֲקֹֽב׃\rb*.
\p \v 43 \rb Thus Jacob|הָאִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb became|מְאֹ֣ד\rb* \rb exceedingly|מְאֹ֑ד\rb* \rb prosperous|וַיִּפְרֹ֥ץ\rb*. \rb He owned|וַֽיְהִי־\rb*\rb |לוֹ֙\rb* \rb large|רַבּ֔וֹת\rb* \rb flocks|צֹ֣אן\rb*, \rb maidservants|וּשְׁפָחוֹת֙\rb* \rb and menservants|וַעֲבָדִ֔ים\rb*, \rb and camels|וּגְמַלִּ֖ים\rb* \rb and donkeys|וַחֲמֹרִֽים׃\rb*.
\c 31
\s1 Jacob Flees from Laban
\p \v 1 \rb Now Jacob heard|וַיִּשְׁמַ֗ע\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb that Laban’s|לָבָן֙\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb sons|בְנֵֽי־\rb* \rb were saying|דִּבְרֵ֤י\rb*, “\rb Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֔ב\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb has taken away|לָקַ֣ח\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb that belonged to|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb our father|לְאָבִ֑ינוּ\rb* \rb and built|עָשָׂ֕ה\rb*\rb |אֵ֥ת\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb wealth|הַכָּבֹ֖ד\rb* \rb at|וּמֵאֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb our father’s expense|לְאָבִ֔ינוּ\rb*.” \v 2 \rb And Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֖ב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb saw|וַיַּ֥רְא\rb* \rb from the countenance|פְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Laban|לָבָ֑ן\rb*\rb |וְהִנֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb that his attitude toward|עִמּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb him|כִּתְמ֥וֹל\rb*\rb |שִׁלְשֽׁוֹם׃\rb* \rb had changed|אֵינֶ֛נּוּ\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֔ב\rb*, “\rb Go back|שׁ֛וּב\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of your fathers|אֲבוֹתֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb and to your kindred|וּלְמוֹלַדְתֶּ֑ךָ\rb*, \rb and I will be|וְאֶֽהְיֶ֖ה\rb* \rb with you|עִמָּֽךְ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 4 \rb So Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֔ב\rb* \rb sent word|וַיִּשְׁלַ֣ח\rb* \rb and called|וַיִּקְרָ֖א\rb* \rb Rachel|לְרָחֵ֣ל\rb* \rb and Leah|וּלְלֵאָ֑ה\rb* \rb to the field|הַשָּׂדֶ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb where his flocks were|צֹאנֽוֹ׃\rb*, \v 5 \rb and he told|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb them|לָהֶ֗ן\rb*, “\rb I|אָנֹכִי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb can see|רֹאֶ֤ה\rb* \rb from your father’s|אֲבִיכֶ֔ן\rb* \rb countenance|פְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb his attitude toward me|אֵלַ֖י\rb* \rb has changed|אֵינֶ֥נּוּ\rb*\rb |כִּתְמֹ֣ל\rb*\rb |שִׁלְשֹׁ֑ם\rb*; \rb but the God|וֵֽאלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of my father|אָבִ֔י\rb* \rb has been|הָיָ֖ה\rb* \rb with me|עִמָּדִֽי׃\rb*. \v 6 \rb You|וְאַתֵּ֖נָה\rb* \rb know|יְדַעְתֶּ֑ן\rb* \rb that|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb I have served|עָבַ֖דְתִּי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your father|אֲבִיכֶֽן׃\rb* \rb with all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb my strength|כֹּחִ֔י\rb*. \v 7 \rb And although he|וַאֲבִיכֶן֙\rb* \rb has cheated|הֵ֣תֶל\rb* \rb me|בִּ֔י\rb* \rb and changed|וְהֶחֱלִ֥ף\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb my wages|מַשְׂכֻּרְתִּ֖י\rb* \rb ten|עֲשֶׂ֣רֶת\rb* \rb times|מֹנִ֑ים\rb*, \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb* \rb has not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb allowed him|נְתָנ֣וֹ\rb* \rb to harm me|לְהָרַ֖ע\rb*.\rb |עִמָּדִֽי׃\rb* \v 8 \rb If|אִם־\rb*\rb |כֹּ֣ה\rb* \rb he said|יֹאמַ֗ר\rb*, ‘\rb The speckled|נְקֻדִּים֙\rb* \rb will be|יִהְיֶ֣ה\rb* \rb your wages|שְׂכָרֶ֔ךָ\rb*,’ \rb then the whole|כָל־\rb* \rb flock|הַצֹּ֖אן\rb* \rb bore|וְיָלְד֥וּ\rb* \rb speckled offspring|נְקֻדִּ֑ים\rb*. \rb If|וְאִם־\rb*\rb |כֹּ֣ה\rb* \rb he said|יֹאמַ֗ר\rb*, ‘\rb The streaked|עֲקֻדִּים֙\rb* \rb will be|יִהְיֶ֣ה\rb* \rb your wages|שְׂכָרֶ֔ךָ\rb*,’ \rb then the whole|כָל־\rb* \rb flock|הַצֹּ֖אן\rb* \rb bore|וְיָלְד֥וּ\rb* \rb streaked offspring|עֲקֻדִּֽים׃\rb*. \v 9 \rb Thus God|אֱלֹהִ֛ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb has taken away|וַיַּצֵּ֧ל\rb* \rb your father’s|אֲבִיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb livestock|מִקְנֵ֥ה\rb* \rb and given|וַיִּתֶּן־\rb* \rb them to me|לִֽי׃\rb*.
\p \v 10 \rb |וַיְהִ֗י\rb* \rb When|בְּעֵת֙\rb* \rb the flocks|הַצֹּ֔אן\rb* \rb were breeding|יַחֵ֣ם\rb*, \rb I saw|וָאֶשָּׂ֥א\rb*\rb |עֵינַ֛י\rb*\rb |וָאֵ֖רֶא\rb* \rb in a dream|בַּחֲל֑וֹם\rb*\rb |וְהִנֵּ֤ה\rb* \rb that the streaked|עֲקֻדִּ֥ים\rb*, \rb spotted|וּבְרֻדִּֽים׃\rb*, \rb and speckled|נְקֻדִּ֖ים\rb* \rb males|הָֽעַתֻּדִים֙\rb* \rb were mating|הָעֹלִ֣ים\rb* \rb with|עַל־\rb* \rb the females|הַצֹּ֔אן\rb*. \v 11 \rb In that dream|בַּחֲל֖וֹם\rb* \rb the angel|מַלְאַ֧ךְ\rb*\f + \fr 31:11 \ft Or \fqa Angel\f* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֛ים\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֜י\rb*, ‘\rb Jacob|יַֽעֲקֹ֑ב\rb*!’
\p \rb And I replied|וָאֹמַ֖ר\rb*, ‘\rb Here I am.|הִנֵּֽנִי׃\rb*’
\p \v 12 ‘\rb Look up|שָׂא־\rb*\rb |נָ֨א\rb*\rb |עֵינֶ֤יךָ\rb*,’ \rb he said|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*, ‘\rb and see|וּרְאֵה֙\rb* \rb that all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the males|הָֽעַתֻּדִים֙\rb* \rb that are mating|הָעֹלִ֣ים\rb* \rb with|עַל־\rb* \rb the flock|הַצֹּ֔אן\rb* \rb are streaked|עֲקֻדִּ֥ים\rb*, \rb spotted|וּבְרֻדִּ֑ים\rb*, \rb or speckled|נְקֻדִּ֖ים\rb*; \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb I have seen|רָאִ֔יתִי\rb*\rb |אֵ֛ת\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb Laban|לָבָ֖ן\rb* \rb has done|עֹ֥שֶׂה\rb* \rb to you|לָּֽךְ׃\rb*. \v 13 \rb I|אָנֹכִ֤י\rb* \rb am the God|הָאֵל֙\rb*\rb |בֵּֽית־\rb* \rb of Bethel|אֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb where|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb you anointed|מָשַׁ֤חְתָּ\rb*\rb |שָּׁם֙\rb* \rb the pillar|מַצֵּבָ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb and made|נָדַ֥רְתָּ\rb*\rb |שָׁ֖ם\rb* \rb a solemn vow|נֶ֑דֶר\rb* \rb to Me|לִּ֛י\rb*. \rb Now|עַתָּ֗ה\rb* \rb get up|ק֥וּם\rb*, \rb leave|צֵא֙\rb*\rb |מִן־\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּ֔את\rb* \rb land at once|הָאָ֣רֶץ\rb*, \rb and return|וְשׁ֖וּב\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb your native|מוֹלַדְתֶּֽךָ׃\rb* \rb land|אֶ֥רֶץ\rb*.’”
\p \v 14 \rb And Rachel|רָחֵל֙\rb* \rb and Leah|וְלֵאָ֔ה\rb* \rb replied|וַתַּ֤עַן\rb*\rb |וַתֹּאמַ֖רְנָה\rb*, “\rb Do we|לָ֛נוּ\rb* \rb have any portion|חֵ֥לֶק\rb* \rb or inheritance|וְנַחֲלָ֖ה\rb* \rb left|הַע֥וֹד\rb* \rb in our father’s|אָבִֽינוּ׃\rb* \rb house|בְּבֵ֥ית\rb*? \v 15 \rb Are we not|הֲל֧וֹא\rb* \rb regarded|נֶחְשַׁ֥בְנוּ\rb* \rb by him|ל֖וֹ\rb* \rb as outsiders|נָכְרִיּ֛וֹת\rb*? \rb Not only|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb has he sold us|מְכָרָ֑נוּ\rb*, \rb but he has|גַּם־\rb* \rb certainly squandered|וַיֹּ֥אכַל\rb*\rb |אָכ֖וֹל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb what was paid for us|כַּסְפֵּֽנוּ׃\rb*. \v 16 \rb Surely|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb all|כָל־\rb* \rb the wealth|הָעֹ֗שֶׁר\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִים֙\rb* \rb has taken away|הִצִּ֤יל\rb* \rb from our father|מֵֽאָבִ֔ינוּ\rb* \rb belongs to us|לָ֥נוּ\rb*\rb |ה֖וּא\rb* \rb and to our children|וּלְבָנֵ֑ינוּ\rb*. \rb So|וְעַתָּ֗ה\rb* \rb do|עֲשֵֽׂה׃\rb* \rb whatever|כֹּל֩\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֛ים\rb* \rb has told|אָמַ֧ר\rb* \rb you|אֵלֶ֖יךָ\rb*.”
\p \v 17 \rb Then Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֑ב\rb* \rb got up|וַיָּ֖קָם\rb* \rb and put|וַיִּשָּׂ֛א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his children|בָּנָ֥יו\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and his wives|נָשָׁ֖יו\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb camels|הַגְּמַלִּֽים׃\rb*, \v 18 \rb and he drove|וַיִּנְהַ֣ג\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb his livestock before him|מִקְנֵ֗הוּ\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb*\rb |מִקְנֵה֙\rb*\rb |קִנְיָנ֔וֹ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb*\rb |רָכַ֖שׁ\rb*\rb |בְּפַדַּ֣ן\rb* \rb along with all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the possessions|רְכֻשׁוֹ֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb he had acquired|רָכָ֔שׁ\rb* \rb in Paddan-aram|אֲרָ֑ם\rb*,\f + \fr 31:18 \ft That is, northwest Mesopotamia\f* \rb to go|לָב֛וֹא\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his father|אָבִ֖יו\rb* \rb Isaac|יִצְחָ֥ק\rb* \rb in the land|אַ֥רְצָה\rb* \rb in Canaan|כְּנָֽעַן׃\rb*.
\p \v 19 \rb Now while Laban|וְלָבָ֣ן\rb* \rb was out|הָלַ֔ךְ\rb* \rb shearing|לִגְזֹ֖ז\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his sheep|צֹאנ֑וֹ\rb*, \rb Rachel|רָחֵ֔ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb stole|וַתִּגְנֹ֣ב\rb* \rb her father’s|לְאָבִֽיהָ׃\rb* \rb household idols|הַתְּרָפִ֖ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb*. \v 20 \rb Moreover, Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֔ב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb deceived|וַיִּגְנֹ֣ב\rb*\rb |לֵ֥ב\rb*\f + \fr 31:20 \ft Or \fqa stole the heart of\ft ; also in verses 26 and 27\f* \rb Laban|לָבָ֖ן\rb* \rb the Aramean|הָאֲרַמִּ֑י\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb by not|בְּלִי֙\rb* \rb telling|הִגִּ֣יד\rb* \rb him|ל֔וֹ\rb* \rb that|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb he|הֽוּא׃\rb* \rb was running away|בֹרֵ֖חַ\rb*. \v 21 \rb So he|הוּא֙\rb* \rb fled|וַיִּבְרַ֥ח\rb* \rb with all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb his possessions|אֲשֶׁר־\rb*,\rb |וַיָּ֖קָם\rb* \rb crossed|וַיַּעֲבֹ֣ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Euphrates|הַנָּהָ֑ר\rb*,\f + \fr 31:21 \ft Hebrew \fqa the River\f* \rb and headed for|וַיָּ֥שֶׂם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |פָּנָ֖יו\rb* \rb the hill country|הַ֥ר\rb* \rb of Gilead|הַגִּלְעָֽד׃\rb*.
\s1 Laban Pursues Jacob
\p \v 22 \rb On the third|הַשְּׁלִישִׁ֑י\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb Laban|לְלָבָ֖ן\rb* \rb was informed|וַיֻּגַּ֥ד\rb* \rb that|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb Jacob|יַעֲקֹֽב׃\rb* \rb had fled|בָרַ֖ח\rb*. \v 23 \rb So he took|וַיִּקַּ֤ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his relatives|אֶחָיו֙\rb* \rb with him|עִמּ֔וֹ\rb*, \rb pursued|וַיִּרְדֹּ֣ף\rb* \rb Jacob|אַחֲרָ֔יו\rb*\rb |דֶּ֖רֶךְ\rb* \rb for seven|שִׁבְעַ֣ת\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֑ים\rb*, \rb and overtook|וַיַּדְבֵּ֥ק\rb* \rb him|אֹת֖וֹ\rb* \rb in the hill country|בְּהַ֥ר\rb* \rb of Gilead|הַגִּלְעָֽד׃\rb*. \v 24 \rb But that night|הַלָּ֑יְלָה\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֛ים\rb* \rb came|וַיָּבֹ֧א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Laban|לָבָ֥ן\rb* \rb the Aramean|הָאֲרַמִּ֖י\rb* \rb in a dream|בַּחֲלֹ֣ם\rb* \rb and warned|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb him|ל֗וֹ\rb*, “\rb Be careful|הִשָּׁ֧מֶר\rb* \rb not|פֶּן־\rb* \rb to say|תְּדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb anything to|עִֽם־\rb* \rb Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֖ב\rb*, \rb either good|מִטּ֥וֹב\rb* \rb or|עַד־\rb* \rb bad|רָֽע׃\rb*.”
\p \v 25 \rb Now Jacob|וְיַעֲקֹ֗ב\rb* \rb had pitched|תָּקַ֤ע\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb his tent|אָהֳלוֹ֙\rb* \rb in the hill country|בָּהָ֔ר\rb* \rb of Gilead|הַגִּלְעָֽד׃\rb* \rb when Laban|לָבָ֖ן\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb overtook|וַיַּשֵּׂ֥ג\rb* \rb him|יַעֲקֹ֑ב\rb*, \rb and Laban|וְלָבָ֛ן\rb* \rb and his relatives|אֶחָ֖יו\rb* \rb camped|תָּקַ֥ע\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb there as well|בְּהַ֥ר\rb*. \v 26 \rb Then Laban|לָבָן֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to Jacob|לְיַעֲקֹ֔ב\rb*, “\rb What|מֶ֣ה\rb* \rb have you done|עָשִׂ֔יתָ\rb*? \rb You have deceived|וַתִּגְנֹ֖ב\rb* \rb me|אֶת־\rb*\rb |לְבָבִ֑י\rb* \rb and carried off my daughters|בְּנֹתַ֔י\rb*\rb |וַתְּנַהֵג֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb like captives|כִּשְׁבֻי֖וֹת\rb* \rb of war|חָֽרֶב׃\rb*! \v 27 \rb Why|לָ֤מָּה\rb* \rb did you run away|לִבְרֹ֔חַ\rb* \rb secretly|נַחְבֵּ֙אתָ֙\rb* \rb and deceive|וַתִּגְנֹ֖ב\rb* \rb me|אֹתִ֑י\rb*, \rb without even|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb telling|הִגַּ֣דְתָּ\rb* \rb me|לִּ֔י\rb*? \rb I would have sent you away|וָֽאֲשַׁלֵּחֲךָ֛\rb* \rb with joy|בְּשִׂמְחָ֥ה\rb* \rb and singing|וּבְשִׁרִ֖ים\rb*, \rb with tambourines|בְּתֹ֥ף\rb* \rb and harps|וּבְכִנּֽוֹר׃\rb*. \v 28 \rb But you did not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb even let me|נְטַשְׁתַּ֔נִי\rb* \rb kiss|לְנַשֵּׁ֥ק\rb* \rb my grandchildren|לְבָנַ֖י\rb* \rb and my daughters goodbye|וְלִבְנֹתָ֑י\rb*. \rb Now|עַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb you have done|עֲשֽׂוֹ׃\rb* \rb a foolish thing|הִסְכַּ֥לְתָּֽ\rb*.
\p \v 29 \rb |יֶשׁ־\rb* \rb I have power to do|לַעֲשׂ֥וֹת\rb*\rb |לְאֵ֣ל\rb*\rb |יָדִ֔י\rb* \rb you|עִמָּכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb great harm|רָ֑ע\rb*, \rb but last night|אֶ֣מֶשׁ׀\rb* \rb the God|וֵֽאלֹהֵ֨י\rb* \rb of your father|אֲבִיכֶ֜ם\rb* \rb said|אָמַ֧ר\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֣י\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֗ר\rb*, ‘\rb Be careful|הִשָּׁ֧מֶר\rb* \rb not to say|מִדַּבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb anything to|עִֽם־\rb* \rb Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֖ב\rb*, \rb either good|מִטּ֥וֹב\rb* \rb or|עַד־\rb* \rb bad|רָֽע׃\rb*.’ \v 30 \rb Now|וְעַתָּה֙\rb* \rb you have gone off|הָלֹ֣ךְ\rb*\rb |הָלַ֔כְתָּ\rb* \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb you long|נִכְסֹ֥ף\rb*\rb |נִכְסַ֖פְתָּה\rb* \rb for your father’s|אָבִ֑יךָ\rb* \rb house|לְבֵ֣ית\rb*. \rb But why|לָ֥מָּה\rb* \rb have you stolen|גָנַ֖בְתָּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb my gods|אֱלֹהָֽי׃\rb*?”
\p \v 31 “\rb |כִּ֣י\rb* \rb I was afraid|יָרֵ֔אתִי\rb*,” \rb Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֖ב\rb* \rb answered|וַיַּ֥עַן\rb*, “\rb for|כִּ֣י\rb*\rb |אָמַ֔רְתִּי\rb*\rb |פֶּן־\rb* \rb I thought|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb you|לְלָבָ֑ן\rb* \rb would take your daughters|בְּנוֹתֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb from me|מֵעִמִּֽי׃\rb* \rb by force|תִּגְזֹ֥ל\rb*.\rb |אֶת־\rb* \v 32 \rb If you find|תִּמְצָ֣א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your gods|אֱלֹהֶיךָ֮\rb* \rb with|עִ֠ם\rb* \rb anyone here|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb*, \rb he shall not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb live|יִֽחְיֶה֒\rb*! \rb In the presence of|נֶ֣גֶד\rb* \rb our relatives|אַחֵ֧ינוּ\rb*, \rb see|הַֽכֶּר־\rb* \rb for yourself|לְךָ֛\rb* \rb if anything|מָ֥ה\rb* \rb is yours|עִמָּדִ֖י\rb*, \rb and take|וְקַֽח־\rb* \rb it back|לָ֑ךְ\rb*.” \rb For Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֔ב\rb* \rb did not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb know|יָדַ֣ע\rb* \rb that|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb Rachel|רָחֵ֖ל\rb* \rb had stolen the idols|גְּנָבָֽתַם׃\rb*.
\p \v 33 \rb So Laban|לָבָ֜ן\rb* \rb went|וַיָּבֹ֨א\rb* \rb into Jacob’s|יַעֲקֹ֣ב׀\rb* \rb tent|בְּאֹ֥הֶל\rb*, \rb then Leah’s|לֵאָ֗ה\rb* \rb tent|וּבְאֹ֣הֶל\rb*, \rb and then the tents|וּבְאֹ֛הֶל\rb* \rb of the two|שְׁתֵּ֥י\rb* \rb maidservants|הָאֲמָהֹ֖ת\rb*, \rb but he found|מָצָ֑א\rb* \rb nothing|וְלֹ֣א\rb*. \rb Then he left|וַיֵּצֵא֙\rb* \rb Leah’s|לֵאָ֔ה\rb* \rb tent|מֵאֹ֣הֶל\rb* \rb and entered|וַיָּבֹ֖א\rb* \rb Rachel’s|רָחֵֽל׃\rb* \rb tent|בְּאֹ֥הֶל\rb*. \v 34 \rb Now Rachel|וְרָחֵ֞ל\rb* \rb had taken|לָקְחָ֣ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Laban’s household idols|הַתְּרָפִ֗ים\rb*, \rb put them|וַתְּשִׂמֵ֛ם\rb* \rb in the saddlebag|בְּכַ֥ר\rb* \rb of her camel|הַגָּמָ֖ל\rb*, \rb and was sitting|וַתֵּ֣שֶׁב\rb* \rb on them|עֲלֵיהֶ֑ם\rb*. \rb And Laban|לָבָ֛ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb searched|וַיְמַשֵּׁ֥שׁ\rb* \rb everything|כָּל־\rb* \rb in the tent|הָאֹ֖הֶל\rb* \rb but found|מָצָֽא׃\rb* \rb nothing|וְלֹ֥א\rb*.
\p \v 35 \rb Rachel said|וַתֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb her father|אָבִ֗יהָ\rb*, “\rb Sir|אֲדֹנִ֔י\rb*, \rb do not|אַל־\rb* \rb be angry|יִ֙חַר֙\rb*\rb |בְּעֵינֵ֣י\rb* \rb that|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb I cannot|ל֤וֹא\rb*\rb |אוּכַל֙\rb* \rb stand up|לָק֣וּם\rb* \rb before you|מִפָּנֶ֔יךָ\rb*; \rb for|כִּי־\rb* \rb I am having my period|דֶ֥רֶךְ\rb*\rb |נָשִׁ֖ים\rb*.” \rb So Laban searched|וַיְחַפֵּ֕שׂ\rb* \rb but could not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb find|מָצָ֖א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the household idols|הַתְּרָפִֽים׃\rb*.
\p \v 36 \rb Then Jacob|לְיַעֲקֹ֖ב\rb* \rb became incensed|וַיִּ֥חַר\rb* \rb and challenged|וַיָּ֣רֶב\rb* \rb Laban|בְּלָבָ֑ן\rb*.\rb |וַיַּ֤עַן\rb* “\rb What|מַה־\rb* \rb is my crime|פִּשְׁעִי֙\rb*?” \rb he|יַעֲקֹב֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*.\rb |לְלָבָ֔ן\rb* “\rb For what|מַ֣ה\rb* \rb sin of mine|חַטָּאתִ֔י\rb*\rb |כִּ֥י\rb* \rb have you so hotly pursued|דָלַ֖קְתָּ\rb* \rb me|אַחֲרָֽי׃\rb*? \v 37 \rb |כִּֽי־\rb* \rb You have searched|מִשַּׁ֣שְׁתָּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb my goods|כֵּלַ֗י\rb*!\rb |מַה־\rb* \rb Have you found|מָּצָ֙אתָ֙\rb* \rb anything|מִכֹּ֣ל\rb* \rb that belongs to you|כְּלֵי־\rb*?\rb |בֵיתֶ֔ךָ\rb* \rb Put|שִׂ֣ים\rb* \rb it here|כֹּ֔ה\rb* \rb before|נֶ֥גֶד\rb* \rb my brothers|אַחַ֖י\rb* \rb and yours|וְאַחֶ֑יךָ\rb*, \rb that they may judge|וְיוֹכִ֖יחוּ\rb* \rb between|בֵּ֥ין\rb* \rb the two of us|שְׁנֵֽינוּ׃\rb*.
\p \v 38 \rb I have|אָנֹכִי֙\rb* \rb been with|עִמָּ֔ךְ\rb* \rb you for|זֶה֩\rb* \rb twenty|עֶשְׂרִ֨ים\rb* \rb years now|שָׁנָ֤ה\rb*. \rb Your sheep|רְחֵלֶ֥יךָ\rb* \rb and goats|וְעִזֶּ֖יךָ\rb* \rb have not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb miscarried|שִׁכֵּ֑לוּ\rb*, \rb nor have I|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb eaten|אָכָֽלְתִּי׃\rb* \rb the rams|וְאֵילֵ֥י\rb* \rb of your flock|צֹאנְךָ֖\rb*. \v 39 \rb I did not|לֹא־\rb* \rb bring|הֵבֵ֣אתִי\rb* \rb you|אֵלֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb anything torn by wild beasts|טְרֵפָה֙\rb*; \rb I|אָנֹכִ֣י\rb* \rb bore the loss myself|אֲחַטֶּ֔נָּה\rb*. \rb And you demanded|תְּבַקְשֶׁ֑נָּה\rb* \rb payment from me|מִיָּדִ֖י\rb* \rb for what was stolen|גְּנֻֽבְתִ֣י\rb* \rb by day|י֔וֹם\rb*\rb |וּגְנֻֽבְתִ֖י\rb* \rb or night|לָֽיְלָה׃\rb*. \v 40 \rb As it was|הָיִ֧יתִי\rb*, \rb the heat|חֹ֖רֶב\rb* \rb consumed me|אֲכָלַ֥נִי\rb* \rb by day|בַיּ֛וֹם\rb* \rb and the frost|וְקֶ֣רַח\rb* \rb by night|בַּלָּ֑יְלָה\rb*, \rb and sleep|שְׁנָתִ֖י\rb* \rb fled|וַתִּדַּ֥ד\rb* \rb from my eyes|מֵֽעֵינָֽי׃\rb*.
\p \v 41 \rb Thus|זֶה־\rb*\rb |לִּ֞י\rb* \rb for twenty|עֶשְׂרִ֣ים\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָה֮\rb* \rb I have served|עֲבַדְתִּ֜יךָ\rb* \rb in your household|בְּבֵיתֶךָ֒\rb*— \rb fourteen|אַרְבַּֽע־\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵ֤ה\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָה֙\rb* \rb for your two|בִּשְׁתֵּ֣י\rb* \rb daughters|בְנֹתֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb and six|וְשֵׁ֥שׁ\rb* \rb years|שָׁנִ֖ים\rb* \rb for your flocks|בְּצֹאנֶ֑ךָ\rb*— \rb and you have changed|וַתַּחֲלֵ֥ף\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb my wages|מַשְׂכֻּרְתִּ֖י\rb* \rb ten|עֲשֶׂ֥רֶת\rb* \rb times|מֹנִֽים׃\rb*! \v 42 \rb If the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of my father|אָבִי֩\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֨י\rb* \rb of Abraham|אַבְרָהָ֜ם\rb* \rb and the Fear|וּפַ֤חַד\rb* \rb of Isaac|יִצְחָק֙\rb*, \rb had not|לוּלֵ֡י\rb* \rb been|הָ֣יָה\rb* \rb with me|לִ֔י\rb*, \rb surely|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb by now|עַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb you would have sent me away|שִׁלַּחְתָּ֑נִי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb empty-handed|רֵיקָ֣ם\rb*. \rb But God|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb has seen|רָאָ֥ה\rb* \rb my affliction|עָנְיִ֞י\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and the toil|יְגִ֧יעַ\rb* \rb of my hands|כַּפַּ֛י\rb*, \rb and last night|אָֽמֶשׁ׃\rb* \rb He rendered judgment|וַיּ֥וֹכַח\rb*.”
\s1 Jacob’s Covenant with Laban
\p \v 43 \rb But Laban|לָבָ֜ן\rb*\rb |וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֶֽל־\rb* \rb answered|וַיַּ֨עַן\rb* \rb Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֗ב\rb*, “\rb These daughters|הַבָּנ֨וֹת\rb* \rb are my daughters|בְּנֹתַ֜י\rb*, \rb these sons|וְהַבָּנִ֤ים\rb* \rb are my sons|בָּנַי֙\rb*, \rb and these flocks|וְהַצֹּ֣אן\rb* \rb are my flocks|צֹאנִ֔י\rb*! \rb Everything|וְכֹ֛ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb you|אַתָּ֥ה\rb* \rb see|רֹאֶ֖ה\rb* \rb is|ה֑וּא\rb* \rb mine|לִי־\rb*! \rb Yet what|מָֽה־\rb* \rb can I do|אֶֽעֱשֶׂ֤ה\rb* \rb today|הַיּ֔וֹם\rb* \rb about these|לָאֵ֙לֶּה֙\rb* \rb daughters|וְלִבְנֹתַ֞י\rb* \rb of mine or|א֥וֹ\rb* \rb the children|לִבְנֵיהֶ֖ן\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb they have borne|יָלָֽדוּ׃\rb*? \v 44 \rb Come|לְכָ֛ה\rb* \rb now|וְעַתָּ֗ה\rb*, \rb let us make|נִכְרְתָ֥ה\rb* \rb a covenant|בְרִ֖ית\rb*, \rb you|וָאָ֑תָּה\rb* \rb and I|אֲנִ֣י\rb*, \rb and let it serve as|וְהָיָ֥ה\rb* \rb a witness|לְעֵ֖ד\rb* \rb between you and me|בֵּינִ֥י\rb*\rb |וּבֵינֶֽךָ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 45 \rb So Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֖ב\rb* \rb picked out|וַיִּקַּ֥ח\rb* \rb a stone|אָ֑בֶן\rb* \rb and set it up|וַיְרִימֶ֖הָ\rb* \rb as a pillar|מַצֵּבָֽה׃\rb*, \v 46 \rb and he|יַעֲקֹ֤ב\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to his relatives|לְאֶחָיו֙\rb*, “\rb Gather|לִקְט֣וּ\rb* \rb some stones|אֲבָנִ֔ים\rb*.” \rb So they took|וַיִּקְח֥וּ\rb* \rb stones|אֲבָנִ֖ים\rb* \rb and made|וַיַּֽעֲשׂוּ־\rb* \rb a mound|גָ֑ל\rb*, \rb and there|שָׁ֖ם\rb* \rb by|עַל־\rb* \rb the mound|הַגָּֽל׃\rb* \rb they ate|וַיֹּ֥אכְלוּ\rb*. \v 47 \rb Laban|לָבָ֔ן\rb* \rb called it|וַיִּקְרָא־\rb*\rb |ל֣וֹ\rb*\rb |יְגַ֖ר\rb* \rb Jegar-sahadutha|שָׂהֲדוּתָ֑א\rb*, \rb and Jacob|וְיַֽעֲקֹ֔ב\rb* \rb called it|קָ֥רָא\rb*\rb |ל֖וֹ\rb* \rb Galeed|גַּלְעֵֽד׃\rb*.\f + \fr 31:47 \ft The Aramaic \fqa Jegar-sahadutha \ft and the Hebrew \fqa Galeed \ft both mean \fqa heap of witnesses\ft .\f*
\p \v 48 \rb Then Laban|לָבָ֔ן\rb* \rb declared|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb This|הַזֶּ֥ה\rb* \rb mound|הַגַּ֨ל\rb* \rb is a witness|עֵ֛ד\rb* \rb between you|בֵּינִ֥י\rb* \rb and me|וּבֵינְךָ֖\rb* \rb this day|הַיּ֑וֹם\rb*.”
\p \rb Therefore|עַל־\rb*\rb |כֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb the place was called|קָרָֽא־\rb*\rb |שְׁמ֖וֹ\rb* \rb Galeed|גַּלְעֵֽד׃\rb*. \v 49 \rb It was also called Mizpah|וְהַמִּצְפָּה֙\rb*,\f + \fr 31:49 \fqa Mizpah \ft means \fqa watchtower\ft .\f* \rb because|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb Laban said|אָמַ֔ר\rb*, “\rb May the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb keep watch|יִ֥צֶף\rb* \rb between you|בֵּינִ֣י\rb* \rb and me|וּבֵינֶ֑ךָ\rb* \rb when|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb we are absent|נִסָּתֵ֖ר\rb* \rb from each other|מֵרֵעֵֽהוּ׃\rb*\rb |אִ֥ישׁ\rb*. \v 50 \rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb you mistreat|תְּעַנֶּ֣ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb my daughters|בְּנֹתַ֗י\rb* \rb or|וְאִם־\rb* \rb take|תִּקַּ֤ח\rb* \rb other|עַל־\rb*\rb |בְּנֹתַ֔י\rb* \rb wives|נָשִׁים֙\rb*, \rb although no|אֵ֥ין\rb* \rb one|אִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb is with us|עִמָּ֑נוּ\rb*, \rb remember|רְאֵ֕ה\rb* \rb that God|אֱלֹהִ֥ים\rb* \rb is a witness|עֵ֖ד\rb* \rb between you and me|בֵּינִ֥י\rb*\rb |וּבֵינֶֽךָ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 51 \rb Laban|לָבָ֖ן\rb* \rb also said|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb* \rb to Jacob|לְיַעֲקֹ֑ב\rb*, “\rb Here is|הִנֵּ֣ה׀\rb* \rb the|הַזֶּ֗ה\rb*\rb |וְהִנֵּה֙\rb* \rb mound|הַגַּ֣ל\rb*, \rb and here is the pillar|הַמַצֵּבָ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I have set up|יָרִ֖יתִי\rb* \rb between you and me|בֵּינִ֥י\rb*\rb |וּבֵינֶֽךָ׃\rb*. \v 52 \rb This|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb mound|הַגַּ֣ל\rb* \rb is a witness|עֵ֚ד\rb*, \rb and this pillar|הַמַּצֵּבָ֑ה\rb* \rb is a witness|וְעֵדָ֖ה\rb*, \rb that|אִם־\rb* \rb I|אָ֗נִי\rb* \rb will not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb go past|אֶֽעֱבֹ֤ר\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb*\rb |וְאִם־\rb* \rb mound|הַגַּ֣ל\rb* \rb to harm you|אֵלֶ֙יךָ֙\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb and you|אַ֠תָּה\rb* \rb will not|לֹא־\rb* \rb go past|תַעֲבֹ֨ר\rb*\rb |אֵלַ֜י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֛ה\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb mound|הַגַּ֥ל\rb* \rb and|הַזֹּ֖את\rb* \rb pillar|הַמַּצֵּבָ֥ה\rb* \rb to harm me|לְרָעָֽה׃\rb*. \v 53 \rb May the God|אֱלֹהֵ֨י\rb* \rb of Abraham|אַבְרָהָ֜ם\rb* \rb and the God|וֵֽאלֹהֵ֤י\rb* \rb of Nahor|נָחוֹר֙\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֖י\rb* \rb of their father|אֲבִיהֶ֑ם\rb*, \rb judge|יִשְׁפְּט֣וּ\rb* \rb between us|בֵינֵ֔ינוּ\rb*.”
\p \rb So Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֔ב\rb* \rb swore|וַיִּשָּׁבַ֣ע\rb* \rb by the Fear|בְּפַ֖חַד\rb* \rb of his father|אָבִ֥יו\rb* \rb Isaac|יִצְחָֽק׃\rb*.
\p \v 54 \rb Then Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֥ב\rb* \rb offered|וַיִּזְבַּ֨ח\rb* \rb a sacrifice|זֶ֙בַח֙\rb* \rb on the mountain|בָּהָ֔ר\rb* \rb and invited|וַיִּקְרָ֥א\rb* \rb his relatives|לְאֶחָ֖יו\rb* \rb to eat|לֶאֱכָל־\rb* \rb a meal|לָ֑חֶם\rb*. \rb And after they had eaten|וַיֹּ֣אכְלוּ\rb*\rb |לֶ֔חֶם\rb*, \rb they spent the night|וַיָּלִ֖ינוּ\rb* \rb on the mountain|בָּהָֽר׃\rb*. \v 55 \rb Early the next morning|בַּבֹּ֗קֶר\rb*, \rb Laban|לָבָ֜ן\rb* \rb got up|וַיַּשְׁכֵּ֨ם\rb* \rb and kissed|וַיְנַשֵּׁ֧ק\rb* \rb his grandchildren|לְבָנָ֛יו\rb* \rb and daughters|וְלִבְנוֹתָ֖יו\rb* \rb and blessed them|וַיְבָ֣רֶךְ\rb*.\rb |אֶתְהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb Then he|לָבָ֖ן\rb* \rb left|וַיֵּ֛לֶךְ\rb* \rb to return|וַיָּ֥שָׁב\rb* \rb home|לִמְקֹמֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\c 32
\s1 Jacob Prepares to Meet Esau
\p \v 1 \rb Jacob also|וְיַעֲקֹ֖ב\rb* \rb went|הָלַ֣ךְ\rb* \rb on his way|לְדַרְכּ֑וֹ\rb*, \rb and the angels|מַלְאֲכֵ֥י\rb* \rb of God|אֱלֹהִֽים׃\rb* \rb met|וַיִּפְגְּעוּ־\rb* \rb him|ב֖וֹ\rb*. \v 2 \rb When|כַּאֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb Jacob saw them|רָאָ֔ם\rb*, \rb he|יַעֲקֹב֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb*, “\rb This|זֶ֑ה\rb* \rb is the camp|מַחֲנֵ֥ה\rb* \rb of God|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb*.” \rb So he named|וַיִּקְרָ֛א\rb*\rb |שֵֽׁם־\rb* \rb that|הַה֖וּא\rb* \rb place|הַמָּק֥וֹם\rb* \rb Mahanaim|מַֽחֲנָֽיִם׃פ\rb*.\f + \fr 32:2 \fqa Mahanaim \ft means \fqa two camps\ft .\f*
\p \v 3 \rb Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֤ב\rb* \rb sent|וַיִּשְׁלַ֨ח\rb* \rb messengers|מַלְאָכִים֙\rb* \rb ahead of him|לְפָנָ֔יו\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his brother|אָחִ֑יו\rb* \rb Esau|עֵשָׂ֖ו\rb* \rb in the land|אַ֥רְצָה\rb* \rb of Seir|שֵׂעִ֖יר\rb*, \rb the country|שְׂדֵ֥ה\rb* \rb of Edom|אֱדֽוֹם׃\rb*. \v 4 \rb He instructed them|וַיְצַ֤ו\rb*,\rb |אֹתָם֙\rb* “\rb You are to say|לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb*\rb |כֹּ֣ה\rb*\rb |תֹאמְר֔וּן\rb* \rb to my master|לַֽאדֹנִ֖י\rb* \rb Esau|לְעֵשָׂ֑ו\rb*\rb |כֹּ֤ה\rb*, ‘\rb Your servant|עַבְדְּךָ֣\rb* \rb Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֔ב\rb* \rb says|אָמַר֙\rb*: \rb I have been staying|גַּ֔רְתִּי\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb Laban|לָבָ֣ן\rb* \rb and have remained there|וָאֵחַ֖ר\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb now|עָֽתָּה׃\rb*. \v 5 \rb I have|וַֽיְהִי־\rb* \rb oxen|שׁ֣וֹר\rb*, \rb donkeys|וַחֲמ֔וֹר\rb*, \rb flocks|צֹ֖אן\rb*, \rb menservants|וְעֶ֣בֶד\rb*, \rb and maidservants|וְשִׁפְחָ֑ה\rb*. \rb I have sent|וָֽאֶשְׁלְחָה֙\rb* \rb this message to inform|לְהַגִּ֣יד\rb* \rb my master|לַֽאדֹנִ֔י\rb*, \rb so that I may find|לִמְצֹא־\rb* \rb favor|חֵ֖ן\rb* \rb in your sight|בְּעֵינֶֽיךָ׃\rb*.’”
\p \v 6 \rb When the messengers|הַמַּלְאָכִ֔ים\rb* \rb returned|וַיָּשֻׁ֙בוּ֙\rb* \rb to|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֖ב\rb*, \rb they said|לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*, “\rb We went|בָּ֤אנוּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb your brother|אָחִ֙יךָ֙\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb Esau|עֵשָׂ֔ו\rb*, \rb and now|וְגַם֙\rb* \rb he is coming|הֹלֵ֣ךְ\rb* \rb to meet you|לִקְרָֽאתְךָ֔\rb*— \rb he and four|וְאַרְבַּע־\rb* \rb hundred|מֵא֥וֹת\rb* \rb men|אִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb with him|עִמּֽוֹ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 7 \rb In great|מְאֹ֖ד\rb* \rb fear|וַיִּירָ֧א\rb* \rb and distress|וַיֵּ֣צֶר\rb*, \rb Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֛ב\rb* \rb divided|וַיַּ֜חַץ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb his|אִתּ֗וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb people|הָעָ֣ם\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb into two|לִשְׁנֵ֥י\rb* \rb camps|מַחֲנֽוֹת׃\rb*, \rb as well as the flocks|הַצֹּ֧אן\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and herds|הַבָּקָ֛ר\rb* \rb and camels|וְהַגְּמַלִּ֖ים\rb*. \v 8 \rb He thought|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*, “\rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb Esau|עֵשָׂ֛ו\rb* \rb comes|יָב֥וֹא\rb* \rb and attacks|וְהִכָּ֑הוּ\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb one|הָאַחַ֖ת\rb* \rb camp|הַמַּחֲנֶ֥ה\rb*, \rb then|וְהָיָ֛ה\rb* \rb the other|הַנִּשְׁאָ֖ר\rb* \rb camp|הַמַּחֲנֶ֥ה\rb* \rb can escape|לִפְלֵיטָֽה׃\rb*.”
\p \v 9 \rb Then Jacob|יַעֲקֹב֒\rb* \rb declared|וַיֹּאמֶר֮\rb*, “\rb O God|אֱלֹהֵי֙\rb* \rb of my father|אָבִ֣י\rb* \rb Abraham|אַבְרָהָ֔ם\rb*, \rb God|וֵאלֹהֵ֖י\rb* \rb of my father|אָבִ֣י\rb* \rb Isaac|יִצְחָ֑ק\rb*, \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֞ה\rb* \rb who told|הָאֹמֵ֣ר\rb* \rb me|אֵלַ֗י\rb*, ‘\rb Go back|שׁ֧וּב\rb* \rb to your country|לְאַרְצְךָ֛\rb* \rb and to your kindred|וּלְמוֹלַדְתְּךָ֖\rb*, \rb and I will make you prosper|וְאֵיטִ֥יבָה\rb*,’\rb |עִמָּֽךְ׃\rb* \v 10 \rb I am unworthy|קָטֹ֜נְתִּי\rb* \rb of all|מִכֹּ֤ל\rb* \rb the kindness|הַחֲסָדִים֙\rb*\rb |וּמִכָּל־\rb* \rb and faithfulness|הָ֣אֱמֶ֔ת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb You have shown|עָשִׂ֖יתָ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Your servant|עַבְדֶּ֑ךָ\rb*. \rb Indeed|כִּ֣י\rb*, \rb with only my staff|בְמַקְלִ֗י\rb* \rb I came across|עָבַ֙רְתִּי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּ֣ן\rb*, \rb but now|וְעַתָּ֥ה\rb* \rb I have become|הָיִ֖יתִי\rb* \rb two|לִשְׁנֵ֥י\rb* \rb camps|מַחֲנֽוֹת׃\rb*. \v 11 \rb Please|נָ֛א\rb* \rb deliver me|הַצִּילֵ֥נִי\rb* \rb from the hand|מִיַּ֥ד\rb* \rb of my brother|אָחִ֖י\rb*\rb |מִיַּ֣ד\rb* \rb Esau|עֵשָׂ֑ו\rb*, \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I|אָנֹכִי֙\rb*\rb |אֹת֔וֹ\rb* \rb am afraid that|יָרֵ֤א\rb*\rb |פֶּן־\rb* \rb he may come|יָב֣וֹא\rb* \rb and attack me|וְהִכַּ֔נִי\rb* \rb and the mothers|אֵ֖ם\rb* \rb and|עַל־\rb* \rb children with me|בָּנִֽים׃\rb*. \v 12 \rb But You|וְאַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb have said|אָמַ֔רְתָּ\rb*, ‘\rb I will surely make you prosper|הֵיטֵ֥ב\rb*\rb |אֵיטִ֖יב\rb*\rb |עִמָּ֑ךְ\rb*, \rb and I will make|וְשַׂמְתִּ֤י\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb your offspring|זַרְעֲךָ֙\rb* \rb like the sand|כְּח֣וֹל\rb* \rb of the sea|הַיָּ֔ם\rb*,\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb*\rb |לֹא־\rb* \rb too numerous|מֵרֹֽב׃\rb* \rb to count|יִסָּפֵ֖ר\rb*.’”
\p \v 13 \rb Jacob spent|וַיָּ֥לֶן\rb* \rb the|הַה֑וּא\rb* \rb night|בַּלַּ֣יְלָה\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֖ם\rb*, \rb and from what he had brought|הַבָּ֧א\rb* \rb with him|בְיָד֛וֹ\rb*, \rb he selected|וַיִּקַּ֞ח\rb*\rb |מִן־\rb* \rb a gift|מִנְחָ֖ה\rb* \rb for his brother|אָחִֽיו׃\rb* \rb Esau|לְעֵשָׂ֥ו\rb*: \v 14 \rb 200|מָאתַ֔יִם\rb* \rb female goats|עִזִּ֣ים\rb*, \rb 20|עֶשְׂרִ֑ים\rb* \rb male goats|וּתְיָשִׁ֖ים\rb*, \rb 200|מָאתַ֖יִם\rb* \rb ewes|רְחֵלִ֥ים\rb*, \rb 20|עֶשְׂרִֽים׃\rb* \rb rams|וְאֵילִ֥ים\rb*, \v 15 \rb 30|שְׁלֹשִׁ֑ים\rb* \rb milk|מֵינִיק֛וֹת\rb* \rb camels|גְּמַלִּ֧ים\rb* \rb with their young|וּבְנֵיהֶ֖ם\rb*, \rb 40|אַרְבָּעִים֙\rb* \rb cows|פָּר֤וֹת\rb*, \rb 10|עֲשָׂרָ֔ה\rb* \rb bulls|וּפָרִ֣ים\rb*, \rb 20|עֶשְׂרִ֔ים\rb* \rb female donkeys|אֲתֹנֹ֣ת\rb*, \rb and 10|עֲשָׂרָֽה׃\rb* \rb male donkeys|וַעְיָרִ֖ם\rb*. \v 16 \rb He entrusted them to|וַיִּתֵּן֙\rb*\rb |בְּיַד־\rb* \rb his servants|עֲבָדָ֔יו\rb* \rb in separate|לְבַדּ֑וֹ\rb* \rb herds|עֵ֥דֶר\rb*\rb |עֵ֖דֶר\rb* \rb and told|וַ֤יֹּאמֶר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb them|עֲבָדָיו֙\rb*, “\rb Go on|עִבְר֣וּ\rb* \rb ahead of me|לְפָנַ֔י\rb*, \rb and keep|תָּשִׂ֔ימוּ\rb* \rb some distance|וְרֶ֣וַח\rb* \rb between|בֵּ֥ין\rb* \rb the herds|עֵ֖דֶר\rb*\rb |וּבֵ֥ין\rb*\rb |עֵֽדֶר׃\rb*.”
\p \v 17 \rb He instructed|וַיְצַ֥ו\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the one in the lead|הָרִאשׁ֖וֹן\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*, “\rb When|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb my brother|אָחִ֗י\rb* \rb Esau|עֵשָׂ֣ו\rb* \rb meets|יִֽפְגָּשְׁךָ֞\rb* \rb you and asks|וִשְׁאֵֽלְךָ֙\rb*,\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* ‘\rb To whom|לְמִי־\rb* \rb do you belong|אַ֙תָּה֙\rb*, \rb where|וְאָ֣נָה\rb* \rb are you going|תֵלֵ֔ךְ\rb*, \rb and whose|וּלְמִ֖י\rb* \rb animals are these|אֵ֥לֶּה\rb* \rb before you|לְפָנֶֽיךָ׃\rb*?’ \v 18 \rb then you are to say|וְאָֽמַרְתָּ֙\rb*, ‘\rb They belong to your servant|לְעַבְדְּךָ֣\rb* \rb Jacob|לְיַעֲקֹ֔ב\rb*. \rb They|הִוא֙\rb* \rb are a gift|מִנְחָ֥ה\rb*, \rb sent|שְׁלוּחָ֔ה\rb* \rb to my lord|לַֽאדֹנִ֖י\rb* \rb Esau|לְעֵשָׂ֑ו\rb*. \rb And behold|וְהִנֵּ֥ה\rb*,\rb |גַם־\rb* \rb Jacob|ה֖וּא\rb* \rb is behind us|אַחֲרֵֽינוּ׃\rb*.’”
\p \v 19 \rb He also|גַּ֣ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb instructed|וַיְצַ֞ו\rb* \rb the second|הַשֵּׁנִ֗י\rb*, \rb the third|הַשְּׁלִישִׁ֔י\rb*,\rb |גַּ֚ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb and|גַּ֚ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all those|כָּל־\rb* \rb following|הַהֹ֣לְכִ֔ים\rb* \rb behind|אַחֲרֵ֥י\rb* \rb the herds|הָעֲדָרִ֖ים\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*: “\rb When you meet|בְּמֹצַאֲכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb Esau|עֵשָׂ֔ו\rb*, \rb you are to say|תְּדַבְּר֣וּן\rb* \rb the same|הַזֶּה֙\rb* \rb thing|כַּדָּבָ֤ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb him|אֹתֽוֹ׃\rb*. \v 20 \rb You are also|גַּ֗ם\rb* \rb to say|וַאֲמַרְתֶּ֕ם\rb*, ‘\rb Look|הִנֵּ֛ה\rb*, \rb your servant|עַבְדְּךָ֥\rb* \rb Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֖ב\rb* \rb is right behind us|אַחֲרֵ֑ינוּ\rb*.’” \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb he thought|אָמַ֞ר\rb*, “\rb I will appease|אֲכַפְּרָ֣ה\rb* \rb Esau|פָנָ֗יו\rb*\f + \fr 32:20 \ft Or \fqa I will appease his face\f* \rb with the gift|בַּמִּנְחָה֙\rb* \rb that is going|הַהֹלֶ֣כֶת\rb* \rb before me|לְפָנָ֔י\rb*. \rb After|וְאַחֲרֵי־\rb* \rb that|כֵן֙\rb* \rb I can face|אֶרְאֶ֣ה\rb* \rb him|פָנָ֔יו\rb*, \rb and perhaps|אוּלַ֖י\rb* \rb he will accept|יִשָּׂ֥א\rb* \rb me|פָנָֽי׃\rb*.\f + \fr 32:20 \ft Literally \fqa perhaps he will lift up my face\f*”
\p \v 21 \rb So Jacob’s gifts|הַמִּנְחָ֖ה\rb* \rb went|וַתַּעֲבֹ֥ר\rb* \rb on before|עַל־\rb* \rb him|פָּנָ֑יו\rb*, \rb while he|וְה֛וּא\rb* \rb spent|לָ֥ן\rb* \rb the|הַה֖וּא\rb* \rb night|בַּלַּֽיְלָה־\rb* \rb in the camp|בַּֽמַּחֲנֶֽה׃\rb*.
\s1 Jacob Wrestles with God
\p \v 22 \rb During the night|בַּלַּ֣יְלָה\rb*\rb |ה֗וּא\rb* \rb Jacob got up|וַיָּ֣קָם׀\rb* \rb and took|וַיִּקַּ֞ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his two|שְׁתֵּ֤י\rb* \rb wives|נָשָׁיו֙\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb his two|שְׁתֵּ֣י\rb* \rb maidservants|שִׁפְחֹתָ֔יו\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and his eleven|אַחַ֥ד\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֖ר\rb* \rb sons|יְלָדָ֑יו\rb*, \rb and crossed|וַֽיַּעֲבֹ֔ר\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb the ford|מַעֲבַ֥ר\rb* \rb of the Jabbok|יַבֹּֽק׃\rb*. \v 23 \rb He took them|וַיִּקָּחֵ֔ם\rb* \rb and sent them across|וַיַּֽעֲבִרֵ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the stream|הַנָּ֑חַל\rb*,\rb |וַֽיַּעֲבֵ֖ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb along with all his possessions|אֲשֶׁר־\rb*.
\p \v 24 \rb So Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֖ב\rb* \rb was left|וַיִּוָּתֵ֥ר\rb* \rb all alone|לְבַדּ֑וֹ\rb*, \rb and there a man|אִישׁ֙\rb*\f + \fr 32:24 \ft Or \fqa Man\ft ; here and in verses 25–28; corresponding pronouns may also be capitalized\f* \rb wrestled|וַיֵּאָבֵ֥ק\rb* \rb with him|עִמּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb until|עַ֖ד\rb* \rb daybreak|עֲל֥וֹת\rb*\rb |הַשָּֽׁחַר׃\rb*. \v 25 \rb When the man saw|וַיַּ֗רְא\rb* \rb that|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb he could not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb overpower|יָכֹל֙\rb* \rb Jacob|ל֔וֹ\rb*, \rb he struck|וַיִּגַּ֖ע\rb* \rb the socket|בְּכַף־\rb* \rb of Jacob’s hip|יְרֵכ֑וֹ\rb* \rb and dislocated|וַתֵּ֙קַע֙\rb*\rb |כַּף־\rb* \rb it|יַעֲקֹ֔ב\rb*\rb |יֶ֣רֶךְ\rb* \rb as they|עִמּֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb wrestled|בְּהֵֽאָבְק֖וֹ\rb*. \v 26 \rb Then the man said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Let me go|שַׁלְּחֵ֔נִי\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb it is daybreak|עָלָ֖ה\rb*\rb |הַשָּׁ֑חַר\rb*.”
\p \rb But Jacob replied|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb*, “\rb I will not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb let you go|אֲשַֽׁלֵּחֲךָ֔\rb* \rb unless|כִּ֖י\rb*\rb |אִם־\rb* \rb you bless me|בֵּרַכְתָּֽנִי׃\rb*.”
\p \v 27 “\rb What|מַה־\rb* \rb is your name|שְּׁמֶ֑ךָ\rb*?” \rb the man asked|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb*.\rb |אֵלָ֖יו\rb*
\p “\rb Jacob|יַעֲקֹֽב׃\rb*,” \rb he replied|וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb*.
\p \v 28 \rb Then the man said|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Your name|שִׁמְךָ֔\rb* \rb will no|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb longer|עוֹד֙\rb* \rb be|יֵאָמֵ֥ר\rb* \rb Jacob|יַעֲקֹב֙\rb*,\f + \fr 32:28 \fqa Jacob \ft means \fqa he grasps the heel \ft or \fqa he deceives\ft .\f* \rb but Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*\rb |כִּֽי־\rb*,\f + \fr 32:28 \fqa Israel \ft means \fqa he struggles with God\ft .\f* \rb because|כִּ֖י\rb*\rb |אִם־\rb* \rb you have struggled|שָׂרִ֧יתָ\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֛ים\rb* \rb and with|וְעִם־\rb* \rb men|אֲנָשִׁ֖ים\rb*, \rb and you have prevailed|וַתּוּכָֽל׃\rb*.”
\p \v 29 \rb And Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֗ב\rb* \rb requested|וַיִּשְׁאַ֣ל\rb*\rb |וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb*, “\rb Please|נָּ֣א\rb* \rb tell me|הַגִּֽידָה־\rb* \rb your name|שְׁמֶ֔ךָ\rb*.”
\p \rb But he replied|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Why|לָ֥מָּה\rb*\rb |זֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb do you ask|תִּשְׁאַ֣ל\rb* \rb my name|לִשְׁמִ֑י\rb*?” \rb Then he blessed|וַיְבָ֥רֶךְ\rb* \rb Jacob|אֹת֖וֹ\rb* \rb there|שָֽׁם׃\rb*.
\p \v 30 \rb So Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֛ב\rb* \rb named|וַיִּקְרָ֧א\rb*\rb |שֵׁ֥ם\rb* \rb the place|הַמָּק֖וֹם\rb* \rb Peniel|פְּנִיאֵ֑ל\rb*,\f + \fr 32:30 \fqa Peniel \ft means \fqa the face of God\ft .\f* \rb saying, “Indeed|כִּֽי־\rb*, \rb I have seen|רָאִ֤יתִי\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִים֙\rb* \rb face|פָּנִ֣ים\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb face|פָּנִ֔ים\rb*, \rb and yet my life|נַפְשִֽׁי׃\rb* \rb was spared|וַתִּנָּצֵ֖ל\rb*.”
\p \v 31 \rb The sun|הַשֶּׁ֔מֶשׁ\rb* \rb rose|וַיִּֽזְרַֽח־\rb* \rb above him|ל֣וֹ\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb he passed by|עָבַ֖ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Penuel|פְּנוּאֵ֑ל\rb*,\f + \fr 32:31 \fqa Penuel \ft is a variant of \fqa Peniel\ft ; see verse 30.\f* \rb and he|וְה֥וּא\rb* \rb was limping|צֹלֵ֖עַ\rb* \rb because of|עַל־\rb* \rb his hip|יְרֵכֽוֹ׃\rb*. \v 32 \rb Therefore|עַל־\rb*\rb |כֵּ֡ן\rb* \rb to|עַ֖ד\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb day|הַיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֜ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb do not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb eat|יֹאכְל֨וּ\rb* \rb the tendon|גִּ֣יד\rb*\rb |הַנָּשֶׁ֗ה\rb* \rb attached|אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb the socket|כַּ֣ף\rb* \rb of the hip|הַיָּרֵ֔ךְ\rb*, \rb because|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb the socket|בְּכַף־\rb* \rb of Jacob’s|יַעֲקֹ֔ב\rb* \rb hip|יֶ֣רֶךְ\rb* \rb was struck|נָגַע֙\rb* \rb near that tendon|בְּגִ֖יד\rb*\rb |הַנָּשֶֽׁה׃\rb*.
\c 33
\s1 Jacob Meets Esau
\p \v 1 \rb Now Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֜ב\rb* \rb looked up|וַיִּשָּׂ֨א\rb*\rb |עֵינָ֗יו\rb* \rb and saw|וַיַּרְא֙\rb*\rb |וְהִנֵּ֣ה\rb* \rb Esau|עֵשָׂ֣ו\rb* \rb coming|בָּ֔א\rb* \rb toward him with|וְעִמּ֕וֹ\rb* \rb four|אַרְבַּ֥ע\rb* \rb hundred|מֵא֖וֹת\rb* \rb men|אִ֑ישׁ\rb*. \rb So he divided|וַיַּ֣חַץ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the children|הַיְלָדִ֗ים\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb among Leah|לֵאָה֙\rb*,\rb |וְעַל־\rb* \rb Rachel|רָחֵ֔ל\rb*,\rb |וְעַ֖ל\rb* \rb and the two|שְׁתֵּ֥י\rb* \rb maidservants|הַשְּׁפָחֽוֹת׃\rb*. \v 2 \rb He put|וַיָּ֧שֶׂם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the maidservants|הַשְּׁפָח֛וֹת\rb* \rb and their|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb children|יַלְדֵיהֶ֖ן\rb* \rb in front|רִֽאשֹׁנָ֑ה\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Leah|לֵאָ֤ה\rb* \rb and her children|וִֽילָדֶ֙יהָ֙\rb* \rb next|אַחֲרֹנִ֔ים\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and Rachel|רָחֵ֥ל\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and Joseph|יוֹסֵ֖ף\rb* \rb at the rear|אַחֲרֹנִֽים׃\rb*. \v 3 \rb But Jacob himself|וְה֖וּא\rb* \rb went on|עָבַ֣ר\rb* \rb ahead|לִפְנֵיהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb and bowed|וַיִּשְׁתַּ֤חוּ\rb* \rb to the ground|אַ֙רְצָה֙\rb* \rb seven|שֶׁ֣בַע\rb* \rb times|פְּעָמִ֔ים\rb* \rb as|עַד־\rb* \rb he approached|גִּשְׁתּ֖וֹ\rb*\rb |עַד־\rb* \rb his brother|אָחִֽיו׃\rb*.
\p \v 4 \rb Esau, however|עֵשָׂ֤ו\rb*,\rb |לִקְרָאתוֹ֙\rb* \rb ran to him|וַיָּ֨רָץ\rb* \rb and embraced him|וַֽיְחַבְּקֵ֔הוּ\rb*, \rb threw his arms around|וַיִּפֹּ֥ל\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb his neck|צַוָּארָ֖ו\rb*, \rb and kissed him|וַׄיִּׄשָּׁׄקֵ֑ׄהׄוּׄ\rb*. \rb And they both wept|וַיִּבְכּֽוּ׃\rb*.
\p \v 5 \rb When Esau looked up|וַיִּשָּׂ֣א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |עֵינָ֗יו\rb* \rb and saw|וַיַּ֤רְא\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the women|הַנָּשִׁים֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and children|הַיְלָדִ֔ים\rb*, \rb he asked|וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Who|מִי־\rb* \rb are these|אֵ֣לֶּה\rb* \rb with you|לָּ֑ךְ\rb*?”
\p \rb Jacob answered|וַיֹּאמַ֕ר\rb*, “\rb These are the children|הַיְלָדִ֕ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb has graciously given|חָנַ֥ן\rb* \rb your servant|עַבְדֶּֽךָ׃\rb*.” \v 6 \rb Then the maidservants|הַשְּׁפָח֛וֹת\rb* \rb and their|הֵ֥נָּה\rb* \rb children|וְיַלְדֵיהֶ֖ן\rb* \rb approached|וַתִּגַּ֧שְׁןָ\rb* \rb and bowed down|וַתִּֽשְׁתַּחֲוֶֽיןָ׃\rb*. \v 7 \rb Leah|לֵאָ֛ה\rb* \rb and her children|וִילָדֶ֖יהָ\rb* \rb also|גַּם־\rb* \rb approached|וַתִּגַּ֧שׁ\rb* \rb and bowed down|וַיִּֽשְׁתַּחֲו֑וּ\rb*, \rb and then|וְאַחַ֗ר\rb* \rb Joseph|יוֹסֵ֛ף\rb* \rb and Rachel|וְרָחֵ֖ל\rb* \rb approached|נִגַּ֥שׁ\rb* \rb and bowed down|וַיִּֽשְׁתַּחֲוֽוּ׃\rb*.
\p \v 8 “\rb What|מִ֥י\rb* \rb do you mean|לְךָ֛\rb* \rb by sending this|הַזֶּ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb company|הַמַּחֲנֶ֥ה\rb* \rb to meet me|פָּגָ֑שְׁתִּי\rb*?” \rb asked Esau|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*.
\p “\rb To find|לִמְצֹא־\rb* \rb favor|חֵ֖ן\rb* \rb in your sight|בְּעֵינֵ֥י\rb*, \rb my lord|אֲדֹנִֽי׃\rb*,” \rb Jacob answered|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*.
\p \v 9 “\rb I already have|יֶשׁ־\rb* \rb plenty|רָ֑ב\rb*, \rb my brother|אָחִ֕י\rb*,” \rb Esau|עֵשָׂ֖ו\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb*. “\rb Keep|יְהִ֥י\rb* \rb what belongs|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb to you|לָֽךְ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 10 \rb But Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֗ב\rb* \rb insisted|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb No|אַל־\rb*, \rb please|נָא֙\rb*! \rb If|אִם־\rb*\rb |נָ֨א\rb* \rb I have found|מָצָ֤אתִי\rb* \rb favor|חֵן֙\rb* \rb in your sight|בְּעֵינֶ֔יךָ\rb*, \rb then receive|וְלָקַחְתָּ֥\rb* \rb this gift|מִנְחָתִ֖י\rb* \rb from my hand|מִיָּדִ֑י\rb*. \rb For|עַל־\rb*\rb |כֵּ֞ן\rb* \rb indeed|כִּ֣י\rb*, \rb I have seen|רָאִ֣יתִי\rb* \rb your face|פָנֶ֗יךָ\rb*, \rb and it is like seeing|כִּרְאֹ֛ת\rb* \rb the face|פְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of God|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb*, \rb since you have received me favorably|וַתִּרְצֵֽנִי׃\rb*. \v 11 \rb Please|נָ֤א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb accept|קַח־\rb* \rb my gift|בִּרְכָתִי֙\rb*\f + \fr 33:11 \ft Or \fqa blessing \ft or \fqa treaty of peace\f* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb was brought|הֻבָ֣את\rb* \rb to you|לָ֔ךְ\rb*, \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb*\rb |וְכִ֣י\rb* \rb has been gracious|חַנַּ֥נִי\rb* \rb to me|לִי־\rb* \rb and I have|יֶשׁ־\rb* \rb all I need|כֹ֑ל\rb*.” \rb So Jacob pressed|וַיִּפְצַר־\rb* \rb him|בּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb until he accepted|וַיִּקָּֽח׃\rb*.
\p \v 12 \rb Then Esau said|וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Let us be on our way|נִסְעָ֣ה\rb*\rb |וְנֵלֵ֑כָה\rb*, \rb and I will go|וְאֵלְכָ֖ה\rb* \rb ahead of you|לְנֶגְדֶּֽךָ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 13 \rb But Jacob replied|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֵלָ֗יו\rb*, “\rb My lord|אֲדֹנִ֤י\rb* \rb knows|יֹדֵ֙עַ֙\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the children|הַיְלָדִ֣ים\rb* \rb are frail|רַכִּ֔ים\rb*, \rb and I must care for|עָלָ֑י\rb* \rb sheep|וְהַצֹּ֥אן\rb* \rb and cattle|וְהַבָּקָ֖ר\rb* \rb that are nursing their young|עָל֣וֹת\rb*. \rb If they are driven hard|וּדְפָקוּם֙\rb* \rb for even a|אֶחָ֔ד\rb* \rb day|י֣וֹם\rb*, \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the animals|הַצֹּֽאן׃\rb* \rb will die|וָמֵ֖תוּ\rb*. \v 14 \rb Please|נָ֥א\rb* \rb let my lord|אֲדֹנִ֖י\rb* \rb go|יַעֲבָר־\rb* \rb ahead of|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb his servant|עַבְדּ֑וֹ\rb*. \rb I|וַאֲנִ֞י\rb* \rb will continue|אֶֽתְנָהֲלָ֣ה\rb* \rb on slowly|לְאִטִּ֗י\rb*, \rb at a comfortable pace|לְרֶ֨גֶל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb*\rb |לְפָנַי֙\rb*\rb |וּלְרֶ֣גֶל\rb* \rb for the livestock|הַמְּלָאכָ֤ה\rb* \rb and children|הַיְלָדִ֔ים\rb*, \rb until|עַ֛ד\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I come|אָבֹ֥א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb my lord|אֲדֹנִ֖י\rb* \rb at Seir|שֵׂעִֽירָה׃\rb*.”
\p \v 15 “\rb Let me leave|אַצִּֽיגָה־\rb*\rb |נָּ֣א\rb* \rb some of|מִן־\rb* \rb my|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb*\rb |אִתִּ֑י\rb* \rb people|הָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb with you|עִמְּךָ֔\rb*,” \rb Esau|עֵשָׂ֔ו\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*.
\p \rb But Jacob replied|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb*, “\rb Why|לָ֣מָּה\rb* \rb do that|זֶּ֔ה\rb*? \rb Let me find|אֶמְצָא־\rb* \rb favor|חֵ֖ן\rb* \rb in the sight|בְּעֵינֵ֥י\rb* \rb of my lord|אֲדֹנִֽי׃\rb*.”
\p \v 16 \rb So that|הַה֥וּא\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֨וֹם\rb* \rb Esau|עֵשָׂ֛ו\rb* \rb started on his way|לְדַרְכּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb back|וַיָּשָׁב֩\rb* \rb to Seir|שֵׂעִֽירָה׃\rb*, \v 17 \rb but Jacob|וְיַעֲקֹב֙\rb* \rb went on|נָסַ֣ע\rb* \rb to Succoth|סֻכֹּ֔תָה\rb*,\f + \fr 33:17 \fqa Succoth \ft means \fqa booths \ft or \fqa shelters \ft or \fqa tabernacles\ft ; twice in this verse.\f* \rb where he built|וַיִּ֥בֶן\rb* \rb a house|בָּ֑יִת\rb* \rb for himself|ל֖וֹ\rb* \rb and shelters|סֻכֹּ֔ת\rb* \rb for his livestock|וּלְמִקְנֵ֙הוּ֙\rb*;\rb |עָשָׂ֣ה\rb* \rb that is why|עַל־\rb*\rb |כֵּ֛ן\rb* \rb the place|הַמָּק֖וֹם\rb* \rb was called|קָרָ֥א\rb*\rb |שֵׁם־\rb* \rb Succoth|סֻכּֽוֹת׃ס\rb*.
\s1 Jacob Settles in Shechem
\p \v 18 \rb After Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֨ב\rb* \rb had come|וַיָּבֹא֩\rb*\rb |מִפַּדַּ֣ן\rb* \rb from Paddan-aram|אֲרָ֑ם\rb*,\f + \fr 33:18 \ft That is, northwest Mesopotamia\f* \rb he arrived|בְּבֹא֖וֹ\rb* \rb safely|שָׁלֵ֜ם\rb* \rb at the city|עִ֣יר\rb* \rb of Shechem|שְׁכֶ֗ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Canaan|כְּנַ֔עַן\rb*, \rb and he camped|וַיִּ֖חַן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb just outside|פְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the city|הָעִֽיר׃\rb*. \v 19 \rb And the plot|חֶלְקַ֣ת\rb* \rb of ground|הַשָּׂדֶ֗ה\rb* \rb where|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb he pitched|נָֽטָה־\rb*\rb |שָׁם֙\rb* \rb his tent|אָהֳל֔וֹ\rb*, \rb he purchased|וַיִּ֜קֶן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb from|מִיַּ֥ד\rb* \rb the sons|בְּנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Hamor|חֲמ֖וֹר\rb*, \rb Shechem’s|שְׁכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb father|אֲבִ֣י\rb*, \rb for a hundred|בְּמֵאָ֖ה\rb* \rb pieces of silver|קְשִׂיטָֽה׃\rb*.\f + \fr 33:19 \ft Hebrew \fqa a hundred kesitahs\ft ; the value or weight of the kesitah is no longer known\f* \v 20 \rb There|שָׁ֖ם\rb* \rb he set up|וַיַּצֶּב־\rb* \rb an altar|מִזְבֵּ֑חַ\rb* \rb and called|וַיִּ֨קְרָא־\rb* \rb it|ל֔וֹ\rb* \rb El-Elohe-Israel|אֵ֖ל\rb*\rb |אֱלֹהֵ֥י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃ס\rb*.\f + \fr 33:20 \fqa El-Elohe-Israel \ft means \fqa God is the God of Israel \ft or \fqa mighty is the God of Israel\ft .\f*
\c 34
\s1 The Defiling of Dinah
\p \v 1 \rb Now Dinah|דִינָה֙\rb*, \rb the daughter|בַּת־\rb* \rb Leah|לֵאָ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb had borne|יָלְדָ֖ה\rb* \rb to Jacob|לְיַעֲקֹ֑ב\rb*, \rb went out|וַתֵּצֵ֤א\rb* \rb to visit|לִרְא֖וֹת\rb* \rb the daughters|בִּבְנ֥וֹת\rb* \rb of the land|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb*. \v 2 \rb When Shechem|שְׁכֶ֧ם\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Hamor|חֲמ֛וֹר\rb* \rb the Hivite|הַֽחִוִּ֖י\rb*, \rb the prince|נְשִׂ֣יא\rb* \rb of the region|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb*, \rb saw|וַיַּ֨רְא\rb* \rb her|אֹתָ֜הּ\rb*, \rb he took|וַיִּקַּ֥ח\rb* \rb her|אֹתָ֛הּ\rb* \rb and lay|וַיִּשְׁכַּ֥ב\rb* \rb with her|אֹתָ֖הּ\rb* \rb by force|וַיְעַנֶּֽהָ׃\rb*. \v 3 \rb And his soul|נַפְשׁ֔וֹ\rb* \rb was drawn|וַתִּדְבַּ֣ק\rb* \rb to Dinah|בְּדִינָ֖ה\rb*, \rb the daughter|בַּֽת־\rb* \rb of Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֑ב\rb*. \rb He loved|וַיֶּֽאֱהַב֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the young girl|הַֽנַּעֲרָ֔\rb* \rb and spoke to her tenderly|וַיְדַבֵּ֖ר\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb*\rb |לֵ֥ב\rb*\rb |הַֽנַּעֲרָֽ׃\rb*. \v 4 \rb So Shechem|שְׁכֶ֔ם\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb told|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb his father|אָבִ֖יו\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb Hamor|חֲמ֥וֹר\rb*, “\rb Get|קַֽח־\rb* \rb me|לִ֛י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּ֖את\rb* \rb girl|הַיַּלְדָּ֥ה\rb* \rb as a wife|לְאִשָּֽׁה׃\rb*.”
\p \v 5 \rb Jacob|וְיַעֲקֹ֣ב\rb* \rb heard|שָׁמַ֗ע\rb* \rb that|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb Shechem had defiled|טִמֵּא֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his daughter|בִתּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb Dinah|דִּינָ֣ה\rb*, \rb but since his sons|וּבָנָ֛יו\rb* \rb were|הָי֥וּ\rb* \rb with|אֶת־\rb* \rb his livestock|מִקְנֵ֖הוּ\rb* \rb in the field|בַּשָּׂדֶ֑ה\rb*, \rb he|יַעֲקֹ֖ב\rb* \rb remained silent about it|וְהֶחֱרִ֥שׁ\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb they returned|בֹּאָֽם׃\rb*. \v 6 \rb Meanwhile, Shechem’s|שְׁכֶ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֶֽל־\rb* \rb father|אֲבִֽי־\rb* \rb Hamor|חֲמ֥וֹר\rb* \rb came|וַיֵּצֵ֛א\rb* \rb to speak|לְדַבֵּ֖ר\rb* \rb with|אִתּֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֑ב\rb*. \v 7 \rb When Jacob’s|יַעֲקֹ֜ב\rb* \rb sons|וּבְנֵ֨י\rb* \rb heard what had happened|כְּשָׁמְעָ֔ם\rb*, \rb they returned|בָּ֤אוּ\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the field|הַשָּׂדֶה֙\rb*. \rb They were filled with|מְאֹ֑ד\rb* \rb grief|וַיִּֽתְעַצְּבוּ֙\rb*\rb |הָֽאֲנָשִׁ֔ים\rb* \rb and fury|וַיִּ֥חַר\rb*, \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb Shechem had committed|עָשָׂ֣ה\rb* \rb an outrage|נְבָלָ֞ה\rb* \rb in Israel|בְיִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb*\f + \fr 34:7 \ft Or \fqa against Israel\f* \rb by lying|לִשְׁכַּב֙\rb* \rb with|אֶת־\rb* \rb Jacob’s|יַעֲקֹ֔ב\rb* \rb daughter|בַּֽת־\rb* — \rb a thing|וְכֵ֖ן\rb* \rb that should not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb be done|יֵעָשֶֽׂה׃\rb*.
\p \v 8 \rb But Hamor|חֲמ֖וֹר\rb* \rb said|וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb to them|אִתָּ֣ם\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*, “\rb My son|בְּנִ֗י\rb* \rb Shechem|שְׁכֶ֣ם\rb* \rb longs for|חָֽשְׁקָ֤ה\rb*\rb |נַפְשׁוֹ֙\rb* \rb your daughter|בְּבִתְּכֶ֔ם\rb*. \rb Please|נָ֥א\rb* \rb give|תְּנ֨וּ\rb* \rb her|אֹתָ֛הּ\rb* \rb to him|ל֖וֹ\rb* \rb as his wife|לְאִשָּֽׁה׃\rb*. \v 9 \rb Intermarry with us|וְהִֽתְחַתְּנ֖וּ\rb*;\rb |אֹתָ֑נוּ\rb* \rb give|תִּתְּנוּ־\rb* \rb us|לָ֔נוּ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb your daughters|בְּנֹֽתֵיכֶם֙\rb* \rb and take|תִּקְח֥וּ\rb* \rb our daughters|בְּנֹתֵ֖ינוּ\rb* \rb for yourselves|לָכֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 10 \rb You may settle|תֵּשֵׁ֑בוּ\rb* \rb among us|וְאִתָּ֖נוּ\rb*, \rb and the land|וְהָאָ֙רֶץ֙\rb* \rb will be|תִּהְיֶ֣ה\rb* \rb open to you|לִפְנֵיכֶ֔ם\rb*. \rb Live here|שְׁבוּ֙\rb*, \rb move about freely|וּסְחָר֔וּהָ\rb*, \rb and acquire your own property|וְהֵֽאָחֲז֖וּ\rb*.”
\p \v 11 \rb Then Shechem|שְׁכֶם֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Dinah’s father|אָבִ֣יה\rb*\rb |וְאֶל־\rb* \rb and brothers|אַחֶ֔יהָ\rb*, “\rb Grant me this favor|אֶמְצָא־\rb*\rb |חֵ֖ן\rb*,\rb |בְּעֵינֵיכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb and I will give|אֶתֵּֽן׃\rb* \rb you whatever|וַאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you ask|תֹּאמְר֛וּ\rb*.\rb |אֵלַ֖י\rb* \v 12 \rb Demand|הַרְבּ֨וּ\rb* \rb a high|עָלַ֤י\rb*\rb |מְאֹד֙\rb* \rb dowry|מֹ֣הַר\rb* \rb and an expensive gift|וּמַתָּ֔ן\rb*, \rb and I will give you|וְאֶ֨תְּנָ֔ה\rb* \rb whatever|כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you ask|תֹּאמְר֖וּ\rb*.\rb |אֵלָ֑י\rb* \rb Only give|וּתְנוּ־\rb* \rb me|לִ֥י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the girl|הַֽנַּעֲרָ֖\rb* \rb as my wife|לְאִשָּֽׁה׃\rb*!”
\s1 The Revenge of Dinah’s Brothers
\p \v 13 \rb But because|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb Shechem had defiled|טִמֵּ֔א\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb their sister|אֲחֹתָֽם׃\rb* \rb Dinah|דִּינָ֥ה\rb*, \rb Jacob’s|יַעֲקֹ֜ב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb sons|בְנֵֽי־\rb* \rb answered|וַיַּעֲנ֨וּ\rb* \rb him|שְׁכֶ֨ם\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and his father|אָבִ֛יו\rb* \rb Hamor|חֲמ֥וֹר\rb* \rb deceitfully|בְּמִרְמָ֖ה\rb*\rb |וַיְדַבֵּ֑רוּ\rb*. \v 14 “\rb We cannot|לֹ֤א\rb*\rb |נוּכַל֙\rb* \rb do|לַעֲשׂוֹת֙\rb* \rb such|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb a thing|הַדָּבָ֣ר\rb*,” \rb they said|וַיֹּאמְר֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֲלֵיהֶ֗ם\rb*. “\rb To give|לָתֵת֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb our sister|אֲחֹתֵ֔נוּ\rb*\rb |לְאִ֖ישׁ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb to|ל֣וֹ\rb* \rb an uncircumcised man|עָרְלָ֑ה\rb*\rb |כִּֽי־\rb* \rb would be a disgrace|חֶרְפָּ֥ה\rb*\rb |הִ֖וא\rb* \rb to us|לָֽנוּ׃\rb*. \v 15 \rb We will consent|נֵא֣וֹת\rb* \rb to this|לָכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb on one|אַךְ־\rb*\rb |בְּזֹ֖את\rb* \rb condition|אִ֚ם\rb*, \rb that you become|תִּהְי֣וּ\rb* \rb circumcised|לְהִמֹּ֥ל\rb* \rb like us|כָמֹ֔נוּ\rb* — \rb every one of|כָּל־\rb* \rb your males|זָכָֽר׃\rb*. \v 16 \rb Then we will give|וְנָתַ֤נּוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb you|לָכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb our daughters|בְּנֹתֵ֙ינוּ֙\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb take|נִֽקַּֽח־\rb* \rb your daughters|בְּנֹתֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb for ourselves|לָ֑נוּ\rb*. \rb We will dwell|וְיָשַׁ֣בְנוּ\rb* \rb among you|אִתְּכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb and become|וְהָיִ֖ינוּ\rb* \rb one|אֶחָֽד׃\rb* \rb people|לְעַ֥ם\rb*. \v 17 \rb But if|וְאִם־\rb* \rb you will not|לֹ֧א\rb* \rb agree|תִשְׁמְע֛וּ\rb*\rb |אֵלֵ֖ינוּ\rb* \rb to be circumcised|לְהִמּ֑וֹל\rb*, \rb then we will take|וְלָקַ֥חְנוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb our sister|בִּתֵּ֖נוּ\rb* \rb and go|וְהָלָֽכְנוּ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 18 \rb Their offer|דִבְרֵיהֶ֖ם\rb*\rb |בְּעֵינֵ֣י\rb* \rb seemed good|וַיִּֽיטְב֥וּ\rb* \rb to Hamor|חֲמ֑וֹר\rb*\rb |וּבְעֵינֵ֖י\rb* \rb and his|חֲמֽוֹר׃\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb Shechem|שְׁכֶ֥ם\rb*. \v 19 \rb The young man|הַנַּ֙עַר֙\rb*, \rb who was|וְה֣וּא\rb* \rb the most respected|נִכְבָּ֔ד\rb* \rb of all|מִכֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb his father’s|אָבִֽיו׃\rb* \rb household|בֵּ֥ית\rb*, \rb did not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb hesitate|אֵחַ֤ר\rb* \rb to fulfill|לַעֲשׂ֣וֹת\rb* \rb this request|הַדָּבָ֔ר\rb*, \rb because|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb he was delighted|חָפֵ֖ץ\rb* \rb with Jacob’s|יַעֲקֹ֑ב\rb* \rb daughter|בְּבַֽת־\rb*.
\p \v 20 \rb So Hamor|חֲמ֛וֹר\rb* \rb and his son|בְּנ֖וֹ\rb* \rb Shechem|וּשְׁכֶ֥ם\rb* \rb went|וַיָּבֹ֥א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the gate|שַׁ֣עַר\rb* \rb of their city|עִירָ֑ם\rb* \rb and addressed|וַֽיְדַבְּר֛וּ\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the men|אַנְשֵׁ֥י\rb* \rb of their city|עִירָ֖ם\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*: \v 21 “\rb These|הָאֵ֜לֶּה\rb* \rb men|הָאֲנָשִׁ֨ים\rb* \rb are at peace|שְֽׁלֵמִ֧ים\rb*\rb |הֵ֣ם\rb* \rb with us|אִתָּ֗נוּ\rb*. \rb Let them live|וְיֵשְׁב֤וּ\rb* \rb and trade|וְיִסְחֲר֣וּ\rb* \rb in our land|בָאָ֙רֶץ֙\rb*;\rb |אֹתָ֔הּ\rb* \rb indeed|הִנֵּ֥ה\rb*, \rb it|וְהָאָ֛רֶץ\rb* \rb is large|רַֽחֲבַת־\rb*\rb |יָדַ֖יִם\rb* \rb enough for them|לִפְנֵיהֶ֑ם\rb*.\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Let us take|נִקַּֽח־\rb*\rb |לָ֣נוּ\rb* \rb their daughters|בְּנֹתָם֙\rb* \rb in marriage|לְנָשִׁ֔ים\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and give|נִתֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb our daughters|בְּנֹתֵ֖ינוּ\rb* \rb to them|לָהֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 22 \rb But only|אַךְ־\rb* \rb on this condition|בְּ֠זֹאת\rb* \rb will the men|הָאֲנָשִׁים֙\rb* \rb agree|יֵאֹ֨תוּ\rb*\rb |לָ֤נוּ\rb* \rb to dwell|לָשֶׁ֣בֶת\rb* \rb with us|אִתָּ֔נוּ\rb* \rb and be|לִהְי֖וֹת\rb* \rb one|אֶחָ֑ד\rb* \rb people|לְעַ֣ם\rb*: \rb if all|כָּל־\rb* \rb our|לָ֙נוּ֙\rb* \rb men|זָכָ֔ר\rb* \rb are circumcised|בְּהִמּ֥וֹל\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb they are|הֵ֥ם\rb*\rb |נִמֹּלִֽים׃\rb*. \v 23 \rb Will not|הֲל֥וֹא\rb* \rb their livestock|מִקְנֵהֶ֤ם\rb*, \rb their possessions|וְקִנְיָנָם֙\rb*, \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb*\rb |לָ֖נוּ\rb* \rb their|הֵ֑ם\rb* \rb animals become ours|בְּהֶמְתָּ֔ם\rb*? \rb Only|אַ֚ךְ\rb* \rb let us consent|נֵא֣וֹתָה\rb* \rb to them|לָהֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb and they will dwell|וְיֵשְׁב֖וּ\rb* \rb among us|אִתָּֽנוּ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 24 \rb All the men|כָּל־\rb* \rb who went out|יֹצְאֵ֖י\rb* \rb of the city|עִיר֑וֹ\rb* \rb gate|שַׁ֣עַר\rb* \rb listened|וַיִּשְׁמְע֤וּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Hamor|חֲמוֹר֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶל־\rb* \rb and his son|בְּנ֔וֹ\rb* \rb Shechem|שְׁכֶ֣ם\rb*, \rb and every|כָּל־\rb* \rb male|זָכָ֔ר\rb*\rb |כָּל־\rb*\rb |יֹצְאֵ֖י\rb*\rb |שַׁ֥עַר\rb* \rb of the city|עִירֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb was circumcised|וַיִּמֹּ֙לוּ֙\rb*.
\p \v 25 \rb Three|הַשְּׁלִישִׁ֜י\rb* \rb days later|בַיּ֨וֹם\rb*, \rb while|בִּֽהְיוֹתָ֣ם\rb* \rb they were|וַיְהִי֩\rb* \rb still in pain|כֹּֽאֲבִ֗ים\rb*, \rb two|שְׁנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Jacob’s|יַ֠עֲקֹב\rb* \rb sons|בְנֵי־\rb* (\rb Dinah’s|דִינָה֙\rb*\rb |אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb brothers|אֲחֵ֤י\rb* \rb Simeon|שִׁמְע֨וֹן\rb* \rb and Levi|וְלֵוִ֜י\rb*) \rb took|וַיִּקְח֣וּ\rb* \rb their swords|חַרְבּ֔וֹ\rb*, \rb went|וַיָּבֹ֥אוּ\rb* \rb into|עַל־\rb* \rb the unsuspecting|בֶּ֑טַח\rb* \rb city|הָעִ֖יר\rb*, \rb and slaughtered|וַיַּֽהַרְג֖וּ\rb* \rb every|כָּל־\rb* \rb male|זָכָֽר׃\rb*. \v 26 \rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb They killed|הָרְג֖וּ\rb*\rb |לְפִי־\rb* \rb Hamor|חֲמוֹר֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and his son|בְּנ֔וֹ\rb* \rb Shechem|שְׁכֶ֣ם\rb* \rb with their swords|חָ֑רֶב\rb*, \rb took|וַיִּקְח֧וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Dinah|דִּינָ֛ה\rb* \rb out of Shechem’s|שְׁכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb house|מִבֵּ֥ית\rb*, \rb and went away|וַיֵּצֵֽאוּ׃\rb*.
\p \v 27 \rb Jacob’s|יַעֲקֹ֗ב\rb* \rb other sons|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb came|בָּ֚אוּ\rb* \rb upon|עַל־\rb* \rb the slaughter|הַ֣חֲלָלִ֔ים\rb* \rb and looted|וַיָּבֹ֖זּוּ\rb* \rb the city|הָעִ֑יר\rb*, \rb because|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb their sister|אֲחוֹתָֽם׃\rb* \rb had been defiled|טִמְּא֖וּ\rb*. \v 28 \rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb They took|לָקָֽחוּ׃\rb* \rb their flocks|צֹאנָ֥ם\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb herds|בְּקָרָ֖ם\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb donkeys|חֲמֹרֵיהֶּ֑ם\rb*,\rb |וְאֵ֧ת\rb* \rb and everything else|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb in the city|בָּעִ֛יר\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb or in the field|בַּשָּׂדֶ֖ה\rb*. \v 29 \rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb They carried off|שָׁב֖וּ\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb their possessions|חֵילָ֤ם\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb women|נְשֵׁיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb*\rb |כָּל־\rb* \rb children|טַפָּם֙\rb*, \rb and they plundered|וַיָּבֹ֑זּוּ\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֖ת\rb* \rb everything|כָּל־\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb in their houses|בַּבָּֽיִת׃\rb*.
\p \v 30 \rb Then Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֜ב\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Simeon|שִׁמְע֣וֹן\rb*\rb |וְאֶל־\rb* \rb and Levi|לֵוִי֮\rb*, “\rb You have brought trouble|עֲכַרְתֶּ֣ם\rb* \rb upon me|אֹתִי֒\rb* \rb by making me a stench|לְהַבְאִישֵׁ֙נִי֙\rb* \rb to the Canaanites|בַּֽכְּנַעֲנִ֖י\rb* \rb and Perizzites|וּבַפְּרִזִּ֑י\rb*, \rb the people|בְּיֹשֵׁ֣ב\rb* \rb of this land|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb*. \rb We|וַאֲנִי֙\rb* \rb are few|מְתֵ֣י\rb* \rb in number|מִסְפָּ֔ר\rb*; \rb if they unite|וְנֶאֶסְפ֤וּ\rb* \rb against me|עָלַי֙\rb* \rb and attack me|וְהִכּ֔וּנִי\rb*, \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb and my household|וּבֵיתִֽי׃\rb* \rb will be destroyed|וְנִשְׁמַדְתִּ֖י\rb*.”
\p \v 31 \rb But they replied|וַיֹּאמְר֑וּ\rb*, “\rb Should he have treated|יַעֲשֶׂ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb our sister|אֲחוֹתֵֽנוּ׃פ\rb* \rb like a prostitute|הַכְזוֹנָ֕ה\rb*?”
\c 35
\s1 Jacob Returns to Bethel
\p \v 1 \rb Then God|אֱלֹהִים֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֔ב\rb*, “\rb Arise|ק֛וּם\rb*, \rb go up|עֲלֵ֥ה\rb* \rb to|בֵֽית־\rb* \rb Bethel|אֵ֖ל\rb*, \rb and settle|וְשֶׁב־\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֑ם\rb*. \rb Build|וַעֲשֵׂה־\rb* \rb an altar|מִזְבֵּ֔חַ\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֣ם\rb* \rb to the God|לָאֵל֙\rb* \rb who appeared|הַנִּרְאֶ֣ה\rb* \rb to|אֵלֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb you when you fled|בְּבָרְחֲךָ֔\rb* \rb from|מִפְּנֵ֖י\rb* \rb your brother|אָחִֽיךָ׃\rb* \rb Esau|עֵשָׂ֥ו\rb*.”
\p \v 2 \rb So Jacob|יַעֲקֹב֙\rb* \rb told|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb his household|בֵּית֔וֹ\rb*\rb |וְאֶ֖ל\rb* \rb and all|כָּל־\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb were with him|עִמּ֑וֹ\rb*, “\rb Get rid of|הָסִ֜רוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the foreign|הַנֵּכָר֙\rb* \rb gods|אֱלֹהֵ֤י\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb are among you|בְּתֹכְכֶ֔ם\rb*. \rb Purify yourselves|וְהִֽטַּהֲר֔וּ\rb* \rb and change|וְהַחֲלִ֖יפוּ\rb* \rb your garments|שִׂמְלֹתֵיכֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 3 \rb Then let us arise|וְנָק֥וּמָה\rb* \rb and go|וְנַעֲלֶ֖ה\rb* \rb to|בֵּֽית־\rb* \rb Bethel|אֵ֑ל\rb*. \rb I will build|וְאֶֽעֱשֶׂה־\rb* \rb an altar|מִזְבֵּ֗חַ\rb* \rb there|שָּׁ֣ם\rb* \rb to God|לָאֵ֞ל\rb*, \rb who answered|הָעֹנֶ֤ה\rb* \rb me|אֹתִי֙\rb* \rb in my day|בְּי֣וֹם\rb* \rb of distress|צָֽרָתִ֔י\rb*. \rb He has been|וַיְהִי֙\rb* \rb with me|עִמָּדִ֔י\rb* \rb wherever|בַּדֶּ֖רֶךְ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I have gone|הָלָֽכְתִּי׃\rb*.”
\p \v 4 \rb So they gave|וַיִּתְּנ֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֶֽל־\rb* \rb Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֗ב\rb*\rb |אֵ֣ת\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb their|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb*\rb |בְּיָדָ֔ם\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb foreign|הַנֵּכָר֙\rb* \rb gods|אֱלֹהֵ֤י\rb* \rb and all their earrings|הַנְּזָמִ֖ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb*,\rb |בְּאָזְנֵיהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb and Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֔ב\rb* \rb buried|וַיִּטְמֹ֤ן\rb* \rb them|אֹתָם֙\rb* \rb under|תַּ֥חַת\rb* \rb the oak|הָאֵלָ֖ה\rb*\f + \fr 35:4 \ft Or \fqa terebinth \ft or \fqa great tree\f*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb near|עִם־\rb* \rb Shechem|שְׁכֶֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 5 \rb As they set out|וַיִּסָּ֑עוּ\rb*, \rb a terror|חִתַּ֣ת\rb* \rb from God|אֱלֹהִ֗ים\rb* \rb fell|וַיְהִ֣י׀\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb the surrounding|סְבִיבֹ֣תֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb cities|הֶֽעָרִים֙\rb*, \rb so that they did not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb pursue|רָֽדְפ֔וּ\rb*\rb |אַחֲרֵ֖י\rb* \rb Jacob’s|יַעֲקֹֽב׃\rb* \rb sons|בְּנֵ֥י\rb*. \v 6 \rb So Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֜ב\rb* \rb and everyone|וְכָל־\rb*\rb |הָעָ֥ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb with him|עִמּֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb arrived|וַיָּבֹ֨א\rb* \rb in Luz|ל֗וּזָה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb (that is|הִ֖וא\rb*,\rb |בֵּֽית־\rb* \rb Bethel)|אֵ֑ל\rb*\rb |ה֖וּא\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Canaan|כְּנַ֔עַן\rb*. \v 7 \rb There|שָׁם֙\rb* \rb Jacob built|וַיִּ֤בֶן\rb* \rb an altar|מִזְבֵּ֔חַ\rb*, \rb and he called|וַיִּקְרָא֙\rb* \rb that place|לַמָּק֔וֹם\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ל\rb*\rb |בֵּֽית־\rb* \rb El-bethel|אֵ֑ל\rb*,\f + \fr 35:7 \fqa El-bethel \ft means \fqa God of Bethel\ft .\f* \rb because|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb it was there|שָׁ֗ם\rb* \rb that God|הָֽאֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb* \rb had revealed Himself|נִגְל֤וּ\rb* \rb to Jacob|אֵלָיו֙\rb* \rb as he fled|בְּבָרְח֖וֹ\rb* \rb from|מִפְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb his brother|אָחִֽיו׃\rb*.
\p \v 8 \rb Now Deborah|דְּבֹרָה֙\rb*, \rb Rebekah’s|רִבְקָ֔ה\rb* \rb nurse|מֵינֶ֣קֶת\rb*, \rb died|וַתָּ֤מָת\rb* \rb and was buried|וַתִּקָּבֵ֛ר\rb* \rb under|מִתַּ֥חַת\rb* \rb the oak|הָֽאַלּ֑וֹן\rb*\f + \fr 35:8 \ft Or \fqa great tree\f* \rb below|תַּ֣חַת\rb*\rb |לְבֵֽית־\rb* \rb Bethel|אֵ֖ל\rb*. \rb So Jacob named|וַיִּקְרָ֥א\rb* \rb it|שְׁמ֖וֹ\rb*\rb |אַלּ֥וֹן\rb* \rb Allon-bacuth|בָּכֽוּת׃פ\rb*.\f + \fr 35:8 \fqa Allon-bacuth \ft means \fqa oak of weeping\ft .\f*
\p \v 9 \rb After Jacob had returned|בְּבֹא֖וֹ\rb* \rb from|מִפַּדַּ֣ן\rb* \rb Paddan-aram|אֲרָ֑ם\rb*,\f + \fr 35:9 \ft That is, northwest Mesopotamia; also in verse 26\f* \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֤ים\rb* \rb appeared|וַיֵּרָ֨א\rb* \rb to|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb him|יַעֲקֹב֙\rb* \rb again|ע֔וֹד\rb* \rb and blessed|וַיְבָ֖רֶךְ\rb* \rb him|אֹתֽוֹ׃\rb*. \v 10 \rb And God|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּֽאמֶר־\rb* \rb to him|ל֥וֹ\rb*, “\rb Though your name|שִׁמְךָ֣\rb* \rb is Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֑ב\rb*,\f + \fr 35:10 \fqa Jacob \ft means \fqa he grasps the heel \ft or \fqa he deceives\ft .\f* \rb you will no|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb longer|ע֜וֹד\rb* \rb be called|יִקָּרֵא֩\rb*\rb |שִׁמְךָ֙\rb* \rb Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֗ב\rb*. \rb Instead|כִּ֤י\rb*\rb |אִם־\rb*, \rb your name|שְׁמֶ֔ךָ\rb* \rb will be|יִהְיֶ֣ה\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb*.\f + \fr 35:10 \fqa Israel \ft means \fqa he struggles with God\ft .\f*” \rb So God named|וַיִּקְרָ֥א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb him|שְׁמ֖וֹ\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*.
\p \v 11 \rb And God|אֱלֹהִ֜ים\rb* \rb told|וַיֹּאמֶר֩\rb* \rb him|ל֨וֹ\rb*, “\rb I|אֲנִ֨י\rb* \rb am God|אֵ֤ל\rb* \rb Almighty|שַׁדַּי֙\rb*.\f + \fr 35:11 \ft Hebrew \fqa El-Shaddai\f* \rb Be fruitful|פְּרֵ֣ה\rb* \rb and multiply|וּרְבֵ֔ה\rb*. \rb A nation|גּ֛וֹי\rb* — \rb even a company|וּקְהַ֥ל\rb* \rb of nations|גּוֹיִ֖ם\rb* — \rb shall come|יִהְיֶ֣ה\rb* \rb from you|מִמֶּ֑ךָּ\rb*, \rb and kings|וּמְלָכִ֖ים\rb* \rb shall descend|יֵצֵֽאוּ׃\rb* \rb from you|מֵחֲלָצֶ֥יךָ\rb*. \v 12 \rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb The land|הָאָ֗רֶץ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I gave|אֶתְּנֶ֑נָּה\rb* \rb to Abraham|לְאַבְרָהָ֥ם\rb* \rb and Isaac|וּלְיִצְחָ֖ק\rb* \rb I will give|נָתַ֛תִּי\rb* \rb to you|לְךָ֣\rb*, \rb and I will give|אֶתֵּ֥ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb this land|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb* \rb to your descendants|וּֽלְזַרְעֲךָ֥\rb* \rb after you|אַחֲרֶ֖יךָ\rb*.”
\p \v 13 \rb Then God|אֱלֹהִ֑ים\rb* \rb went up|וַיַּ֥עַל\rb* \rb from|מֵעָלָ֖יו\rb* \rb the place|בַּמָּק֖וֹם\rb* \rb where|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb He had spoken|דִּבֶּ֥ר\rb* \rb with him|אִתּֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\p \v 14 \rb So Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֜ב\rb* \rb set up|וַיַּצֵּ֨ב\rb* \rb a pillar|מַצֵּבָ֗ה\rb* \rb in the place|בַּמָּק֛וֹם\rb* \rb where|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb God had spoken|דִּבֶּ֥ר\rb* \rb with him|אִתּ֖וֹ\rb*— \rb a stone|אָ֑בֶן\rb* \rb marker|מַצֶּ֣בֶת\rb*— \rb and he poured out|וַיַּסֵּ֤ךְ\rb* \rb a drink offering|נֶ֔סֶךְ\rb* \rb on it|עָלֶ֙יהָ֙\rb* \rb and anointed it|וַיִּצֹ֥ק\rb*\rb |עָלֶ֖יהָ\rb* \rb with oil|שָֽׁמֶן׃\rb*. \v 15 \rb Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֜ב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb called|וַיִּקְרָ֨א\rb*\rb |שֵׁ֣ם\rb* \rb the place|הַמָּק֗וֹם\rb* \rb where|אֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb had spoken|דִּבֶּ֨ר\rb* \rb with him|אִתּ֥וֹ\rb*\rb |שָׁ֛ם\rb*\rb |בֵּֽית־\rb* \rb Bethel|אֵֽל׃\rb*.\f + \fr 35:15 \fqa Bethel \ft means \fqa house of God\ft .\f*
\s1 Benjamin Born, Rachel Dies
\p \v 16 \rb Later, they set out|וַיִּסְעוּ֙\rb* \rb from|מִבֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb Bethel|אֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb and while they were|וַֽיְהִי־\rb* \rb still|ע֥וֹד\rb* \rb some distance|כִּבְרַת־\rb*\rb |הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb*\rb |לָב֣וֹא\rb* \rb from Ephrath|אֶפְרָ֑תָה\rb*, \rb Rachel|רָחֵ֖ל\rb* \rb began to give birth|וַתֵּ֥לֶד\rb*, \rb and her labor|בְּלִדְתָּֽהּ׃\rb* \rb was difficult|וַתְּקַ֥שׁ\rb*. \v 17 \rb During|וַיְהִ֥י\rb* \rb her severe|בְהַקְשֹׁתָ֖הּ\rb* \rb labor|בְּלִדְתָּ֑הּ\rb*, \rb the midwife|הַמְיַלֶּ֙דֶת֙\rb* \rb said|וַתֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to her|לָ֤הּ\rb*, “\rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb be afraid|תִּ֣ירְאִ֔י\rb*, \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb you|לָ֖ךְ\rb* \rb are having|זֶ֥ה\rb* \rb another|גַם־\rb* \rb son|בֵּֽן׃\rb*.”
\p \v 18 \rb And|וַיְהִ֞י\rb* \rb with her last|בְּצֵ֤את\rb* \rb breath|נַפְשָׁהּ֙\rb*— \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb she was dying|מֵ֔תָה\rb*— \rb she named|וַתִּקְרָ֥א\rb*\rb |שְׁמ֖וֹ\rb* \rb vvv him|בֶּן־\rb* \rb Ben-oni|אוֹנִ֑י\rb*.\f + \fr 35:18 \fqa Ben-oni \ft could mean \fqa son of my sorrow \ft or \fqa son of my strength\ft .\f* \rb But his father|וְאָבִ֖יו\rb* \rb called|קָֽרָא־\rb* \rb him|ל֥וֹ\rb* \rb Benjamin|בִנְיָמִֽין׃\rb*.\f + \fr 35:18 \fqa Benjamin \ft means \fqa son of my right hand\ft .\f*
\p \v 19 \rb So Rachel|רָחֵ֑ל\rb* \rb died|וַתָּ֖מָת\rb* \rb and was buried|וַתִּקָּבֵר֙\rb* \rb on the way|בְּדֶ֣רֶךְ\rb* \rb to Ephrath|אֶפְרָ֔תָה\rb* \rb (that is|הִ֖וא\rb*,\rb |בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb Bethlehem)|לָֽחֶם׃\rb*. \v 20 \rb Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֛ב\rb* \rb set up|וַיַּצֵּ֧ב\rb* \rb a pillar|מַצֵּבָ֖ה\rb* \rb on her|עַל־\rb* \rb grave|קְבֻרָתָ֑הּ\rb*; \rb it|הִ֛וא\rb* \rb marks|מַצֶּ֥בֶת\rb* \rb Rachel’s|רָחֵ֖ל\rb* \rb tomb|קְבֻֽרַת־\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb* \rb this day|הַיּֽוֹם׃\rb*.
\s1 The Sons of Jacob
\p \v 21 \rb Israel again|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb set out|וַיִּסַּ֖ע\rb* \rb and pitched|וַיֵּ֣ט\rb* \rb his tent|אָֽהֳלֹ֔ה\rb* \rb beyond|מֵהָ֖לְאָה\rb*\rb |לְמִגְדַּל־\rb* \rb the Tower of Eder|עֵֽדֶר׃\rb*. \v 22 \rb While|וַיְהִ֗י\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb was living|בִּשְׁכֹּ֤ן\rb* \rb in that|הַהִ֔וא\rb* \rb region|בָּאָ֣רֶץ\rb*, \rb Reuben|רְאוּבֵ֔ן\rb* \rb went in|וַיֵּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb and slept with|וַיִּשְׁכַּ֕ב֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his father’s|אָבִ֑֔יו\rb* \rb concubine|פִּילֶ֣גֶשׁ\rb* \rb Bilhah|בִּלְהָ֖ה֙\rb*, \rb and Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽ֑ל פ\rb*\rb |וַיִּֽהְי֥וּ\rb* \rb heard about it|וַיִּשְׁמַ֖ע\rb*.
\p \rb Jacob had|יַעֲקֹ֖ב\rb* \rb twelve|שְׁנֵ֥ים\rb*\rb |עָשָֽׂר׃\rb* \rb sons|בְנֵֽי־\rb*:
\b 
\li1 \v 23 \rb The sons|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Leah|לֵאָ֔ה\rb* \rb were Reuben|רְאוּבֵ֑ן\rb* \rb the firstborn|בְּכ֥וֹר\rb* \rb of Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֖ב\rb*, \rb Simeon|וְשִׁמְעוֹן֙\rb*, \rb Levi|וְלֵוִ֣י\rb*, \rb Judah|וִֽיהוּדָ֔ה\rb*, \rb Issachar|וְיִשָּׂשכָ֖ר\rb*, \rb and Zebulun|וּזְבוּלֻֽן׃\rb*.
\li1 \v 24 \rb The sons|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Rachel were|רָחֵ֔ל\rb* \rb Joseph|יוֹסֵ֖ף\rb* \rb and Benjamin|וּבִנְיָמִֽן׃\rb*.
\li1 \v 25 \rb The sons|וּבְנֵ֤י\rb* \rb of Rachel’s|רָחֵ֔ל\rb* \rb maidservant|שִׁפְחַ֣ת\rb* \rb Bilhah were|בִלְהָה֙\rb* \rb Dan|דָּ֖ן\rb* \rb and Naphtali|וְנַפְתָּלִֽי׃\rb*.
\li1 \v 26 \rb And the sons|וּבְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Leah’s|לֵאָ֖ה\rb* \rb maidservant|שִׁפְחַ֥ת\rb* \rb Zilpah|זִלְפָּ֛ה\rb* \rb were Gad|גָּ֣ד\rb* \rb and Asher|וְאָשֵׁ֑ר\rb*.
\p \rb These|אֵ֚לֶּה\rb* \rb are the sons|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֔ב\rb*, \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb were born|יֻלַּד־\rb* \rb to him|ל֖וֹ\rb* \rb in|בְּפַדַּ֥ן\rb* \rb Paddan-aram|אֲרָֽם׃\rb*.
\s1 The Death of Isaac
\p \v 27 \rb Jacob|יַעֲקֹב֙\rb* \rb returned|וַיָּבֹ֤א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his father|אָבִ֔יו\rb* \rb Isaac|יִצְחָ֣ק\rb* \rb at Mamre|מַמְרֵ֖א\rb*,\rb |קִרְיַ֣ת\rb* \rb near Kiriath-arba|הָֽאַרְבַּ֑ע\rb* \rb (that is|הִ֣וא\rb*, \rb Hebron)|חֶבְר֔וֹן\rb*, \rb where|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb Abraham|אַבְרָהָ֖ם\rb* \rb and Isaac|וְיִצְחָֽק׃\rb* \rb had stayed|גָּֽר־\rb*\rb |שָׁ֥ם\rb*.
\p \v 28 \rb And Isaac|יִצְחָ֑ק\rb* \rb lived|וַיִּֽהְי֖וּ\rb*\rb |יְמֵ֣י\rb* \rb 180|מְאַ֥ת\rb*\rb |וּשְׁמֹנִ֥ים\rb*\rb |שָׁנָֽה׃\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָ֖ה\rb*. \v 29 \rb Then he|יִצְחָ֤ק\rb* \rb breathed his last|וַיִּגְוַ֨ע\rb* \rb and died|וַיָּ֙מָת֙\rb* \rb and was gathered|וַיֵּאָ֣סֶף\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his people|עַמָּ֔יו\rb*, \rb old|זָקֵ֖ן\rb* \rb and full|וּשְׂבַ֣ע\rb* \rb of years|יָמִ֑ים\rb*. \rb And his sons|בָּנָֽיו׃פ\rb* \rb Esau|עֵשָׂ֥ו\rb* \rb and Jacob|וְיַעֲקֹ֖ב\rb* \rb buried him|וַיִּקְבְּר֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֹת֔וֹ\rb*.
\c 36
\s1 The Descendants of Esau
\p \v 1 \rb This|וְאֵ֛לֶּה\rb* \rb is the account|תֹּלְד֥וֹת\rb* \rb of Esau|עֵשָׂ֖ו\rb* \rb (that is|ה֥וּא\rb*, \rb Edom)|אֱדֽוֹם׃\rb*. \v 2 \rb Esau|עֵשָׂ֛ו\rb* \rb took|לָקַ֥ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his wives|נָשָׁ֖יו\rb* \rb from the daughters|מִבְּנ֣וֹת\rb* \rb of Canaan|כְּנָ֑עַן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*: \rb Adah|עָדָ֗ה\rb* \rb daughter|בַּת־\rb* \rb of Elon|אֵילוֹן֙\rb* \rb the Hittite|הַֽחִתִּ֔י\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Oholibamah|אָהֳלִֽיבָמָה֙\rb* \rb daughter|בַּת־\rb* \rb of Anah|עֲנָ֔ה\rb* \rb and granddaughter|בַּת־\rb* \rb of Zibeon|צִבְע֖וֹן\rb* \rb the Hivite|הַֽחִוִּֽי׃\rb*, \v 3 \rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and Basemath|בָּשְׂמַ֥ת\rb* \rb daughter|בַּת־\rb* \rb of Ishmael|יִשְׁמָעֵ֖אל\rb* \rb and sister|אֲח֥וֹת\rb* \rb of Nebaioth|נְבָיֽוֹת׃\rb*. \v 4 \rb And Adah|עָדָ֛ה\rb* \rb bore|וַתֵּ֧לֶד\rb* \rb Eliphaz|אֱלִיפָ֑ז\rb* \rb to Esau|לְעֵשָׂ֖ו\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Basemath|וּבָ֣שְׂמַ֔ת\rb* \rb gave birth to|יָלְדָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Reuel|רְעוּאֵֽל׃\rb*, \v 5 \rb and Oholibamah|וְאָהֳלִֽיבָמָה֙\rb* \rb gave birth to|יָֽלְדָ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Jeush|יְעִישׁ\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Jalam|יַעְלָ֖ם\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and Korah|קֹ֑רַח\rb*. \rb These|אֵ֚לֶּה\rb* \rb were the sons|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Esau|עֵשָׂ֔ו\rb*, \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb were born|יֻלְּדוּ־\rb* \rb to him|ל֖וֹ\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Canaan|כְּנָֽעַן׃\rb*.
\p \v 6 \rb Later, Esau|עֵשָׂ֡ו\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb took|וַיִּקַּ֣ח\rb* \rb his wives|נָ֠שָׁיו\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb sons|בָּנָ֣יו\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb daughters|בְּנֹתָיו֮\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the people|נַפְשׁ֣וֹת\rb* \rb of his household|בֵּיתוֹ֒\rb*, \rb along with|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb his livestock|מִקְנֵ֣הוּ\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb his other animals|בְּהֶמְתּ֗וֹ\rb*,\rb |וְאֵת֙\rb* \rb and all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the property|קִנְיָנ֔וֹ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb he had acquired|רָכַ֖שׁ\rb* \rb in Canaan|כְּנָ֑עַן\rb*, \rb and he moved|וַיֵּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb*\rb |אֶ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb a land|בְּאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb far away from|מִפְּנֵ֖י\rb* \rb his brother|אָחִֽיו׃\rb* \rb Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֥ב\rb*. \v 7 \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb their possessions|רְכוּשָׁ֛ם\rb* \rb were|הָיָ֧ה\rb* \rb too great|רָ֖ב\rb* \rb for them to dwell|מִשֶּׁ֣בֶת\rb* \rb together|יַחְדָּ֑ו\rb*; \rb the land|אֶ֤רֶץ\rb* \rb where they stayed|מְגֽוּרֵיהֶם֙\rb* \rb could|יָֽכְלָ֜ה\rb* \rb not|וְלֹ֨א\rb* \rb support them|לָשֵׂ֣את\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֔ם\rb* \rb because|מִפְּנֵ֖י\rb* \rb of their livestock|מִקְנֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 8 \rb So Esau|עֵשָׂו֙\rb*\rb |עֵשָׂ֖ו\rb* \rb (that is|ה֥וּא\rb*, \rb Edom|אֱדֽוֹם׃\rb*) \rb settled|וַיֵּ֤שֶׁב\rb* \rb in the area of Mount|בְּהַ֣ר\rb* \rb Seir|שֵׂעִ֔יר\rb*.
\p \v 9 \rb This|וְאֵ֛לֶּה\rb* \rb is the account|תֹּלְד֥וֹת\rb* \rb of Esau|עֵשָׂ֖ו\rb*, \rb the father|אֲבִ֣י\rb* \rb of the Edomites|אֱד֑וֹם\rb*, \rb in the area of Mount|בְּהַ֖ר\rb* \rb Seir|שֵׂעִֽיר׃\rb*.
\p \v 10 \rb These|אֵ֖לֶּה\rb* \rb are the names|שְׁמ֣וֹת\rb* \rb of Esau’s|עֵשָׂ֑ו\rb* \rb sons|בְּנֵֽי־\rb*: \rb Eliphaz|אֱלִיפַ֗ז\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Esau’s|עֵשָׂ֔ו\rb* \rb wife|אֵ֣שֶׁת\rb* \rb Adah|עָדָה֙\rb*, \rb and Reuel|רְעוּאֵ֕ל\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Esau’s|עֵשָֽׂו׃\rb* \rb wife|אֵ֥שֶׁת\rb* \rb Basemath|בָּשְׂמַ֖ת\rb*.
\p \v 11 \rb The sons|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Eliphaz|אֱלִיפָ֑ז\rb* \rb were|וַיִּהְי֖וּ\rb* \rb Teman|תֵּימָ֣ן\rb*, \rb Omar|אוֹמָ֔ר\rb*, \rb Zepho|צְפ֥וֹ\rb*, \rb Gatam|וְגַעְתָּ֖ם\rb*, \rb and Kenaz|וּקְנַֽז׃\rb*. \v 12 \rb Additionally, Timna|וְתִמְנַ֣ע׀\rb*,\rb |הָיְתָ֣ה\rb* \rb a concubine|פִילֶ֗גֶשׁ\rb* \rb of Esau’s|עֵשָׂ֔ו\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb Eliphaz|לֶֽאֱלִיפַז֙\rb*, \rb gave birth to|וַתֵּ֥לֶד\rb* \rb Amalek|עֲמָלֵ֑ק\rb*\rb |לֶאֱלִיפַ֖ז\rb*.\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb These|אֵ֕לֶּה\rb* \rb are the grandsons|בְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Esau’s|עֵשָֽׂו׃\rb* \rb wife|אֵ֥שֶׁת\rb* \rb Adah|עָדָ֖ה\rb*.
\p \v 13 \rb These are|וְאֵ֙לֶּה֙\rb* \rb the sons|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Reuel|רְעוּאֵ֔ל\rb*: \rb Nahath|נַ֥חַת\rb*, \rb Zerah|וָזֶ֖רַח\rb*, \rb Shammah|שַׁמָּ֣ה\rb*, \rb and Mizzah|וּמִזָּ֑ה\rb*. \rb They|אֵ֣לֶּ֣ה\rb* \rb are|הָי֔וּ\rb* \rb the grandsons|בְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Esau’s|עֵשָֽׂו׃\rb* \rb wife|אֵ֥שֶׁת\rb* \rb Basemath|בָשְׂמַ֖ת\rb*.
\p \v 14 \rb These|וְאֵ֣לֶּה\rb* \rb are|הָי֗וּ\rb* \rb the sons|בְּנֵ֨י\rb* \rb of Esau’s|עֵשָׂ֑ו\rb* \rb wife|אֵ֣שֶׁת\rb* \rb Oholibamah|אָהֳלִיבָמָ֧ה\rb* (\rb daughter|בַת־\rb* \rb of Anah|עֲנָ֛ה\rb* \rb and granddaughter|בַּת־\rb* \rb of Zibeon|צִבְע֖וֹן\rb*) \rb whom she bore|וַתֵּ֣לֶד\rb* \rb to Esau|לְעֵשָׂ֔ו\rb*:\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Jeush|יְעִישׁ\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Jalam|יַעְלָ֖ם\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and Korah|קֹֽרַח׃\rb*.
\p \v 15 \rb These|אֵ֖לֶּה\rb* \rb are the chiefs|אַלּוּפֵ֣י\rb* \rb among the sons|בְנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Esau|עֵשָׂ֑ו\rb*. \rb The sons|בְּנֵ֤י\rb* \rb of Eliphaz|אֱלִיפַז֙\rb* \rb the firstborn|בְּכ֣וֹר\rb* \rb of Esau|עֵשָׂ֔ו\rb*: \rb Chiefs|אַלּ֤וּף\rb* \rb Teman|תֵּימָן֙\rb*,\rb |אַלּ֣וּף\rb* \rb Omar|אוֹמָ֔ר\rb*,\rb |אַלּ֥וּף\rb* \rb Zepho|צְפ֖וֹ\rb*,\rb |אַלּ֥וּף\rb* \rb Kenaz|קְנַֽז׃\rb*, \v 16 \rb |אַלּֽוּף־\rb* \rb Korah|קֹ֛רַח\rb*,\f + \fr 36:16 \ft Hebrew; SP (also in verse 11 and 1 Chronicles 1:36) does not include \fqa Korah\ft .\f*\rb |אַלּ֥וּף\rb* \rb Gatam|גַּעְתָּ֖ם\rb*,\rb |אַלּ֣וּף\rb* \rb and Amalek|עֲמָלֵ֑ק\rb*. \rb They|אֵ֣לֶּה\rb* \rb are the chiefs|אַלּוּפֵ֤י\rb* \rb of Eliphaz|אֱלִיפַז֙\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Edom|אֱד֔וֹם\rb*, \rb and they|אֵ֖לֶּה\rb* \rb are the grandsons|בְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Adah|עָדָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 17 \rb These|וְאֵ֗לֶּה\rb* \rb are the sons|בְּנֵ֤י\rb* \rb of Esau’s|עֵשָׂ֔ו\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb Reuel|רְעוּאֵל֙\rb*: \rb Chiefs|אַלּ֥וּף\rb* \rb Nahath|נַ֙חַת֙\rb*,\rb |אַלּ֣וּף\rb* \rb Zerah|זֶ֔רַח\rb*,\rb |אַלּ֥וּף\rb* \rb Shammah|שַׁמָּ֖ה\rb*,\rb |אַלּ֣וּף\rb* \rb and Mizzah|מִזָּ֑ה\rb*. \rb They|אֵ֣לֶּה\rb* \rb are the chiefs|אַלּוּפֵ֤י\rb* \rb descended from Reuel|רְעוּאֵל֙\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Edom|אֱד֔וֹם\rb*, \rb and they|אֵ֕לֶּה\rb* \rb are the grandsons|בְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Esau’s|עֵשָֽׂו׃\rb* \rb wife|אֵ֥שֶׁת\rb* \rb Basemath|בָשְׂמַ֖ת\rb*.
\p \v 18 \rb These|וְאֵ֗לֶּה\rb* \rb are the sons|בְּנֵ֤י\rb* \rb of Esau’s|עֵשָׂ֔ו\rb* \rb wife|אֵ֣שֶׁת\rb* \rb Oholibamah|אָהֳלִֽיבָמָה֙\rb*: \rb Chiefs|אַלּ֥וּף\rb* \rb Jeush|יְע֛וּשׁ\rb*,\rb |אַלּ֥וּף\rb* \rb Jalam|יַעְלָ֖ם\rb*,\rb |אַלּ֣וּף\rb* \rb and Korah|קֹ֑רַח\rb*. \rb They|אֵ֣לֶּה\rb* \rb are the chiefs|אַלּוּפֵ֞י\rb* \rb descended from Esau’s|עֵשָֽׂו׃\rb* \rb wife|אֵ֥שֶׁת\rb* \rb Oholibamah|אָֽהֳלִיבָמָ֛ה\rb*, \rb the daughter|בַּת־\rb* \rb of Anah|עֲנָ֖ה\rb*.
\p \v 19 \rb All these|אֵ֧לֶּה\rb* \rb are the sons|בְנֵי־\rb* \rb of Esau|עֵשָׂ֛ו\rb* \rb (that is|ה֥וּא\rb*, \rb Edom|אֱדֽוֹם׃ס\rb*), \rb and they|וְאֵ֥לֶּה\rb* \rb were their chiefs|אַלּוּפֵיהֶ֖ם\rb*.
\s1 The Descendants of Seir
\p \v 20 \rb These|אֵ֤לֶּה\rb* \rb are the sons|בְנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Seir|שֵׂעִיר֙\rb* \rb the Horite|הַחֹרִ֔י\rb*, \rb who were living|יֹשְׁבֵ֖י\rb* \rb in the land|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb*: \rb Lotan|לוֹטָ֥ן\rb*, \rb Shobal|וְשׁוֹבָ֖ל\rb*, \rb Zibeon|וְצִבְע֥וֹן\rb*, \rb Anah|וַעֲנָֽה׃\rb*, \v 21 \rb Dishon|וְדִשׁ֥וֹן\rb*, \rb Ezer|וְאֵ֖צֶר\rb*, \rb and Dishan|וְדִישָׁ֑ן\rb*. \rb They|אֵ֣לֶּה\rb* \rb are the chiefs|אַלּוּפֵ֧י\rb* \rb of the Horites|הַחֹרִ֛י\rb*, \rb the descendants|בְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Seir|שֵׂעִ֖יר\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Edom|אֱדֽוֹם׃\rb*.
\p \v 22 \rb The sons|בְנֵי־\rb* \rb of Lotan|לוֹטָ֖ן\rb* \rb were|וַיִּהְי֥וּ\rb* \rb Hori|חֹרִ֣י\rb* \rb and Hemam|וְהֵימָ֑ם\rb*.\f + \fr 36:22 \fqa Hemam \ft is a variant of \fqa Homam\ft ; see 1 Chronicles 1:39.\f* \rb Timna|תִּמְנָֽע׃\rb* \rb was Lotan’s|לוֹטָ֖ן\rb* \rb sister|וַאֲח֥וֹת\rb*.
\p \v 23 \rb These|וְאֵ֙לֶּה֙\rb* \rb are the sons|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Shobal|שׁוֹבָ֔ל\rb*: \rb Alvan|עַלְוָ֥ן\rb*, \rb Manahath|וּמָנַ֖חַת\rb*, \rb Ebal|וְעֵיבָ֑ל\rb*, \rb Shepho|שְׁפ֖וֹ\rb*, \rb and Onam|וְאוֹנָֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 24 \rb These|וְאֵ֥לֶּה\rb* \rb are the sons|בְנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Zibeon|צִבְע֖וֹן\rb*: \rb Aiah|וְאַיָּ֣ה\rb* \rb and Anah|וַעֲנָ֑ה\rb*. (\rb This is|ה֣וּא\rb* \rb the Anah|עֲנָ֗ה\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb found|מָצָ֤א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the hot springs|הַיֵּמִם֙\rb* \rb in the wilderness|בַּמִּדְבָּ֔ר\rb* \rb as he was pasturing|בִּרְעֹת֥וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the donkeys|הַחֲמֹרִ֖ים\rb* \rb of his father|אָבִֽיו׃\rb* \rb Zibeon|לְצִבְע֥וֹן\rb*.)
\p \v 25 \rb These|וְאֵ֥לֶּה\rb* \rb are the children|בְנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Anah|עֲנָ֖ה\rb*: \rb Dishon|דִּשֹׁ֑ן\rb* \rb and Oholibamah|וְאָהֳלִיבָמָ֖ה\rb* \rb daughter|בַּת־\rb* \rb of Anah|עֲנָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 26 \rb These|וְאֵ֖לֶּה\rb* \rb are the sons|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Dishon|דִישָׁ֑ן\rb*:\f + \fr 36:26 \ft Hebrew \fqa Dishan\ft , a variant of \fqa Dishon\f* \rb Hemdan|חֶמְדָּ֥ן\rb*, \rb Eshban|וְאֶשְׁבָּ֖ן\rb*, \rb Ithran|וְיִתְרָ֥ן\rb*, \rb and Cheran|וּכְרָֽן׃\rb*.
\p \v 27 \rb These|אֵ֖לֶּה\rb* \rb are the sons|בְּנֵי־\rb* \rb of Ezer|אֵ֑צֶר\rb*: \rb Bilhan|בִּלְהָ֥ן\rb*, \rb Zaavan|וְזַעֲוָ֖ן\rb*, \rb and Akan|וַעֲקָֽן׃\rb*.
\p \v 28 \rb These|אֵ֥לֶּה\rb* \rb are the sons|בְנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Dishan|דִישָׁ֖ן\rb*: \rb Uz|ע֥וּץ\rb* \rb and Aran|וַאֲרָֽן׃\rb*.
\p \v 29 \rb These|אֵ֖לֶּה\rb* \rb are the chiefs|אַלּוּפֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the Horites|הַחֹרִ֑י\rb*: \rb Chiefs|אַלּ֤וּף\rb* \rb Lotan|לוֹטָן֙\rb*,\rb |אַלּ֣וּף\rb* \rb Shobal|שׁוֹבָ֔ל\rb*,\rb |אַלּ֥וּף\rb* \rb Zibeon|צִבְע֖וֹן\rb*,\rb |אַלּ֥וּף\rb* \rb Anah|עֲנָֽה׃\rb*, \v 30 \rb |אַלּ֥וּף\rb* \rb Dishon|דִּשֹׁ֛ן\rb*,\rb |אַלּ֥וּף\rb* \rb Ezer|אֵ֖צֶר\rb*,\rb |אַלּ֣וּף\rb* \rb and Dishan|דִּישָׁ֑ן\rb*. \rb They|אֵ֣לֶּה\rb* \rb are the chiefs|אַלּוּפֵ֧י\rb* \rb of the Horites|הַחֹרִ֛י\rb*, \rb according to their divisions|לְאַלֻּפֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Seir|שֵׂעִֽיר׃פ\rb*.
\s1 The Kings of Edom
\p \v 31 \rb These|וְאֵ֙לֶּה֙\rb* \rb are the kings|הַמְּלָכִ֔ים\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb reigned|מָלְכ֖וּ\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Edom|אֱד֑וֹם\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb any king|מֶ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb reigned|מְלָךְ־\rb* \rb over the Israelites|לִבְנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*:\f + \fr 36:31 \ft Or \fqa before an Israelite king reigned over them:\f*
\b 
\li1 \v 32 \rb Bela|בֶּ֖לַע\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Beor|בְּע֑וֹר\rb* \rb reigned|וַיִּמְלֹ֣ךְ\rb* \rb in Edom|בֶּאֱד֔וֹם\rb*; \rb the name|וְשֵׁ֥ם\rb* \rb of his city|עִיר֖וֹ\rb* \rb was Dinhabah|דִּנְהָֽבָה׃\rb*.
\b 
\li1 \v 33 \rb When Bela|בָּ֑לַע\rb* \rb died|וַיָּ֖מָת\rb*, \rb Jobab|יוֹבָ֥ב\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Zerah|זֶ֖רַח\rb* \rb from Bozrah|מִבָּצְרָֽה׃\rb* \rb reigned|וַיִּמְלֹ֣ךְ\rb* \rb in his place|תַּחְתָּ֔יו\rb*.
\b 
\li1 \v 34 \rb When Jobab|יוֹבָ֑ב\rb* \rb died|וַיָּ֖מָת\rb*, \rb Husham|חֻשָׁ֖ם\rb* \rb from the land|מֵאֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of the Temanites|הַתֵּימָנִֽי׃\rb* \rb reigned|וַיִּמְלֹ֣ךְ\rb* \rb in his place|תַּחְתָּ֔יו\rb*.
\b 
\li1 \v 35 \rb When Husham|חֻשָׁ֑ם\rb* \rb died|וַיָּ֖מָת\rb*, \rb Hadad|הֲדַ֣ד\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Bedad|בְּדַ֗ד\rb*, \rb who defeated|הַמַּכֶּ֤ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Midian|מִדְיָן֙\rb* \rb in the country|בִּשְׂדֵ֣ה\rb* \rb of Moab|מוֹאָ֔ב\rb*, \rb reigned|וַיִּמְלֹ֨ךְ\rb* \rb in his place|תַּחְתָּ֜יו\rb*. \rb And the name|וְשֵׁ֥ם\rb* \rb of his city|עִיר֖וֹ\rb* \rb was Avith|עֲוִֽית׃\rb*.
\b 
\li1 \v 36 \rb When Hadad|הֲדָ֑ד\rb* \rb died|וַיָּ֖מָת\rb*, \rb Samlah|שַׂמְלָ֖ה\rb* \rb from Masrekah|מִמַּשְׂרֵקָֽה׃\rb* \rb reigned|וַיִּמְלֹ֣ךְ\rb* \rb in his place|תַּחְתָּ֔יו\rb*.
\b 
\li1 \v 37 \rb When Samlah|שַׂמְלָ֑ה\rb* \rb died|וַיָּ֖מָת\rb*, \rb Shaul|שָׁא֖וּל\rb* \rb from Rehoboth|מֵרְחֹב֥וֹת\rb* \rb on the Euphrates|הַנָּהָֽר׃\rb*\f + \fr 36:37 \ft Hebrew \fqa the River\f* \rb reigned|וַיִּמְלֹ֣ךְ\rb* \rb in his place|תַּחְתָּ֔יו\rb*.
\b 
\li1 \v 38 \rb When Shaul|שָׁא֑וּל\rb* \rb died|וַיָּ֖מָת\rb*,\rb |בַּ֥עַל\rb* \rb Baal-hanan|חָנָ֖ן\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Achbor|עַכְבּֽוֹר׃\rb* \rb reigned|וַיִּמְלֹ֣ךְ\rb* \rb in his place|תַּחְתָּ֔יו\rb*.
\b 
\li1 \v 39 \rb |בַּ֣עַל\rb* \rb When Baal-hanan|חָנָ֣ן\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Achbor|עַכְבּוֹר֒\rb* \rb died|וַיָּמָת֮\rb*, \rb Hadad|הֲדַ֔ר\rb*\f + \fr 36:39 \ft Some MT manuscripts, SP, and Syriac (see also 1 Chronicles 1:50); other MT manuscripts \fqa Hadar\f* \rb reigned|וַיִּמְלֹ֤ךְ\rb* \rb in his place|תַּחְתָּיו֙\rb*. \rb His city|עִיר֖וֹ\rb* \rb was named|וְשֵׁ֥ם\rb* \rb Pau|פָּ֑עוּ\rb*, \rb and his wife’s|אִשְׁתּ֤וֹ\rb* \rb name|וְשֵׁ֨ם\rb* \rb was Mehetabel|מְהֵֽיטַבְאֵל֙\rb* \rb daughter|בַּת־\rb* \rb of Matred|מַטְרֵ֔ד\rb*, \rb the daughter|בַּ֖ת\rb*\rb |מֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Me-zahab|זָהָֽב׃\rb*.
\p \v 40 \rb These|וְ֠אֵלֶּה\rb* \rb are the names|שְׁמ֞וֹת\rb* \rb of Esau’s|עֵשָׂו֙\rb* \rb chiefs|אַלּוּפֵ֤י\rb*, \rb according to their families|לְמִשְׁפְּחֹתָ֔ם\rb* \rb and regions|לִמְקֹמֹתָ֖ם\rb*, \rb by their names|בִּשְׁמֹתָ֑ם\rb*: \rb Chiefs|אַלּ֥וּף\rb* \rb Timna|תִּמְנָ֛ע\rb*,\rb |אַלּ֥וּף\rb* \rb Alvah|עַֽלְוָ֖ה\rb*,\rb |אַלּ֥וּף\rb* \rb Jetheth|יְתֵֽת׃\rb*, \v 41 \rb |אַלּ֧וּף\rb* \rb Oholibamah|אָהֳלִיבָמָ֛ה\rb*,\rb |אַלּ֥וּף\rb* \rb Elah|אֵלָ֖ה\rb*,\rb |אַלּ֥וּף\rb* \rb Pinon|פִּינֹֽן׃\rb*, \v 42 \rb |אַלּ֥וּף\rb* \rb Kenaz|קְנַ֛ז\rb*,\rb |אַלּ֥וּף\rb* \rb Teman|תֵּימָ֖ן\rb*,\rb |אַלּ֥וּף\rb* \rb Mibzar|מִבְצָֽר׃\rb*, \v 43 \rb |אַלּ֥וּף\rb* \rb Magdiel|מַגְדִּיאֵ֖ל\rb*,\rb |אַלּ֣וּף\rb* \rb and Iram|עִירָ֑ם\rb*. \rb These|אֵ֣לֶּה׀\rb* \rb were the chiefs|אַלּוּפֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Edom|אֱד֗וֹם\rb*, \rb according to their settlements|לְמֹֽשְׁבֹתָם֙\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb they possessed|אֲחֻזָּתָ֔ם\rb*.\rb |ה֥וּא\rb* \rb Esau|עֵשָׂ֖ו\rb* \rb was the father|אֲבִ֥י\rb* \rb of the Edomites|אֱדֽוֹם׃פ\rb*.
\c 37
\s1 Joseph’s Dreams
\p \v 1 \rb Now Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֔ב\rb* \rb lived|וַיֵּ֣שֶׁב\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb where his father|אָבִ֑יו\rb* \rb had resided|מְגוּרֵ֣י\rb*, \rb the land|בְּאֶ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb of Canaan|כְּנָֽעַן׃\rb*.
\p \v 2 \rb This|אֵ֣לֶּה׀\rb* \rb is the account|תֹּלְד֣וֹת\rb* \rb of Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֗ב\rb*. \rb When Joseph|יוֹסֵ֞ף\rb* \rb was seventeen|שְׁבַֽע־\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵ֤ה\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָה֙\rb* \rb old|בֶּן־\rb*, \rb he was|הָיָ֨ה\rb* \rb tending|רֹעֶ֤ה\rb* \rb the flock|בַּצֹּ֔אן\rb*\rb |וְה֣וּא\rb* \rb with|אֶת־\rb* \rb his brothers|אֶחָיו֙\rb*,\rb |נַ֗עַר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the sons|בְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of his father’s|אָבִ֑יו\rb* \rb wives|נְשֵׁ֣י\rb* \rb Bilhah|בִלְהָ֛ה\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb*\rb |בְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb and Zilpah|זִלְפָּ֖ה\rb*, \rb and he|יוֹסֵ֛ף\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb brought|וַיָּבֵ֥א\rb* \rb their father|אֲבִיהֶֽם׃\rb* \rb a bad|רָעָ֖ה\rb* \rb report|דִּבָּתָ֥ם\rb* \rb about them|אֶל־\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb Now Israel|וְיִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb loved|אָהַ֤ב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Joseph|יוֹסֵף֙\rb* \rb more than|מִכָּל־\rb* \rb his other sons|בָּנָ֔יו\rb*, \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb Joseph|ה֖וּא\rb* \rb had been born|בֶן־\rb* \rb to him|ל֑וֹ\rb* \rb in his old age|זְקֻנִ֥ים\rb*; \rb so he made|וְעָ֥שָׂה\rb* \rb him|ל֖וֹ\rb* \rb a robe|כְּתֹ֥נֶת\rb* \rb of many colors|פַּסִּֽים׃\rb*.\f + \fr 37:3 \ft Possibly \fqa a robe with long sleeves\ft ; also in verses 23 and 32\f* \v 4 \rb When Joseph’s brothers|אֶחָ֗יו\rb* \rb saw|וַיִּרְא֣וּ\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb their father|אֲבִיהֶם֙\rb* \rb loved|אָהַ֤ב\rb* \rb him|אֹת֞וֹ\rb* \rb more than any|מִכָּל־\rb* \rb of them|אֶחָ֔יו\rb*, \rb they hated|וַֽיִּשְׂנְא֖וּ\rb* \rb him|אֹת֑וֹ\rb* \rb and could|יָכְל֖וּ\rb* \rb not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb speak|דַּבְּר֥וֹ\rb* \rb a kind word to him|לְשָׁלֹֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 5 \rb Then Joseph|יוֹסֵף֙\rb* \rb had a dream|וַיַּחֲלֹ֤ם\rb*\rb |חֲל֔וֹם\rb*, \rb and when he told|וַיַּגֵּ֖ד\rb* \rb it to his brothers|לְאֶחָ֑יו\rb*, \rb they hated|שְׂנֹ֥א\rb* \rb him|אֹתֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb even more|וַיּוֹסִ֥פוּ\rb*\rb |ע֖וֹד\rb*. \v 6 \rb He said|וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb* \rb to them|אֲלֵיהֶ֑ם\rb*, “\rb Listen|שִׁמְעוּ־\rb*\rb |נָ֕א\rb* \rb to this|הַזֶּ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb dream I had|חָלָֽמְתִּי׃\rb*\rb |הַחֲל֥וֹם\rb*: \v 7 \rb |וְ֠הִנֵּה\rb* \rb We|אֲנַ֜חְנוּ\rb* \rb were binding|מְאַלְּמִ֤ים\rb* \rb sheaves of grain|אֲלֻמִּים֙\rb* \rb in|בְּת֣וֹךְ\rb* \rb the field|הַשָּׂדֶ֔ה\rb*, \rb and suddenly|וְהִנֵּ֛ה\rb* \rb my sheaf|אֲלֻמָּתִ֖י\rb* \rb rose|קָ֥מָה\rb* \rb and|וְגַם־\rb* \rb stood upright|נִצָּ֑בָה\rb*\rb |וְהִנֵּ֤ה\rb*, \rb while your sheaves|אֲלֻמֹּ֣תֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb gathered around|תְסֻבֶּ֙ינָה֙\rb* \rb and bowed down|וַתִּֽשְׁתַּחֲוֶ֖יןָ\rb* \rb to mine|לַאֲלֻמָּתִֽי׃\rb*.”
\p \v 8 “\rb Do you intend to reign|הֲמָלֹ֤ךְ\rb*\rb |תִּמְלֹךְ֙\rb* \rb over us|עָלֵ֔ינוּ\rb*?”\rb |אִם־\rb* \rb his brothers|אֶחָ֔יו\rb* \rb asked|וַיֹּ֤אמְרוּ\rb*. “\rb Will you actually rule|מָשׁ֥וֹל\rb*\rb |תִּמְשֹׁ֖ל\rb* \rb us|בָּ֑נוּ\rb*?” \rb So they hated|שְׂנֹ֣א\rb* \rb him|אֹת֔וֹ\rb* \rb even more|וַיּוֹסִ֤פוּ\rb*\rb |עוֹד֙\rb* \rb because of|עַל־\rb* \rb his dream|חֲלֹמֹתָ֖יו\rb*\rb |וְעַל־\rb* \rb and his statements|דְּבָרָֽיו׃\rb*.
\p \v 9 \rb Then Joseph had another|עוֹד֙\rb*\rb |אַחֵ֔ר\rb* \rb dream|וַיַּחֲלֹ֥ם\rb*\rb |חֲל֣וֹם\rb* \rb and told|וַיְסַפֵּ֥ר\rb*\rb |אֹת֖וֹ\rb* \rb it to his brothers|לְאֶחָ֑יו\rb*. “\rb Look|הִנֵּ֨ה\rb*,” \rb he said|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*, “\rb I had another|ע֔וֹד\rb*\rb |וְהִנֵּ֧ה\rb* \rb dream|חָלַ֤מְתִּֽי\rb*\rb |חֲלוֹם֙\rb*, \rb and this time the sun|הַשֶּׁ֣מֶשׁ\rb* \rb and moon|וְהַיָּרֵ֗חַ\rb* \rb and eleven|וְאַחַ֤ד\rb*\rb |עָשָׂר֙\rb* \rb stars|כּֽוֹכָבִ֔ים\rb* \rb were bowing down|מִֽשְׁתַּחֲוִ֖ים\rb* \rb to me|לִֽי׃\rb*.”
\p \v 10 \rb He told|וַיְסַפֵּ֣ר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb his father|אָבִיו֮\rb*\rb |וְאֶל־\rb* \rb and brothers|אֶחָיו֒\rb*, \rb but his father|אָבִ֔יו\rb* \rb rebuked|וַיִּגְעַר־\rb* \rb him|בּ֣וֹ\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*\rb |ל֔וֹ\rb*, “\rb What|מָ֛ה\rb* \rb is this dream|הַזֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb you have had|הַחֲל֥וֹם\rb*\rb |חָלָ֑מְתָּ\rb*? \rb Will your mother|וְאִמְּךָ֣\rb* \rb and brothers|וְאַחֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb and I|אֲנִי֙\rb* \rb actually|הֲב֣וֹא\rb* \rb come|נָב֗וֹא\rb* \rb and bow down|לְהִשְׁתַּחֲוֺ֥ת\rb* \rb to the ground|אָֽרְצָה׃\rb* \rb before you|לְךָ֖\rb*?” \v 11 \rb And his brothers|אֶחָ֑יו\rb* \rb were jealous|וַיְקַנְאוּ־\rb* \rb of him|ב֖וֹ\rb*, \rb but his father|וְאָבִ֖יו\rb* \rb kept in mind|שָׁמַ֥ר\rb* \rb what he had said|הַדָּבָֽר׃\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*.
\s1 Joseph Sold into Egypt
\p \v 12 \rb Some time later, Joseph’s brothers|אֶחָ֑יו\rb* \rb had gone|וַיֵּלְכ֖וּ\rb* \rb to pasture|לִרְע֛וֹת\rb*\rb |אֶׄתׄ־\rb* \rb their father’s|אֲבִיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb flocks|צֹ֥אן\rb* \rb near Shechem|בִּשְׁכֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 13 \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֜ל\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb him|יוֹסֵ֗ף\rb*, “\rb Are not|הֲל֤וֹא\rb* \rb your brothers|אַחֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb pasturing|רֹעִ֣ים\rb* \rb the flocks at Shechem|בִּשְׁכֶ֔ם\rb*? \rb Get ready|לְכָ֖ה\rb*; \rb I am sending|וְאֶשְׁלָחֲךָ֣\rb* \rb you to them|אֲלֵיהֶ֑ם\rb*.”
\p “\rb I am ready|הִנֵּֽנִי׃\rb*,” \rb Joseph replied|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb*.
\p \v 14 \rb Then Israel told|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb him|ל֗וֹ\rb*, “\rb Go|לֶךְ־\rb* \rb now|נָ֨א\rb* \rb and see|רְאֵ֜ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |שְׁל֤וֹם\rb* \rb how your brothers|אַחֶ֙יךָ֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and the flocks|הַצֹּ֔אן\rb* \rb are faring|שְׁל֣וֹם\rb*, \rb and bring word|דָּבָ֑ר\rb* \rb back to me|וַהֲשִׁבֵ֖נִי\rb*.”
\p \rb So he sent him off|וַיִּשְׁלָחֵ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb from the Valley|מֵעֵ֣מֶק\rb* \rb of Hebron|חֶבְר֔וֹן\rb*. \rb And when Joseph arrived|וַיָּבֹ֖א\rb* \rb in Shechem|שְׁכֶֽמָה׃\rb*, \v 15 \rb |וְהִנֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb a man|אִ֔ישׁ\rb* \rb found him|וַיִּמְצָאֵ֣הוּ\rb* \rb wandering|תֹעֶ֖ה\rb* \rb in the field|בַּשָּׂדֶ֑ה\rb* \rb and asked|וַיִּשְׁאָלֵ֧הוּ\rb*,\rb |הָאִ֛ישׁ\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֖ר\rb* “\rb What|מַה־\rb* \rb are you looking for|תְּבַקֵּֽשׁ׃\rb*?”
\p \v 16 “\rb I am|אָנֹכִ֣י\rb* \rb looking for|מְבַקֵּ֑שׁ\rb* \rb my brothers|אַחַ֖י\rb*,” \rb Joseph replied|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*.\rb |אֶת־\rb* “\rb Can you please tell|הַגִּֽידָה־\rb*\rb |נָּ֣א\rb* \rb me|לִ֔י\rb* \rb where|אֵיפֹ֖ה\rb* \rb they|הֵ֥ם\rb* \rb are pasturing their flocks?|רֹעִֽים׃\rb*”
\p \v 17 “\rb They have moved on|נָסְע֣וּ\rb* \rb from here|מִזֶּ֔ה\rb*,”\rb |כִּ֤י\rb* \rb the man|הָאִישׁ֙\rb* \rb answered|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb*. “\rb I heard them|שָׁמַ֙עְתִּי֙\rb* \rb say|אֹֽמְרִ֔ים\rb*, ‘\rb Let us go|נֵלְכָ֖ה\rb* \rb to Dothan|דֹּתָ֑יְנָה\rb*.’” \rb So Joseph|יוֹסֵף֙\rb* \rb set out|וַיֵּ֤לֶךְ\rb* \rb after|אַחַ֣ר\rb* \rb his brothers|אֶחָ֔יו\rb* \rb and found them|וַיִּמְצָאֵ֖ם\rb* \rb at Dothan|בְּדֹתָֽן׃\rb*.
\p \v 18 \rb Now Joseph’s brothers saw|וַיִּרְא֥וּ\rb* \rb him|אֹת֖וֹ\rb* \rb in the distance|מֵרָחֹ֑ק\rb*, \rb and before|וּבְטֶ֙רֶם֙\rb* \rb he arrived|יִקְרַ֣ב\rb*,\rb |אֲלֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb they plotted|וַיִּֽתְנַכְּל֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֹת֖וֹ\rb* \rb to kill him|לַהֲמִיתֽוֹ׃\rb*. \v 19 “\rb Here|הִנֵּ֗ה\rb* \rb comes|בָּֽא׃\rb* \rb that|הַלָּזֶ֖ה\rb* \rb dreamer|בַּ֛עַל\rb*\rb |הַחֲלֹמ֥וֹת\rb*!” \rb they said|וַיֹּאמְר֖וּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb one|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb another|אָחִ֑יו\rb*. \v 20 “\rb Come|לְכ֣וּ\rb* \rb now|וְעַתָּ֣ה׀\rb*, \rb let us kill him|וְנַֽהַרְגֵ֗הוּ\rb* \rb and throw him|וְנַשְׁלִכֵ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb into one|בְּאַחַ֣ד\rb* \rb of the pits|הַבֹּר֔וֹת\rb*. \rb We can say|וְאָמַ֕רְנוּ\rb* \rb that a vicious|רָעָ֖ה\rb* \rb animal|חַיָּ֥ה\rb* \rb has devoured him|אֲכָלָ֑תְהוּ\rb*. \rb Then we shall see|וְנִרְאֶ֕ה\rb* \rb what|מַה־\rb* \rb becomes|יִּהְי֖וּ\rb* \rb of his dreams|חֲלֹמֹתָֽיו׃\rb*!”
\p \v 21 \rb When Reuben|רְאוּבֵ֔ן\rb* \rb heard this|וַיִּשְׁמַ֣ע\rb*, \rb he tried to rescue Joseph|וַיַּצִּלֵ֖הוּ\rb* \rb from their hands|מִיָּדָ֑ם\rb*. “\rb Let us not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb take|נַכֶּ֖נּוּ\rb* \rb his life|נָֽפֶשׁ׃\rb*,” \rb he said|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*. \v 22 “\rb Do not shed|תִּשְׁפְּכוּ־\rb* \rb his blood|דָם֒\rb*. \rb Throw|הַשְׁלִ֣יכוּ\rb* \rb him|אֹת֗וֹ\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּה֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb pit|הַבּ֤וֹר\rb* \rb in the wilderness|בַּמִּדְבָּ֔ר\rb*, \rb but do not|אַל־\rb* \rb lay|תִּשְׁלְחוּ־\rb* \rb a hand|וְיָ֖ד\rb* \rb on him|ב֑וֹ\rb*.” \rb Reuben|רְאוּבֵן֮\rb*\rb |אַל־\rb* \rb said this|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֲלֵהֶ֣ם׀\rb* \rb so that|לְמַ֗עַן\rb* \rb he could rescue|הַצִּ֤יל\rb* \rb Joseph|אֹתוֹ֙\rb* \rb from their hands|מִיָּדָ֔ם\rb* \rb and return him|לַהֲשִׁיב֖וֹ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his father|אָבִֽיו׃\rb*.
\p \v 23 \rb So|וַֽיְהִ֕י\rb* \rb when|כַּֽאֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb Joseph|יוֹסֵ֖ף\rb* \rb came|בָּ֥א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his brothers|אֶחָ֑יו\rb*, \rb they stripped|וַיַּפְשִׁ֤יטוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb him|יוֹסֵף֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb of his robe|כֻּתָּנְתּ֔וֹ\rb* —\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the robe|כְּתֹ֥נֶת\rb* \rb of many colors|הַפַּסִּ֖ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb he was wearing|עָלָֽיו׃\rb* — \v 24 \rb and they took him|וַיִּ֨קָּחֻ֔הוּ\rb* \rb and threw|וַיַּשְׁלִ֥כוּ\rb* \rb him|אֹת֖וֹ\rb* \rb into the pit|הַבֹּ֑רָה\rb*. \rb Now the pit|וְהַבּ֣וֹר\rb* \rb was empty|רֵ֔ק\rb*, \rb with no|אֵ֥ין\rb* \rb water|מָֽיִם׃\rb* \rb in it|בּ֖וֹ\rb*.
\p \v 25 \rb And as they sat down|וַיֵּשְׁבוּ֮\rb* \rb to eat|לֶֽאֱכָל־\rb* \rb a meal|לֶחֶם֒\rb*, \rb they looked up|וַיִּשְׂא֤וּ\rb*\rb |עֵֽינֵיהֶם֙\rb*\rb |וַיִּרְא֔וּ\rb* \rb and saw|וְהִנֵּה֙\rb* \rb a caravan|אֹרְחַ֣ת\rb* \rb of Ishmaelites|יִשְׁמְעֵאלִ֔ים\rb* \rb coming|בָּאָ֖ה\rb* \rb from Gilead|מִגִּלְעָ֑ד\rb*. \rb Their camels|וּגְמַלֵּיהֶ֣ם\rb* \rb were carrying|נֹֽשְׂאִ֗ים\rb* \rb spices|נְכֹאת֙\rb*, \rb balm|וּצְרִ֣י\rb*, \rb and myrrh|וָלֹ֔ט\rb* \rb on their way|הוֹלְכִ֖ים\rb* \rb down|לְהוֹרִ֥יד\rb* \rb to Egypt|מִצְרָֽיְמָה׃\rb*.
\p \v 26 \rb Then Judah|יְהוּדָ֖ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his brothers|אֶחָ֑יו\rb*, “\rb What|מַה־\rb* \rb profit will we gain|בֶּ֗צַע\rb* \rb if|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb we kill|נַהֲרֹג֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb our brother|אָחִ֔ינוּ\rb* \rb and cover up|וְכִסִּ֖ינוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his blood|דָּמֽוֹ׃\rb*? \v 27 \rb Come|לְכ֞וּ\rb*, \rb let us sell him|וְנִמְכְּרֶ֣נּוּ\rb* \rb to the Ishmaelites|לַיִּשְׁמְעֵאלִ֗ים\rb* \rb and not|אַל־\rb* \rb lay|תְּהִי־\rb* \rb a hand|וְיָדֵ֙נוּ֙\rb* \rb on him|ב֔וֹ\rb*; \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb he|ה֑וּא\rb* \rb is our brother|אָחִ֥ינוּ\rb*, \rb our own flesh|בְשָׂרֵ֖נוּ\rb*.” \rb And they|אֶחָֽיו׃\rb* \rb agreed|וַֽיִּשְׁמְע֖וּ\rb*. \v 28 \rb So when the Midianite|מִדְיָנִ֜ים\rb* \rb traders|סֹֽחֲרִ֗ים\rb* \rb passed by|וַיַּֽעַבְרוּ֩\rb*,\rb |אֲנָשִׁ֨ים\rb* \rb his brothers pulled|וַֽיִּמְשְׁכוּ֙\rb*\rb |וַיַּֽעֲל֤וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Joseph|יוֹסֵף֙\rb* \rb out of|מִן־\rb* \rb the pit|הַבּ֔וֹר\rb* \rb and sold|וַיִּמְכְּר֧וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb him|יוֹסֵ֛ף\rb* \rb for twenty shekels|בְּעֶשְׂרִ֣ים\rb* \rb of silver|כָּ֑סֶף\rb*\f + \fr 37:28 \fqa 20 shekels \ft is approximately 8 ounces or 228 grams of silver.\f* \rb to the Ishmaelites|לַיִּשְׁמְעֵאלִ֖ים\rb*, \rb who took|וַיָּבִ֥יאוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb him|יוֹסֵ֖ף\rb* \rb to Egypt|מִצְרָֽיְמָה׃\rb*.
\p \v 29 \rb When Reuben|רְאוּבֵן֙\rb* \rb returned|וַיָּ֤שָׁב\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the pit|הַבּ֔וֹר\rb* \rb and saw|וְהִנֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb that Joseph|יוֹסֵ֖ף\rb* \rb was not there|אֵין־\rb*\rb |בַּבּ֑וֹר\rb*, \rb he tore|וַיִּקְרַ֖ע\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his clothes|בְּגָדָֽיו׃\rb*, \v 30 \rb returned|וַיָּ֥שָׁב\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his brothers|אֶחָ֖יו\rb*, \rb and said|וַיֹּאמַ֑ר\rb*, “\rb The boy|הַיֶּ֣לֶד\rb* \rb is gone|אֵינֶ֔נּוּ\rb*! \rb What am I going to do|וַאֲנִ֖י\rb*\rb |אָ֥נָה\rb*\rb |אֲנִי־\rb*\rb |בָֽא׃\rb*?”
\s1 Jacob Mourns Joseph
\p \v 31 \rb Then they took|וַיִּקְח֖וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Joseph’s|יוֹסֵ֑ף\rb* \rb robe|כְּתֹ֣נֶת\rb*, \rb slaughtered|וַֽיִּשְׁחֲטוּ֙\rb* \rb a young goat|שְׂעִ֣יר\rb*\rb |עִזִּ֔ים\rb*, \rb and dipped|וַיִּטְבְּל֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the robe|הַכֻּתֹּ֖נֶת\rb* \rb in its blood|בַּדָּֽם׃\rb*. \v 32 \rb They sent|וַֽיְשַׁלְּח֞וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the robe|כְּתֹ֣נֶת\rb* \rb of many colors|הַפַּסִּ֗ים\rb*\rb |וַיָּבִ֙יאוּ֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb their father|אֲבִיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּאמְר֖וּ\rb*, “\rb We found|מָצָ֑אנוּ\rb* \rb this|זֹ֣את\rb*. \rb Examine it|הַכֶּר־\rb* \rb to see whether|נָ֗א\rb* \rb it is|הִ֖וא\rb* \rb your son’s|בִּנְךָ֛\rb* \rb robe|הַכְּתֹ֧נֶת\rb* \rb or|אִם־\rb* \rb not|לֹֽא׃\rb*.”
\p \v 33 \rb His father recognized it|וַיַּכִּירָ֤הּ\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb*, “\rb It is my son’s|בְּנִ֔י\rb* \rb robe|כְּתֹ֣נֶת\rb*! \rb A vicious|רָעָ֖ה\rb* \rb animal|חַיָּ֥ה\rb* \rb has devoured him|אֲכָלָ֑תְהוּ\rb*. \rb Joseph|יוֹסֵֽף׃\rb* \rb has surely been torn to pieces|טָרֹ֥ף\rb*\rb |טֹרַ֖ף\rb*!” \v 34 \rb Then Jacob|יַעֲקֹב֙\rb* \rb tore|וַיִּקְרַ֤ע\rb* \rb his clothes|שִׂמְלֹתָ֔יו\rb*, \rb put|וַיָּ֥שֶׂם\rb* \rb sackcloth|שַׂ֖ק\rb* \rb around his waist|בְּמָתְנָ֑יו\rb*, \rb and mourned|וַיִּתְאַבֵּ֥ל\rb* \rb for|עַל־\rb* \rb his son|בְּנ֖וֹ\rb* \rb many|רַבִּֽים׃\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֥ים\rb*. \v 35 \rb |וַיָּקֻמוּ֩\rb* \rb All|כָל־\rb* \rb his sons|בָּנָ֨יו\rb*\rb |וְכָל־\rb* \rb and daughters|בְּנֹתָ֜יו\rb* \rb tried to comfort him|לְנַחֲמ֗וֹ\rb*, \rb but he refused|וַיְמָאֵן֙\rb* \rb to be comforted|לְהִתְנַחֵ֔ם\rb*. “\rb No, ” he said|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*.\rb |כִּֽי־\rb* “\rb I will go down|אֵרֵ֧ד\rb* \rb to Sheol|שְׁאֹ֑לָה\rb* \rb mourning|אָבֵ֖ל\rb* \rb for|אֶל־\rb* \rb my son|בְּנִ֛י\rb*.” \rb So his father|אָבִֽיו׃\rb* \rb wept|וַיֵּ֥בְךְּ\rb* \rb for him|אֹת֖וֹ\rb*.
\p \v 36 \rb Meanwhile, the Midianites|וְהַ֨מְּדָנִ֔ים\rb*\f + \fr 37:36 \ft Hebrew \fqa the Medanites\f* \rb sold|מָכְר֥וּ\rb* \rb Joseph|אֹת֖וֹ\rb* \rb in|אֶל־\rb* \rb Egypt|מִצְרָ֑יִם\rb* \rb to Potiphar|לְפֽוֹטִיפַר֙\rb*, \rb an officer|סְרִ֣יס\rb* \rb of Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹ֔ה\rb* \rb and captain|שַׂ֖ר\rb* \rb of the guard|הַטַּבָּחִֽים׃פ\rb*.
\c 38
\s1 Judah and Tamar
\p \v 1 \rb About|וַֽיְהִי֙\rb* \rb that|הַהִ֔וא\rb* \rb time|בָּעֵ֣ת\rb*, \rb Judah|יְהוּדָ֖ה\rb*\rb |מֵאֵ֣ת\rb* \rb left|וַיֵּ֥רֶד\rb* \rb his brothers|אֶחָ֑יו\rb* \rb and settled|וַיֵּ֛ט\rb* \rb near|עַד־\rb* \rb a man|אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb named|וּשְׁמ֥וֹ\rb* \rb Hirah|חִירָֽה׃\rb*, \rb an Adullamite|עֲדֻלָּמִ֖י\rb*. \v 2 \rb There|שָׁ֧ם\rb* \rb Judah|יְהוּדָ֛ה\rb* \rb saw|וַיַּרְא־\rb* \rb the daughter|בַּת־\rb* \rb of a Canaanite|כְּנַעֲנִ֖י\rb* \rb man|אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb named|וּשְׁמ֣וֹ\rb* \rb Shua|שׁ֑וּעַ\rb*, \rb and he took her as a wife|וַיִּקָּחֶ֖הָ\rb* \rb and slept with|וַיָּבֹ֥א\rb* \rb her|אֵלֶֽיהָ׃\rb*. \v 3 \rb So she conceived|וַתַּ֖הַר\rb* \rb and gave birth to|וַתֵּ֣לֶד\rb* \rb a son|בֵּ֑ן\rb*, \rb and Judah named|וַיִּקְרָ֥א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb him|שְׁמ֖וֹ\rb* \rb Er|עֵֽר׃\rb*. \v 4 \rb Again|ע֖וֹד\rb* \rb she conceived|וַתַּ֥הַר\rb* \rb and gave birth to|וַתֵּ֣לֶד\rb* \rb a son|בֵּ֑ן\rb*, \rb and she named|וַתִּקְרָ֥א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb him|שְׁמ֖וֹ\rb* \rb Onan|אוֹנָֽן׃\rb*. \v 5 \rb Then she gave birth to|וַתֵּ֣לֶד\rb* \rb another|וַתֹּ֤סֶף\rb*\rb |עוֹד֙\rb* \rb son|בֵּ֔ן\rb* \rb and named|וַתִּקְרָ֥א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb him|שְׁמ֖וֹ\rb* \rb Shelah|שֵׁלָ֑ה\rb*; \rb it was|וְהָיָ֥ה\rb* \rb at Chezib|בִכְזִ֖יב\rb* \rb that she gave birth to him|בְּלִדְתָּ֥הּ\rb*\rb |אֹתֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\p \v 6 \rb Now Judah|יְהוּדָ֛ה\rb* \rb acquired|וַיִּקַּ֧ח\rb* \rb a wife|אִשָּׁ֖ה\rb* \rb for Er|לְעֵ֣ר\rb*, \rb his firstborn|בְּכוֹר֑וֹ\rb*, \rb and her name|וּשְׁמָ֖הּ\rb* \rb was Tamar|תָּמָֽר׃\rb*. \v 7 \rb But|וַיְהִ֗י\rb* \rb Er|עֵ֚ר\rb*, \rb Judah’s|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb firstborn|בְּכ֣וֹר\rb*, \rb was wicked|רַ֖ע\rb* \rb in the sight|בְּעֵינֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*; \rb so the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb put him to death|וַיְמִתֵ֖הוּ\rb*. \v 8 \rb Then Judah|יְהוּדָה֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to Onan|לְאוֹנָ֔ן\rb*, “\rb Sleep with|בֹּ֛א\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb your brother’s|אָחִ֖יךָ\rb* \rb wife|אֵ֥שֶׁת\rb*. \rb Perform your duty as her brother-in-law|וְיַבֵּ֣ם\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֑הּ\rb* \rb and raise up|וְהָקֵ֥ם\rb* \rb offspring|זֶ֖רַע\rb* \rb for your brother|לְאָחִֽיךָ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 9 \rb But Onan|אוֹנָ֔ן\rb* \rb knew|וַיֵּ֣דַע\rb* \rb that|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb the offspring|הַזָּ֑רַע\rb*\rb |וְהָיָ֞ה\rb* \rb would not|לֹּ֥א\rb* \rb belong|יִהְיֶ֣ה\rb* \rb to him|ל֖וֹ\rb*; \rb so whenever|אִם־\rb* \rb he would sleep with|בָּ֨א\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb his brother’s|אָחִיו֙\rb* \rb wife|אֵ֤שֶׁת\rb*, \rb he would spill his seed|וְשִׁחֵ֣ת\rb* \rb on the ground|אַ֔רְצָה\rb* \rb so that he would not|לְבִלְתִּ֥י\rb* \rb produce|נְתָן־\rb* \rb offspring|זֶ֖רַע\rb* \rb for his brother|לְאָחִֽיו׃\rb*. \v 10 \rb What|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb he did|עָשָׂ֑ה\rb* \rb was wicked|וַיֵּ֛רַע\rb* \rb in the sight|בְּעֵינֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*, \rb so He put Onan to death|וַיָּ֖מֶת\rb* \rb as well|גַּם־\rb*\rb |אֹתֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\p \v 11 \rb Then Judah|יְהוּדָה֩\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to his daughter-in-law|כַּלָּת֜וֹ\rb* \rb Tamar|לְתָמָ֨ר\rb*, “\rb Live|שְׁבִ֧י\rb* \rb as a widow|אַלְמָנָ֣ה\rb* \rb in your father’s|אָבִ֗יךְ\rb* \rb house|בֵית־\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb my son|בְנִ֔י\rb* \rb Shelah|שֵׁלָ֣ה\rb* \rb grows up|יִגְדַּל֙\rb*.” \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb he thought|אָמַ֔ר\rb*, “\rb He|ה֖וּא\rb* \rb may|פֶּן־\rb* \rb die|יָמ֥וּת\rb* \rb too|גַּם־\rb*, \rb like his brothers|כְּאֶחָ֑יו\rb*.” \rb So Tamar|תָּמָ֔ר\rb* \rb went|וַתֵּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb to live|וַתֵּ֖שֶׁב\rb* \rb in her father’s|אָבִֽיהָ׃\rb* \rb house|בֵּ֥ית\rb*.
\p \v 12 \rb After a long|וַיִּרְבּוּ֙\rb* \rb time|הַיָּמִ֔ים\rb* \rb Judah’s|יְהוּדָ֑ה\rb* \rb wife|אֵֽשֶׁת־\rb*, \rb the daughter|בַּת־\rb* \rb of Shua|שׁ֣וּעַ\rb*, \rb died|וַתָּ֖מָת\rb*. \rb When Judah|יְהוּדָ֗ה\rb* \rb had finished mourning|וַיִּנָּ֣חֶם\rb*, \rb he|ה֗וּא\rb* \rb and his friend|רֵעֵ֥הוּ\rb* \rb Hirah|וְחִירָ֛ה\rb* \rb the Adullamite|הָעֲדֻלָּמִ֖י\rb* \rb went up|וַיַּ֜עַל\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb his sheepshearers|גֹּֽזֲזֵ֤י\rb*\rb |צֹאנוֹ֙\rb* \rb at Timnah|תִּמְנָֽתָה׃\rb*. \v 13 \rb When Tamar|לְתָמָ֖ר\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*\rb |הִנֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb was told|וַיֻּגַּ֥ד\rb*, “\rb Your father-in-law|חָמִ֛יךְ\rb* \rb is going up|עֹלֶ֥ה\rb* \rb to Timnah|תִמְנָ֖תָה\rb* \rb to shear|לָגֹ֥ז\rb* \rb his sheep|צֹאנֽוֹ׃\rb*,” \v 14 \rb she removed|וַתָּסַר֩\rb* \rb her|מֵֽעָלֶ֗יהָ\rb* \rb widow’s|אַלְמְנוּתָ֜הּ\rb* \rb garments|בִּגְדֵ֨י\rb*, \rb covered her face|וַתִּתְעַלָּ֔ף\rb* \rb with a veil|בַּצָּעִיף֙\rb* \rb to disguise herself|וַתְּכַ֤ס\rb*, \rb and sat|וַתֵּ֙שֶׁב֙\rb* \rb at the entrance|בְּפֶ֣תַח\rb* \rb to Enaim|עֵינַ֔יִם\rb*, \rb which|אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb is on|עַל־\rb* \rb the way|דֶּ֣רֶךְ\rb* \rb to Timnah|תִּמְנָ֑תָה\rb*. \rb For|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb she saw|רָאֲתָה֙\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb although Shelah|שֵׁלָ֔ה\rb* \rb had grown up|גָדַ֣ל\rb*, \rb she|וְהִ֕וא\rb* \rb had not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb been given|נִתְּנָ֥ה\rb* \rb to him|ל֖וֹ\rb* \rb as a wife|לְאִשָּֽׁה׃\rb*.
\p \v 15 \rb When Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb saw her|וַיִּרְאֶ֣הָ\rb*, \rb he thought|וַֽיַּחְשְׁבֶ֖הָ\rb* \rb she was a prostitute|לְזוֹנָ֑ה\rb* \rb because|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb she had covered|כִסְּתָ֖ה\rb* \rb her face|פָּנֶֽיהָ׃\rb*. \v 16 \rb |הַדֶּ֗רֶךְ\rb*\rb |כִּ֚י\rb* \rb Not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb realizing|יָדַ֔ע\rb* \rb that|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb she|הִ֑וא\rb* \rb was his daughter-in-law|כַלָּת֖וֹ\rb*, \rb he went over|וַיֵּ֨ט\rb* \rb to her|אֵלֶ֜יהָ\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb*, “\rb Come|הָֽבָה־\rb* \rb now|נָּא֙\rb*, \rb let me sleep with|אָב֣וֹא\rb* \rb you|אֶל־\rb*.”
\p “\rb What|מַה־\rb* \rb will you give|תִּתֶּן־\rb* \rb me|לִּ֔י\rb* \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb sleeping with|תָב֖וֹא\rb*\rb |אֵלָֽי׃\rb* \rb you|אֵלַ֔יִךְ\rb*?” \rb she inquired|וַתֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb*.
\p \v 17 “\rb I|אָנֹכִ֛י\rb* \rb will send you|אֲשַׁלַּ֥ח\rb* \rb a young goat|גְּדִֽי־\rb*\rb |עִזִּ֖ים\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb my flock|הַצֹּ֑אן\rb*,” \rb Judah answered|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*.
\p \rb But she replied|וַתֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Only if|אִם־\rb* \rb you leave me|תִּתֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb something as a pledge|עֵרָב֖וֹן\rb* \rb until|עַ֥ד\rb* \rb you send it|שָׁלְחֶֽךָ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 18 “\rb What|מָ֣ה\rb* \rb pledge|הָֽעֵרָבוֹן֮\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb should I give|אֶתֶּן־\rb* \rb you|לָּךְ֒\rb*?” \rb he asked|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*.
\p \rb She answered|וַתֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Your seal|חֹתָֽמְךָ֙\rb* \rb and your cord|וּפְתִילֶ֔ךָ\rb*, \rb and the staff|וּמַטְּךָ֖\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb in your hand|בְּיָדֶ֑ךָ\rb*.” \rb So he gave them|וַיִּתֶּן־\rb* \rb to her|לָּ֛הּ\rb* \rb and slept with|וַיָּבֹ֥א\rb* \rb her|אֵלֶ֖יהָ\rb*, \rb and she became pregnant|וַתַּ֥הַר\rb* \rb by him|לֽוֹ׃\rb*. \v 19 \rb Then Tamar got up|וַתָּ֣קָם\rb* \rb and departed|וַתֵּ֔לֶךְ\rb*. \rb And she removed|וַתָּ֥סַר\rb* \rb her veil|צְעִיפָ֖הּ\rb*\rb |מֵעָלֶ֑יהָ\rb* \rb and put on her widow’s|אַלְמְנוּתָֽהּ׃\rb* \rb garments|בִּגְדֵ֥י\rb* \rb again|וַתִּלְבַּ֖שׁ\rb*.
\p \v 20 \rb Now when Judah|יְהוּדָ֜ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb sent|וַיִּשְׁלַ֨ח\rb* \rb his friend Hirah|רֵעֵ֣הוּ\rb* \rb the Adullamite|הָֽעֲדֻלָּמִ֔י\rb* \rb with|בְּיַד֙\rb* \rb the young goat|גְּדִ֣י\rb*\rb |הָֽעִזִּ֗ים\rb* \rb to collect|לָקַ֥חַת\rb* \rb the items he had left with|הָעֵרָב֖וֹן\rb*\rb |מִיַּ֣ד\rb* \rb the woman|הָאִשָּׁ֑ה\rb*, \rb he could not|וְלֹ֖א\rb* \rb find her|מְצָאָֽהּ׃\rb*. \v 21 \rb He asked|וַיִּשְׁאַ֞ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the men|אַנְשֵׁ֤י\rb* \rb of that place|מְקֹמָהּ֙\rb*, “\rb Where|אַיֵּ֧ה\rb* \rb is the shrine prostitute|הַקְּדֵשָׁ֛ה\rb* \rb who|הִ֥וא\rb* \rb was beside|עַל־\rb* \rb the road|הַדָּ֑רֶךְ\rb* \rb at Enaim|בָעֵינַ֖יִם\rb*?”
\p “\rb No|לֹא־\rb* \rb shrine prostitute|קְדֵשָֽׁה׃\rb* \rb has been|הָיְתָ֥ה\rb* \rb here|בָזֶ֖ה\rb*,” \rb they answered|וַיֹּ֣אמְר֔וּ\rb*.
\p \v 22 \rb So Hirah returned|וַיָּ֙שָׁב֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb*, “\rb I could not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb find her|מְצָאתִ֑יהָ\rb*, \rb and furthermore|וְגַ֨ם\rb*, \rb the men|אַנְשֵׁ֤י\rb* \rb of that place|הַמָּקוֹם֙\rb* \rb said|אָֽמְר֔וּ\rb*, ‘\rb No|לֹא־\rb* \rb shrine prostitute|קְדֵשָֽׁה׃\rb* \rb has been|הָיְתָ֥ה\rb* \rb here|בָזֶ֖ה\rb*.’”
\p \v 23 “\rb Let her|לָ֔הּ\rb* \rb keep the items|תִּֽקַּֽח־\rb*,” \rb Judah|יְהוּדָה֙\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb*. “\rb Otherwise|פֶּ֖ן\rb* \rb we will become|נִהְיֶ֣ה\rb* \rb a laughingstock|לָב֑וּז\rb*.\f + \fr 38:23 \ft Or \fqa we will become despised\f* \rb After all|הִנֵּ֤ה\rb*, \rb I did send her|שָׁלַ֙חְתִּי֙\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb young goat|הַגְּדִ֣י\rb*, \rb but you|וְאַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb could not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb find her|מְצָאתָֽהּ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 24 \rb About|וַיְהִ֣י׀\rb* \rb three|כְּמִשְׁלֹ֣שׁ\rb* \rb months later|חֳדָשִׁ֗ים\rb*, \rb Judah|לִֽיהוּדָ֤ה\rb* \rb was told|וַיֻּגַּ֨ד\rb*, “\rb Your daughter-in-law|כַּלָּתֶ֔ךָ\rb* \rb Tamar|תָּמָ֣ר\rb* \rb has prostituted herself|זָֽנְתָה֙\rb*, \rb and|וְגַ֛ם\rb* \rb now|הִנֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb she is pregnant|הָרָ֖ה\rb*\rb |לִזְנוּנִ֑ים\rb*.”
\p “\rb Bring her out|הוֹצִיא֖וּהָ\rb*!” \rb Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*. “\rb Let her be burned to death|וְתִשָּׂרֵֽף׃\rb*!”
\p \v 25 \rb As she|הִ֣וא\rb* \rb was being brought out|מוּצֵ֗את\rb*, \rb Tamar|וְהִ֨יא\rb* \rb sent|שָׁלְחָ֤ה\rb* \rb a message|לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb to her|אֶל־\rb* \rb father-in-law|חָמִ֙יהָ֙\rb*: “\rb I am|אָנֹכִ֖י\rb* \rb pregnant|הָרָ֑ה\rb* \rb by the man to whom|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb these items|אֵ֣לֶּה\rb* \rb belong|לּ֔וֹ\rb*.” \rb And she added|וַתֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb*, “\rb Please|נָ֔א\rb* \rb examine them|הַכֶּר־\rb*. \rb Whose|לְמִ֞י\rb* \rb seal|הַחֹתֶ֧מֶת\rb* \rb and cord|וְהַפְּתִילִ֛ים\rb* \rb and staff|וְהַמַּטֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb are these|הָאֵֽלֶּה׃\rb*?”
\p \v 26 \rb Judah|יְהוּדָ֗ה\rb* \rb recognized the items|וַיַּכֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb*, “\rb She is more righteous|צָֽדְקָ֣ה\rb* \rb than I|מִמֶּ֔נִּי\rb*, \rb since|כִּֽי־\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb*\rb |כֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb I did not|לֹא־\rb* \rb give her|נְתַתִּ֖יהָ\rb* \rb to my son|בְנִ֑י\rb* \rb Shelah|לְשֵׁלָ֣ה\rb*.” \rb And he did not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb have relations with her|לְדַעְתָּֽה׃\rb* \rb again|יָסַ֥ף\rb*\rb |ע֖וֹד\rb*.
\s1 The Birth of Perez and Zerah
\p \v 27 \rb When the time|בְּעֵ֣ת\rb* \rb came|וַיְהִ֖י\rb* \rb for Tamar to give birth|לִדְתָּ֑הּ\rb*, \rb there|וְהִנֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb were twins|תְאוֹמִ֖ים\rb* \rb in her womb|בְּבִטְנָֽהּ׃\rb*. \v 28 \rb And|וַיְהִ֥י\rb* \rb as she was giving birth|בְלִדְתָּ֖הּ\rb*, \rb one of them put out|וַיִּתֶּן־\rb* \rb his hand|יָ֑ד\rb*; \rb so the midwife|הַמְיַלֶּ֗דֶת\rb* \rb took|וַתִּקַּ֣ח\rb* \rb a scarlet thread|שָׁנִי֙\rb* \rb and tied it|וַתִּקְשֹׁ֨ר\rb* \rb around|עַל־\rb* \rb his wrist|יָד֤וֹ\rb*. “\rb This|זֶ֖ה\rb* \rb one came out|יָצָ֥א\rb* \rb first|רִאשֹׁנָֽה׃\rb*,” \rb she announced|לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb*. \v 29 \rb |וַיְהִ֣י׀\rb* \rb But when he pulled his hand|יָד֗וֹ\rb*\rb |וְהִנֵּה֙\rb* \rb back|כְּמֵשִׁ֣יב\rb* \rb and his brother|אָחִ֔יו\rb* \rb came out|יָצָ֣א\rb*, \rb she said|וַתֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*,\rb |מַה־\rb* “\rb You have broken out first|פָּרַ֖צְתָּ\rb*\rb |עָלֶ֣יךָ\rb*\rb |פָּ֑רֶץ\rb*!” \rb So he was named|וַיִּקְרָ֥א\rb*\rb |שְׁמ֖וֹ\rb* \rb Perez|פָּֽרֶץ׃\rb*.\f + \fr 38:29 \fqa Perez \ft means \fqa breaking out\ft .\f* \v 30 \rb Then|וְאַחַר֙\rb* \rb his brother|אָחִ֔יו\rb* \rb came out|יָצָ֣א\rb* \rb with|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb the scarlet thread|הַשָּׁנִ֑י\rb* \rb around|עַל־\rb* \rb his wrist|יָד֖וֹ\rb*, \rb and he was named|וַיִּקְרָ֥א\rb*\rb |שְׁמ֖וֹ\rb* \rb Zerah|זָֽרַח׃ס\rb*.\f + \fr 38:30 \fqa Zerah \ft can mean \fqa scarlet \ft or \fqa brightness\ft .\f*
\c 39
\s1 Joseph and Potiphar’s Wife
\p \v 1 \rb Meanwhile, Joseph|וְיוֹסֵ֖ף\rb* \rb had been taken down|הוּרַ֣ד\rb* \rb to Egypt|מִצְרָ֑יְמָה\rb*, \rb where an Egyptian|מִצְרִ֔י\rb* \rb named Potiphar|פּוֹטִיפַר֩\rb*, \rb an officer|סְרִ֨יס\rb* \rb of Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹ֜ה\rb* \rb and captain|שַׂ֤ר\rb* \rb of the guard|הַטַּבָּחִים֙\rb*,\rb |אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb bought him|וַיִּקְנֵ֡הוּ\rb* \rb from|מִיַּד֙\rb* \rb the Ishmaelites|הַיִּשְׁמְעֵאלִ֔ים\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb had taken him|הוֹרִדֻ֖הוּ\rb* \rb there|שָֽׁמָּה׃\rb*. \v 2 \rb And the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb was|וַיְהִ֤י\rb* \rb with|אֶת־\rb* \rb Joseph|יוֹסֵ֔ף\rb*, \rb and he became|וַיְהִ֖י\rb* \rb a successful|מַצְלִ֑יחַ\rb* \rb man|אִ֣ישׁ\rb*, \rb serving|וַיְהִ֕י\rb* \rb in the household|בְּבֵ֥ית\rb* \rb of his Egyptian|הַמִּצְרִֽי׃\rb* \rb master|אֲדֹנָ֖יו\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb When his master|אֲדֹנָ֔יו\rb* \rb saw|וַיַּ֣רְא\rb* \rb that|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb was with him|אִתּ֑וֹ\rb* \rb and|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb made him prosper|מַצְלִ֥יחַ\rb*\rb |בְּיָדֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb in all|וְכֹל֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb he|ה֣וּא\rb* \rb did|עֹשֶׂ֔ה\rb*, \v 4 \rb Joseph|יוֹסֵ֥ף\rb* \rb found|וַיִּמְצָ֨א\rb* \rb favor|חֵ֛ן\rb* \rb in his sight|בְּעֵינָ֖יו\rb* \rb and became his personal attendant|וַיְשָׁ֣רֶת\rb*\rb |אֹת֑וֹ\rb*.
\p \rb Potiphar put him|וַיַּפְקִדֵ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb in charge of|עַל־\rb* \rb his household|בֵּית֔וֹ\rb* \rb and entrusted|נָתַ֥ן\rb*\rb |ל֖וֹ\rb* \rb him|בְּיָדֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb with everything|וְכָל־\rb* \rb he owned|יֶשׁ־\rb*. \v 5 \rb From the time|מֵאָז֩\rb* \rb that he put Joseph in charge|הִפְקִ֨יד\rb*\rb |אֹת֜וֹ\rb* \rb of his household|בְּבֵית֗וֹ\rb* \rb and|וְעַל֙\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb he owned|יֶשׁ־\rb*,\rb |ל֔וֹ\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb blessed|וַיְבָ֧רֶךְ\rb* \rb the Egyptian’s|הַמִּצְרִ֖י\rb* \rb household|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb on account of|בִּגְלַ֣ל\rb* \rb him|יוֹסֵ֑ף\rb*.\rb |וַיְהִ֞י\rb* \rb The LORD’s|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb blessing|בִּרְכַּ֤ת\rb* \rb was on everything|בְּכָל־\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb he owned|יֶשׁ־\rb*\rb |ל֔וֹ\rb*, \rb both in his house|בַּבַּ֖יִת\rb* \rb and in his field|וּבַשָּׂדֶֽה׃\rb*. \v 6 \rb So Potiphar left|וַיַּעֲזֹ֣ב\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb he owned|לוֹ֮\rb* \rb in Joseph’s|יוֹסֵף֒\rb* \rb care|בְּיַד־\rb*; \rb he did not|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb concern himself|יָדַ֤ע\rb*\rb |אִתּוֹ֙\rb* \rb with anything|מְא֔וּמָה\rb* \rb except|כִּ֥י\rb*\rb |אִם־\rb* \rb the food|הַלֶּ֖חֶם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb he|ה֣וּא\rb* \rb ate|אוֹכֵ֑ל\rb*.
\p \rb Now Joseph|יוֹסֵ֔ף\rb* \rb was|וַיְהִ֣י\rb* \rb well-built|יְפֵה־\rb*\rb |תֹ֖אַר\rb* \rb and handsome|וִיפֵ֥ה\rb*\rb |מַרְאֶֽה׃\rb*, \v 7 \rb and|וַיְהִ֗י\rb* \rb after some time|אַחַר֙\rb*\rb |הַדְּבָרִ֣ים\rb*\rb |הָאֵ֔לֶּה\rb* \rb his master’s|אֲדֹנָ֛יו\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb wife|אֵֽשֶׁת־\rb* \rb cast|וַתִּשָּׂ֧א\rb* \rb her eyes|עֵינֶ֖יהָ\rb* \rb upon|אֶל־\rb* \rb Joseph|יוֹסֵ֑ף\rb* \rb and said|וַתֹּ֖אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Sleep|שִׁכְבָ֥ה\rb* \rb with me|עִמִּֽי׃\rb*.”
\p \v 8 \rb But he refused|וַיְמָאֵ֓ן׀\rb*. “\rb Look|הֵ֣ן\rb*,” \rb he said|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his master’s|אֲדֹנָ֔יו\rb* \rb wife|אֵ֣שֶׁת\rb*, “\rb with me here|אִתִּ֖י\rb*, \rb my master|אֲדֹנִ֔י\rb* \rb does not|לֹא־\rb* \rb concern himself|יָדַ֥ע\rb* \rb with anything|מַה־\rb* \rb in his house|בַּבָּ֑יִת\rb*, \rb and he has entrusted|נָתַ֥ן\rb* \rb everything|וְכֹ֥ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb he owns|יֶשׁ־\rb* \rb to|ל֖וֹ\rb* \rb my care|בְּיָדִֽי׃\rb*. \v 9 \rb No|אֵינֶ֨נּוּ\rb* \rb one in this|הַזֶּה֮\rb* \rb house|בַּבַּ֣יִת\rb* \rb is greater|גָד֜וֹל\rb* \rb than I am|מִמֶּנִּי֒\rb*. \rb He has withheld|חָשַׂ֤ךְ\rb* \rb nothing|וְלֹֽא־\rb*\rb |מְא֔וּמָה\rb* \rb from me|מִמֶּ֙נִּי֙\rb* \rb except|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb you|אִם־\rb*,\rb |אוֹתָ֖ךְ\rb* \rb because|בַּאֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb you|אַתְּ־\rb* \rb are his wife|אִשְׁתּ֑וֹ\rb*. \rb So how|וְאֵ֨יךְ\rb* \rb could I do|אֶֽעֱשֶׂ֜ה\rb* \rb such|הַזֹּ֔את\rb* \rb a great|הַגְּדֹלָה֙\rb* \rb evil|הָרָעָ֤ה\rb* \rb and sin|וְחָטָ֖אתִי\rb* \rb against God|לֵֽאלֹהִֽים׃\rb*?”
\p \v 10 \rb Although|וַיְהִ֕י\rb* \rb Potiphar’s wife spoke|כְּדַבְּרָ֥הּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Joseph|יוֹסֵ֖ף\rb* \rb day|י֣וֹם׀\rb* \rb after day|י֑וֹם\rb*, \rb he refused|וְלֹא־\rb*\rb |שָׁמַ֥ע\rb*\rb |אֵלֶ֛יהָ\rb* \rb to go to bed|לִשְׁכַּ֥ב\rb* \rb with her|אֶצְלָ֖הּ\rb* \rb or even be|לִהְי֥וֹת\rb* \rb near her|עִמָּֽהּ׃\rb*. \v 11 \rb One day|כְּהַיּ֣וֹם\rb*\rb |הַזֶּ֔ה\rb*, \rb however|וַיְהִי֙\rb*, \rb Joseph went|וַיָּבֹ֥א\rb* \rb into the house|הַבַּ֖יְתָה\rb* \rb to attend to|לַעֲשׂ֣וֹת\rb* \rb his work|מְלַאכְתּ֑וֹ\rb*, \rb and not|וְאֵ֨ין\rb* \rb a single|אִ֜ישׁ\rb* \rb household|הַבַּ֛יִת\rb* \rb servant|מֵאַנְשֵׁ֥י\rb* \rb was|שָׁ֖ם\rb* \rb inside|בַּבָּֽיִת׃\rb*. \v 12 \rb She grabbed Joseph|וַתִּתְפְּשֵׂ֧הוּ\rb* \rb by his cloak|בְּבִגְד֛וֹ\rb* \rb and said|לֵאמֹ֖ר\rb*, “\rb Sleep|שִׁכְבָ֣ה\rb* \rb with me|עִמִּ֑י\rb*!” \rb But leaving|וַיַּעֲזֹ֤ב\rb* \rb his cloak|בִּגְדוֹ֙\rb* \rb in her hand|בְּיָדָ֔הּ\rb*, \rb he escaped|וַיָּ֖נָס\rb* \rb and ran|וַיֵּצֵ֥א\rb* \rb outside|הַחֽוּצָה׃\rb*.
\s1 Joseph Falsely Imprisoned
\p \v 13 \rb |וַיְהִי֙\rb* \rb When she saw|כִּרְאוֹתָ֔הּ\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb he had left|עָזַ֥ב\rb* \rb his cloak|בִּגְד֖וֹ\rb* \rb in her hand|בְּיָדָ֑הּ\rb* \rb and had run|וַיָּ֖נָס\rb* \rb out of the house|הַחֽוּצָה׃\rb*, \v 14 \rb she called|וַתִּקְרָ֞א\rb* \rb her household|בֵיתָ֗הּ\rb* \rb servants|לְאַנְשֵׁ֣י\rb*. “\rb Look|רְא֗וּ\rb*,” \rb she said|וַתֹּ֤אמֶר\rb*,\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* “\rb this Hebrew|עִבְרִ֖י\rb*\rb |אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb has been brought|הֵ֥בִיא\rb* \rb to us|לָ֛נוּ\rb* \rb to make sport|לְצַ֣חֶק\rb* \rb of us|בָּ֑נוּ\rb*. \rb He came|בָּ֤א\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַי֙\rb* \rb so he could sleep|לִשְׁכַּ֣ב\rb* \rb with me|עִמִּ֔י\rb*, \rb but I screamed|וָאֶקְרָ֖א\rb* \rb as loud|בְּק֥וֹל\rb* \rb as I could|גָּדֽוֹל׃\rb*. \v 15 \rb |וַיְהִ֣י\rb* \rb When he heard me|כְשָׁמְע֔וֹ\rb*\rb |כִּֽי־\rb* \rb scream for help|הֲרִימֹ֥תִי\rb*\rb |קוֹלִ֖י\rb*,\rb |וָאֶקְרָ֑א\rb* \rb he left|וַיַּעֲזֹ֤ב\rb* \rb his cloak|בִּגְדוֹ֙\rb* \rb beside me|אֶצְלִ֔י\rb* \rb and ran|וַיָּ֖נָס\rb*\rb |וַיֵּצֵ֥א\rb* \rb out of the house|הַחֽוּצָה׃\rb*.”
\p \v 16 \rb So Potiphar’s wife kept|וַתַּנַּ֥ח\rb* \rb Joseph’s cloak|בִּגְד֖וֹ\rb* \rb beside her|אֶצְלָ֑הּ\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb his master|אֲדֹנָ֖יו\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb came|בּ֥וֹא\rb* \rb home|בֵּיתֽוֹ׃\rb*. \v 17 \rb Then she told him|וַתְּדַבֵּ֣ר\rb*\rb |אֵלָ֔יו\rb* \rb the same|הָאֵ֖לֶּה\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb story|כַּדְּבָרִ֥ים\rb*: “\rb The Hebrew|הָֽעִבְרִ֛י\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb slave|הָעֶ֧בֶד\rb* \rb you brought|בָּֽא־\rb* \rb us|אֵלַ֞י\rb* \rb came|הֵבֵ֥אתָ\rb* \rb to me|לָּ֖נוּ\rb* \rb to make sport|לְצַ֥חֶק\rb* \rb of me|בִּֽי׃\rb*, \v 18 \rb |וַיְהִ֕י\rb* \rb but when I screamed for help|כַּהֲרִימִ֥י\rb*\rb |קוֹלִ֖י\rb*,\rb |וָאֶקְרָ֑א\rb* \rb he left|וַיַּעֲזֹ֥ב\rb* \rb his cloak|בִּגְד֛וֹ\rb* \rb beside me|אֶצְלִ֖י\rb* \rb and ran|וַיָּ֥נָס\rb* \rb out of the house|הַחֽוּצָה׃\rb*.”
\p \v 19 \rb When|וַיְהִי֩\rb* \rb his master|אֲדֹנָ֜יו\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb heard|כִשְׁמֹ֨עַ\rb* \rb the story|דִּבְרֵ֣י\rb* \rb his wife|אִשְׁתּ֗וֹ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb told|דִּבְּרָ֤ה\rb* \rb him|אֵלָיו֙\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb*, “\rb This|הָאֵ֔לֶּה\rb* \rb is what|כַּדְּבָרִ֣ים\rb* \rb your slave|עַבְדֶּ֑ךָ\rb* \rb did|עָ֥שָׂהּ\rb* \rb to me|לִ֖י\rb*,” \rb he burned|וַיִּ֖חַר\rb* \rb with anger|אַפּֽוֹ׃\rb*. \v 20 \rb So Joseph’s|יוֹסֵ֜ף\rb* \rb master|אֲדֹנֵ֨י\rb* \rb took|וַיִּקַּח֩\rb* \rb him|אֹת֗וֹ\rb* \rb and had him thrown|וַֽיִּתְּנֵ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb the prison|בֵּ֣ית\rb*\rb |הַסֹּ֔הַר\rb* \rb where|מְק֕וֹם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the king’s|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb prisoners|אֲסוּרִ֑ים\rb* \rb were confined|אֲסוּרֵי\rb*.
\p \rb While Joseph was|וַֽיְהִי־\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֖ם\rb* \rb in the prison|בְּבֵ֥ית\rb*\rb |הַסֹּֽהַר׃\rb*, \v 21 \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb was|וַיְהִ֤י\rb* \rb with|אֶת־\rb* \rb him|יוֹסֵ֔ף\rb* \rb and extended|וַיֵּ֥ט\rb* \rb kindness|חָ֑סֶד\rb* \rb to him|אֵלָ֖יו\rb*, \rb granting him|וַיִּתֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb favor|חִנּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb in the eyes|בְּעֵינֵ֖י\rb* \rb of the prison|בֵּית־\rb*\rb |הַסֹּֽהַר׃\rb* \rb warden|שַׂ֥ר\rb*. \v 22 \rb And the warden|שַׂ֤ר\rb*\rb |בֵּית־\rb*\rb |הַסֹּ֙הַר֙\rb* \rb put|וַיִּתֵּ֞ן\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the prisoners|הָ֣אֲסִירִ֔ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֨ת\rb* \rb under Joseph’s|יוֹסֵ֔ף\rb*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb* \rb care|בְּיַד־\rb*, \rb so that he|ה֖וּא\rb* \rb was|הָיָ֥ה\rb* \rb responsible|עֹשִׂים֙\rb* \rb for all|כָּל־\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb was done|עֹשֶֽׂה׃\rb*\rb |שָׁ֔ם\rb* \rb in|בְּבֵ֣ית\rb* \rb the prison|הַסֹּ֑הַר\rb*. \v 23 \rb The warden|שַׂ֣ר\rb*\rb |בֵּית־\rb*\rb |הַסֹּ֗הַר\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb did not|אֵ֣ין׀\rb* \rb concern himself|רֹאֶ֤ה\rb* \rb with anything|כָּל־\rb*\rb |מְא֙וּמָה֙\rb* \rb under Joseph’s care|בְּיָד֔וֹ\rb*, \rb because|בַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb was with Joseph|אִתּ֑וֹ\rb*\rb |יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb and gave him success|מַצְלִֽיחַ׃ס\rb* \rb in whatever|וַֽאֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb he|ה֥וּא\rb* \rb did|עֹשֶׂ֖ה\rb*.
\c 40
\s1 The Cupbearer and the Baker
\p \v 1 \rb |וַיְהִ֗י\rb* \rb Some time later|אַחַר֙\rb*\rb |הַדְּבָרִ֣ים\rb*\rb |הָאֵ֔לֶּה\rb*,\rb |מִצְרַ֖יִם\rb* \rb the king’s|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb cupbearer|מַשְׁקֵ֥ה\rb* \rb and baker|וְהָאֹפֶ֑ה\rb* \rb offended|חָֽטְא֛וּ\rb* \rb their master|לַאֲדֹנֵיהֶ֖ם\rb*, \rb the king|לְמֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרָֽיִם׃\rb*. \v 2 \rb Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹ֔ה\rb* \rb was angry|וַיִּקְצֹ֣ף\rb* \rb with|עַ֖ל\rb* \rb his two|שְׁנֵ֣י\rb* \rb officers|סָרִיסָ֑יו\rb*,\rb |עַ֚ל\rb* \rb the chief|שַׂ֣ר\rb* \rb cupbearer|הַמַּשְׁקִ֔ים\rb*\rb |וְעַ֖ל\rb* \rb and the chief|שַׂ֥ר\rb* \rb baker|הָאוֹפִֽים׃\rb*, \v 3 \rb and imprisoned them|וַיִּתֵּ֨ן\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֜ם\rb*\rb |בְּמִשְׁמַ֗ר\rb* \rb in the house|בֵּ֛ית\rb* \rb of the captain|שַׂ֥ר\rb* \rb of the guard|הַטַבָּחִ֖ים\rb*, \rb the same prison|בֵּ֣ית\rb*\rb |הַסֹּ֑הַר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |מְק֕וֹם\rb* \rb where|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb Joseph|יוֹסֵ֖ף\rb* \rb was confined|אָס֥וּר\rb*\rb |שָֽׁם׃\rb*. \v 4 \rb The captain|שַׂ֣ר\rb* \rb of the guard|הַטַּבָּחִ֧ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb assigned|וַ֠יִּפְקֹד\rb* \rb them|אִתָּ֖ם\rb* \rb to Joseph|יוֹסֵ֛ף\rb*, \rb and he became their personal attendant|וַיְשָׁ֣רֶת\rb*.\rb |אֹתָ֑ם\rb*
\p \rb After they had been|וַיִּהְי֥וּ\rb* \rb in custody|בְּמִשְׁמָֽר׃\rb* \rb for some time|יָמִ֖ים\rb*, \v 5 \rb both|שְׁנֵיהֶ֜ם\rb* \rb of these men|אִ֤ישׁ\rb* — \rb the Egyptian|מִצְרַ֔יִם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb king’s|לְמֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb cupbearer|הַמַּשְׁקֶ֣ה\rb* \rb and baker|וְהָאֹפֶ֗ה\rb*, \rb who|אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb were being held|אֲסוּרִ֖ים\rb* \rb in the prison|בְּבֵ֥ית\rb*\rb |הַסֹּֽהַר׃\rb* — \rb had a dream|וַיַּֽחַלְמוּ֩\rb*\rb |חֲל֨וֹם\rb*\rb |חֲלֹמוֹ֙\rb* \rb on the same|אֶחָ֔ד\rb*\rb |אִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb night|בְּלַ֣יְלָה\rb*, \rb and each dream|חֲלֹמ֑וֹ\rb* \rb had its own meaning|כְּפִתְר֣וֹן\rb*.
\p \v 6 \rb When Joseph|יוֹסֵ֖ף\rb* \rb came|וַיָּבֹ֧א\rb* \rb to them|אֲלֵיהֶ֛ם\rb* \rb in the morning|בַּבֹּ֑קֶר\rb*, \rb he saw|וַיַּ֣רְא\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֔ם\rb*\rb |וְהִנָּ֖ם\rb* \rb that they were distraught|זֹעֲפִֽים׃\rb*. \v 7 \rb So he asked|וַיִּשְׁאַ֞ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the officials|סְרִיסֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Pharaoh|פַרְעֹ֗ה\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb were in custody|בְמִשְׁמַ֛ר\rb* \rb with him|אִתּ֧וֹ\rb* \rb in his master’s|אֲדֹנָ֖יו\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb house|בֵּ֥ית\rb*, “\rb Why|מַדּ֛וּעַ\rb* \rb are your faces|פְּנֵיכֶ֥ם\rb* \rb so downcast|רָעִ֖ים\rb* \rb today|הַיּֽוֹם׃\rb*?”
\p \v 8 “\rb We both had dreams|חֲל֣וֹם\rb*\rb |חָלַ֔מְנוּ\rb*,” \rb they replied|וַיֹּאמְר֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֵלָ֔יו\rb*, “\rb but there is no one|אֵ֣ין\rb*\rb |אֹת֑וֹ\rb* \rb to interpret them|וּפֹתֵ֖ר\rb*.”
\p \rb Then Joseph|יוֹסֵ֗ף\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to them|אֲלֵהֶ֜ם\rb*, “\rb Don’t|הֲל֤וֹא\rb* \rb interpretations|פִּתְרֹנִ֔ים\rb* \rb belong to God|לֵֽאלֹהִים֙\rb*? \rb Tell me your dreams|סַפְּרוּ־\rb*\rb |נָ֖א\rb*.”
\p \v 9 \rb So the chief|שַֽׂר־\rb* \rb cupbearer|הַמַּשְׁקִ֛ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb told|וַיְסַפֵּ֧ר\rb* \rb Joseph|לְיוֹסֵ֑ף\rb* \rb his dream|חֲלֹמ֖וֹ\rb*\rb |וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*: “\rb In my dream|בַּחֲלוֹמִ֕י\rb* \rb there|וְהִנֵּה־\rb* \rb was a vine|גֶ֖פֶן\rb* \rb before me|לְפָנָֽי׃\rb*, \v 10 \rb and on the vine|וּבַגֶּ֖פֶן\rb* \rb were three|שְׁלֹשָׁ֣ה\rb* \rb branches|שָׂרִיגִ֑ם\rb*. \rb As it|וְהִ֤יא\rb* \rb budded|כְפֹרַ֙חַת֙\rb*, \rb its blossoms|נִצָּ֔הּ\rb* \rb opened|עָלְתָ֣ה\rb* \rb and its clusters|אַשְׁכְּלֹתֶ֖יהָ\rb* \rb ripened|הִבְשִׁ֥ילוּ\rb* \rb into grapes|עֲנָבִֽים׃\rb*. \v 11 \rb Pharaoh’s|פַּרְעֹ֖ה\rb* \rb cup|וְכ֥וֹס\rb* \rb was in my hand|בְּיָדִ֑י\rb*, \rb and I took|וָאֶקַּ֣ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the grapes|הָֽעֲנָבִ֗ים\rb*, \rb squeezed|וָֽאֶשְׂחַ֤ט\rb* \rb them|אֹתָם֙\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb his|פַּרְעֹ֔ה\rb* \rb cup|כּ֣וֹס\rb*, \rb and placed|וָאֶתֵּ֥ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the cup|הַכּ֖וֹס\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb his|פַּרְעֹֽה׃\rb* \rb hand|כַּ֥ף\rb*.”
\p \v 12 \rb Joseph|יוֹסֵ֔ף\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb*\rb |לוֹ֙\rb*, “\rb This is|זֶ֖ה\rb* \rb the interpretation|פִּתְרֹנ֑וֹ\rb*: \rb The three|שְׁלֹ֙שֶׁת֙\rb* \rb branches|הַשָּׂ֣רִגִ֔ים\rb* \rb are three|שְׁלֹ֥שֶׁת\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֖ים\rb*\rb |הֵֽם׃\rb*. \v 13 \rb Within|בְּע֣וֹד׀\rb* \rb three|שְׁלֹ֣שֶׁת\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֗ים\rb* \rb Pharaoh|פַרְעֹה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb will lift up|יִשָּׂ֤א\rb* \rb your head|רֹאשֶׁ֔ךָ\rb* \rb and restore|וַהֲשִֽׁיבְךָ֖\rb* \rb your|עַל־\rb* \rb position|כַּנֶּ֑ךָ\rb*. \rb You will put|וְנָתַתָּ֤\rb* \rb Pharaoh’s|פַּרְעֹה֙\rb* \rb cup|כוֹס־\rb* \rb in his hand|בְּיָד֔וֹ\rb*, \rb just as|כַּמִּשְׁפָּט֙\rb* \rb you did|הָֽרִאשׁ֔וֹן\rb* \rb when|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you were|הָיִ֖יתָ\rb* \rb his cupbearer|מַשְׁקֵֽהוּ׃\rb*. \v 14 \rb But|כִּ֧י\rb*\rb |אִם־\rb* \rb when|כַּאֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb it goes well|יִ֣יטַב\rb* \rb for you|לָ֔ךְ\rb*, \rb please|נָּ֥א\rb* \rb remember|זְכַרְתַּ֣נִי\rb* \rb me|אִתְּךָ֗\rb* \rb and show|וְעָשִֽׂיתָ־\rb* \rb me|עִמָּדִ֖י\rb* \rb kindness|חָ֑סֶד\rb* \rb by mentioning me|וְהִזְכַּרְתַּ֙נִי֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹ֔ה\rb*, \rb that he might bring me out|וְהוֹצֵאתַ֖נִי\rb* \rb of|מִן־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb prison|הַבַּ֥יִת\rb*. \v 15 \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I was kidnapped|גֻנֹּ֣ב\rb*\rb |גֻּנַּ֔בְתִּי\rb* \rb from the land|מֵאֶ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb of the Hebrews|הָעִבְרִ֑ים\rb*, \rb and even|וְגַם־\rb* \rb here|פֹּה֙\rb* \rb I have done|עָשִׂ֣יתִֽי\rb* \rb nothing|לֹא־\rb*\rb |מְא֔וּמָה\rb* \rb for which|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb they should have put|שָׂמ֥וּ\rb* \rb me|אֹתִ֖י\rb* \rb in this dungeon|בַּבּֽוֹר׃\rb*.”
\p \v 16 \rb When the chief|שַׂר־\rb* \rb baker|הָאֹפִ֖ים\rb* \rb saw|וַיַּ֥רְא\rb* \rb that|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb the interpretation|פָּתָ֑ר\rb* \rb was favorable|ט֣וֹב\rb*, \rb he said|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Joseph|יוֹסֵ֔ף\rb*, “\rb I|אֲנִי֙\rb* \rb too|אַף־\rb* \rb had a dream|בַּחֲלוֹמִ֔י\rb*: \rb There were|וְהִנֵּ֗ה\rb* \rb three|שְׁלֹשָׁ֛ה\rb* \rb baskets|סַלֵּ֥י\rb* \rb of white bread|חֹרִ֖י\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb my head|רֹאשִֽׁי׃\rb*. \v 17 \rb In the top|הָֽעֶלְי֔וֹן\rb* \rb basket|וּבַסַּ֣ל\rb* \rb were all sorts of|מִכֹּ֛ל\rb* \rb baked|אֹפֶ֑ה\rb* \rb goods|מַאֲכַ֥ל\rb* \rb for Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹ֖ה\rb*,\rb |מַעֲשֵׂ֣ה\rb* \rb but the birds|וְהָע֗וֹף\rb* \rb were eating|אֹכֵ֥ל\rb* \rb them|אֹתָ֛ם\rb* \rb out of|מִן־\rb* \rb the basket|הַסַּ֖ל\rb* \rb on|מֵעַ֥ל\rb* \rb my head|רֹאשִֽׁי׃\rb*.”
\p \v 18 \rb Joseph|יוֹסֵף֙\rb*\rb |וַיֹּ֔אמֶר\rb* \rb replied|וַיַּ֤עַן\rb*, “\rb This|זֶ֖ה\rb* \rb is the interpretation|פִּתְרֹנ֑וֹ\rb*: \rb The three|שְׁלֹ֙שֶׁת֙\rb* \rb baskets|הַסַּלִּ֔ים\rb* \rb are three|שְׁלֹ֥שֶׁת\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֖ים\rb*\rb |הֵֽם׃\rb*. \v 19 \rb Within|בְּע֣וֹד׀\rb* \rb three|שְׁלֹ֣שֶׁת\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֗ים\rb* \rb Pharaoh|פַרְעֹ֤ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb will lift off|יִשָּׂ֨א\rb* \rb your head|רֹֽאשְׁךָ֙\rb*\rb |מֵֽעָלֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb and hang|וְתָלָ֥ה\rb* \rb you|אוֹתְךָ֖\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb a tree|עֵ֑ץ\rb*.\f + \fr 40:19 \ft Or \fqa and impale you on a pole\ft ; similarly in verse 22\f* \rb Then the birds|הָע֛וֹף\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb will eat|וְאָכַ֥ל\rb* \rb the flesh|בְּשָׂרְךָ֖\rb* \rb of your body|מֵעָלֶֽיךָ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 20 \rb |וַיְהִ֣י׀\rb* \rb On the third|הַשְּׁלִישִׁ֗י\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb*, \rb which was Pharaoh’s|פַּרְעֹ֔ה\rb* \rb birthday|י֚וֹם\rb*\rb |הֻלֶּ֣דֶת\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb he held|וַיַּ֥עַשׂ\rb* \rb a feast|מִשְׁתֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb for all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb his officials|עֲבָדָ֑יו\rb*, \rb and in|בְּת֥וֹךְ\rb* \rb their presence|עֲבָדָֽיו׃\rb* \rb he lifted up|וַיִּשָּׂ֞א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the heads|רֹ֣אשׁ׀\rb* \rb of the chief|שַׂ֣ר\rb* \rb cupbearer|הַמַּשְׁקִ֗ים\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb*\rb |רֹ֛אשׁ\rb* \rb and the chief|שַׂ֥ר\rb* \rb baker|הָאֹפִ֖ים\rb*. \v 21 \rb Pharaoh restored|וַיָּ֛שֶׁב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the chief|שַׂ֥ר\rb* \rb cupbearer|הַמַּשְׁקִ֖ים\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb his position|מַשְׁקֵ֑הוּ\rb*, \rb so that he once again placed|וַיִּתֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb the cup|הַכּ֖וֹס\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb Pharaoh’s|פַּרְעֹֽה׃\rb* \rb hand|כַּ֥ף\rb*. \v 22 \rb But|וְאֵ֛ת\rb* \rb Pharaoh hanged|תָּלָ֑ה\rb* \rb the chief|שַׂ֥ר\rb* \rb baker|הָאֹפִ֖ים\rb*, \rb just as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb Joseph|יוֹסֵֽף׃\rb* \rb had described|פָּתַ֛ר\rb* \rb to them in his interpretation|לָהֶ֖ם\rb*.\f + \fr 40:22 \ft Literally \fqa had interpreted to them\f*
\p \v 23 \rb The chief|שַֽׂר־\rb* \rb cupbearer|הַמַּשְׁקִ֛ים\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb however, did not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb remember|זָכַ֧ר\rb* \rb Joseph|יוֹסֵ֖ף\rb*; \rb he forgot all about him|וַיִּשְׁכָּחֵֽהוּ׃פ\rb*.
\c 41
\s1 The Dreams of Pharaoh
\p \v 1 \rb After|וַיְהִ֕י\rb* \rb two full years|שְׁנָתַ֣יִם\rb*\rb |יָמִ֑ים\rb* \rb had passed|מִקֵּ֖ץ\rb*, \rb Pharaoh|וּפַרְעֹ֣ה\rb* \rb had a dream|חֹלֵ֔ם\rb*:\rb |וְהִנֵּ֖ה\rb* \rb He was standing|עֹמֵ֥ד\rb* \rb beside|עַל־\rb* \rb the Nile|הַיְאֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 2 \rb |וְהִנֵּ֣ה\rb* \rb when seven|שֶׁ֣בַע\rb* \rb cows|פָּר֔וֹת\rb*, \rb sleek|יְפ֥וֹת\rb*\rb |מַרְאֶ֖ה\rb* \rb and well-fed|וּבְרִיאֹ֣ת\rb*\rb |בָּשָׂ֑ר\rb*, \rb came up|עֹלֹת֙\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the river|הַיְאֹ֗ר\rb* \rb and began to graze|וַתִּרְעֶ֖ינָה\rb* \rb among the reeds|בָּאָֽחוּ׃\rb*. \v 3 \rb |וְהִנֵּ֞ה\rb* \rb After them|אַחֲרֵיהֶן֙\rb*, \rb seven|שֶׁ֧בַע\rb* \rb other|אֲחֵר֗וֹת\rb* \rb cows|פָּר֣וֹת\rb*, \rb sickly|רָע֥וֹת\rb*\rb |מַרְאֶ֖ה\rb* \rb and thin|וְדַקּ֣וֹת\rb*\rb |בָּשָׂ֑ר\rb*, \rb came up|עֹל֤וֹת\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the Nile|הַיְאֹ֔ר\rb* \rb and stood|וַֽתַּעֲמֹ֛דְנָה\rb* \rb beside|אֵ֥צֶל\rb* \rb the well-fed cows|הַפָּר֖וֹת\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the bank|שְׂפַ֥ת\rb* \rb of the river|הַיְאֹֽר׃\rb*. \v 4 \rb And the cows|הַפָּר֗וֹת\rb* \rb that were sickly|רָע֤וֹת\rb*\rb |הַמַּרְאֶה֙\rb* \rb and thin|וְדַקֹּ֣ת\rb*\rb |הַבָּשָׂ֔ר\rb*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb* \rb devoured|וַתֹּאכַ֣לְנָה\rb* \rb the seven|שֶׁ֣בַע\rb* \rb sleek|יְפֹ֥ת\rb*\rb |הַמַּרְאֶ֖ה\rb*, \rb well-fed|וְהַבְּרִיאֹ֑ת\rb* \rb cows|הַפָּר֔וֹת\rb*.
\p \rb Then Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹֽה׃\rb* \rb woke up|וַיִּיקַ֖ץ\rb*, \v 5 \rb but he fell back asleep|וַיִּישָׁ֕ן\rb* \rb and dreamed|וַֽיַּחֲלֹ֖ם\rb* \rb a second time|שֵׁנִ֑ית\rb*:\rb |וְהִנֵּ֣ה׀\rb* \rb Seven|שֶׁ֣בַע\rb* \rb heads of grain|שִׁבֳּלִ֗ים\rb*, \rb plump|בְּרִיא֥וֹת\rb* \rb and ripe|וְטֹבֽוֹת׃\rb*, \rb came up|עֹל֛וֹת\rb* \rb on one|אֶחָ֖ד\rb* \rb stalk|בְּקָנֶ֥ה\rb*. \v 6 \rb |וְהִנֵּה֙\rb* \rb After them|אַחֲרֵיהֶֽן׃\rb*, \rb seven other|שֶׁ֣בַע\rb* \rb heads of grain|שִׁבֳּלִ֔ים\rb* \rb sprouted|צֹמְח֖וֹת\rb*, \rb thin|דַּקּ֖וֹת\rb* \rb and scorched|וּשְׁדוּפֹ֣ת\rb* \rb by the east wind|קָדִ֑ים\rb*. \v 7 \rb And the thin|הַדַּקּ֔וֹת\rb*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb* \rb heads of grain|הַשִּׁבֳּלִ֣ים\rb* \rb swallowed up|וַתִּבְלַ֙עְנָה֙\rb* \rb the seven|שֶׁ֣בַע\rb* \rb plump|הַבְּרִיא֖וֹת\rb*, \rb ripe|וְהַמְּלֵא֑וֹת\rb* \rb ones|הַֽשִּׁבֳּלִ֔ים\rb*. \rb Then Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹ֖ה\rb* \rb awoke|וַיִּיקַ֥ץ\rb* \rb and realized|וְהִנֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb it was a dream|חֲלֽוֹם׃\rb*.
\p \v 8 \rb In the morning|בַבֹּ֙קֶר֙\rb*\rb |וַיְהִ֤י\rb* \rb his spirit|רוּח֔וֹ\rb* \rb was troubled|וַתִּפָּ֣עֶם\rb*, \rb so he summoned|וַיִּשְׁלַ֗ח\rb*\rb |וַיִּקְרָ֛א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the magicians|חַרְטֻמֵּ֥י\rb* \rb and|כָּל־\rb* \rb wise men|חֲכָמֶ֑יהָ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֖יִם\rb*.\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹ֤ה\rb* \rb told|וַיְסַפֵּ֨ר\rb* \rb them|לָהֶם֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his dreams|חֲלֹמ֔וֹ\rb*, \rb but no one|וְאֵין־\rb* \rb could interpret|פּוֹתֵ֥ר\rb* \rb them|אוֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb for him|לְפַרְעֹֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 9 \rb Then the chief|שַׂ֣ר\rb* \rb cupbearer|הַמַּשְׁקִ֔ים\rb* \rb said|וַיְדַבֵּר֙\rb* \rb to|אֶת־\rb* \rb Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹ֖ה\rb*,\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* “\rb Today|הַיּֽוֹם׃\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֖י\rb* \rb recall|מַזְכִּ֥יר\rb* \rb my failures|חֲטָאַ֕י\rb*. \v 10 \rb Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹ֖ה\rb* \rb was once angry|קָצַ֣ף\rb* \rb with|עַל־\rb* \rb his servants|עֲבָדָ֑יו\rb*, \rb and he put|וַיִּתֵּ֨ן\rb*\rb |אֹתִ֜י\rb* \rb me|אֹתִ֕י\rb* \rb and|וְאֵ֖ת\rb* \rb the chief|שַׂ֣ר\rb* \rb baker|הָאֹפִֽים׃\rb* \rb in the custody|בְּמִשְׁמַ֗ר\rb*\rb |בֵּ֚ית\rb* \rb of the captain|שַׂ֥ר\rb* \rb of the guard|הַטַּבָּחִ֔ים\rb*. \v 11 \rb One|אֶחָ֖ד\rb* \rb night|בְּלַ֥יְלָה\rb* \rb both the chief baker|וָה֑וּא\rb* \rb and I|אֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb had dreams|וַנַּֽחַלְמָ֥ה\rb*\rb |חֲל֛וֹם\rb*, \rb and each|אִ֛ישׁ\rb* \rb dream|חֲלֹמ֖וֹ\rb*\rb |חָלָֽמְנוּ׃\rb* \rb had its own meaning|כְּפִתְר֥וֹן\rb*. \v 12 \rb Now a young|נַ֣עַר\rb* \rb Hebrew|עִבְרִ֗י\rb* \rb was there|וְשָׁ֨ם\rb* \rb with us|אִתָּ֜נוּ\rb*, \rb a servant|עֶ֚בֶד\rb* \rb of the captain|לְשַׂ֣ר\rb* \rb of the guard|הַטַּבָּחִ֔ים\rb*. \rb We told him|וַנְּ֨סַפֶּר־\rb* \rb our dreams|ל֔וֹ\rb* \rb and he interpreted|וַיִּפְתָּר־\rb* \rb them|חֲלֹמֹתֵ֑ינוּ\rb* \rb for|לָ֖נוּ\rb* \rb us|אֶת־\rb* \rb individually|אִ֥ישׁ\rb*\rb |כַּחֲלֹמ֖וֹ\rb*\rb |פָּתָֽר׃\rb*. \v 13 \rb And it happened|וַיְהִ֛י\rb* \rb to us|לָ֖נוּ\rb* \rb just as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb he had interpreted|פָּֽתַר־\rb*:\rb |כֵּ֣ן\rb*\rb |הָיָ֑ה\rb*\rb |אֹתִ֛י\rb* \rb I was restored|הֵשִׁ֥יב\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb my position|כַּנִּ֖י\rb*,\rb |וְאֹת֥וֹ\rb* \rb and the other man was hanged|תָלָֽה׃\rb*.”
\s1 Joseph Interprets Pharaoh’s Dreams
\p \v 14 \rb So Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹה֙\rb* \rb sent for|וַיִּשְׁלַ֤ח\rb*\rb |וַיִּקְרָ֣א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Joseph|יוֹסֵ֔ף\rb*, \rb who was quickly brought|וַיְרִיצֻ֖הוּ\rb* \rb out of|מִן־\rb* \rb the dungeon|הַבּ֑וֹר\rb*. \rb After he had shaved|וַיְגַלַּח֙\rb* \rb and changed|וַיְחַלֵּ֣ף\rb* \rb his clothes|שִׂמְלֹתָ֔יו\rb*, \rb he went in|וַיָּבֹ֖א\rb* \rb before|אֶל־\rb* \rb Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 15 \rb Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹה֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Joseph|יוֹסֵ֔ף\rb*, “\rb I had a dream|חֲל֣וֹם\rb*\rb |חָלַ֔מְתִּי\rb*, \rb and no|אֵ֣ין\rb*\rb |אֹת֑וֹ\rb* \rb one can interpret it|וּפֹתֵ֖ר\rb*. \rb But I|וַאֲנִ֗י\rb* \rb have heard|שָׁמַ֤עְתִּי\rb* \rb it said|לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb of you|עָלֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb that when you hear|תִּשְׁמַ֥ע\rb* \rb a dream|חֲל֖וֹם\rb* \rb you can interpret it|לִפְתֹּ֥ר\rb*\rb |אֹתֽוֹ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 16 “\rb I myself cannot do it|בִּלְעָדָ֑י\rb*,” \rb Joseph|יוֹסֵ֧ף\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb replied|וַיַּ֨עַן\rb*\rb |פַּרְעֹ֛ה\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֖ר\rb*, “\rb but God|אֱלֹהִ֕ים\rb* \rb will give Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹֽה׃\rb* \rb a sound|שְׁל֥וֹם\rb* \rb answer|יַעֲנֶ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*.”
\p \v 17 \rb Then Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹ֖ה\rb* \rb said|וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Joseph|יוֹסֵ֑ף\rb*: “\rb In my dream|בַּחֲלֹמִ֕י\rb*\rb |הִנְנִ֥י\rb* \rb I was standing|עֹמֵ֖ד\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the bank|שְׂפַ֥ת\rb* \rb of the Nile|הַיְאֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 18 \rb |וְהִנֵּ֣ה\rb* \rb when seven|שֶׁ֣בַע\rb* \rb cows|פָּר֔וֹת\rb*, \rb well-fed|בְּרִיא֥וֹת\rb*\rb |בָּשָׂ֖ר\rb* \rb and sleek|וִיפֹ֣ת\rb*,\rb |תֹּ֑אַר\rb* \rb came up|עֹלֹת֙\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the river|הַיְאֹ֗ר\rb* \rb and began to graze|וַתִּרְעֶ֖ינָה\rb* \rb among the reeds|בָּאָֽחוּ׃\rb*. \v 19 \rb |וְהִנֵּ֞ה\rb* \rb After them|אַחֲרֵיהֶ֔ן\rb*,\rb |דַּלּ֨וֹת\rb* \rb seven|שֶֽׁבַע־\rb* \rb other|אֲחֵרוֹת֙\rb* \rb cows|פָּר֤וֹת\rb*— \rb sickly|וְרָע֥וֹת\rb*, \rb ugly|תֹּ֛אַר\rb*,\rb |מְאֹ֖ד\rb* \rb and thin|וְרַקּ֣וֹת\rb*\rb |בָּשָׂ֑ר\rb*— \rb came up|עֹל֣וֹת\rb*. \rb I have never|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb seen|רָאִ֧יתִי\rb* \rb such ugly|לָרֹֽעַ׃\rb* \rb cows|כָהֵ֛נָּה\rb* \rb in all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֖יִם\rb*! \v 20 \rb Then the thin|הָרַקּ֖וֹת\rb*, \rb ugly|וְהָרָע֑וֹת\rb*\rb |אֵ֣ת\rb* \rb cows|הַפָּר֔וֹת\rb* \rb devoured|וַתֹּאכַ֙לְנָה֙\rb* \rb the seven|שֶׁ֧בַע\rb* \rb well-fed|הַבְּרִיאֹֽת׃\rb* \rb cows|הַפָּר֛וֹת\rb* \rb that were there first|הָרִאשֹׁנ֖וֹת\rb*. \v 21 \rb When they had devoured|וַתָּבֹ֣אנָה\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb them, however|קִרְבֶּ֗נָה\rb*, \rb no one could|וְלֹ֤א\rb* \rb tell|נוֹדַע֙\rb* \rb that|כִּי־\rb* \rb they had done so|בָ֣אוּ\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |קִרְבֶּ֔נָה\rb*; \rb their appearance|וּמַרְאֵיהֶ֣ן\rb* \rb was as ugly|רַ֔ע\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb it had been before|בַּתְּחִלָּ֑ה\rb*. \rb Then I awoke|וָאִיקָֽץ׃\rb*.
\p \v 22 \rb In my dream|בַּחֲלֹמִ֑י\rb*\rb |וְהִנֵּ֣ה׀\rb* \rb I also saw|וָאֵ֖רֶא\rb* \rb seven|שֶׁ֣בַע\rb* \rb heads of grain|שִׁבֳּלִ֗ים\rb*, \rb plump|מְלֵאֹ֥ת\rb* \rb and ripe|וְטֹבֽוֹת׃\rb*, \rb growing on|עֹלֹ֛ת\rb* \rb a single|אֶחָ֖ד\rb* \rb stalk|בְּקָנֶ֥ה\rb*. \v 23 \rb |וְהִנֵּה֙\rb* \rb After them|אַחֲרֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*, \rb seven other|שֶׁ֣בַע\rb* \rb heads of grain|שִׁבֳּלִ֔ים\rb* \rb sprouted|צֹמְח֖וֹת\rb*— \rb withered|צְנֻמ֥וֹת\rb*, \rb thin|דַּקּ֖וֹת\rb*, \rb and scorched|שְׁדֻפ֣וֹת\rb* \rb by the east wind|קָדִ֑ים\rb*. \v 24 \rb And the thin|הַדַּקֹּ֔ת\rb*\rb |אֵ֛ת\rb* \rb heads of grain|הָשִׁבֳּלִ֣ים\rb* \rb swallowed|וַתִּבְלַ֙עְןָ֙\rb* \rb the seven|שֶׁ֥בַע\rb* \rb plump|הַטֹּב֑וֹת\rb* \rb ones|הַֽשִׁבֳּלִ֖ים\rb*.
\p \rb I told|וָֽאֹמַר֙\rb* \rb this dream to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the magicians|הַֽחַרְטֻמִּ֔ים\rb*, \rb but no|וְאֵ֥ין\rb* \rb one could explain it|מַגִּ֖יד\rb* \rb to me|לִֽי׃\rb*.”
\p \v 25 \rb At this, Joseph|יוֹסֵף֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹ֔ה\rb*, “\rb The dreams|חֲל֥וֹם\rb* \rb of Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹ֖ה\rb* \rb are one and the same|אֶחָ֣ד\rb*.\rb |ה֑וּא\rb*\rb |אֵ֣ת\rb* \rb God|הָאֱלֹהִ֛ים\rb* \rb has revealed|הִגִּ֥יד\rb* \rb to Pharaoh|לְפַרְעֹֽה׃\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb* \rb He is about to do|עֹשֶׂ֖ה\rb*. \v 26 \rb The seven|שֶׁ֧בַע\rb* \rb good|הַטֹּבֹ֗ת\rb* \rb cows|פָּרֹ֣ת\rb* \rb are seven|שֶׁ֤בַע\rb* \rb years|שָׁנִים֙\rb*,\rb |הֵ֔נָּה\rb* \rb and the seven|וְשֶׁ֤בַע\rb* \rb ripe|הַטֹּבֹ֔ת\rb* \rb heads of grain|הַֽשִּׁבֳּלִים֙\rb* \rb are seven|שֶׁ֥בַע\rb* \rb years|שָׁנִ֖ים\rb*.\rb |הֵ֑נָּה\rb* \rb The dreams|חֲל֖וֹם\rb* \rb have the same meaning|אֶחָ֥ד\rb*\rb |הֽוּא׃\rb*. \v 27 \rb Moreover, the seven|וְשֶׁ֣בַע\rb* \rb thin|הָֽרַקּ֨וֹת\rb*, \rb ugly|וְהָרָעֹ֜ת\rb* \rb cows|הַ֠פָּרוֹת\rb* \rb that came up|הָעֹלֹ֣ת\rb* \rb after them|אַחֲרֵיהֶ֗ן\rb* \rb are seven|שֶׁ֤בַע\rb* \rb years|שָׁנִים֙\rb*, \rb and so are|הֵ֔נָּה\rb* \rb the seven|וְשֶׁ֤בַע\rb* \rb worthless|הָרֵק֔וֹת\rb* \rb heads of grain|הַֽשִׁבֳּלִים֙\rb* \rb scorched|שְׁדֻפ֖וֹת\rb* \rb by the east wind|הַקָּדִ֑ים\rb* — \rb they are|יִהְי֕וּ\rb* \rb seven|שֶׁ֖בַע\rb* \rb years|שְׁנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of famine|רָעָֽב׃\rb*.
\p \v 28 \rb It|ה֣וּא\rb*\rb |הַדָּבָ֔ר\rb* \rb is just as|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I said|דִּבַּ֖רְתִּי\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹ֑ה\rb*: \rb God|הָאֱלֹהִ֛ים\rb* \rb has shown|הֶרְאָ֥ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹֽה׃\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb* \rb He is about to do|עֹשֶׂ֖ה\rb*. \v 29 \rb Behold|הִנֵּ֛ה\rb*, \rb seven|שֶׁ֥בַע\rb* \rb years|שָׁנִ֖ים\rb* \rb of great|גָּד֖וֹל\rb* \rb abundance|שָׂבָ֥ע\rb* \rb are coming|בָּא֑וֹת\rb* \rb throughout|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרָֽיִם׃\rb*, \v 30 \rb but seven|שֶׁ֜בַע\rb* \rb years|שְׁנֵ֤י\rb* \rb of famine|רָעָב֙\rb* \rb will follow|וְ֠קָמוּ\rb* \rb them|אַחֲרֵיהֶ֔ן\rb*. \rb Then all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the abundance|הַשָּׂבָ֖ע\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרָ֑יִם\rb* \rb will be forgotten|וְנִשְׁכַּ֥ח\rb*, \rb and the famine|הָרָעָ֖ב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb will devastate|וְכִלָּ֥ה\rb* \rb the land|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb*. \v 31 \rb The abundance|הַשָּׂבָע֙\rb* \rb in the land|בָּאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb will not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb be remembered|יִוָּדַ֤ע\rb*, \rb since|מִפְּנֵ֛י\rb* \rb the|הַה֖וּא\rb* \rb famine|הָרָעָ֥ב\rb* \rb that follows|אַחֲרֵי־\rb* \rb it|כֵ֑ן\rb*\rb |כִּֽי־\rb* \rb will be so|מְאֹֽד׃\rb* \rb severe|כָבֵ֥ד\rb*\rb |ה֖וּא\rb*.
\p \v 32 \rb Moreover|וְעַ֨ל\rb*, \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the dream|הַחֲל֛וֹם\rb* \rb was given|פַּעֲמָ֑יִם\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹ֖ה\rb* \rb in two versions|הִשָּׁנ֧וֹת\rb*, \rb the matter|הַדָּבָר֙\rb* \rb has been decreed|נָכ֤וֹן\rb* \rb by|מֵעִ֣ם\rb* \rb God|הָאֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb*, \rb and He|הָאֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb will carry it out|לַעֲשֹׂתֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb shortly|וּמְמַהֵ֥ר\rb*.
\p \v 33 \rb Now, therefore|וְעַתָּה֙\rb*, \rb Pharaoh|פַרְעֹ֔ה\rb* \rb should look for|יֵרֶ֣א\rb* \rb a discerning|נָב֣וֹן\rb* \rb and wise|וְחָכָ֑ם\rb* \rb man|אִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb and set him|וִישִׁיתֵ֖הוּ\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרָֽיִם׃\rb*. \v 34 \rb Let Pharaoh|פַרְעֹ֔ה\rb* \rb take action|יַעֲשֶׂ֣ה\rb* \rb and appoint|וְיַפְקֵ֥ד\rb* \rb commissioners|פְּקִדִ֖ים\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb* \rb to take a fifth|וְחִמֵּשׁ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb of the harvest|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb*\f + \fr 41:34 \ft See LXX; MT \fqa a fifth from the land\f* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb during the seven|בְּשֶׁ֖בַע\rb* \rb years|שְׁנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of abundance|הַשָּׂבָֽע׃\rb*. \v 35 \rb Under|תַּ֧חַת\rb* \rb the authority|יַד־\rb* \rb of Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹ֛ה\rb*, \rb let them collect|וְיִקְבְּצ֗וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the excess food|אֹ֙כֶל֙\rb* \rb from these|הָאֵ֑לֶּה\rb* \rb good|הַטֹּבֹ֔ת\rb* \rb years|הַשָּׁנִ֣ים\rb*, \rb that they may come|הַבָּאֹ֖ת\rb* \rb and lay up|וְיִצְבְּרוּ־\rb* \rb the grain|בָ֞ר\rb* \rb to be preserved|וְשָׁמָֽרוּ׃\rb* \rb as food|אֹ֥כֶל\rb* \rb in the cities|בֶּעָרִ֖ים\rb*. \v 36 \rb This food|הָאֹ֤כֶל\rb* \rb will be|וְהָיָ֨ה\rb* \rb a reserve|לְפִקָּדוֹן֙\rb* \rb for the land|לָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb during the seven|לְשֶׁ֙בַע֙\rb* \rb years|שְׁנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of famine|הָרָעָ֔ב\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb to come|תִּהְיֶ֖יןָ\rb* \rb upon the land|בְּאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרָ֑יִם\rb*. \rb Then the country|הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb will not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb perish|תִכָּרֵ֥ת\rb* \rb in the famine|בָּרָעָֽב׃\rb*.”
\s1 Joseph Given Charge of Egypt
\p \v 37 \rb This proposal|הַדָּבָ֖ר\rb* \rb pleased|וַיִּיטַ֥ב\rb*\rb |בְּעֵינֵ֣י\rb* \rb Pharaoh|פַרְעֹ֑ה\rb*\rb |וּבְעֵינֵ֖י\rb* \rb and all|כָּל־\rb* \rb his officials|עֲבָדָֽיו׃\rb*. \v 38 \rb So Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹ֖ה\rb* \rb asked|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb them|עֲבָדָ֑יו\rb*, “\rb Can we find|הֲנִמְצָ֣א\rb* \rb anyone like this|כָזֶ֔ה\rb* \rb man|אִ֕ישׁ\rb*, \rb in whom|אֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb the Spirit|ר֥וּחַ\rb* \rb of God|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb*\f + \fr 41:38 \ft Or \fqa the spirit of the gods\f* \rb abides|בּֽוֹ׃\rb*?”
\p \v 39 \rb Then Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹה֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Joseph|יוֹסֵ֔ף\rb*, “\rb Since|אַחֲרֵ֨י\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֛ים\rb*\rb |אוֹתְךָ֖\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb has made all|כָּל־\rb* \rb this|זֹ֑את\rb* \rb known to you|הוֹדִ֧יעַ\rb*, \rb there is no one|אֵין־\rb* \rb as discerning|נָב֥וֹן\rb* \rb and wise|וְחָכָ֖ם\rb* \rb as you|כָּמֽוֹךָ׃\rb*. \v 40 \rb You|אַתָּה֙\rb* \rb shall be|תִּהְיֶ֣ה\rb* \rb in charge of|עַל־\rb* \rb my house|בֵּיתִ֔י\rb*,\rb |וְעַל־\rb* \rb and all|כָּל־\rb* \rb my people|עַמִּ֑י\rb* \rb are to obey|יִשַּׁ֣ק\rb* \rb your commands|פִּ֖יךָ\rb*. \rb Only|רַ֥ק\rb* \rb with regard to the throne|הַכִּסֵּ֖א\rb* \rb will I be greater|אֶגְדַּ֥ל\rb* \rb than you|מִמֶּֽךָּ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 41 \rb Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹ֖ה\rb* \rb also told|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb Joseph|יוֹסֵ֑ף\rb*, “\rb |רְאֵה֙\rb* \rb I hereby place|נָתַ֣תִּי\rb*\rb |אֹֽתְךָ֔\rb* \rb you over|עַ֖ל\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרָֽיִם׃\rb*.” \v 42 \rb Then Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹ֤ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb removed|וַיָּ֨סַר\rb* \rb the signet ring|טַבַּעְתּוֹ֙\rb* \rb from|מֵעַ֣ל\rb* \rb his finger|יָד֔וֹ\rb*, \rb put|וַיִּתֵּ֥ן\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֖הּ\rb* \rb it on|עַל־\rb* \rb Joseph’s|יוֹסֵ֑ף\rb* \rb finger|יַ֣ד\rb*, \rb clothed|וַיַּלְבֵּ֤שׁ\rb* \rb him|אֹתוֹ֙\rb* \rb in garments|בִּגְדֵי־\rb* \rb of fine linen|שֵׁ֔שׁ\rb*, \rb and placed|וַיָּ֛שֶׂם\rb* \rb a gold|הַזָּהָ֖ב\rb* \rb chain|רְבִ֥ד\rb* \rb around|עַל־\rb* \rb his neck|צַוָּארֽוֹ׃\rb*. \v 43 \rb He had Joseph ride|וַיַּרְכֵּ֣ב\rb*\rb |אֹת֗וֹ\rb* \rb in his second|הַמִּשְׁנֶה֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb*\rb |ל֔וֹ\rb* \rb chariot|בְּמִרְכֶּ֤בֶת\rb*, \rb with men calling out|וַיִּקְרְא֥וּ\rb* \rb before him|לְפָנָ֖יו\rb*, “\rb Bow the knee|אַבְרֵ֑ךְ\rb*!”\f + \fr 41:43 \ft That is, \fqa “Abrek,” \ft probably an Egyptian word that sounds similar to the Hebrew for \fqa kneel\f* \rb So he placed|וְנָת֣וֹן\rb* \rb him|אֹת֔וֹ\rb* \rb over|עַ֖ל\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרָֽיִם׃\rb*.
\p \v 44 \rb And Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹ֛ה\rb* \rb declared|וַיֹּ֧אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Joseph|יוֹסֵ֖ף\rb*, “\rb I|אֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb am Pharaoh|פַרְעֹ֑ה\rb*, \rb but without your permission|וּבִלְעָדֶ֗יךָ\rb*, \rb no|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb one|אִ֧ישׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb in all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרָֽיִם׃\rb* \rb shall lift|יָרִ֨ים\rb* \rb his hand|יָד֛וֹ\rb* \rb or|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb foot|רַגְל֖וֹ\rb*.”
\p \v 45 \rb Pharaoh|פַרְעֹ֣ה\rb* \rb gave|וַיִּקְרָ֨א\rb* \rb Joseph|יוֹסֵף֮\rb* \rb the name|שֵׁם־\rb*\rb |צָֽפְנַ֣ת\rb* \rb Zaphenath-paneah|פַּעְנֵחַ֒\rb*,\f + \fr 41:45 \fqa Zaphenath-paneah \ft probably means \fqa Revealer of Mysteries \ft or \fqa God speaks and lives\ft .\f* \rb and he gave|וַיִּתֶּן־\rb* \rb him|ל֣וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Asenath|אָֽסְנַ֗ת\rb* \rb daughter|בַּת־\rb*\rb |פּ֥וֹטִי\rb* \rb of Potiphera|פֶ֛רַע\rb*, \rb priest|כֹּהֵ֥ן\rb* \rb of On|אֹ֖ן\rb*,\f + \fr 41:45 \ft That is, Heliopolis, as in LXX; also in verse 50\f* \rb to be his wife|לְאִשָּׁ֑ה\rb*. \rb And Joseph|יוֹסֵ֖ף\rb* \rb took charge|וַיֵּצֵ֥א\rb* \rb of all|עַל־\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרָֽיִם׃\rb*.
\s1 The Seven Years of Plenty
\p \v 46 \rb Now Joseph|וְיוֹסֵף֙\rb* \rb was thirty|שְׁלֹשִׁ֣ים\rb* \rb years old|בֶּן־\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֔ה\rb* \rb when he entered the service|בְּעָמְד֕וֹ\rb*\rb |לִפְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb of Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹ֣ה\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרָ֑יִם\rb*. \rb And Joseph|יוֹסֵף֙\rb* \rb left|וַיֵּצֵ֤א\rb* \rb Pharaoh’s|פַרְעֹ֔ה\rb* \rb presence|מִלִּפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb and traveled|וַֽיַּעְבֹ֖ר\rb* \rb throughout|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרָֽיִם׃\rb*.
\p \v 47 \rb During the seven|בְּשֶׁ֖בַע\rb* \rb years|שְׁנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of abundance|הַשָּׂבָ֑ע\rb*, \rb the land|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb brought forth|וַתַּ֣עַשׂ\rb* \rb bountifully|לִקְמָצִֽים׃\rb*. \v 48 \rb During those seven|שֶׁ֣בַע\rb* \rb years|שָׁנִ֗ים\rb*, \rb Joseph collected|וַיִּקְבֹּ֞ץ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the excess food|אֹ֣כֶל׀\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֔יִם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb*\rb |הָיוּ֙\rb* \rb and stored|וַיִּתֶּן־\rb* \rb it|אֹ֖כֶל\rb* \rb in the cities|בֶּעָרִ֑ים\rb*. \rb In every city|הָעִ֛יר\rb* \rb he laid up|נָתַ֥ן\rb* \rb the food|אֹ֧כֶל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb from the fields|שְׂדֵה־\rb* \rb around it|סְבִיבֹתֶ֖יהָ\rb*. \v 49 \rb So Joseph|יוֹסֵ֥ף\rb* \rb stored up|וַיִּצְבֹּ֨ר\rb* \rb grain|בָּ֛ר\rb* \rb in such abundance|הַרְבֵּ֣ה\rb*\rb |מְאֹ֑ד\rb*,\rb |עַ֛ד\rb* \rb like the sand|כְּח֥וֹל\rb* \rb of the sea|הַיָּ֖ם\rb*, \rb that|כִּי־\rb* \rb he stopped|חָדַ֥ל\rb* \rb keeping track of it|לִסְפֹּ֖ר\rb*; \rb for|כִּי־\rb* \rb it was beyond|אֵ֥ין\rb* \rb measure|מִסְפָּֽר׃\rb*.
\p \v 50 \rb Before|בְּטֶ֥רֶם\rb* \rb the years|שְׁנַ֣ת\rb* \rb of famine|הָרָעָ֑ב\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb arrived|תָּב֖וֹא\rb*, \rb two|שְׁנֵ֣י\rb* \rb sons|בָנִ֔ים\rb* \rb were born|יֻלַּד֙\rb* \rb to Joseph|וּלְיוֹסֵ֤ף\rb* \rb by Asenath|אָֽסְנַ֔ת\rb* \rb daughter|בַּת־\rb*\rb |פּ֥וֹטִי\rb* \rb of Potiphera|פֶ֖רַע\rb*, \rb priest|כֹּהֵ֥ן\rb* \rb of On|אֽוֹן׃\rb*\rb |יָֽלְדָה־\rb*\rb |לּוֹ֙\rb*. \v 51 \rb Joseph|יוֹסֵ֛ף\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb named|וַיִּקְרָ֥א\rb*\rb |שֵׁ֥ם\rb* \rb the firstborn|הַבְּכ֖וֹר\rb* \rb Manasseh|מְנַשֶּׁ֑ה\rb*,\f + \fr 41:51 \fqa Manasseh \ft sounds like the Hebrew for \fqa making to forget\ft .\f* \rb saying|כִּֽי־\rb*, “\rb God|אֱלֹהִים֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb has made me forget|נַשַּׁ֤נִי\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb my hardship|עֲמָלִ֔י\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֖ת\rb* \rb and all|כָּל־\rb* \rb my father’s|אָבִֽי׃\rb* \rb household|בֵּ֥ית\rb*.” \v 52 \rb |וְאֵ֛ת\rb* \rb And the second son|הַשֵּׁנִ֖י\rb* \rb he named|שֵׁ֥ם\rb*\rb |קָרָ֣א\rb* \rb Ephraim|אֶפְרָ֑יִם\rb*,\f + \fr 41:52 \fqa Ephraim \ft sounds like the Hebrew for \fqa making fruitful \ft or \fqa twice fruitful\ft .\f* \rb saying|כִּֽי־\rb*, “\rb God|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb has made me fruitful|הִפְרַ֥נִי\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of my affliction|עָנְיִֽי׃\rb*.”
\s1 The Famine Begins
\p \v 53 \rb When the seven|שֶׁ֖בַע\rb* \rb years|שְׁנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of abundance|הַשָּׂבָ֑ע\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb*\rb |הָיָ֖ה\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרָֽיִם׃\rb* \rb came to an end|וַתִּכְלֶ֕ינָה\rb*, \v 54 \rb the seven|שֶׁ֣בַע\rb* \rb years|שְׁנֵ֤י\rb* \rb of famine|הָרָעָב֙\rb*\rb |לָב֔וֹא\rb* \rb began|וַתְּחִלֶּ֜ינָה\rb*, \rb just as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb Joseph|יוֹסֵ֑ף\rb* \rb had said|אָמַ֣ר\rb*. \rb And although there was|וַיְהִ֤י\rb* \rb famine|רָעָב֙\rb* \rb in every|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb country|הָ֣אֲרָצ֔וֹת\rb*, \rb there was|הָ֥יָה\rb* \rb food|לָֽחֶם׃\rb* \rb throughout|וּבְכָל־\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֖יִם\rb*. \v 55 \rb When extreme hunger|וַתִּרְעַב֙\rb* \rb came to all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb and the people|הָעָ֛ם\rb* \rb cried out|וַיִּצְעַ֥ק\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹ֖ה\rb* \rb for food|לַלָּ֑חֶם\rb*, \rb he|פַּרְעֹ֤ה\rb* \rb told|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb the Egyptians|מִצְרַ֙יִם֙\rb*, “\rb Go|לְכ֣וּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Joseph|יוֹסֵ֔ף\rb* \rb and do|תַּעֲשֽׂוּ׃\rb* \rb whatever|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb he tells|יֹאמַ֥ר\rb* \rb you|לָכֶ֖ם\rb*.”
\p \v 56 \rb When the famine|וְהָרָעָ֣ב\rb* \rb had spread|הָיָ֔ה\rb* \rb over|עַ֖ל\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the|פְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb land|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb*, \rb Joseph|יוֹסֵ֜ף\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb opened up|וַיִּפְתַּ֨ח\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the storehouses|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb and sold grain|וַיִּשְׁבֹּ֣ר\rb* \rb to the Egyptians|לְמִצְרַ֔יִם\rb*; \rb for the famine|הָֽרָעָ֖ב\rb* \rb was severe|וַיֶּחֱזַ֥ק\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרָֽיִם׃\rb*. \v 57 \rb And every|וְכָל־\rb* \rb nation|הָאָ֙רֶץ֙\rb* \rb came|בָּ֣אוּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Joseph|יוֹסֵ֑ף\rb* \rb in Egypt|מִצְרַ֔יְמָה\rb* \rb to buy grain|לִשְׁבֹּ֖ר\rb*, \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the famine|הָרָעָ֖ב\rb* \rb was severe|חָזַ֥ק\rb* \rb over all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb the earth|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb*.
\c 42
\s1 Joseph’s Brothers Sent to Egypt
\p \v 1 \rb When Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֔ב\rb* \rb learned|וַיַּ֣רְא\rb* \rb that|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb there was|יֶשׁ־\rb* \rb grain|שֶׁ֖בֶר\rb* \rb in Egypt|בְּמִצְרָ֑יִם\rb*, \rb he|יַעֲקֹב֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to his sons|לְבָנָ֔יו\rb*, “\rb Why|לָ֖מָּה\rb* \rb are you staring at one another|תִּתְרָאֽוּ׃\rb*?”
\p \v 2 “\rb Look|הִנֵּ֣ה\rb*,” \rb he added|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*, “\rb I have heard|שָׁמַ֔עְתִּי\rb* \rb that|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb there is|יֶשׁ־\rb* \rb grain|שֶׁ֖בֶר\rb* \rb in Egypt|בְּמִצְרָ֑יִם\rb*. \rb Go down|רְדוּ־\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֙מָּה֙\rb* \rb and buy|וְשִׁבְרוּ־\rb* \rb some for us|לָ֣נוּ\rb*\rb |מִשָּׁ֔ם\rb*, \rb so that we may live|וְנִחְיֶ֖ה\rb* \rb and not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb die|נָמֽוּת׃\rb*.”
\p \v 3 \rb So ten|עֲשָׂרָ֑ה\rb* \rb of Joseph’s|יוֹסֵ֖ף\rb* \rb brothers|אֲחֵֽי־\rb* \rb went down|וַיֵּרְד֥וּ\rb* \rb to buy|לִשְׁבֹּ֥ר\rb* \rb grain|בָּ֖ר\rb* \rb from Egypt|מִמִּצְרָֽיִם׃\rb*. \v 4 \rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb But Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֖ב\rb* \rb did not|לֹא־\rb* \rb send|שָׁלַ֥ח\rb* \rb Joseph’s|יוֹסֵ֔ף\rb* \rb brother|אֲחִ֣י\rb* \rb Benjamin|בִּנְיָמִין֙\rb* \rb with|אֶת־\rb* \rb his brothers|אֶחָ֑יו\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb he said|אָמַ֔ר\rb*, “\rb I am afraid that|פֶּן־\rb* \rb harm|אָסֽוֹן׃\rb* \rb might befall him|יִקְרָאֶ֖נּוּ\rb*.”
\p \v 5 \rb So the sons|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb were among|בְּת֣וֹךְ\rb* \rb those who|הַבָּאִ֑ים\rb* \rb came|וַיָּבֹ֙אוּ֙\rb* \rb to buy grain|לִשְׁבֹּ֖ר\rb*, \rb since|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the famine|הָרָעָ֖ב\rb* \rb had also spread|הָיָ֥ה\rb* \rb to the land|בְּאֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Canaan|כְּנָֽעַן׃\rb*.
\p \v 6 \rb Now Joseph|וְיוֹסֵ֗ף\rb* \rb was|ה֚וּא\rb* \rb the ruler|הַשַּׁלִּ֣יט\rb* \rb of|עַל־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb*; \rb he was the one who|ה֥וּא\rb* \rb sold grain|הַמַּשְׁבִּ֖יר\rb* \rb to all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb its|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb* \rb people|עַ֣ם\rb*. \rb So when his|יוֹסֵ֔ף\rb* \rb brothers|אֲחֵ֣י\rb* \rb arrived|וַיָּבֹ֙אוּ֙\rb*, \rb they bowed down|וַיִּשְׁתַּֽחֲווּ־\rb* \rb before him|ל֥וֹ\rb* \rb with their faces|אַפַּ֖יִם\rb* \rb to the ground|אָֽרְצָה׃\rb*. \v 7 \rb And when Joseph|יוֹסֵ֛ף\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb saw|וַיַּ֥רְא\rb* \rb his brothers|אֶחָ֖יו\rb*, \rb he recognized them|וַיַּכִּרֵ֑ם\rb*, \rb but he treated them as strangers|וַיִּתְנַכֵּ֨ר\rb*\rb |אֲלֵיהֶ֜ם\rb* \rb and spoke|וַיְדַבֵּ֧ר\rb* \rb harshly|קָשׁ֗וֹת\rb* \rb to them|אִתָּ֣ם\rb*. “\rb Where|מֵאַ֣יִן\rb* \rb have you come from|בָּאתֶ֔ם\rb*?” \rb he asked|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֲלֵהֶם֙\rb*.
\p “\rb From the land|מֵאֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Canaan|כְּנַ֖עַן\rb*,” \rb they replied|וַיֹּ֣אמְר֔וּ\rb*. “\rb We are here to buy|לִשְׁבָּר־\rb* \rb food|אֹֽכֶל׃\rb*.”
\p \v 8 \rb Although Joseph|יוֹסֵ֖ף\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb recognized|וַיַּכֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb his brothers|אֶחָ֑יו\rb*, \rb they|וְהֵ֖ם\rb* \rb did not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb recognize him|הִכִּרֻֽהוּ׃\rb*. \v 9 \rb Joseph|יוֹסֵ֔ף\rb*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb* \rb remembered|וַיִּזְכֹּ֣ר\rb* \rb his dreams|הַחֲלֹמ֔וֹת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb*\rb |חָלַ֖ם\rb* \rb about them|לָהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֲלֵהֶם֙\rb*, “\rb You|אַתֶּ֔ם\rb* \rb are spies|מְרַגְּלִ֣ים\rb*! \rb You have come|בָּאתֶֽם׃\rb* \rb to see|לִרְא֛וֹת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb if our land|הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb is vulnerable|עֶרְוַ֥ת\rb*.”
\p \v 10 “\rb Not so|לֹ֣א\rb*, \rb my lord|אֲדֹנִ֑י\rb*,” \rb they replied|וַיֹּאמְר֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֵלָ֖יו\rb*. “\rb Your servants|וַעֲבָדֶ֥יךָ\rb* \rb have come|בָּ֖אוּ\rb* \rb to buy|לִשְׁבָּר־\rb* \rb food|אֹֽכֶל׃\rb*. \v 11 \rb We|נָ֑חְנוּ\rb* \rb are all|כֻּלָּ֕נוּ\rb* \rb sons|בְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of one|אֶחָ֖ד\rb* \rb man|אִישׁ־\rb*. \rb Your servants|עֲבָדֶ֖יךָ\rb*\rb |אֲנַ֔חְנוּ\rb* \rb are|הָי֥וּ\rb* \rb honest men|כֵּנִ֣ים\rb*, \rb not|לֹא־\rb* \rb spies|מְרַגְּלִֽים׃\rb*.”
\p \v 12 “\rb No|לֹ֕א\rb*,”\rb |כִּֽי־\rb* \rb he told|וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb* \rb them|אֲלֵהֶ֑ם\rb*. “\rb You have come|בָּאתֶ֥ם\rb* \rb to see|לִרְאֽוֹת׃\rb* \rb if our land|הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb is vulnerable|עֶרְוַ֥ת\rb*.”
\p \v 13 \rb But they answered|וַיֹּאמְר֗וּ\rb*, “\rb Your servants|עֲבָדֶ֨יךָ\rb*\rb |אֲנַ֛חְנוּ\rb* \rb are twelve|שְׁנֵ֣ים\rb*\rb |עָשָׂר֩\rb* \rb brothers|אַחִ֧ים׀\rb*, \rb the sons|בְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of one|אֶחָ֖ד\rb* \rb man|אִישׁ־\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Canaan|כְּנָ֑עַן\rb*.\rb |וְהִנֵּ֨ה\rb* \rb The youngest|הַקָּטֹ֤ן\rb* \rb is now|הַיּ֔וֹם\rb* \rb with|אֶת־\rb* \rb our father|אָבִ֙ינוּ֙\rb*, \rb and one|וְהָאֶחָ֖ד\rb* \rb is no more|אֵינֶֽנּוּ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 14 \rb Then Joseph|יוֹסֵ֑ף\rb*\rb |ה֗וּא\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb declared|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֲלֵהֶ֖ם\rb*, “\rb Just as I said|דִּבַּ֧רְתִּי\rb*\rb |אֲלֵכֶ֛ם\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֖ר\rb*, \rb you|אַתֶּֽם׃\rb* \rb are spies|מְרַגְּלִ֥ים\rb*! \v 15 \rb And this is how|בְּזֹ֖את\rb* \rb you will be tested|תִּבָּחֵ֑נוּ\rb*: \rb As surely as Pharaoh|פַרְעֹה֙\rb* \rb lives|חֵ֤י\rb*, \rb you shall not|אִם־\rb* \rb leave|תֵּצְא֣וּ\rb* \rb this|מִזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb place unless|כִּ֧י\rb*\rb |אִם־\rb* \rb your youngest|הַקָּטֹ֖ן\rb* \rb brother|אֲחִיכֶ֥ם\rb* \rb comes|בְּב֛וֹא\rb* \rb here|הֵֽנָּה׃\rb*. \v 16 \rb Send|שִׁלְח֨וּ\rb* \rb one|אֶחָד֮\rb* \rb of your number|מִכֶּ֣ם\rb* \rb to get|וְיִקַּ֣ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your brother|אֲחִיכֶם֒\rb*; \rb the rest of you|וְאַתֶּם֙\rb* \rb will be confined|הֵאָ֣סְר֔וּ\rb* \rb so that the truth|הַֽאֱמֶ֖ת\rb* \rb of your words|דִּבְרֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb may be tested|וְיִבָּֽחֲנוּ֙\rb*.\rb |אִתְּכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb If|וְאִם־\rb* \rb they are untrue|לֹ֕א\rb*, \rb then as surely as Pharaoh|פַרְעֹ֔ה\rb*\rb |כִּ֥י\rb* \rb lives|חֵ֣י\rb*, \rb you|אַתֶּֽם׃\rb* \rb are spies|מְרַגְּלִ֖ים\rb*!”
\p \v 17 \rb So Joseph imprisoned them|וַיֶּאֱסֹ֥ף\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֛ם\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |מִשְׁמָ֖ר\rb* \rb for three|שְׁלֹ֥שֶׁת\rb* \rb days|יָמִֽים׃\rb*, \v 18 \rb and on the third|הַשְּׁלִישִׁ֔י\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb he|יוֹסֵף֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to them|אֲלֵהֶ֤ם\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* “\rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb fear|יָרֵֽא׃\rb* \rb God|הָאֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb*. \rb So do|עֲשׂ֖וּ\rb* \rb this|זֹ֥את\rb* \rb and you will live|וִֽחְי֑וּ\rb*: \v 19 \rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb you|אַתֶּ֔ם\rb*\rb |אֲחִיכֶ֣ם\rb* \rb are honest|כֵּנִ֣ים\rb*, \rb leave one|אֶחָ֔ד\rb* \rb of your brothers in custody|יֵאָסֵ֖ר\rb*\rb |בְּבֵ֣ית\rb*\rb |מִשְׁמַרְכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb while the rest of you|וְאַתֶּם֙\rb* \rb go|לְכ֣וּ\rb* \rb and take back|הָבִ֔יאוּ\rb* \rb grain|שֶׁ֖בֶר\rb* \rb to relieve the hunger|רַעֲב֥וֹן\rb* \rb of your households|בָּתֵּיכֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 20 \rb Then|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb bring|תָּבִ֣יאוּ\rb* \rb your youngest|הַקָּטֹן֙\rb* \rb brother|אֲחִיכֶ֤ם\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֔י\rb* \rb so that your words|דִבְרֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb can be verified|וְיֵאָמְנ֥וּ\rb*, \rb that you may not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb die|תָמ֑וּתוּ\rb*.”
\p \rb And to this|כֵֽן׃\rb* \rb they consented|וַיַּעֲשׂוּ־\rb*.
\p \v 21 \rb Then they said|וַיֹּאמְר֞וּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb one|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb another|אָחִ֗יו\rb*, “\rb Surely|אֲבָל֮\rb* \rb we|אֲנַחְנוּ֮\rb* \rb are being punished|אֲשֵׁמִ֣ים׀\rb* \rb because of|עַל־\rb* \rb our brother|אָחִינוּ֒\rb*.\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb We saw|רָאִ֜ינוּ\rb* \rb his|נַפְשׁ֛וֹ\rb* \rb anguish|צָרַ֥ת\rb* \rb when he pleaded|בְּהִתְחַֽנְנ֥וֹ\rb* \rb with us|אֵלֵ֖ינוּ\rb*, \rb but we would not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb listen|שָׁמָ֑עְנוּ\rb*. \rb That is why|עַל־\rb*\rb |כֵּן֙\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּֽאת׃\rb* \rb distress|הַצָּרָ֖ה\rb* \rb has come|בָּ֣אָה\rb* \rb upon us|אֵלֵ֔ינוּ\rb*.”
\p \v 22 \rb And Reuben|רְאוּבֵ֨ן\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֜ם\rb* \rb responded|וַיַּעַן֩\rb*, “\rb Didn’t|הֲלוֹא֩\rb*\rb |אָמַ֨רְתִּי\rb*\rb |אֲלֵיכֶ֧ם׀\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֛ר\rb* \rb I tell|לֵאמֹ֗ר\rb* \rb you not|אַל־\rb* \rb to sin against|תֶּחֶטְא֥וּ\rb* \rb the boy|בַיֶּ֖לֶד\rb*? \rb But you would not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb listen|שְׁמַעְתֶּ֑ם\rb*.\rb |וְגַם־\rb* \rb Now|הִנֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb we must account for|נִדְרָֽשׁ׃\rb* \rb his blood|דָּמ֖וֹ\rb*!”
\p \v 23 \rb They|וְהֵם֙\rb* \rb did not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb realize|יָֽדְע֔וּ\rb* \rb that|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb Joseph|יוֹסֵ֑ף\rb* \rb understood them|שֹׁמֵ֖עַ\rb*, \rb since|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb there was an interpreter|הַמֵּלִ֖יץ\rb* \rb between them|בֵּינֹתָֽם׃\rb*. \v 24 \rb And he turned away|וַיִּסֹּ֥ב\rb* \rb from them|מֵֽעֲלֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb and wept|וַיֵּ֑בְךְּ\rb*. \rb When he turned back|וַיָּ֤שָׁב\rb* \rb and spoke|וַיְדַבֵּ֣ר\rb*\rb |אֲלֵהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb to them|אֲלֵהֶם֙\rb*, \rb he took|וַיִּקַּ֤ח\rb* \rb Simeon|שִׁמְע֔וֹן\rb* \rb from them|מֵֽאִתָּם֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb and had him bound|וַיֶּאֱסֹ֥ר\rb*\rb |אֹת֖וֹ\rb* \rb before their eyes|לְעֵינֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*.
\s1 Joseph’s Brothers Return to Canaan
\p \v 25 \rb Then Joseph|יוֹסֵ֗ף\rb* \rb gave orders|וַיְצַ֣ו\rb* \rb to fill their bags|כְּלֵיהֶם֮\rb* \rb with|וַיְמַלְא֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb grain|בָּר֒\rb*, \rb to return|וּלְהָשִׁ֤יב\rb* \rb each man’s|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb silver|כַּסְפֵּיהֶם֙\rb*\f + \fr 42:25 \ft Or \fqa money\ft ; here and throughout chapters 42–44\f* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his sack|שַׂקּ֔וֹ\rb*, \rb and to give|וְלָתֵ֥ת\rb* \rb them|לָהֶ֛ם\rb* \rb provisions|צֵדָ֖ה\rb* \rb for their journey|לַדָּ֑רֶךְ\rb*. \rb This|כֵּֽן׃\rb* \rb order was carried out|וַיַּ֥עַשׂ\rb*, \v 26 \rb and they loaded|וַיִּשְׂא֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the grain|שִׁבְרָ֖ם\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb their donkeys|חֲמֹרֵיהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb and departed|וַיֵּלְכ֖וּ\rb*\rb |מִשָּֽׁם׃\rb*.
\p \v 27 \rb At the place where they lodged for the night|בַּמָּל֑וֹן\rb*, \rb one|הָאֶחָ֜ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb of them opened|וַיִּפְתַּ֨ח\rb* \rb his sack|שַׂקּ֗וֹ\rb* \rb to get|לָתֵ֥ת\rb* \rb feed|מִסְפּ֛וֹא\rb* \rb for his donkey|לַחֲמֹר֖וֹ\rb*, \rb and he saw|וַיַּרְא֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his silver|כַּסְפּ֔וֹ\rb*\rb |וְהִנֵּה־\rb*\rb |ה֖וּא\rb* \rb in the mouth|בְּפִ֥י\rb* \rb of the sack|אַמְתַּחְתּֽוֹ׃\rb*. \v 28 “\rb My silver|כַּסְפִּ֔י\rb*\rb |וְגַ֖ם\rb* \rb has been returned|הוּשַׁ֣ב\rb*!” \rb he said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his brothers|אֶחָיו֙\rb*. “\rb It is here|הִנֵּ֣ה\rb* \rb in my sack|בְאַמְתַּחְתִּ֑י\rb*.”
\p \rb Their hearts|לִבָּ֗ם\rb* \rb sank|וַיֵּצֵ֣א\rb*, \rb and trembling|וַיֶּֽחֶרְד֞וּ\rb*, \rb they turned to|אֶל־\rb* \rb one|אִ֤ישׁ\rb* \rb another|אָחִיו֙\rb* \rb and said|לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb*, “\rb What|מַה־\rb* \rb is this|זֹּ֛את\rb* \rb that God|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb has done|עָשָׂ֥ה\rb* \rb to us|לָֽנוּ׃\rb*?”
\p \v 29 \rb When they reached|וַיָּבֹ֛אוּ\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb their father|אֲבִיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֥ב\rb* \rb in the land|אַ֣רְצָה\rb* \rb of Canaan|כְּנָ֑עַן\rb*, \rb they described|וַיַּגִּ֣ידוּ\rb* \rb to|ל֔וֹ\rb* \rb him|אֵ֛ת\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb that had happened to them|הַקֹּרֹ֥ת\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֖ם\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*: \v 30 “\rb The man|הָאִ֨ישׁ\rb* \rb who is lord|אֲדֹנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the land|הָאָ֛רֶץ\rb* \rb spoke|דִּ֠בֶּר\rb* \rb harshly|קָשׁ֑וֹת\rb*\rb |וַיִּתֵּ֣ן\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֔נוּ\rb* \rb to us|אִתָּ֖נוּ\rb* \rb and accused us of spying|כִּֽמְרַגְּלִ֖ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb on the country|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb*.
\p \v 31 \rb But we told|וַנֹּ֥אמֶר\rb* \rb him|אֵלָ֖יו\rb*, ‘\rb We|אֲנָ֑חְנוּ\rb* \rb are|הָיִ֖ינוּ\rb* \rb honest men|כֵּנִ֣ים\rb*, \rb not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb spies|מְרַגְּלִֽים׃\rb*. \v 32 \rb We|אֲנַ֛חְנוּ\rb* \rb are twelve|שְׁנֵים־\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֥ר\rb* \rb brothers|אַחִ֖ים\rb*, \rb sons|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of one father|אָבִ֑ינוּ\rb*. \rb One|הָאֶחָ֣ד\rb* \rb is no more|אֵינֶ֔נּוּ\rb*, \rb and the youngest|וְהַקָּטֹ֥ן\rb* \rb is now|הַיּ֛וֹם\rb* \rb with|אֶת־\rb* \rb our father|אָבִ֖ינוּ\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Canaan|כְּנָֽעַן׃\rb*.’
\p \v 33 \rb Then the man|הָאִישׁ֙\rb* \rb who is lord|אֲדֹנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the land|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to us|אֵלֵ֗ינוּ\rb*, ‘\rb This is how|בְּזֹ֣את\rb* \rb I will know|אֵדַ֔ע\rb* \rb whether|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb you|אַתֶּ֑ם\rb* \rb are honest|כֵנִ֖ים\rb*: \rb Leave|הַנִּ֣יחוּ\rb* \rb one|הָֽאֶחָד֙\rb* \rb brother|אֲחִיכֶ֤ם\rb* \rb with me|אִתִּ֔י\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb take|קְח֥וּ\rb* \rb food to relieve the hunger|רַעֲב֥וֹן\rb* \rb of your households|בָּתֵּיכֶ֖ם\rb*, \rb and go|וָלֵֽכוּ׃\rb*. \v 34 \rb But bring|וְ֠הָבִיאוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your youngest|הַקָּטֹן֮\rb* \rb brother|אֲחִיכֶ֣ם\rb* \rb back to me|אֵלַי֒\rb* \rb so I will know|וְאֵֽדְעָ֗ה\rb* \rb that|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb you|אַתֶּ֔ם\rb* \rb are not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb spies|מְרַגְּלִים֙\rb* \rb but|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb honest men|כֵנִ֖ים\rb*\rb |אַתֶּ֑ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*. \rb Then I will give|אֶתֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb your brother|אֲחִיכֶם֙\rb* \rb back to you|לָכֶ֔ם\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and you can trade|תִּסְחָֽרוּ׃\rb* \rb in the land|הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb*.’”
\p \v 35 \rb |וַיְהִ֗י\rb* \rb As they|הֵ֚ם\rb* \rb began emptying|מְרִיקִ֣ים\rb* \rb their sacks|שַׂקֵּיהֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb there|וְהִנֵּה־\rb* \rb in each man’s|אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb sack|בְּשַׂקּ֑וֹ\rb* \rb was his bag|צְרוֹר־\rb* \rb of silver|כַּסְפּ֖וֹ\rb*! \rb And when they|הֵ֥מָּה\rb* \rb and their father|וַאֲבִיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb saw|וַיִּרְא֞וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the bags|צְרֹר֧וֹת\rb* \rb of silver|כַּסְפֵּיהֶ֛ם\rb*, \rb they were dismayed|וַיִּירָֽאוּ׃\rb*.
\p \v 36 \rb Their father|אֲבִיהֶ֔ם\rb*\rb |אֹתִ֖י\rb* \rb Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֣ב\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to them|אֲלֵהֶם֙\rb*, “\rb You have deprived me of my sons|שִׁכַּלְתֶּ֑ם\rb*. \rb Joseph|יוֹסֵ֤ף\rb* \rb is gone|אֵינֶ֙נּוּ֙\rb* \rb and Simeon|וְשִׁמְע֣וֹן\rb* \rb is no more|אֵינֶ֔נּוּ\rb*.\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Now you want to take|תִּקָּ֔חוּ\rb* \rb Benjamin|בִּנְיָמִ֣ן\rb*. \rb Everything|כֻלָּֽנָה׃\rb* \rb is going|הָי֥וּ\rb* \rb against me|עָלַ֖י\rb*!”
\p \v 37 \rb Then Reuben|רְאוּבֵן֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his father|אָבִ֣יו\rb*,\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* “\rb You may kill|תָּמִ֔ית\rb* \rb my two|שְׁנֵ֤י\rb* \rb sons|בָנַי֙\rb* \rb if|אִם־\rb* \rb I fail|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb to bring him back|אֲבִיאֶ֖נּוּ\rb* \rb to you|אֵלֶ֑יךָ\rb*. \rb Put|תְּנָ֤ה\rb* \rb him|אֹתוֹ֙\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb my care|יָדִ֔י\rb*, \rb and I|וַאֲנִ֖י\rb* \rb will return him|אֲשִׁיבֶ֥נּוּ\rb*\rb |אֵלֶֽיךָ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 38 \rb But Jacob replied|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*, “\rb My son|בְּנִ֖י\rb* \rb will not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb go down there|יֵרֵ֥ד\rb* \rb with you|עִמָּכֶ֑ם\rb*, \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb his brother|אָחִ֨יו\rb* \rb is dead|מֵ֜ת\rb*, \rb and he|וְה֧וּא\rb* \rb alone|לְבַדּ֣וֹ\rb* \rb is left|נִשְׁאָ֗ר\rb*. \rb If any harm comes|וּקְרָאָ֤הוּ\rb*\rb |אָסוֹן֙\rb* \rb to him on your|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb*\rb |תֵּֽלְכוּ־\rb*\rb |בָ֔הּ\rb* \rb journey|בַּדֶּ֙רֶךְ֙\rb*, \rb you will bring my gray hair|שֵׂיבָתִ֛י\rb* \rb down|וְהוֹרַדְתֶּ֧ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb to Sheol|שְׁאֽוֹלָה׃\rb* \rb in sorrow|בְּיָג֖וֹן\rb*.”
\c 43
\s1 The Return to Egypt with Benjamin
\p \v 1 \rb Now the famine|וְהָרָעָ֖ב\rb* \rb was still severe|כָּבֵ֥ד\rb* \rb in the land|בָּאָֽרֶץ׃\rb*. \v 2 \rb |וַיְהִ֗י\rb* \rb So when|כַּאֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Jacob’s sons had eaten all|כִּלּוּ֙\rb*\rb |לֶאֱכֹ֣ל\rb* \rb the grain|הַשֶּׁ֔בֶר\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb they had brought|הֵבִ֖יאוּ\rb* \rb from Egypt|מִמִּצְרָ֑יִם\rb*, \rb their father|אֲבִיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to them|אֲלֵיהֶם֙\rb*, “\rb Go back|שֻׁ֖בוּ\rb* \rb and buy|שִׁבְרוּ־\rb* \rb us|לָ֥נוּ\rb* \rb a little more|מְעַט־\rb* \rb food|אֹֽכֶל׃\rb*.”
\p \v 3 \rb But Judah|יְהוּדָ֖ה\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֧אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֵלָ֛יו\rb*, “\rb The man|הָאִ֤ישׁ\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹר֙\rb* \rb solemnly warned|הָעֵ֣ד\rb*\rb |הֵעִד֩\rb* \rb us|בָּ֨נוּ\rb*, ‘\rb You will not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb see|תִרְא֣וּ\rb* \rb my face|פָנַ֔י\rb* \rb again unless|בִּלְתִּ֖י\rb* \rb your brother|אֲחִיכֶ֥ם\rb* \rb is with you|אִתְּכֶֽם׃\rb*.’ \v 4 \rb If|אִם־\rb*\rb |יֶשְׁךָ֛\rb* \rb you will send|מְשַׁלֵּ֥חַ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb our brother|אָחִ֖ינוּ\rb* \rb with us|אִתָּ֑נוּ\rb*, \rb we will go down|נֵרְדָ֕ה\rb* \rb and buy|וְנִשְׁבְּרָ֥ה\rb* \rb food|אֹֽכֶל׃\rb* \rb for you|לְךָ֖\rb*. \v 5 \rb But if|וְאִם־\rb* \rb you will not|אֵינְךָ֥\rb* \rb send him|מְשַׁלֵּ֖חַ\rb*, \rb we will not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb go|נֵרֵ֑ד\rb*; \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the man|הָאִ֞ישׁ\rb* \rb told|אָמַ֤ר\rb* \rb us|אֵלֵ֙ינוּ֙\rb*, ‘\rb You will not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb see|תִרְא֣וּ\rb* \rb my face|פָנַ֔י\rb* \rb again unless|בִּלְתִּ֖י\rb* \rb your brother|אֲחִיכֶ֥ם\rb* \rb is with you|אִתְּכֶֽם׃\rb*.’”
\p \v 6 “\rb Why|לָמָ֥ה\rb* \rb did you bring this trouble|הֲרֵעֹתֶ֖ם\rb* \rb upon me|לִ֑י\rb*?” \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb asked|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb*. “\rb Why did you tell|לְהַגִּ֣יד\rb* \rb the man|לָאִ֔ישׁ\rb* \rb you had another|הַע֥וֹד\rb*\rb |לָכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb brother|אָֽח׃\rb*?”
\p \v 7 \rb They replied|וַיֹּאמְר֡וּ\rb*, “\rb The man|הָ֠אִישׁ\rb* \rb questioned|שָׁא֣וֹל\rb* \rb us|לָ֣נוּ\rb* \rb in detail|שָֽׁאַל־\rb* \rb about ourselves and our family|וּלְמֽוֹלַדְתֵּ֜נוּ\rb*: ‘\rb Is your father|אֲבִיכֶ֥ם\rb* \rb still|הַע֨וֹד\rb* \rb alive|חַי֙\rb*? \rb Do you have|הֲיֵ֣שׁ\rb*\rb |לָכֶ֣ם\rb* \rb another brother|אָ֔ח\rb*?’ \rb And we answered|וַנַ֨גֶּד־\rb* \rb him|ל֔וֹ\rb* \rb accordingly|עַל־\rb*\rb |פִּ֖י\rb*.\rb |הַדְּבָרִ֣ים\rb*\rb |הָאֵ֑לֶּה\rb* \rb How could we possibly know|הֲיָד֣וֹעַ\rb*\rb |נֵדַ֔ע\rb* \rb that|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb he would say|יֹאמַ֔ר\rb*, ‘\rb Bring|הוֹרִ֖ידוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your brother here|אֲחִיכֶֽם׃\rb*’?”
\p \v 8 \rb And Judah|יְהוּדָ֜ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his father|אָבִ֗יו\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֣ל\rb*, “\rb Send|שִׁלְחָ֥ה\rb* \rb the boy|הַנַּ֛עַר\rb* \rb with me|אִתִּ֖י\rb*,\rb |וְנָק֣וּמָה\rb* \rb and we will go at once|וְנֵלֵ֑כָה\rb*, \rb so that we may live|וְנִֽחְיֶה֙\rb* \rb and not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb die|נָמ֔וּת\rb*—\rb |גַּם־\rb* \rb neither we|אֲנַ֥חְנוּ\rb*,\rb |גַם־\rb* \rb nor you|אַתָּ֖ה\rb*,\rb |גַּם־\rb* \rb nor our children|טַפֵּֽנוּ׃\rb*. \v 9 \rb I|אָֽנֹכִי֙\rb* \rb will guarantee his safety|אֶֽעֶרְבֶ֔נּוּ\rb*. \rb You may hold me|תְּבַקְשֶׁ֑נּוּ\rb* \rb personally responsible|מִיָּדִ֖י\rb*. \rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb I do not|לֹ֨א\rb* \rb bring him back|הֲבִיאֹתִ֤יו\rb*\rb |אֵלֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb and set him|וְהִצַּגְתִּ֣יו\rb* \rb before you|לְפָנֶ֔יךָ\rb*, \rb then may I|לְךָ֖\rb* \rb bear the guilt before you|וְחָטָ֥אתִֽי\rb* \rb all my life|כָּל־\rb*\rb |הַיָּמִֽים׃\rb*. \v 10 \rb If we had not|כִּ֖י\rb*\rb |לוּלֵ֣א\rb* \rb delayed|הִתְמַהְמָ֑הְנוּ\rb*,\rb |כִּֽי־\rb* \rb we could have come and gone|שַׁ֖בְנוּ\rb*\rb |זֶ֥ה\rb* \rb twice|פַעֲמָֽיִם׃\rb* \rb by now|עַתָּ֥ה\rb*.”
\p \v 11 \rb Then their father|אֲבִיהֶ֗ם\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֣ל\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to them|אֲלֵהֶ֜ם\rb*, “\rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb it must be so|כֵּ֣ן׀\rb*, \rb then|אֵפוֹא֮\rb* \rb do|עֲשׂוּ֒\rb* \rb this|זֹ֣את\rb*: \rb Put|קְח֞וּ\rb* \rb some of the best products|מִזִּמְרַ֤ת\rb* \rb of the land|הָאָ֙רֶץ֙\rb* \rb in your packs|בִּכְלֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb and carry them down|וְהוֹרִ֥ידוּ\rb* \rb as a gift|מִנְחָ֑ה\rb* \rb for the man|לָאִ֖ישׁ\rb* — \rb a little|מְעַ֤ט\rb* \rb balm|צֳרִי֙\rb* \rb and a little|וּמְעַ֣ט\rb* \rb honey|דְּבַ֔שׁ\rb*, \rb spices|נְכֹ֣את\rb* \rb and myrrh|וָלֹ֔ט\rb*, \rb pistachios|בָּטְנִ֖ים\rb* \rb and almonds|וּשְׁקֵדִֽים׃\rb*. \v 12 \rb Take|קְח֣וּ\rb* \rb double|מִשְׁנֶ֖ה\rb* \rb the silver|וְכֶ֥סֶף\rb* \rb with you|בְיֶדְכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb so that|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb you may return|הַמּוּשָׁ֨ב\rb* \rb the silver|הַכֶּ֜סֶף\rb* \rb that was put back|תָּשִׁ֣יבוּ\rb*\rb |בְיֶדְכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb into the mouths|בְּפִ֤י\rb* \rb of your sacks|אַמְתְּחֹֽתֵיכֶם֙\rb*. \rb Perhaps|אוּלַ֥י\rb* \rb it|הֽוּא׃\rb* \rb was a mistake|מִשְׁגֶּ֖ה\rb*. \v 13 \rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Take|קָ֑חוּ\rb* \rb your brother as well|אֲחִיכֶ֖ם\rb*, \rb and return|שׁ֥וּבוּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the man|הָאִֽישׁ׃\rb* \rb at once|וְק֖וּמוּ\rb*. \v 14 \rb May God|וְאֵ֣ל\rb* \rb Almighty|שַׁדַּ֗י\rb*\f + \fr 43:14 \ft Hebrew \fqa El-Shaddai\f* \rb grant|יִתֵּ֨ן\rb* \rb you|לָכֶ֤ם\rb* \rb mercy|רַחֲמִים֙\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the man|הָאִ֔ישׁ\rb*, \rb that he may release|וְשִׁלַּ֥ח\rb* \rb your|לָכֶ֛ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb other|אַחֵ֖ר\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb brother|אֲחִיכֶ֥ם\rb* \rb along with Benjamin|בִּנְיָמִ֑ין\rb*. \rb As for me|וַאֲנִ֕י\rb*, \rb if|כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I am bereaved|שָׁכֹ֖לְתִּי\rb*, \rb I am bereaved|שָׁכָֽלְתִּי׃\rb*.”
\p \v 15 \rb So the men|הָֽאֲנָשִׁים֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb took|וַיִּקְח֤וּ\rb* \rb these|הַזֹּ֔את\rb* \rb gifts|הַמִּנְחָ֣ה\rb*, \rb along with double|וּמִשְׁנֶה־\rb* \rb the amount of silver|כֶּ֛סֶף\rb*\rb |לָקְח֥וּ\rb*\rb |בְיָדָ֖ם\rb*, \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Benjamin as well|בִּנְיָמִ֑ן\rb*.\rb |וַיָּקֻ֙מוּ֙\rb* \rb Then they hurried down|וַיֵּרְד֣וּ\rb* \rb to Egypt|מִצְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb and stood|וַיַּֽעַמְד֖וּ\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb Joseph|יוֹסֵֽף׃\rb*.
\s1 Joseph’s Hospitality to His Brothers
\p \v 16 \rb When Joseph|יוֹסֵ֣ף\rb* \rb saw|וַיַּ֨רְא\rb* \rb Benjamin|בִּנְיָמִין֒\rb* \rb with his brothers|אִתָּם֮\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb he said|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb* \rb to the steward|לַֽאֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb of|עַל־\rb* \rb his house|בֵּית֔וֹ\rb*, “\rb Take|הָבֵ֥א\rb* \rb these men|הָאֲנָשִׁ֖ים\rb* \rb to my house|הַבָּ֑יְתָה\rb*. \rb Slaughter|וּטְבֹ֤חַ\rb* \rb an animal|טֶ֙בַח֙\rb* \rb and prepare it|וְהָכֵ֔ן\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb they shall dine|יֹאכְל֥וּ\rb*\rb |הָאֲנָשִׁ֖ים\rb* \rb with me|אִתִּ֛י\rb* \rb at noon|בַּֽצָּהֳרָֽיִם׃\rb*.” \v 17 \rb The man|הָאִ֔ישׁ\rb* \rb did|וַיַּ֣עַשׂ\rb* \rb as|כַּֽאֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb Joseph|יוֹסֵ֑ף\rb* \rb had commanded|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb and took|וַיָּבֵ֥א\rb* \rb the brothers|הָאִ֛ישׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |הָאֲנָשִׁ֖ים\rb* \rb to Joseph’s|יוֹסֵֽף׃\rb* \rb house|בֵּ֥יתָה\rb*.
\p \v 18 \rb But the brothers|הָֽאֲנָשִׁ֗ים\rb* \rb were frightened|וַיִּֽירְא֣וּ\rb* \rb that|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb they had been taken|הֽוּבְאוּ֮\rb* \rb to Joseph’s|יוֹסֵף֒\rb* \rb house|בֵּ֣ית\rb*. “\rb We|אֲנַ֖חְנוּ\rb* \rb have been brought|מֽוּבָאִ֑ים\rb* \rb here because of|עַל־\rb*\rb |דְּבַ֤ר\rb* \rb the silver|הַכֶּ֙סֶף֙\rb* \rb that was returned|הַשָּׁ֤ב\rb* \rb in our bags|בְּאַמְתְּחֹתֵ֙ינוּ֙\rb* \rb the first time|בַּתְּחִלָּ֔ה\rb*,” \rb they said|וַיֹּאמְר֗וּ\rb*. “\rb They intend|לְהִתְגֹּלֵ֤ל\rb*\rb |עָלֵ֙ינוּ֙\rb* \rb to overpower|וּלְהִתְנַפֵּ֣ל\rb* \rb us|עָלֵ֔ינוּ\rb* \rb and take|וְלָקַ֧חַת\rb* \rb us|אֹתָ֛נוּ\rb* \rb as slaves|לַעֲבָדִ֖ים\rb*, \rb along with|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb our donkeys|חֲמֹרֵֽינוּ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 19 \rb So they approached|וַֽיִּגְּשׁוּ֙\rb* \rb Joseph’s|יוֹסֵ֑ף\rb* \rb steward|הָאִ֔ישׁ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb*\rb |בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb and spoke|וַיְדַבְּר֥וּ\rb* \rb to him|אֵלָ֖יו\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb at the entrance|פֶּ֥תַח\rb* \rb to the house|הַבָּֽיִת׃\rb*. \v 20 “\rb Please|בִּ֣י\rb*, \rb sir|אֲדֹנִ֑י\rb*,” \rb they said|וַיֹּאמְר֖וּ\rb*, “\rb we really did come down|יָרֹ֥ד\rb*\rb |יָרַ֛דְנוּ\rb* \rb here the first time|בַּתְּחִלָּ֖ה\rb* \rb to buy|לִשְׁבָּר־\rb* \rb food|אֹֽכֶל׃\rb*. \v 21 \rb But|וַֽיְהִ֞י\rb* \rb when|כִּי־\rb* \rb we came|בָ֣אנוּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the place we lodged for the night|הַמָּל֗וֹן\rb*, \rb we opened|וַֽנִּפְתְּחָה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb our sacks|אַמְתְּחֹתֵ֔ינוּ\rb* \rb and, behold|וְהִנֵּ֤ה\rb*, \rb each of us found|אִישׁ֙\rb* \rb his silver|כֶֽסֶף־\rb* \rb in the mouth|בְּפִ֣י\rb* \rb of his sack|אַמְתַּחְתּ֔וֹ\rb*! \rb It was the full amount|בְּמִשְׁקָל֑וֹ\rb* \rb of our silver|כַּסְפֵּ֖נוּ\rb*, \rb and we have brought it back|וַנָּ֥שֶׁב\rb*\rb |אֹת֖וֹ\rb* \rb with us|בְּיָדֵֽנוּ׃\rb*. \v 22 \rb We have brought|הוֹרַ֥דְנוּ\rb* \rb additional|אַחֵ֛ר\rb* \rb silver|וְכֶ֧סֶף\rb* \rb with us|בְיָדֵ֖נוּ\rb* \rb to buy|לִשְׁבָּר־\rb* \rb food|אֹ֑כֶל\rb*. \rb We do not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb know|יָדַ֔עְנוּ\rb* \rb who|מִי־\rb* \rb put|שָׂ֥ם\rb* \rb our silver|כַּסְפֵּ֖נוּ\rb* \rb in our sacks|בְּאַמְתְּחֹתֵֽינוּ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 23 “\rb It is fine|שָׁל֨וֹם\rb*\rb |לָכֶ֜ם\rb*,” \rb said the steward|וַיֹּאמֶר֩\rb*. “\rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb be afraid|תִּירָ֗אוּ\rb*. \rb Your God|אֱלֹ֨הֵיכֶ֜ם\rb*, \rb the God|וֵֽאלֹהֵ֤י\rb* \rb of your father|אֲבִיכֶם֙\rb*, \rb gave|נָתַ֨ן\rb* \rb you|לָכֶ֤ם\rb* \rb the treasure|מַטְמוֹן֙\rb* \rb that was in your sacks|בְּאַמְתְּחֹ֣תֵיכֶ֔ם\rb*. \rb I received|בָּ֣א\rb*\rb |אֵלָ֑י\rb* \rb your silver|כַּסְפְּכֶ֖ם\rb*.” \rb Then he brought Simeon|שִׁמְעֽוֹן׃\rb* \rb out|וַיּוֹצֵ֥א\rb* \rb to them|אֲלֵהֶ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*. \v 24 \rb And the steward|הָאִ֛ישׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb took|וַיָּבֵ֥א\rb* \rb the men|הָאֲנָשִׁ֖ים\rb* \rb into Joseph’s|יוֹסֵ֑ף\rb* \rb house|בֵּ֣יתָה\rb*, \rb gave them|וַיִּתֶּן־\rb* \rb water|מַ֙יִם֙\rb* \rb to wash|וַיִּרְחֲצ֣וּ\rb* \rb their feet|רַגְלֵיהֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb and provided|וַיִּתֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb food|מִסְפּ֖וֹא\rb* \rb for their donkeys|לַחֲמֹֽרֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 25 \rb Since|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb the brothers had been told|שָֽׁמְע֔וּ\rb* \rb that|כִּי־\rb* \rb they were going to eat|יֹ֥אכְלוּ\rb* \rb a meal|לָֽחֶם׃\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֖ם\rb*, \rb they prepared|וַיָּכִ֙ינוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their gift|הַמִּנְחָ֔ה\rb* \rb for|עַד־\rb* \rb Joseph’s|יוֹסֵ֖ף\rb* \rb arrival|בּ֥וֹא\rb* \rb at noon|בַּֽצָּהֳרָ֑יִם\rb*. \v 26 \rb When Joseph|יוֹסֵף֙\rb* \rb came|וַיָּבֹ֤א\rb* \rb home|הַבַּ֔יְתָה\rb*, \rb they presented|וַיָּבִ֥יאּוּ\rb*\rb |ל֛וֹ\rb* \rb him|אֶת־\rb* \rb with the gifts|הַמִּנְחָ֥ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb they had brought|בְּיָדָ֖ם\rb*\rb |הַבָּ֑יְתָה\rb*, \rb and they bowed|וַיִּשְׁתַּחֲווּ־\rb*\rb |ל֖וֹ\rb* \rb to the ground before him|אָֽרְצָה׃\rb*.
\p \v 27 \rb He asked|וַיִּשְׁאַ֤ל\rb*\rb |לָהֶם֙\rb* \rb if they were well|לְשָׁל֔וֹם\rb*, \rb and then he asked|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*, “\rb |הֲשָׁל֛וֹם\rb* \rb How is your elderly|הַזָּקֵ֖ן\rb* \rb father|אֲבִיכֶ֥ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb you told me about|אֲמַרְתֶּ֑ם\rb*? \rb Is he still|הַעוֹדֶ֖נּוּ\rb* \rb alive|חָֽי׃\rb*?”
\p \v 28 “\rb Your servant|לְעַבְדְּךָ֥\rb* \rb our father|לְאָבִ֖ינוּ\rb* \rb is well|שָׁל֛וֹם\rb*,” \rb they answered|וַיֹּאמְר֗וּ\rb*. “\rb He is still|עוֹדֶ֣נּוּ\rb* \rb alive|חָ֑י\rb*.” \rb And they bowed down|וַֽיִּקְּד֖וּ\rb* \rb to honor him|וַיִּשְׁתַּחוּ׃\rb*.
\p \v 29 \rb When Joseph looked up|וַיִּשָּׂ֣א\rb*\rb |עֵינָ֗יו\rb* \rb and saw|וַיַּ֞רְא\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his brother|אָחִיו֮\rb* \rb Benjamin|בִּנְיָמִ֣ין\rb*, \rb his own mother’s|אִמּוֹ֒\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb*, \rb he asked|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Is this|הֲזֶה֙\rb* \rb your youngest|הַקָּטֹ֔ן\rb* \rb brother|אֲחִיכֶ֣ם\rb*, \rb the one|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you told me about|אֲמַרְתֶּ֖ם\rb*?”\rb |אֵלָ֑י\rb* \rb Then he declared|וַיֹּאמַ֕ר\rb*, “\rb May God|אֱלֹהִ֥ים\rb* \rb be gracious to you|יָחְנְךָ֖\rb*, \rb my son|בְּנִֽי׃\rb*.”
\p \v 30 \rb Joseph|יוֹסֵ֗ף\rb* \rb hurried|וַיְמַהֵ֣ר\rb* \rb out because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb he was moved|נִכְמְר֤וּ\rb*\rb |רַחֲמָיו֙\rb* \rb to tears|וַיְבַקֵּ֖שׁ\rb*\rb |לִבְכּ֑וֹת\rb* \rb for|אֶל־\rb* \rb his brother|אָחִ֔יו\rb*, \rb and he went|וַיָּבֹ֥א\rb* \rb to a private room|הַחַ֖דְרָה\rb* \rb to weep|וַיֵּ֥בְךְּ\rb*\rb |שָֽׁמָּה׃\rb*. \v 31 \rb Then he washed|וַיִּרְחַ֥ץ\rb* \rb his face|פָּנָ֖יו\rb* \rb and came back out|וַיֵּצֵ֑א\rb*. \rb Regaining his composure|וַיִּ֨תְאַפַּ֔ק\rb*, \rb he said|וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Serve|שִׂ֥ימוּ\rb* \rb the meal|לָֽחֶם׃\rb*.”
\p \v 32 \rb They separately served|וַיָּשִׂ֥ימוּ\rb* \rb Joseph|לְבַדּ֖וֹ\rb*, \rb his brothers|לְבַדָּ֑ם\rb*, \rb and the Egyptians|וְלַמִּצְרִ֞ים\rb*. \rb They ate|הָאֹכְלִ֤ים\rb*\rb |אִתּוֹ֙\rb* \rb separately|לְבַדָּ֔ם\rb* \rb because|כִּי֩\rb* \rb the Egyptians|הַמִּצְרִ֗ים\rb* \rb would|יוּכְל֜וּן\rb* \rb not|לֹ֨א\rb* \rb eat|לֶאֱכֹ֤ל\rb*\rb |לֶ֔חֶם\rb* \rb with|אֶת־\rb* \rb the Hebrews|הָֽעִבְרִים֙\rb*, \rb since|כִּי־\rb* \rb that|הִ֖וא\rb* \rb was detestable|תוֹעֵבָ֥ה\rb* \rb to them|לְמִצְרָֽיִם׃\rb*. \v 33 \rb They were seated|וַיֵּשְׁב֣וּ\rb* \rb before Joseph|לְפָנָ֔יו\rb* \rb in order by age|כִּבְכֹ֣רָת֔וֹ\rb*,\rb |כִּצְעִרָת֑וֹ\rb* \rb from the firstborn|הַבְּכֹר֙\rb* \rb to the youngest|וְהַצָּעִ֖יר\rb*, \rb and the men|הָאֲנָשִׁ֖ים\rb* \rb looked at|אֶל־\rb* \rb one|אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb another|רֵעֵֽהוּ׃\rb* \rb in astonishment|וַיִּתְמְה֥וּ\rb*. \v 34 \rb When the portions|מַשְׂאֹ֜ת\rb*\rb |מֵאֵ֣ת\rb* \rb were served|וַיִּשָּׂ֨א\rb* \rb to them|אֲלֵהֶם֒\rb* \rb from Joseph’s table|פָּנָיו֮\rb*, \rb Benjamin’s|בִּנְיָמִ֛ן\rb*\rb |מִמַּשְׂאֹ֥ת\rb* \rb portion|מַשְׂאַ֧ת\rb* \rb was five|חָמֵ֣שׁ\rb* \rb times|יָד֑וֹת\rb* \rb larger than|וַתֵּ֜רֶב\rb* \rb any of the others|כֻּלָּ֖ם\rb*. \rb So they feasted|וַיִּשְׁתּ֥וּ\rb* \rb and drank freely|וַֽיִּשְׁכְּר֖וּ\rb* \rb with Joseph|עִמּֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\c 44
\s1 Benjamin and the Silver Cup
\p \v 1 \rb Then Joseph instructed|וַיְצַ֞ו\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his steward|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb*\rb |בֵּיתוֹ֮\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹר֒\rb*: “\rb Fill the men’s|הָֽאֲנָשִׁים֙\rb* \rb sacks|אַמְתְּחֹ֤ת\rb* \rb with|מַלֵּ֞א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb as much food|אֹ֔כֶל\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb they can|יוּכְל֖וּן\rb* \rb carry|שְׂאֵ֑ת\rb*, \rb and put|וְשִׂ֥ים\rb* \rb each one’s|אִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb silver|כֶּֽסֶף־\rb* \rb in the mouth|בְּפִ֥י\rb* \rb of his sack|אַמְתַּחְתּֽוֹ׃\rb*. \v 2 \rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Put|תָּשִׂים֙\rb* \rb my cup|גְּבִיעִ֞י\rb*, \rb the silver|הַכֶּ֗סֶף\rb* \rb one|גְּבִ֣יעַ\rb*, \rb in the mouth|בְּפִי֙\rb* \rb of the youngest one’s|הַקָּטֹ֔ן\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֖ת\rb* \rb sack|אַמְתַּ֣חַת\rb*, \rb along with the silver|כֶּ֣סֶף\rb* \rb for his grain|שִׁבְר֑וֹ\rb*.”
\p \rb So the steward did|וַיַּ֕עַשׂ\rb*\rb |כִּדְבַ֥ר\rb* \rb as Joseph|יוֹסֵ֖ף\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb had instructed|דִּבֵּֽר׃\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb At daybreak|הַבֹּ֖קֶר\rb*\rb |א֑וֹר\rb*, \rb the men|וְהָאֲנָשִׁ֣ים\rb* \rb were sent on their way|שֻׁלְּח֔וּ\rb*\rb |הֵ֖מָּה\rb* \rb with their donkeys|וַחֲמֹרֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 4 \rb They|הֵ֠ם\rb* \rb had not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb gone|יָֽצְא֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb far|הִרְחִיקוּ֒\rb* \rb from the city|הָעִיר֮\rb* \rb when Joseph|וְיוֹסֵ֤ף\rb* \rb told|אָמַר֙\rb* \rb his steward|לַֽאֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb*\rb |בֵּית֔וֹ\rb*, “\rb Pursue|רְדֹ֖ף\rb*\rb |אַחֲרֵ֣י\rb* \rb the men|הָֽאֲנָשִׁ֑ים\rb* \rb at once|ק֥וּם\rb*, \rb and when you overtake them|וְהִשַּׂגְתָּם֙\rb*, \rb ask|וְאָמַרְתָּ֣\rb*\rb |אֲלֵהֶ֔ם\rb*, ‘\rb Why|לָ֛מָּה\rb* \rb have you repaid|שִׁלַּמְתֶּ֥ם\rb*\rb |תַּ֥חַת\rb* \rb good|טוֹבָֽה׃\rb* \rb with evil|רָעָ֖ה\rb*?\f + \fr 44:4 \ft LXX includes \fqa Why have you stolen my silver cup?\f* \v 5 \rb Is this not the cup|הֲל֣וֹא\rb*\rb |זֶ֗ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb*\f + \fr 44:5 \ft Hebrew \fqa Is it not this which\f* \rb my master|אֲדֹנִי֙\rb*\rb |וְה֕וּא\rb* \rb drinks from|יִשְׁתֶּ֤ה\rb* \rb and uses for divination|נַחֵ֥שׁ\rb*\rb |יְנַחֵ֖שׁ\rb*? \rb What|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you have done|עֲשִׂיתֶֽם׃\rb* \rb is wicked|הֲרֵעֹתֶ֖ם\rb*!’”
\p \v 6 \rb When the steward overtook them|וַֽיַּשִּׂגֵ֑ם\rb*, \rb he relayed|וַיְדַבֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb these|הָאֵֽלֶּה׃\rb* \rb words|הַדְּבָרִ֖ים\rb* \rb to them|אֲלֵהֶ֔ם\rb*.\rb |אֶת־\rb*
\p \v 7 “\rb Why|לָ֚מָּה\rb* \rb does my lord|אֲדֹנִ֔י\rb* \rb say|יְדַבֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֑לֶּה\rb* \rb things|כַּדְּבָרִ֖ים\rb*?” \rb they asked|וַיֹּאמְר֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֵלָ֔יו\rb*. “\rb Your servants|לַעֲבָדֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb could not possibly|חָלִ֙ילָה֙\rb* \rb do|מֵעֲשׂ֖וֹת\rb* \rb such|הַזֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb a thing|כַּדָּבָ֥ר\rb*. \v 8 \rb |הֵ֣ן\rb* \rb We even brought back|הֱשִׁיבֹ֥נוּ\rb* \rb to you|אֵלֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb from the land|מֵאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Canaan|כְּנָ֑עַן\rb* \rb the silver|כֶּ֗סֶף\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb we found|מָצָ֙אנוּ֙\rb* \rb in the mouths|בְּפִ֣י\rb* \rb of our sacks|אַמְתְּחֹתֵ֔ינוּ\rb*. \rb Why|וְאֵ֗יךְ\rb* \rb would we steal|נִגְנֹב֙\rb* \rb silver|כֶּ֖סֶף\rb* \rb or|א֥וֹ\rb* \rb gold|זָהָֽב׃\rb* \rb from your master’s|אֲדֹנֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb house|מִבֵּ֣ית\rb*? \v 9 \rb If any|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb of your servants|מֵעֲבָדֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb is found|יִמָּצֵ֥א\rb* \rb to have it|אִתּ֛וֹ\rb*, \rb he must die|וָמֵ֑ת\rb*, \rb and the rest|אֲנַ֕חְנוּ\rb*\rb |וְגַם־\rb* \rb will become|נִֽהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb slaves|לַעֲבָדִֽים׃\rb* \rb of my lord|לַֽאדֹנִ֖י\rb*.”
\p \v 10 “\rb |גַּם־\rb*\rb |עַתָּ֥ה\rb* \rb As you say|כְדִבְרֵיכֶ֖ם\rb*,” \rb replied the steward|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*.\rb |כֶּן־\rb* “\rb But only the one|ה֑וּא\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb is found|יִמָּצֵ֤א\rb* \rb with the cup|אִתּוֹ֙\rb* \rb will be|יִהְיֶה־\rb* \rb my|לִּ֣י\rb* \rb slave|עָ֔בֶד\rb*, \rb and the rest of you|וְאַתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb shall be|תִּהְי֥וּ\rb* \rb free of blame|נְקִיִּֽם׃\rb*.”
\p \v 11 \rb So each|אִ֥ישׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb one quickly|וַֽיְמַהֲר֗וּ\rb* \rb lowered|וַיּוֹרִ֛דוּ\rb* \rb his sack|אַמְתַּחְתּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb to the ground|אָ֑רְצָה\rb* \rb and opened|וַֽיִּפְתְּח֖וּ\rb*\rb |אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb it|אַמְתַּחְתּֽוֹ׃\rb*. \v 12 \rb The steward searched|וַיְחַפֵּ֕שׂ\rb*, \rb beginning|הֵחֵ֔ל\rb* \rb with the oldest|בַּגָּד֣וֹל\rb* \rb and ending|כִּלָּ֑ה\rb* \rb with the youngest|וּבַקָּטֹ֖ן\rb* — \rb and the cup|הַגָּבִ֔יעַ\rb* \rb was found|וַיִּמָּצֵא֙\rb* \rb in Benjamin’s|בִּנְיָמִֽן׃\rb* \rb sack|בְּאַמְתַּ֖חַת\rb*. \v 13 \rb Then they all tore|וַֽיִּקְרְע֖וּ\rb* \rb their clothes|שִׂמְלֹתָ֑ם\rb*,\rb |אִ֣ישׁ\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb loaded|וַֽיַּעֲמֹס֙\rb* \rb their donkeys|חֲמֹר֔וֹ\rb*, \rb and returned|וַיָּשֻׁ֖בוּ\rb* \rb to the city|הָעִֽירָה׃\rb*.
\p \v 14 \rb When Judah|יְהוּדָ֤ה\rb* \rb and his brothers|וְאֶחָיו֙\rb* \rb arrived at|וַיָּבֹ֨א\rb* \rb Joseph’s|יוֹסֵ֔ף\rb* \rb house|בֵּ֣יתָה\rb*, \rb he|וְה֖וּא\rb* \rb was still|עוֹדֶ֣נּוּ\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֑ם\rb*, \rb and they fell|וַיִּפְּל֥וּ\rb* \rb to the ground|אָֽרְצָה׃\rb* \rb before him|לְפָנָ֖יו\rb*.
\p \v 15 “\rb What|מָֽה־\rb* \rb is this|הַזֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb deed|הַמַּעֲשֶׂ֥ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb you have done|עֲשִׂיתֶ֑ם\rb*?” \rb Joseph|יוֹסֵ֔ף\rb* \rb declared|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb*. “\rb Do you not|הֲל֣וֹא\rb* \rb know|יְדַעְתֶּ֔ם\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb a man|אִ֖ישׁ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb like me|כָּמֹֽנִי׃\rb* \rb can surely divine the truth|נַחֵ֧שׁ\rb*\rb |יְנַחֵ֛שׁ\rb*?”
\p \v 16 “\rb What|מַה־\rb* \rb can we say|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to my lord|לַֽאדֹנִ֔י\rb*?” \rb Judah|יְהוּדָ֗ה\rb* \rb replied|נֹּאמַר֙\rb*. “\rb How|מַה־\rb* \rb can we plead|נְּדַבֵּ֖ר\rb*? \rb How|וּמַה־\rb* \rb can we justify ourselves|נִּצְטַדָּ֑ק\rb*? \rb God|הָאֱלֹהִ֗ים\rb* \rb has exposed|מָצָא֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the iniquity|עֲוֺ֣ן\rb* \rb of your servants|עֲבָדֶ֔יךָ\rb*. \rb We are now|הִנֶּנּ֤וּ\rb* \rb my lord’s|לַֽאדֹנִ֔י\rb* \rb slaves|עֲבָדִים֙\rb*— \rb both|גַּם־\rb* \rb we|אֲנַ֕חְנוּ\rb* \rb and|גַּ֛ם\rb* \rb the one|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb who was found|נִמְצָ֥א\rb* \rb with|בְּיָדֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb the cup|הַגָּבִ֖יעַ\rb*.”
\p \v 17 \rb But Joseph replied|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Far be it|חָלִ֣ילָה\rb* \rb from me|לִּ֔י\rb* \rb to do|מֵעֲשׂ֖וֹת\rb* \rb this|זֹ֑את\rb*. \rb The man|הָאִ֡ישׁ\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb was found|נִמְצָ֨א\rb* \rb with|בְּיָד֗וֹ\rb*\rb |ה֚וּא\rb* \rb the cup|הַגָּבִ֜יעַ\rb* \rb will be|יִהְיֶה־\rb* \rb my|לִּ֣י\rb* \rb slave|עָ֔בֶד\rb*. \rb The rest of you|וְאַתֶּ֕ם\rb* \rb may return|עֲל֥וּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb your father|אֲבִיכֶֽם׃פ\rb* \rb in peace|לְשָׁל֖וֹם\rb*.”
\s1 Judah Pleads for Benjamin
\p \v 18 \rb Then Judah|יְהוּדָ֗ה\rb* \rb approached|וַיִּגַּ֨שׁ\rb* \rb Joseph|אֵלָ֜יו\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּאמֶר֮\rb*, “\rb Sir|בִּ֣י\rb*\rb |אֲדֹנִי֒\rb*, \rb please|נָ֨א\rb* \rb let your servant|עַבְדְּךָ֤\rb*\rb |דָבָר֙\rb*\rb |בְּאָזְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb speak|יְדַבֶּר־\rb* \rb personally to my lord|אֲדֹנִ֔י\rb*. \rb Do not|וְאַל־\rb* \rb be angry|יִ֥חַר\rb*\rb |אַפְּךָ֖\rb* \rb with your servant|בְּעַבְדֶּ֑ךָ\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb you are equal to|כָמ֖וֹךָ\rb* \rb Pharaoh himself|כְּפַרְעֹֽה׃\rb*. \v 19 \rb My lord|אֲדֹנִ֣י\rb* \rb asked|שָׁאַ֔ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his servants|עֲבָדָ֖יו\rb*,\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* ‘\rb Do you have|הֲיֵשׁ־\rb*\rb |לָכֶ֥ם\rb* \rb a father|אָ֖ב\rb* \rb or|אוֹ־\rb* \rb a brother|אָֽח׃\rb*?’
\p \v 20 \rb And we answered|וַנֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |אֲדֹנִ֔י\rb*, ‘\rb We have|יֶשׁ־\rb*\rb |לָ֙נוּ֙\rb* \rb an elderly|זָקֵ֔ן\rb* \rb father|אָ֣ב\rb* \rb and a younger brother|קָטָ֑ן\rb*, \rb the child|וְיֶ֥לֶד\rb* \rb of his old age|זְקֻנִ֖ים\rb*. \rb The boy’s brother|וְאָחִ֨יו\rb* \rb is dead|מֵ֜ת\rb*. \rb He|ה֧וּא\rb* \rb is the only|לְבַדּ֛וֹ\rb* \rb one of his mother’s|לְאִמּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb sons left|וַיִּוָּתֵ֨ר\rb*, \rb and his father|וְאָבִ֥יו\rb* \rb loves him|אֲהֵבֽוֹ׃\rb*.’
\p \v 21 \rb Then you told|וַתֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb your servants|עֲבָדֶ֔יךָ\rb*, ‘\rb Bring him down|הוֹרִדֻ֖הוּ\rb* \rb to me|אֵלָ֑י\rb* \rb so that I can see|וְאָשִׂ֥ימָה\rb* \rb him|עָלָֽיו׃\rb* \rb for myself|עֵינִ֖י\rb*.’
\p \v 22 \rb So we said|וַנֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb my lord|אֲדֹנִ֔י\rb*, ‘\rb The boy|הַנַּ֖עַר\rb* \rb cannot|לֹא־\rb*\rb |יוּכַ֥ל\rb* \rb leave|לַעֲזֹ֣ב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his father|אָבִ֑יו\rb*. \rb If he were to leave|וְעָזַ֥ב\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his father|אָבִ֖יו\rb* \rb would die|וָמֵֽת׃\rb*.’
\p \v 23 \rb But you said|וַתֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb your servants|עֲבָדֶ֔יךָ\rb*, ‘\rb |אִם־\rb* \rb Unless|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb your younger|הַקָּטֹ֖ן\rb* \rb brother|אֲחִיכֶ֥ם\rb* \rb comes down|יֵרֵ֛ד\rb* \rb with you|אִתְּכֶ֑ם\rb*, \rb you will not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb see|לִרְא֥וֹת\rb* \rb my face|פָּנָֽי׃\rb* \rb again|תֹסִפ֖וּן\rb*.’
\p \v 24 \rb Now when|וַיְהִי֙\rb*\rb |כִּ֣י\rb* \rb we returned|עָלִ֔ינוּ\rb* \rb to|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb your servant|עַבְדְּךָ֖\rb* \rb my father|אָבִ֑י\rb*, \rb we relayed|וַנַּ֨גֶּד־\rb* \rb your words|דִּבְרֵ֥י\rb*\rb |אֲדֹנִֽי׃\rb* \rb to|ל֔וֹ\rb* \rb him|אֵ֖ת\rb*.
\p \v 25 \rb Then our father|אָבִ֑ינוּ\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb*, ‘\rb Go back|שֻׁ֖בוּ\rb* \rb and buy|שִׁבְרוּ־\rb* \rb us|לָ֥נוּ\rb* \rb some|מְעַט־\rb* \rb food|אֹֽכֶל׃\rb*.’
\p \v 26 \rb But we answered|וַנֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*, ‘\rb We cannot|לֹ֥א\rb*\rb |נוּכַ֖ל\rb* \rb go down there|לָרֶ֑דֶת\rb* \rb unless|אִם־\rb*\rb |יֵשׁ֩\rb* \rb our younger|הַקָּטֹ֤ן\rb* \rb brother|אָחִ֨ינוּ\rb* \rb goes|וְיָרַ֔דְנוּ\rb*\rb |כִּי־\rb* \rb with us|אִתָּ֙נוּ֙\rb*. \rb So if our younger|הַקָּטֹ֖ן\rb* \rb brother|וְאָחִ֥ינוּ\rb* \rb is not|אֵינֶ֥נּוּ\rb* \rb with us|אִתָּֽנוּ׃\rb*, \rb we cannot|לֹ֣א\rb*\rb |נוּכַ֗ל\rb* \rb see|לִרְאוֹת֙\rb*\rb |פְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the man|הָאִ֔ישׁ\rb*.’
\p \v 27 \rb And your servant|עַבְדְּךָ֥\rb* \rb my father|אָבִ֖י\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֛אמֶר\rb* \rb to us|אֵלֵ֑ינוּ\rb*, ‘\rb You|אַתֶּ֣ם\rb* \rb know|יְדַעְתֶּ֔ם\rb* \rb that|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb my wife|אִשְׁתִּֽי׃\rb* \rb bore|יָֽלְדָה־\rb* \rb me|לִּ֥י\rb* \rb two sons|שְׁנַ֖יִם\rb*. \v 28 \rb When one of them|הָֽאֶחָד֙\rb* \rb was gone|וַיֵּצֵ֤א\rb*\rb |מֵֽאִתִּ֔י\rb*, \rb I said|וָאֹמַ֕ר\rb*: “\rb Surely|אַ֖ךְ\rb* \rb he has been torn to pieces|טָרֹ֣ף\rb*\rb |טֹרָ֑ף\rb*.” \rb And I have not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb seen him|רְאִיתִ֖יו\rb*\rb |עַד־\rb* \rb since|הֵֽנָּה׃\rb*. \v 29 \rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Now if you also take|וּלְקַחְתֶּ֧ם\rb*\rb |גַּם־\rb* \rb this one|זֶ֛ה\rb* \rb from|מֵעִ֥ם\rb* \rb me|פָּנַ֖י\rb* \rb and harm|אָס֑וֹן\rb* \rb comes to him|וְקָרָ֣הוּ\rb*, \rb you will bring my gray hair|שֵׂיבָתִ֛י\rb* \rb down|וְהֽוֹרַדְתֶּ֧ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb to Sheol|שְׁאֹֽלָה׃\rb* \rb in sorrow|בְּרָעָ֖ה\rb*.’
\p \v 30 \rb So|וְעַתָּ֗ה\rb* \rb if the boy|וְהַנַּ֖עַר\rb* \rb is not|אֵינֶ֣נּוּ\rb* \rb with us|אִתָּ֑נוּ\rb* \rb when I return|כְּבֹאִי֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb your servant|עַבְדְּךָ֣\rb*, \rb and if my father|אָבִ֔י\rb*, \rb whose life|וְנַפְשׁ֖וֹ\rb* \rb is wrapped up|קְשׁוּרָ֥ה\rb* \rb in the boy’s life|בְנַפְשֽׁוֹ׃\rb*, \v 31 \rb |וְהָיָ֗ה\rb* \rb sees|כִּרְאוֹת֛וֹ\rb* \rb that|כִּי־\rb* \rb the boy|הַנַּ֖עַר\rb* \rb is not with us|אֵ֥ין\rb*, \rb he will die|וָמֵ֑ת\rb*. \rb Then your servants|עֲבָדֶ֜יךָ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb will have brought the gray hair|שֵׂיבַ֨ת\rb* \rb of your servant|עַבְדְּךָ֥\rb* \rb our father|אָבִ֛ינוּ\rb* \rb down|וְהוֹרִ֨ידוּ\rb* \rb to Sheol|שְׁאֹֽלָה׃\rb* \rb in sorrow|בְּיָג֖וֹן\rb*. \v 32 \rb Indeed|כִּ֤י\rb*, \rb your servant|עַבְדְּךָ֙\rb* \rb guaranteed|עָרַ֣ב\rb* \rb the boy’s safety|הַנַּ֔עַר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb to|מֵעִ֥ם\rb* \rb my father|אָבִ֖י\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*, ‘\rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb I do not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb return him|אֲבִיאֶ֙נּוּ֙\rb* \rb to you|אֵלֶ֔יךָ\rb*, \rb I will|כָּל־\rb* \rb bear the guilt|וְחָטָ֥אתִי\rb* \rb before you, my father|לְאָבִ֖י\rb*, \rb all my life|הַיָּמִֽים׃\rb*.’
\p \v 33 \rb Now|וְעַתָּ֗ה\rb* \rb please|נָ֤א\rb* \rb let your servant|עַבְדְּךָ֙\rb* \rb stay here|יֵֽשֶׁב־\rb* \rb as my lord’s|לַֽאדֹנִ֑י\rb*\rb |וְהַנַּ֖עַר\rb* \rb slave|עֶ֖בֶד\rb* \rb in place of|תַּ֣חַת\rb* \rb the boy|הַנַּ֔עַר\rb*. \rb Let him return|יַ֥עַל\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb his brothers|אֶחָֽיו׃\rb*. \v 34 \rb For|כִּי־\rb* \rb how|אֵיךְ֙\rb* \rb can I go back|אֶֽעֱלֶ֣ה\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb my father|אָבִ֔י\rb* \rb without|אֵינֶ֣נּוּ\rb*\rb |אִתִּ֑י\rb* \rb the boy|וְהַנַּ֖עַר\rb*? \rb I could not bear|פֶּ֚ן\rb* \rb to see|אֶרְאֶ֣ה\rb* \rb the misery|בָרָ֔ע\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb would overwhelm|יִמְצָ֖א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb him|אָבִֽי׃\rb*.”
\c 45
\s1 Joseph Reveals His Identity
\p \v 1 \rb Then Joseph|יוֹסֵ֜ף\rb* \rb could|יָכֹ֨ל\rb* \rb no longer|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb control himself|לְהִתְאַפֵּ֗ק\rb* \rb before all|לְכֹ֤ל\rb* \rb his attendants|הַנִּצָּבִים֙\rb*,\rb |עָלָ֔יו\rb* \rb and he cried out|וַיִּקְרָ֕א\rb*, “\rb Send everyone|כָל־\rb*\rb |אִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb away|הוֹצִ֥יאוּ\rb* \rb from me|מֵעָלָ֑י\rb*!”
\p \rb So none|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb of them were with|עָ֤מַד\rb*\rb |אִישׁ֙\rb* \rb Joseph|אִתּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb when he|יוֹסֵ֖ף\rb* \rb made himself known|בְּהִתְוַדַּ֥ע\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his brothers|אֶחָֽיו׃\rb*. \v 2 \rb But he wept|בִּבְכִ֑י\rb* \rb so loudly|וַיִּתֵּ֥ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |קֹל֖וֹ\rb* \rb that the Egyptians|מִצְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb heard him|וַיִּשְׁמְע֣וּ\rb*, \rb and Pharaoh’s|פַּרְעֹֽה׃\rb* \rb household|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb soon heard of it|וַיִּשְׁמַ֖ע\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb Joseph|יוֹסֵ֤ף\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his brothers|אֶחָיו֙\rb*, “\rb I|אֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb am Joseph|יוֹסֵ֔ף\rb*! \rb Is my father|אָבִ֖י\rb* \rb still|הַע֥וֹד\rb* \rb alive|חָ֑י\rb*?”
\p \rb But they|אֶחָיו֙\rb* \rb were unable|וְלֹֽא־\rb*\rb |יָכְל֤וּ\rb* \rb to answer|לַעֲנ֣וֹת\rb* \rb him|אֹת֔וֹ\rb*, \rb because|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb they were terrified|נִבְהֲל֖וּ\rb* \rb in his presence|מִפָּנָֽיו׃\rb*.
\p \v 4 \rb Then Joseph|יוֹסֵ֧ף\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his brothers|אֶחָ֛יו\rb*, “\rb Please|נָ֥א\rb*\rb |אֵלַ֖י\rb* \rb come near me|גְּשׁוּ־\rb*.” \rb And they did so|וַיִּגָּ֑שׁוּ\rb*.
\p “\rb I|אֲנִי֙\rb* \rb am Joseph|יוֹסֵ֣ף\rb*, \rb your brother|אֲחִיכֶ֔ם\rb*,” \rb he said|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*, “\rb the one|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb you sold|מְכַרְתֶּ֥ם\rb*\rb |אֹתִ֖י\rb* \rb into Egypt|מִצְרָֽיְמָה׃\rb*! \v 5 \rb And now|וְעַתָּ֣ה׀\rb*, \rb do not|אַל־\rb* \rb be distressed|תֵּעָ֣צְב֗וּ\rb*\rb |וְאַל־\rb* \rb or angry|יִ֙חַר֙\rb* \rb with yourselves|בְּעֵ֣ינֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb you sold|מְכַרְתֶּ֥ם\rb* \rb me|אֹתִ֖י\rb* \rb into this place|הֵ֑נָּה\rb*, \rb because|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb it was to save lives|לְמִֽחְיָ֔ה\rb* \rb that God|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb sent me|שְׁלָחַ֥נִי\rb* \rb before you|לִפְנֵיכֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 6 \rb For|כִּי־\rb* \rb the famine|הָרָעָ֖ב\rb* \rb has covered|בְּקֶ֣רֶב\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb* \rb these|זֶ֛ה\rb* \rb two years|שְׁנָתַ֥יִם\rb*, \rb and there will be five|חָמֵ֣שׁ\rb* \rb more|וְעוֹד֙\rb* \rb years|שָׁנִ֔ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb without|אֵין־\rb* \rb plowing|חָרִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb or harvesting|וְקָצִּֽיר׃\rb*. \v 7 \rb God|אֱלֹהִים֙\rb* \rb sent me|וַיִּשְׁלָחֵ֤נִי\rb* \rb before you|לִפְנֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb to preserve|לָשׂ֥וּם\rb* \rb you|לָכֶ֛ם\rb* \rb as a remnant|שְׁאֵרִ֖ית\rb* \rb on the earth|בָּאָ֑רֶץ\rb* \rb and to save your lives|וּלְהַחֲי֣וֹת\rb*\rb |לָכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb by a great|גְּדֹלָֽה׃\rb* \rb deliverance|לִפְלֵיטָ֖ה\rb*.\f + \fr 45:7 \ft Or \fqa and to keep you alive as a great band of survivors\f* \v 8 \rb Therefore|וְעַתָּ֗ה\rb* \rb it was not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb you|אַתֶּ֞ם\rb* \rb who sent|שְׁלַחְתֶּ֤ם\rb* \rb me|אֹתִי֙\rb* \rb here|הֵ֔נָּה\rb*, \rb but|כִּ֖י\rb* \rb God|הָאֱלֹהִ֑ים\rb*, \rb who has made me|וַיְשִׂימֵ֨נִֽי\rb* \rb a father|לְאָ֜ב\rb* \rb to Pharaoh|לְפַרְעֹ֗ה\rb* — \rb lord|וּלְאָדוֹן֙\rb* \rb of all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb his household|בֵּית֔וֹ\rb* \rb and ruler|וּמֹשֵׁ֖ל\rb* \rb over all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרָֽיִם׃\rb*.
\s1 Joseph Sends for His Father
\p \v 9 \rb Now return|וַעֲל֣וּ\rb* \rb quickly|מַהֲרוּ֮\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb my father|אָבִי֒\rb* \rb and tell|וַאֲמַרְתֶּ֣ם\rb* \rb him|אֵלָ֗יו\rb*, ‘\rb This is what|כֹּ֤ה\rb* \rb your son|בִּנְךָ֣\rb* \rb Joseph|יוֹסֵ֔ף\rb* \rb says|אָמַר֙\rb*: \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֛ים\rb* \rb has made me|שָׂמַ֧נִי\rb* \rb lord|לְאָד֖וֹן\rb* \rb of all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb Egypt|מִצְרָ֑יִם\rb*. \rb Come down|רְדָ֥ה\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֖י\rb* \rb without|אַֽל־\rb* \rb delay|תַּעֲמֹֽד׃\rb*. \v 10 \rb You shall settle|וְיָשַׁבְתָּ֣\rb* \rb in the land|בְאֶֽרֶץ־\rb* \rb of Goshen|גֹּ֗שֶׁן\rb* \rb and be|וְהָיִ֤יתָ\rb* \rb near me|קָרוֹב֙\rb*—\rb |אֵלַ֔י\rb* \rb you|אַתָּ֕ה\rb* \rb and your children|וּבָנֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb and grandchildren|וּבְנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |בָנֶ֑יךָ\rb*, \rb your flocks|וְצֹאנְךָ֥\rb* \rb and herds|וּבְקָרְךָ֖\rb*, \rb and everything you own|וְכָל־\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb*. \v 11 \rb And there|שָׁ֔ם\rb* \rb I will provide|וְכִלְכַּלְתִּ֤י\rb* \rb for you|אֹֽתְךָ֙\rb*, \rb because|כִּי־\rb* \rb there will be five|חָמֵ֥שׁ\rb* \rb more|ע֛וֹד\rb* \rb years|שָׁנִ֖ים\rb* \rb of famine|רָעָ֑ב\rb*. \rb Otherwise|פֶּן־\rb*, \rb you|אַתָּ֥ה\rb* \rb and your household|וּבֵֽיתְךָ֖\rb* \rb and everything|וְכָל־\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb you own|לָֽךְ׃\rb* \rb will come to destitution|תִּוָּרֵ֛שׁ\rb*.’
\p \v 12 \rb Behold|וְהִנֵּ֤ה\rb*! \rb You|עֵֽינֵיכֶם֙\rb* \rb and my brother|אָחִ֣י\rb* \rb Benjamin|בִנְיָמִ֑ין\rb*\rb |וְעֵינֵ֖י\rb* \rb can see|רֹא֔וֹת\rb* \rb that|כִּי־\rb* \rb I, Joseph,|פִ֖י\rb* \rb am the one speaking|הַֽמְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb with you|אֲלֵיכֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 13 \rb Tell|וְהִגַּדְתֶּ֣ם\rb* \rb my father|לְאָבִ֗י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb about all|כָּל־\rb* \rb my splendor|כְּבוֹדִי֙\rb* \rb in Egypt|בְּמִצְרַ֔יִם\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֖ת\rb* \rb and everything|כָּל־\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb you have seen|רְאִיתֶ֑ם\rb*. \rb And bring|וְהוֹרַדְתֶּ֥ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb my father|אָבִ֖י\rb* \rb down here|הֵֽנָּה׃\rb* \rb quickly|וּמִֽהַרְתֶּ֛ם\rb*.”
\p \v 14 \rb Then Joseph threw his arms around|וַיִּפֹּ֛ל\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb*\rb |צַוְּארֵ֥י\rb* \rb his brother|אָחִ֖יו\rb* \rb Benjamin|בִנְיָמִֽן־\rb* \rb and wept|וַיֵּ֑בְךְּ\rb*, \rb and Benjamin|וּבִנְיָמִ֔ן\rb* \rb wept|בָּכָ֖ה\rb* \rb as|עַל־\rb* \rb they embraced|צַוָּארָֽיו׃\rb*. \v 15 \rb Joseph kissed|וַיְנַשֵּׁ֥ק\rb* \rb each|לְכָל־\rb* \rb of his brothers|אֶחָ֖יו\rb* \rb as he wept|וַיֵּ֣בְךְּ\rb* \rb over them|עֲלֵיהֶ֑ם\rb*. \rb And afterward|וְאַ֣חֲרֵי\rb*\rb |כֵ֔ן\rb* \rb his brothers|אֶחָ֖יו\rb* \rb talked|דִּבְּר֥וּ\rb* \rb with him|אִתּֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\s1 Pharaoh Invites Jacob to Egypt
\p \v 16 \rb When the news|וְהַקֹּ֣ל\rb* \rb reached|נִשְׁמַ֗ע\rb* \rb Pharaoh’s|פַּרְעֹה֙\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb house|בֵּ֤ית\rb* \rb that Joseph’s|יוֹסֵ֑ף\rb* \rb brothers|אֲחֵ֣י\rb* \rb had come|בָּ֖אוּ\rb*, \rb Pharaoh|פַרְעֹ֔ה\rb*\rb |וּבְעֵינֵ֖י\rb* \rb and his servants|עֲבָדָֽיו׃\rb* \rb were pleased|וַיִּיטַב֙\rb*\rb |בְּעֵינֵ֣י\rb*.
\p \v 17 \rb Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹה֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Joseph|יוֹסֵ֔ף\rb*, “\rb Tell|אֱמֹ֥ר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb your brothers|אַחֶ֖יךָ\rb*, ‘\rb Do|עֲשׂ֑וּ\rb* \rb as follows|זֹ֣את\rb*: \rb Load|טַֽעֲנוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your animals|בְּעִ֣ירְכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb and return|וּלְכוּ־\rb*\rb |בֹ֖אוּ\rb* \rb to the land|אַ֥רְצָה\rb* \rb of Canaan|כְּנָֽעַן׃\rb*. \v 18 \rb Then bring|וּקְח֧וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your father|אֲבִיכֶ֛ם\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and your families|בָּתֵּיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb and return|וּבֹ֣אוּ\rb* \rb to me|אֵלָ֑י\rb*. \rb I will give|וְאֶתְּנָ֣ה\rb*\rb |לָכֶ֗ם\rb* \rb you|אֶת־\rb* \rb the best|טוּב֙\rb* \rb of the land|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֔יִם\rb*, \rb and you shall eat|וְאִכְל֖וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb from the fat|חֵ֥לֶב\rb* \rb of the land|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb*.’ \v 19 \rb You|וְאַתָּ֥ה\rb* \rb are also directed to tell them|צֻוֵּ֖יתָה\rb*\rb |עֲשׂ֑וּ\rb*\rb |זֹ֣את\rb*: ‘\rb Take|קְחוּ־\rb*\rb |לָכֶם֩\rb* \rb wagons|עֲגָל֗וֹת\rb* \rb from the land|מֵאֶ֨רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֜יִם\rb* \rb for your young children|לְטַפְּכֶם֙\rb* \rb and your wives|וְלִנְשֵׁיכֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb and bring|וּנְשָׂאתֶ֥ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your father|אֲבִיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb and come back|וּבָאתֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 20 \rb |אַל־\rb* \rb But pay no regard|וְעֵ֣ינְכֶ֔ם\rb*\rb |תָּחֹ֖ס\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb your belongings|כְּלֵיכֶ֑ם\rb*, \rb for|כִּי־\rb* \rb the best|ט֛וּב\rb* \rb of all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֖יִם\rb* \rb is|הֽוּא׃\rb* \rb yours|לָכֶ֥ם\rb*.’”
\p \v 21 \rb So the sons|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb did|וַיַּֽעֲשׂוּ־\rb* \rb as they were told|כֵן֙\rb*. \rb Joseph|יוֹסֵ֛ף\rb* \rb gave|וַיִּתֵּ֨ן\rb* \rb them|לָהֶ֥ם\rb* \rb wagons|עֲגָל֖וֹת\rb* \rb as|עַל־\rb* \rb Pharaoh|פַרְעֹ֑ה\rb* \rb had instructed|פִּ֣י\rb*, \rb and he also gave|וַיִּתֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb them|לָהֶ֛ם\rb* \rb provisions|צֵדָ֖ה\rb* \rb for their journey|לַדָּֽרֶךְ׃\rb*. \v 22 \rb |לְכֻלָּ֥ם\rb* \rb He gave|נָתַ֛ן\rb* \rb new|חֲלִפ֣וֹת\rb* \rb garments|שְׂמָלֹ֑ת\rb* \rb to each of them|לָאִ֖ישׁ\rb*, \rb but to Benjamin|וּלְבִנְיָמִ֤ן\rb* \rb he gave|נָתַן֙\rb* \rb three|שְׁלֹ֣שׁ\rb* \rb hundred shekels|מֵא֣וֹת\rb* \rb of silver|כֶּ֔סֶף\rb*\f + \fr 45:22 \fqa 300 shekels \ft is approximately 7.5 pounds or 3.4 kilograms of silver.\f* \rb and five|וְחָמֵ֖שׁ\rb* \rb sets|חֲלִפֹ֥ת\rb* \rb of clothes|שְׂמָלֹֽת׃\rb*. \v 23 \rb And he sent|שָׁלַ֤ח\rb* \rb to his father|וּלְאָבִ֞יו\rb* \rb the following|כְּזֹאת֙\rb*: \rb ten|עֲשָׂרָ֣ה\rb* \rb donkeys|חֲמֹרִ֔ים\rb* \rb loaded|נֹשְׂאִ֖ים\rb* \rb with the best|מִטּ֣וּב\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרָ֑יִם\rb*, \rb and ten|וְעֶ֣שֶׂר\rb* \rb female donkeys|אֲתֹנֹ֡ת\rb* \rb loaded|נֹֽ֠שְׂאֹת\rb* \rb with grain|בָּ֣ר\rb* \rb and bread|וָלֶ֧חֶם\rb* \rb and provisions|וּמָז֛וֹן\rb* \rb for his father’s|לְאָבִ֖יו\rb* \rb journey|לַדָּֽרֶךְ׃\rb*.
\p \v 24 \rb Then Joseph sent his brothers|אֶחָ֖יו\rb* \rb on their way|וַיְשַׁלַּ֥ח\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb and as they were leaving|וַיֵּלֵ֑כוּ\rb*, \rb he said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to them|אֲלֵהֶ֔ם\rb*, “\rb Do not|אַֽל־\rb* \rb quarrel|תִּרְגְּז֖וּ\rb* \rb on the way|בַּדָּֽרֶךְ׃\rb*!”
\s1 The Revival of Jacob
\p \v 25 \rb So the brothers went up|וַֽיַּעֲל֖וּ\rb* \rb out of Egypt|מִמִּצְרָ֑יִם\rb* \rb and came|וַיָּבֹ֙אוּ֙\rb* \rb to|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb their father|אֲבִיהֶֽם׃\rb* \rb Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֖ב\rb* \rb in the land|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Canaan|כְּנַ֔עַן\rb*. \v 26 “\rb Joseph|יוֹסֵ֣ף\rb* \rb is still|ע֚וֹד\rb* \rb alive|חַ֔י\rb*,” \rb they said|וַיַּגִּ֨דוּ\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֗ר\rb*, “\rb and|וְכִֽי־\rb* \rb he|ה֥וּא\rb* \rb is ruler|מֹשֵׁ֖ל\rb* \rb over all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרָ֑יִם\rb*!”
\p \rb But Jacob was stunned|וַיָּ֣פָג\rb*\rb |לִבּ֔וֹ\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb he did not|לֹא־\rb* \rb believe|הֶאֱמִ֖ין\rb* \rb them|לָהֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 27 \rb However, when they relayed|וַיְדַבְּר֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֵ֣ת\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb*\rb |דִּבְרֵ֤י\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb Joseph|יוֹסֵף֙\rb* \rb had told|דִּבֶּ֣ר\rb* \rb them|אֲלֵהֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb and when he saw|וַיַּרְא֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the wagons|הָ֣עֲגָל֔וֹת\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb Joseph|יוֹסֵ֖ף\rb* \rb had sent|שָׁלַ֥ח\rb* \rb to carry him|לָשֵׂ֣את\rb* \rb back|אֹת֑וֹ\rb*, \rb the spirit|ר֖וּחַ\rb* \rb of their father|אֲבִיהֶֽם׃\rb* \rb Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֥ב\rb* \rb was revived|וַתְּחִ֕י\rb*.
\p \v 28 “\rb Enough|רַ֛ב\rb*!” \rb declared|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*. “\rb My son|בְּנִ֖י\rb* \rb Joseph|יוֹסֵ֥ף\rb* \rb is still|עוֹד־\rb* \rb alive|חָ֑י\rb*! \rb I will go|אֵֽלְכָ֥ה\rb* \rb to see him|וְאֶרְאֶ֖נּוּ\rb* \rb before|בְּטֶ֥רֶם\rb* \rb I die|אָמֽוּת׃\rb*.”
\c 46
\s1 Jacob’s Journey to Egypt
\p \v 1 \rb So Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb set out|וַיִּסַּ֤ע\rb* \rb with all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb he had|ל֔וֹ\rb*, \rb and when he came|וַיָּבֹ֖א\rb* \rb to|בְּאֵ֣רָה\rb* \rb Beersheba|שָּׁ֑בַע\rb*, \rb he offered|וַיִּזְבַּ֣ח\rb* \rb sacrifices|זְבָחִ֔ים\rb* \rb to the God|לֵאלֹהֵ֖י\rb* \rb of his father|אָבִ֥יו\rb* \rb Isaac|יִצְחָֽק׃\rb*. \v 2 \rb And that night|הַלַּ֔יְלָה\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֤ים׀\rb* \rb spoke|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to Israel|לְיִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb in a vision|בְּמַרְאֹ֣ת\rb*: “\rb Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֣ב׀\rb*, \rb Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֑ב\rb*!” \rb He said|וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb*.
\p “\rb Here I am|הִנֵּֽנִי׃\rb*,” \rb replied Jacob|וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb*.
\p \v 3 “\rb I|אָנֹכִ֥י\rb* \rb am God|הָאֵ֖ל\rb*,” \rb He said|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*, “\rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of your father|אָבִ֑יךָ\rb*. \rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb be afraid|תִּירָא֙\rb* \rb to go down|מֵרְדָ֣ה\rb* \rb to Egypt|מִצְרַ֔יְמָה\rb*, \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I will make|אֲשִֽׂימְךָ֥\rb* \rb you into a great|גָּד֖וֹל\rb* \rb nation|לְג֥וֹי\rb* \rb there|שָֽׁם׃\rb*. \v 4 \rb I|אָנֹכִ֗י\rb* \rb will go down|אֵרֵ֤ד\rb* \rb with|עִמְּךָ֙\rb* \rb you to Egypt|מִצְרַ֔יְמָה\rb*, \rb and I|וְאָנֹכִ֖י\rb* \rb will surely|גַם־\rb*\rb |עָלֹ֑ה\rb* \rb bring you back|אַֽעַלְךָ֣\rb*. \rb And Joseph’s|וְיוֹסֵ֕ף\rb* \rb own hands|יָד֖וֹ\rb* \rb will close|יָשִׁ֥ית\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb your eyes|עֵינֶֽיךָ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 5 \rb Then Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֖ב\rb* \rb departed|וַיָּ֥קָם\rb* \rb from|מִבְּאֵ֣ר\rb* \rb Beersheba|שָׁ֑בַע\rb*, \rb and the sons|בְנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֜ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb took|וַיִּשְׂא֨וּ\rb* \rb their father|אֲבִיהֶ֗ם\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֣ב\rb* \rb in the wagons|בָּעֲגָל֕וֹת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹ֖ה\rb* \rb had sent|שָׁלַ֥ח\rb* \rb to carry him|לָשֵׂ֥את\rb*,\rb |אֹתֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb along with their children|טַפָּם֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and wives|נְשֵׁיהֶ֔ם\rb*. \v 6 \rb They also took|וַיִּקְח֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the livestock|מִקְנֵיהֶ֗ם\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and possessions|רְכוּשָׁם֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb they had acquired|רָֽכְשׁוּ֙\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Canaan|כְּנַ֔עַן\rb*, \rb and Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֖ב\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb his offspring|זַרְע֥וֹ\rb* \rb went|וַיָּבֹ֖אוּ\rb*\rb |אִתּֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb to Egypt|מִצְרָ֑יְמָה\rb*.
\s1 Those Who Went to Egypt
\p \v 7 \rb Jacob took|הֵבִ֥יא\rb* \rb with him|אִתּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb to Egypt|מִצְרָֽיְמָה׃ס\rb* \rb his sons|בָּנָ֞יו\rb* \rb and grandsons|וּבְנֵ֤י\rb*\rb |בָנָיו֙\rb*,\rb |אִתּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb and his daughters|בְּנֹתָ֛יו\rb* \rb and granddaughters|וּבְנ֥וֹת\rb*\rb |בָּנָ֖יו\rb* — \rb all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb his offspring|זַרְע֑וֹ\rb*.
\s2 The Children of Leah
\li1 \v 8 \rb Now these|וְאֵ֨לֶּה\rb* \rb are the names|שְׁמ֧וֹת\rb* \rb of the sons|בְּנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֛ל\rb* (\rb Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֣ב\rb* \rb and his descendants|וּבָנָ֑יו\rb*) \rb who went|הַבָּאִ֥ים\rb* \rb to Egypt|מִצְרַ֖יְמָה\rb*: \rb Reuben|רְאוּבֵֽן׃\rb*, \rb Jacob’s|יַעֲקֹ֖ב\rb* \rb firstborn|בְּכֹ֥ר\rb*.
\li1 \v 9 \rb The sons|וּבְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb of Reuben|רְאוּבֵ֑ן\rb*: \rb Hanoch|חֲנ֥וֹךְ\rb*, \rb Pallu|וּפַלּ֖וּא\rb*, \rb Hezron|וְחֶצְר֥וֹן\rb*, \rb and Carmi|וְכַרְמִֽי׃\rb*.
\li1 \v 10 \rb The sons|וּבְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Simeon|שִׁמְע֗וֹן\rb*: \rb Jemuel|יְמוּאֵ֧ל\rb*,\f + \fr 46:10 \fqa Jemuel \ft is another name for \fqa Nemuel\ft ; see Numbers 26:12.\f* \rb Jamin|וְיָמִ֛ין\rb*, \rb Ohad|וְאֹ֖הַד\rb*, \rb Jachin|וְיָכִ֣ין\rb*, \rb Zohar|וְצֹ֑חַר\rb*,\f + \fr 46:10 \fqa Zohar \ft is a variant of \fqa Zerah\ft ; see Numbers 26:13 and 1 Chronicles 4:24.\f* \rb and Shaul|וְשָׁא֖וּל\rb* \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of a Canaanite woman|הַֽכְּנַעֲנִֽית׃\rb*.
\li1 \v 11 \rb The sons|וּבְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb of Levi|לֵוִ֑י\rb*: \rb Gershon|גֵּרְשׁ֕וֹן\rb*, \rb Kohath|קְהָ֖ת\rb*, \rb and Merari|וּמְרָרִֽי׃\rb*.
\li1 \v 12 \rb The sons|וּבְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֗ה\rb*: \rb Er|עֵ֧ר\rb*, \rb Onan|וְאוֹנָ֛ן\rb*, \rb Shelah|וְשֵׁלָ֖ה\rb*, \rb Perez|וָפֶ֣רֶץ\rb*, \rb and Zerah|וָזָ֑רַח\rb*; \rb but Er|עֵ֤ר\rb* \rb and Onan|וְאוֹנָן֙\rb* \rb died|וַיָּ֨מָת\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Canaan|כְּנַ֔עַן\rb*.
\li1 \rb The sons|בְנֵי־\rb*\rb |וַיִּהְי֥וּ\rb* \rb of Perez|פֶ֖רֶץ\rb*: \rb Hezron|חֶצְר֥וֹן\rb* \rb and Hamul|וְחָמֽוּל׃\rb*.
\li1 \v 13 \rb The sons|וּבְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb of Issachar|יִשָׂשכָ֑ר\rb*: \rb Tola|תּוֹלָ֥ע\rb*, \rb Puvah|וּפֻוָּ֖ה\rb*,\f + \fr 46:13 \ft Hebrew; SP and Syriac \fqa Puah\ft ; see 1 Chronicles 7:1.\f* \rb Job|וְי֥וֹב\rb*,\f + \fr 46:13 \ft Hebrew; SP and some LXX manuscripts \fqa Jashub\ft ; see Numbers 26:24 and 1 Chronicles 7:1.\f* \rb and Shimron|וְשִׁמְרֽוֹן׃\rb*.
\li1 \v 14 \rb The sons|וּבְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb of Zebulun|זְבוּלֻ֑ן\rb*: \rb Sered|סֶ֥רֶד\rb*, \rb Elon|וְאֵל֖וֹן\rb*, \rb and Jahleel|וְיַחְלְאֵֽל׃\rb*.
\li1 \v 15 \rb These|אֵ֣לֶּה׀\rb* \rb are the sons|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Leah|לֵאָ֗ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb born|יָֽלְדָ֤ה\rb* \rb to Jacob|לְיַעֲקֹב֙\rb* \rb in|בְּפַדַּ֣ן\rb* \rb Paddan-aram|אֲרָ֔ם\rb*,\f + \fr 46:15 \ft That is, northwest Mesopotamia\f*\rb |וְאֵ֖ת\rb* \rb in addition to his daughter|בִתּ֑וֹ\rb* \rb Dinah|דִּינָ֣ה\rb*. \rb The total|כָּל־\rb* \rb number|נֶ֧פֶשׁ\rb* \rb of sons|בָּנָ֛יו\rb* \rb and daughters|וּבְנוֹתָ֖יו\rb* \rb was thirty-three|שְׁלֹשִׁ֥ים\rb*\rb |וְשָׁלֹֽשׁ׃\rb*.
\s2 The Children of Zilpah
\li1 \v 16 \rb The sons|וּבְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Gad|גָ֔ד\rb*: \rb Ziphion|צִפְי֥וֹן\rb*,\f + \fr 46:16 \ft SP and LXX \fqa Zephon\ft ; see also Numbers 26:15.\f* \rb Haggi|וְחַגִּ֖י\rb*, \rb Shuni|שׁוּנִ֣י\rb*, \rb Ezbon|וְאֶצְבֹּ֑ן\rb*, \rb Eri|עֵרִ֥י\rb*, \rb Arodi|וַֽאֲרוֹדִ֖י\rb*,\f + \fr 46:16 \fqa Arodi \ft is a variant of \fqa Arod\ft ; see Numbers 26:17.\f* \rb and Areli|וְאַרְאֵלִֽי׃\rb*.
\li1 \v 17 \rb The children|וּבְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Asher|אָשֵׁ֗ר\rb*: \rb Imnah|יִמְנָ֧ה\rb*, \rb Ishvah|וְיִשְׁוָ֛ה\rb*, \rb Ishvi|וְיִשְׁוִ֥י\rb*, \rb Beriah|וּבְרִיעָ֖ה\rb*, \rb and their sister|אֲחֹתָ֑ם\rb* \rb Serah|וְשֶׂ֣רַח\rb*.
\li1 \rb The sons|וּבְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Beriah|בְרִיעָ֔ה\rb*: \rb Heber|חֶ֖בֶר\rb* \rb and Malchiel|וּמַלְכִּיאֵֽל׃\rb*.
\li1 \v 18 \rb These|אֵ֚לֶּה\rb* \rb are the sons|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |אֵ֙לֶּה֙\rb* \rb of Jacob|לְיַעֲקֹ֔ב\rb* \rb born|וַתֵּ֤לֶד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb to Zilpah|זִלְפָּ֔ה\rb* — \rb whom|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb Laban|לָבָ֖ן\rb* \rb gave|נָתַ֥ן\rb* \rb to his daughter|בִתּ֑וֹ\rb* \rb Leah|לְלֵאָ֣ה\rb* — \rb sixteen|שֵׁ֥שׁ\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵ֖ה\rb* \rb in all|נָֽפֶשׁ׃\rb*.
\s2 The Children of Rachel
\li1 \v 19 \rb The sons|בְּנֵ֤י\rb* \rb of Jacob’s|יַֽעֲקֹ֔ב\rb* \rb wife|אֵ֣שֶׁת\rb* \rb Rachel|רָחֵל֙\rb*: \rb Joseph|יוֹסֵ֖ף\rb* \rb and Benjamin|וּבִנְיָמִֽן׃\rb*.
\li1 \v 20 \rb Manasseh|מְנַשֶּׁ֖ה\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and Ephraim|אֶפְרָֽיִם׃\rb* \rb were born|וַיִּוָּלֵ֣ד\rb* \rb to Joseph|לְיוֹסֵף֮\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַיִם֒\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb*\rb |יָֽלְדָה־\rb*\rb |לּוֹ֙\rb* \rb by Asenath|אָֽסְנַ֔ת\rb* \rb daughter|בַּת־\rb*\rb |פּ֥וֹטִי\rb* \rb of Potiphera|פֶ֖רַע\rb*, \rb priest|כֹּהֵ֣ן\rb* \rb of On|אֹ֑ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*.\f + \fr 46:20 \ft That is, Heliopolis, as in LXX\f*
\li1 \v 21 \rb The sons|וּבְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Benjamin|בִנְיָמִ֗ן\rb*: \rb Bela|בֶּ֤לַע\rb*, \rb Becher|וָבֶ֙כֶר֙\rb*, \rb Ashbel|וְאַשְׁבֵּ֔ל\rb*, \rb Gera|גֵּרָ֥א\rb*, \rb Naaman|וְנַעֲמָ֖ן\rb*, \rb Ehi|אֵחִ֣י\rb*, \rb Rosh|וָרֹ֑אשׁ\rb*, \rb Muppim|מֻפִּ֥ים\rb*, \rb Huppim|וְחֻפִּ֖ים\rb*, \rb and Ard|וָאָֽרְדְּ׃\rb*.
\li1 \v 22 \rb These|אֵ֚לֶּה\rb* \rb are the sons|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Rachel|רָחֵ֔ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb born|יֻלַּ֖ד\rb* \rb to Jacob|לְיַעֲקֹ֑ב\rb* —\rb |כָּל־\rb* \rb fourteen|אַרְבָּעָ֥ה\rb*\rb |עָשָֽׂר׃\rb* \rb in all|נֶ֖פֶשׁ\rb*.
\s2 The Children of Bilhah
\li1 \v 23 \rb The son|וּבְנֵי־\rb* \rb of Dan|דָ֖ן\rb*: \rb Hushim|חֻשִֽׁים׃\rb*.
\li1 \v 24 \rb The sons|וּבְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb of Naphtali|נַפְתָּלִ֑י\rb*: \rb Jahzeel|יַחְצְאֵ֥ל\rb*, \rb Guni|וְגוּנִ֖י\rb*, \rb Jezer|וְיֵ֥צֶר\rb*, \rb and Shillem|וְשִׁלֵּֽם׃\rb*.
\li1 \v 25 \rb These|אֵ֚לֶּה\rb* \rb are the sons|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Jacob|לְיַעֲקֹ֖ב\rb* \rb born|וַתֵּ֧לֶד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |אֵ֛לֶּה\rb* \rb to Bilhah|בִלְהָ֔ה\rb*, \rb whom|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb Laban|לָבָ֖ן\rb* \rb gave|נָתַ֥ן\rb* \rb to his daughter|בִּתּ֑וֹ\rb* \rb Rachel|לְרָחֵ֣ל\rb* — \rb seven|שִׁבְעָֽה׃\rb* \rb in all|כָּל־\rb*.
\p \v 26 \rb All those|כָּל־\rb* \rb belonging to Jacob|לְיַעֲקֹ֤ב\rb* \rb who came|הַבָּאָ֨ה\rb* \rb to Egypt|מִצְרַ֙יְמָה֙\rb*— \rb his direct descendants|יֹצְאֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יְרֵכ֔וֹ\rb*, \rb besides|מִלְּבַ֖ד\rb* \rb the wives|נְשֵׁ֣י\rb* \rb of Jacob’s|יַעֲקֹ֑ב\rb*\rb |כָּל־\rb*\rb |נֶ֖פֶשׁ\rb* \rb sons|בְנֵי־\rb*— \rb numbered sixty-six|שִׁשִּׁ֥ים\rb*\rb |וָשֵֽׁשׁ׃\rb* \rb persons|הַ֠נֶּפֶשׁ\rb*. \v 27 \rb And with the two|שְׁנָ֑יִם\rb*\rb |נֶ֣פֶשׁ\rb* \rb sons|וּבְנֵ֥י\rb*\f + \fr 46:27 \ft Hebrew; LXX \fqa the nine sons\ft , probably including Joseph’s grandsons through Ephraim and Manasseh; see 1 Chronicles 7:14–29.\f* \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb had been born|יֻלַּד־\rb* \rb to|ל֥וֹ\rb* \rb Joseph|יוֹסֵ֛ף\rb* \rb in Egypt|בְמִצְרַ֖יִם\rb*, \rb the members|הַנֶּ֧פֶשׁ\rb* \rb of Jacob’s|יַעֲקֹ֛ב\rb* \rb family|לְבֵֽית־\rb* \rb who went|הַבָּ֥אָה\rb* \rb to Egypt were|מִצְרַ֖יְמָה\rb* \rb seventy|שִׁבְעִֽים׃פ\rb*\f + \fr 46:27 \ft Hebrew (see also Exodus 1:5); LXX (see also Acts 7:14) \fqa seventy-five\f* \rb in all|כָּל־\rb*.
\s1 Jacob Arrives in Egypt
\p \v 28 \rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Now Jacob had sent|שָׁלַ֤ח\rb* \rb Judah|יְהוּדָ֞ה\rb* \rb ahead of him|לְפָנָיו֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Joseph|יוֹסֵ֔ף\rb* \rb to get directions|לְהוֹרֹ֥ת\rb*\rb |לְפָנָ֖יו\rb* \rb to Goshen|גֹּ֑שְׁנָה\rb*. \rb When Jacob’s family arrived|וַיָּבֹ֖אוּ\rb* \rb in the land|אַ֥רְצָה\rb* \rb of Goshen|גֹּֽשֶׁן׃\rb*, \v 29 \rb Joseph|יוֹסֵף֙\rb* \rb prepared|וַיֶּאְסֹ֤ר\rb* \rb his chariot|מֶרְכַּבְתּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb and went|וַיַּ֛עַל\rb* \rb there|גֹּ֑שְׁנָה\rb* \rb to meet|לִקְרַֽאת־\rb* \rb his father|אָבִ֖יו\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֥ל\rb*. \rb Joseph presented himself|וַיֵּרָ֣א\rb* \rb to him|אֵלָ֗יו\rb*, \rb embraced|וַיִּפֹּל֙\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb him|צַוָּארָ֔יו\rb*, \rb and wept|וַיֵּ֥בְךְּ\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb*\rb |צַוָּארָ֖יו\rb* \rb profusely|עֽוֹד׃\rb*.
\p \v 30 \rb Then Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֛ל\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֧אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Joseph|יוֹסֵ֖ף\rb*, “\rb Finally I can die|אָמ֣וּתָה\rb*, \rb now|הַפָּ֑עַם\rb*\rb |אַחֲרֵי֙\rb* \rb that I have seen|רְאוֹתִ֣י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your face|פָּנֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb and know that|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb you are still|עוֹדְךָ֖\rb* \rb alive|חָֽי׃\rb*!”
\p \v 31 \rb Joseph|יוֹסֵ֤ף\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his brothers|אֶחָיו֙\rb* \rb and to|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb his father’s|אָבִ֔יו\rb* \rb household|בֵּ֣ית\rb*, “\rb I will go up|אֶעֱלֶ֖ה\rb* \rb and inform|וְאַגִּ֣ידָה\rb* \rb Pharaoh|לְפַרְעֹ֑ה\rb*\rb |וְאֹֽמְרָ֣ה\rb*: ‘\rb My brothers|אַחַ֧י\rb* \rb and my father’s|אָבִ֛י\rb* \rb household|וּבֵית־\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb from the land|בְּאֶֽרֶץ־\rb* \rb of Canaan|כְּנַ֖עַן\rb* \rb have come|בָּ֥אוּ\rb* \rb to me|אֵלָֽי׃\rb*. \v 32 \rb The men|וְהָאֲנָשִׁים֙\rb* \rb are shepherds|רֹ֣עֵי\rb*\rb |צֹ֔אן\rb*;\rb |כִּֽי־\rb*\rb |אַנְשֵׁ֥י\rb* \rb they raise livestock|מִקְנֶ֖ה\rb*,\rb |הָי֑וּ\rb* \rb and they have brought|הֵבִֽיאוּ׃\rb* \rb their flocks|וְצֹאנָ֧ם\rb* \rb and herds|וּבְקָרָ֛ם\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb they own|לָהֶ֖ם\rb*.’
\p \v 33 \rb |וְהָיָ֕ה\rb* \rb When|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹ֑ה\rb* \rb summons|יִקְרָ֥א\rb* \rb you|לָכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb and asks|וְאָמַ֖ר\rb*, ‘\rb What|מַה־\rb* \rb is your occupation|מַּעֲשֵׂיכֶֽם׃\rb*?’ \v 34 \rb you are to say|וַאֲמַרְתֶּ֗ם\rb*, ‘\rb Your servants|עֲבָדֶ֙יךָ֙\rb*\rb |אַנְשֵׁ֨י\rb* \rb have raised livestock|מִקְנֶ֜ה\rb*\rb |הָי֤וּ\rb* \rb ever since our youth|מִנְּעוּרֵ֣ינוּ\rb*\rb |וְעַד־\rb*\rb |עַ֔תָּה\rb* — \rb both|גַּם־\rb* \rb we|אֲנַ֖חְנוּ\rb* \rb and|גַּם־\rb* \rb our fathers|אֲבֹתֵ֑ינוּ\rb*.’ \rb Then|בַּעֲב֗וּר\rb* \rb you will be allowed to settle|תֵּשְׁבוּ֙\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Goshen|גֹּ֔שֶׁן\rb*, \rb since|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb shepherds|רֹ֥עֵה\rb*\rb |צֹֽאן׃\rb* \rb are detestable|תוֹעֲבַ֥ת\rb* \rb to the Egyptians|מִצְרַ֖יִם\rb*.”
\c 47
\s1 Jacob Settles in Goshen
\p \v 1 \rb So Joseph|יוֹסֵף֮\rb* \rb went|וַיָּבֹ֣א\rb* \rb and told|וַיַּגֵּ֣ד\rb* \rb Pharaoh|לְפַרְעֹה֒\rb*\rb |וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*: “\rb My father|אָבִ֨י\rb* \rb and my brothers|וְאַחַ֜י\rb*, \rb with their flocks|וְצֹאנָ֤ם\rb* \rb and herds|וּבְקָרָם֙\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb they own|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb*, \rb have come|בָּ֖אוּ\rb* \rb from the land|מֵאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Canaan|כְּנָ֑עַן\rb* \rb and are now|וְהִנָּ֖ם\rb*\rb |בְּאֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb in Goshen|גֹּֽשֶׁן׃\rb*.”
\p \v 2 \rb |וּמִקְצֵ֣ה\rb* \rb And he chose|לָקַ֖ח\rb* \rb five|חֲמִשָּׁ֣ה\rb* \rb of|אֲנָשִׁ֑ים\rb* \rb his brothers|אֶחָ֔יו\rb* \rb and presented them|וַיַּצִּגֵ֖ם\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb Pharaoh|פַרְעֹֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 3 “\rb What|מַה־\rb* \rb is your occupation|מַּעֲשֵׂיכֶ֑ם\rb*?” \rb Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹ֛ה\rb* \rb asked|וַיֹּ֧אמֶר\rb* \rb Joseph’s brothers|אֶחָ֖יו\rb*.
\p “\rb Your servants|עֲבָדֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb are shepherds|רֹעֵ֥ה\rb*\rb |צֹאן֙\rb*,” \rb they replied|וַיֹּאמְר֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |פַּרְעֹ֗ה\rb*, “\rb both|גַּם־\rb* \rb we|אֲנַ֖חְנוּ\rb* \rb and|גַּם־\rb* \rb our fathers|אֲבוֹתֵֽינוּ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 4 \rb Then they said|וַיֹּאמְר֣וּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹ֗ה\rb*, “\rb We have come|בָּאנוּ֒\rb* \rb to live in the land|בָּאָרֶץ֮\rb* \rb for a time|לָג֣וּר\rb*, \rb because|כִּי־\rb* \rb there is no|אֵ֣ין\rb* \rb pasture|מִרְעֶ֗ה\rb* \rb for the flocks|לַצֹּאן֙\rb* \rb of your servants|לַעֲבָדֶ֔יךָ\rb*,\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb since|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the famine|הָרָעָ֖ב\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Canaan|כְּנָ֑עַן\rb* \rb has been severe|כָבֵ֥ד\rb*. \rb So now|וְעַתָּ֛ה\rb*, \rb please|נָ֥א\rb* \rb allow your servants|עֲבָדֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb to settle|יֵֽשְׁבוּ־\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Goshen|גֹּֽשֶׁן׃\rb*.”
\p \v 5 \rb Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹ֔ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Joseph|יוֹסֵ֖ף\rb*,\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* “\rb Now that your father|אָבִ֥יךָ\rb* \rb and brothers|וְאַחֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb have come|בָּ֥אוּ\rb* \rb to you|אֵלֶֽיךָ׃\rb*, \v 6 \rb the land|אֶ֤רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֙יִם֙\rb* \rb is before you|לְפָנֶ֣יךָ\rb*;\rb |הִ֔וא\rb* \rb settle|הוֹשֵׁ֥ב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your father|אָבִ֖יךָ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and brothers|אַחֶ֑יךָ\rb* \rb in the best|בְּמֵיטַ֣ב\rb* \rb part of the land|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb*. \rb They may dwell|יֵשְׁבוּ֙\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Goshen|גֹּ֔שֶׁן\rb*. \rb And if|וְאִם־\rb* \rb you know of|יָדַ֗עְתָּ\rb*\rb |וְיֶשׁ־\rb* \rb any talented|חַ֔יִל\rb* \rb men among them|אַנְשֵׁי־\rb*, \rb put them|וְשַׂמְתָּ֛ם\rb* \rb in charge of|שָׂרֵ֥י\rb* \rb my own livestock|מִקְנֶ֖ה\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb*.”
\p \v 7 \rb Then Joseph|יוֹסֵף֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb brought in|וַיָּבֵ֤א\rb* \rb his father|אָבִ֔יו\rb* \rb Jacob|יַֽעֲקֹ֣ב\rb* \rb and presented him|וַיַּֽעֲמִדֵ֖הוּ\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb Pharaoh|פַרְעֹ֑ה\rb*, \rb and Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֖ב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb blessed|וַיְבָ֥רֶךְ\rb* \rb Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 8 “\rb How many|כַּמָּ֕ה\rb* \rb years|יְמֵ֖י\rb*\rb |שְׁנֵ֥י\rb* \rb have you lived|חַיֶּֽיךָ׃\rb*?” \rb Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹ֖ה\rb* \rb asked|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֶֽל־\rb*\rb |יַעֲקֹ֑ב\rb*.
\p \v 9 “\rb My travels|מְגוּרַ֔י\rb*\f + \fr 47:9 \ft Hebrew \fqa sojourns\ft ; twice in this verse\f* \rb have lasted 130|וּמְאַ֖ת\rb*\rb |שְׁלֹשִׁ֥ים\rb* \rb years|שְׁנֵ֣י\rb*,” \rb Jacob|יַעֲקֹב֙\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |פַּרְעֹ֔ה\rb*. “\rb My years|יְמֵי֙\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֑ה\rb*\rb |חַיַּ֔י\rb* \rb have been|הָיוּ֙\rb* \rb few|מְעַ֣ט\rb* \rb and hard|וְרָעִ֗ים\rb*, \rb and they have not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb matched|הִשִּׂ֗יגוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the years|יְמֵי֙\rb*\rb |שְׁנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |חַיֵּ֣י\rb*\rb |בִּימֵ֖י\rb*\rb |יְמֵי֙\rb*\rb |שְׁנֵי֙\rb* \rb of the travels|מְגוּרֵיהֶֽם׃\rb* \rb of my fathers|אֲבֹתַ֔י\rb*.”
\p \v 10 \rb Then Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֖ב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb blessed|וַיְבָ֥רֶךְ\rb* \rb Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹ֑ה\rb* \rb and departed|וַיֵּצֵ֖א\rb* \rb from his|פַרְעֹֽה׃\rb* \rb presence|מִלִּפְנֵ֥י\rb*.
\p \v 11 \rb So Joseph|יוֹסֵף֮\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb settled|וַיּוֹשֵׁ֣ב\rb* \rb his father|אָבִ֣יו\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and brothers|אֶחָיו֒\rb*\rb |וַיִּתֵּ֨ן\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb and gave them|לָהֶ֤ם\rb* \rb property|אֲחֻזָּה֙\rb* \rb in the best|בְּמֵיטַ֥ב\rb* \rb part of the land|הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb*, \rb the district|בְּאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Rameses|רַעְמְסֵ֑ס\rb*, \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb Pharaoh|פַרְעֹֽה׃\rb* \rb had commanded|צִוָּ֥ה\rb*. \v 12 \rb Joseph also|יוֹסֵף֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb provided|וַיְכַלְכֵּ֤ל\rb* \rb his father|אָבִ֣יו\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb brothers|אֶחָ֔יו\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֖ת\rb* \rb and all|כָּל־\rb* \rb his father’s|אָבִ֑יו\rb* \rb household|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb with food|לֶ֖חֶם\rb* \rb for|לְפִ֥י\rb* \rb their families|הַטָּֽף׃\rb*.
\s1 The Famine Continues
\p \v 13 \rb There was no|אֵין֙\rb* \rb food, however|וְלֶ֤חֶם\rb*, \rb in all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb that region|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb*, \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the famine|הָרָעָ֖ב\rb* \rb was so|מְאֹ֑ד\rb* \rb severe|כָבֵ֥ד\rb*; \rb the lands|אֶ֤רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֙יִם֙\rb* \rb and|וְאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb Canaan|כְּנַ֔עַן\rb* \rb had been exhausted|וַתֵּ֜לַהּ\rb* \rb by|מִפְּנֵ֖י\rb* \rb the famine|הָרָעָֽב׃\rb*. \v 14 \rb Joseph|יוֹסֵ֗ף\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb collected|וַיְלַקֵּ֣ט\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the money|הַכֶּ֙סֶף֙\rb* \rb to be found|הַנִּמְצָ֤א\rb* \rb in the land|בְאֶֽרֶץ־\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֙יִם֙\rb* \rb and the land|וּבְאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Canaan|כְּנַ֔עַן\rb* \rb in exchange for the grain|בַּשֶּׁ֖בֶר\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb they|הֵ֣ם\rb* \rb were buying|שֹׁבְרִ֑ים\rb*, \rb and he|יוֹסֵ֛ף\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb brought|וַיָּבֵ֥א\rb* \rb it|הַכֶּ֖סֶף\rb* \rb into Pharaoh’s|פַרְעֹֽה׃\rb* \rb palace|בֵּ֥יתָה\rb*. \v 15 \rb When the money|הַכֶּ֗סֶף\rb* \rb from the lands|מֵאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַיִם֮\rb* \rb and|וּמֵאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb Canaan|כְּנַעַן֒\rb* \rb was gone|וַיִּתֹּ֣ם\rb*, \rb all|כָל־\rb* \rb the Egyptians|מִצְרַ֨יִם\rb* \rb came|וַיָּבֹאוּ֩\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Joseph|יוֹסֵ֤ף\rb* \rb and said|לֵאמֹר֙\rb*, “\rb Give|הָֽבָה־\rb* \rb us|לָּ֣נוּ\rb* \rb food|לֶ֔חֶם\rb*. \rb Why|וְלָ֥מָּה\rb* \rb should we die|נָמ֖וּת\rb* \rb before your eyes|נֶגְדֶּ֑ךָ\rb*? \rb For|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb our funds|כָּֽסֶף׃\rb* \rb have run out|אָפֵ֖ס\rb*!”
\p \v 16 “\rb Then bring me|הָב֣וּ\rb* \rb your livestock|מִקְנֵיכֶ֔ם\rb*,” \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb Joseph|יוֹסֵף֙\rb*. “\rb Since|אִם־\rb* \rb the money|כָּֽסֶף׃\rb* \rb is gone|אָפֵ֖ס\rb*, \rb I will sell|וְאֶתְּנָ֥ה\rb* \rb you food|לָכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb in exchange for your livestock|בְּמִקְנֵיכֶ֑ם\rb*.” \v 17 \rb So they brought|וַיָּבִ֣יאוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their livestock|מִקְנֵיהֶם֮\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Joseph|יוֹסֵף֒\rb*, \rb and he|יוֹסֵ֨ף\rb* \rb gave|וַיִּתֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb them|לָהֶם֩\rb* \rb food|לֶ֜חֶם\rb* \rb in exchange for their horses|בַּסּוּסִ֗ים\rb*,\rb |וּבְמִקְנֵ֥ה\rb* \rb their flocks|הַצֹּ֛אן\rb*\rb |וּבְמִקְנֵ֥ה\rb* \rb and herds|הַבָּקָ֖ר\rb*, \rb and their donkeys|וּבַחֲמֹרִ֑ים\rb*. \rb Throughout that|הַהִֽוא׃\rb* \rb year|בַּשָּׁנָ֖ה\rb* \rb he provided them|וַיְנַהֲלֵ֤ם\rb* \rb with food|בַּלֶּ֙חֶם֙\rb* \rb in exchange for all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb their livestock|מִקְנֵהֶ֔ם\rb*.
\p \v 18 \rb When that|הַהִוא֒\rb* \rb year|הַשָּׁנָ֣ה\rb* \rb was over|וַתִּתֹּם֮\rb*, \rb they came|וַיָּבֹ֨אוּ\rb* \rb to him|אֵלָ֜יו\rb* \rb the second|הַשֵּׁנִ֗ית\rb* \rb year|בַּשָּׁנָ֣ה\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֤אמְרוּ\rb*, “\rb We cannot|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb hide|נְכַחֵ֣ד\rb* \rb from our lord|מֵֽאֲדֹנִ֔י\rb* \rb that|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb our money|הַכֶּ֔סֶף\rb* \rb is gone|תַּ֣ם\rb* \rb and all our livestock|וּמִקְנֵ֥ה\rb*\rb |הַבְּהֵמָ֖ה\rb* \rb belongs to|אֶל־\rb* \rb you|אֲדֹנִ֑י\rb*. \rb There is nothing|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb left|נִשְׁאַר֙\rb* \rb for|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb our lord|אֲדֹנִ֔י\rb* \rb except|בִּלְתִּ֥י\rb*\rb |אִם־\rb*\rb |אִם־\rb* \rb our bodies|גְּוִיָּתֵ֖נוּ\rb* \rb and our land|וְאַדְמָתֵֽנוּ׃\rb*. \v 19 \rb Why|לָ֧מָּה\rb* \rb should we perish|נָמ֣וּת\rb* \rb before your eyes|לְעֵינֶ֗יךָ\rb*— \rb we|אֲנַ֙חְנוּ֙\rb* \rb and|גַּ֣ם\rb* \rb our land|אַדְמָתֵ֔נוּ\rb* \rb as well|גַּם־\rb*? \rb Purchase|קְנֵֽה־\rb* \rb us|אֹתָ֥נוּ\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb our land|אַדְמָתֵ֖נוּ\rb* \rb in exchange for food|בַּלָּ֑חֶם\rb*. \rb Then we|אֲנַ֤חְנוּ\rb*, \rb along with our land|וְאַדְמָתֵ֙נוּ֙\rb*, \rb will be|וְנִֽהְיֶ֞ה\rb* \rb slaves|עֲבָדִ֣ים\rb* \rb to Pharaoh|לְפַרְעֹ֔ה\rb*. \rb Give us|וְתֶן־\rb* \rb seed|זֶ֗רַע\rb* \rb that we may live|וְנִֽחְיֶה֙\rb* \rb and not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb die|נָמ֔וּת\rb*, \rb and that the land|וְהָאֲדָמָ֖ה\rb* \rb may not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb become desolate|תֵשָֽׁם׃\rb*.”
\p \v 20 \rb So Joseph|יוֹסֵ֜ף\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb acquired|וַיִּ֨קֶן\rb* \rb for Pharaoh|לְפַרְעֹ֔ה\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the land|אַדְמַ֤ת\rb* \rb in Egypt|מִצְרַ֙יִם֙\rb*;\rb |כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the Egyptians|מִצְרַ֙יִם֙\rb*, \rb one and all|אִ֣ישׁ\rb*, \rb sold|מָכְר֤וּ\rb* \rb their fields|שָׂדֵ֔הוּ\rb* \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the famine|הָרָעָ֑ב\rb* \rb was so severe|חָזַ֥ק\rb* \rb upon them|עֲלֵהֶ֖ם\rb*. \rb The land|הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb became Pharaoh’s|וַתְּהִ֥י\rb*\rb |לְפַרְעֹֽה׃\rb*, \v 21 \rb |וְאֶ֨ת־\rb* \rb and Joseph reduced|הֶעֱבִ֥יר\rb*\rb |אֹת֖וֹ\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֔ם\rb* \rb to servitude|לֶעָרִ֑ים\rb*\f + \fr 47:21 \ft SP, LXX, Vulgate; Hebrew \fqa removed the people to the cities\f* \rb from one end|מִקְצֵ֥ה\rb*\rb |גְבוּל־\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֖יִם\rb* \rb to|וְעַד־\rb* \rb the other|קָצֵֽהוּ׃\rb*. \v 22 \rb However|רַ֛ק\rb*, \rb he did not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb acquire|קָנָ֑ה\rb* \rb the priests’ portion|הַכֹּהֲנִ֖ים\rb* \rb of the land|אַדְמַ֥ת\rb*, \rb for|כִּי֩\rb* \rb it had been given to them by Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹ֗ה\rb*. \rb They ate|וְאָֽכְל֤וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the rations that|חֻקָּם֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb*\rb |חֹ֨ק\rb*\rb |לַכֹּהֲנִ֜ים\rb*\rb |מֵאֵ֣ת\rb* \rb Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹ֔ה\rb* \rb supplied|נָתַ֤ן\rb*; \rb so|עַל־\rb*\rb |כֵּ֕ן\rb* \rb they did not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb sell|מָכְר֖וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their land|אַדְמָתָֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 23 \rb Then Joseph|יוֹסֵף֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֔ם\rb*, “\rb Now that|הֵן֩\rb* \rb I have acquired|קָנִ֨יתִי\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶ֥ם\rb* \rb you and your land|אַדְמַתְכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb for Pharaoh|לְפַרְעֹ֑ה\rb* \rb this day|הַיּ֛וֹם\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb*, \rb here|הֵֽא־\rb* \rb is seed|זֶ֔רַע\rb* \rb for you|לָכֶ֣ם\rb* \rb to sow|וּזְרַעְתֶּ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb in the land|הָאֲדָמָֽה׃\rb*. \v 24 \rb At harvest time|בַּתְּבוּאֹ֔ת\rb*, \rb you are to give|וּנְתַתֶּ֥ם\rb* \rb a fifth|חֲמִישִׁ֖ית\rb* \rb of it to Pharaoh|לְפַרְעֹ֑ה\rb*, \rb and four-fifths|וְאַרְבַּ֣ע\rb*\rb |הַיָּדֹ֡ת\rb* \rb will be|יִהְיֶ֣ה\rb* \rb yours|לָכֶם֩\rb* \rb as seed|לְזֶ֨רַע\rb* \rb for the field|הַשָּׂדֶ֧ה\rb* \rb and food for yourselves|וּֽלְאָכְלְכֶ֛ם\rb*\rb |וְלַאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb and your households|בְּבָתֵּיכֶ֖ם\rb*\rb |וְלֶאֱכֹ֥ל\rb* \rb and children|לְטַפְּכֶֽם׃\rb*.”
\p \v 25 “\rb You have saved our lives|הֶחֱיִתָ֑נוּ\rb*,” \rb they said|וַיֹּאמְר֖וּ\rb*. “\rb We have found|נִמְצָא־\rb* \rb favor|חֵן֙\rb* \rb in our lord’s|אֲדֹנִ֔י\rb* \rb eyes|בְּעֵינֵ֣י\rb*, \rb and we will be|וְהָיִ֥ינוּ\rb* \rb Pharaoh’s|לְפַרְעֹֽה׃\rb* \rb servants|עֲבָדִ֖ים\rb*.” \v 26 \rb So Joseph|יוֹסֵ֡ף\rb* \rb established|וַיָּ֣שֶׂם\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֣הּ\rb* \rb a law|לְחֹק֩\rb* \rb that a fifth|לַחֹ֑מֶשׁ\rb* \rb of the produce belongs to Pharaoh|לְפַרְעֹ֖ה\rb*, \rb and it is in effect|עַד־\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb the land|אַדְמַ֥ת\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֛יִם\rb* \rb to this|הַזֶּ֜ה\rb* \rb day|הַיּ֨וֹם\rb*. \rb Only|רַ֞ק\rb* \rb the priests’|הַכֹּֽהֲנִים֙\rb*\rb |לְבַדָּ֔ם\rb* \rb land|אַדְמַ֤ת\rb* \rb does not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb belong to|הָיְתָ֖ה\rb* \rb Pharaoh|לְפַרְעֹֽה׃\rb*.
\s1 The Israelites Prosper in Goshen
\p \v 27 \rb Now the Israelites|יִשְׂרָאֵ֛ל\rb* \rb settled|וַיֵּ֧שֶׁב\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֖יִם\rb*, \rb in the region|בְּאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Goshen|גֹּ֑שֶׁן\rb*. \rb They acquired property|וַיֵּאָחֲז֣וּ\rb* \rb there|בָ֔הּ\rb* \rb and became fruitful|וַיִּפְר֥וּ\rb* \rb and increased greatly|מְאֹֽד׃\rb* \rb in number|וַיִּרְבּ֖וּ\rb*. \v 28 \rb And Jacob|יַעֲקֹב֙\rb* \rb lived|וַיְחִ֤י\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֔יִם\rb*\rb |שְׁבַ֥ע\rb* \rb seventeen|עֶשְׂרֵ֖ה\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָ֑ה\rb*, \rb and the length of his life|שְׁנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |חַיָּ֔יו\rb* \rb was|וַיְהִ֤י\rb*\rb |יְמֵֽי־\rb*\rb |יַעֲקֹב֙\rb* \rb 147|וּמְאַ֖ת\rb*\rb |שֶׁ֣בַע\rb*\rb |וְאַרְבָּעִ֥ים\rb*\rb |שָׁנָֽה׃\rb* \rb years|שָׁנִ֔ים\rb*.
\p \v 29 \rb When the time|יְמֵֽי־\rb* \rb drew near|וַיִּקְרְב֣וּ\rb* \rb for Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֘ל\rb* \rb to die|לָמוּת֒\rb*, \rb he called|וַיִּקְרָ֣א׀\rb* \rb his son|לִבְנ֣וֹ\rb* \rb Joseph|לְיוֹסֵ֗ף\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to him|לוֹ֙\rb*, “\rb If|אִם־\rb*\rb |נָ֨א\rb* \rb I have found|מָצָ֤אתִי\rb* \rb favor|חֵן֙\rb* \rb in your eyes|בְּעֵינֶ֔יךָ\rb*, \rb put|שִֽׂים־\rb*\rb |נָ֥א\rb* \rb your hand|יָדְךָ֖\rb* \rb under|תַּ֣חַת\rb* \rb my thigh|יְרֵכִ֑י\rb* \rb and promise to show|וְעָשִׂ֤יתָ\rb* \rb me|עִמָּדִי֙\rb* \rb kindness|חֶ֣סֶד\rb* \rb and faithfulness|וֶאֱמֶ֔ת\rb*. \rb Do not|אַל־\rb*\rb |נָ֥א\rb* \rb bury me|תִקְבְּרֵ֖נִי\rb* \rb in Egypt|בְּמִצְרָֽיִם׃\rb*, \v 30 \rb but when I lie down|וְשָֽׁכַבְתִּי֙\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb my fathers|אֲבֹתַ֔י\rb*, \rb carry me|וּנְשָׂאתַ֙נִי֙\rb* \rb out of Egypt|מִמִּצְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb and bury me|וּקְבַרְתַּ֖נִי\rb* \rb with them|בִּקְבֻרָתָ֑ם\rb*.”
\p \rb Joseph answered|וַיֹּאמַ֕ר\rb*, “\rb I|אָנֹכִ֖י\rb* \rb will do|אֶֽעֱשֶׂ֥ה\rb* \rb as you have requested|כִדְבָרֶֽךָ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 31 “\rb Swear|הִשָּֽׁבְעָה֙\rb* \rb to me|לִ֔י\rb*,” \rb Jacob said|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*.
\p \rb So Joseph swore|וַיִּשָּׁבַ֖ע\rb* \rb to him|ל֑וֹ\rb*, \rb and Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb bowed in worship|וַיִּשְׁתַּ֥חוּ\rb* \rb at|עַל־\rb* \rb the head|רֹ֥אשׁ\rb* \rb of his bed|הַמִּטָּֽה׃פ\rb*.\f + \fr 47:31 \ft Hebrew; LXX \fqa Israel worshiped as he leaned on the top of his staff\ft ; see Hebrews 11:21.\f*
\c 48
\s1 Jacob Blesses Ephraim and Manasseh
\p \v 1 \rb |וַיְהִ֗י\rb* \rb Some time later|אַחֲרֵי֙\rb*\rb |הַדְּבָרִ֣ים\rb*\rb |הָאֵ֔לֶּה\rb* \rb Joseph|לְיוֹסֵ֔ף\rb*\rb |הִנֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb was told|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Your father|אָבִ֖יךָ\rb* \rb is ill|חֹלֶ֑ה\rb*.” \rb So he set out|וַיִּקַּ֞ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb with|עִמּ֔וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his two|שְׁנֵ֤י\rb* \rb sons|בָנָיו֙\rb*, \rb Manasseh|מְנַשֶּׁ֖ה\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and Ephraim|אֶפְרָֽיִם׃\rb*. \v 2 \rb When Jacob|לְיַעֲקֹ֔ב\rb*\rb |וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*\rb |הִנֵּ֛ה\rb* \rb was told|וַיַּגֵּ֣ד\rb*, “\rb Your son|בִּנְךָ֥\rb* \rb Joseph|יוֹסֵ֖ף\rb* \rb has come|בָּ֣א\rb* \rb to you|אֵלֶ֑יךָ\rb*,” \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb rallied his strength|וַיִּתְחַזֵּק֙\rb* \rb and sat up|וַיֵּ֖שֶׁב\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb bed|הַמִּטָּֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb Jacob|יַעֲקֹב֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Joseph|יוֹסֵ֔ף\rb*, “\rb God|אֵ֥ל\rb* \rb Almighty|שַׁדַּ֛י\rb*\f + \fr 48:3 \ft Hebrew \fqa El-Shaddai\f* \rb appeared|נִרְאָֽה־\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֥י\rb* \rb at Luz|בְּל֖וּז\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Canaan|כְּנָ֑עַן\rb*, \rb and there He blessed|וַיְבָ֖רֶךְ\rb* \rb me|אֹתִֽי׃\rb* \v 4 \rb and told|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb me|אֵלַ֗י\rb*, ‘\rb Behold|הִנְנִ֤י\rb*, \rb I will make you fruitful|מַפְרְךָ֙\rb* \rb and multiply you|וְהִרְבִּיתִ֔ךָ\rb*; \rb I will make you|וּנְתַתִּ֖יךָ\rb* \rb a multitude|לִקְהַ֣ל\rb* \rb of peoples|עַמִּ֑ים\rb*, \rb and will give|וְנָ֨תַתִּ֜י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּ֛את\rb* \rb land|הָאָ֧רֶץ\rb* \rb to your descendants|לְזַרְעֲךָ֥\rb* \rb after you|אַחֲרֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb as an everlasting|עוֹלָֽם׃\rb* \rb possession|אֲחֻזַּ֥ת\rb*.’
\p \v 5 \rb And now|וְעַתָּ֡ה\rb* \rb your two|שְׁנֵֽי־\rb* \rb sons|בָנֶיךָ֩\rb* \rb born|הַנּוֹלָדִ֨ים\rb* \rb to you|לְךָ֜\rb*\rb |בְּאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb in Egypt|מִצְרַ֗יִם\rb* \rb before|עַד־\rb* \rb I came|בֹּאִ֥י\rb* \rb to you|אֵלֶ֛יךָ\rb* \rb here|מִצְרַ֖יְמָה\rb* \rb shall be reckoned as|הֵ֑ם\rb* \rb mine|לִי־\rb*; \rb Ephraim|אֶפְרַ֙יִם֙\rb* \rb and Manasseh|וּמְנַשֶּׁ֔ה\rb* \rb shall be|יִֽהְיוּ־\rb* \rb mine|לִֽי׃\rb*, \rb just as Reuben|כִּרְאוּבֵ֥ן\rb* \rb and Simeon are mine|וְשִׁמְע֖וֹן\rb*. \v 6 \rb Any children|וּמוֹלַדְתְּךָ֛\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb born|הוֹלַ֥דְתָּ\rb* \rb to you|לְךָ֣\rb* \rb after them|אַחֲרֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb shall be yours|יִהְי֑וּ\rb*, \rb and they shall be called|יִקָּרְא֖וּ\rb* \rb by|עַ֣ל\rb* \rb the names|שֵׁ֧ם\rb* \rb of their brothers|אֲחֵיהֶ֛ם\rb* \rb in the territory they inherit|בְּנַחֲלָתָֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 7 \rb Now as for me|וַאֲנִ֣י׀\rb*, \rb when I was returning|בְּבֹאִ֣י\rb* \rb from Paddan|מִפַּדָּ֗ן\rb*,\f + \fr 48:7 \ft That is, northwest Mesopotamia\f* \rb to my sorrow|עָלַ֨י\rb* \rb Rachel|רָחֵ֜ל\rb* \rb died|מֵ֩תָה֩\rb* \rb along the way|בַּדֶּ֔רֶךְ\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֤רֶץ\rb* \rb of Canaan|כְּנַ֙עַן֙\rb*,\rb |בְּע֥וֹד\rb* \rb some distance|כִּבְרַת־\rb*\rb |אֶ֖רֶץ\rb*\rb |לָבֹ֣א\rb* \rb from Ephrath|אֶפְרָ֑תָה\rb*. \rb So I buried her|וָאֶקְבְּרֶ֤הָ\rb* \rb there|שָּׁם֙\rb* \rb beside the road|בְּדֶ֣רֶךְ\rb* \rb to Ephrath|אֶפְרָ֔ת\rb*” \rb (that|הִ֖וא\rb* \rb is|בֵּ֥ית\rb*, \rb Bethlehem|לָֽחֶם׃\rb*).
\p \v 8 \rb When Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb saw|וַיַּ֥רְא\rb* \rb the sons|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Joseph|יוֹסֵ֑ף\rb*, \rb he asked|וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Who|מִי־\rb* \rb are these|אֵֽלֶּה׃\rb*?”
\p \v 9 \rb Joseph|יוֹסֵף֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his father|אָבִ֔יו\rb*, “\rb They|הֵ֔ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb are the sons|בָּנַ֣י\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb has given|נָֽתַן־\rb* \rb me|לִ֥י\rb* \rb in this place|בָּזֶ֑ה\rb*.”
\p \rb So Jacob said|וַיֹּאמַ֕ר\rb*, “\rb Please|נָ֥א\rb* \rb bring them|קָֽחֶם־\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֖י\rb*, \rb that I may bless them|וַאֲבָרֲכֵֽם׃\rb*.”
\p \v 10 \rb Now Israel’s|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb eyesight|וְעֵינֵ֤י\rb* \rb was poor|כָּבְד֣וּ\rb* \rb because of old age|מִזֹּ֔קֶן\rb*; \rb he could|יוּכַ֖ל\rb* \rb hardly|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb see|לִרְא֑וֹת\rb*. \rb Joseph brought|וַיַּגֵּ֤שׁ\rb*\rb |אֹתָם֙\rb* \rb his sons to him|אֵלָ֔יו\rb*, \rb and his father kissed|וַיִּשַּׁ֥ק\rb* \rb them|לָהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb and embraced|וַיְחַבֵּ֥ק\rb* \rb them|לָהֶֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 11 “\rb I never|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb expected|פִלָּ֑לְתִּי\rb* \rb to see|רְאֹ֥ה\rb* \rb your face again|פָנֶ֖יךָ\rb*,” \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Joseph|יוֹסֵ֔ף\rb*, “\rb but now|וְהִנֵּ֨ה\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb has let me see|הֶרְאָ֥ה\rb*\rb |אֹתִ֛י\rb* \rb your children|זַרְעֶֽךָ׃\rb* \rb as well|גַּ֥ם\rb*.”
\p \v 12 \rb Then Joseph|יוֹסֵ֛ף\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb removed his sons|וַיּוֹצֵ֥א\rb* \rb from|מֵעִ֣ם\rb* \rb his father’s knees|בִּרְכָּ֑יו\rb* \rb and bowed|וַיִּשְׁתַּ֥חוּ\rb* \rb facedown|לְאַפָּ֖יו\rb*\rb |אָֽרְצָה׃\rb*.
\p \v 13 \rb And Joseph|יוֹסֵף֮\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb took|וַיִּקַּ֣ח\rb* \rb both|שְׁנֵיהֶם֒\rb* \rb of them|אֶת־\rb*— \rb with Ephraim|אֶפְרַ֤יִם\rb* \rb in his right hand|בִּֽימִינוֹ֙\rb* \rb toward Israel’s|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb left hand|מִשְּׂמֹ֣אל\rb*, \rb and Manasseh|מְנַשֶּׁ֥ה\rb* \rb in his left hand|בִשְׂמֹאל֖וֹ\rb* \rb toward Israel’s|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb right hand|מִימִ֣ין\rb*— \rb and brought them close|וַיַּגֵּ֖שׁ\rb* \rb to him|אֵלָֽיו׃\rb*. \v 14 \rb But Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֨ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb stretched out|וַיִּשְׁלַח֩\rb* \rb his right hand|יְמִינ֜וֹ\rb* \rb and put|וַיָּ֨שֶׁת\rb* \rb it on|עַל־\rb* \rb the head|רֹ֤אשׁ\rb* \rb of Ephraim|אֶפְרַ֙יִם֙\rb*,\rb |וְה֣וּא\rb* \rb the younger|הַצָּעִ֔יר\rb*;\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and crossing|שִׂכֵּל֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his hands|יָדָ֔יו\rb*, \rb he put his left|שְׂמֹאל֖וֹ\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb Manasseh’s|מְנַשֶּׁ֑ה\rb* \rb head|רֹ֣אשׁ\rb*, \rb although|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb Manasseh|מְנַשֶּׁ֖ה\rb* \rb was the firstborn|הַבְּכֽוֹר׃\rb*. \v 15 \rb Then he blessed|וַיְבָ֥רֶךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Joseph|יוֹסֵ֖ף\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּאמַ֑ר\rb*:
\b 
\q1 “\rb May the God|הָֽאֱלֹהִ֡ים\rb* \rb before|לְפָנָיו֙\rb* \rb whom|אֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb my fathers|אֲבֹתַ֤י\rb* \rb Abraham|אַבְרָהָ֣ם\rb* \rb and Isaac|וְיִצְחָ֔ק\rb* \rb walked|הִתְהַלְּכ֨וּ\rb*,
\q2 \rb the God|הָֽאֱלֹהִים֙\rb* \rb who has been my shepherd|הָרֹעֶ֣ה\rb*\rb |אֹתִ֔י\rb* \rb all my life|מֵעוֹדִ֖י\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb day|הַיּ֥וֹם\rb*,
\q1 \v 16 \rb the angel|הַמַּלְאָךְ֩\rb*\f + \fr 48:16 \ft Or \fqa Angel\f* \rb who has redeemed|הַגֹּאֵ֨ל\rb* \rb me|אֹתִ֜י\rb* \rb from all|מִכָּל־\rb* \rb harm|רָ֗ע\rb*—
\q2 \rb may He bless|יְבָרֵךְ֮\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb these boys|הַנְּעָרִים֒\rb*.
\q1 \rb And may they be called|וְיִקָּרֵ֤א\rb* \rb by my name|שְׁמִ֔י\rb*
\q2 \rb and the names|וְשֵׁ֥ם\rb* \rb of my fathers|אֲבֹתַ֖י\rb* \rb Abraham|אַבְרָהָ֣ם\rb* \rb and Isaac|וְיִצְחָ֑ק\rb*,
\q2 \rb and may they grow|וְיִדְגּ֥וּ\rb* \rb into a multitude|לָרֹ֖ב\rb* \rb upon|בְּקֶ֥רֶב\rb* \rb the earth|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 17 \rb When Joseph|יוֹסֵ֗ף\rb* \rb saw|וַיַּ֣רְא\rb* \rb that|כִּי־\rb* \rb his father|אָבִ֧יו\rb* \rb had placed|יָשִׁ֨ית\rb* \rb his right|יְמִינ֛וֹ\rb* \rb hand|יַד־\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb Ephraim’s|אֶפְרַ֖יִם\rb* \rb head|רֹ֥אשׁ\rb*, \rb he was displeased|וַיֵּ֣רַע\rb*\rb |בְּעֵינָ֑יו\rb* \rb and took|וַיִּתְמֹ֣ךְ\rb* \rb his father’s|אָבִ֗יו\rb* \rb hand|יַד־\rb* \rb to move|לְהָסִ֥יר\rb* \rb it|אֹתָ֛הּ\rb* \rb from|מֵעַ֥ל\rb* \rb Ephraim’s|אֶפְרַ֖יִם\rb* \rb head|רֹאשׁ־\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb*\rb |רֹ֥אשׁ\rb* \rb Manasseh’s|מְנַשֶּֽׁה׃\rb*. \v 18 “\rb Not|לֹא־\rb* \rb so|כֵ֣ן\rb*, \rb my father|אָבִ֑י\rb*!” \rb Joseph|יוֹסֵ֛ף\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֧אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |אָבִ֖יו\rb*. “\rb |כִּי־\rb* \rb This|זֶ֣ה\rb* \rb one is the firstborn|הַבְּכֹ֔ר\rb*; \rb put|שִׂ֥ים\rb* \rb your right hand|יְמִינְךָ֖\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb his head|רֹאשֽׁוֹ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 19 \rb But his father|אָבִ֗יו\rb* \rb refused|וַיְמָאֵ֣ן\rb*. “\rb I know|יָדַ֤עְתִּֽי\rb*, \rb my son|בְנִי֙\rb*, \rb I know|יָדַ֔עְתִּי\rb*!” \rb he said|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb*. “\rb He|ה֥וּא\rb* \rb too|גַּם־\rb* \rb shall become|יִֽהְיֶה־\rb* \rb a people|לְּעָ֖ם\rb*, \rb and he|ה֣וּא\rb* \rb too|וְגַם־\rb* \rb shall be great|יִגְדָּ֑ל\rb*; \rb nevertheless|וְאוּלָ֗ם\rb*, \rb his younger|הַקָּטֹן֙\rb* \rb brother|אָחִ֤יו\rb* \rb shall be greater|יִגְדַּ֣ל\rb* \rb than he|מִמֶּ֔נּוּ\rb*, \rb and his offspring|וְזַרְע֖וֹ\rb* \rb shall become|יִהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb a multitude|מְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb of nations|הַגּוֹיִֽם׃\rb*.”
\p \v 20 \rb So that day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb Jacob blessed|וַיְבָ֨רֲכֵ֜ם\rb* \rb them|הַהוּא֮\rb* \rb and said|לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb*:
\b 
\q1 “\rb By you|בְּךָ֗\rb* \rb shall Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb pronounce|לֵאמוֹר֒\rb* \rb this blessing|יְבָרֵ֤ךְ\rb*:
\q2 ‘\rb May God|אֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb* \rb make|יְשִֽׂמְךָ֣\rb* \rb you like Ephraim|כְּאֶפְרַ֖יִם\rb* \rb and Manasseh|וְכִמְנַשֶּׁ֑ה\rb*.’”
\p \rb So he put|וַיָּ֥שֶׂם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Ephraim|אֶפְרַ֖יִם\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb Manasseh|מְנַשֶּֽׁה׃\rb*.
\p \v 21 \rb Then Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Joseph|יוֹסֵ֔ף\rb*, “\rb Look|הִנֵּ֥ה\rb*, \rb I|אָנֹכִ֖י\rb* \rb am about to die|מֵ֑ת\rb*, \rb but God|אֱלֹהִים֙\rb* \rb will be|וְהָיָ֤ה\rb* \rb with you|עִמָּכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb and bring|וְהֵשִׁ֣יב\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb back to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb of your fathers|אֲבֹתֵיכֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 22 \rb And to you|לְךָ֛\rb*, \rb as one who is above|עַל־\rb* \rb your brothers|אַחֶ֑יךָ\rb*, \rb I|וַאֲנִ֞י\rb* \rb give|נָתַ֧תִּֽי\rb* \rb the|אַחַ֖ד\rb* \rb ridge of land|שְׁכֶ֥ם\rb*\f + \fr 48:22 \ft Or \fqa one portion of the land\ft ; Hebrew \fqa shekem\ft , which sounds like the town and district called \fqa Shechem\f* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb I took|לָקַ֙חְתִּי֙\rb* \rb from|מִיַּ֣ד\rb* \rb the Amorites|הָֽאֱמֹרִ֔י\rb* \rb with my sword|בְּחַרְבִּ֖י\rb* \rb and bow|וּבְקַשְׁתִּֽי׃פ\rb*.”
\c 49
\s1 Jacob Blesses His Sons
\p \v 1 \rb Then Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֖ב\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb called for|וַיִּקְרָ֥א\rb* \rb his sons|בָּנָ֑יו\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Gather around|הֵאָֽסְפוּ֙\rb* \rb so that I can tell|וְאַגִּ֣ידָה\rb* \rb you|לָכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb will happen|יִקְרָ֥א\rb* \rb to you|אֶתְכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb in the days|הַיָּמִֽים׃\rb* \rb to come|בְּאַחֲרִ֥ית\rb*:
\b 
\q1 \v 2 \rb Come together|הִקָּבְצ֥וּ\rb* \rb and listen|וְשִׁמְע֖וּ\rb*, \rb O sons|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֑ב\rb*;
\q2 \rb listen|וְשִׁמְע֖וּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb your father|אֲבִיכֶֽם׃\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֥ל\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 3 \rb Reuben|רְאוּבֵן֙\rb*, \rb you|אַ֔תָּה\rb* \rb are my firstborn|בְּכֹ֣רִי\rb*, \rb my might|כֹּחִ֖י\rb*,
\q2 \rb and the beginning|וְרֵאשִׁ֣ית\rb* \rb of my strength|אוֹנִ֑י\rb*,
