\p \v 29 \rb Then Jacob instructed them|וַיְצַ֣ו\rb*,\rb |אוֹתָ֗ם\rb*\rb |וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* “\rb I|אֲנִי֙\rb* \rb am about to be gathered|נֶאֱסָ֣ף\rb* \rb to|אֲלֵהֶם֙\rb* \rb my people|עַמִּ֔י\rb*. \rb Bury|קִבְר֥וּ\rb* \rb me|אֹתִ֖י\rb* \rb with|אֶל־\rb* \rb my fathers|אֲבֹתָ֑י\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb in|אֶל־\rb* \rb the cave|הַ֨מְּעָרָ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb in the field|בִּשְׂדֵ֖ה\rb* \rb of Ephron|עֶפְר֥וֹן\rb* \rb the Hittite|הַֽחִתִּֽי׃\rb*. \v 30 \rb The cave|בַּמְּעָרָ֞ה\rb* \rb is in the field|בִּשְׂדֵ֧ה\rb* \rb of Machpelah|הַמַּכְפֵּלָ֛ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb near|עַל־\rb*\rb |פְּנֵי־\rb* \rb Mamre|מַמְרֵ֖א\rb*, \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Canaan|כְּנָ֑עַן\rb*. \rb This|אֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb is the field|הַשָּׂדֶ֗ה\rb* \rb Abraham|אַבְרָהָ֜ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb purchased|קָנָ֨ה\rb* \rb from|מֵאֵ֛ת\rb* \rb Ephron|עֶפְרֹ֥ן\rb* \rb the Hittite|הַחִתִּ֖י\rb* \rb as a burial|קָֽבֶר׃\rb* \rb site|לַאֲחֻזַּת־\rb*. \v 31 \rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb There|שָׁ֣מָּה\rb* \rb Abraham|אַבְרָהָ֗ם\rb*\rb |וְאֵת֙\rb* \rb and his wife|אִשְׁתּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb Sarah|שָׂרָ֣ה\rb* \rb are buried|קָֽבְר֞וּ\rb*, \rb there|שָׁ֚מָּה\rb* \rb Isaac|יִצְחָ֔ק\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֖ת\rb* \rb and his wife|אִשְׁתּ֑וֹ\rb* \rb Rebekah|רִבְקָ֣ה\rb* \rb are buried|קָבְר֣וּ\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb and there|וְשָׁ֥מָּה\rb* \rb I buried|קָבַ֖רְתִּי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Leah|לֵאָֽה׃\rb*. \v 32 \rb The field|הַשָּׂדֶ֛ה\rb* \rb and the cave|וְהַמְּעָרָ֥ה\rb* \rb that is|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb in it|בּ֖וֹ\rb*\rb |מֵאֵ֥ת\rb* \rb were purchased|מִקְנֵ֧ה\rb* \rb from the Hittites|בְּנֵי־\rb*\rb |חֵֽת׃\rb*.”
\p \v 33 \rb When Jacob|יַעֲקֹב֙\rb* \rb had finished|וַיְכַ֤ל\rb* \rb instructing|לְצַוֺּ֣ת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his sons|בָּנָ֔יו\rb*, \rb he pulled|וַיֶּאֱסֹ֥ף\rb* \rb his feet|רַגְלָ֖יו\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb the bed|הַמִּטָּ֑ה\rb* \rb and breathed his last|וַיִּגְוַ֖ע\rb*, \rb and he was gathered|וַיֵּאָ֥סֶף\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his people|עַמָּֽיו׃\rb*.
\c 50
\s1 Mourning and Burial for Jacob
\p \v 1 \rb Then Joseph|יוֹסֵ֖ף\rb* \rb fell|וַיִּפֹּ֥ל\rb* \rb upon|עַל־\rb* \rb his father’s|אָבִ֑יו\rb* \rb face|פְּנֵ֣י\rb*, \rb wept|וַיֵּ֥בְךְּ\rb* \rb over him|עָלָ֖יו\rb*, \rb and kissed|וַיִּשַּׁק־\rb* \rb him|לֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\p \v 2 \rb And Joseph|יוֹסֵ֤ף\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb directed|וַיְצַ֨ו\rb* \rb the physicians|הָרֹ֣פְאִ֔ים\rb* \rb in his service|עֲבָדָיו֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb to embalm|לַחֲנֹ֖ט\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his father|אָבִ֑יו\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*. \rb So they|הָרֹפְאִ֖ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb embalmed him|וַיַּחַנְט֥וּ\rb*, \v 3 \rb taking the forty|אַרְבָּעִ֣ים\rb* \rb days|י֔וֹם\rb* \rb required to complete|וַיִּמְלְאוּ־\rb*\rb |כִּ֛י\rb*\rb |כֵּ֥ן\rb*\rb |יִמְלְא֖וּ\rb* \rb the embalming|הַחֲנֻטִ֑ים\rb*. \rb And the Egyptians|מִצְרַ֖יִם\rb* \rb mourned|וַיִּבְכּ֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֹת֛וֹ\rb* \rb for him seventy|שִׁבְעִ֥ים\rb* \rb days|יֽוֹם׃\rb*.
\p \v 4 \rb When the days|יְמֵ֣י\rb* \rb of mourning|בְכִית֔וֹ\rb* \rb had passed|וַיַּֽעַבְרוּ֙\rb*, \rb Joseph|יוֹסֵ֔ף\rb* \rb said|וַיְדַבֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Pharaoh’s|פַּרְעֹ֖ה\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb court|בֵּ֥ית\rb*, “\rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb I have found|מָצָ֤אתִי\rb* \rb favor|חֵן֙\rb* \rb in your eyes|בְּעֵ֣ינֵיכֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb please|נָ֨א\rb* \rb tell|דַּבְּרוּ־\rb*\rb |נָ֕א\rb*\rb |בְּאָזְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb Pharaoh that|פַרְעֹ֖ה\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 5 \rb my father|אָבִ֞י\rb* \rb made me swear an oath|הִשְׁבִּיעַ֣נִי\rb* \rb when he said|לֵאמֹ֗ר\rb*, ‘\rb |הִנֵּ֣ה\rb* \rb I|אָנֹכִי֮\rb* \rb am about to die|מֵת֒\rb*. \rb You must bury me|תִּקְבְּרֵ֑נִי\rb*\rb |שָׁ֖מָּה\rb* \rb in the tomb|בְּקִבְרִ֗י\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb I dug|כָּרִ֤יתִי\rb* \rb for myself in the land|בְּאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Canaan|כְּנַ֔עַן\rb*.’ \rb Now|וְעַתָּ֗ה\rb* \rb let me go|אֶֽעֱלֶה־\rb*\rb |נָּ֛א\rb* \rb and bury|וְאֶקְבְּרָ֥ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb my father|אָבִ֖י\rb*, \rb and then return|וְאָשֽׁוּבָה׃\rb*.”
\p \v 6 \rb Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹ֑ה\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Go up|עֲלֵ֛ה\rb* \rb and bury|וּקְבֹ֥ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your father|אָבִ֖יךָ\rb*, \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb he made you swear to do|הִשְׁבִּיעֶֽךָ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 7 \rb Then Joseph|יוֹסֵ֖ף\rb* \rb went|וַיַּ֥עַל\rb* \rb to bury|לִקְבֹּ֣ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his father|אָבִ֑יו\rb*, \rb and all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the servants|עַבְדֵ֤י\rb* \rb of Pharaoh|פַרְעֹה֙\rb* \rb accompanied|וַיַּֽעֲל֨וּ\rb* \rb him|אִתּ֜וֹ\rb* — \rb the elders|זִקְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Pharaoh’s household|בֵית֔וֹ\rb* \rb and all|וְכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb the elders|זִקְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the land|אֶֽרֶץ־\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרָֽיִם׃\rb* — \v 8 \rb along with all|וְכֹל֙\rb* \rb of Joseph’s|יוֹסֵ֔ף\rb* \rb household|בֵּ֣ית\rb*, \rb and his brothers|וְאֶחָ֖יו\rb*, \rb and his father’s|אָבִ֑יו\rb* \rb household|וּבֵ֣ית\rb*. \rb Only|רַ֗ק\rb* \rb their children|טַפָּם֙\rb* \rb and flocks|וְצֹאנָ֣ם\rb* \rb and herds|וּבְקָרָ֔ם\rb* \rb were left|עָזְב֖וּ\rb*\rb |בְּאֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb in Goshen|גֹּֽשֶׁן׃\rb*.
\p \v 9 \rb Chariots|רֶ֖כֶב\rb* \rb and|גַּם־\rb* \rb horsemen|פָּרָשִׁ֑ים\rb* \rb alike|גַּם־\rb* \rb went up|וַיַּ֣עַל\rb* \rb with him|עִמּ֔וֹ\rb*, \rb and it was|וַיְהִ֥י\rb* \rb an exceedingly|מְאֹֽד׃\rb* \rb large|כָּבֵ֥ד\rb* \rb procession|הַֽמַּחֲנֶ֖ה\rb*. \v 10 \rb When they reached|וַיָּבֹ֜אוּ\rb*\rb |עַד־\rb* \rb the threshing floor|גֹּ֣רֶן\rb* \rb of Atad|הָאָטָ֗ד\rb*, \rb which|אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb is across|בְּעֵ֣בֶר\rb* \rb the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּ֔ן\rb*, \rb they lamented|וַיִּ֨סְפְּדוּ־\rb*\rb |שָׁ֔ם\rb* \rb and wailed|מִסְפֵּ֛ד\rb* \rb loudly|גָּד֥וֹל\rb*,\rb |וְכָבֵ֖ד\rb*\rb |מְאֹ֑ד\rb* \rb and Joseph mourned|וַיַּ֧עַשׂ\rb*\rb |אֵ֖בֶל\rb* \rb for his father|לְאָבִ֛יו\rb* \rb seven|שִׁבְעַ֥ת\rb* \rb days|יָמִֽים׃\rb*.
\p \v 11 \rb When the Canaanites|הַֽכְּנַעֲנִ֜י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |יוֹשֵׁב֩\rb* \rb of the land|הָאָ֨רֶץ\rb* \rb saw|וַיַּ֡רְא\rb* \rb the mourning|הָאֵ֗בֶל\rb*\rb |בְּגֹ֙רֶן֙\rb* \rb at the threshing floor of Atad|הָֽאָטָ֔ד\rb*, \rb they said|וַיֹּ֣אמְר֔וּ\rb*, “\rb This|זֶ֖ה\rb* \rb is a solemn|כָּבֵ֥ד\rb* \rb ceremony of mourning|אֵֽבֶל־\rb* \rb by the Egyptians|לְמִצְרָ֑יִם\rb*.” \rb Thus|עַל־\rb*\rb |כֵּ֞ן\rb* \rb the place|אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb across|בְּעֵ֥בֶר\rb* \rb the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּֽן׃\rb* \rb is called|קָרָ֤א\rb*\rb |שְׁמָהּ֙\rb*\rb |אָבֵ֣ל\rb* \rb Abel-mizraim|מִצְרַ֔יִם\rb*.\f + \fr 50:11 \fqa Abel-mizraim \ft means \fqa mourning of the Egyptians\ft .\f*
\p \v 12 \rb So Jacob’s sons|בָנָ֖יו\rb*\rb |כֵּ֖ן\rb* \rb did|וַיַּעֲשׂ֥וּ\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb he had charged them|צִוָּֽם׃\rb*. \v 13 \rb They|בָנָיו֙\rb* \rb carried|וַיִּשְׂא֨וּ\rb* \rb him|אֹת֤וֹ\rb* \rb to the land|אַ֣רְצָה\rb* \rb of Canaan|כְּנַ֔עַן\rb* \rb and buried|וַיִּקְבְּר֣וּ\rb* \rb him|אֹת֔וֹ\rb* \rb in the cave|בִּמְעָרַ֖ת\rb* \rb at Machpelah|הַמַּכְפֵּלָ֑ה\rb* \rb in the field|שְׂדֵ֣ה\rb* \rb near|עַל־\rb*\rb |פְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb Mamre|מַמְרֵֽא׃\rb*, \rb which|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb Abraham|אַבְרָהָ֨ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |הַשָּׂדֶ֜ה\rb* \rb had purchased|קָנָה֩\rb* \rb from Ephron|עֶפְרֹ֥ן\rb* \rb the Hittite|הַחִתִּ֖י\rb* \rb as a burial|קֶ֗בֶר\rb*\rb |מֵאֵ֛ת\rb* \rb site|לַאֲחֻזַּת־\rb*.
\p \v 14 \rb After|אַחֲרֵ֖י\rb*\rb |קָבְר֥וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Joseph|יוֹסֵ֤ף\rb* \rb had buried|לִקְבֹּ֣ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his father|אָבִ֑יו\rb*, \rb he returned|וַיָּ֨שָׁב\rb* \rb to Egypt|מִצְרַ֙יְמָה֙\rb*\rb |ה֣וּא\rb* \rb with his brothers|וְאֶחָ֔יו\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb who had gone|הָעֹלִ֥ים\rb* \rb with him|אִתּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb to bury his father|אָבִֽיו׃\rb*.
\s1 Joseph Comforts His Brothers
\p \v 15 \rb When Joseph’s|יוֹסֵף֙\rb* \rb brothers|אֲחֵֽי־\rb* \rb saw|וַיִּרְא֤וּ\rb* \rb that|כִּי־\rb* \rb their father|אֲבִיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb was dead|מֵ֣ת\rb*, \rb they said|וַיֹּ֣אמְר֔וּ\rb*, “\rb What if|ל֥וּ\rb* \rb Joseph|יוֹסֵ֑ף\rb* \rb bears a grudge|יִשְׂטְמֵ֖נוּ\rb*? \rb Then he will surely repay|וְהָשֵׁ֤ב\rb*\rb |יָשִׁיב֙\rb* \rb us|לָ֔נוּ\rb*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb* \rb for all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the evil|הָ֣רָעָ֔ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb we did|גָּמַ֖לְנוּ\rb* \rb to him|אֹתֽוֹ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 16 \rb So they sent word|וַיְצַוּ֕וּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Joseph|יוֹסֵ֖ף\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*, “\rb Before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb he died|מוֹת֖וֹ\rb*,\rb |לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb* \rb your father|אָבִ֣יךָ\rb* \rb commanded|צִוָּ֔ה\rb*, \v 17 ‘\rb This is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb you are to say|תֹאמְר֣וּ\rb* \rb to Joseph|לְיוֹסֵ֗ף\rb*: \rb I beg you|אָ֣נָּ֡א\rb*, \rb please|נָ֠א\rb* \rb forgive|שָׂ֣א\rb* \rb the transgression|פֶּ֣שַׁע\rb* \rb and sin|וְחַטָּאתָם֙\rb* \rb of your brothers|אַחֶ֤יךָ\rb*, \rb for|כִּי־\rb* \rb they did|גְמָל֔וּךָ\rb* \rb you wrong|רָעָ֣ה\rb*.’ \rb So now, Joseph|וְעַתָּה֙\rb*, \rb please|נָ֔א\rb* \rb forgive|שָׂ֣א\rb* \rb the transgression|לְפֶ֥שַׁע\rb* \rb of the servants|עַבְדֵ֖י\rb* \rb of the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of your father|אָבִ֑יךָ\rb*.”
\p \rb When their message|בְּדַבְּרָ֥ם\rb* \rb came to him|אֵלָֽיו׃\rb*, \rb Joseph|יוֹסֵ֖ף\rb* \rb wept|וַיֵּ֥בְךְּ\rb*. \v 18 \rb His brothers|אֶחָ֔יו\rb* \rb also|גַּם־\rb* \rb came to him|וַיֵּלְכוּ֙\rb*, \rb bowed down|וַֽיִּפְּל֖וּ\rb* \rb before him|לְפָנָ֑יו\rb*, \rb and said|וַיֹּ֣אמְר֔וּ\rb*,\rb |הִנֶּ֥נּֽוּ\rb* “\rb We are your slaves|לַעֲבָדִֽים׃\rb*!”
\p \v 19 \rb But Joseph|יוֹסֵ֖ף\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֧אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֲלֵהֶ֛ם\rb*, “\rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb be afraid|תִּירָ֑אוּ\rb*.\rb |כִּ֛י\rb* \rb Am I|אָֽנִי׃\rb* \rb in the place of|הֲתַ֥חַת\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb*? \v 20 \rb As for you|וְאַתֶּ֕ם\rb*, \rb what you intended|חֲשַׁבְתֶּ֥ם\rb* \rb against me|עָלַ֖י\rb* \rb for evil|רָעָ֑ה\rb*, \rb God|אֱלֹהִים֙\rb* \rb intended|חֲשָׁבָ֣הּ\rb* \rb for good|לְטֹבָ֔ה\rb*, \rb in order to|לְמַ֗עַן\rb* \rb accomplish|עֲשֹׂ֛ה\rb* \rb a day|כַּיּ֥וֹם\rb* \rb like this|הַזֶּ֖ה\rb*— \rb to preserve the lives|לְהַחֲיֹ֥ת\rb* \rb of many|רָֽב׃\rb* \rb people|עַם־\rb*. \v 21 \rb Therefore|וְעַתָּה֙\rb* \rb do not|אַל־\rb* \rb be afraid|תִּירָ֔אוּ\rb*. \rb I|אָנֹכִ֛י\rb* \rb will provide for|אֲכַלְכֵּ֥ל\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶ֖ם\rb*\rb |וְאֶֽת־\rb* \rb and your little ones|טַפְּכֶ֑ם\rb*.” \rb So Joseph reassured|וַיְנַחֵ֣ם\rb* \rb his brothers|אוֹתָ֔ם\rb* \rb and spoke|וַיְדַבֵּ֖ר\rb* \rb kindly to them|עַל־\rb*\rb |לִבָּֽם׃\rb*.
\s1 The Death of Joseph
\p \v 22 \rb Now Joseph|יוֹסֵף֙\rb* \rb and his father’s|אָבִ֑יו\rb* \rb household|וּבֵ֣ית\rb* \rb remained|וַיֵּ֤שֶׁב\rb* \rb in Egypt|בְּמִצְרַ֔יִם\rb*,\rb |ה֖וּא\rb* \rb and Joseph|יוֹסֵ֔ף\rb* \rb lived|וַיְחִ֣י\rb* \rb to the age|שָׁנִֽים׃\rb* \rb of 110|מֵאָ֥ה\rb*\rb |וָעֶ֖שֶׂר\rb*. \v 23 \rb He|יוֹסֵף֙\rb* \rb saw|וַיַּ֤רְא\rb* \rb Ephraim’s|לְאֶפְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb sons|בְּנֵ֖י\rb* \rb to the third generation|שִׁלֵּשִׁ֑ים\rb*, \rb and indeed|גַּ֗ם\rb* \rb the sons|בְּנֵ֤י\rb* \rb of Machir|מָכִיר֙\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Manasseh|מְנַשֶּׁ֔ה\rb* \rb were brought up|יֻלְּד֖וּ\rb*\f + \fr 50:23 \ft Or \fqa born \ft or \fqa placed at birth\f* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb Joseph’s|יוֹסֵֽף׃\rb* \rb knees|בִּרְכֵּ֥י\rb*.
\p \v 24 \rb Then Joseph|יוֹסֵף֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his brothers|אֶחָ֔יו\rb*, “\rb I|אָנֹכִ֖י\rb* \rb am about to die|מֵ֑ת\rb*, \rb but God|וֵֽאלֹהִ֞ים\rb* \rb will surely visit|פָּקֹ֧ד\rb*\rb |יִפְקֹ֣ד\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶ֗ם\rb* \rb and bring you up|וְהֶעֱלָ֤ה\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶם֙\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּ֔את\rb* \rb land|הָאָ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֕רֶץ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb He promised on oath|נִשְׁבַּ֛ע\rb* \rb to Abraham|לְאַבְרָהָ֥ם\rb*, \rb Isaac|לְיִצְחָ֖ק\rb*, \rb and Jacob|וּֽלְיַעֲקֹֽב׃\rb*.” \v 25 \rb And Joseph|יוֹסֵ֔ף\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb made the sons|בְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb take an oath|וַיַּשְׁבַּ֣ע\rb* \rb and said|לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*, “\rb God|אֱלֹהִים֙\rb* \rb will surely attend to|פָּקֹ֨ד\rb*\rb |יִפְקֹ֤ד\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb and then you must carry|וְהַעֲלִתֶ֥ם\rb* \rb my bones|עַצְמֹתַ֖י\rb* \rb up from this place|מִזֶּֽה׃\rb*.”
\p \v 26 \rb So Joseph|יוֹסֵ֔ף\rb* \rb died|וַיָּ֣מָת\rb* \rb at the age|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of 110|מֵאָ֥ה\rb*\rb |וָעֶ֖שֶׂר\rb*\rb |שָׁנִ֑ים\rb*. \rb And they embalmed|וַיַּחַנְט֣וּ\rb* \rb his body|אֹת֔וֹ\rb* \rb and placed it|וַיִּ֥ישֶׂם\rb* \rb in a coffin|בָּאָר֖וֹן\rb* \rb in Egypt|בְּמִצְרָֽיִם׃\rb*.
